\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Conservative justices? Yeah, in what way?\u8217\'20\'19 Key senator on a supreme court in thrall to special interests\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,844 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par 11:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sheldon Whitehouse says recent court may be undergoing a \u8216\'20\'18course correction\u8217\'20\'19 following backlash to its extremist ruling and ethics scandals\par \par \uc2 The conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  may be undergoing a \u8220\'20\'1Ccourse correction\u8221\'20\'1D after witnessing a public backlash to its extremist rulings and ethics scandals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sheldon Whitehouse}}}\uc2 , chairman of the Senate judiciary subcommittee on the federal courts, has told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s highest court has made a series of radical decisions, including in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Dobbs case}}}\uc2  that overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  one year ago on Saturday, while two rightwing justices, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , have been exposed for failing disclose luxury gifts from billionaires.\par \par \uc2 But with trust in the court collapsing, it has this month defended the Voting Rights Act by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/08/supreme-court-voting-rights-decision-allen-milligan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling in favor }}}\uc2  of Black voters in Alabama and preserved a law that aims to keep Native American children with tribal families. Both were unexpected victories for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 and a sign that they might finally be awakening to public opinion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrankly, I think the recent Alabama decision would have gone the other way had it not been for the blowback on Dobbs,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator Whitehouse said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CThe challenge that they\u8217\'20\'19re not \u8216\'20\'18conservative\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re captured \u8211\'20\'13 and the preposterous behavior of Thomas. That was a pretty heavy course correction. Some of them said, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, damn, looks like we\u8217\'20\'19re going have to act like judges for a while. Till this blows over!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse found it strange that the Alabama voters decision rested so heavily on precedent \u8211\'20\'13 something that the current justices, three of whom were appointed by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , have often been content to ignore.\par \par \uc2 He says: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere was all that when you were throwing out Dobbs? They have not let precedent get in their way when they\u8217\'20\'19ve wanted the result for quite a while and to have it pop up so flagrantly in the middle of the Alabama case? You guys, that\u8217\'20\'19s funny.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The senator believes that the court\u8217\'20\'19s new sensitivity to public opinion could extend to the upcoming case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/moore-v-harper-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Moore v Harper}}}\uc2 , another gerrymandering case in which Republican legislators in North Carolina are asking the court to grant them unfettered power to set rules for voting and elections \u8211\'20\'13 a dangerous notion in the era of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of a stolen election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always thought that was probably a throwaway case for them. If you look at the people who are pitching the case to them, so many of them are under investigation, under indictment, in disbarment proceedings. It\u8217\'20\'19s the whole creepy \u8216\'20\'18big lie\u8217\'20\'19 apparatus that came in with that and I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure the court wants to take a look at that crowd and say, yeah, we\u8217\'20\'19re going with them to develop a completely wacky new argument that nobody\u8217\'20\'19s ever accepted as being anything but a fever dream before. That\u8217\'20\'19s just a bad combo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse, 67, has been a senator for Rhode Island, America\u8217\'20\'19s smallest state, since 2007 and is currently chairman of the Senate budget committee. He has spent years delivering speeches on the Senate floor in two series: \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/news/release/with-climate-bill-stalled-whitehouse-delivers-280th-time-to-wake-up-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time to Wake Up}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, about the climate crisis, and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/feb/22/the-scheme-senators-highlight-rightwing-influence-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Scheme}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, about a decades-long plot to remake the supreme court in service to shadowy billionaires and big special interests.\par \par \uc2 One of his \u8220\'20\'1CThe Scheme\u8221\'20\'1D speeches came to the attention of Lawrence O\u8217\'20\'19Donnell, an MSNBC host and former congressional aide, who suggested that the subject would make good podcast material. Whitehouse discovered that the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s own studio could produce it. The first episode of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.senate.gov/news/release/whitehouse-launches-making-the-case-podcast-to-shine-light-on-far-right-scheme-to-capture-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Making the Case}}}\uc2  offers an accessible history lesson with Congressman Hank Johnson, Slate senior editor Dahlia Lithwick and Lisa Graves of True North Research.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse reflects on the new venture while sitting in an airy Capitol Hill office surrounded by photographs of himself with Democratic presidents \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , Barack Obama and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . There are also pictures of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2011/07/23/us/23sundlun.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bruce Sundlun}}}\uc2 , a former governor of Rhode Island and mentor, and President \uc2 Franklin Roosevelt\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with a hand-signed note to Whitehouse\u8217\'20\'19s grandfather, also named Sheldon Whitehouse, who served as a foreign service officer.\par \par \uc2 The senator is speaking just hours before the \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published an article}}}\uc2  raising questions about Alito\u8217\'20\'19s failure to report taking a private jet to Alaska for a luxury fishing trip in 2008, provided by a billionaire hedge fund manager whose business interests have come before the court. Whitehouse will tweet in response: \u8220\'20\'1CThis just keeps getting worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2  that Thomas accepted decades of undisclosed trips from a longtime friend, the Republican mega-donor Harlan Crow, that included stays at Crow\u8217\'20\'19s private resort, flights on his jet, and a vacation onboard Crow\u8217\'20\'19s yacht in Indonesia. \uc2 Crow\uc2  also purchased property from Thomas and paid private school tuition for a Thomas great-nephew.\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls show that such revelations have shaken public faith in the court as never before. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.axios.com/click/31863425.7964/aHR0cHM6Ly9wb2xsLnF1LmVkdS9wb2xsLXJlbGVhc2U_cmVsZWFzZWlkPTM4NzQmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NzbmVha3BlZWsmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/58c6e533a79328702e8b4bbfBdaa8f817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quinnipiac poll}}}\uc2  published this week found that it has a 30% approval rating among registered voters \u8211\'20\'13 the lowest since Quinnipiac first asked the question in 2004. This mood has created an appetite for speeches, podcasts and journalistic investigations to lift the curtain on an institution that once seemed above the political fray and beyond reproach.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse, who wrote about Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with Crow in a book about dark money and the supreme court, tells the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1CA couple of things are happening and they interact with each other. One is that people are just grossed out by the Harlan Crow/\uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  revelations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI checked: in Rhode Island, if you\u8217\'20\'19re a municipal employee, you can have three lunches not exceeding $25 and they have to be reported, and here\u8217\'20\'19s this guy who\u8217\'20\'19s supposedly a judge going on quarter-million-dollar free vacations and not reporting it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThen people are beginning to realise that this is not a conservative court. This is a special interests-captured court. But we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a very ready narrative in American society for explaining the difference and we still get people who cover the court and know a fair amount about it saying the \u8216\'20\'18conservative\u8217\'20\'19 justices. Yeah, in what way?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 2022 the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/06/21/us/major-supreme-court-cases-2022.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upended precedents}}}\uc2  at an astonishing clip, curtailing or revoking rights such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and due process while expanding religious rights and rights to carry guns. It twice delivered blows to the ability of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  to combat pollution.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse believes that the term conservative has been \u8220\'20\'1Cobsolete\u8221\'20\'1D since dark money began funding groups such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/leonard-leo-watchdog-complaint-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leonard Leo\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  Federalist Society to handpick justices for the court. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing about the way they\u8217\'20\'19re behaving as judges that meets any definition of small \u8216\'20\'18c\u8217\'20\'19 conservative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continues: \u8220\'20\'1CLittle by little, the facts of the decisions they\u8217\'20\'19ve been up to are beginning to break through with something more than just them being \u8216\'20\'18conservative\u8217\'20\'19. There\u8217\'20\'19s this overlay of who\u8217\'20\'19s in charge behind the scenes. Of course that pops up everywhere, in the amicus briefs, in the dark money behind their confirmations. You can\u8217\'20\'19t make it stop. Harlan Crow intersects with it. And then Dobbs was a clang the gong moment where everybody realised, oh, this is a little not normal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One fix might lie with Congress. Dick Durbin, chairman of the Senate judiciary committee, has announced plans to take up supreme court ethics legislation. But in April the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/25/politics/john-roberts-congress-supreme-court-ethics/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turned down an invitation}}}\uc2  from Durbin to testify, citing the \u8220\'20\'1Cexceedingly rare\u8221\'20\'1D nature of such an appearance.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse comments: \u8220\'20\'1CI can understand that he had horrible questions he\u8217\'20\'19d have to answer and, for that reason, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to. I very much disagree that his separation of powers argument holds any water at all. That\u8217\'20\'19s pure window dressing for, \u8216\'20\'18I just don\u8217\'20\'19t want to come over and have to explain what he did\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 thinking of Thomas. I have some human sympathy for him not wanting to come over and answer questions for his wayward colleague but he was very slippery about the way he did it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse wants Roberts to demonstrate that he is taking the ethics issue seriously and believes he might be pushed to do so by the judicial conference, the policymaking body of the federal courts that has a code of conduct followed by lower court judges. At an awards ceremony last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/24/us/chief-justice-roberts-supreme-court-ethics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roberts acknowledged}}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe are continuing to look at things we can do\u8221\'20\'1D to adhere to the highest standards of conduct.\par \par \uc2 But no action by the current court has been as tangible or devastating for millions of people as Dobbs, which resulted in the decision to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that had in effect legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-samuel-alito-66c301d223759e842ad95e89f597d587#:~:text=Alito%20said%20the%20justices%20who,unequivocally%20leaves%20for%20the%20people."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito\u8217\'20\'19s majority opinion}}}\uc2  stated that \u8220\'20\'1Ca right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not deeply rooted in the Nation\u8217\'20\'19s history and traditions\u8221\'20\'1D. The procedure is now almost completely banned in 14 states.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse naturally has a podcast episode marking the first anniversary. He reflects: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you really are going to throw out a decision that stood for so long and matters so much to so many people, you expect that they try to keep within existing law. Instead, they make up a whole new analysis that allows them to get where they want to get \u8211\'20\'13 the whole \u8216\'20\'18history and tradition\u8217\'20\'19 shtick that they pulled together,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The ruling was a prime example of the court being out of step with public opinion. Republicans paid the price in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections. Now candidates for president in 2024 are tiptoeing around the issue, with Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-abortion-2024-president-d453c0cc7589568673b1c5209dfded51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusing to commit}}}\uc2  to a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit and rival \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida, facing scrutiny over a six-week ban in his home state.\par \par \uc2 Whitehouse comments: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge liability that they\u8217\'20\'19ve opened up for themselves in a party that has hung with the extremists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs decision galvanised activists to demand Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s resignation, push for reforms such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/21/supreme-court-expansion-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding the number of justices}}}\uc2  and make the case to voters that the supreme court is a defining issue at the ballot box, not merely a nice-to-have.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of the advocacy groups that work in this space \u8211\'20\'13 whether it\u8217\'20\'19s environmental groups, civil rights groups, labour groups \u8211\'20\'13 have awakened to the nature of the problem at the supreme court and are now taking it on in a whole different way, looking at the dark money, looking at the capture, looking at the mischievous and mysterious briefing just prepared.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLooking at that whole scenario and realising, wow, we got outplayed for about 20 years now and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to figure out how to fight back. This can\u8217\'20\'19t be issue 15 for us any longer. This has to be right at the top across a whole array of advocacy areas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230626ej6q0018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
