\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A year of trauma and terror\u8217\'20\'19: Democrats issue calls to action as US marks Roe reversal\b0\par\par\uc2 Victoria Bekiempis and agencies \par \uc2 892 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2023\par 11:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18States have imposed extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8217\'20\'19 says President Biden while Vice-President Harris gives fiery speech\par \par \uc2 As the US on Saturday marked one year since the country\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters and politicians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/24/abortion-demonstrations-expected-roe-v-wade-dobbs-anniversary-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-649703408f084ea43c43f95b#maincontent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a call to action}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and prepared for reproductive health to be a flashpoint of the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jun/23/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed the landmark 1973 decision}}}\uc2  that had enshrined a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the wake of its overturning, more than one dozen states have green-lighted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and many others have passed laws dramatically restricting access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStates have imposed extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that put the health and lives of women in jeopardy, force women to travel hundreds of miles for care, and threaten to criminalize doctors for providing the health care that their patients need and that they are trained to provide,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The president added: \u8220\'20\'1CYet state bans are just the beginning. Congressional Republicans want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, but go beyond that, by taking \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medication for terminating a pregnancy off the market and [to] make it harder to obtain contraception. Their agenda is extreme, dangerous, and out-of-step with the vast majority of Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy administration will continue to protect access to reproductive health care and call on Congress to restore the protections of Roe v Wade in federal law once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During a powerful speech in North Carolina on Saturday, Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  called for the restoration of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the US, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CExtremist Republicans in Congress have proposed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. But I have news for them. We\u8217\'20\'19re not having that. We\u8217\'20\'19re not standing for that. We won\u8217\'20\'19t let that happen. And by the way, the majority of Americans are with us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of Americans, I do believe, agree that one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body. The \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  must put back in place what the supreme court took away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic Congress member Jasmine Crockett described the period post-Dobbs as \u8220\'20\'1Ca year of trauma & terror for women across the country, especially in states like Texas where Roe was our last line of defense\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy district is 40% Black and majority women. It\u8217\'20\'19s the people I represent that are hurt by life-saving medical care the most,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CNorth Texas has the highest rate of hospitalization due to pregnancy complications in the entire state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor all their talk about protecting babies, let me ask you this: What happens to the already born children of a mother who dies from pregnancy complications because she can\u8217\'20\'19t get the treatment she needs during an ectopic pregnancy? Who\u8217\'20\'19s protecting them?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , decried \u8220\'20\'1Crightwing extremists on the supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D for \u8220\'20\'1Cshamefully\u8221\'20\'1D reversing the decades-long precedent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans in Congress want to impose a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D the New York Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJeffries/status/1672626482328248321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1672626482328248321%7Ctwgr%5E7c36134941ebff4d227aac52e1032bbac8faa6b1%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2023%2Fjun%2F24%2Fabortion-demonstrations-expected-roe-v-wade-dobbs-anniversary-live%3FfilterKeyEvents%3Dfalsepage%3Dwith3Ablock-649703408f084ea43c43f95b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2 , referring to the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency\u8217\'20\'19s Make American Great Again slogan. \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Dems are working hard to stop these extremists and restore reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As many issued calls to action, some took steps to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovernorHobbs/status/1672298922805710849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1672298922805710849%7Ctwgr%5Ec46b10f9f021f9db439c8a5850a51889d35a7c67%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2023%2Fjun%2F24%2Fabortion-demonstrations-expected-roe-v-wade-dobbs-anniversary-live%3FfilterKeyEvents%3Dfalsepage%3Dwith3Ablock-649700e28f08c081c5bb7965"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an executive order}}}\uc2  to better protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the south-western state.\par \par \uc2 The executive order makes central all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related prosecutions under Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general so that local prosecutors don\u8217\'20\'19t limit access to abortions. Hobbs\u8217\'20\'19s executive order also directs state agencies not to aid in any investigations relating to providing, assisting, seeking or obtaining reproductive health care that would be legal in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Hobbs\u8217\'20\'19s order also calls on Arizona to refuse extradition requests from other states that want to prosecute persons seeking or providing legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Amid Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 calls for the restoration of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a group of influential reproductive rights organizations \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 endorsed Biden and Harris in the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 A statement from \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , head of the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/pressroom/planned-parenthood-endorses-biden-for-re-election-amid-continued-attacks-on-reproductive-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare. \u8230\'20\'26 We need leaders who are committed to protecting our freedoms, not taking them away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the upcoming presidential election is unlikely to be a landslide for either party \u8211\'20\'13 victories and losses in recent elections have been decided with thin margins \u8211\'20\'13 most American voters disagree with Roe\u8217\'20\'19s reversal.\par \par \uc2 In an NBC News poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/first-read/poll-61-voters-disapprove-supreme-court-decision-overturning-roe-rcna90415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  Friday, 61% of voters said they disagreed with the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs. Sixty-seven percent of women disapproved of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Despite the fact that Roe\u8217\'20\'19s reversal appears to have little popular support, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders are describing the decision as a first step.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are at the starting line,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1672646749264007168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1672646749264007168%7Ctwgr%5Ee4724bb5465e131501e4b5677c675a1531704731%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Flive%2F2023%2Fjun%2F24%2Fabortion-demonstrations-expected-roe-v-wade-dobbs-anniversary-live%3FfilterKeyEvents%3Dfalsepage%3Dwith3Ablock-6496010f8f08657ec7321dc3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Marjorie Dannenfelser}}}\uc2 , president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have just begun. We have just begun a journey to start saving lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Protests opposing the Dobbs decision are expected across the US throughout the weekend.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230626ej6q0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
