\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18How dare they?\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says in fiery speech on Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturn as protests mark anniversary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 5,543 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2023\par 20:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats pledge to protect reproductive rights as US marks one year since supreme court overturned federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It is slightly past 4pm in Washington DC. Here is a wrap up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement to mark the one-year anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe, which he said \u8220\'20\'1Chas already had devastating consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CStates have imposed extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that put the health and lives of women in jeopardy, force women to travel hundreds of miles for care, and threaten to criminalize doctors for providing the health care that their patients need and that they are trained to provide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the stage in North Carolina on Saturday and delivered an impassioned address on restoring nationwide reproductive freedoms following a year since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strip them. Speaking to a crowd full of supporters including healthcare professionals and activists, Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they? How dare they attack basic healthcare? How dare they attack our fundamental rights? How dare they attack our freedom?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A handful of Democratic lawmakers have pledged their support on Saturday to protect and fight for reproductive rights as the country marks first anniversary of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturn. \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Dems are working hard to stop these extremists and restore reproductive freedom. Together we will win,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , House minority leader. US representative \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  of Maryland tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CPro-choice America won\u8217\'20\'19t rest until we restore women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom as law of the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As reproductive rights activists protested against the end of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders celebrated one year since the landmark decision was overturned. Speaking at the Faith & Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority conference in Washington, Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, framed the end of Roe as just the beginning of right-wing activists\u8217\'20\'19 work.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  has signed an executive order that will further protect reproductive rights across the state and curtail restrictive reproductive legislation from Republicans. On Friday, Hobbs tweeted about her executive order, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI will not allow extreme and out of touch politicians to get in the way of the fundamental rights of Arizonans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Several reproductive rights organizations have announced their endorsement of the Biden-Harris administration in the upcoming 2024 presidential election. The organizations include \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , NARAL (National Association for the Repeal of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  Laws) Pro-Choice America , and EMILYs List, a political action committee dedicated to electing Democratic pro-choice women into office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than a quarter of registered US voters say they will only vote for candidates who share their beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll released earlier this week}}}\uc2 , a total (28%) one point higher than last year. The survey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Gallup}}}\uc2 , was released before the first anniversary of Dobbs v Jackson, by which conservatives on the supreme court removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been safeguarded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/roe-reversal-dobbs-decision-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 1973.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  on Roe v Wade overturn: 'Unprecedented human rights crisis'\par \par \uc2 Human rights organization \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  has issued a statement condemning the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision a year ago to strip federal reproductive right protections.\par \par \uc2 Tarah Demant, the national programs director at \uc2 Amnesty International USA\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne year after the Supreme Court shamefully stripped millions of their rights, women, girls, and people who can become pregnant in the United States are facing an unprecedented human rights crisis.\par \par \uc2 A patchwork of devastating laws now blankets the country. One in three women and girls of reproductive age now live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is either totally or near-totally inaccessible\u8230\'20\'26and a climate of fear is being purposefully sewn to restrict women, girls, and people who can get pregnant from finding legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYet despite these coordinated and vitriolic attacks on our rights, Americans continue to overwhelmingly support access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , multiple states have added new protections, and activists across states continue to advocate for their rights. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a human right and basic healthcare, and activists across the country and around the world are more determined than ever to ensure that people across the USA will be able to access this right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators hold up signs during the demonstration of Amnesty International Italy, on 4 July 2022 in Rome, near the US embassy, to protest against the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling that, on 24 June 2022, reversed Roe v Wade. Photograph: Stefano Montesi/Corbis/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Planned Parenthood \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -providing clinic in Fairview Heights, Illinois saw a 700% increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -seeking patients from out of state.\par \par \uc2 According to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/planned-parenthood-saw-700-spike-in-abortion-patients-1850571119"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by Jezebel, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  said that the 700% increase in out-of-stage patients seeking abortions in their Fairview Heights clinic comes along with a 35% increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients overall who came to the clinic in the last year.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the outlet, Yamelsie Rodriguez, president and CEO of Reproductive Health Services of St. Louis region\u8217\'20\'19s Planned Parenthood branch, said that the patients coming to her clinic hail from 29 states and are \u8220\'20\'1Cmostly from the South.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/illinois/abortion-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 categorized}}}\uc2  Illinois as a state with \u8220\'20\'1Cprotective\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. Currently, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned at fetal viability, generally 24\u8211\'20\'1326 weeks of pregnancy, and state Medicaid funds cover abortions.\par \par \uc2 In addition, Illinois has a shield law that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers from investigations launched by other states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following the overturn of Roe vs. Wade, women of color have found themselves struggling even more to access reproductive healthcare in a medical and political landscape that has traditionally failed them.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights reporter Poppy Noor profiled two women, Anya Cook and Samantha Casiano, on their experiences of being denied abortions in post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 Here is the full story on Cook and Samantha\u8217\'20\'19s experiences and how they reflect the harsh realities faced by countless of other women of color in America:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/post-roe-abortion-women-of-color"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They forced me to carry my baby to the end\u8217\'20\'19: women of color on being denied \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 A patient waits to have an ultrasound before a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on opening day at Alamo Women\u8217\'20\'19s Clinic in Albuquerque, New Mexico, on 22 August 2022. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a video address on Saturday, New York attorney general Letitia James reaffirmed New York\u8217\'20\'19s status as a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers and promised to continue fighting for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 James said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA ban on abortions will not ban abortions. It will only ban safe abortions.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s important to know that New York is a sanctuary city and state and that we provide assistance to young women, individuals who need reproductive care\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Here in New York, we believe in you having control over your body and we believe in providing you with healthcare.\par \par \uc2 I will continue to fight and to use the law to protect your rights each and every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 New York Attorney General Letitia James speaks at a rally in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Tuesday, May 3, 2022, in New York. Photograph: Jason DeCrow/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barbara Lee, a US representative from California since 1998, has pledged to continue fighting for reproductive rights in light of the first anniversary of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep fighting for every person who finds herself in the same situation I was once in: pregnant, out of options, and forced to take extreme measures,\u8221\'20\'1D Lee tweeted.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs we mark the 1 year anniversary of losing our right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Roe?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Roe}}}\uc2 , I'm vowing to keep fighting.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep fighting for every person who finds herself in the same situation I was once in: pregnant, out of options, and forced to take extreme measures. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0xyJb9tnhQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0xyJb9tnhQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Barbara Lee (@RepBarbaraLee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBarbaraLee/status/1672315186823458816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Lee, a longtime champion of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, is the author of the EACH Woman Act which would repeal the discriminatory Hyde Amendment that has restricted many women\u8217\'20\'19s access to reproductive healthcare, her website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lee.house.gov/issues/reproductive-justice-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Singer Demi Lovato has released a new song inspired by the first anniversary of Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19s overturn.\par \par \uc2 Lovato titled the pro-choice song \u8220\'20\'1CSwine,\u8221\'20\'1D which was released on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been one year since the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to dismantle the constitutional right to a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and although the path forward will be challenging, we must continue to be united in our fight for reproductive justice.\par \par \uc2 I created \u8216\'20\'18SWINE\u8217\'20\'19 to amplify the voices of those who advocate for choice and bodily autonomy. I want this song to empower not only the birthing people of this country, but everyone who stands up for equality, to embrace their agency and fight for a world where every person\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions about their own body is honored,\u8221\'20\'1D Lovato {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/Cty5MQurykK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  caption.\par \par \uc2 The music video features Lovato in front of men who appear to represent supreme court justices as she leads a revolt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy life, my voice/My rights, my choice/It\u8217\'20\'19s mine, or I\u8217\'20\'19m just swine,\u8221\'20\'1D she sings. \u8220\'20\'1CMy blood, my loins/My lungs, my noise/It\u8217\'20\'19s mine, or I\u8217\'20\'19m just swine,\u8221\'20\'1D she sings.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s been one year since the Supreme Court's decision to dismantle the constitutional right to a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and although the path forward will be challenging, we must continue to be united in our fight for reproductive justice. I created \u8216\'20\'18SWINE\u8217\'20\'19 to amplify the voices of those\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bOayj5Z3Qj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bOayj5Z3Qj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Demi Lovato (@ddlovato) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ddlovato/status/1671882115150143491?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some images coming through the newswires as people across the country attend rallies marking the one-year anniversary of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturn:\par \par \uc2 A woman wearing a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights T-shirt listens to speakers before Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaks on the one year anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision at the Grady Cole Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, on Saturday. Photograph: Erik S Lesser/\uc2 EPA\uc2  A person holds a banner at the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March at Columbus Circle in Washington, on Saturday, the first anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade. Photograph: Bryan Olin Dozier/NurPhoto/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  A woman holds a sign at the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March at Columbus Circle in Washington, on Saturday. Photograph: Bryan Olin Dozier/NurPhoto/Shutterstock People gather for the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March at Columbus Circle in Washington, on Saturday, to advocate for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the first anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe. Photograph: Bryan Olin Dozier/NurPhoto/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  Suanna Bruinooge from Alexandria, Virginia, attends \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists rally in Washington, on Saturday. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters Protest signs lie on the ground at the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March in Washington. Photograph: Bryan Olin Dozier/NurPhoto/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chelsea Clinton\uc2  has also chimed in on first anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision that stripped federal protections of reproductive rights from women, saying that she\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Creally f**king angry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an interview at Aspen: Health in Aspen, Colorado, NBC host Kristen Welker asked the daughter of former president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and former secretary of state \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  on her thoughts about the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Clinton replied:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really f**king angry and I am \u8212\'20\'14 and that is an uncomfortable place to be because of the historical women tropes that so often have been used to kind of silence and diminish women and our voices, not just in this country but throughout human history. But I\u8217\'20\'19m really angry because we know that women have died.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr'I'm really f*cking angry... women have died' \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chelsea Clinton\uc2  shared candid thoughts about the upcoming 1-year anniversary of SCOTUS' Dobbs decision while speaking at the Aspen Ideas: Health summit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OC3mRPsMWX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OC3mRPsMWX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1672221213245198338?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on supreme court's overturn of Roe: 'How dare they?'\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the stage in North Carolina on Saturday and delivered an impassioned address on restoring nationwide reproductive freedoms following a year since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strip them.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to a crowd full of supporters including healthcare professionals and activists, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they? How dare they attack basic healthcare? How dare they attack our fundamental rights? How dare they attack our freedom?\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In the midst of this healthcare crisis, extremist so-called leaders in states across our nation have proposed or passed more than 350 new laws to restrict these freedoms and the right to have access to reproductive healthcare. Right now in our country, 23 million women of reproductive age live in a state with an extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in effect\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Most of us here know is that many women don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they are pregnant in six weeks. Which by the way tells us most of these politicians don\u8217\'20\'19t even understand how the body actually works. They don\u8217\'20\'19t get it,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris continued.\par \par \uc2 She went on to issue a strong warning towards Republican lawmakers in Congress, saying:\par \par \uc2 Extremist Republicans in Congress have proposed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. But I have news for them. We\u8217\'20\'19re not having that. We\u8217\'20\'19re not standing for that. We won\u8217\'20\'19t let that happen. And by the way, the majority of Americans are with us.\par \par \uc2 The majority of Americans, I do believe, agree that one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  must put back in place what the Supreme court took away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaks on the one year anniversary of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision at the Grady Cole Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, on Saturday. Photograph: Erik S Lesser/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 A handful of Democratic lawmakers have pledged their support on Saturday to protect and fight for reproductive rights as the country marks first anniversary of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s overturn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Dems are working hard to stop these extremists and restore reproductive freedom. Together we will win,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , House minority leader.\par \par \uc2 enltrRight-wing extremists on the Supreme Court shamefully overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RoevWade?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RoevWade}}}\uc2  1 yr ago.\par \par \uc2 MAGA Republicans in Congress want to impose a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 House Dems are working hard to stop these extremists and restore reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 Together we will win.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  (@RepJeffries) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJeffries/status/1672626482328248321?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA year after \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 disastrous Dobbs decision, I\u8217\'20\'19m highlighting that districts like mine \u8211\'20\'13 and Black women in particular \u8211\'20\'13 are hurting the most,\u8221\'20\'1D said US representative Jasmine Crockett of Texas\u8217\'20\'19s 30th district.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy district is 40% Black and majority women. It\u8217\'20\'19s the people I represent that are hurt by life-saving medical care the most \u8230\'20\'26 North Texas has the highest rate of hospitalization due to pregnancy complications in the entire state \u8230\'20\'26 For all their talk about protecting babies, let me ask you this: What happens to the already born children of a mother who dies from pregnancy complications because she can\u8217\'20\'19t get the treatment she needs during an ectopic pregnancy? Who\u8217\'20\'19s protecting them?\u8221\'20\'1D Crockett added.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's been a year of trauma & terror for women across the country, especially in states like Texas where Roe was our last line of defense.\par \par \uc2 A year after \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2 ' disastrous Dobbs decision, I'm highlighting that districts like mine\u8212\'20\'14and Black women in particular\u8212\'20\'14are hurting the most. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vfz2P44YKH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vfz2P44YKH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congresswoman Jasmine Crockett (@RepJasmine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJasmine/status/1672602475290066944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 US representative \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  of Maryland tweeted: \u8220\'20\'1CPro-choice America won\u8217\'20\'19t rest until we restore women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom as law of the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOne year after the Supreme Court's disgraceful Dobbs decision, two American futures stand opposed: one upholding women\u8217\'20\'19s rights & health care, one defined by theocrats, misogynists and fanatics.\par \par \uc2 Pro-choice America won't rest until we restore women\u8217\'20\'19s freedom as law of the land.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  (@RepRaskin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin/status/1672618362491359232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Senator Tammy Duckworth of Illinois echoed similar sentiments, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be honest: Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 anti-choice agenda is not about protecting life. If it was, perhaps they would help us tackle our maternal mortality crisis or do something\u8211\'20\'13anything\u8211\'20\'13to help end gun violence. But they don\u8217\'20\'19t. Because it\u8217\'20\'19s not about saving lives. It\u8217\'20\'19s about control\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Look, I know that a lot of us are tired from the seemingly endless fight to protect our most basic human rights. But we have to do more. Congress has to do more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrLook, I know that a lot of us are tired from the seemingly endless fight to protect our most basic human rights.\par \par \uc2 But we have to do more.\par \par \uc2 Congress has to do more.\par \par \uc2 I'll never stop working to restore and enshrine the right to choose for every American in every state.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tammy Duckworth (@SenDuckworth) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenDuckworth/status/1672609784816709632?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 House Democrats also joined the pledges as they released compilation of various members promising to protect reproductive freedoms:\par \par \uc2 enltrOne year ago, \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  overturned Roe v. Wade \u8212\'20\'14 leaving millions of Americans without access to essential health care.\par \par \uc2 Every day since the Dobbs decision, House Democrats have fought to restore reproductive freedom and protect access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 We won\u8217\'20\'19t back down. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jMVeGicHiw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jMVeGicHiw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Democrats (@HouseDemocrats) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDemocrats/status/1672615454807040001?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 As reproductive rights activists protested against the end of Roe v Wade, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders celebrated one year since the landmark decision was overturned.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Faith & Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority conference in Washington, Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, framed the end of Roe as just the beginning of right-wing activists\u8217\'20\'19 work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are at the starting line,\u8221\'20\'1D Dannenfelser said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have just begun. We have just begun a journey to start saving lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMarjorie Dannenfelser, president of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony List, says she just came from the Lincoln Memorial, where she was celebrating one year since the end of Roe:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re at the starting line. We\u8217\'20\'19ve just begun. We\u8217\'20\'19ve just begun a journey to start saving lives.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4CrNQ2Celh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4CrNQ2Celh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1672646749264007168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\uc2  Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters listen as Republican presidential candidate and former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  addresses \u8216\'20\'18National Celebrate Life Day Rally\u8217\'20\'19 on first anniversary of the supreme court overturning Roe. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 More people are feeling backed into a corner after the supreme court struck down the nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, with many turning to birth control.\par \par \uc2 In one of our latest features in our \u8216\'20\'18A year without Roe\u8217\'20\'19 series, \uc2 Ema O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\uc2  explores the way that people\u8217\'20\'19s relationships with birth control have evolved over the past year.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Connor reports:\par \par \uc2 Dr Rachel Neal, an OB-GYN working out of Atlanta, Georgia, said she has seen a trend toward LARCs nationally over the past six years, in part due to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, as well as medicaid expansion and more insurance plans covering long term contraceptives.\par \par \uc2 But in the past year Dr Neal has also seen an increased skepticism about any methods \u8211\'20\'13 including many birth control pills and IUDS \u8211\'20\'13 that pause or stop menstruation altogether.\par \par \uc2 Before Roe was overturned, Dr Neal said that patients often saw not getting their periods as a positive side effect because they didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to deal with cramps or spend money on tampons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow they\u8217\'20\'19re uneasy towards methods that cause them to have no periods because they want to \u8230\'20\'26 prove to themselves that they\u8217\'20\'19re not pregnant,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Neal said.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/roe-reversal-dobbs-decision-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The people turning to birth control after the fall of Roe: \u8216\'20\'18I feel a little safer\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden issues statement on one-year anniversary of Roe v Wade overturn\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement to mark the one-year anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe, which he said \u8220\'20\'1Chas already had devastating consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 "States have imposed extreme and dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that put the health and lives of women in jeopardy, force women to travel hundreds of miles for care, and threaten to criminalize doctors for providing the health care that their patients need and that they are trained to provide.\par \par \uc2 Yet state bans are just the beginning. Congressional Republicans want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, but go beyond that, by taking \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved medication for terminating a pregnancy, off the market, and make it harder to obtain contraception. Their agenda is extreme, dangerous, and out-of-step with the vast majority of Americans.\par \par \uc2 My administration will continue to protect access to reproductive health care and call on Congress to restore the protections of Roe. vs. Wade in federal law once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOne year ago, the Supreme Court took away a constitutional right from the American people, denying women the right to choose.\par \par \uc2 My Administration has taken swift and strong action \u8211\'20\'13 but the job isn't finished until Congress codifies the protections of Roe v. Wade once and for all. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NjoQrW6Kj3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NjoQrW6Kj3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1672601262716493826?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a recent interview, actor and comedian Natalie Morales spoke to the Guardian about her fight for reproductive rights, her own coming out journey and her film Plan B.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Andrew Lawrence reports:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the main things in it is the conscience clause, a law that already exists in many states and is growing in others where a pharmacist can deny a prescription to anybody based on their personal beliefs, even if that prescription is legal,\u8221\'20\'1D Morales said of the film during a Zoom call earlier this month\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Not only that, but many places are trying to outlaw the Plan B pill \u8211\'20\'13 which is not even an abortifacient! I\u8217\'20\'19ve never understood why, if you\u8217\'20\'19re against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you would also be against contraceptives. That has never made sense to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the full interview, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/20/actor-natalie-morales-interview-abortion-contraception"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Actor Natalie Morales on the end of Roe: \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to sow divisiveness any more\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 Natalie Morales New York Premiere Sony Pictures\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1CNo Hard Feelings\u8221\'20\'1D, AMC Lincoln Square, USA - 20 Jun 2023 Photograph: Marion Curtis/StarPix for Sony Pictures/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 61% of voters disapprove of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade, according to a new poll by NBC.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/first-read/poll-61-voters-disapprove-supreme-court-decision-overturning-roe-rcna90415"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 results}}}\uc2 , which NBC released on Friday, showed that amongst women, 67% disapproved of the decision while 31% approved.\par \par \uc2 Amongst 18 and 49-year old women, 77% disapproved while 21% indicated otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Two-thirds of suburban women, 66%, surveyed also cited their disapproval, while 33% said they approved.\par \par \uc2 Amongst white, Black and Latino voters, a majority said they disagreed with the decision (with 57% of white voters, 78% of Black voters, and 70% of Latino voters indicating so).\par \par \uc2 92% of Democrats surveyed disagreed with the decision while 31% of Republicans said they disproved.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights reporter Poppy Noor reflects on her year of covering the erosion of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights across the country following the overturn of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In her personal piece, Noor describes her experience of reporting on harrowing and heartbreaking stories of women struggling with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and the multitude of complexities they face following the stripping of federal reproductive rights in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  context obsessed with a very particular kind of religious morality, the changes a body goes through in a pregnancy sometimes feel like an afterthought,\u8221\'20\'1D Noor writes.\par \par \uc2 For Noor\u8217\'20\'19s full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/abortion-reporting-while-pregnant-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What it\u8217\'20\'19s like to cover \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  while pregnant: \u8216\'20\'18People saw me as a container for a child\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona governor signs executive order to protect reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  has signed an executive order that will further protect reproductive rights across the state and curtail restrictive reproductive legislation from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Hobbs tweeted about her executive order, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI will not allow extreme and out of touch politicians to get in the way of the fundamental rights of Arizonans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The executive order includes the following measures:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Centralizes all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  related prosecutions under the state attorney general\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Directs state agencies to not assist in investigations relating to providing, assisting seeking or obtaining reproductive healthcare\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Declines extradition requests from other states seeking to prosecute individuals who provide, assist, seek or receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services legal in Arizona\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Establishes the Governor\u8217\'20\'19s Advisory Council on Protecting Reproductive Freedom to make recommendations that expand access to reproductive healthcare\par \par \uc2 enltrI signed an Executive Order protecting Arizonans\u8217\'20\'19 reproductive freedom. I will not allow extreme and out of touch politicians to get in the way of the fundamental rights of Arizonans. My Executive Order does four things to the full extent of my authority: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2digbGB6EM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2digbGB6EM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  (@GovernorHobbs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovernorHobbs/status/1672298922805710849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights organization endorse Biden-Harris administration for 2024\par \par \uc2 Several reproductive rights organizations have announced their endorsement of the Biden-Harris administration in the upcoming 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The organizations include \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , NARAL (National Association for the Repeal of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Laws) Pro-Choice America , and EMILYs List, a political action committee dedicated to electing Democratic pro-choice women into office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have been committed to fighting back against the onslaught of attacks against our reproductive freedom. And we need them to continue this critical work.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is health care\u8230\'20\'26 We need leaders who are committed to protecting our freedoms, not taking them away. That is why we must re-elect President Biden and Vice President Harris: people we can trust to keep rebuilding a path forward, because we know the journey to rebuilding our rights will be met with challenges,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/pressroom/planned-parenthood-endorses-biden-for-re-election-amid-continued-attacks-on-reproductive-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said }}}\uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NARAL-Pro Choice America\uc2  echoed similar sentiments, with its president Mini Timmaraju {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/2023/06/23/naral-pro-choice-america-endorses-president-joe-biden-and-vice-president-kamala-harris-for-reelection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying:}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are the strongest advocates for reproductive freedom ever to occupy the White House, and \uc2 NARAL Pro-Choice America\uc2  proudly endorses their reelection. It\u8217\'20\'19s as simple as this: \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters to Americans. In elections since the Supreme Court took away our right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voters have mobilized in massive numbers to elect Democrats who will fight to restore it...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 EMILYs List president Laphonza Butler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emilyslist.org/news/emilys-list-endorses-vice-president-kamala-harris-for-reelection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  the following statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the Dobbs decision ended a constitutional right for the first time in this country\u8217\'20\'19s history, we were grateful to have leaders in the White House like President Biden and Vice President Harris, who have been vocal advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the government and across the country\u8230\'20\'26 For her work as a groundbreaker, tireless advocate for reproductive freedom, and inspiring change-maker, EMILYs List is thrilled to endorse Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for reelection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters gather for a \u8220\'20\'1Cpink out\u8221\'20\'1D protest organized by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  in the rotunda of the Wisconsin Capitol, on 22 June 2022, in Madison, Wisconsin. Photograph: Harm Venhuizen/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than a quarter of registered US voters say they will only vote for candidates who share their beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll released earlier this week}}}\uc2 , a total (28%) one point higher than last year.\par \par \uc2 The survey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Gallup}}}\uc2 , was released before the first anniversary of Dobbs v Jackson, by which conservatives on the supreme court removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been safeguarded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/roe-reversal-dobbs-decision-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 1973.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal at least in some form. Since Dobbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has been seen as a vital motivating factor in a succession of Democratic successes.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/abortion-poll-election-voters-roe-v-wade-gallup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Increase in Americans planning to vote for candidate who shares \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  view}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 One aspect of Roe being overturned is that trainee OB-GYNs in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned lost their access to training.\par \par \uc2 Texas is one of those states where clinics have stopped providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care to patients as well as training to medical residents.\par \par \uc2 Yet as a part of a national program requirement, under the \uc2 Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education\uc2  (\uc2 ACGME\uc2 ), medics need to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acgme.org/globalassets/pfassets/programrequirements/220_obstetricsandgynecology_9-17-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experience in \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  procedures}}}\uc2  to become an OB-GYN physician.\par \par \uc2 In Texas, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  training is now limited to miscarriage procedures, but not hands-on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Melanie Sevcenko spoke to OB-GYN residents to find out how they\u8217\'20\'19ve been coping in the past 12 months and how Dobbs has changed the practice of medicine in the US:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/18/obgyn-doctor-abortion-law-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8216\'20\'18We weren\u8217\'20\'19t meant to be criminals\u8217\'20\'19: the gynecologists training out of state post-Roe}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstrators attend a rally at the Texas Capitol in Austin, Texas, May 14, 2022. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 While the American public is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/15/gallup-survey-abortion-support-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largely in favour of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  provision}}}\uc2 , a large part of the Republican party is not.\par \par \uc2 And yesterday, some of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s most influential evangelical Christian figures assembled in Washington to celebrate the anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs ruling.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 At Friday\u8217\'20\'19s Faith & Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s annual conference, activists urged Republican presidential candidates to push for more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, on the other hand, insist the issue will help them going into the 2024 election. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to give the keynote address Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  called for a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least 15 weeks of pregnancy. He told the conference:\par \par \uc2 The battle for life is far from over. We\u8217\'20\'19ve not come to the end of our cause. We\u8217\'20\'19ve simply come to the end of the beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must not rest and we must not relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law in every state in this country. Every Republican candidate for president should support a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before 15 weeks as a minimum nationwide standard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 South Carolina Senator Tim Scott, who is also running for the Republican 2024 nomination, thanked God for the high court\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court ruling to overturn Roe v Wade has led to a patchwork of vastly unequal access to reproductive care across the US.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned in 14 states and severely restricted in five more. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Andrew Witherspoon, Jessica Glenza, Noa Yachot and Alvin Chang crunched the data and compiled the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans now in place to create the map in the article below to show where state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws stand as of 13 June 2023.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tracking where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws stand in every state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of the first anniversary of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization and the overturning of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 A year ago today, \uc2 Scotus\uc2  ruled that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no longer federally protected, which means states now have the power to regulate the procedure as they see fit.\par \par \uc2 Since the Dobbs ruling, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans invalidated by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in some states were resurrected. Elsewhere, \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D, designed to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if federal protections were overturned, went into effect. In other states, new bans were passed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned in 14 US states and severely restricted in many others.\par \par \uc2 As demonstrations crop up around the country and we look back on the last year, we will bring you all the latest updates as they happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230624ej6o001e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
