\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House restates call for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to be enshrined in law as Biden signs contraception protection \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang(now); Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 4,834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2023\par 20:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House spokesperson says Congress must pass law restoring protections of Roe as US president signs executive order protecting contraception access\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It is slightly past 4pm in Washington DC. Here is a wrap up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has rejected Texas and Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s challenge to Biden deportation policy prioritizing groups of unauthorized immigrants, including suspected terrorists, convicts and those caught at the border for deportation. The states wanted the authority to fight the policy in court. The court holds that the states do not have legal standing to challenge the policy, another win for the Biden administration, especially since conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  was the only dissent.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed an executive order Friday to protect access to contraception, one day before the anniversary of the supreme court decision that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down the federal right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/06/23/fact-sheet-president-biden-issues-executive-order-on-strengthening-access-to-contraception/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2 , the president highlighted reproductive health as a top priority of his administration in the wake of the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization ruling from the conservative-led court that reversed the Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in place for half a century.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two Russian intelligence officers who attempted to interfere in a local election as part of Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal malign influence operations\u8221\'20\'1D were sanctioned Friday by the \uc2 US government\uc2 . Yegor Sergeyevich Popov and Aleksei Borisovich Sukhodolov, both members of \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s federal security service\uc2 , worked to undermine democratic processes in the US and other countries through a network of co-conspirators, the treasury department said in a statement, reported by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith has offered limited immunity to at least two Republican fake electors in return for their testimonies to a grand jury over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to overturn the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/06/23/politics/special-counsel-fake-electors-immunity-testimony-jan-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  according to}}}\uc2  a new CNN report. Sources familiar with the matter told CNN that in instances where prosecutors granted immunity to witnesses, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office arrived at the courthouse in Washington ready to compel their testimony after the witnesses indicated they would decline to answer questions under the fifth amendment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  reaffirmed the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for reproductive healthcare rights. Speaking to reporters on Friday, Jean-Pierre said: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and Vice-President Harris stand with the majority of Americans who believe the right to choose is fundamental. As the president has made clear, the only way to ensure women in every state have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is for Congress to pass a law, restoring the protections of Roe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida governor and presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has rolled out a list of 15 endorsements from South Carolina lawmakers on Thursday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ron-desantis-south-carolina-endorsements-2024-1624e1148cc234cf32179e4a5ec15be9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the Associated Press which reviewed the list, the endorsement includes 11 state House members and four state senators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Several reproductive rights organizations have announced their endorsement of the Biden-Harris administration in the upcoming 2024 presidential election. The organizations include \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , NARAL (National Association for the Repeal of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Laws) Pro-Choice America , and EMILYs List, a political action committee dedicated to electing Democratic pro-choice women into office.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor and presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has rolled out a list of 15 endorsements from South Carolina lawmakers on Thursday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ron-desantis-south-carolina-endorsements-2024-1624e1148cc234cf32179e4a5ec15be9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to}}}\uc2  the Associated Press which reviewed the list, the endorsement includes 11 state House members and four state senators.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 leadership has made Florida a refuge for those seeking freedom in a nation where it is under attack,\u8221\'20\'1D said state senator Josh Kimbrell, one of DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s endorsers, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4062148-desantis-rolls-out-endorsements-from-15-south-carolina-state-lawmakers-ahead-of-visit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports. }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo Republican in the country has beaten the radical left more than governor DeSantis, and he is the only candidate in this race who can defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , put energy back in the executive, and deliver on a bold conservative agenda that Republicans across South Carolina are looking for,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, DeSantis campaigned in North Augusta, South Carolina, drawing a crowd of supporters whom he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wrdw.com/2023/06/22/desantis-picks-up-sc-endorsements-ahead-north-augusta-visit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CYou run this process, you compete and you respect the outcome of the process\u8230\'20\'26 I think I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be the nominee no matter what happens I\u8217\'20\'19m going to work to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , that\u8217\'20\'19s what you have to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , R-Fla., high-fives voters as he walks towards the stage during his campaign stop at Riverview Park Activities Center in North Augusta, S.C., Thursday, June 22, 2023. Photograph: Katie Goodale/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP presidential hopeful \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  got booed on stage as he delivered his address at the Freedom and Faith Coalition in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 In his address, the former New Jersey governor criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m running because he has let us down. He has let us down because he\u8217\'20\'19s unwilling to take any responsibility of the mistakes that were made, any of the faults that he has and any of the things he has done. And that is not leadership, everybody. That is a failure of leadership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, the crowd quickly booed Christie.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can boo all you want. But here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing: Our faith teaches us that people have to take responsibility for what they do,\u8221\'20\'1D Christie continued.\par \par \uc2 enltrChris Christie battles boos as he goes after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the Faith & Freedom Coalition conference:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m running because he has let us down \u8230\'20\'26 You can boo all you want. But here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing: Our faith teaches us that people have to take responsibility for what they do.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ak5YomhKAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ak5YomhKAA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1672278590501666820?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He addressed the boos in a later interview with CNN, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI knew that\u8217\'20\'19s what was going to happen when I accepted the invitation but I\u8217\'20\'19m not changing my message and pandering to anybody. The truth matters and I\u8217\'20\'19m telling the truth about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D Christie told host Dana Bash.\par \par \uc2 enltr2024 presidential candidate \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  (R) on getting booed for criticizing Trump at today's Faith & Freedom Coalition conference:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI knew that's what was going to happen when I accepted the invitation... The truth matters and I'm telling the truth about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SMJIPkbY41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SMJIPkbY41}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1672286338148597761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 This is the third executive order that Biden has passed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since the rollback of Roe v Wade last June.\par \par \uc2 Read more on his first and second executive order here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden signs executive order protecting access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden signs second executive order to protect US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several reproductive rights organizations have announced their endorsement of the Biden-Harris administration in the upcoming 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The organizations include \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , NARAL (National Association for the Repeal of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Laws) Pro-Choice America , and EMILYs List, a political action committee dedicated to electing Democratic pro-choice women into office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have been committed to fighting back against the onslaught of attacks against our reproductive freedom. And we need them to continue this critical work.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is health care\u8230\'20\'26 We need leaders who are committed to protecting our freedoms, not taking them away. That is why we must re-elect President Biden and Vice President Harris: people we can trust to keep rebuilding a path forward, because we know the journey to rebuilding our rights will be met with challenges,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of the \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NARAL-Pro Choice America\uc2  echoed similar sentiments, with its president Mini Timmaraju saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are the strongest advocates for reproductive freedom ever to occupy the White House, and \uc2 NARAL Pro-Choice America\uc2  proudly endorses their reelection. It\u8217\'20\'19s as simple as this: \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters to Americans. In elections since the Supreme Court took away our right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voters have mobilized in massive numbers to elect Democrats who will fight to restore it...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 EMILYs List president Laphonza Butler released the following statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the Dobbs decision ended a constitutional right for the first time in this country\u8217\'20\'19s history, we were grateful to have leaders in the White House like President Biden and Vice President Harris, who have been vocal advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the government and across the country\u8230\'20\'26 For her work as a groundbreaker, tireless advocate for reproductive freedom, and inspiring change-maker, EMILYs List is thrilled to endorse Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for reelection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  pushed back against claims that president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest executive action on expanding contraception access is \u8220\'20\'1Clargely symbolic \u8221\'20\'1D, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt builds on the progress that we believe that we have made already and expanding contraception access for women. If you think about the Affordable Care Act, it helped millions of women save billions of dollars on birth control that they need and want. And so we understand that there are gaps still as it relates to that snd so that\u8217\'20\'19s what this executive order does today.\par \par \uc2 It does a couple of things. It\u8217\'20\'19s strengthening access to affordable high quality contraception and family planning services, and increased contraception options. It lowers out-of-pocket costs. It maximizes contraception access through the following ways: insurance coverage for those covered under the Affordable Care Act \u8230\'20\'26 Medicaid, Medicare, federal funded healthcare programs, including community health centers \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 So we don\u8217\'20\'19t believe this is symbolic. We believe that this is another step to really deal with this gap that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing across the country and to do everything that we can to continue to fight for fundamental rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to a question from a reporter on whether president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calling China\u8217\'20\'19s president Xi Jinping a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator\u8221\'20\'1D is the \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial position\u8221\'20\'1D of the White House, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president spoke for himself. I\u8217\'20\'19m just not going to go beyond what he said\u8230\'20\'26 The president is going to speak candidly. That will never change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House says Congress must pass law to restore protections of Roe\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  reaffirmed the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for reproductive healthcare rights.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on Friday, Jean-Pierre said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and vice president Harris stand with the majority of Americans who believe the right to choose is fundamental. As the president has made clear, the only way to ensure women in every state have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is for Congress to pass a law, restoring the protections of Roe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also spoke of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new executive order on furthering contraception access, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccess to contraception has become more important than ever following the Supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision and ensuing crisis for women\u8217\'20\'19s health. And today\u8217\'20\'19s action helps ensure that women can make decisions about their own health lives and also their families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has responded to concerns from Republicans over the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s integrity, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CNothing could be further from the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a press briefing on Friday, a reporter asked Garland:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans in Congress have flirted with the idea with holding the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director in contempt, it\u8217\'20\'19s become a talking point on the campaign trail, the alleged corruption in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and federal law enforcement agencies. Do the American people have cause to be concerned about the integrity of components of this justice department and\u8230\'20\'26how they\u8217\'20\'19re acting?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, Garland said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI certainly understand that some have chose to attack the integrity of the justice department as components and its employees by claiming that we do not treat like cases alike. This constitutes an attack on an institution that is essential to American democracy... Nothing could be further from the truth\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 We make our cases based on the facts and the law. These are not just words. These are what we live by\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrGarland: "Some have chose to attack the integrity of the Justice Department by claiming that we do not treat cases alike. This constitutes an attack on an institution that is essential to American democracy... Nothing could be further from the truth." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fHkHPUiNyn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fHkHPUiNyn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Price (@greg_price11) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/greg_price11/status/1672287386791755789?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  pledged to end gender-affirming services amongst minors during his Faith and Freedom Coalition address today in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I am President, American families will have a champion in the White House!\par \par \uc2 We will give every parent the right to choose where their child goes to school, we will end the gender ideology that is running rampant in our schools and we will ban chemical and surgical gender transition treatment for kids under the age of 18!\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen I am President, American families will have a champion in the White House! We will give every parent the right to choose where their child goes to school, we will end the gender ideology that is running rampant in our schools and we will ban chemical and surgical gender\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DzgcsAFRF8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DzgcsAFRF8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  (@Mike_Pence) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mike_Pence/status/1672267357358620672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s comments come amid multiple Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 pledges to end \u8216\'20\'18wokeism,\u8217\'20\'19 should they become president, including presidential candidate and Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel offered limited immunity in return for fake electors testimony - report\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith has offered limited immunity to at least two Republican fake electors in return for their testimonies to a grand jury over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to overturn the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/06/23/politics/special-counsel-fake-electors-immunity-testimony-jan-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  according to}}}\uc2  a new CNN report.\par \par \uc2 Sources familiar with the matter told CNN that in instances where prosecutors granted immunity to witnesses, \u8220\'20\'1CThe special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office arrived at the courthouse in Washington ready to compel their testimony after the witnesses indicated they would decline to answer questions under the Fifth Amendment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Within the last two weeks, at least one other witness spoke with federal investigators outside of the federal grand jury with an agreement that the witness be granted limited immunity from prosecution, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The testimonies in recent days have largely surrounded fake electors\u8217\'20\'19 schemes that were designed by attorneys affiliated with the Trump campaign three years ago.\par \par \uc2 According to sources familiar with the matter who spoke to CNN, \u8220\'20\'1CThe numbers, profile of the witnesses and prosecutor tactics suggest a probe picking up its pace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jack Smith. Photograph: Charles Dharapak/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 An Arizona Republican election official has filed a lawsuit against unsuccessful gubernatorial candidate and staunch \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporter Kari Lake who claims that she lost the 2022 race due to fraud.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/opinion/op-ed/2023/06/22/kari-lake-defamation-lawsuit-stephen-richer-explains/70348533007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  published in the Arizona Republic, Maricopa county recorder Stephen Richer said that as a result of Lake\u8217\'20\'19s false claims, he has faced \u8220\'20\'1Cviolent vitriol and other dire consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRather than accept political defeat, rather than get a new job, she has sought to undermine confidence in our elections and has mobilized millions of her followers against me,\u8221\'20\'1D Richer wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe has gone far outside of the bounds of protected free speech as guaranteed under the First Amendment and the Arizona Constitution.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m suing Kari Lake, her campaign and her political action committee for engaging in a concerted campaign to defame, threaten and isolate me,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in Maricopa county, Arizona on Thursday, names Lake, her political campaign, as well as her fundraising roup as defendants.\par \par \uc2 According to the lawsuit, Richer is seeking unspecified monetary damages, as well as the removal of all false claims from Lake\u8217\'20\'19s social media.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  has issued a statement in response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s rejection of Texas and Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s challenge to the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s deportation policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision soundly rejects the misguided attempt by Texas and Louisiana to force the government to implement the most draconian immigration enforcement policy,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Omar Jadwat\uc2 , director of the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Immigrants\u8217\'20\'19 Rights Project.\par \par \uc2 In the case which \uc2 ACLU\uc2  filed an amicus brief, the supreme court ruled that the states lacked the standing to \u8220\'20\'1Corder the Executive Branch to alter its arrest policy so as to make more arrests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  appeared undeterred from his staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, according to a new interview with Politico.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Martin Pengelly reports from Washington:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/23/mike-pence-abortion-dobbs-roe-anniversary-00103353"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking}}}\uc2  one year since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  removed the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  said candidates for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination should stand firm on the electorally unpopular issue and take a hard line on bringing in national limits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, for our campaign, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand where we\u8217\'20\'19ve always stood, and that is without apology for the right to life,\u8221\'20\'1D the former congressman, Indiana governor and vice-president to \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/06/23/mike-pence-abortion-dobbs-roe-anniversary-00103353"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Later, addressing the Faith & Freedom conference in Washington, Pence said every Republican candidate \u8220\'20\'1Cshould support a ban on abortions before 15 weeks, as a minimum nationwide standard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Claiming this was a \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable and mainstream standard\u8221\'20\'1D, Pence said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has more in common with China and North Korea than it does with the nations of Europe \u8211\'20\'13 and it is time for that to change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/mike-pence-abortion-ban-voters-republicans-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pence tells Republicans to take hard line on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  despite electoral liability}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 An Indiana chapter of the right-wing nonprofit Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  has apologized for using an Adolf Hitler quote in its newsletter.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the Hamilton county chapter of the far-right group, which the the watchdog \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/extremist-files/group/moms-liberty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 designated }}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist,\u8221\'20\'1D published a newsletter which featured the quote, \u8220\'20\'1CHe alone, who OWNS the youth, GAINS the future\u8221\'20\'1D and cited Hitler.\par \par \uc2 Following swift {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benryanwriter/status/1672032444298457088?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash }}}\uc2  online, the group which advocated for increased parental rights apologized and attempted to clarify its actions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe condemn Adolf Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s actions and his dark place in human history,\u8221\'20\'1D chapter chair Paige Miller {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/moms-for-liberty-hitler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement on a revised version of the newsletter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should not have quoted him in our newsletter and express our deepest apology,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis Hitler quote from Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  was on the top of the front page. Good lord. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/asSQaaHCLQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/asSQaaHCLQ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VrZLlFnyvK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VrZLlFnyvK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1671968392369020933?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 22, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The newest Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/will-hurd-republican-presidential-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 candidate}}}\uc2 Will Hurd\uc2  said that he will not sign a \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  loyalty pledge towards the GOP presidential nominee.\par \par \uc2 Hurd, a former Texas congressman and harsh critic of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , told CNN in a new interview that he will not pledge his allegiance to whoever the GOP nominee is for the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI won\u8217\'20\'19t be signing any kind of pledges, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that parties should be trying to rig who should be on a debate stage,\u8221\'20\'1D Hurd {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.25newsnow.com/video/2023/06/23/will-hurd-says-he-wont-sign-rnc-pledge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not in the business of lying to the American people in order to get a microphone, and I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so I can\u8217\'20\'19t honestly say I\u8217\'20\'19m going to sign something even if he may or may not be the nominee,\u8221\'20\'1D Hurd continued.\par \par \uc2 Hurd\u8217\'20\'19s comments follows \uc2 RNC\uc2  chair \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s calls for a loyalty pledge.\par \par \uc2 McDaniel told Fox News this week, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the Republican Party nomination and the pledge is staying,\u8221\'20\'1D the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4063914-mcdaniel-doubles-down-on-need-for-gop-loyalty-pledge/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 US sanctions Russians over election interference\par \par \uc2 Two Russian intelligence officers who attempted to interfere in a local election as part of Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal malign influence operations\u8221\'20\'1D were sanctioned Friday by the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yegor Sergeyevich Popov and Aleksei Borisovich Sukhodolov, both members of \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s federal security service\uc2 , worked to undermine democratic processes in the US and other countries through a network of co-conspirators, the treasury department said in a statement, reported by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 They are alleged to worked with Aleksandr Viktorovich Ionov, a Russian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/us-citizens-and-russian-intelligence-officers-charged-conspiring-use-us-citizens-illegal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged last year}}}\uc2  by the justice department with conducting a multi-year effort to use political groups in Florida, Georgia and California to interfere in elections.\par \par \uc2 Treasury department official Brian Nelson said in the statement:\par \par \uc2 The US will not tolerate threats to our democracy, and today\u8217\'20\'19s action builds on the whole of government approach to protect our system of representative government.\par \par \uc2 The department did not specify which election the two Russians are accused of attempting to influence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has not yet issued its widely anticipated decision on race-based affirmative action in college admissions, or several other significant cases. But even with the panel still in session, Republican presidential hopefuls are weighing in on its future and their hopes for the court.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Faith and Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority conference in Washington DC this morning, entrepreneur and 2024 candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  praised America as a meritocratic nation.\par \par \uc2 enltrEntrepreneur and 2024 candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  gets some audience members on their feet as he speaks at the Road to Majority conference in DC. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZSk5rJbmhd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZSk5rJbmhd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1672251313038536704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou do get ahead in this country based not on the color of your skin, but on the content of your character and your contributions,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramaswamy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I expect the supreme court in the coming days to end affirmative action in college.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The line was met with applause from the conservative crowd.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden signs executive order to protect contraception\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was signing an executive order Friday to protect access to contraception, one day before the anniversary of the supreme court decision that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down the federal right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/06/23/fact-sheet-president-biden-issues-executive-order-on-strengthening-access-to-contraception/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2 , the president highlighted reproductive health as a top priority of his administration in the wake of the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization ruling from the conservative-led court that reversed the Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in place for half a century:\par \par \uc2 Contraception is an essential component of reproductive health care that has only become more important in the wake of Dobbs and the ensuing crisis in women\u8217\'20\'19s access to healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Biden is seeking to enhance strengthen access to \u8220\'20\'1Caffordable, high quality contraception and family planning services,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement says. It\u8217\'20\'19s his third executive order on reproductive health care access since the Dobbs ruling.\par \par \uc2 The measures include expanding access and services through Medicaid, improving coverage of contraception through Medicare and seeking ways to compel private health insurance companies to provide contraception and family planning services as needed.\par \par \uc2 Biden and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are set to speak at reproductive rights event at the Mayflower hotel in Washington DC, scheduled for 4pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  again with the day\u8217\'20\'19s third ruling, writing the 5-4 majority opinion in the case of \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  v Bielski, a case about cryptocurrency. And the final ruling this morning is the case of Samia v US, another non-biggie, so to speak.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have some more details of those coming up, but essentially the court has whiffed again on dropping its rulings on any of the most-watched, most significant cases of the current session.\par \par \uc2 The next decision day is next Tuesday. There are 11 cases still to be decided, including civil rights, LBGTQ+ rights, affirmative action in colleges and universities, and perhaps most significant of all, the fate of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s program for student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court rejects Texas and Louisiana challenge to Biden deportation policy\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  has written the second ruling of the day, an 8-1 majority in the case of US v Texas.\par \par \uc2 The state was joined by Louisiana in challenging a Biden administration policy prioritizing groups of unauthorized immigrants, including suspected terrorists, convicts, and those caught at the border for deportation. The states wanted the authority to fight the policy in court.\par \par \uc2 The court holds that the states do not have legal standing to challenge the policy, another win for the Biden administration, especially since conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  was the only dissent.\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh calls it an \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinarily unusual lawsuit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Texas and Louisiana do not have a right to sue here, he says, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe do not suggest that federal courts may never entertain cases involving the executive branch\u8217\'20\'19s alleged failure to make more arrests or bring more prosecutions,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote, according to Scotusblog.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/22pdf/22-58_i425.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s that ruling.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court immigration ruling backs Biden administration\par \par \uc2 The first supreme court decision of the day is in. It\u8217\'20\'19s the case of United States v Hansen, a 7-2 ruling that concerns a man who ran an allegdly illegal adoption scheme to gain citizenship for foreign nationals.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not one of the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig\u8221\'20\'1D cases. But it is being seen as win for the Biden administration in its defense of a law that criminalizes the solicitation or encouragement of improper immigration. More details to come, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/22pdf/22-179_o75q.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here\u8217\'20\'19s the ruling in full}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re thinking that we are likely to see one or more of the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig\u8221\'20\'1D supreme court decisions coming down this morning, after yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s batch \u8211\'20\'13 while still significant \u8211\'20\'13 weren\u8217\'20\'19t among the most talked about.\par \par \uc2 The highlight of Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s opinions was a ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/supreme-court-navajo-nation-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against the Navajo nation}}}\uc2  on water rights, and the court soon closed up shop for the day after delivering only four of the 18 cases still outstanding at that stage.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amylhowe.com/2023/06/22/after-the-release-of-4-opinions-14-cases-remaining/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excellent guide to the 14 left to come}}}\uc2  from veteran supreme court analyst Amy Howe. Two of them relate to affirmative action, and how race plays a role in the college admissions process.\par \par \uc2 And while we\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for this morning\u8217\'20\'19s developments, have a read of some more high court news from my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  about mounting pressure on conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  over ethics controversies:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/harlan-crow-senate-investigation-clarence-thomas-gifts-tax-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harlan Crow on collision course with Senate over Clarence Thomas gifts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics blog readers, and welcome to our Friday edition rounding out an eventful week in Washington DC and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 This morning we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to see a batch more decisions coming down from the supreme court as the clock ticks towards the end of its current session next week.\par \par \uc2 By our reckoning, there are 14 cases that the justices still have to release opinions on. They include \u8220\'20\'1Cblockbusters\u8221\'20\'1D covering civil rights, LBGTQ+ rights, affirmative action in colleges and universities, and perhaps most significant of all, the fate of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s program for student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 The court opens for business at 10am ET, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll be here to bring you decisions as they\u8217\'20\'19re announced.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else were watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s day three of Indian prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s state visit, after he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/joe-biden-narendra-modi-visit-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressed on his human rights record}}}\uc2  on Thursday. Later this morning, Modi and Biden will meet leaders of US and Indian businesses as one of the final acts of his trip.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is reportedly gearing up for an appearance alongside other Republican presidential hopefuls at the conservative Faith & Freedom Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s Road to Majority conference in Washington DC. The former vice-president is expected to call for even tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions nationwide, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaker Kevin McCarthy is feeling the heat from moderates after Republican House extremists pushed through measures this week to censure California Democrat Adam Schiff for investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and sent dead-on-arrival impeachment articles for Biden, introduced by Colorado rightwinger \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , for committee debate.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230623ej6n001pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
