\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: number of Britons who want to rejoin EU highest since 2016\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,818 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 June 2023\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Data showed 58% would vote to re-enter bloc, while more respondents trust the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  over the \uc2 UK government\uc2  than vice versa. Plus, the 1,572 US politicians who have helped ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Seven years after the Brexit referendum, the proportion of Britons who want to rejoin the EU has climbed to its highest level since 2016, according to a survey.\par \par \uc2 Britons and Europeans also think the UK\u8217\'20\'19s return to the EU is becoming more likely, while British respondents are more optimistic about the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s future \u8211\'20\'13 to the extent of trusting the \uc2 European Commission\uc2  more than their own government.\par \par \uc2 Data from \uc2 YouGov\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest Brexit tracker survey found that, excluding those who said they would not vote or did not know, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2023/jun/23/britons-who-want-to-rejoin-eu-at-highest-since-2016-survey-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 58.2% of people in Britain would vote to rejoin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The percentage is only fractionally down on the 60% recorded in February this year \u8211\'20\'13 the highest figure since comparable records began in February 2012 \u8211\'20\'13 and has risen more or less consistently since a post-referendum low of 47% in early 2021.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else did the survey find? Europeans are a lot less likely to think other countries would follow Britain\u8217\'20\'19s example, the survey found. Asked whether they would vote to remain in the EU or leave in a Brexit-style referendum, 62% of respondents in France and 63% in Italy, which are traditionally among the least enthusiastic EU member states, said they would vote to stay.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why is the EU flag in the news? Ministers in the UK have been accused of criminalising the flying of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  flag on government buildings in England after London\u8217\'20\'19s City Hall was told it could be prosecuted for displaying it on the anniversary of the Brexit referendum.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18True explorers\u8217\'20\'19: tributes paid to men killed in \u8216\'20\'18catastrophic implosion\u8217\'20\'19 of Titan sub\par \par \uc2 Tributes have been paid to the five people who are now believed to have been instantly killed in a \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic implosion\u8221\'20\'1D of the Titan submersible during its dive to the Titanic.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, after days of aerial and underwater searches, a robotic diving vehicle deployed from a Canadian ship discovered a debris field from the submersible Titan on the seabed 1,600ft (488 metres) from the bow of the Titanic.\par \par \uc2 Five major fragments of the 22ft Titan were located in the debris field left from its disintegration, including the vessel\u8217\'20\'19s tail cone and two sections of the pressure hull, officials said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe debris field here is consistent with a catastrophic implosion of the vehicle,\u8221\'20\'1D said R Adm John Mauger of the \uc2 US Coast Guard\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Titan, operated by the US-based company \uc2 OceanGate Expeditions\uc2 , had been missing since it lost contact with its surface support ship on Sunday morning about an hour and 45 minutes into what should have been a two-hour dive to the world\u8217\'20\'19s most famous shipwreck.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has the White House said? The White House said the loved ones of the five men had endured a \u8220\'20\'1Charrowing ordeal\u8221\'20\'1D over the past week. \u8220\'20\'1COur hearts go out to the families and loved ones of those who lost their lives on the Titan,\u8221\'20\'1D it said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThey have been through a harrowing ordeal over the past few days, and we are keeping them in our thoughts and prayers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Was the sound of the implosion heard? The US navy has said it detected an \u8220\'20\'1Canomaly\u8221\'20\'1D that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/23/titanic-sub-us-navy-james-cameron-detected-likely-implosion-titan-submersible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 probably the Titan\u8217\'20\'19s fatal implosion}}}\uc2 , soon after the submersible went missing, while the film director, James Cameron, claims his sources in the deep-sea exploration industry also detected a \u8220\'20\'1Cloud bang\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 US honeybees suffer second deadliest season on record\par \par \uc2 The US\u8217\'20\'19s honeybee hives staggered through their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jun/23/us-honeybees-second-deadliest-season"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second highest death rate on record}}}\uc2 , with beekeepers losing nearly half of their managed colonies, an annual bee survey found.\par \par \uc2 But by using costly and herculean measures to create new colonies, beekeepers are somehow keeping afloat. Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s University of Maryland and \uc2 Auburn University\uc2  survey found that even though 48% of colonies were lost in the year that ended 1 April, the number of US honeybee colonies \u8220\'20\'1Cremained relatively stable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Honeybees are crucial to the food supply, pollinating more than 100 of the crops we eat, including nuts, vegetables, berries, citruses and melons. Scientists said a combination of parasites, pesticides, starvation and effects of the climate crisis keep causing large die-offs.\par \par \uc2 Last year\u8217\'20\'19s 48% annual loss is up from the previous year\u8217\'20\'19s loss of 39% and the 12-year average of 39.6%, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not as high as 2020-21\u8217\'20\'19s 50.8% mortality rate, according to the survey, which was funded and administered by the nonprofit research group Bee Informed Partnership. Beekeepers told the surveying scientists that a 21% loss over the winter is acceptable and more than three-fifths of beekeepers surveyed said their losses were greater than that.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why are bees so important? The demand for pollination from commercial bee colonies is growing even as beekeepers have to work harder to make up for losses. The \uc2 US Department of Agriculture\uc2  says 35% of the human diet comes from insect-pollinated plants and the honeybee is responsible for 80% of that pollination.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A painting has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2023/jun/23/lost-portrait-allegorical-painting-of-two-ladies-compton-verney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saved for the UK}}}\uc2  in recognition of its \u8220\'20\'1Coutstanding significance\u8221\'20\'1D for the study of race and gender in 17th-century Britain, it will be announced today. The \u8220\'20\'1Chighly unusual\u8221\'20\'1D portrait of two women \u8211\'20\'13 one black and one white \u8211\'20\'13 depicted as companions and equals with similar dress, hair and jewellery, dates to about 1650.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government has reportedly reprimanded the US ambassador to China over comments made by\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden in which he referred to\par \par \uc2 Xi Jinping as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdictator\u8221\'20\'1D. Nicholas Burns {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/23/china-reportedly-rebukes-us-ambassador-after-biden-called-xi-a-dictator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received the diplomatic note}}}\uc2  hours after Biden made comments about Xi at a fundraiser in California.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The weapons supervisor charged with involuntary manslaughter over the shooting death of a cinematographer on the set of the Alec Baldwin film Rust has been charged with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/rust-film-weapons-supervisor-on-alec-baldwin-movie-charged-with-evidence-tampering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evidence tampering}}}\uc2  for allegedly passing drugs to someone else on the day of the shooting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Paul McCartney\uc2  has clarified how artificial intelligence has been used to create a new Beatles song, saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing has been artificially or synthetically created\u8221\'20\'1D. Last week, McCartney announced that he had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/jun/23/paul-mccartney-says-theres-nothing-artificial-in-new-beatles-song-made-using-ai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 employed AI technology}}}\uc2  on an unreleased Beatles demo from the 70s.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: 1,572 US politicians have helped ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Roe fell. They\u8217\'20\'19re mostly men\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been one year since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The procedure is now prohibited in 14 states and restricted in six more, leaving large swaths of the midwest and south without access to basic reproductive care. To mark the first anniversary of the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization decision, the case that overturned Roe v Wade, the Guardian has created {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2023/jun/22/abortion-ban-politicians-who-voted-for-restrictions-who-are-they-men-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a visual directory of state legislators}}}\uc2  who embraced the opportunity to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. These are the faces of lawmakers and governors whose votes helped pass bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception or after six weeks, before most women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Heartache, horror, hope \u8211\'20\'13 my year reporting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  while pregnant\par \par \uc2 In her final piece before going on maternity leave, Poppy Noor writes about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/23/abortion-reporting-while-pregnant-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 witnessing the decimation of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights}}}\uc2  while on the road as a reproductive rights reporter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve driven across America\u8217\'20\'19s varied terrain as a reporter throughout this tidal wave of new laws, bearing witness to a monumental assault on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. I have faced, head on, the fury that comes from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists for daring to write about abortions. And I have seen the dogged organization and jubilance of those who have protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their states after months of pounding on doors, rain or shine \u8230\'20\'26 Covering this beat, especially while pregnant, has changed my depth of vision. To see this assault up close and personal is to see it for what it is: not a journey to protect life; but to stifle, suppress and suffocate freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Or this: \u8216\'20\'18You can\u8217\'20\'19t pour from an empty cup\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 US violence prevention workers tell of burnout\par \par \uc2 For the past 24 years, Jose Gomez has been on call at any hour. Gomez works as a community violence interrupter in Stockton, California, focused on extracting high-risk young people from the cycles of violence in their own neighborhoods. Sometimes he\u8217\'20\'19s in the aftermath of a shooting to guide survivors and their families away from retaliation. Sometimes he mediates conflicts before they turn violent. The work of violence prevention specialists has long gone under the radar. In recent years, however, there\u8217\'20\'19s been more recognition of their work, with the White House praising this model for violence reduction and a growing number of cities investing in it. But as the profile of community violence interrupters grows, these workers say they have to navigate secondhand trauma, unpredictable hours and the ebb and flow of grant funding that their jobs rely on \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/22/violene-prevention-worker-burnout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 burnout}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Beijing records hottest June day since weather records began as heatwave hits China\par \par \uc2 Beijing logged its hottest June day since records began yesterday, the national weather service said, as swathes of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/23/beijing-weather-hottest-june-day-since-records-began-heatwave-northern-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 northern China sweltered in 40C heat}}}\uc2 . On Friday the capital upgraded its warning for hot weather to red, saying most parts of the city could roast in temperatures of up to 40C (104F). China has a four-tier weather warning system, with red the most severe, followed by orange, yellow and blue. Scientists say rising global temperatures \u8211\'20\'13 caused largely by burning fossil fuels \u8211\'20\'13 are aggravating extreme weather worldwide, and many countries in Asia have experienced deadly heatwaves and record temperatures in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Weather tracker: China issues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jun/23/weather-tracker-china-issues-heatstroke-alert-amid-historic-heatwave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heatstroke alert}}}\uc2  amid historic heatwave\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Guest spends 603 nights at five-star Indian hotel \u8216\'20\'18without paying\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Indian police are investigating a suspected fraudster who spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/22/guest-spends-603-nights-at-five-star-indian-hotel-without-paying"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly two years in a five-star hotel without paying}}}\uc2 , local media have said. Ankush Dutta booked a room at Roseate House hotel in Delhi on 30 May 2019 and was supposed to check out the next day. But he extended his stay for 603 nights until 22 January 2021, leaving behind unpaid bills of $70,000. \u8220\'20\'1CAccounts were falsified to conceal the actual outstanding dues,\u8221\'20\'1D the police complaint read, quoted by the Indian Express newspaper. Hotel managers also filed a police complaint against several employees for conspiracy, forgery and cheating, with officials saying they suspected staff members had been bribed to manipulate in-house software systems.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230623ej6n001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
