\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senior senators threaten to step up supreme court ethics reform after \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  revelations \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang (now); Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 6,887 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 June 2023\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Alito reportedly accepted seat on private plane owned by \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 ; expert says he should have recused himself from Singer cases before the courtFull report: Alito did not declare gifts from billionaire with cases before supreme court\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It is slightly past 4pm in Washington DC. Here is a wrap up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-undisclosed-gifts-billionaire-paul-singer-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing questions}}}\uc2  for not declaring several gifts received from conservative billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 , and for not recusing himself when Singer had cases presented before the court. The latest report questioning the ethics of supreme court justices came from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2 , which recently published several articles on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/series/supreme-court-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relationship}}}\uc2  between justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and Republican billionaire Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The powerful governor of Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s state-backed investment fund has been invited to testify before a Senate committee in the wake of a proposed merger between Saudi-backed LIV Tour and the PGA, raising the possibility the executive could be questioned under oath about issues ranging from the future of golf to the execution of journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/jamal-khashoggi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamal Khashoggi}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Yasir al-Rumayyan\uc2 , governor of Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s Public Investment Fund, was invited to testify on July 11 by the Senate permanent subcommittee on investigations, whose chairman, Democratic senator Dick Blumenthal, is one of the toughest critics of Saudi on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A January 6 rioter who attacked a Capitol Hill police officer in the neck with a stun gun has been jailed for 12 years. Daniel \u8220\'20\'1CDJ\u8221\'20\'1D Rodriguez yelled, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump won!\u8221\'20\'1D as he was led out of the courtroom where the US district judge Amy Berman Jackson sentenced him to 12 years and seven months behind bars for his role in the attack on Congress. Only two other January 6 defendants have received longer prison terms after hundreds of sentencings for Capitol riot cases.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Over a quarter of registered voters in the US have indicated that they will only vote for candidates who share the same beliefs as them on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More than a quarter of registered US voters say they will only vote for candidates who share their beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll released on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , a total (28%) one point higher than last year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As the US marks one year since the end of Roe v Wade, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  is launching a six-figure ad campaign to highlight the stakes of the 2024 elections. The campaign, which starts tomorrow, includes billboards and digital ads in battleground states like Georgia and Arizona, as well as marquee locations like Times Square in New York City.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two senior senators have threatened to step up legislation on supreme court ethics reform following a report saying \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  had failed to declare a flight paid for by a conservative billionaire. \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , chair of the Senate judiciary committee, and Sheldon Whitehouse, chair of the Senate judiciary subcommittee on federal courts, oversight, agency action, and federal rights, have announced a markup in the judiciary committee on ethics reform legislation surrounding the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing representative \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/118/bills/hres503/BILLS-118hres503ih.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  a resolution calling for the impeachment of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Boebert introduced the resolution as a privileged resolution which will in turn force the House to vote on the measure in two days.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  has filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , accusing the company of knowingly enrolling millions of consumers into its Amazon Prime paid subscription without their consent. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.wawd.323520/gov.uscourts.wawd.323520.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed in federal court in Seattle, the FTC accused \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of using \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulative, coercive, or deceptive user-interface designs known as \u8216\'20\'18dark patterns\u8217\'20\'19 to trick consumers into enrolling in automatically-renewing Prime subscriptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. For the full story on \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure to disclose his luxury gifts, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-undisclosed-gifts-billionaire-paul-singer-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Samuel Alito did not declare gifts from billionaire with case before US supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The powerful governor of Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s state-backed investment fund has been invited to testify before a Senate committee in the wake of a proposed merger between Saudi-backed LIV Tour and the PGA, raising the possibility the executive could be questioned under oath about issues ranging from the future of golf to the execution of journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/jamal-khashoggi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jamal Khashoggi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yasir al-Rumayyan\uc2 , governor of Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s Public Investment Fund, was invited to testify on July 11 by the Senate permanent subcommittee on investigations, whose chairman, Democratic senator Dick Blumenthal, is one of the toughest critics of Saudi on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 Jay Monahan\uc2 , the PGA commissioner, and LIV {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/golf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Golf}}}\uc2  League chief executive and commissioner \uc2 Greg Norman\uc2 , were also invited to testify.\par \par \uc2 The proposed merger of LIV Tour and PGA, which also involves the DP World Tour, has received a frosty reception on Capitol Hill, where it is facing questions not only from Blumenthal, but also the Senate finance committee. The call for Rumayyan to testify at a hearing, however, marks a new twist.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/us-senate-saudi-yasir-al-rumayyan-pga-golf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate asks governor of Saudi wealth fund to testify over LIV-PGA merger}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic representative \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  has responded critically to recent reports of \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure to disclose luxury gifts from conservative billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans used to respect the Supreme Court,\u8221\'20\'1D Lieu tweeted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow with the flagrant violations of ethical rules and possibly laws by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  (and potentially other Justices), Americans can rightfully ask: has the Supreme Court turned into a cesspool of corruption?\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrAmericans used to respect the Supreme Court. Now with the flagrant violations of ethical rules and possibly laws by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  (and potentially other Justices), Americans can rightfully ask: has the Supreme Court turned into a cesspool of corruption? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TCpAZt6cnX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/TCpAZt6cnX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  (@tedlieu) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tedlieu/status/1671369733961138178?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 A January 6 rioter who attacked a Capitol Hill police officer in the neck with a stun gun has been jailed for 12 years:\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 Daniel \u8220\'20\'1CDJ\u8221\'20\'1D Rodriguez yelled, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump won!\u8221\'20\'1D as he was led out of the courtroom where the US district judge Amy Berman Jackson sentenced him to 12 years and seven months behind bars for his role in the attack on Congress.\par \par \uc2 Only two other January 6 defendants have received longer prison terms after hundreds of sentencings for Capitol riot cases.\par \par \uc2 The judge said Rodriguez, 40, was \u8220\'20\'1Ca one-man army of hate, attacking police and destroying property\u8221\'20\'1D at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou showed up in DC spoiling for a fight,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t blame what you did once you got there on anyone but yourself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A body camera worn by Fanone captured the Metropolitan police officer screaming after Rodriguez shocked him with a stun gun while he was surrounded by a mob.\par \par \uc2 Another rioter had dragged Fanone into the crowd outside a tunnel on the Lower West Terrace of the Capitol, where police were guarding an entrance. Other rioters began beating Fanone, who lost consciousness and suffered a heart attack after Rodriguez pressed the stun gun against his neck and repeatedly shocked him.\par \par \uc2 Fanone addressed the judge before she imposed the sentence. The former officer described how the January 6 attack prematurely ended his law enforcement career and turned him into a target for Trump supporters who cling to the lie that Democrats stole the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/jan-6-capitol-attack-jail-sentence-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 rioter who attacked police officer with stun gun jailed for 12 years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two major political action committees have released a statement in response to reports over \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s disclosure failures.\par \par \uc2 The End Citizens United and Let America Vote Action Fund called Alito\u8217\'20\'19s actions \u8220\'20\'1Cshameful\u8221\'20\'1D and also condemned justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  surrounding his own failures to disclose luxury trips provided by billionaire GOP donor Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJustice Alito\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with billionaire mega-donor \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2  is improper and downright shameful. The mere existence of such a relationship undermines the public\u8217\'20\'19s trust and confidence in the Supreme Court, but what is even more alarming is the concrete evidence proving the corruption within the ranks of the Justices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese scandals affirm Americans\u8217\'20\'19 fears about impartiality and fairness. The fundamental question arises: Is justice truly blind, or is it simply a commodity to be bought and sold by those with deep pockets? Justices Alito and Thomas have put a price tag on it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese scandals should serve as a wake-up call for Congress to implement and enforce a strict code of ethics. Anything short of this will empower the extremist conservative Justices to continue to engage in this reprehensible behavior.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 End Citizen United // Let America Vote Action Fund supports two pieces of legislation that would tackle the ethics problems plaguing the court: the Supreme Court Ethics, Recusal, and Transparency (SCERT) Act and the DISCLOSE Act. These bills will offer more transparency into the justices\u8217\'20\'19 outside activities to identify any potential conflicts of interests, and accountability when they run afoul of the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Over a quarter of registered voters in the US have indicated that they will only vote for candidates who share the same beliefs as them on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Erum Salam reports:\par \par \uc2 More than a quarter of registered US voters say they will only vote for candidates who share their beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll released on Wednesday}}}\uc2 , a total (28%) one point higher than last year.\par \par \uc2 The survey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/507527/abortion-remains-potent-issue-pro-choice-voters.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from Gallup}}}\uc2 , was released before the first anniversary of Dobbs v Jackson, by which conservatives on the supreme court removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been safeguarded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/roe-reversal-dobbs-decision-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in 1973.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal at least in some form. Since Dobbs, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has been seen as a vital motivating factor in a succession of Democratic successes.\par \par \uc2 According to another poll released on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/06/21/1183253121/roe-dobbs-abortion-affirmative-action-gender-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by NPR/PBS News Hour/Marist}}}\uc2 , 57% of Americans say the court was wrong to bring down Roe.\par \par \uc2 According to Gallup, for many voters who do not solely base their vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the issue is still important: just 14% of respondents said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not a major issue in deciding how they vote. That was down two points on the same survey last year and nine points from the previous low, 23%, in 2007.\par \par \uc2 In the new Gallup survey, 56% said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was just one issue out of many when deciding how to vote. In 2022, 54% gave that answer.\par \par \uc2 Primary elections continue to serve as a testing ground for the issue.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/abortion-poll-election-voters-roe-v-wade-gallup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Increase in Americans planning to vote for candidate who shares \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  view}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers across California are voicing their discontent with senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s absence in recent years as a result of her old age and health issues.\par \par \uc2 In May, Feinstein returned to senate following an extended medical absence due to shingles.\par \par \uc2 Despite aides reassuring that Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s health is improving and that she is playing a more active role on Capitol Hill, Democrats remain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/dianne-feinstein-democrats-divided-health-questions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frustrated}}}\uc2  over the 89-year old senator, with several of them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/06/21/politics/feinstein-absence-california-delegation-complaints/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking to}}}\uc2  CNN.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Raul Ruiz\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe last time I spoke with her on anything face-to-face was right before the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to a a conversation he had over three years ago with Feinstein about designating a natural monument in his district.\par \par \uc2 Representative Mike Levin told CNN that the last conversation he remembers having with Feinstein is in 2018, after he won his San Diego area seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been quite a while,\u8221\'20\'1D Levin said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t speak with her on a regular basis, and that\u8217\'20\'19s been before any of the recent health challenges she\u8217\'20\'19s had.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh boy, I can\u8217\'20\'19t remember. Probably when I was a freshman member,\u8221\'20\'1D representative \uc2 Nanette Barrag\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , who was elected in 2016 from a district near Los Angeles, told CNN.\par \par \uc2 In response to when the last time they spoke was and whether he could recall any collaborations with Feinstein, six-term representative Mark Takano said, \u8220\'20\'1CGosh,\u8221\'20\'1D adding, \u8220\'20\'1CHard to say anything we\u8217\'20\'19ve done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver my 11 years in Congress, I haven\u8217\'20\'19t worked that closely with her,\u8221\'20\'1D representative \uc2 Ami Bera\uc2  told the outlet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the US marks one year since the end of Roe v Wade, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  is launching a six-figure ad campaign to highlight the stakes of the 2024 elections.\par \par \uc2 The campaign, which starts tomorrow, includes billboards and digital ads in battleground states like Georgia and Arizona, as well as marquee locations like Times Square in New York City.\par \par \uc2 The DNC\u8217\'20\'19s digital ad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u3lQyx8BMI8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brings attention }}}\uc2  to some of the Republican presidential candidates\u8217\'20\'19 past controversial comments and legislative actions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is heard bragging, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the one that got rid of Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D and Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is seen signing his state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on a press call today, DNC chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  noted that total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/27/abortion-laws-exceptions-polling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely unpopular}}}\uc2  with the American people. The Roe reversal is believed to have contributed significantly to Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 disappointing performance in the 2022 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile these Republicans are in a race to see who can have the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  platform, one thing is for certain: the American people have repeatedly -- repeatedly -- rejected these extremists,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they will do it again in 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Suzan DelBene, chair of House Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 campaign arm, predicted Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access would determine control of the lower chamber next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2024, the threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide will be clearer than ever,\u8221\'20\'1D DelBene told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Republicans will not stop until they ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, and this extremism on reproductive freedoms will cost Republicans the House majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior senators \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  and Sheldon Whitehouse threaten to step up supreme court ethics reform\par \par \uc2 Two senior senators have threatened to step up legislation on supreme court ethics reform following a report saying \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  had failed to declare a flight paid for by a conservative billionaire.\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , chair of the Senate judiciary committee, and Sheldon Whitehouse, chair of the Senate judiciary subcommittee on federal courts, oversight, agency action, and federal rights, have announced a markup in the judiciary committee on ethics reform legislation surrounding the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The announcement said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court is in an ethical crisis of its own making due to the acceptance of lavish gifts from parties with business before the court that several justices have not disclosed. The reputation and credibility of the court are at stake. Chief justice Roberts could resolve this today, but he has not acted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe highest court in the land should not have the lowest ethical standards. But for too long that has been the case with the United States supreme court. That needs to change. That\u8217\'20\'19s why when the Senate returns after the July 4th recess, the Senate judiciary committee will mark up supreme court ethics legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope that before that time, chief justice Roberts will take the lead and bring supreme court ethics in line with all other federal judges. But if the court won\u8217\'20\'19t act, then Congress must.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s right wing representative \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/118/bills/hres503/BILLS-118hres503ih.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  a resolution calling for the impeachment of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Boebert introduced the resolution as a privileged resolution which will in turn force the House to vote on the measure in two days.\par \par \uc2 The resolution calls for Biden to be impeached for \u8220\'20\'1Chigh crimes and misdemeanors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Using the powers of his high office, President Biden 17 has knowingly presided over an executive branch that has 18 continuously, overtly, and consistently violated Federal 19 immigration law by pursuing an aggressive, open-borders 20 agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D it added, accusing Biden of intentionally facilitating a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete and total invasion of the southern border,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy has commented on the resolution, telling reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing to do,\u8221\'20\'1D the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4060468-republicans-bash-boebert-for-forcing-impeachment-vote-frivolous/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is one of the most serious things you can do as a member of Congress. I think you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to go through the process. You\u8217\'20\'19ve got to have the investigation \u8230\'20\'26 And throwing something on the floor actually harms the investigation that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s Republican representative \uc2 Don Bacon\uc2  called Boebert\u8217\'20\'19s move \u8220\'20\'1Cplayground games\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be playground games, in my view. This should be serious,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on Wednesday, the Hill reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there\u8217\'20\'19s real facts for impeachment then you go there. But doing this is wrong, and I think the majority of the conference feels that way \u8230\'20\'26 Impeachment shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be something that is frivolous \u8230\'20\'26 We should get to the facts of that, but just doing a privileged motion is wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate committee chair Whitehouse, who has organized 10 climate-focused hearings since he took the helm of the Senate budget committee, asked Oreskes to \u8220\'20\'1Cdescribe for us the academic study of the fossil fuel disinformation operation \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She explained that in 2004, she published a paper on the scientific consensus on the human-caused climate crisis, and that as a result of that paper, she was targeted by a disinformation campaign herself.\par \par \uc2 I started getting hate mail,\u8221\'20\'1D she said \u8220\'20\'1CI had people file complaints against me at my university and went through some unpleasant experiences as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She wasn\u8217\'20\'19t alone. Others, like climate scientist Michael Mann, were attacked in similar ways.\par \par \uc2 That experience of being attacked led me to try to understand what these attacks were, who was funding them, who was behind them, and why they were doing it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The field of study into climate disinformation, she said, is \u8220\'20\'1Cmature\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Later, ranking member Grassley asked Pielke to talk about the influence dark money has on Democrats.\par \par \uc2 In 10 climate hearings, Democrats have never asked a single one of their witnesses about their receipts of dark money, let alone attempted to impugn their integrity or accuse them of conspiracy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pielke responded: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t explain exactly why your colleagues aren\u8217\'20\'19t willing to look at the dark money ties of their own witnesses,\u8221\'20\'1D going on to lob accusations.\par \par \uc2 Oregon senator \uc2 Jeff Merkley\uc2  spoke about these accusations later on.\par \par \uc2 He offered a solution for his Republican colleagues who are concerned about dark money\u8217\'20\'19s influence on Democrats.\par \par \uc2 We should simply have all political money be disclosed. And the citizens can decide on what impacts that has.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The DISCLOSE Act, introduced by Whitehouse in the Senate this year, would expose the sources of these clandestine funds.\par \par \uc2 I would invite my colleagues across the aisle to join us in ending dark money on both sides,\u8221\'20\'1D said Merkley.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are intensifying their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related attacks on Republicans, as the US prepares to mark one year since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a press conference on Capitol Hill this morning, Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , a Democrat of Washington, noted that 14 states have passed total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans since Roe was reversed on 24 June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Every day, women across our country are confronting a dystopian reality, one where Republican politicians have the final say in their healthcare decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray said. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are forced to stay pregnant against their will, even when their health and lives are at risk.\par \par \uc2 enltrMake no mistake: the health care crisis that has unfolded in the aftermath of the Dobbs decision is a direct result of Republicans' radical, decades-long agenda to control women's bodies and futures.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (@PattyMurray) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PattyMurray/status/1671237710411968513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats plan to push for legislation providing federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception access, but such a bill will almost certainly fail in the Republican-controlled House.\par \par \uc2 Despite those challenges, Murray emphasized that Democrats would not abandon their efforts to expand and reinforce reproductive rights across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are not going to settle for a country where men in state legislatures are taking away their fundamental freedom to decide what happens to their bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to settle for a country where their daughters and granddaughters have fewer rights than they did just a year ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  has filed a lawsuit against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , accusing the company of knowingly enrolling millions of consumers into its Amazon Prime paid subscription without their consent.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.wawd.323520/gov.uscourts.wawd.323520.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed in federal court in Seattle, the FTC accused \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of using \u8220\'20\'1Cmanipulative, coercive, or deceptive user-interface designs known as \u8216\'20\'18dark patterns\u8217\'20\'19 to trick consumers into enrolling in automatically-renewing Prime subscriptions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It went on to detail the ways \uc2 Amazon\uc2  allegedly complicated the cancellation process, which the company called \u8220\'20\'1CIliad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For years, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also knowingly complicated the cancellation process for Prime subscribers who sought to end their membership.\par \par \uc2 Under significant pressure from the Commission \u8211\'20\'13 and aware that its practices are legally indefensible \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  substantially revamped its Prime cancellation process for at least some subscribers shortly before the filing of this Complaint.\par \par \uc2 However, prior to that time, the primary purpose of the Prime cancellation process was not to enable subscribers to cancel, but rather to thwart them.\par \par \uc2 Fittingly, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  named that process \u8220\'20\'1CIliad,\u8221\'20\'1D which refers to Homer\u8217\'20\'19s epic about the long, arduous Trojan War. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  designed the Iliad cancellation process (\u8220\'20\'1CIliad Flow\u8221\'20\'1D) to be labyrinthine, and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and its leadership \u8230\'20\'26 slowed or rejected user experience changes that would have made Iliad simpler for consumers because those changes adversely affected \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bottom line.\par \par \uc2 It added that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  generates $25bn in revenue from Prime memberships and that one of the company\u8217\'20\'19s goals is \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasing subscriber numbers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rhode Island\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse has issued a slew of harsh responses to Alito\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/live/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-gifts-supreme-court-trump-biden-latest-news?page=with:block-6492f8b48f08c081c5bb5405#block-6492f8b48f08c081c5bb5405"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defense}}}\uc2  of himself in the Wall Street Journal following \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reports of his disclosure failures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, my, the questions: First, who orchestrated this weird pre-buttal with the infamous WSJ Polluter Page, and did Alito get help from a PR firm? If so, who paid?\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Whitehouse.\par \par \uc2 enltrOh, my, the questions:\par \par \uc2 First, who orchestrated this weird pre-buttal with the infamous WSJ Polluter Page, and did Alito get help from a PR firm?\par \par \uc2 If so, who paid? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vPRbOgfsRC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vPRbOgfsRC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1671323049067524097?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThird, why not ask the Financial Disclosure Committee of the Judicial Conference, the body set up exactly for that purpose, for its advice on what should be disclosed? That\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s there,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitehouse continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd what, he just happened to be flying to Alaska and there just happened to be a private jet going to Alaska with an empty seat, and he just happened to find that out, like on some weird billionaire shared-ride \uc2 Uber\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D the senator wrote, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, and would that \u8220\'20\'1Cempty seat\u8221\'20\'1D trick fly with legislative or executive ethics disclosures? (Hint: no.) And how about with the Financial Disclosure Committee? (Right, you didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask.) This just keeps getting worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOh, and would that \u8220\'20\'1Cempty seat\u8221\'20\'1D trick fly with legislative or executive ethics disclosures? (Hint: no.) And how about with the Financial Disclosure Committee? (Right, you didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask.)\par \par \uc2 This just keeps getting worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sheldon Whitehouse (@SenWhitehouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1671323063374282753?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The unidentified bail guarantors of George Santos will be revealed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that federal judge Joanna Seybert announced that the two people who guaranteed bail for the Republican representative will have their names publicly revealed.\par \par \uc2 Seybert, who said the names will be publicized on Thursday at 12pm ET, rejected \uc2 Santos\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims that the public disclosure could threaten the individuals\u8217\'20\'19 safety.\par \par \uc2 Santos, who has pled not guilty to a 13-count indictment accusing him of fraud, money laundering and theft of public funds, has suggested that his guarantors are family members.\par \par \uc2 For more details, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/21/george-santos-bail-guarantors-revealed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Santos mystery bail guarantors to be revealed on Thursday}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  will raise pro-choice \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  billboards across key voting states as the country gears up for the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The billboard campaign will begin on Thursday in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Times Square and will also feature in Atlanta, Phoenix, Milwaukee, Tallahassee, and Raleigh, \uc2 CBS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/dnc-abortion-rights-billboards-anniversary-roe-v-wade-struck-down/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 The billboards will highlight the contrast between Democrats and Republicans over their efforts at protecting and banning abortions, a DNC official told \uc2 CBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With the one-year anniversary of Roe vs Wade\u8217\'20\'19s overturn coming on Saturday, the DNC will also run social media campaigns this week on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , as well as CTV ads across Wisconsin, North Carolina, Florida, Georgia and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CBS\uc2 , the DNC also plans to deploy officials and surrogates across multiple states to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the country this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Christine Arena, a former public relations executive at the firm Edelman who now works in social impact film-making, testified second.\par \par \uc2 She drew comparisons between the fossil fuel industry\u8217\'20\'19s decades-long misinformation campaign and that helmed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/14/congress-hearing-oil-exxon-bp-shell-chevron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tobacco industry}}}\uc2  to cover up the harms of smoking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust like the tobacco executives before them, [fossil fuel executives] characterize peer-reviewed science and investigative journalism that illustrates the extent of their deceptions as biased or inconclusive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Arena, who was invited to testify by committee chair Sheldon Whitehouse.\par \par \uc2 Richard Painter, a professor of corporate law at University of Minnesota Law School who was the chief White House ethics lawyer in the \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration, later testified that he is a political independent, and that Americans should get on board with the push to end climate misinformation no matter where they fall on the political spectrum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a partisan issue. This is not about being a Democrat or Republican, or an independent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Painter, who was also invited by Whitehouse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about caring, and doing something about a grave threat to the human race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Painter was followed by two witnesses invited by Republican Senators. The first was Dr Roger Pielke Jr, professor of environmental studies \uc2 University of Colorado Boulder\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said in 2015, he testified in Congress about climate science, and in response, a member of Congress suggested that he may have been the recipient of undisclosed funding from fossil fuel companies.\par \par \uc2 His university investigated him and found the accusations were not true, he said.\u8220\'20\'1CHowever, the very public accusation was enough to derail my work and upset my career in ways that continue today,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pielke said he believes climate change is real, human-caused and dangerous, but that the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 concerns are overblown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne important role of us experts is to call things as we see them,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes research results are inconvenient or uncomfortable to certain interests, and that includes political interest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott Walker, president of conservative non-profit organization Capital Research Center who also served in the \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration as special assistant to the president for domestic policy, claimed that the subject of the hearing \u8211\'20\'13 dark money \u8211\'20\'13 is not a major problem in American politics.\par \par \uc2 Further, he insisted, the political left takes more money than the right.\par \par \uc2 To say that a group uses dark money is like saying the group uses telephones. It\u8217\'20\'19s a universal technology,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate budget committee begins hearing on fossil fuel industry and climate change\par \par \uc2 Senate budget committee chair Sheldon Whitehouse kicked off Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here today because fossil fuel funded climate disinformation and obstruction is directly causing systemic financial risks to the economy and to the federal budget,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He explained the well-documented misinformation campaign that fossil fuel companies and their allies have waged on the American public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeginning as early as the 1950s, industry scientists became aware of climate change, measuring and predicting it decades before it became a public issue,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey knew their products were responsible for it\u8230\'20\'26 but industry management and CEOs spent decades promoting climate misinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ranking member Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , a Republican from Iowa, pushed back on the need for such a hearing, saying it constituted a \u8220\'20\'1Cmissed opportunity to work together on a responsible budget\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats have claimed that climate change will cause catastrophic economic collapse due to devastating natural disasters. They have also attributed a Republican rejection of extreme climate policy to win alleged fossil fuel disinformation conspiracy to defraud the public,\u8221\'20\'1D said Grassley.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis premise either insults the integrity or the intelligence of Republican legislators that diligently serve their constituents, as well as our constituents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The first witness to testify was Harvard history of science professor Naomi Oreskes, who has written several books on oil industry misinformation and who was invited by committee chair Whitehouse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClimate change is a market failure, and market failures require government action to address,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Fossil fuel companies\u8217\'20\'19 and their front groups\u8217\'20\'19 concerted efforts to disrupt climate policies have come at great expense to America, including not only financial costs, but also human suffering and lives lost, she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  joins other conservative justices in facing ethics questions for not disclosing multiple gifts he received from billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In April, conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  came under fire from watchdogs and Democratic lawmakers after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow?utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=TwitterThread"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2  revealed that he had accepted luxury trips from Harlan Crow, a Republican real estate developer and megadonor.\par \par \uc2 In its investigation, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  found that \uc2 Crow\uc2  has donated over $10m in publicly disclosed political contributions. He has also donated to groups that conceal their donors and once said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t disclose what I\u8217\'20\'19m not required to disclose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Recent reports also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/neil-gorsuch-us-supreme-court-property-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  that conservative justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  reportedly failed to disclose the buyer of a $1.8m Colorado property which he co-owned in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The buyer was eventually revealed by Politico to be a chief executive of \uc2 Greenberg Traurig\uc2 , one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest law firms which has made multiple appearances in front of the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The disclosure failures from multiple conservative justices have prompted widespread criticism among Democrats, who have since been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/23/supreme-court-justices-regulation-senate-democrats-clarence-thomas-john-roberts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/28/supreme-court-sheldon-whitehouse-ethics-reform"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ethics reforms}}}\uc2  across the court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not going to be easy,\u8221\'20\'1D Rhode Island\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse told NBC in May. \u8220\'20\'1CThe work that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing on ethics in the court ought to be easy. And yet it\u8217\'20\'19s not. It\u8217\'20\'19s partisan also.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo I think that the first step is going to be for the judicial conference, the other judges, to put some constraints around the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s behavior and treat the supreme court the way all other federal judges are treated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Democratic representative \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2  has announced her bid to run for senator.\par \par \uc2 In a campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=irgGiG9JXhM&ab_channel=LisaBluntRochesterforSenate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  released on Wednesday, Rochester said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been the greatest honor of my life to represent Delaware, to protect our seniors, our environment, our small businesses and women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights. But we\u8217\'20\'19ve got so much more to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rochester went on to talk about the January 6, 2021 Capitol Hill riots, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople ask me if January 6 was my worst day. It was but it was also one of my proudest moments. Because we walked back in that House chamber and we completed our work. The forces of fear did not win and democracy prevailed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Currently, the Delaware Senate seat is occupied by Democratic senator \uc2 Thomas Carper\uc2 , who announced last month that he will not seek re-election after 2025.\par \par \uc2 Carper has indicated his support for Rochester, who used to intern for him when he served in the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In May, Carper announced his endorsement for Rochester, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe love Lisa, and I spoke with her this morning and I said you\u8217\'20\'19ve been patiently waiting for me to get out the way, and I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna get out of the way, and I hope you run, and I hope you will let me support you and support you in that mission,\u8221\'20\'1D CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/06/21/politics/lisa-blunt-rochester-senate-delaware/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate budget committee will hold a hearing on Wednesday morning, scrutinizing the role of oil and gas-linked \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money\u8221\'20\'1D in delaying climate action \u8211\'20\'13 and tearing through local and federal budgets.\par \par \uc2 The fossil fuel sector has spent billions on a decades-long campaign to sow doubt about climate science and policies, despite its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jan/12/exxon-climate-change-global-warming-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 own findings}}}\uc2  from as early as the 1950s that emissions from oil and gas warm the planet. Some of that funding has been anonymized through trade associations and other groups, research {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insideclimatenews.org/news/03022023/dark-money-is-fueling-climate-denial-and-delaying-action-watchdogs-warn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The hearing will be led by Rhode Island senator Sheldon Whitehouse, who chairs the committee and who has given {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cckyb6dJOEo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 300 speeches}}}\uc2  about the climate crisis on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs chairman of the budget committee, I am shining a light on the massive, well-documented economic risks of climate change,\u8221\'20\'1D said Whitehouse. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are risks that have the potential to cascade across our entire economy and trigger widespread financial hardship and calamity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It will feature five witnesses: Harvard history of science professor Naomi Oreskes, who has long studied climate misinformation; Christine Arena, former public relations executive at the firm Edelman who now works in social impact filmmaking; Richard Painter, a professor of corporate law at University of Minnesota Law School who was the chief White House ethics lawyer in the \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration; Dr Roger Pielke Jr, professor of environmental studies \uc2 University of Colorado Boulder\uc2 ; and Scott Walker, president of conservative non-profit organization Capital Research Center who also served in the \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  administration as special assistant to the president for domestic policy.\par \par \uc2 The hearing follows one launched by Democrats in 2021 on what was then called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/business/2022/dec/09/oil-gas-companies-fossil-fuel-industry-house-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House oversight and reform committee}}}\uc2 , which focused on big oil\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to mislead the public about the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kyle Herrig, the president of the watchdog Accountable.US, calls out \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  and \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  in a statement this morning about \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blockbuster story}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and the billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Herrig said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs the supreme court corruption crisis grows with yet another apparent violation of the court\u8217\'20\'19s bare minimum ethics code, it\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  is right in the middle. He\u8217\'20\'19s the corrupting influence responsible for the rot .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Leo is a rightwing activist who has done much to shape conservative dominance of federal courts including the supreme court, and who recently received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/22/us/politics/republican-dark-money.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.6bn}}}\uc2  to further his work. He accompanied Alito and Singer to Alaska on the fishing trip at the heart of the \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report.\par \par \uc2 Leo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ProPublica}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CNo objective and well-informed observer of the judiciary honestly could believe that they decide cases in order to cull favour with friends, or in return for a free plane seat or fishing trip.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Herrig continued: \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as Chief Justice Roberts continues to dodge responsibility by refusing to take action, public trust in our court will continue to plummet. We need reform now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Roberts has rebuffed calls to testify in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 over previous \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reports about \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , another hardline rightwing justice, and his relationship with another rightwing billionaire, Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 As quoted in the \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  story, \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , the Illinois Democrat who chairs the Senate judiciary committee, has recently said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t tolerate this [Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s behaviour] from a city council member or an alderman. And yet the supreme court won\u8217\'20\'19t even acknowledge it\u8217\'20\'19s a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-undisclosed-gifts-billionaire-paul-singer-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Samuel Alito did not declare gifts from billionaire with case before US supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alito published a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/propublica-misleads-its-readers-alito-gifts-disclosure-alaska-singer-23b51eda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal op-ed}}}\uc2  in response to \uc2 Pro Publica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reporting, but declined to answer direct questions from \uc2 Pro Publica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the op-ed published hours before \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report, Alito said that he did not know Singer was connected to cases heard before the court.\par \par \uc2 Alito also claimed to have spoken to Singer \u8220\'20\'1Con no more than a handful of occasions\u8221\'20\'1D, including during the aforementioned fishing trip.\par \par \uc2 From the Wall Street Journal:\par \par \uc2 On no occasion have we discussed the activities of his businesses, and we have never talked about any case or issue before the Court\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It was and is my judgment that these facts would not cause a reasonable and unbiased person to doubt my ability to decide the matters in question impartially\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26When I reviewed the cases in question to determine whether I was required to recuse, I was not aware and had no good reason to be aware that Mr. Singer had an interest in any party\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 But experts have pushed back against Alito\u8217\'20\'19s defenses, telling \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that they could not recall an instance of a justice ruling on a case after receiving a gift from a donor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you were good friends, what were you doing ruling on his case?\u8221\'20\'1D said Charles Geyh, an \uc2 Indiana University\uc2  law professor and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bookstore.gpo.gov/products/judicial-disqualification-analysis-federal-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expert on recusals}}}\uc2  to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if you weren\u8217\'20\'19t good friends, what were you doing accepting this?\u8221\'20\'1D said Geyh, referring to the flight on the private jet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alito is facing ethics questions related to a 2008 fishing trip the supreme court justice took with Republican billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 , first reported by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 On 8 July 2008, Alito flew on Singer\u8217\'20\'19s private jet to Alaska, where the pair stayed at King Salmon Lodge, a fishing resort that costs more than $1,000 a day.\par \par \uc2 The private plane to Alaska would have cost Alito more than $100,000 if he had chartered it himself, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 In the years after the trip, Singer\u8217\'20\'19s hedge fund was involved in cases presented before the court at least 10 times. In 2014, the court resolved a key question stemming from a decades-long battle between Singer\u8217\'20\'19s hedge fund and Argentina. Alito voted in Singer\u8217\'20\'19s favor, in a 7-1 majority.\par \par \uc2 The hedge fund ultimately received $2.4bn.\par \par \uc2 enltrSupreme Court Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  took a luxury fishing trip to Alaska with billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 , whose hedge fund then had repeated business before \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  over the years that followed.\par \par \uc2 Alito never disclosed the trip or recused himself from Singer's cases. (THREAD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mVWEInOUfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mVWEInOUfa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  (@propublica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/propublica/status/1671504541076815876?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alito facing questions over undeclared gifts from billionaire with case before supreme court\par \par \uc2 Good morning,\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/21/samuel-alito-undisclosed-gifts-billionaire-paul-singer-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing questions}}}\uc2  for not declaring several gifts received from conservative billionaire \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 , and for not recusing himself when Singer had cases presented before the court.\par \par \uc2 The latest report questioning the ethics of supreme court justices came from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2 , which recently published several articles on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/series/supreme-court-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relationship}}}\uc2  between justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and Republican billionaire Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report published on Tuesday night, Alito accepted a seat on a private plane owned by Singer and flew to Alaska for a luxury fishing trip at the King Salmon Lodge, which costs $1,000 a night.\par \par \uc2 Abbe Smith, a Georgetown law professor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/samuel-alito-luxury-fishing-trip-paul-singer-scotus-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told ProPublica}}}\uc2  Alito should have recused himself because of the gift from Singer.\par \par \uc2 If she were representing a client in such a case and \u8220\'20\'1Cfound out [about the gift] after the fact\u8221\'20\'1D, Smith said, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d be outraged on behalf of my client. And, frankly, I\u8217\'20\'19d be outraged on behalf of the legal system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alito did not respond to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s questions for the piece. Instead, the justice published a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/propublica-misleads-its-readers-alito-gifts-disclosure-alaska-singer-23b51eda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal op-ed}}}\uc2  about the trip, several hours before the \uc2 Propublica\uc2  piece published.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , at the White House on Wednesday evening. Several democrats are calling on Biden to question Modi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com./world/biden-will-not-lecture-modi-human-rights-white-house-says-2023-06-21/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on his human rights\u8217\'20\'19 record}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230621ej6l001s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
