\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Well-funded Christian group behind US effort to roll back LGBTQ+ rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt in New York \par \uc2 1,348 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2023\par 10:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Advocacy groups condemn \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  as \u8216\'20\'18a danger to every American who values their freedoms\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 With the US besieged by a rightwing culture war campaign that aims to strip away rights from LGBTQ+ people and others, blame tends to be focused on Republican politicians and conservative media figures.\par \par \uc2 But lurking behind efforts to roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, to demonize trans people, and to peel back the protections afforded to gay and queer Americans is a shadowy, well-funded rightwing legal organization, experts say.\par \par \uc2 Since it was formed in 1994, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  has been at the center of a nationwide effort to limit the rights of women and LGBTQ+ people, all in the name of Christianity. \uc2 The Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2  has termed it an \u8220\'20\'1Canti-LGBTQ hate group\u8221\'20\'1D that has extended its tentacles into nearly every area of the culture wars.\par \par \uc2 In the process, it has won the ear of some of the most influential people in the US, and become \u8220\'20\'1Ca danger to every American who values their freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Glaad, the LGBTQ+ advocacy organization.\par \par \uc2 Through \u8220\'20\'1Cmodel legislation\u8221\'20\'1D and lawsuits filed across the country, \uc2 ADF\uc2  aims to overturn same-sex marriage, enact a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and strip away the already minimal rights that trans people are afforded in the US.\par \par \uc2 Under the Trump administration, the group found its way into the highest echelons of power, advising Jeff Sessions, the then attorney general, before he announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/press-release/file/1001891/download?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping guidance}}}\uc2  to protect \u8220\'20\'1Creligious liberty\u8221\'20\'1D which chipped away at LGBTQ+ protections.\par \par \uc2 The organization counts among its sometime associates \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , the supreme court justice who the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/coney-barrett-christian-law-fellowship-blackstone/2020/09/27/7ae41892-fdc5-11ea-b555-4d71a9254f4b_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  spoke five times at an \uc2 ADF\uc2  training program established to push a \u8220\'20\'1Cdistinctly Christian worldview in every area of law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ADF\uc2  is engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Ca very strong campaign to put a certain type of religious view at the center of American life\u8221\'20\'1D, said Rabia Muqaddam, senior staff attorney at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The \uc2 ADF\uc2  campaign] extends to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it extends to LGBTQ folks, to immigration, to what kind of religion we think is America, what kind of people we think are American,\u8221\'20\'1D Muqaddam said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s as dramatic as that. I think we are in a fight to preserve democracy and preserve America as a place where we do tolerate and encourage and empower everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ADF\uc2  was founded in 1994 by a group of \u8220\'20\'1Cleaders in the Christian community\u8221\'20\'1D, according to its website. Among those leaders was James Dobson, the founder of the anti-LGBTQ+ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/press-releases/10-things-you-should-know-about-focus-on-the-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Focus on the Family}}}\uc2  organization who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.christianpost.com/news/james-dobson-connecticut-shooting-a-result-of-god-allowing-judgment-to-fall-on-america-newtown-ct-sandy-hook.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the 2012 Sandy Hook mass shooting, in which 20 children and six adults were killed, was a \u8220\'20\'1Cjudgment\u8221\'20\'1D from God because of declining church numbers.\par \par \uc2 Its leaders remain involved in niche interpretations of Christianity. \uc2 Kristen Waggoner\uc2 , the \uc2 ADF\uc2  chief executive, also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.ag.org/News/Kristen-Waggoner-Named-Legal-Counsel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serves as legal counsel}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ag.org/Beliefs/Our-Core-Doctrines/Divine-Healing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Assemblies of God}}}\uc2 , a church which encourages worshippers to speak in tongues and believes in \u8220\'20\'1Cdivine healing\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the power of prayer \u8211\'20\'13 as a medical tool.\par \par \uc2 Over the past two decades, \uc2 ADF\uc2  has been a main driver in dozens of pieces of rightwing legislation and lawsuits.\par \par \uc2 The organization is currently behind the lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/cases/303-creative-inc-v-elenis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 303 Creative, Inc v Elenis}}}\uc2 , which the supreme court is expected to decide this month, and which could chip away at LGBTQ+ rights. It\u8217\'20\'19s a case that is classic \uc2 ADF\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a seemingly manufactured issue which the group has managed to chase all the way through the American legal system.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiff, 303 Creative, is a website design company. 303 Creative has never made wedding websites, but its owner, Lorie Smith, claims her first amendment rights are being impinged because, if she were to start making wedding websites, she would not want to make them for same-sex couples \u8211\'20\'13 which would violate Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s anti-discrimination laws.\par \par \uc2 Another \uc2 ADF\uc2  obsession is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was involved, Muqaddam said, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/alliance-defending-freedom-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crafting a 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in Mississippi \u8211\'20\'13 which prompted a legal case that found its way to the supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 eventually resulting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , being overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  has been instrumental in the dismantling of Roe and the ongoing efforts to eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Muqaddam said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey enacted a law that they knew was unconstitutional, they enacted it for the purpose of generating case after case after case to push it out to the supreme court until they found a court that was sympathetic to their argument,\u8221\'20\'1D Muqaddam said.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what is happening in the LGBTQ context as well. Their goal is to limit individual rights as much as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=ppc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2  shows the breadth of its involvement in rightwing culture wars. The organization touts its work opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on opposing same-sex marriage and opposing trans rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe advocate for laws and precedents that promote human flourishing by recognizing the important differences between men and women and honoring God\u8217\'20\'19s design for marriage between one man and one woman,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s website reads.\par \par \uc2 But Emerson Hodges, a research analyst at the \uc2 SPLC\uc2 , said what \uc2 ADF\uc2  is really doing is attempting to \u8220\'20\'1Cundo LGBTQ social and legislative progress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey go under the guise of religious liberty, and religious freedom. What that means, though, is this religious liberty to discriminate and the religious freedom to invalidate LGBTQ individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D Hodges said.\par \par \uc2 Worryingly, there are signs that \uc2 ADF\uc2 , and other groups like it, are growing in influence. As Republican politicians and rightwing media fan the flames of an extremist culture war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-news/groups-opposed-gay-rights-rake-millions-states-debate-anti-lgbtq-bills-rcna21016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC reported}}}\uc2  that donations to \uc2 ADF\uc2 , which is a registered non-profit, more than doubled from 2011 to 2021.\par \par \uc2 As it has grown in influence, \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmodel legislation\u8221\'20\'1D has found its way into state legislatures across the country, as the group attempts to strip away LGBTQ+ rights, and the rights of trans people in particular.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve worked to ban the right to choose, and are in cahoots with other extremist groups to oppress marginalized people\par \par \uc2 Glaad\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust about every anti-LGBT legislation that you\u8217\'20\'19ve seen probably in the past decade was probably copied or paraphrased off of a model legislation built by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hodges said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey provide legal advocacy support, litigation and policy models for government officials.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An article on \uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s website states that it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cbiblical truth\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cmen and women are physically different\u8221\'20\'1D, and the organization has duly worked to prevent trans people taking part in women\u8217\'20\'19s sports.\par \par \uc2 The group sued a school district in Minnesota in 2016, and in 2021 a judge in Connecticut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/sports-e881f5a74c82b931650142dee0e59fd3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  an \uc2 ADF\uc2  lawsuit which sought to prevent transgender athletes competing in high school sports. The same year, \uc2 ADF{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/education/loudoun-tanner-cross-lawsuit-transgender-students/2021/11/15/49520ce8-464a-11ec-95dc-5f2a96e00fa3_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  brought by a teacher in Virginia who had said he would not use a transgender child\u8217\'20\'19s preferred pronouns because that would amount to \u8220\'20\'1Csinning against our God\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In April, \uc2 ADF\uc2 , which did not respond to a Guardian request for comment, filed in Oregon on behalf of a Christian woman who wanted to foster children, but said she would not agree to \u8220\'20\'1Crespect, accept, and support \u8230\'20\'26 the sexual orientation, gender identity, [and] gender expression\u8221\'20\'1D of a child placed with her, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesmanjournal.com/story/news/local/2023/04/05/woman-hoping-to-adopt-foster-children-sues-oregon-lgbtq-religion-alliance-defending-freedom/70080142007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Statesman Journal reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[\uc2 ADF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s] obsession with targeting LGBTQ people is unhinged and drastically out of touch with supermajorities of Americans who support LGBTQ people and laws to protect us from discrimination,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Sarah Kate Ellis\uc2 , the president and chief executive of Glaad.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone should understand the truth: the \uc2 ADF\uc2  is simply an anti-LGBTQ group trying to abuse levers of government to push discrimination and keep their warped sense of control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve also worked to ban the right to choose, and are in cahoots with other extremist groups to oppress marginalized people. \uc2 ADF\uc2  is a danger to every American who values their freedoms \u8211\'20\'13 to be ourselves, live freely, and be welcome to contribute and to succeed in every area of society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230619ej6j001h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
