\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US rightwing group planned $6m for anti-trans messaging in 2022 midterms\b0\par\par\uc2 Robin Buller \par \uc2 1,623 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2023\par 06:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Voice turned resources to fighting trans rights in 10 key swing states, documents reveal\par \par \uc2 In the months leading up to the 2022 US midterm elections, hundreds of thousands of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  users in swing states were targeted with advertisements asking them to sign the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights \u8211\'20\'13 a relatively innocuous-sounding initiative presented as a crusade for women\u8217\'20\'19s empowerment. \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/ads/library/?id=1048886899332712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Real Fight For Women}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, read one version featuring a woman looking down at a cityscape and flexing her biceps. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what a woman is,\u8221\'20\'1D proclaimed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/ads/library/?id=371041918567122"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another}}}\uc2 , its text hovering over a closeup of the Statue of Liberty.\par \par \uc2 But the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights is a weapon in a war against gender equity being waged by a conservative non-profit women\u8217\'20\'19s group. Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Voice, or IWV, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iwv.org/issue/equality-for-women/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lobbies against the equal rights amendment}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iwv.org/issue/education/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  criticizes public school curriculum}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iwv.org/issue/earned-leave-for-new-parents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposes government-funded parental leave}}}\uc2 . Recently, they have turned their resources to fighting transgender rights. And, according to documents shared with the Guardian by watchdog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truenorthresearch.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 True North Research}}}\uc2 , IWV budgeted nearly $6m to promote anti-trans messaging in 10 swing states in advance of last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not be fooled by their name,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alyssa Bowen, senior researcher and managing editor at True North. \u8220\'20\'1CThis group is a tool of the right to advance an extremist agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Facebook\uc2  users follow a link to sign the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights, they are taken to a website that promotes traditional gender roles and characterizes transgender people as a threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s success and safety. The page includes a copy of the bill itself, which insists \u8220\'20\'1Cmales and females possess unique and immutable biological differences\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological differences \u8230\'20\'26 warrant the creation of separate social, educational, athletic, or other spaces in order to ensure safety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 To researchers and policy experts, these bullet points are thinly veiled attempts to stoke anti-LGBTQ+ fears and erase legal protections for transgender people. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights does nothing for women,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gillian Branstetter of \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAll they do is seek to target trans people. They\u8217\'20\'19re trying not only to suggest that trans people are a threat to women, but that they are the only threat to women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The documents show this messaging has significant fiscal backing. The \u8220\'20\'1CWomen\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights Proposal\u8221\'20\'1D indicates that in order to promote women\u8217\'20\'19s rights as a midterm issue in states with \u8220\'20\'1Ctossups or tight races\u8221\'20\'1D, as much as $575,000 per state was allotted for marketing in Arizona, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Ohio, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, though the documents do not show how much of this total was actually spent. When asked to confirm, Heather R Higgins, IWV\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, said they \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t discuss specifics with the media on non-reportable education and advocacy expenses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Another document uncovered by True North \u8211\'20\'13 authored by the Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center, a project of IWV\u8217\'20\'19s sister organization, the Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Forum \u8211\'20\'13 states that focusing on issues other than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  separates the Independent Women brand from other conservative women\u8217\'20\'19s groups, enabling it to more successfully \u8220\'20\'1Cconvince moderates\u8221\'20\'1D to support initiatives like abolishing the equal rights amendment by voting Republican.\par \par \uc2 That disclosure adds important context to IWV promotional materials rolled out in advance of the midterms that challenge their claims to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  neutrality. These include a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factsaboutabortionnow.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website for \u8220\'20\'1C\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  facts\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that downplays the fall of Roe, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/10/13/abortion-midterms-independent-womens-voice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media ads}}}\uc2  that encourage voters to worry about crime and inflation rather than reproductive rights. Another difficulty is their association with Erin Hawley, an attorney who is fighting to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/03/erin-josh-hawley-abortion-medication-texas-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bar access to medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and worked for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msmagazine.com/2023/02/06/fda-abortion-pills/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit that overturned Roe}}}\uc2 . Hawley was formerly an Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iwf.org/people/erin-hawley/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fellow}}}\uc2 . She is also the wife of Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , who has been accused of transphobia and has a track record of supporting anti-choice legislation.\par \par \uc2 IWV denies any intention to draw eyes away from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no connection whatsoever between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and WBOR,\u8221\'20\'1D said Higgins. \u8220\'20\'1CFar from being a distraction, supporting WBOR is the first test of whether anyone from across the political spectrum is serious about whether they stand with women,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, claiming the bill has bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 True North argues that IWV\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iwv.org/issue/title-ix-womens-sports/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 present trans rights as threatening to cis women}}}\uc2  could be part of a through-line strategy to distract voters from the fallout of last summer\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling against the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Policy experts are not surprised. \u8220\'20\'1CGOP candidates really suffered from headlines about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelly Baden, vice-president for public policy at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which tracks policies related to sexual and reproductive health. \u8220\'20\'1CIt makes absolute sense that they would rather talk about a 12-year-old being on puberty blockers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The connection between anti-trans and anti-choice initiatives, she says, runs deeper than electoral strategy; preventing women from getting abortions and blocking people from accessing gender-affirming care are attacks on bodily autonomy. \u8220\'20\'1CThe messaging strategy for both is that [the bans] have to do with our own health and protection. But what they\u8217\'20\'19re saying is that they know better than a family or a physician,\u8221\'20\'1D said Baden.\par \par \uc2 Baden also sees parallels in the \u8220\'20\'1Cshared tactics\u8221\'20\'1D of anti-trans and anti-choice legislative methods. In both cases, \u8220\'20\'1Cmodel bills are pushed into the hands of state legislators\u8221\'20\'1D from outside groups, she explained. Organizations like the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2  and \uc2 Americans United for Life\uc2 , for instance, are credited with having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/07/08/1110299496/trigger-laws-13-states-two-groups-laid-groundwork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drafted many of the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  trigger bans}}}\uc2  that went into law shortly after Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 As of publication, IWV\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/05/03/1172821119/kansas-montana-tennessee-narrowly-define-sex-female-male-transgender-intersex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  in Kansas and Tennessee, and Montana has ratified a similar oppressive bill that defines \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological gender\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Branstetter says another commonality is the perpetuation of rigid traditional gender norms, a Republican priority, especially among members of the religious right. \u8220\'20\'1CAnti-trans and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws both define women by their reproductive functions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that the issues are not connected is fantastical.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The effectiveness of the messaging is hard to gauge. The 2022 midterms were a largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/08/republicans-midterm-election-poor-preformance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsuccessful election cycle}}}\uc2  for Republicans, who squandered key races and failed to win the Senate. That performance has been attributed by many \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/04/republican-lawmakers-reject-abortion-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  including Republicans}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/abortion-midterm-elections-republicans-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  losing the votes of women and young people}}}\uc2  who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The chair of the New Hampshire Democratic party, \uc2 Ray Buckley\uc2 , doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think swing voters in his state are so easily distracted. \u8220\'20\'1COur independent women are more progressive than that,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Last fall, far-right New Hampshire Republican candidate Karoline Leavitt sent out mailers spotlighting her crusade against trans athletes in women\u8217\'20\'19s sports. She lost to Democrat \uc2 Chris Pappas\uc2  by more than seven points. \u8220\'20\'1CIf that was their goal in New Hampshire, they failed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Buckley.\par \par \uc2 In Colorado, former Trump aide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coloradosun.com/2022/10/25/colorado-latino-voter-targeted-spanish-language-ads/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephen Miller\u8217\'20\'19s political non-profit sent anti-transgender brochures to Latino voters}}}\uc2 . Democratic strategists there believe such messaging pushed voters away. \u8220\'20\'1CI think they\u8217\'20\'19re just weirding people out,\u8221\'20\'1D said the state party chair, Shad Murib.\par \par \uc2 Both New Hampshire and Colorado were targeted states in IWV\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights proposal. Looking to 2024, Buckley and Murib expect to see more anti-transgender vitriol, but doubt it will win over moderates and independents. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they want to distract from [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ], there are plenty of things we can talk about, but they picked another wedge issue, and Colorado is just not going to bite,\u8221\'20\'1D said Murib, pointing to voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about employment, drought and housing.\par \par \uc2 Others aren\u8217\'20\'19t so sure. Bowen emphasizes the outsized influence that scare tactics can have on voters. \u8220\'20\'1CThe GOP is manufacturing fear of the LGBTQ+ community to try to drive fleeing moderates back to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s party to aid the 2024 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Higgins confirmed that \u8220\'20\'1Cadvancing WBOR remains a top priority for Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Voice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Baden believes tactics to block access to both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-affirming care will intensify as the next election cycle approaches, with young people as a key messaging strategy. She points to Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s recently enacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/idaho-abortion-trafficking-law-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel ban for minors seeking abortions out of state}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey start with minors because they think they have both an easier messaging win and easier legal avenues,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19ll see more of those kinds of bills next year, but \u8230\'20\'26 that is just a testing ground for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Branstetter, too, sees restrictions for young people as the beginning of a larger escalation. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re dropping the pretense that this was about young people,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re probably stepping into a legislative session and an election where outright bans on gender transitions for anyone of any age are on the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For her, that prospect is yet another reason to see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and transgender rights as two sides of the same coin. Both impact historically marginalized groups, both employ technologies that help people break free of gender norms, and both save lives. Said Branstetter, \u8220\'20\'1CTheir goal is to make people so scared of trans freedom that you\u8217\'20\'19ll sacrifice your own \u8230\'20\'26 [but] trans rights are women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  contacted Republican party leadership in each of the\par \par \uc2 10 states identified in the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Bill of Rights Proposal, but received no response.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 17 June 2023. A previous version stated that Erin Hawley was an Independent Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center fellow, which is no longer the case.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230617ej6h0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
