\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Wednesday briefing: The tragic case shining a light on the UK\u8217\'20\'19s archaic  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws\b0\par\par\uc2 Esther Addley \par \uc2 2,335 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2023\par 06:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: A woman has been jailed for two years for using \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills after the legal limit, renewing fury about rules many believe are an injusticeSign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 One in three women in the UK will have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the time they are 45 years old \u8211\'20\'13 and, with a few important caveats, accessing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a pregnancy at less than the 24-week limit is usually relatively straightforward.\par \par \uc2 So it comes as a surprise to many, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bpas.org/abortion-care/considering-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 British Pregnancy Advisory Service (BPAS)}}}\uc2 , that in most of Britain the procedure is still governed by a 160-year-old law that declares \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime, and another, passed almost 60 years ago, that outlines the specific exceptions in which it can be allowed.\par \par \uc2 The distressing story this week of a woman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/12/woman-in-uk-jailed-for-28-months-over-taking-abortion-pills-after-legal-time-limit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jailed for more than two years}}}\uc2  for lying to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, ending her pregnancy after the legal limit, has highlighted just how high the stakes can be.\par \par \uc2 Campaigners and politicians of all parties expressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/12/woman-in-uk-jailed-for-28-months-over-taking-abortion-pills-after-legal-time-limit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shock and outrage}}}\uc2  at the sentence, pointing out that the case occurred in the early months of the pandemic, when face to face services were unavailable. They argue that there was no public interest in jailing the woman, who has three children, one with special needs, and that the sentence could also deter others from seeking help. But her case has also cast light on the archaic laws that govern \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the UK \u8211\'20\'13 and the urgent need, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/13/call-overhaul-out-of-date-uk-abortion-laws-woman-jailed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigners believe}}}\uc2 , to reform them.\par \par \uc2 With the number of people being investigated by police for procuring abortions having risen over the past three years, I spoke to Katherine O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, associate director of \uc2 BPAS\uc2 , about why \u8211\'20\'13 and what she believes needs to change. More on that after the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\par \par \uc2 | The former US president has pleaded not guilty to all counts related to his alleged mishandling of classified documents as he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/13/donald-trump-hearing-court-cameras-judge-arraignment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formally arraigned in Miami, Florida,}}}\uc2  becoming the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/13/trump-arraignment-not-guilty-charges-mar-a-lago-documents-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first former US president to face federal criminal charges}}}\uc2 . Later at his golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey, Trump railed against his prosecution and made baseless claims that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was behind it.\par \par \uc2 Nottingham\par \par \uc2 | Among the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/jun/13/its-really-scary-two-students-among-those-killed-in-nottingham-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victims of the stabbing attacks}}}\uc2  in the early hours of Tuesday morning were two 19-year-old students named locally as Barnaby Webber and Grace Kumar. A third victim, in his 50s, has yet to be named. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2023/jun/13/nottingham-in-shock-after-three-die-in-early-morning-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A 31-year-old man has been arrested on suspicion of murder.}}}\uc2  Counter-terror police were helping officers with their investigation but Nottinghamshire police insisted they were keeping an \u8220\'20\'1Copen mind\u8221\'20\'1D about the motive.\par \par \uc2 House of Lords\par \par \uc2 | Rami Ranger, a prominent Conservative peer and donor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2023/jun/13/tory-peer-undermined-and-humiliated-journalist-finds-lords-commissioner-rami-ranger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bullied and harassed a female journalist}}}\uc2  after she publicly criticised him and an organisation he runs, a committee has ruled. Ranger has apologised and promised to attend a behavioural course.\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 | Three families seeking asylum in the UK {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/jun/13/home-office-plans-to-ditch-housing-protections-for-asylum-seekers-face-legal-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have launched a legal challenge}}}\uc2  against new Home Office rules to ditch basic housing protections for tens of thousands in this group.\par \par \uc2 Romania\par \par \uc2 | Prosecutors in Romania say they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2023/jun/13/andrew-tate-romanian-authorities-change-human-trafficking-charge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have changed the human trafficking charge against Andrew Tate}}}\uc2  to a more serious one. Tate, his brother Tristan and two other suspects are now being investigated for human trafficking in continued form, reportedly a more serious crime than separate counts of trafficking.\par \par \uc2 In depth: \u8216\'20\'18What we\u8217\'20\'19re calling for is for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be treated in the same way as any other healthcare procedure\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Abortions after 24 weeks are rare in Britain, and the case of the woman jailed for illegally procuring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills is a particularly tragic one, as even the trial judge acknowledged.\par \par \uc2 Estranged from the father of her children and pregnant by another man, she was forced by the pandemic to move back in with her former partner and \u8220\'20\'1Cin emotional turmoil\u8221\'20\'1D as she tried to conceal the pregnancy. She was between 32 and 34 weeks pregnant when she induced the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Her actions in lying to obtain tablets under the hurriedly introduced \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/30/mps-vote-to-continue-abortion-pills-by-post-scheme-in-england"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pills by post}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D scheme may have been born out of desperation, but they were also expressly criminal under UK law. Though she now felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvery deep and genuine remorse\u8221\'20\'1D and was haunted by flashbacks of her dead child\u8217\'20\'19s face, the judge said, \u8220\'20\'1Cin my view your culpability was high\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 hence the harshness of her sentence.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 What does the law say at present?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is, healthcare in this area can\u8217\'20\'19t advance because it\u8217\'20\'19s still a criminal offence governed by legislation passed in 1967,\u8221\'20\'1D Katherine O\u8217\'20\'19Brien tells me. No other medical procedure is carried out according to what MPs believed 60 years ago \u8211\'20\'13 before \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills were even invented \u8211\'20\'13 she points out. \u8220\'20\'1CWe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t accept that in any other area of healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In England, Wales and Scotland, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bpas.org/get-involved/campaigns/briefings/abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is outlawed}}}\uc2  under the Offences against the Person Act 1861, and this is the legislation under which the woman was prosecuted. Crucially, while the 1967 \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act outlines circumstances in which it can be allowed \u8211\'20\'13 and gives what \uc2 BPAS\uc2  calls \u8220\'20\'1Cbroad discretion\u8221\'20\'1D on how it is interpreted \u8211\'20\'13 it does not overturn the earlier legislation, so any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside its terms carries a potential life sentence.\par \par \uc2 The 1967 law allows an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before 24 weeks if the pregnancy would risk harming the physical or mental health of the pregnant woman, and potentially later if it risks her life, could cause her \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave permanent injury\u8221\'20\'1D or if there is a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial risk\u8221\'20\'1D the foetus would be \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously handicapped\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While the woman in this week\u8217\'20\'19s case terminated her pregnancy later than the legal limit, says O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, \u8220\'20\'1Cshe could have been prosecuted at any gestation\u8221\'20\'1D if she had acted outside the terms of the 1967 act. Prior to the pandemic-related introduction of pills by post (last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/30/mps-vote-to-continue-abortion-pills-by-post-scheme-in-england"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made permanent}}}\uc2  in England after a vote by MPs), \u8220\'20\'1Cwe were aware that every week, every month, women were trying to buy pills online. Any woman who bought the pills online could be sentenced to up to life imprisonment under the law as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 What do campaigners want?\par \par \uc2 One of the great ironies of British \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is that campaigners are now calling for all the home nations to be given the same legal status as Northern Ireland \u8211\'20\'13 where until recently \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/abortion-services-in-northern-ireland-almost-nonexistent-despite-legalisation#:~:text=Abortion%20was%20legalised%20in%20Northern%20Ireland%20in%20October%202019%2C%20bringing,the%20Labour%20MP%20Stella%20Creasy."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effectively illegal}}}\uc2  altogether.\par \par \uc2 A Westminster vote led by the Labour MP \uc2 Stella Creasy\uc2  (pictured above) in 2019 explicitly repealed the 1861 act where it relates to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making Northern Ireland the only part of the UK where it is decriminalised. \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems absurd that we\u8217\'20\'19re calling for women in Great Britain to be given the same protections as women in Northern Ireland,\u8221\'20\'1D says O\u8217\'20\'19Brien. The fact that MPs have already voted to repeal in part of the UK, however, arguably shows they have accepted the principle. (While the law in Northern Ireland may have changed, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien notes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/abortion-services-in-northern-ireland-almost-nonexistent-despite-legalisation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  provision there remains very limited}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 most women needing surgical procedures still need to travel to Great Britain.)\par \par \uc2 More broadly, modernised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation could include things like provision for nurse-led services, she says. \u8220\'20\'1CBut at the moment, given that this woman has been criminalised, the priority is to reform, to protect more women going forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some of those who argue against decriminalisation suggest it could lead to a free for all, but O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said this has not been the case in other countries, such as Canada, that have decriminalised. \u8220\'20\'1CNo woman aspires to have a late \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; the vast majority of women want to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care as soon as possible. And decriminalisation does not mean deregulation. What we\u8217\'20\'19re calling for is for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be treated in the same way as any other healthcare procedure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Why are police investigations rising?\par \par \uc2 One of the most troubling aspects highlighted by this week\u8217\'20\'19s case is the rise of police investigations, over the past three years, into alleged illegal abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the passing of pills by post has improved women\u8217\'20\'19s access hugely across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D says O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat it has also done, I would say, is [bring about] a growing suspicion that women might have used these pills outside the terms of the law.\u8221\'20\'1D She cites {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/02/women-accused-of-abortions-in-england-and-wales-after-miscarriages-and-stillbirths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the case of a 15-year-old girl}}}\uc2  whose unexplained stillbirth led to a year-long police investigation, until a coroner found her baby had died of natural causes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn all of the cases that I\u8217\'20\'19m aware of personally, these are women who had been reported to the police by healthcare professionals,\u8221\'20\'1D says O\u8217\'20\'19Brien. \u8220\'20\'1CThat puts us in a very frightening position, whereby a woman attending hospital, potentially what she might disclose in that medical consultation could then trigger a police investigation. The chilling effect that could have is really quite concerning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In this week\u8217\'20\'19s TechScape newsletter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/jun/13/techscape-us-sec-crypto-lawsuits-uk-rishi-sunak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alex Hern takes a look }}}\uc2  at the lawsuits launched by US regulators against two cryptocurrency exchanges and what it means for \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 . You can sign up to the newsletter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2022/sep/20/sign-up-for-the-techscape-newsletter-our-free-technology-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Nimo Omer, assistant editor, First Edition\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Man City forward, and now treble winner, Jack Grealish \u8220\'20\'1Cis having the best week of his life\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/jun/13/jack-grealish-is-having-the-best-week-of-his-life-manchester-city-treble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes Simon Hattenstone}}}\uc2  in this entertaining appreciation of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe hedonist\u8217\'20\'19s hedonist\u8221\'20\'1D, and his epic post-Champions League final bender. Esther\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 For nearly two decades, Lara Logan was a respected war correspondent who was racking in awards and acclaim. Now she spends her time touting conspiracy theories so extreme that fringe far-right media are distancing themselves from her. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2023/07/lara-logan-60-minutes-correspondent-conspiracy-theories/674168/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 For the Atlantic (\u163\'00\'A3), Elaina Plott Calabro}}}\uc2  tracks Logan\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbreak from reality\u8221\'20\'1D. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Joan Baez is still doing beautiful, cool stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/culture/the-new-yorker-interview/joan-baez-is-still-doing-beautiful-cool-stuff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline of the New Yorker\u8217\'20\'19s lovely interview}}}\uc2  with the legendary folk singer. Baez, full of gentle wisdom, explains why she has taken to drawing upside down \u8211\'20\'13 and sleeps on a mattress halfway up a tree. Esther\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2023/jun/13/indiepop-veterans-heavenly-we-saw-the-world-of-grownups-and-we-didnt-like-that-very-much"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Hann\u8217\'20\'19s interview}}}\uc2  with indie pop veterans Heavenly is a really enjoyable read that covers everything from music industry snobbishness, 90s misogyny and the bands huge popularity on the other side of the pond. Nimo\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | Ben Stokes, pictured above, is pushing hard to fulfil his pledge of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/13/ben-stokes-england-the-ashes-australia-cricket"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bowling in the first Ashes Test at Edgbaston}}}\uc2  on Friday, with the England captain to decide whether to hit Australia with the pace of Mark Wood or the experience of Stuart Broad. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/12/ashes-2023-cricket-guide-england-australia-teams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all the key player info for England and Australia}}}\uc2 , and our team\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/13/bazball-unpacked-england-test-cricket-analysis-ashes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 how England have turned up the dial in Test cricket.}}}\par \par \uc2 Basketball\par \par \uc2 | In an open letter, British basketball\u8217\'20\'19s chairman, Chris Grant, has written that the sport {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2023/jun/13/british-basketball-in-untenable-position-due-to-lack-of-uk-sport-funding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces an \u8220\'20\'1Cunsustainable and untenable\u8221\'20\'1D position}}}\uc2 , so lacking in resources it is unable to employ a single person full-time. Grant published this letter two days before GB Basketball\u8217\'20\'19s women aim to take a major step towards qualifying for the Olympics for the first time.\par \par \uc2 Football\par \par \uc2 | A damning report by \uc2 Fifpro\uc2  involving responses from 362 internationals found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/jun/13/fifpro-says-players-were-placed-at-risk-during-womens-world-cup-qualifiers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 footballers were placed \u8220\'20\'1Cat risk\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  during qualifying for next month\u8217\'20\'19s Women\u8217\'20\'19s World Cup in Australia and New Zealand by a lack of medical support and substandard working conditions.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStudents among victims stabbed to death in Nottingham rampage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s lead story this morning. \u8220\'20\'1CMurdered 5 minutes from home\u8221\'20\'1D says the Daily Mirror about the \u8220\'20\'1Ckilling rampage\u8221\'20\'1D in Nottingham. \u8220\'20\'1CStudents killed in dawn knife attacks\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the Daily Telegraph while the Times has \u8220\'20\'1CKnifeman kills three in rampage through city\u8221\'20\'1D. The Daily Express says \u8220\'20\'1CKilled at random \u8230\'20\'26 just five minutes from home\u8221\'20\'1D while the Daily Mail\u8217\'20\'19s headline is \u8220\'20\'1CHorror in Nottingham / Killed as they walked home from night out\u8221\'20\'1D and the Sun says \u8220\'20\'1CKnifed to death in rampage\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CStudents die in white van knife horror\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the Metro. The Nottingham story gets a puff on the front of the i (the report is inside) but its splash is \u8220\'20\'1CMortgage stress to hit levels last seen in 1980s \u8211\'20\'13 as interest rate heads for 5.75%\u8221\'20\'1D. The top story in the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1CBailey highlights stubborn inflation as wage growth triggers rate rise bets\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 How Saudi Arabia took over professional golf\par \par \uc2 After months of bitter divisions in the world of professional golf, a major deal has resulted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2023/jun/14/how-saudi-arabia-took-over-professional-golf-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victory for Saudi Arabia and its bid to influence the future of the sport}}}\uc2 . Ewan Murray reports\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Henny Beaumont\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 Born in Jamaica in 1959, Tessa Sanderson came to the UK as part of the Windrush generation. At school, her PE teacher noticed her exceptional sporting talent and became her mentor \u8211\'20\'13 they have remained friends all these years later.\par \par \uc2 With her encouragement, Sanderson practised and honed her craft and, despite health and funding issues as well as racism from British Athletics, Sanderson made her way to the 1984 Olympics in Barcelona, where she set a new Olympic record to win javelin gold. Although she did not realise it at the time, she became the first Black British woman to win an Olympic title.\par \par \uc2 In an interview for the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Black lives series, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2023/jun/13/tessa-sanderson-how-the-first-black-british-woman-to-win-an-olympic-title-fought-her-way-to-the-top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sanderson reflects on her extraordinary sporting career}}}\uc2 , her rivalry with Fatima Whitbread and the example she has set for her children. \u8220\'20\'1CA couple of months ago, my daughter had a \u8216\'20\'18Who would you like to be?\u8217\'20\'19 day at her school and she dressed up in my Barcelona Olympics top,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s puzzles are here to keep you entertained throughout the day \u8211\'20\'13 with plenty more on the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Puzzles app for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/app/id1487780661?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iOS}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=uk.co.guardian.puzzles&hl=en_GB&gl=US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Android}}}\uc2 . Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16569"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29096"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wordiply}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230614ej6e000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
