\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican red meat: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  bids to outflank Trump on the right\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,507 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2023\par 10:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 From Covid to crime, from immigration to cultural issues, the Florida governor is aiming to paint Trump as too liberal\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not the most rightwing candidate running for the White House. That is a statement few would have thought possible after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s brand of nativist-populism reshaped the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 But as the Republican primary election for 2024 gathers pace, Trump finds himself eclipsed on the right by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the governor of Florida, who is betting that the party\u8217\'20\'19s voters are spoiling for an even more extreme agenda.\par \par \uc2 From Covid to crime, from immigration to cultural issues, DeSantis is staking out territory that leaves the 76-year-old frontrunner fending off a once unthinkable criticism: he might be a bit too liberal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s strategy for now is that he is going to try to outflank Trump to the right and there\u8217\'20\'19s opportunity there,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hoover.org/profiles/bill-whalen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Whalen}}}\uc2 , a research fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2  thinktank at \uc2 Stanford University\uc2  in Palo Alto, California. \u8220\'20\'1CHe can go after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s record as president on spending. He can go after Trump on refusing to address entitlement reform, which Republicans seemed to abandon writ large.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week, Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/08/donald-trump-charged-retention-classified-documents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  indicted}}}\uc2  on charges of mishandling classified documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida. DeSantis did not attempt to capitalise but rather condemned the \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponization of federal law enforcement\u8221\'20\'1D. He has been dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1Cmini-Trump\u8221\'20\'1D who seeks to emulate the former president. But in his first 10 days on the campaign trail, DeSantis has assailed Trump from the right.\par \par \uc2 He told a conservative radio host \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is a different guy than 2015, 2016,\u8221\'20\'1D before deriding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/b59668424ae246bca00107943361ba79"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan criminal justice reform legislation}}}\uc2  that Trump championed as \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically a jailbreak bill\u8221\'20\'1D letting dangerous people out of prison.\par \par \uc2 On immigration, DeSantis has played to the base by flying migrants from Florida to Massachusetts and California while arguing that Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/politics/read-the-full-transcript-of-desantis-call-with-conservative-media-hammering-trump-directly-after-2024-launch/ar-AA1bHkLq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cendorsed and tried to ram\u8221\'20\'1D an \u8220\'20\'1Camnesty\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2  through Congress. The governor even claimed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s signature issue for himself by asserting that he would finish building a wall on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-immigration-mexico-473c8491da5061e8632a4dd5593ad3d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US-Mexico border}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis can point to a hard-right record in Florida and suggest that he gets the job done in contrast to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unfulfilled promises at the White House. He has accused Trump of \u8220\'20\'1Cturning the reins over\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , America\u8217\'20\'19s top infectious disease expert, during the Covid pandemic while he says he kept Florida open for business. \u8220\'20\'1CWe chose freedom over Faucism,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis told voters last week.\par \par \uc2 Whalen, who served as a speechwriter for the Bush-Quayle re-election campaign, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat DeSantis is going to attack him on is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  turned loose \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 . Trump at no point fired anybody. Trump let Fauci drive children\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare policy . If Trump wants to engage with this on a conversation over who handled Covid better, boy, if I\u8217\'20\'19m \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , bring it on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Extraordinarily, Trump finds himself on the defensive over what many neutral observers and critics regard as one his few positive achievements: the development of coronavirus vaccines in less than a year.\par \par \uc2 Campaigning in Grimes, Iowa, he received a pointed question from a woman who claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe have lost people because you supported the jab,\u8221\'20\'1D a reference to conspiracy theories about mRNA vaccines, which have been credited with saving millions of lives.\par \par \uc2 While Trump did not dismiss her suggestion \u8211\'20\'13 and stressed that he was never in favour of mandates \u8211\'20\'13 he explained that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a big portion of the country that thinks that was a great thing, you understand that. Not a lot of the people in this room, but there is a big portion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has also taken a swipe at Trump for saying he did not like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ron-desantis-new-college-florida-woke-d281e84b0d8ce2bdd66652074a090cd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the term \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  because people struggle to define it. The governor retorted: \u8220\'20\'1CWoke is an existential threat to our society. To say it\u8217\'20\'19s not a big deal, that just shows you don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what a lot of these issues are right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The skirmishes imply that DeSantis and Trump are running separate races. While the governor is aiming to woo Republican primary voters who have spent years embracing extremism, Trump is already looking ahead to a general election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  where moderate swing state voters are critical.\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly hit DeSantis from the left, arguing that his votes to cut social security and Medicare in Congress will make him unelectable in a general election \u8211\'20\'13 even though Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposed budgets also repeatedly called for major entitlement cuts.\par \par \uc2 Although Trump is quick to remind voters that he appointed three supreme court justices who, last year, helped end the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he has also suggested that Florida\u8217\'20\'19s new six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo harsh\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/01/fox-news-trump-town-hall-iowa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News town hall}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , he urged pragmatism with an eye on the general election: \u8220\'20\'1CI happen to be of the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  school in terms of exemptions, where you have the life of the mother, rape and incest. For me, that\u8217\'20\'19s something that works very well and for probably 80, 85%, because don\u8217\'20\'19t forget, we do have to win elections .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tarasetmayer.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tara Setmayer}}}\uc2 , a senior adviser to the Lincoln Project, an anti-Trump group, said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s current campaign strategists know that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a huge weakness for the Republicans on a national stage going into 2024, evidenced by what happened in the midterms with the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is trying to thread the needle and sound more pragmatic on that because he\u8217\'20\'19s actually thinking about the general at this point for that specific issue. There\u8217\'20\'19s a good chunk of Republican voters who are not happy with the extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that are being pushed by the party .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s even-harder right approach could backfire in a national race against Biden, according to Setmayer, a former Republican communications director on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a risky proposition by the DeSantis camp to try to run to the right of Trump at this point because it feels as though it\u8217\'20\'19s a very myopic strategy to just get out of the primary. Given how extreme his policies have been in Florida and what he\u8217\'20\'19s advocated for, if by some miracle he did defeat Trump in the primaries, how does he walk all of that back to appeal to a general election electorate in this country?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis idea that he wants to scale up Florida is anathema to what the majority of the American people across the country actually want policy-wise. It\u8217\'20\'19s not out of the ordinary that candidates tack more to the middle once they get into a general but we have never seen this level of extreme policy positions in a primary translate to a general election and be successful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump is not willing to be entirely out-Trumped.\par \par \uc2 He has pushed the death penalty for drug dealers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rumble.com/v2rd9jg-agenda47-ending-the-scourge-of-drug-addiction-in-america.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=230601-agenda47_ending_the_scourge_of_drug_addiction_in_america&utm_content=ncl-pxmkzPyDAV&_nlid=pxmkzPyDAV&_nhids=GKBiPNv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 renewed his pledge to use the US military}}}\uc2  to attack foreign drug cartels. He also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rumble.com/v2qxy9q-agenda47-day-one-executive-order-ending-automatic-citizenship-for-children-.html?utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=230530-agenda47_day_one_executive_order_ending_citizenship_for_children_of_illegals_and_outlawing_birth_tourism&utm_content=ncl-GCJ8pwdCDk&_nlid=GCJ8pwdCDk&_nhids=pE8tgoP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revived his pledge to end birthright citizenship}}}\uc2 , saying he would sign an executive order on the first day of his second term to change the long-settled interpretation of the 14th amendment.\par \par \uc2 The posturing from both men might come to nought. History suggests that policy can be less important to voters than personality. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhh.umn.edu/directory/larry-jacobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Jacobs}}}\uc2 , director of the Center for the Study of Politics and Governance at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis is running to the right of Trump on policy. The particular niche of Trump is that his rhetoric and his populism remains further right than DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis has been a governor, a member of Congress. For all of his rhetorical policy stances and the policies he\u8217\'20\'19s signed into law, he\u8217\'20\'19s still part of the government. Sure, Trump was president, but he has carved a place for himself as a demagogue, as someone who is running both for and against the political and economic system in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jacobs added: \u8220\'20\'1C DeSantis would like him to run on policy and then DeSantis can run on his record of what he\u8217\'20\'19s accomplished and try to win over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing base.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I don\u8217\'20\'19t think Trump is going to let him do that. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to continue to mock and portray DeSantis as part of the problem, someone who\u8217\'20\'19s feeble and lacks the grit and the guts of a strong leader .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump allies dismiss DeSantis as an imitator who rings hollow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roger-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roger Stone}}}\uc2 , a political consultant and self-proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1Cdirty trickster\u8221\'20\'1D based in Florida, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe can try to sound like Trump, he can try to position himself like Trump, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t think those are his real politics. He\u8217\'20\'19s an establishment Republican . If you have a choice of seeing the Beatles or seeing a Beatles tribute band, which one are you going to go see? \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230611ej6b000rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
