\par\par \uc2 Books\par \b \uc2 The Shadow Docket review: how the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  keeps sunlight out\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 1,003 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2023\par 06:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Steve Vladeck offers a closely argued, detailed case against the justices\u8217\'20\'19 use of procedure to advance a rightwing agenda\par \par \uc2 Only a quarter of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/394103/confidence-supreme-court-sinks-historic-low.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have confidence}}}\uc2  in the supreme court. As the country strives to navigate a post-Roe v Wade world, the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/MLSPSC14Toplines.html#C7:_FavUnfav:_Alito"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regard for the right wing of the court is scarcer still}}}\uc2 . Justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  have negative ratings with the public. Kavanaugh and Thomas are underwater by double-digits.\par \par \uc2 Being perceived as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/brett-kavanaugh-investigation-omissions-senate-sexual-assault-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predator}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Kavanaugh \u8211\'20\'13 engenders disdain or worse. Taking undisclosed gifts from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jun/07/harlan-crow-senate-subpoena-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Republican mega-donor}}}\uc2  and being married to an election-denier who trades on her spouse\u8217\'20\'19s judgeship \u8211\'20\'13 Thomas \u8211\'20\'13 triggers demands for renewed oversight.\par \par \uc2 When Ginni Thomas visited the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cyou knew your day was wrecked\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/inside-ginni-thomas-insane-hiring-memos-for-former-president-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said a senior Trump aide}}}\uc2 , according to the Daily Beast. This week came news that \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and Alito have not yet filed their financial disclosures and have received extensions. The circus rumbles on.\par \par \uc2 Against such a backdrop, Stephen Vladeck, a professor at the University of Texas law school and CNN commentator, delivers The Shadow Docket.\par \par \uc2 Under the subtitle \u8220\'20\'1CHow the Supreme Court Uses Stealth Rulings to Amass Power and Undermine the Republic\u8221\'20\'1D, Vladeck offers a well-researched indictment of how the supreme court has grown to rely on using procedural orders rather than rulings to make new law, escaping scrutiny while delivering major victories to the political right.\par \par \uc2 The term \u8220\'20\'1Cshadow docket\u8221\'20\'1D was coined in 2015, by William Baude, a \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  law professor. In Vladeck\u8217\'20\'19s words, it was \u8220\'20\'1Ca catch-all for a body of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s work that was, to that point, receiving virtually no academic or public attention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Strictly speaking, the shadow docket is a vehicle for addressing issues that demand urgent attention, usually injunctions and orders to preserve the status quo. But it has morphed into a fraught topic. The court has adjudicated cases involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , voting rights and Covid policy by means of the shadow docket. The docket also became the prime location for the elevation and reordering of religious rights, under the free exercise clause of the first amendment.\par \par \uc2 Almost by definition, docket rulings are sparse. They are often unaccompanied by reasoning, Vladeck writes. \u8220\'20\'1CInvariably\u8221\'20\'1D, they lack \u8220\'20\'1Cidentification of how (or how many of) the justices voted and can be handed down at all times of day or, as has increasingly become the norm, in the middle of the night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vladeck knows his subject. In September 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/Vladeck%20testimony1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he testified to the Senate judiciary committee}}}\uc2  about \u8220\'20\'1CTexas\u8217\'20\'19s Unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ban and the Role of the Shadow Docket\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/05/19/supreme-court-stephen-vladeck-interview-00096719"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s remarkable is that the court repeatedly acquiesced and acquiesced [to the right] \u8230\'20\'26 and almost always without any explanation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the page, he observes that few such Trumpian wins have resulted in actual binding precedents. Rather, shadow docket triumphs mainly satisfy political needs. Vladeck credits \uc2 Noel Francisco\uc2 , the solicitor general under Trump, and his deputy, for hatching the legal strategy that for example salvaged the Muslim travel ban and efforts to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild the wall\u8221\'20\'1D on the southern border without express congressional appropriation.\par \par \uc2 SB-8, the Texas six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, provides a stark illustration of how the process continues to work. In September 2021, the supreme court did not formally opine on the constitutionality of the draconian Texas law. Instead, in an unsigned shadow docket order, a bare majority allowed the statute to slide into effect. It read:\par \par \uc2 The application for injunctive relief or, in the alternative, to vacate stays of the district court proceedings presented to Justice Alito and by him referred to the court is denied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The text made no mention of Roe, the 1973 ruling then in place, safeguarding federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But everyone could see what was coming.\par \par \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice, a \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  appointee, would have stopped the Texas law from going into effect, pending a decision on the merits. The statutory rubric was \u8220\'20\'1Cunusual\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D, he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe legislature has imposed a prohibition on abortions after roughly six weeks, and then essentially delegated enforcement of that prohibition to the populace at large.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Months later, Roberts voted with the three liberals to save Roe. No matter. The court struck it down.\par \par \uc2 Not everyone welcomes the attention Vladeck and others have brought to the use of the shadow docket. Alito publicly twitted the media for portraying it as something \u8220\'20\'1Csinister\u8221\'20\'1D, and depicting the court as \u8220\'20\'1Chaving been captured by a dangerous cabal that resorts to sneaky and improper methods to get its ways\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s friendship with the mega-donor Harlan Crowe should surely give any observer clear reason to pause.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Coney Barrett has denied that the court engages in results-oriented decision-making, urging an audience at the Reagan Library in April 2022 to \u8220\'20\'1Cread the opinion\u8221\'20\'1D instead.\par \par \uc2 Vladeck is unswayed: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s essential context to point out that, just two days later, she joined a 5-4 shadow docket ruling with no opinion for the public to read. It\u8217\'20\'19s all part of the story \u8211\'20\'13 or, at least, it should be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rise of the shadow docket \u8230\'20\'26 has negative effects on public perception of the court \u8211\'20\'13 and of the perceived legitimacy of the justices\u8217\'20\'19 work,\u8221\'20\'1D Vladeck writes.\par \par \uc2 The legitimacy of the court erodes.\par \par \uc2 The Shadow Docket is comprehensive and sensitive to nuance, written for concerned audiences. Members of Congress, the bar, the press and engaged non-lawyers come to mind. Vladeck covers more than two centuries of legal history, together with the transformation of the court into a visibly co-equal branch of government.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night, news broke of 37 federal criminal counts against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The next election is 17 months away. The legitimacy and resilience of all US institutions stands to be tested like never before.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Shadow Docket is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bookshop.org/p/books/the-shadow-docket-how-the-supreme-court-uses-stealth-rulings-to-amass-power-and-undermine-the-republic-stephen-vladeck/18831478?ean=9781541602632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 by Hachette\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230611ej6b000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
