\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s historic challenge: can Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loyal deputy become his nemesis?\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Washington \par \uc2 1,051 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2023\par 18:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The former vice-president has joined the Republican presidential field for 2024 but his White House experience may count for little\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  enters the 2024 presidential race with a murky path to capturing the Republican nomination and a contentious relationship with his former boss and now primary opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pence formally launched his campaign on Wednesday with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mike_Pence/status/1666377457157668865"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video announcement}}}\uc2  and an event in Des Moines, Iowa, after the former vice-president spent months traveling to early voting states and speaking at Republican party events.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be easy to stay on the sidelines. That\u8217\'20\'19s not how I was raised,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence told the Iowa crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve long believed that to whom much is given much would be required. That\u8217\'20\'19s why today, before God and my family, I\u8217\'20\'19m announcing that I\u8217\'20\'19m running for president of the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s campaign launch kicks off a historic primary battle, as this marks the first time in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/6285105/pence-2024-trump-vice-presidents-history/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 80 years}}}\uc2  that a former vice-president has competed against his former boss in a nomination fight.\par \par \uc2 In his speech on Wednesday, Pence did not shy away from attacking Trump, accusing the former president of straying from the rightwing priorities that carried him to victory in 2016.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know we can bring this country back,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19ll require new leadership in the White House and the Republican Party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president becomes the latest Republican to join a growing field of candidates looking to deprive Trump of the nomination. Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida, the South Carolina senator Tim Scott, the former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  and North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  have all jumped into the race in just the past few weeks, following the campaign announcements of Trump, the former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley, the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2  and the entrepreneur \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Historically, vice-presidents have been able to use their past White House experience to make a strong case for their party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. But Pence faces unique challenges that could complicate his already difficult task of attempting to topple Trump, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continues to lead}}}\uc2  in polls of Republican primary voters.\par \par \uc2 Pence left the vice-presidency in 2021, weeks after the January 6 attack on the US Capitol. As part of his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election, Trump attempted to pressure Pence into using his role as president of the Senate to disrupt the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory.\par \par \uc2 Pence refused to do so, as he argued that the vice-president has no authority to object to the election results, an assessment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/fact-checking-275776015398"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported}}}\uc2  by constitutional experts. Trump lashed out against Pence, accusing the vice-president of cowardice for refusing to meddle in a free and fair election. The vice-president then became a target for the insurrectionists who attacked the Capitol, some of whom chanted, \u8220\'20\'1CHang \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 !\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Secret Service officers safely evacuated Pence for the Capitol, and he was ultimately able to oversee the certification of the election results. But the horror of that day has become an ongoing source of tension between Pence and Trump, who has continued to falsely claim that his vice-president could have stepped in to overturn the election results. When asked at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MpCoVxa_kVM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN town hall}}}\uc2  last month whether he owed Pence an apology for endangering him on January 6, Trump said no.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Pence offered pointed criticism of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions on January 6, insinuating that they should disqualify the former president from seeking another term.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that anyone who puts themselves over the constitution should never be president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd anyone who asks someone else to put them over the constitution should never be president of the United States again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Pence\u8217\'20\'19s actions on January 6 have been lauded by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/-real-moral-force-conservatives-praise-pence-courage-jan-6-rcna39120"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/now/democratic-impeachment-manager-lavishes-praise-on-mike-pence-for-standing-up-to-trump-210057599.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  in Congress, they have not made him as popular with the primary voters whose support he will need to win the nomination.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3872"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quinnipiac University poll}}}\uc2  taken last month, 48% of Republican voters have a favorable opinion of Pence, compared with 35% who have an unfavorable opinion of him. Pence\u8217\'20\'19s favorability rating of +13 among Republican voters is considerably lower than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rating of +75 and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s of +74.\par \par \uc2 Pence appears to be counting on white evangelical voters, who make up a significant portion of the Republican base, to boost his standing. To appeal to those voters, Pence has leaned heavily into the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of Roe v Wade last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have become an even more crucial issue in America\u8217\'20\'19s elections. Other Republican presidential candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/25/nikki-haley-address-abortion-directly-00093799"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/05/31/tim-scott-2024-abortion-axios-event"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled}}}\uc2  to clarify their stances on a potential federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DNCWarRoom/status/1641800698114322432?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  that he would \u8220\'20\'1Cof course\u8221\'20\'1D support a six-week nationwide ban.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Iowa voters on Wednesday, Pence emphasized his commitment to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and attacked fellow Republican primary candidates for failing to do the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter leading the most pro-life administration in American history, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others in this race are retreating from the cause of the unborn,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs your president, I will always stand for the sanctity of life and I will not rest and I will not relent until we restore the sanctity of life to the center of American law in every state in the land.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite his staunch support for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, it remains unclear whether Pence can sway a large number of evangelical voters, many of whom remain loyal to Trump after helping him secure his 2016 win. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/documents/monmouthpoll_us_020923.pdf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monmouth University survey}}}\uc2  released in February found that 3% of evangelical voters wanted Pence to be the Republican presidential nominee, compared with 34% who said the same of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Pence has his work cut out for him, but he projected optimism as he entered what promises to be a bruising primary fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people have always been great. We just need government as good as our people,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we\u8217\'20\'19ll have it soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230607ej670023c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
