\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  officially enters 2024 US presidential race, pitting himself against former boss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Fran Lawther (earlier) \par \uc2 4,723 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former vice president filed papers on Monday; Democrats criticise Haley on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance after CNN town hall\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e01818f0800f47c1f29e6#block-647e01818f0800f47c1f29e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed the paperwork necessary}}}\uc2  to run for president, though he will wait till Wednesday to make his campaign official with a speech in Iowa. Meanwhile in Washington, attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647dff788f08fb4d89a3298e#block-647dff788f08fb4d89a3298e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stopped by}}}\uc2  the justice department, where special counsel Jack Smith is reportedly nearing a decision on whether to recommend charges over the classified documents federal agents discovered last year at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire governor Chris Sununu{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e10878f08e2e6a7f95a04#block-647e10878f08e2e6a7f95a04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  to jump into the race for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, instead {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e33ea8f08ebf1ed87464f#block-647e33ea8f08ebf1ed87464f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  he will work to defeat Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 But the 2024 campaign did get {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e1f0f8f0800788fac9d29#block-647e1f0f8f0800788fac9d29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another entrant}}}\uc2  : philosopher, author, critic, actor and civil rights activist Cornel West.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Military jets{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e38188f08e2e6a7f95b62#block-647e38188f08e2e6a7f95b62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempted to establish contact}}}\uc2  with a plane that overflew restricted airspace in Washington, DC on Sunday and later crashed, killing all onboard, but the pilot appeared slumped over and never responded.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley participated in a CNN-moderated town hall last night, but even they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647deb288f0849bab8a2e8d3#block-647deb288f0849bab8a2e8d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get}}}\uc2  her to make her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access clear.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s edge over other Republicans: he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e09b58f0832a4cdaa92da#block-647e09b58f0832a4cdaa92da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 actually rides}}}\uc2  motorcycles.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN has inserted itself prominently in the American political conversation in recent weeks by hosting town halls with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Nikki Haley and, on Wednesday, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 . But the network was also heavily criticized for how it handled the event with Trump, and to make matters worse, the Atlantic last week published a damning portrait of the network\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive Chris Licht and his decision making. It\u8217\'20\'19s a major story in American media, and here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  with the latest:\par \par \uc2 The embattled CNN chief executive, Chris Licht, apologized to his employees on Monday after an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2023/06/cnn-ratings-chris-licht-trump/674255/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlantic magazine profile}}}\uc2  revealed he had been aware of the \u8220\'20\'1Cextra-Trumpy\u8221\'20\'1D make-up of the crowd at a widely criticized town hall with the former president last month.\par \par \uc2 According to the Atlantic, Licht had also been critical of CNN\u8217\'20\'19s performance under his predecessor, telling employees they had alienated potential viewers through hostility to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an editorial call Monday morning, Licht \u8211\'20\'13 who had committed to a number of interviews for the Atlantic profile \u8211\'20\'13 apologized for his involvement in the piece.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jun/05/chris-licht-atlantic-profile-cnn-trump-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Licht apologizes to staff for taking spotlight with Atlantic profile}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Washington, DC area was yesterday rattled by a sonic boom caused by military jets sent to pursue a wayward plane that later crashed into a remote part of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/transportation/2023/06/05/cessna-citation-plane-crash-sonic-boom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  that military F-16s and air traffic controllers received no response from the Cessna Citation despite repeated attempts to establish contact, but one aviator saw the pilot slumped over. That may be an indication that the cabin had lost pressure, rendering all onboard unconscious and leaving the aircraft to fly on until it lost fuel and crashed, killing all four people onboard.\par \par \uc2 At today\u8217\'20\'19s White House press briefing, National Security Council spokesman John Kirby gave reporters a full account of how the military responded to the plane\u8217\'20\'19s overflight of the city, which saw it traverse airspace restricted since the 9/11 attacks:\par \par \uc2 enltrJohn Kirby on Sunday's NORAD intercept: "Six F-16s from three different air bases...launched to intercept this particular Cessna Citation...the two from Andrews...they had to turn on the speed to get to him, which is why people here in the District area heard a sonic boom..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0PKiqikPAk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0PKiqikPAk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1665792185890115585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 These sorts of rants from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are one reason why he\u8217\'20\'19s earned the ire of a segment of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Count New Hampshire governor \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  among them. Today, the moderate Republican told CNN he would not stand for president in 2024, and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2023/06/05/chris-sununu-trump-gop-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a column for the Washington Post}}}\uc2  elaborated on his reasons why.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince 2017, the national Republican Party has lost up and down the ballot, in red states and in blue states, and in elections spanning the House, Senate and presidency. That will happen again unless we Republicans undergo a course correction,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 The governor continued:\par \par \uc2 Current polls indicate Trump is the leading Republican candidate in 2024. He did not deliver on his promises to drain the swamp, secure the border and instill fiscal responsibility while in office \u8212\'20\'14 and added $8 trillion to our national debt \u8212\'20\'14 yet now he wants four more years.\par \par \uc2 If he is the nominee, Republicans will lose again. Just as we did in 2018, 2020 and 2022. This is indisputable, and I am not willing to let it happen without a fight.\par \par \uc2 By choosing not to seek the nomination, I can be more effective for the Republican Party in ways few other leaders can. The microphone afforded to the governor of New Hampshire plays a critical role in an early nominating state. I plan to endorse, campaign and support the candidate I believe has the best chance of winning in November 2024.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll see how big of a threat Sununu\u8217\'20\'19s opposition poses to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign for another four years in the White House. But here are a few other considerations that may have kept Sununu out of the race: his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmur.com/article/sununu-special-session-abortion-rights/40437549"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparatively loose stance}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/10/1104025539/new-hampshire-redistricting-competitive-districts-sununu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unwillingness to adopt}}}\uc2  an aggressive gerrymander of the state\u8217\'20\'19s district maps in favor of the GOP, and other centrist policies. He may have figured he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have had a chance of winning over the party\u8217\'20\'19s powerful conservative base.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made liberal use of the caps lock key in crafting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110492504108368110"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this Truth social post}}}\uc2  from a few hours ago, on the day his attorneys paid a visit to the justice department:\par \par \uc2 zxxltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/61lr8u3gF9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/61lr8u3gF9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1665793297376239616?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers met with justice department staff, not Garland\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports that the lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who turned up today at the justice department were meeting with senior officials, but not attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , as they had requested:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Trump lawyers Jim Trusty, John Rowley and Lindsey Halligan met with the senior career official in the Deputy AG\u8217\'20\'19s office earlier today; Trump lawyers raised instances of what they viewed as prosecutorial misconduct in the Mar-a-Lago docs case, per ppl familiar.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1665767777758584835?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Such meetings are typical when justice department investigations near their conclusion, as special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago appears to be.\par \par \uc2 Smith is also looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the January 6 insurrection, and the broader plot to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election win. Those inquiries appear to be ongoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new feud with California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  head to the courts, it would be just the latest instance in which the Florida governor and presidential aspirant\u8217\'20\'19s policies have cost his state money, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Since Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , took office in 2019 and embarked on his culture wars, lawsuits from various communities whose rights have been violated have been stacking up against the far-right Republican.\par \par \uc2 As DeSantis fights the lawsuits with what critics have described as a blank check from the state\u8217\'20\'19s supermajority Republican legislature, the mounting legal costs have come heavily at the expense of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s ultra-conservative legislative agenda has drawn ire from a slew of marginalized communities as well as major corporations including \uc2 Disney\uc2 . The so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/republican-states-mimic-florida-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans#:~:text=Ron%20DeSantis%20signs%20bill%20approving%20six%2Dweek%20abortion%20ban%20in%20Florida,-This%20article%20is&text=The%20Republican%2Ddominated%20Florida%20legislature,for%20an%20expected%20presidential%20run."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans}}}\uc2  and prohibition of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/19/ron-desantis-bans-african-american-studies-florida-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 African American studies}}}\uc2  are just a few of DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s many extremist policies that have been met with costly lawsuits in a state where residents are already struggling with costs of living.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/04/ron-desantis-lawsuits-cost-florida-taxpayers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida taxpayers pick up bill for Ron DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s culture war lawsuits}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 California governor accuses DeSantis of kidnapping over migrant flight to Sacramento\par \par \uc2 The California governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , has weighed into the row between his state and Florida over the case of a group of 16 migrants who were left outside a Sacramento church.\par \par \uc2 A rights group said the group had been \u8220\'20\'1Clied to\u8221\'20\'1D and deceived after being transported from Texas to California. The circumstances are similar to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/16/migrants-marthas-vineyard-desantis-biden-democrats-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stunt orchestrated by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing Republican governor}}}\uc2  last year in Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 Now Newsom has mentioned kidnapping charges in relation to the incident. Here\u8217\'20\'19s his tweet, criticising \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  after California authorities pointed the finger at the Florida governor over the incident:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RonDeSantis}}}\uc2  you small, pathetic man.\par \par \uc2 This isn't Martha's Vineyard.\par \par \uc2 Kidnapping charges?\par \par \uc2 Read the following. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kvuxe8Fb6F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kvuxe8Fb6F}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KyE1lJiIYo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KyE1lJiIYo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1665769565261840387?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cornel West, the philosopher, author, critic, actor and civil rights activist, has announced he is running for president.\par \par \uc2 West launched his campaign for the People\u8217\'20\'19s Party with a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  video on Monday.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI care about you. I care about the quality of your life, I care about whether you have access to a job with a living wage, decent housing, women having control over their bodies, healthcare for all, the escalating destruction of the planet, the destruction of American democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Watch his whole campaign launch video here:\par \par \uc2 enltrI am running for truth and justice as a presidential candidate for the People\u8217\'20\'19s Party to reintroduce America to the best of itself - fighting to end poverty, mass incarceration, ending wars and ecological collapse, guaranteeing housing, health care, education and living wages for\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u3NYGUbG1S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u3NYGUbG1S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cornel West (@CornelWest) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CornelWest/status/1665743761551548416?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency exchange, \uc2 Binance\uc2 , is being sued by the SEC over allegations of mishandling customer funds and lying to regulators and investors.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  has hit back at the claims and my colleague Lauren Aratani is reporting all the latest on the lawsuit in our dedicated blog. You can follow latest updates here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/jun/05/sec-sues-binance-crypto-cftc-changpeng-zhao-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrency exchange Binance hits back at SEC lawsuit, saying allegations \u8216\'20\'18simply wrong\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e01818f0800f47c1f29e6#block-647e01818f0800f47c1f29e6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed the paperwork necessary}}}\uc2  to run for president, though he will wait till Wednesday to make the campaign official with a speech in Iowa. Meanwhile in Washington, attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647dff788f08fb4d89a3298e#block-647dff788f08fb4d89a3298e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have stopped by}}}\uc2  the justice department, where special counsel Jack Smith is reportedly nearing a decision on whether to recommend charges over the classified documents federal agents discovered last year at Mar-a-Lago. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear who the lawyers met with, but when we find out, we\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New Hampshire governor Chris Sununu{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e10878f08e2e6a7f95a04#block-647e10878f08e2e6a7f95a04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has declined}}}\uc2  to jump into the race for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley participated in a CNN-moderated town hall last night, but even they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647deb288f0849bab8a2e8d3#block-647deb288f0849bab8a2e8d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get}}}\uc2  her to make her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access clear.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s edge over other Republicans: he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/jun/05/trump-nikki-haley-2024-washington-sonic-boom-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-647e09b58f0832a4cdaa92da#block-647e09b58f0832a4cdaa92da"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 actually rides}}}\uc2  motorcycles.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican voters pining to send a governor to the White House needn\u8217\'20\'19t worry \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to forgo a run.\par \par \uc2 North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who is little known outside his home state \u8211\'20\'13 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/president-republican-north-dakota-burgum-trump-4d3f36344cf254733057a7f7acd54f32"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to also on Wednesday}}}\uc2  declare his candidacy for president, the same day \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  kicks off his campaign in Iowa. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a teaser video Burgum just posted:\par \par \uc2 enltrComing Soon. Watch for a preview of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s big announcement. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rvzYMr4SYc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rvzYMr4SYc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  (@DougBurgum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DougBurgum/status/1665739410900434951?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Other governor options for Republican voters: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is a distant second place to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the latest polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 GOP governor Sununu says no to presidential run - interview\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/05/politics/chris-sununu-not-running-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with CNN}}}\uc2 , New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  said he will not run for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve taken the last six months to really kind of look at things where everything is and I\u8217\'20\'19ve made the decision not to run for president on the Republican ticket in 2024,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sununu, who was re-elected to a fourth two-year term as governor last year.\par \par \uc2 Sununu has maintained his popularity in what\u8217\'20\'19s considering a blue-leaning swing state, and also attempted to distance himself from Trump, telling CNN last year that he thinks that \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly moving on\u8221\'20\'1D from the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 You know who else was at the \u8220\'20\'1CRoast and Ride\u8221\'20\'1D in Iowa this weekend? \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  ! He has the full story on what he aptly calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca slice of pure Americana\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 There were hay bales and Harley-Davidsons. There was sliced pork and campaign paraphernalia. There were earnest speeches about defeating Democrats winning back the White House. But at the centre of it all was a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -shaped hole.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential primary for 2024 got under way in earnest on Saturday when eight contenders \u8211\'20\'13 minus Trump \u8211\'20\'13 took part in Iowa senator \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CRoast and Ride\u8221\'20\'1D, a combination of barbecue-rally and motorcycle ride.\par \par \uc2 The annual event is a slice of pure Americana. When a young pastor offered a prayer from the back of a pickup truck outside a big yellow barn owned by \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2 , bikers removed their caps, placed them over their hearts and bowed their heads. The convoy rode in staggered formation past churches, suburban houses with clipped lawns, shopping malls and rolling farmland to the Iowa state fairgrounds.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , set to make his entry into the primary official next week, was the only White House hopeful to actually take part in the charity parade. The former vice-president, who turns 64 next week, rode a cobalt blue bike and wore jeans, boots, a white helmet and a black leather vest with patches that said \u8220\'20\'1CIndiana\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CPence\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Crolling thunder\u8221\'20\'1D and messages supportive of the military.\par \par \uc2 Pence was among the Republican aspirants who, speaking in front of bales of hay and an outline of the Iowa map, delivered speeches of about 10 minutes each inside a wooden-roofed building where about a thousand voters ate lunch on green table cloths. But none mentioned Trump by name, giving the impression of a party in denial.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/04/republican-presidential-primary-revs-up-with-bikers-bbqs-and-a-donald-trump-shaped-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Roast and Ride\u8217\'20\'19: Republican primary revs up with bikers, BBQs and a Trump-shaped hole}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 First on the left, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and first on the right senator \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2 , at the \u8220\'20\'1CRoast and Ride\u8221\'20\'1D. Photograph: Dave Kaup/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Say what you will about \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , but the former president was the only candidate to actually get on a motorcycle this past weekend, when several GOP presidential contenders went to the \u8220\'20\'1CRoast and Ride\u8221\'20\'1D in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 The event, organized by the state\u8217\'20\'19s GOP senator \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2 , was attended by Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , senator Tim Scott and Nikki Haley, all official contenders. Pence hadn\u8217\'20\'19t made his campaign official yet at the time of the rally, but distinguished himself by not just roasting, but also riding:\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , looking pretty happy on the bike. His wife, Karen, is to the right. Photograph: Scott Olson/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have welcomed \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to the presidential race with a big smile and open arms.\par \par \uc2 Just kidding \u8212\'20\'14 they hate him. Pence may have broken with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on January 6 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/mike-pence-40ft-from-mob-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended up running}}}\uc2  from a mob of his infuriated supporters, but the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  does not want voters to forget about the policies he supported as vice-president, Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s governor, and a member of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what DNC chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  had to say about Pence, now that he\u8217\'20\'19s officially on the campaign trail:\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s own words, he was a member of the extreme Tea Party \u8216\'20\'18before it was cool,\u8217\'20\'19 and he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t slowed down since. Pence pushed an extreme agenda in Congress and the Indiana statehouse before becoming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s MAGA wingman for four years and then campaigning for election deniers last year. Now, he\u8217\'20\'19s promising to take the Trump-Pence agenda even further, leading the charge for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, cutting Medicare, and ending Social Security as we know it.\par \par \uc2 Pence\u8217\'20\'19s entrance will no doubt drag an increasingly MAGA 2024 GOP field even further to the extremes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence makes presidential bid official\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has officially entered the 2024 presidential race, pitting him against his former boss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a host of other candidates including Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/P40013435/1706462"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Federal Election Commission\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2  shows Pence and his campaign committee, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  for President located in Carmel, Indiana, officially registering today. The former vice-president will publicly announce the bid on Wednesday in Des Moines, Iowa.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are at the justice department today to argue to top officials that the former president should not be charged over the classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/06/05/trump-lawyers-meeting-justice-doj/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The attorneys at the meeting include John Rowley and James Trusty, who last month sent a letter to attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , asking for a meeting and complaining about the investigation into Trump, which is led by special counsel Jack Smith.\par \par \uc2 According to the Post, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear who at the justice department they are meeting today. While it\u8217\'20\'19s not unusual for lawyers of people being investigated to seek a meeting with prosecutors before they decide on filing charges, the attorney general usually does not take part in such meetings, the Post reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence to officially enter presidential race today\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will later today file paperwork to officially enter the presidential race, ahead of his public launch scheduled for Wednesday in Iowa, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Pence, who served under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but fell out with him when the former president pressed him to take part in his plans to disrupt the transfer of power to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , will publicly kick off the campaign in Des Moines, Iowa on Wednesday with the release of a video and an in-person event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers visit justice department as special counsel mulls charges over documents - report\par \par \uc2 CBS News reports that attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are today visiting the justice department as special counsel Jack Smith nears a decision on whether to bring charges over the classified documents found at his Mar-a-Lago resort:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers just spotted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}\uc2  entering the Justice Department, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobLegare?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RobLegare}}}\uc2  who is on site\u8230\'20\'26 comes as sources tell me the special counsel is moving toward a charging decision in the classified documents case\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1665722395095605248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSources tell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are expected to raise concerns about how prosecutors have handled atty-client questions during the grand jury but there is no sign the special counsel is going to waver from how he and his team have handled the crime-fraud exception\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1665723334418415619?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMust credit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobLegare?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RobLegare}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CbR9042N31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CbR9042N31}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1665724348664102912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/evan-corcoran-trump-lawyer-waved-off-secret-document-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian reported}}}\uc2  last week that Evan Corcoran, a lawyer for the former president, was waved off by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s associates when he asked to search his office at Mar-a-Lago for classified documents, and instead only checked a storage room. When federal agents last August searched the property, the office was one of the areas where the classified documents were found.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 In normal times, the ex-governor of a solidly red state would be expected to mount a competitive challenge for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Not this year, apparently. Former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , who has criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  more harshly than most others on the campaign trail, is nowhere in the polls. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say about that, and his chances for appearing in the first GOP presidential debate scheduled for 23 August, in an interview with Fox Business:\par \par \uc2 enltrFox Business\u8217\'20\'19 Cheryl Casone: \u8220\'20\'1CRight now RealClearPolitics has you polling at just about 0.4%. Are you confident that you\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have a spot on the stage for this first debate?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2024 GOP candidate Asa Hutchinson: \u8220\'20\'1COur polling numbers show higher than that \u8230\'20\'26 I will be there.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ydCeerqAnr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ydCeerqAnr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1665721746337710080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN may have deemed Nikki Haley prominent enough to warrant her own town hall, but it\u8217\'20\'19s still tough out there for any Republican trying to take down \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Just take a look at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this chart}}}\uc2  from poll aggregator FiveThirtyEight. Trump is at 53.9% support, compared to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 21.1% \u8211\'20\'13 and that\u8217\'20\'19s just for second place. The aggregator has Haley at a depressing 4.5%, below \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president who he has fallen out with.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment from the CNN town hall last night when Nikki Haley made her position on a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban clear \u8211\'20\'13 as mud:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jaketapper?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jaketapper}}}\uc2  : "If a six-week [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] ban theoretically came to your desk, would you sign it?"\par \par \uc2 2024 GOP candidate Nikki Haley: "I will answer that when you ask Kamala and Biden if they would agree to 37 weeks, 38 weeks, 39 weeks. Then I'll answer your question." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d98A6QKtkh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d98A6QKtkh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1665704939455225857?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Her waffling was yet another indication of how Republicans are now struggling with the decision by their conservative appointees on the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade last year. Though the party has for years pledged to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, now that they finally have the legal clearance to do so, they\u8217\'20\'19re finding out that it\u8217\'20\'19s not exactly a winning prospect among voters. Just ask all the GOP candidates who did not get elected in last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Though there\u8217\'20\'19s no shortage of alternatives, polls consistently show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the most popular candidate for the Republican presidential nomination. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Peter Stone reports, those familiar with his rhetoric and proposals are deeply worried about what a second term in the White House would mean for America:\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  begins another campaign for the presidency, his extremist rhetoric and lies about the 2020 election signal that in a second term, Trump would attempt to thwart the rule of law at the justice department and other agencies in an effort to expand his power and attack critics.\par \par \uc2 Former DoJ officials, some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  and academics say that if Trump becomes the Republican nominee and is elected again in 2024, he would most likely appoint officials who would reflexively do his bidding, target dissenters he deems part of the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D and mount zealous drives to rein in independent agencies.\par \par \uc2 Donald Ayer, a former deputy attorney general during the \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2  administration, told the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1COf all the many reasons \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s candidacy should be rejected out of hand, none is more important than his utter disdain for the rule of law \u8211\'20\'13 the idea that we are a society governed by rules and not by the will of one person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/05/trump-criticis-doj-rule-of-law-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump critics warn of \u8216\'20\'18deep decline of rule of law\u8217\'20\'19 if he wins second term}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 When she announced her campaign, Nikki Haley made headlines by calling for mental competency tests for politicians over 75 years old.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are both past that age, but, like many other Republicans, Haley has mostly directed the criticism at the sitting president.\par \par \uc2 Here she is on Fox News, implying that Biden wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t make it through another four years in office:\par \par \uc2 enltr2024 GOP candidate Nikki Haley:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA vote for President Biden is actually a vote for President Harris. We are running against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ... Every liberal knows it, they know it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna end up being president if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wins this election.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gvdYfw3IUH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gvdYfw3IUH}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1665709223819264000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats accuse Haley of 'Maga agenda'\par \par \uc2 As Nikki Haley made her pitch to Republican voters last night, Democrats sought to remind the public that the former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador is not as different from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as she may say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaley spent an hour and a half doubling down on her Maga agenda \u8211\'20\'13 reminding Americans she supports a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and ending Social Security and Medicare as we know it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rhyan Lake, a spokesperson for the \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC)\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTake it from Team Haley \u8211\'20\'13 her extreme, anti-freedom candidacy is just as Maga as the rest of the 2024 GOP field.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the town hall, Haley attempted to distance herself from Trump and the January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHe thinks it was a beautiful day; I think it was a terrible day.\u8221\'20\'1D But the DNC noted she has endorsed election denying Republicans across the country, including Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , and New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Don Bolduc\uc2 , both failed Senate candidates.\par \par \uc2 Haley attacked Trump and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Cnot being honest\u8221\'20\'1D about the sustainability of social security and medicare, two major government aid programs. But the DNC said she has embraced cuts to the programs proposed by \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 , a former Republican speaker of the House. \u8220\'20\'1CHaley has been shamelessly campaigning to end Social Security and Medicare as we know it \u8212\'20\'14 which would hurt hard working families and seniors across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Haley stays vague on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , attacks Trump, DeSantis at town hall\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. We heard more from presidential candidate Nikki Haley at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/04/politics/nikki-haley-cnn-town-hall-takeaways/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a CNN-hosted town hall last night}}}\uc2 , who, like all Republicans not named \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has a tough hill to climb to overcome the party\u8217\'20\'19s frontrunner for the nomination. She criticized both the former president (also her ex-boss, since she worked as his \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador) and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who is viewed as the next-best contender. But in some ways, Haley is more like Trump than she lets on. Pressed about her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say what sort of restrictions on the procedure she would support, only that she\u8217\'20\'19d aim to get some sort of legislation through Congress. That sounds a lot like the former president, who has demurred on saying whether he\u8217\'20\'19d sign a national ban. Expect to hear more reactions to Haley\u8217\'20\'19s town hall appearance as today goes on.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host Denmark\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Mette Frederiksen\uc2  at the White House at 1.30pm eastern time, then Super Bowl Champions the \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  three hours later.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will talk to reporters, who will talk back to her, at 1.45pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There were no survivors from a plane that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/04/sonic-boom-from-us-military-aircraft-rattles-washington-dc-residents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed in Virginia on Sunday}}}\uc2  after flying over Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s restricted airspace, causing the military to scramble jets and a sonic boom heard across the region.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230605ej65001h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
