\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  fund anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  lawmakers through complex shell game\b0\par\par\uc2 Nick Robins-Early \par \uc2 964 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2023\par 13:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Blue-chip companies gave to Republican group funneling money to lawmakers who overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ban veto in North Carolina\par \par \uc2 As North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is due to come into effect on 1 July, an analysis from the non-profit Center for Political Accountability (CPA) shows several major corporations donated large sums to a Republican political organization which in turn funded groups working to elect anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  state legislators.\par \par \uc2 The Republican State Leadership Committee (RSLC) received donations of tens of thousands of dollars each from corporations including \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , \uc2 Intuit\uc2 , \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  last year, the CPA\u8217\'20\'19s analysis of \uc2 IRS\uc2  filings shows. The contributions were made in the months after Politico published a leaked supreme court decision indicating that the court would end the right to nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  contributed $45,000 to the RSLC after the leak of the draft decision, according to the CPA\u8217\'20\'19s review of the tax filings. Others contributed even more in the months after the leak, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2  ($50,000), \uc2 Intuit\uc2  ($100,000) and \uc2 Comcast\uc2  ($147,000).\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  did not respond to requests for comment. An \uc2 Intuit\uc2  spokesperson pointed out that the company also donates to Democratic political organizations, and that \u8220\'20\'1Cour financial support does not indicate a full endorsement of every position taken by an individual policymaker or organization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Intuit\uc2  is non-partisan and works with policymakers and leaders from both sides of the aisle to advocate for our customers,\u8221\'20\'1D an \uc2 Intuit\uc2  spokesperson said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe engagement with policymakers is essential to a robust democracy and political giving is just one of the many ways \uc2 Intuit\uc2  engages on behalf of its customers, employees, and the communities it serves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  spokesperson pointed to the company\u8217\'20\'19s policy that donations to so-called 527 organizations such as the RSLC come with the caveat that they only be used for operational and administrative purposes, not to support any candidates or ballot initiatives. The CPA, meanwhile, argues that since the RSLC\u8217\'20\'19s operations are explicitly designed to support candidates and ballot initiatives, such a policy is a distinction without a difference.\par \par \uc2 Although these companies did not directly give these vast sums to North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers, the CPA\u8217\'20\'19s analysis is a case study in how corporate contributions to organizations such as the RSLC can end up being funneled into anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  causes. When Republican state legislators successfully {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/north-carolina-abortion-ban-veto-override"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned a veto}}}\uc2  from the Democratic governor last month to pass the upcoming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, nine of lawmakers voting to overturn the veto had received campaign contributions from a group with links to the RSLC.\par \par \uc2 The RSLC, which works to elect Republican lawmakers and promote rightwing policies at the state level, is at the top of a chain of spending and donations which eventually connected to rightwing candidates in North Carolina. This type of spending, which relies on channeling money through various third-party groups from larger organizations, is a common part of modern political campaign financing.\par \par \uc2 Companies need to know where their money is ending up\par \par \uc2 Bruce Freed of the Center for Political Accountability\par \par \uc2 In this case, the RSLC gave $5m to the Good Government Coalition political organization between June and November last year, which in turn gave $6.45m to the rightwing political group Citizens for a Better North Carolina. Finally, that organization gave $1m in independent expenditures to support nine anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  state lawmakers who later voted to overturn the governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill.\par \par \uc2 These donations are evidence that corporations are proving to be complicit in the broader movement to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the CPA non-profit argues, even as many of these companies publicly tout women\u8217\'20\'19s empowerment and employee access to healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCompanies need to know where their money is ending up,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bruce Freed, the president of the CPA. \u8220\'20\'1CThis should be a lesson \u8211\'20\'13 a lesson that they should have taken a while ago but that frankly is driven home right now with what has been happening in North Carolina.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several of the companies, including \uc2 Intuit\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/abortion-companies-travel-expenses.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made statements}}}\uc2  last year offering to cover healthcare costs for employees who needed to travel out of state for medical procedures, in some cases explicitly mentioning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an example. \uc2 Google\uc2  sent an email to employees acknowledging that Roe v Wade had been overturned and informed them about options for relocating to \uc2 Google\uc2  offices in different states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEquity is extraordinarily important to us as a company, and we share concerns about the impact this ruling will have on people\u8217\'20\'19s health, lives and careers,\u8221\'20\'1D the email stated.\par \par \uc2 The companies which donated to the RSLC are also large donors to Democratic political groups, and tech giants such as \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  tend to spend millions each year more broadly on lobbying efforts.\par \par \uc2 The RSLC, whose board members include former lawmakers, governors and White House advisers such as Karl Rove, boasts on its website that it spent more than $45m on supporting Republican candidates during the 2021 and 2022 election cycle.\par \par \uc2 In addition to North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, South Carolina also passed a bill last week that would criminalize most abortions at six weeks into a pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 generally a period before people know they are pregnant. A state judge issued a temporary halt on the ban within hours of Governor \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  signing it into law, and it will now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/south-carolina-abortion-ban-state-supreme-court-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 be reviewed}}}\uc2  by the state supreme court.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is scheduled to go into effect on 1 July, drastically curtailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as many other southern states have passed near total bans.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230603ej63001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
