\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 House passes debt ceiling bill just days before deadline \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh and Maya Yang \par \uc2 9,399 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2023\par 03:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bill has reached the crucial 218 threshold to pass \u8211\'20\'13 though some Republicans may attempt to derail the process\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Today in summay\par \par \uc2 The House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/debt-ceiling-final-vote-house-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  passed a debt limit }}}\uc2  deal with bipartisan support, just days before the US is set to run out of money to keep paying its bills. Now, the Senate will take up the debt limit deal \u8211\'20\'13 and both the Democratic and Republican leaders have said they want to get it passed.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was captured on tape acknowledging that he kept a classified Pentagon document regarding a potential attack on Iran, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/05/31/politics/trump-tape-classified-document-iran-milley/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\uc2  According to report, federal prosecutors obtained the recording which was made during a meeting in summer 2021 at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey. Sources familiar with the matter told CNN that Trump made comments that suggested that he would like to share the information but that he was aware of his post-presidency limitations surrounding classified records.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll}}}\uc2 , released a week after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign announcement, shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a narrowing lead. The Florida governor shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get too excited, though: Morning Consult {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 puts}}}\uc2  the former president up by 34 points, 56%-22% and notes that though \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s lead has shrunk \u8230\'20\'26 by 10 points \u8230\'20\'26 since mid-May, much of that dip came before DeSantis officially began his bid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Iowa yesterday, the Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WillFiteForYou/status/1663693115419443202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used}}}\uc2  as his walkout music a song long used for the same purpose by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hulkhogan.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hulk Hogan}}}\uc2 , one of the most famous names in wrestling. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s recent memoir is called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/26/the-courage-to-be-free-review-ron-desantis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Courage to be Free}}}\uc2 . At 44, the Florida governor is a member of Gen X whose childhood coincided with Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s heyday as a star of World Wrestling Entertainment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is expected to launch his 2024 presidential bid within the next two weeks, The Messenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/former-vice-president-mike-pence-to-launch-campaign-for-white-house-within-two-weeks-exclusive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\uc2  The outlet reports that Pence is scheduled to headline a CNN town hall, in Des Moines, Iowa (a crucial early-voting state) on 7 June. Four Republicans familiar with the matter told The Messenger that Pence\u8217\'20\'19s team have begun ramping up their outreach two weeks ago and have told supporters that his presidential campaign launch is imminent and is set to take place in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Seems the Senate won\u8217\'20\'19t be wasting any time to get the process going\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 enltrMOMENTS AGO: Sen. Majority Leader Schumer arrived back at the Capitol and headed toward his office.\par \par \uc2 His office tells me {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scrippsnews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @scrippsnews}}}\uc2  the Leader will take steps to begin consideration of the Fiscal Responsibility Act TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nathaniel Reed (@ReedReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReedReports/status/1664086872669188100?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Republican minority leader, is echoing Kevin McCarthy and other Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 line that this deal was a big win for their party \u8211\'20\'13 because Republicans brought \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to the negotiating table after he\u8217\'20\'19d originally said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get involved.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 unity forced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  to negotiate with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerMcCarthy}}}\uc2  and agree to cut government spending. Tonight\u8217\'20\'19s passage of the Fiscal Responsibility Act is an important step in the right direction. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s turn to pass this agreement without delay.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1664081545945071618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 1, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 That sort of messaging will likely continue. Senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , a Republican from Utah who was seen on the House floor, has already indicated he\u8217\'20\'19ll try to push through amendments and derail the bills passage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Tonight, the House took a critical step forward to prevent a first-ever default and protect our country\u8217\'20\'19s hard-earned and historic economic recovery,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in a statement reacting to the news.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 This budget agreement is a bipartisan compromise. Neither side got everything it wanted. That\u8217\'20\'19s the responsibility of governing. I want to thank Speaker McCarthy and his team for negotiating in good faith, as well as Leader Jeffries for his leadership.This agreement is good news for the American people and the American economy. It protects key priorities and accomplishments from the past two years, including historic investments that are creating good jobs across the country. And, it honors my commitment to safeguard Americans\u8217\'20\'19 health care and protect Social Security, Medicare, and Medicaid.\par \par \uc2 I urge the Senate to pass it as quickly as possible so that I can sign it into law, and our country can continue building the strongest economy in the world.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Ultimately the bill has passed with 314 votes.\par \par \uc2 More Democrats (165) than Republicans (149) supported the measure \u8211\'20\'13 something the rightwing may use as evidence that the bill was a bad deal for their side. Indeed, the Republican opposition to the bill is much louder than that of progressive Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The progressive caucus chair, \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  said the bill contained measures progressives were \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously concerned about\u8221\'20\'1D like work requirement exemptions, and some have indicated that they won\u8217\'20\'19t support it for that reason. Other progressives however, reluctantly supported the bill as a way to avoid catastrophic default. Underlying these conversations was the assumption that there would be enough support even without their votes for the deal to pass.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Debt limit deal passes\par \par \uc2 The bill has reached the crucial 218 threshold to pass, though members are still voting. Now it\u8217\'20\'19ll advance to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The leaders of both parties in Senate have signalled that they want to get the deal passed \u8211\'20\'13 though some Republicans may attempt to derail the process with amendments.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Members are taking a final vote\par \par \uc2 Some progressive Democrats and several right-wing Freedom Caucus members have already signalled they\u8217\'20\'19re voting against the bill, but the bill seems to have a good chance of passing tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 The debate rolls on \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 So far, members have voiced the concerns we expected them to. Moderate Republicans have talked up the deal as a major win for the party, touting historic cuts. Democrats have presented this as an imperfect, but crucial compromise to save the economy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy took the floor to make remarks ahead of an upcoming vote. He claimed that this would be the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest savings in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not quite true \u8211\'20\'13 but the White House has tactically avoided pushing back against that line, as McCarthy needs to sell this deal to his party \u8211\'20\'13 with many hard right members already in opposition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna give America hope,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  of New York, the Democratic leader, praised party members for pushing back against \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme Maga Republican efforts\u8221\'20\'1D to cut essential spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Debate begins on debt ceiling deal\par \par \uc2 The House is now debating the legislation to increase the nation\u8217\'20\'19s debt limit until January 2025.\par \par \uc2 If the debt limit isn\u8217\'20\'19t raised or suspended, Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said that the United States will run out of money to pay its bills by 5 June.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 An estimated 750,000 could lose food stamp benefits due to the new work requirements, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbpp.org/research/food-assistance/debt-ceiling-agreements-snap-changes-would-increase-hunger-and-poverty-for"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Center on Budget and Policy Priorities\uc2 , a progressive think tank.\par \par \uc2 Work requirements already exist for most able-bodied adults up to the age of 49. The bill would bump requirements for people up to the age of 54, but expand benefits for veterans and unhoused people. The congressional budget office estimates that due to those expansions, overall, more people would be protected by the benefits program.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Center on Budget and Policy Priorities\uc2  contends:\par \par \uc2 It is important to note that the overwhelming majority of people aged 50-54 who would be newly subject to the requirement are not veterans or people experiencing homelessness.\par \par \uc2 The agreement would also restrict states\u8217\'20\'19 discretion to mitigate the impact of the work-reporting requirement by reducing the cap on individual hardship exemptions and limiting carryover of unused exemptions.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that several studies have shown that the work requirements for benefits do little to boost recipients\u8217\'20\'19 employment or earnings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 US debt ceiling deal: what\u8217\'20\'19s in and out of Biden and McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s agreement\par \par \uc2 With the details of the deal now clear, here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s in and out:\par \par \uc2 Two-year debt limit suspension, spending limits\par \par \uc2 The agreement would keep non-defense spending roughly flat in the 2024 fiscal year and increase it by 1% the following year, as well as suspend the debt limit until January 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 past the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 For the next fiscal year, the bill matches Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposed defense budget of $886bn and allots $704bn for non-defense spending. It also requires Congress to approve 12 annual spending bills or face a snapback to spending limits from the previous year, which would mean a 1% cut.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the White House estimates that the plan would reduce government spending by at least $1tn, but official calculations have not yet been released.\par \par \uc2 Care for military veterans\par \par \uc2 The agreement would fully fund medical care for veterans at the levels included in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposed 2024 budget blueprint, including a fund dedicated to veterans who have been exposed to toxic substances or environmental hazards. Biden sought $20.3bn for the toxic exposure fund in his budget.\par \par \uc2 Unspent money from Covid-19 pandemic\par \par \uc2 The agreement would rescind about $30bn in unspent coronavirus relief money that Congress approved through previous bills, including federal programs for rental assistance, small business loans and broadband internet for rural areas.\par \par \uc2 The legislation protects pandemic funding for veterans\u8217\'20\'19 medical care, housing assistance, the \uc2 Indian Health Service\uc2  and developing the next generation of Covid-19 vaccines and treatments.\par \par \uc2 Funding for the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\par \par \uc2 Republicans targeted money that the federal tax agency was allotted last year to crack down on tax fraud. The bill bites into some \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  (IRS) funding, rescinding $1.4bn.\par \par \uc2 Work-for-benefits requirement\par \par \uc2 The agreement would expand work requirements attached to the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, Snap, formerly known as food stamps \u8211\'20\'13 a longtime Republican priority. But the changes are pared down from a hardline debt ceiling bill previously generated and passed in the House, which are a huge no for progressive Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Work requirements already exist for most able-bodied adults between the ages of 18 and 49. The bill would phase in higher age limits, bringing the maximum age to 54 by 2025. But the provision expires, bringing the maximum age back down to age 49 five years later, in 2030.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also won some new expanded benefits for veterans, homeless people and young people ageing out of foster care. The agreement would also make a small boost to the Temporary Assistance to Needy Families program, which gives cash aid to families with children, making it harder for states to avoid paying.\par \par \uc2 Energy projects\par \par \uc2 The deal puts in place changes in the National Environmental Policy Act for the first time in nearly four decades that would designate \u8220\'20\'1Ca single lead agency\u8221\'20\'1D to develop and schedule environmental reviews, in hopes of streamlining the process for approval for energy projects \u8211\'20\'13 both involving fossil fuels and renewable energy.\par \par \uc2 The bill also gives special treatment to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/joe-manchin-west-virginia-mountain-valley-pipeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial Mountain Valley pipeline}}}\uc2 , a West Virginia natural gas pipeline championed by pivotal Democratic senator Joe Manchin, and Republican senator \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2 , by approving all its outstanding permit requests.\par \par \uc2 Student loans\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long sought to reel back Biden\u8217\'20\'19s temporary relief on student loans during the coronavirus pandemic. Biden has agreed that the pause in loan repayments will end in late August. Meanwhile, a GOP proposal to rescind the White House\u8217\'20\'19s plan to waive $10,000 to $20,000 in debt for nearly all student borrowers is not in the debt ceiling package. The conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is due to rule next month on whether Biden has the power to waive the debt.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s left out?\par \par \uc2 House Republicans passed legislation last month that would have created new work requirements for some Medicaid recipients, but the White House successfully blocked that from the deal. Also absent is a GOP proposal to repeal many of the clean energy tax credits Democrats passed in party-line votes last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Guardian\uc2  staff and agencies\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 It is 6pm in Washington DC where House lawmakers are set to vote a final round on the debt ceiling bill tonight. Here is where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is now in recess subject to the call of the chair. The House will reconvene again at 7:15pm for one hour of debate that will be evenly divided between Republicans and Democrats before voting on the bill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was captured on tape acknowledging that he kept a classified Pentagon document regarding a potential attack on Iran, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/05/31/politics/trump-tape-classified-document-iran-milley/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\uc2  According to report, federal prosecutors obtained the recording which was made during a meeting in summer 2021 at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey. Sources familiar with the matter told CNN that Trump made comments that suggested that he would like to share the information but that he was aware of his post-presidency limitations surrounding classified records.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin McCarthy}}}\uc2  has announced that he is putting together a commission to look into budget cuts in entitlement programs. In an interview with Fox News, McCarthy said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to announce a commission coming forward from the speaker from\u8230\'20\'26both sides of the aisle. We only got to look at 11% of the budget to find these cuts. We have to look at the entire budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll}}}\uc2 , released a week after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign announcement, shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a narrowing lead. The Florida governor shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get too excited, though: Morning Consult {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 puts}}}\uc2  the former president up by 34 points, 56%-22% and notes that though \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s lead has shrunk \u8230\'20\'26 by 10 points \u8230\'20\'26 since mid-May, much of that dip came before DeSantis officially began his bid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Iowa yesterday, the Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WillFiteForYou/status/1663693115419443202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used}}}\uc2  as his walkout music a song long used for the same purpose by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hulkhogan.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hulk Hogan}}}\uc2 , one of the most famous names in wrestling. DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s recent memoir is called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/26/the-courage-to-be-free-review-ron-desantis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Courage to be Free}}}\uc2 . At 44, the Florida governor is a member of Gen X whose childhood coincided with Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s heyday as a star of World Wrestling Entertainment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is expected to launch his 2024 presidential bid within the next two weeks, The Messenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/former-vice-president-mike-pence-to-launch-campaign-for-white-house-within-two-weeks-exclusive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\uc2  The outlet reports that Pence is scheduled to headline a CNN town hall, in Des Moines, Iowa (a crucial early-voting state) on 7 June. Four Republicans familiar with the matter told The Messenger that Pence\u8217\'20\'19s team have begun ramping up their outreach two weeks ago and have told supporters that his presidential campaign launch is imminent and is set to take place in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The debt ceiling bill will become law, Republican House speaker {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin McCarthy}}}\uc2  said on Wednesday ahead of a final House vote later today on the bill which if passed, will move next into Senate. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to become law,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told reporters, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  has said that she plans to vote against the debt limit bill. \u8220\'20\'1CMy red line has already been surpassed \u8230\'20\'26 I mean, where do we start? [No] clean debt ceiling. Work requirements. Cuts to programs. I would never \u8211\'20\'13 I would never \u8211\'20\'13 vote for that,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-vote-against-us-debt-ceiling-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Ocasio-Cortez.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican representative Andy Biggs said that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned\u8221\'20\'1D about Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s speakership amid his dissatisfaction with the tentative bill.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet on Wednesday, Biggs wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m concerned about the trajectory of Speaker McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s term. The McCarthy-Biden debt ceiling deal represents a new coalition where Speaker McCarthy will go to Democrats more than his own party. That\u8217\'20\'19s concerning to me and should be concerning to the GOP conference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking with Fox News, McCarthy his concern, saying, that he is worried about the \u8220\'20\'1Ctrajectory of the term because does this represent a new coalition and a new trajectory where the speaker is going to go to the Democrats more and more to try to put forward what he thinks his agenda ought to be?\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s really concerning to me and I think it should be concerning to members of our conference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm concerned about the trajectory of Speaker McCarthy's term.\par \par \uc2 The McCarthy-Biden debt ceiling deal represents a new coalition where Speaker McCarthy will go to Democrats more than his own party.\par \par \uc2 That's concerning to me and should be concerning to the GOP conference. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0T60DIrsKd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0T60DIrsKd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep Andy Biggs (@RepAndyBiggsAZ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ/status/1663908553952841729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Transport secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  has weighed in on the debt ceiling deal debate , saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cno one\u8217\'20\'19s going to get everything they want when you have a negotiation like this\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During an interview with NBC host Chuck Todd on Meet The Press, Todd asked Buttigieg what responsibility he believes Democrats have to pass the bill for president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg replied:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, we all would have loved to see a clean bill that separated the budget conversation from the default conversation but also we\u8217\'20\'19re in a moment of divided government where no one side, no one party is going to get everything that they want\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 No one\u8217\'20\'19s going to get everything they want when you have a negotiation like this, but this is one that we believe in that we think is the right way forward that also allows us to move on to the next conversation, putting the terrible and unacceptable specter default behind us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked whether Congress and the Biden administration are \u8220\'20\'1Cmainstreaming\u8221\'20\'1D using debt ceiling as a budget negotiation tool, Buttigieg replied:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, we didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask for this situation that some of the more extreme voices in the House GOP put this country into \u8230\'20\'26 most reasonable people could agree, the best way to handle the budget negotiations is through the regular order process that the law and the Constitution set out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has promised to strip away birthright US citizenship if he gets elected into office again.\par \par \uc2 In a video posted onto social media yesterday, Trump said if he becomes president, he will sign an executive order that will make sure children of undocumented migrants \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not receive automatic US citizenship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that his order "will \u8220\'20\'1Cchoke off a major incentive for continued illegal immigration, deter more migrants from coming and encourage many of the aliens \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has unlawfully let into our country to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s reiteration of birthright removal comes 125 years after the supreme court settled the issue.\par \par \uc2 During his first presidential run he condemned the right by inaccurately saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re the only country in the world where a person comes in and has a baby, and the baby is essentially a citizen of the United States... with all of those benefits. It\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous. It\u8217\'20\'19s ridiculous. And it has to end,\u8221\'20\'1D as over 30 countries currently offer birthright citizenship.\par \par \uc2 Martin Pengelly has more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/donald-trump-birthright-us-citizenship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump reiterates pledge to scrap birthright US citizenship}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 House in recess subject to the call of the chair\par \par \uc2 The House is now in recess subject to the call of the chair.\par \par \uc2 The House will reconvene again at 7:15pm for one hour of debate that will be evenly divided between Republicans and Democrats before voting on the bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The special counsel investigating former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 presidential election results is looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s firing of a cybersecurity official whose office called the election \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most secure in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 The US special counsel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn his 2020 election defeat is examining his firing of a cybersecurity official whose office said the vote was secure, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Jack Smith, who is also investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents, has subpoenaed former Trump White House staffers as well as Christopher Krebs, who oversaw the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  (\uc2 Cisa\uc2 ) under Trump, the Times said, citing unnamed sources.\par \par \uc2 Trump fired Krebs in November 2020, days after \uc2 Cisa\uc2  issued a statement calling the 3 November election \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most secure in American history\u8221\'20\'1D, as the then-president made his unsupported accusations that the vote was rigged.\par \par \uc2 Cisa\uc2 , part of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , works to protect US elections. Krebs told associates at the time he expected to be fired.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Smith declined to comment on the Times report. Representatives for Krebs and Trump could not be reached for comment.\par \par \uc2 For more, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/trump-firing-chris-krebs-election-2020-cybersecurity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel reportedly examining Trump\u8217\'20\'19s firing of cybersecurity official}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 The debt ceiling bill has passed the first procedural hurdle in the House, with 52 Democrats bailing out the Republican lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 In addition to 52 Democrats voting yes for the rule governing debate in the chamber, 189 Republicans voted yes. Voting no were 158 Democrats and 29 Republicans.\par \par \uc2 One more hour of debate is left before the final voting round commences later tonight.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe debt limit bill clears the first procedural hurdle on the House floor, as 52 Democrats bailed out the GOP. Still come, one hour of debate and a final vote. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ujx8voQUJh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ujx8voQUJh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jamie Dupree (@jamiedupree) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jamiedupree/status/1664006417538330629?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump remarks on classified document reportedly caught on tape\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was captured on tape acknowledging that he kept a classified Pentagon document regarding a potential attack on Iran, CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/05/31/politics/trump-tape-classified-document-iran-milley/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 According to report, federal prosecutors obtained the recording which was made during a meeting in summer 2021 at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf club in Bedminster, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Sources familiar with the matter told CNN that Trump made comments that suggested that he would like to share the information but that he was aware of his post-presidency limitations surrounding classified records.\par \par \uc2 The report also cited sources saying that the meeting attendees did not have security clearance. Attendees included two people working on the autobiography of \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, in addition to former Trump aides including communications specialist Margo Martin.\par \par \uc2 According to sources, the recording is an \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant\u8221\'20\'1D piece of evidence in a potential case against Trump over his handling over classified documents following his presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  echoed similar sentiments alongside Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , saying that he will support the debt ceiling bill once it reaches the Senate chamber.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 unity gave them the upper hand, they used it to secure a much needed step in the right direction. When this agreement reaches the Senate, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be proud to support it without delay,\u8221\'20\'1D said McConnell.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWhen this agreement reaches the Senate, I'll be proud to support it without delay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  on the debt ceiling deal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/q4nebYC6s6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/q4nebYC6s6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1663919388989480960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas governor Greg Abbott has declared John Scott as the state\u8217\'20\'19s temporary attorney general following the state House\u8217\'20\'19s vote to impeach Republican attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision to impeach Paxton comes as a result of years of allegations including corruption, bribery, unfitness for office and abuse of public trust.\par \par \uc2 According to the Texas Tribune, investigators testified at the state House general investigating committee, saying that they believed Paxton wrongly used official funds and abused his authority to assist a friend and financial backer.\par \par \uc2 In response to the impeachment, Paxton said it was an attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Coverthrow the will of the people and disenfranchise the voters of our state\u8221\'20\'1D and that the charges are based on \u8220\'20\'1Chearsay and gossip, parroting long-disproven claims,\u8221\'20\'1D the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Abbott, who has largely been silent during the whole ordeal, said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CJohn Scott has the background and experience needed to step in as a short-term interim Attorney General during the time the Attorney General has been suspended from duty,\u8221\'20\'1D the Associated Press added.\par \par \uc2 Texas Secretary of State John B. Scott is pictured, Feb. 10, 2022, in Austin, Texas. Texas Gov. Greg Abbott on Wednesday, May 31, 2023, appointed Scott to temporarily serve as Texas' attorney general after the House of Representatives voted to impeach \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , a Republican, over allegations of misconduct and crimes. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York Republican representative Marcus Molinaro hailed the tentative bill, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Can agreement [that] will move this nation forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Fiscal Responsibility Act takes important action, not at all to punish our most vulnerable. In fact, it takes real steps to ensure those most vulnerable among us are protected and served and have access to the support that they deserve, and by the way, find their way to work.\par \par \uc2 This bill hold states like New York and others accountable for waving restrictions, expanding access, not to help the most vulnerable, but to bloat and to grow and to increase state government. Because of action states have taken, the most vulnerable are left to fend for themselves\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 States like New York increased their infrastructure, their government and leveraged federal taxpayer dollars, not to benefit those who need the help the most but to benefit state government. And this bill starts a very important step of holding states accountable\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 We have an opportunity here to make a measurable difference in the lives of those who struggle the most. And this is an effort to ensure that that happens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Texas Republican representative Chip Roy lashed out against Democrats over the tentative bill during the House debate, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t wanna hear a whole hell of a lot about what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing to devastate American families with rampant inflation, because we keep spending money we don\u8217\'20\'19t have.\par \par \uc2 To my colleagues on this side of the aisle, my beef isn\u8217\'20\'19t that I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand the struggle with the negotiators against that kind of reasoning. My beef is that you cut a deal that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been cut...\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 House of Representatives begin debate on debt ceiling bill\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives has started its debate ahead of the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s final vote on the debt ceiling bill.\par \par \uc2 We will be bringing you all the latest details.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/us-debt-ceiling-deal-explainer-biden-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excerpts}}}\uc2  from our explainer on the ins and outs of the tentative debt limit bill reached following negotiations led by House speaker Kevin McCarthy and president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Two-year debt limit suspension, spending limits:\par \par \uc2 The agreement would keep non-defense spending roughly flat in the 2024 fiscal year and increase it by 1% the following year, as well as suspend the debt limit until January 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 past the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Care for military veterans:\par \par \uc2 The agreement would fully fund medical care for veterans at the levels included in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposed 2024 budget blueprint, including a fund dedicated to veterans who have been exposed to toxic substances or environmental hazards. Biden sought $20.3bn for the toxic exposure fund in his budget.\par \par \uc2 Unspent money from Covid-19 pandemic:\par \par \uc2 The agreement would rescind about $30bn in unspent coronavirus relief money that Congress approved through previous bills, including federal programs for rental assistance, small business loans and broadband internet for rural areas.\par \par \uc2 Work-for-benefits requirement:\par \par \uc2 The agreement would expand work requirements attached to the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, Snap, formerly known as food stamps \u8211\'20\'13 a longtime Republican priority. But the changes are pared down from a hardline debt ceiling bill previously generated and passed in the House, which are a huge no for progressive Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Energy projects:\par \par \uc2 The deal puts in place changes in the National Environmental Policy Act for the first time in nearly four decades that would designate \u8220\'20\'1Ca single lead agency\u8221\'20\'1D to develop and schedule environmental reviews, in hopes of streamlining the process for approval for energy projects \u8211\'20\'13 both involving fossil fuels and renewable energy.\par \par \uc2 Student loans:\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long sought to reel back Biden\u8217\'20\'19s temporary relief on student loans during the coronavirus pandemic. Biden has agreed that the pause in loan repayments will end in late August. Meanwhile, a GOP proposal to rescind the White House\u8217\'20\'19s plan to waive $10,000 to $20,000 in debt for nearly all student borrowers is not in the debt ceiling package. The conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is due to rule next month on whether Biden has the power to waive the debt.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s left out:\par \par \uc2 House Republicans passed legislation last month that would have created new work requirements for some Medicaid recipients, but the White House successfully blocked that from the deal. Also absent is a GOP proposal to repeal many of the clean energy tax credits Democrats passed in party-line votes last year.\par \par \uc2 For full details, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/29/us-debt-ceiling-deal-explainer-biden-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US debt ceiling deal: what\u8217\'20\'19s in and out of Biden and McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s agreement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma supreme court ruled on Wednesday that two state laws banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional, but the procedure remains illegal in the state in most cases.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 In a 6-3 ruling, the high court said the two bans are unconstitutional because they require a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D before a doctor can perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The court said this language conflicts with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-oklahoma-ban-overturns-supreme-court-7fd43143fa0580460e09a9796ec30a82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous ruling it issued}}}\uc2  in March. That ruling found the Oklahoma Constitution provides an \u8220\'20\'1Cinherent right of a pregnant woman to terminate a pregnancy when necessary to preserve her life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The laws struck down Wednesday both included a civil-enforcement mechanism that allowed citizens to sue someone who either performed or helped someone perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions today on SB 1603 and HB 4327, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s 1910 law prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains in place,\u8221\'20\'1D Oklahoma Attorney General Gentner Drummond said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CExcept for certain circumstances outlined in that statute, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still unlawful in the state of Oklahoma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy announces commission to look into cuts to entitlement programs\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy has announced that he is putting together a commission to look into budget cuts in entitlement programs.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Fox News, McCarthy said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was elected to help lead this nation. So the first thing we did, open the House up. The bills, you get to see them before you ever vote on them and now we\u8217\'20\'19re cutting\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to announce a commission coming forward from the speaker from\u8230\'20\'26both sides of the aisle. We only got to look at 11% of the budget to find these cuts. We have to look at the entire budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked why the entire budget was not seen, McCarthy said that president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwalled of all the others,\u8221\'20\'1D adding, \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority driver of the budget is mandatory spending. It\u8217\'20\'19s Medicare, Social Security, interest on the debt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker Kevin McCarthy announces he is assembling \u8220\'20\'1Ca commission\u8221\'20\'1D to look at potential cuts in entitlement programs:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president walled off all the others. The majority driver of the budget is mandatory spending. It\u8217\'20\'19s Medicare, Social Security, interest on the debt.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vm3jUuL6fO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vm3jUuL6fO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1663935439873404929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lead over DeSantis narrows slightly, poll suggests\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new poll}}}\uc2 , released a week after \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign announcement, shows \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a narrowing lead.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get too excited, though: Morning Consult {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 puts}}}\uc2  the former president up by 34 points, 56%-22% and notes that though \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s lead has shrunk \u8230\'20\'26 by 10 points \u8230\'20\'26 since mid-May, much of that dip came before DeSantis officially began his bid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , yet to announce his bid, took third in the poll, with a less-than-whopping 5% support, one point ahead of Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, another declared contender, was a point further back. Asa Hutchinson, also declared, attracted a princely 1% support. \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , whose announcement next week was trailed today, must be content with his unknowable share of the 1% who plumped for \u8220\'20\'1C Someone else \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Other interesting primary findings from Morning Consult, some of them perhaps in the straw-clutching lane of the race:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott is struggling to get anyone to hear anything about his candidacy, with 56% of respondents saying they\u8217\'20\'19d heard nothing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 That said, those who had heard something about the South Carolina senator were 31 points more likely to have heard something positive than negative.\par \par \uc2 In terms of the general election last year, the poll contains a mild rejoinder for DeSantis, who while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2023/may/31/debt-ceiling-vote-house-republicans-mccarthy-biden-live-updates?page=with:block-64774e708f08b007454b7570#block-64774e708f08b007454b7570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 channeling his inner Hulk Hogan}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/ron-desantis-fox-news-interview-destroy-leftism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claiming}}}\uc2  to be ready to \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy leftism in this country\u8221\'20\'1D has also said only he can beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBiden leads DeSantis, 43% to 40%, in a hypothetical general election matchup,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.morningconsult.com/trackers/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Morning Consult says}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile Trump is tied against the incumbent Democrat. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s standing against Biden has improved five points since the beginning of May, while DeSantis has hovered around the same place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has said that once the debt ceiling reaches the Senate, he will bring it to the floor as soon as possible, Reuters reported on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In a letter addressed to his fellow lawmakers, Schumer wrote, \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the bill passes the House, I will move to immediately begin consideration of the agreement in the Senate. Due to the time it may take to process the legislation in the Senate without cooperation, Senators should prepare for potential Friday and weekend votes,\u8221\'20\'1D the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4024512-schumer-warns-debt-limit-debate-may-stretch-right-up-to-june-5-deadline/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports. }}}\par \par \uc2 He went on to warn senators of the 5 June deadline, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CAs you are aware, Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  has notified Congress that the United States will no longer be able to meet all of its obligations on time by June 5.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Republican Utah senator tweeted last week that he will do everything in his power to delay the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will use every procedural tool at my disposal to impede a debt-ceiling deal that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t contain substantial spending and budgetary reforms. I fear things are moving in that direction. If they do, that proposal will not face smooth sailing in the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrI will use every procedural tool at my disposal to impede a debt-ceiling deal that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t contain substantial spending and budgetary reforms. I fear things are moving in that direction. If they do, that proposal will not face smooth sailing in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  (@BasedMikeLee) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BasedMikeLee/status/1661716721575804928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has lashed out at his former White House press secretary over \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong\u8221\'20\'1D poll numbers, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4027450-trump-slams-his-former-press-secretary-kayleigh-mcenany/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports. }}}\par \par \uc2 In a post on his social media platform Truth Social, Trump wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKayleigh \u8216\'20\'18Milktoast\u8217\'20\'19 McEnany just gave out the wrong poll numbers on FoxNews. I am 34 points up on DeSanctimonious, not 25 up,\u8221\'20\'1D using a nickname he made for Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , his current chief opponent in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments come after McEnany said on Fox News that according to polling in Iowa, DeSantis was \u8220\'20\'1Cclosing the gap\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump. It remains unclear which poll McEnany was referring to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile 25 is great, it\u8217\'20\'19s not 34\u8230\'20\'26 She knew the number was corrected upwards by the group that did the poll. The RINOS & Globalists can have her. FoxNews should only use REAL Stars!!!\u8221\'20\'1D added Trump, referring to Republicans In Name Only, a pejorative used to describe Republicans who are seen as insufficient to the GOP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis channels his inner Hulk (Hogan)\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Iowa yesterday, the Republican presidential hopeful \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WillFiteForYou/status/1663693115419443202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used}}}\uc2  as his walkout music a song long used for the same purpose by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hulkhogan.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hulk Hogan}}}\uc2 , one of the most famous names in wrestling.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Fritz Nordengren/ZUMA Press Wire/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Lyrics to Real American by Rick Derringer include \u8220\'20\'1CI am a real American/ Fight for the rights of every man\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got something deep inside of me/ Courage is the thing that keeps us free\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s recent memoir is called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/26/the-courage-to-be-free-review-ron-desantis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Courage to be Free}}}\uc2 . At 44 the Florida governor is a member of Gen X whose childhood coincided with Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s heyday as a star of World Wrestling Entertainment.\par \par \uc2 However, further reading suggests DeSantis may be advised to consider changing his tune.\par \par \uc2 In March, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abrahamriesman.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Abraham Josephine Riesman}}}\uc2  , author of Ringmaster: \uc2 Vince McMahon\uc2  and the Unmaking of America, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/03/24/trump-wrestling-mcmahon-villain-election-00088590"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussed with Politico}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CHow Pro Wrestling Explains Today\u8217\'20\'19s GOP\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The interview focused on the long relationship between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and McMahon, the \uc2 WWE\uc2  owner, and how it shaped Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political persona. But the piece also contained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/03/24/trump-wrestling-mcmahon-villain-election-00088590"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussion}}}\uc2  of how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s primary battle with DeSantis might be thought of in wrestling terms.\par \par \uc2 Politico said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt might be more useful, Riesman suggests, to think in terms of roles: heroes and villains \u8211\'20\'13 in industry lingo, faces and heels \u8211\'20\'13 and the fluidity of such positioning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked \u8220\'20\'1Cwho\u8217\'20\'19s the face and who\u8217\'20\'19s the heel?\u8221\'20\'1D in Trump v DeSantis, Riesman said that to Republicans, they were two faces.\par \par \uc2 But she also said that in 1990, when DeSantis was 11, \u8220\'20\'1CVince executed a very risky maneuver, which was that he had in his biggest match of the year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfqV3xI8l_s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the main event at WrestleMania}}}\uc2 , the two faces going against each other.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHogan and [ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wwe.com/superstars/ultimatewarrior"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Ultimate] Warrior}}}\uc2  were both faces. And Hogan was the champ and Warrior was an up-and-comer who was very popular. And they were going to have this match. And it was mind-blowing for fans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHogan and Warrior, right after that, both of them \u8211\'20\'13 their careers tanked.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some say DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is already tanking, his polling numbers falling while Trump capitalises on unprecedented legal jeopardy to fire up supporters. Trump leads most polling averages by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 30 points}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Clive, Iowa on Tuesday, DeSantis took a tentative jab at Trump over attacks about his handling of Covid, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to fight back. Hell, his whole family moved to Florida under my governorship. Are you kidding me?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One attendee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/desantis-trump-iowa-2024-president-republican-7be1c1d07c267b0ccdee6571891a50ac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Associated Press}}}\uc2  she voted for Trump twice but could switch.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is a \u8220\'20\'1Clittle softer\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmore appealing to the masses\u8221\'20\'1D, said Kim Riesberg, 59, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CAt some point, I would like to see them on the same team.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Riesman had a warning for such voters. Hulk v Warrior, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwas kind of the last gasp of that era \u8230\'20\'26 because it sort of broke the system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFans had to pick a side. You can\u8217\'20\'19t just cheer for both guys. You have to cheer for one. And that means somebody is getting written out of the story. Someone has to lose. Someone has to look bad in your eyes. And that kind of confusion [can be] very damaging to \u8230\'20\'26 both participants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has nominated a highly decorated Marine officer who has been involved in the transformation of the force to be the next Marine Corps commandant.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 The nomination of Gen. Eric Smith, now the assistant commandant, had been widely expected and has been forwarded to the Senate. The current top Marine, Gen. David Berger, is wrapping up his four-year term and preparing to retire.\par \par \uc2 Smith, a career infantry officer, has commanded at every level, serving multiple tours in Afghanistan and Iraq, including time in Fallujah and Ramadi during heavy combat in 2004 and 2005 in Operation Iraq Freedom. He later was the senior military adviser to Defense Secretary \uc2 Ash Carter\uc2  and in in 2019 took over as the deputy commandant for combat development.\par \par \uc2 In that post, Smith worked with \uc2 Berger\uc2  on a broad campaign to transform the Marine Corps to better be able to fight amphibious wars in the Pacific after years of battling terrorist groups in the Middle East. The plan was lauded by many in the Pentagon and Congress as a critical way for the Marines to prepare for a potential conflict with China.\par \par \uc2 Smith and Berger argued that the changes will improve the Marine Corps\u8217\'20\'19 ability to fight in contested areas, particularly within striking range of an enemy. That element is critical in the Indo-Pacific, where thousands of U.S. and allied forces are easily within missile \u8212\'20\'14 or even rocket \u8212\'20\'14 range of both China and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 But some of the moves, including the transfer of Marine tanks to the Army, triggered sharp criticism from a group of retired Marine generals.\par \par \uc2 Gen. Eric Smith is shown in this undated handout photo provided by the U.S. Dept. of Defense. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has nominated a highly decorated Marine officer who's been involved in the transformation of the force to be the next commandant of the Marine Corps. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  has hailed the tentative debt ceiling bill and president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in a news conference ahead of the House\u8217\'20\'19s vote on the bill.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, Jeffries said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome things that were incredibly important to the American people, all of which were on the chopping block because of the extreme MAGA Republicans and their ransom demands\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 But because president Biden held the line, some very important things were protected in this resolution. President Biden protected social security\u8230\'20\'26Medicare\u8230\'20\'26Medicaid\u8230\'20\'26veterans\u8230\'20\'26the Inflation Reduction Act\u8230\'20\'26the clean energy tax credits that will be transformational\u8230\'20\'26billions of dollars in funding to combat environmental injustice. And president Biden protected the American people from the types of devastating cuts proposed by right-wing extremists that would have hurt millions of everyday Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Minority Leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  expressed his support for the debt ceiling bill expected to go up for a vote Wednesday, crediting Pres. Biden with negotiating a deal that helps protect Social Security, Medicare, veterans\u8217\'20\'19 benefits, and more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EFFXUawwy6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EFFXUawwy6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1663930760745701376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  urges Democrats to vote for bill\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  has urged divided Democratic lawmakers to vote for the debt ceiling bill, a source familiar with the matter told CNN correspondent Manu Raju.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn closed meeting with WH officials this morning, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  strongly urged the divided Democratic caucus to back the debt ceiling bill, according to a person in the room. Dem votes will be needed to pass the bill\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1663914731189436425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former vice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to launch presidential bid: reports\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  is expected to launch his 2024 presidential bid within the next two weeks, The Messenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/politics/former-vice-president-mike-pence-to-launch-campaign-for-white-house-within-two-weeks-exclusive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 In a screenshot of an email sent by former Arizona Republican gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake to delegates of the Georgia Republican Party, Lake wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  was originally slated but has been forced to re-schedule because of a televised national town hall at which he will be making an announcement regarding his future plans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The outlet reports that Pence is scheduled to headline a CNN town hall, in Des Moines, Iowa (a crucial early-voting state) on June 7.\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer GOP Arizona gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake, who is weighing a 2024 Senate bid, will headline the Georgia GOP convention's Friday night event. She has refused to concede her narrow election defeat, and she's become a favorite among Trump supporters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oSSbfewIeG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oSSbfewIeG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1663897443610554372?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Four Republicans familiar with the matter told The Messenger that Pence\u8217\'20\'19s team have begun ramping up their outreach two weeks ago and have told supporters that his presidential campaign launch is imminent and is set to take place in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 Should Pence join the race, he will be facing off against several Republican heavyweights including his former boss and current chief contender \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  began his presidential campaign in Iowa yesterday, telling a crowd of several hundred reporters:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe tired dogmas of the past are inadequate for a vibrant future. We must look forward, not look backwards,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must have the courage to lead, and we must have the strength to win, because the stakes couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be higher,\u8221\'20\'1D Des Moines Register {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/elections/presidential/caucus/2023/05/30/desantis-kicks-off-2024-campaign-in-iowa-the-stakes-couldnt-be-higher/70268146007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports. }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish the elites in Washington, D.C., would take a page out of the Iowa playbook, but instead, they have ignored what works and they have continued to plunge this nation into the abyss,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Iowa comes weeks after he visited the crucial early-voting state earlier this month after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/13/desantis-secures-endorsements-on-visit-to-iowa-in-preparation-for-likely-2024-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secured}}}\uc2  37 endorsements from Republican Iowa state senators and representatives.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 As a result of a state supreme court ruling that allows partisan gerrymandering, North Carolina residents will likely be put into congressional districts that will be in favor of GOP, despite the state having less registered Republicans than Democrats and unaffiliated voters.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Walton reports:\par \par \uc2 The ruling will permit the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature, which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/05/1168246535/north-carolina-democrats-republicans-tricia-cotham-abortion-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controlled by Republican supermajorities}}}\uc2  in both chambers, to draw new congressional district maps in advance of the 2024 election. North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation is likely to go from its current even split to 10-4 or 11-3 in favor of Republicans, despite the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vt.ncsbe.gov/RegStat/Results/?date=05%2F13%2F2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 having fewer registered Republicans}}}\uc2  than either Democrats or unaffiliated voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard for me to think of a more consequential decision,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Cooper, a political science professor at \uc2 Western Carolina University\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/04/north-carolina-supreme-court-redistricting-maps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In February 2022}}}\uc2 , the court had ruled that maps drawn for partisan advantage by GOP lawmakers in 2021 were \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional beyond a reasonable doubt\u8221\'20\'1D, and North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 elections were held using district lines {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumlocalnews.com/nc/charlotte/news/2022/02/23/ruling-coming-on-replacement-north-carolina-redistricting-maps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawn by a panel of court-appointed experts}}}\uc2 . Those districts resulted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govtrack.us/congress/members/NC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a congressional delegation}}}\uc2  of seven Democrats and seven Republicans, mirroring the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://er.ncsbe.gov/?election_dt=11/03/2020&county_id=0&office=FED&contest=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 roughly even split of state voters}}}\uc2  between Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 But elections for the supreme court itself, also conducted in 2022, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailytarheel.com/article/2022/11/city-nc-supreme-court-2022-election-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 switched its makeup}}}\uc2  from a 4-3 Democratic-Republican split to 5-2 in favor of the GOP. The new Republican majority agreed to take up the gerrymandering case again \u8211\'20\'13 an unusual move, as the court had previously agreed to rehearings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/north-carolina-voting-rights-cases-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just twice over 30 years}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23792068-harpervhall042823"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the previous decision}}}\uc2 , with both Democrats in dissent.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-controlled legislature now has no legal barrier to creating congressional lines that concentrate Democratic voting power in a handful of districts, thus tilting the scales for GOP candidates in more parts of the state.\par \par \uc2 For more, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/north-carolina-gerrymander-republicans-2024-us-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s gerrymandered districts set stage for 2024 Republican wins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  is expected to announce his presidential bid next Tuesday, Axios reports.\par \par \uc2 Christie, who will be joining a race including former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , is expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/chris-christie-2024-presidential-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deliver }}}\uc2  his announcement at a 6.30pm town hall at Saint Anselm College in Manchester, New Hampshire.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/05/31/chris-christie-presidential-campaign-2024-gop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to }}}\uc2  an adviser, Christie, a former Trump ally, will be delivering a \u8220\'20\'1Ca non-traditional campaign that is highly focused on earned media, mixing it up in the news cycle and engaging Trump\u8230\'20\'26 Will not be geographic dependent, but nimble.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former New Jersey governor, in New Hampshire in April. Photograph: Charles Krupa/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another far-right Republican lawmaker who condemned the tentative bill is Colorado representative \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a video posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  yesterday, Boebert said the debt limit deal is bad for the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bill Biden negotiated fuels inflation, adds trillions to our debt and leaves a blank check for more of the same nonsense I came here to stop. I am not for an unlimited debt ceiling increase,\u8221\'20\'1D said Boebert.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am voting no,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I am pushing right now to make sure this new bill is allowed to be debated and amended, if not killed entirely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe debt limit deal is a bad deal for America.\par \par \uc2 As the bill is currently presented, my vote will be NO on tomorrow's anti-deal. Unit then, I hope the House will either amend it or kill it entirely. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6vdXFsevTV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6vdXFsevTV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  (@RepBoebert) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBoebert/status/1663647166299078657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 30, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy: debt ceiling bill 'going to become law'\par \par \uc2 The debt ceiling bill will become law, Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy said on Wednesday ahead of a final House vote later today on the bill which if passed, will move next into Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s going to become law,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told reporters, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters yesterday, Republican Florida representative Byron Donalds urged Republican lawmakers to vote against the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo my Republican colleagues, do not vote for this bill\u8230\'20\'26 Your voters back home are going to look at you and say, \u8216\'20\'18Why did you vote for a bill that keeps all of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies in place and all you did was raise the debt ceiling?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrTo my Republican colleagues: DO NOT vote for this deal.\par \par \uc2 Your constituents will ask you why you voted to keep ALL of Biden's policies intact while all you did was raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 They'll ask why you didn't STAND UP & DEMAND renegotiation.\par \par \uc2 Now is the time to weigh in. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5vfLIS6EUR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5vfLIS6EUR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congressman Byron Donalds (@RepDonaldsPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDonaldsPress/status/1663707897858080768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 31, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow it\u8217\'20\'19s time for Republican members of Congress to weigh in on the negotiations. That is why I am a \u8216\'20\'18No,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  to vote against debt limit bill\par \par \uc2 New York representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  has said that she plans to vote against the debt limit bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy red line has already been surpassed \u8230\'20\'26 I mean, where do we start? [No] clean debt ceiling. Work requirements. Cuts to programs. I would never \u8211\'20\'13 I would never \u8211\'20\'13 vote for that,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-vote-against-us-debt-ceiling-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Ocasio-Cortez.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Michigan representative \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  echoed similar sentiments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4019978-liberals-and-conservatives-are-bashing-the-emerging-debt-deal-and-thats-progress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling}}}\uc2  reporters that she would \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely not\u8221\'20\'1D support a bill that includes tougher work requirements.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, an aide to a progressive lawmaker in the Congressional Progressive Caucus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/05/30/progressives-debt-ceiling-deal-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  Axios anonymously, \u8220\'20\'1CMy boss is leaning no and we think a good number of [CPC] members will follow suit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-vote-against-us-debt-ceiling-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez says she will vote against US debt ceiling deal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican-led House to hold final vote on debt ceiling bill amid far-right pushback\par \par \uc2 The House is set to convene today to hold a final vote on the debt ceiling bill amid opposition from far-right lawmakers, including members of the House Freedom Caucus who have vowed to vote against the bill (some Freedom Caucus members previously opposed House speaker Kevin McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s speakership bid in January).\par \par \uc2 The tentative deal reached by McCarthy and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would raise the debt ceiling until 2025 and includes measures such as rescinding \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  funding and expanded work requirements.\par \par \uc2 With the House scheduled to convene at 2pm today, the first round of votes is expected at 3.30pm and the last round of votes is expected at 8.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Over 20 Republicans have vowed to vote against the bill, with Pennsylvania Scott Perry, chair of the Freedom Caucus saying on Tuesday, \u8220\'20\'1CWe had the time to act, and this deal fails \u8211\'20\'13 fails completely \u8230\'20\'26 We will do everything in our power to stop it and end it now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas representative and Freedom Caucus member Chip Roy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/republicans-mccarthy-debt-ceiling-deal-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the deal a \u8220\'20\'1Cturd sandwich\u8221\'20\'1D as it did not include spending cuts demanded by far-right lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina representative and Freedom Caucus member \uc2 Dan Bishop\uc2  predicted that the majority of House Republicans will oppose the bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/us-debt-ceiling-republican-hard-right-vows-to-sink-deal-hours-before-vote-expected"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a career-defining vote for every Republican \u8230\'20\'26 This bill, if it passes, must pass with less than half of the Republican conference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, House Democratic leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  emphasized the importance of Republicans providing the majority of the 218 votes required to approve the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an agreement that, at their insistence, they negotiated with the administration,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeffries said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s our full and complete expectation that they are going to produce at least 150 votes,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Should the bill pass, it will move on to the Senate where lawmakers will have only a few days to approve it before the 5 June default deadline.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 House to hold final vote on debt ceiling bill\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. The House is expected to hold a final vote on the debt ceiling bill as opposition from far-right Republicans continue to grow.\par \par \uc2 Last weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/republicans-mccarthy-debt-ceiling-deal-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks}}}\uc2  spearheaded by House speaker Kevin McCarthy and president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  culminated in a tentative deal to raise the $31.4tn US debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters, McCarthy said that the bill was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most conservative deal we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the two-year agreement which includes spending freezes and slashing Internal Revue Service funding.\par \par \uc2 As the deal heads into a chamber vote in the Republican-led House today, more than 20 Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/4026487-here-are-the-house-republicans-who-said-they-will-vote-against-debt-ceiling-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  to vote against the deal. On Tuesday, Texas representative Chip Roy, a member of the powerful House rules committee which met to review the deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/30/us-debt-ceiling-process-deal-vote-house-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Fox News, \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the deal that we should be taking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House will convene at 2pm today, with the first round of votes expected at 3.30pm, and the last round of votes expected at 8.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  is expected to announce his presidential bid next Tuesday in new Hampshire, Axios {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2023/05/31/chris-christie-presidential-campaign-2024-gop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/31/donald-trump-birthright-us-citizenship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  his pledge to strip birthright US citizenship if he becomes president again.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with leaders of his federal emergency preparedness and response team today to receive annual briefing on extreme weather preparedness.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230601ej61000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
