\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge pauses South Carolina  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban; emerging debt ceiling agreement \u8216\'20\'18has fewer cuts than expected\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein (now) and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 5,312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2023\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Temporary block on restrictions until state supreme court can review; \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy reportedly closing in on a deal\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Talks are ongoing over reaching a debt ceiling deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470ac778f08b6593e869cd4#block-6470ac778f08b6593e869cd4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid reports}}}\uc2  that negotiators for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy are nearing an agreement that would cut some government spending while preserving many of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s priorities. Meanwhile, the GOP-led push to tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was dealt a setback in South Carolina, where a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470d2bf8f08e69f068325f7#block-6470d2bf8f08e69f068325f7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily halted}}}\uc2  a newly passed ban on procedures past the sixth week of pregnancy until the state supreme court can review it.\par \par \uc2 Here is what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Officials in \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470c9b98f08b6593e869ecc#block-6470c9b98f08b6593e869ecc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have asked}}}\uc2  lobbyists for contributions to his newly announced presidential campaign, raising ethical and potentially legal questions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas lawmakers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470c2678f08e69f068324ca#block-6470c2678f08e69f068324ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could as soon as today}}}\uc2  oust the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general over an array of misconduct.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, Republican governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  signed a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64710b728f08e69f06832861#block-64710b728f08e69f06832861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curtailing}}}\uc2  children\u8217\'20\'19s access to information about gender and sexuality in schools.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No matter how the debt limit standoff is resolved, the United States is on a worrying financial path, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470bd418f08b6593e869df8#block-6470bd418f08b6593e869df8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a government report concludes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor Doug Burgum{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64710b728f08e69f06832861#block-64710b728f08e69f06832861"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is poised}}}\uc2  to jump into the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential field will gain a new entrant early next month, when North Dakota governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  announces his campaign for president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/05/26/republican-presidential-primary-burgum-north-dakota/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Burgum does not have much of a national profile, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how he will differentiate himself from the race\u8217\'20\'19s frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his strongest challenger, Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Burgum has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/24/north-dakota-passes-strictest-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a law}}}\uc2  banning almost all abortions in the reliably-Republican state, and another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/08/anti-trans-bill-teachers-students-north-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cracking down}}}\uc2  on transgender rights.\par \par \uc2 Despite his pursuit of rightwing policies typical of Republican governors nationwide, Burgum {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inforum.com/news/north-dakota/doug-burgum-is-mulling-a-run-for-president-could-he-be-a-contender-in-a-party-that-loves-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complained}}}\uc2  to the editorial board of North Dakota newspaper the Forum that many Americans feel alienated from the political process. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s definitely a yearning for some alternatives right now,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just what is keeping the debt ceiling negotiators from finding a deal? Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy said earlier today that overall government spending was the biggest point of contention.\par \par \uc2 But CNN reports that \uc2 Garret Graves\uc2 , the Louisiana congressman who is McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s lead negotiators with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s deputies, said the GOP is insisting on stricter work requirements for government aid programs:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CHell no,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Garret Graves\uc2  just said to me when asked if GOP was willing to drop work requirements on social safety not programs to get a deal on debt ceiling. Issue remains a huge sticking point to avoid default\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1662152420632166404?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if he\u8217\'20\'19s willing to drop work requirements to get a deal, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CHell no, not a chance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1662155152785014794?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Studies have shown that more stringent requirements for government aid recipients to work {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbpp.org/research/poverty-and-inequality/work-requirements-dont-cut-poverty-evidence-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undercut the programs\u8217\'20\'19 effectiveness}}}\uc2 . Perhaps most importantly for the talks aimed at warding off a \uc2 US government\uc2  default, several Democrats say they\u8217\'20\'19re opposed to tightening work requirements, potentially threatening the path to enactment of any compromise that includes such provisions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s have a quick vibe check of the US Capitol, home to both behind-closed-doors negotiations that may determine whether the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy is brought to its knees by a debt default in a few days, and tour groups.\par \par \uc2 Those who lead visitors around the Capitol are maintaining their sense of humor about all this, the Associated Press finds:\par \par \uc2 enltrA Capitol Hill tour guide just walked past reporters staking out McCarthys office and said, \u8220\'20\'1COver here on your right, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see a nation on the brink of economic collapse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Farnoush Amiri (@FarnoushAmiri) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FarnoushAmiri/status/1662133707338022913?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Some of the tourists are, unfortunately, not, The Messenger reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s up, fake news,\u8221\'20\'1D random tourist tells group of journalists who\u8217\'20\'19ve been standing against a wall for hours waiting to talk to key debt limit negotiators to keep the nation informed on where talks stand on keeping the U.S. from defaulting on its debt\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nolan D. McCaskill (@NolanDMcCaskill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NolanDMcCaskill/status/1662171815827890176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of the moment a \uc2 Louisiana State University\uc2  women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball player fainted onstage at the White House:\par \par \uc2 enltrA player on the \uc2 LSU\uc2  women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team faints during a visit to the White House today honoring their national championship. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4Yfz5yEiid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4Yfz5yEiid}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1662171027634307092?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The team\u8217\'20\'19s coach told reporters on scene that the player was \u8220\'20\'1Cfine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks during an event to honor the \uc2 Louisiana State University\uc2  women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team, before someone collapsed onstage. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 At the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was in the middle of remarks honoring the \uc2 Louisiana State University\uc2  women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team for winning the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  title when someone collapsed onstage.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith was covering the event when it happened, and reports the person has been taken out of the room.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden breaks off as it appears someone is down on the podium. There are calls for water. Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything\u8217\'20\'19s OK\u8230\'20\'26 A lot of standing, I apologise.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1tWwpJ6Na1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1tWwpJ6Na1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1662165855717687303?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s OK. It\u8217\'20\'19s happened lost of times.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1662166354005196820?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPerson who fell ill is taken out of the east room. Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CLike I said, this is not the first time it\u8217\'20\'19s happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1662167125127987226?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill now on hold was approved on Tuesday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit more on what it contained:\par \par \uc2 If signed into law the bill would ban most abortions at about six weeks, a period when most people are unaware they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The Fetal Heartbeat and Protection From \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act would ban abortions at the earliest detection of cardiac activity, and, if signed into law, would set up a judicial battle over whether the bill is constitutional. The bill already passed the state house legislature with overwhelming support, and is part of a wave of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation passed or proposed throughout the country since the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/24/1102305878/supreme-court-abortion-roe-v-wade-decision-overturn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last year and eliminated the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south \u8211\'20\'13 which already has some of the most restrictive laws in the country \u8211\'20\'13 has been dramatically curtailed with new legislation in North Carolina and Florida. A series of Texas laws prohibit abortions after six weeks and make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-abortion-law-lawsuit-6346a3b98dd3ece069177f88172ce7b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performing abortions a felony}}}\uc2  punishable up to life in prison.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nick-robins-early"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nick Robins-Early}}}\uc2  reported for us on the decision earlier this week:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina passes six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban after heated debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some markets news. Traders are in a better mood.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Wall Street jumped on Friday following progress in negotiations on raising the U.S. debt ceiling, while chip stocks surged for a second straight day on optimism about artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 After several rounds of talks, U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and top congressional Republican Kevin McCarthy appeared to be nearing a deal to increase the government\u8217\'20\'19s $31.4 trillion debt limit for two years, while capping spending on most items, a U.S. official told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average was set to end a five-day losing streak, while the Nasdaq Composite Index jumped to its highest level since August 2022.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Investors were closely watching debt ceiling talks as Biden and McCarthy still seemed at odds over several issues heading into the long weekend, with the U.S. stock market closed on Monday for the Memorial Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the signs point to a deal getting done and this rally being sustained, but if we get through the weekend and we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a deal or it falls apart in some way, then we\u8217\'20\'19re going to wake up Tuesday morning to some pretty material losses,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Scott Ladner\uc2 , chief investment officer at Horizon Investments in Charlotte, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street entrance to the New York Stock Exchange. File photo. Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an amazing/excruciating time to be alive when waiting for a debt ceiling deal. Into every news vacuum a little vacillation, vacuousness and vim must rush.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a news \u8220\'20\'1Csnap\u8221\'20\'1D from Reuters, moments ago.\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING DEAL IS POSSIBLE ON FRIDAY BUT COULD EASILY SLIP INTO WEEKEND \u8211\'20\'13 BIDEN ADMINISTRATION OFFICIAL.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As we wait for more information, here\u8217\'20\'19s a brilliant tweet from a CNN reporter/producer.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe devil works hard but the Hill press corps works harder ?????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dyRCfvu6By"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dyRCfvu6By}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Haley Talbot (@haleytalbotcnn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/haleytalbotcnn/status/1662151586435432460?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are buoyant in Minnesota after a powerhouse legislative session and former US president Barack Obama has noticed and is holding the state up as an example and a fillip for his politics and party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you need a reminder that elections have consequences, check out what\u8217\'20\'19s happening in Minnesota,\u8221\'20\'1D he tweeted earlier today.\par \par \uc2 enltrIf you need a reminder that elections have consequences, check out what's happening in Minnesota. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JCMdLRantC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JCMdLRantC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1662120328275828739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Obama further tweets that: \u8220\'20\'1CEarlier this year, Democrats took control of the State Senate by one seat after winning a race by just 321 votes. It gave Democrats control of both chambers of the state legislature and the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince then, Minnesota has made progress on a whole host of issues \u8211\'20\'13 from protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and new gun safety measures to expanding access to the ballot and reducing child poverty. These laws will make a real difference in the lives of Minnesotans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And a further optimistic note.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's a reminder that, while the pace of change can often be slow, a small group of people can still help us take a giant leap forward \u8211\'20\'13 but only if we vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1662120331794841600?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Minpost.com {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/state-government/2023/05/transformational-and-also-bonkers-minnesota-legislature-ends-its-session-of-historic-spending-policy-changes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 article Obama linked to}}}\uc2  in the first tweet describes the legislative session just ended as \u8220\'20\'1Ctransformational\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbonkers\u8221\'20\'1D depending on your party.\par \par \uc2 The so-called DFL, which stands for Democratic Farmer Labor party, aka the Democrats in Minnesota, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/state-government/2023/05/minnesota-lawmakers-plan-to-solidify-courts-rejection-of-abortion-restrictions-limit-state-data-reporting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 codified \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , paid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/politics-policy/2023/04/legislators-work-out-details-of-bill-that-would-create-a-paid-family-and-medical-leave-program-in-minnesota/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 family and medical leave}}}\uc2 , sick leave, transgender rights protections, drivers licenses for undocumented residents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/state-government/2023/02/minnesota-supreme-court-state-can-bar-felons-from-voting-until-probation-ends/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restoration of voting rights}}}\uc2  for people when they are released from prison or jail, wider voting access, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/politics-policy/2023/05/will-historic-tax-cuts-do-enough-to-help-minnesotans-lawmakers-at-odds-over-tax-rebate-checks-vs-spending-on-priorities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one-time rebates}}}\uc2 , a tax credit aimed at low-income parents with kids, and a $1 billion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.minnpost.com/state-government/2023/05/minnesota-legislative-big-big-deal-spends-1b-on-affordable-housing-adds-metro-sales-tax/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investment in affordable housing}}}\uc2  including for rental assistance,\u8221\'20\'1D the publication noted.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota State Representative Leigh Finke poses for a photo with supporters before the Minnesota Senate introduces the Trans Refuge Bill at the State Capitol Building in Saint Paul, Minnesota, on April 21, 2023. - The Minnesota legislature passed a "trans refuge" bill that would guarantee legal protection for trans people coming to Minnesota from elsewhere to access medical care. "We're trying to not just say it's okay to be trans, but you can come here and be safe," said Leigh Finke, Minnesota's first openly trans legislator, who sponsored the legislation. Photograph: Stephen Maturen/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 As Republican legislatures continue their march to the right, Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s latest move is to ban teachers from raising gender identity and sexual orientation issues with students up to grade six (typically 11-years-old), and all books depicting sex acts will be removed from school libraries, under a bill Republican governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  signed today.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 The new law is among similar measures that have been approved in other Republican-dominated statehouses around the country. As with many of those proposals, Iowa Republicans framed their action as a commonsense effort to ensure that parents can oversee what their children are learning in school and that teachers not delve into topics such as gender and sexuality.\par \par \uc2 Despite the opposition of all Democratic legislators, Republicans who hold large majorities in Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s state House and Senate approved the measure in April and there was little doubt that Reynolds would sign it; she had made issues related to gender identity and sexuality a focal point of her legislative agenda this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis legislative session, we secured transformational education reform that puts parents in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat, eliminates burdensome regulations on public schools, provides flexibility to raise teacher salaries, and empowers teachers to prepare our kids for their future,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Under the new law, school administrators also would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/transgender-students-pronouns-names-ec0b2c5de329d82c563ffb95262935f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 required to notify parents}}}\uc2  if students asked to change their pronouns or names. Religious texts will be exempt from the library ban on books depicting sex acts.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and LGBTQ+ groups argued that the restrictions would hurt children by limiting their ability to be open with teachers about gender and sexuality issues and to see their lives reflected in books and other curriculum.\par \par \uc2 The law also requires schools to post online a list of books in libraries, along with instructions for parents on how to review them and classroom instructional material, and to request that any material be removed. Schools would need parental approval before they could give surveys to students related to numerous topics, including mental health issues, sex and political affiliation.\par \par \uc2 This builds on two bills that Reynolds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/reynolds-iowa-transgender-ban-bathroom-e1651a8785586274f66819dad28b471e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law}}}\uc2  earlier in the year, restricting the restrooms transgender students can use and banning gender-affirming medical care, such as puberty blockers, for people younger than 18.\par \par \uc2 Iowa's Republican Governor \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2  delivers her inaugural address in January, 2023 in Des Moines. Photograph: Charlie Neibergall/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that a judge in South Carolina {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/south-carolina-abortion-ban-state-supreme-court-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just blocked}}}\uc2  is similar to a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once cardiac activity can be detected that lawmakers there had passed in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press adds:\par \par \uc2 The state supreme court decided previously that the 2021 law violated the state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy. Legislative leaders said the new law makes technical tweaks. But judge Clifton Newman said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe status quo should be maintained until the supreme court reviews its decision. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to end up there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s law went into effect immediately after it was signed and Planned Parenthood reported that nearly all of the 75 women with appointments for abortions over the next several days appeared to be past six weeks pregnant, an attorney for the women\u8217\'20\'19s health group, Kathleen McDaniel said, who said the harm to women \u8220\'20\'1Cis happening. It has already happened.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina measure joins stiff limitations pending in North Carolina and Florida, states that had been holdouts providing wider access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 We are awaiting news of a debt ceiling deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470ac778f08b6593e869cd4#block-6470ac778f08b6593e869cd4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid reports}}}\uc2  that negotiators for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy are nearing an agreement that would cut some government spending while preserving many of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s priorities. Meanwhile, the GOP-led push to tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was dealt a setback in South Carolina, where a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470d2bf8f08e69f068325f7#block-6470d2bf8f08e69f068325f7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily halted}}}\uc2  a newly passed ban on procedures past the sixth week of pregnancy until the state supreme court can review it.\par \par \uc2 Here is what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Officials in \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470c9b98f08b6593e869ecc#block-6470c9b98f08b6593e869ecc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have asked}}}\uc2  lobbyists for contributions to his newly announced presidential campaign, raising ethical and potentially legal questions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas lawmakers{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470c2678f08e69f068324ca#block-6470c2678f08e69f068324ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could as soon as today}}}\uc2  oust the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general over an array of misconduct.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No matter how the debt limit standoff is resolved, the United States is on a worrying financial path, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/26/debt-ceiling-deal-deadline-talks-mccarthy-biden-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6470bd418f08b6593e869df8#block-6470bd418f08b6593e869df8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a government report concludes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Roe v Wade was overturned, an Indiana doctor went public with the story of a 10-year-old rape victim from Ohio who had to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, which prompted Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general to demand that the doctor be disciplined for her statements. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  reports on a new development in the case:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/indiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2  state medical board has ruled that it will allow Dr Caitlin Bernard to continue practicing in Indiana after she spoke out about a 10-year-old rape victim who traveled to Indiana for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care due to restrictions in the girl\u8217\'20\'19s own state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The doctor will not lose her license, although the seven-person board ruled that Bernard violated patient privacy laws in discussing the 10-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s case with media. Bernard was not found to have violated reporting requirements about child abuse in the case \u8211\'20\'13 another charge against her.\par \par \uc2 The board was asked by the state attorney general to discipline Bernard last summer, in a nationally watched case that has drawn accusations of being motivated by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/indiana-abortion-ruling-caitlin-bernard-medical-license"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  doctor who spoke out about child rape victim can keep license}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the debt ceiling negotiations have worn on, progressive Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/biden-14-amendment-debt-ceiling-default-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have called on}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to consider invoking the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s 14th amendment to continue paying the government\u8217\'20\'19s bills, even if no increase is agreed on.\par \par \uc2 Biden never seemed that willing to entertain the idea, and in an interview with CNN today, deputy Treasury secretary \uc2 Wally Adeyemo\uc2  confirmed the idea was off the table:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I think the president and the secretary have been very clear that that will not solve our problems now, so, yes, that is a no."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Deputy Treasury Secretary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/wallyadeyemo?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @wallyadeyemo}}}\uc2  makes it clear to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PoppyHarlowCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PoppyHarlowCNN}}}\uc2  that Biden will not invoke the 14th to solve the debt ceiling situation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nYiQQA4Jtb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nYiQQA4Jtb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1662073734318964736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was the victim yesterday of a roasting from an unusual party \u8211\'20\'13 his own son:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  accidentally insulted his father on Thursday night, mixing up his words while trying to condemn \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s closest rival for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has the charisma of a mortician and the energy that makes Jeb Bush look like an Olympian,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr said on his online show, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rumble.com/v2pymvg-desantis-botches-rollout-plus-live-with-sen-tommy-tuberville-triggered-ep.-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Triggered With Don Jr}}}\uc2 , on the \uc2 Rumble\uc2  video platform on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 Jeb Bush was a former governor of Florida and party establishment favourite when Trump Sr won the Republican primary in 2016.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, the current {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/ron-desantis-disney-culture-war-us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 governor of Florida}}}\uc2 , made his 2024 campaign official on Wednesday, with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/ron-desantis-campaign-primary-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 glitch-filled launch}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/donald-trump-jr-mix-up-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Trump has the charisma of a mortician\u8217\'20\'19: Donald Jr confuses dad with DeSantis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign heats up, there\u8217\'20\'19s still the matter of his ongoing fight with entertainment giant \uc2 Disney\uc2  over the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s approach to gay and transgender rights. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  takes a look at the feud, and what it might mean for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s White House bid:\par \par \uc2 It has become one of the most compelling \uc2 Disney\uc2  stories ever told, but so far without a happily ever after. In fact, the entrance this week of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  into the race for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/ron-desantis-campaign-primary-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination}}}\uc2  only adds gasoline to his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/09/disney-v-desantis-florida-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raging feud}}}\uc2  with the theme park giant over diversity and transgender rights.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a battle that is, conversely, both an essential ingredient to the culture war agenda DeSantis believes will win him the White House in 2024; and a headache he could well do without as he attempts to prove his credentials as a fiscally responsible conservative.\par \par \uc2 From the moment \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bosses dared to speak out in March 2022 against DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s notorious parental rights in education bill, the so-called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/04/florida-dont-say-gay-bill-children-mental-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law}}}\uc2  that outlaws discussion in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s classrooms of sexual orientation and gender identity, the governor climbed aboard a rollercoaster he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to want to get off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis is running for president and looking for issues that will appeal to potential Republican primary voters all across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Aubrey Jewett, professor of political science at the University of Central {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 , and a long-time \uc2 Disney\uc2  observer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCertainly the main reason for attacking \uc2 Disney\uc2  is he believes it will increase his name recognition and visibility in a positive way, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make a lot of sense.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/26/ron-desantis-disney-culture-war-us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Ron DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s culture war with Disney threaten his White House run?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge temporarily halts new South Carolina \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions\par \par \uc2 A judge has blocked a South Carolina law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enacted this week}}}\uc2  that bans most abortions past the six-week mark, a point at which most women are not yet aware they are pregnant, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The ruling by judge Clifton Newman is the latest complication conservative state lawmakers have faced as they move to cut off \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last year overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to restrict the procedure entirely. Newman ordered the law put on hold until the state supreme court can review it, in a ruling that came 24 hours after the law was signed by governor \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2 , the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The state now reverts to a previous law that bans abortions at about the 20-week mark.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News has announced it will host \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a town hall with Iowa voters next Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/lifestyle/fox-news-sets-trump-town-233443235.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yahoo News reports}}}\uc2 , weeks after CNN held a similar \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/10/donald-trump-cnn-town-hall-media-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and most controversial}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 event.\par \par \uc2 The 1 June event beginning at 9pm eastern time in Clive, Iowa will be pre-recorded and moderated by conservative commentator \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , and see the former president take questions from the audience.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s event was roundly criticized for serving as a platform for Trump to hurl insults at his enemies and repeat various lies, including his debunked conspiracy theories about the 2020 election. There may nonetheless be expensive consequences to the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s statements: E Jean Carroll, the advice columnist who recently won a $5m civil judgment against him, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/22/e-jean-carroll-donald-trump-cnn-town-hall-damages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing Trump again}}}\uc2  over statements he made at the CNN event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis officials ask lobbyists for campaign contributions in potential breach of state law\par \par \uc2 Officials working for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration in Florida have been asking lobbyists for contributions to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-announces-2024-presidential-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just-announced}}}\uc2  presidential campaign, a breach of political norms and potentially the state\u8217\'20\'19s laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-administration-officials-solicit-campaign-cash-lobbyists-rcna86357"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Campaign staff typically handle fundraising outreach, but the texts from people who work in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office have raised eyebrows from lobbyists, particularly those who are advocating for projects that would be funded by the state\u8217\'20\'19s budget, which DeSantis has yet to approve.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the f--- am I supposed to do?\u8221\'20\'1D an unnamed lobbyist told NBC. \u8220\'20\'1CI have a lot of business in front of the DeSantis administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is walking a very close line to what is ethical and possibly legal. It is state employees leveraging their official position to ask people whose livelihood depend on access to state government for money,\u8221\'20\'1D another lobbyist said.\par \par \uc2 While the report says the fundraising tactic is unorthodox at best, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if it is illegal. That would depend on whether the officials who sent the text messages asking for donations were using state-owned phones or were doing so while located on state property. NBC quotes an election law attorney as saying that no matter how they did it, it comes off as unsavory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt a minimum, even if they are sitting in their home at 9 p.m. using their personal phone and contacting lobbyists that they somehow magically met in their personal capacity and not through their role in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office, it still smells yucky,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawyer said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he walked into the Capitol, Kevin McCarthy reaffirmed to the press that progress has been made in debt ceiling talks, Punchbowl News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy says he thought negotiators made progress last night. Says spending is still the big issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Max Cohen (@maxpcohen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maxpcohen/status/1662104992126316544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shifting away from Washington for a moment, there\u8217\'20\'19s a significant story developing in Texas, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis}}}\uc2  reports. Lawmakers there may as soon as today impeach the state\u8217\'20\'19s conservative attorney general on the recommendation of an investigative committee that found a host of improper conduct:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , teetered on the brink of impeachment Thursday after years of scandal, criminal charges and corruption accusations.\par \par \uc2 In an unanimous decision, a Republican-led House investigative committee recommended impeaching the state\u8217\'20\'19s top lawyer on 20 articles, including bribery, unfitness for office and abuse of public trust.\par \par \uc2 The state house of representatives could vote on the recommendation as soon as Friday. If the house impeaches Paxton, he would be forced to leave office immediately. Only two officials in Texas\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 200-year history have been impeached.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/ken-paxton-allegations-texas-committee-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas panel recommends impeaching state attorney general Ken Paxton}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 However the latest debt ceiling standoff is resolved, a recent government report underscores that the United States is on an unsustainable path when it comes to accumulating debt and budget deficits.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gao.gov/assets/830/820358.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Government Accountability Office reported}}}\uc2  earlier this month that America\u8217\'20\'19s public debt will soon be growing at a faster pace than the economy, and within a decade exceed its peak reached in the aftermath of World War II. If nothing is changed by 2051, the debt could grow to more than twice the size of the economy.\par \par \uc2 What this means is that Washington will have to allocate more money for interest payments, taking funds from elsewhere and potentially harming economic growth. The report also warns that even if the US never defaults, the repeated delays and brinkmanship over increasing the debt ceiling carry their own costs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese delays could create disruptions to financial markets, and investors may require higher interest rates to hedge against increased risks, which, in turn, could increase borrowing costs. Failure to raise the debt limit in time to prevent a default would have much more dire economic and reputational consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Their deputies may be negotiating behind closed doors, but the feud over who is to blame for America\u8217\'20\'19s high levels of debt continues between Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy and the White House.\par \par \uc2 He kicked it off this morning with a tweet blaming \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for adding to the national debt:\par \par \uc2 enltrDo you have an extra $800 lying around? That's how much more you owe as your share of the national debt since January 12th\u8212\'20\'14when I first called on President Biden to negotiate.\par \par \uc2 His delay has real consequences. His default would be even worse.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1662060343466622978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 To which White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  responded:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe debt went up more than $20,000 per person during the Trump presidency. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GmyzDAWPZK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GmyzDAWPZK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1662088553805885441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 26, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Take a look at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/GFDEBTN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this graph}}}\uc2  and you\u8217\'20\'19ll notice something consistent: the national debt increasing over the past years and decades, under presidents Republican and Democratic alike.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  on the debt ceiling talks and the deal that may be taking shape:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Republican lawmakers on Thursday appeared to be nearing a deal to cut spending and raise the debt ceiling, with little time to spare to avoid a potential default that could wreak havoc on the economy and global markets.\par \par \uc2 The deal under consideration by negotiators would raise the government\u8217\'20\'19s $31.4tn debt ceiling for two years while capping spending on most items, a US official told Reuters. It would also increase funding for discretionary spending on military and veterans while essentially holding non-defense discretionary spending at current year levels, the official said.\par \par \uc2 The agreement would specify the total amount the government could spend on discretionary programs including housing and education, according to a person familiar with the talks. The two sides, who met virtually on Thursday, are just $70bn apart on a total figure that would be well over $1tn, according to another source.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/25/us-debt-ceiling-deal-house-memorial-day-weekend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Debt ceiling deal within sight as Biden and Republicans continue to negotiate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Emerging debt limit deal would cut spending by less than GOP demanded - reports\par \par \uc2 The deal \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s negotiators are closing in on would satisfy the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s demand that government spending be reduced, but by less than initially proposed, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/05/26/debt-ceiling-deal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/25/us/politics/republicans-debt-limit-talks-biden.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  report.\par \par \uc2 Spending on defense and veterans programs would be allowed to rise, while expenditures on every other aspect of government would be cut under the deal \u8211\'20\'13 but replaced by money removed from funding the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  (IRS) and other government offices, according to the reports. That would be a much less drastic outcome than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.speaker.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Limit-Save-Grow-Act.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bill Republicans passed last month}}}\uc2  that would have put government spending back at where it was in the 2022 fiscal year, and rescinded $80bn apportioned to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  in the Inflation Reduction Act to help improve its services and crack down on tax cheats.\par \par \uc2 If the new deal holds, it looks to be typical of the sorts of compromises Democrats and Republicans in Washington reach. McCarthy could claim he forced the president to cut spending, while Biden could tell his allies he protected his signature legislative accomplishments.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Debt ceiling compromise reportedly at hand \u8212\'20\'14 but passing it is another matter\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. It looks like negotiators for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy are getting close to agreeing on an outline of a deal to raise the debt ceiling through the 2024 in exchange for cutting some government spending, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/25/us/politics/republicans-debt-limit-talks-biden.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2023/05/26/debt-ceiling-deal/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that}}}\uc2  emerged yesterday. That\u8217\'20\'19ll quell fears that the standoff could lead to the \uc2 US government\uc2  defaulting on its debt for the first time in history sometime around 1 June, and likely wreck the economy. But McCarthy and Biden are only two men \u8211\'20\'13 powerful men yes, but there are 100 senators and 435 House representatives who must decide whether to vote for whatever deal they agree to or not. Expect to hear plenty from them as the agreement is fleshed out.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Unable to borrow any money, the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cash balance dipped to $49.5bn on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 less than 24 billionaires, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaileyleinz/status/1661839764880760842"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House and Senate are holding only brief sessions today, but House lawmakers are on 24-hour notice to come back to Washington during the Memorial Day holiday weekend to vote on the debt limit deal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden welcomes \uc2 NCAA\uc2  champions the Louisiana State University Tigers women\u8217\'20\'19s basketball team to the White House at 2pm eastern time, and \uc2 NCAA\uc2  men\u8217\'20\'19s basketball champions the University of Connecticut Huskies at 5pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230526ej5q001ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
