\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Indiana  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  doctor who spoke out about child rape victim can keep license\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 586 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 May 2023\par 15:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Medical board rules Dr Caitlin Bernard can continue practicing after discussing case of 10-year-old who travelled for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Indiana state medical board has ruled that it will allow Dr Caitlin Bernard to continue practicing in Indiana after she spoke out about a 10-year-old rape victim who traveled to Indiana for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care due to restrictions in the girl\u8217\'20\'19s own state of Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The doctor will not lose her license, although the seven-person board ruled that Bernard violated patient privacy laws in discussing the 10-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s case with media. Bernard was not found to have violated reporting requirements about child abuse in the case \u8211\'20\'13 another charge against her.\par \par \uc2 The board was asked by the state attorney general to discipline Bernard last summer, in a nationally watched case that has drawn accusations of being motivated by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the board weighed whether to reprimand Bernard over her alleged conduct, including whether to revoke or temporarily suspend her medical license, in a theatrical and emotional hearing that lasted several hours. During the hearing, counsel for Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Todd Rokita, repeatedly asked Bernard about her personal views in a case that was supposed to centre on privacy laws \u8211\'20\'13 asking Bernard whether she had a coat hanger tattoo on her ankle and whether she considered herself a reproductive rights advocate.\par \par \uc2 The board found Bernard violated privacy laws, and unanimously agreed that she did not violate reporting requirements, another charge against her. Bernard will now pay $3,000 in fines and receive a letter of reprimand.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike we have said for a year, this case was about patient privacy and the trust between the doctor and patient that was broken,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rokita in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat if it was your child or your parent or your sibling who was going through a sensitive medical crisis, and the doctor who you thought was on your side, ran to the press for political reasons?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When Indiana passed its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in September 2022, Bernard\u8217\'20\'19s experience and testimony was pivotal in getting rape and incest exceptions added to the law.\par \par \uc2 Dr Bernard has drawn a mixture of praise and condemnation for highlighting the child\u8217\'20\'19s case and the real-life impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 she was personally called by the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , last year, who thanked the doctor for speaking out.\par \par \uc2 Rokita initially accused Bernard of fabricating the story, and then of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indianacapitalchronicle.com/2023/05/09/bernard-to-go-before-medical-licensing-board-this-month-despite-rokita-attempt-to-delay-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exploiting the 10-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s trauma for her own interests}}}\uc2 . The attorney general then opened an investigation into Bernard\u8217\'20\'19s conduct, accusing her of breaking state law by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.in.gov/apps/pla/litigation/viewer.aspx?id=21742"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not reporting the child\u8217\'20\'19s abuse}}}\uc2  and of violating patient privacy protections. Bernard subsequently sued the attorney general, claiming he tarnished her reputation by opening a baseless investigation into her.\par \par \uc2 During questioning, Dr Bernard said she felt it was important to speak publicly about the real-life impacts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, and maintained that she never publicly spoke out about any details that could have identified the girl in the case. Her lawyers maintain that it was press statements by Rotika\u8217\'20\'19s team that intensified a media search for the 10-year-old, impacting on her privacy.\par \par \uc2 The makeup of the board for Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing has drawn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eu.indystar.com/story/news/local/2023/05/24/todd-rokita-prosecution-abortion-doctor-caitlin-bernard-medical-board-hearing/70248885007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutiny from local press}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 for including a number of members appointed by the attorney general who have donated to his campaign.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230526ej5q001uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
