\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  doubles down on rightwing agenda in glitchy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  campaign launch \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now); Chris Stein and Fran Lawther (earlier) \par \uc2 8,036 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2023\par 00:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Florida governor took swipes at the media and \uc2 NAACP\uc2  during trouble-plagued announcement Full report: DeSantis confirms he is running for Republican nomination\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Recap\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  announced his presidential bid in a glitchy, chaotic forum on \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  commemorated the tragedy in Uvalde, Texas, and called for gun control measures, one year after a gunman killed 19 students and two teachers at an elementary school.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in the Capitol, negotiations continue over raising the debt ceiling, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e33ac8f088e0216a846b7#block-646e33ac8f088e0216a846b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no breakthrough yet apparent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e1ad48f087efbd541dc69#block-646e1ad48f087efbd541dc69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested a meeting}}}\uc2  with attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and aired a litany of grievances about special counsel Jack Smith and other prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e206d8f087efbd541dca9#block-646e206d8f087efbd541dca9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be moving}}}\uc2  to curb political power in its most-populous county, which is run by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden marked Uvalde anniversary with a call for gun control\par \par \uc2 In a brief speech at the White House, the president asked: \u8220\'20\'1CHow many more parents will live their worst nightmare before we stand up to the gun lobby?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and first lady Jill Biden stand in front of memorial candles for the victims of the shootings at Robb Elementary School in Uvalde, Texas, in 2022. Photograph: \uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 He and first lady Jill Biden stood in front of 21 burning candles to honor the victims of the school shooting. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to make our voices heard, not as Democrats or as Republicans but as friends, as neighbors as parents, as fellow Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The president offered his empathy to the friends and family of those who were killed. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile everyone\u8217\'20\'19s pain is different, we like many of you have some understanding of what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to lose a child \u8211\'20\'13 on more than one occasion,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ll never be gone from your heart, they\u8217\'20\'19ll always be part of you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insistence that the glitches were due to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s popularity has not been particularly convincing.\par \par \uc2 enltrBuzzFeed exploding the watermelon hit 820,000 concurrent viewers in 2016 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EKtwBBV2j6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EKtwBBV2j6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Gara (@tomgara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tomgara/status/1661500590243864579?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe had more people join when I played Among Us ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zBoDCM0XmL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zBoDCM0XmL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1661502529207775236?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 The launch is already being panned, including by Fox News and the Daily Mail.\par \par \uc2 enltrFox News, which was snubbed for the announcement, is going after DeSantis aggressively: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/roObJO8Ac1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/roObJO8Ac1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Swan (@jonathanvswan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonathanvswan/status/1661509756396220424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrDaily Mail right now: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PNRMlsqJnu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PNRMlsqJnu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Swan (@jonathanvswan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonathanvswan/status/1661503999307046912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Musk ended by welcoming any other candidates who want to go through the same rigamarole to come through. And that\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap!\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is also expected on Fox News tonight. \u8220\'20\'1CPROGRAMMING ALERT: Want to actually see and hear \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ? Tune into Fox News at 8pm ET,\u8221\'20\'1D the network splashed on its website.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis ended by speaking about Bitcoin and ESG investments \u8211\'20\'13 niche topics that are likely to lose many followers.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, DeSantis signed a bill barring officials from investing public money to promote environmental, social and governance (ESG) goals. It was one of the farthest-reaching efforts by a Republican lawmaker to stop sustainable investing efforts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis spoke on education and immigration \u8211\'20\'13 two realms in which he has pushed unprecedented, authoritarian measures as governor.\par \par \uc2 On education:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere has not been a single book banned in the state of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis, who often repeats this lie.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pen.org/report/banned-in-the-usa-state-laws-supercharge-book-suppression-in-schools/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pen America}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2023, to comply with new laws, some Florida schools were directed to empty libraries and cover classroom bookshelves. Teachers in Manatee county and Duval county were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/2023/01/31/florida-hide-books-stop-woke-manatee-county-duval-county-desantis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  they had to have each book in their classrooms reviewed before they could go back. Martin county removed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tcpalm.com/story/news/education/martin-county-schools/2023/03/07/martin-county-schools-remove-books-for-sexual-racial-content/69968648007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozens of books}}}\uc2  after they were objected to by one person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On immigration:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou need to shut the border down,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said, vowing to follow though on his anti-immigrant policies and go further than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been able to.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Richard Luscome has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/14/ron-desantis-immigration-laws-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , DeSantis has made hardline, anti-immigrant policies a cornerstone of his gubernatorial policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 David Sacks also asked DeSantis about \uc2 Disney\uc2 , which has become the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s top foe.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1Creally been outed as trying to inject matters of sex in the programming for the youth\u8221\'20\'1D, DeSantis said. The governor\u8217\'20\'19s beef with the corporation started when \uc2 Disney\uc2 , one of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s biggest employers, publicly opposed his so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D ban. He retaliated by seizing control of \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s self-governing special district, and threatened to build a state prison near the area.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 This odd launch to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has partly become an advertisement for \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk and Sacks played off the glitches on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  as DeSantis \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking the internet\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear why \uc2 Twitter\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t anticipate 500,000 listeners for a presidential announcement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 After taking swipes at the media and the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  (which recently issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/22/naacp-florida-travel-warning-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel advisory}}}\uc2  for Florida under DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s leadership), the right-wing governor talked up \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of what \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is standing for is people should be exposed to different viewpoints,\u8221\'20\'1D said DeSantis, who has been working to ban viewpoints in classrooms across his state. He signed a bill that prohibits public school teachers in Florida from holding classroom instruction about sexual orientation or gender identity.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis also called making his Covid-era policies a \u8216\'20\'18lonely\u8217\'20\'19 time when he had to make different decisions than the rest of the country.\par \par \uc2 The governor went against public health guidance to end mask mandates early, surround himself with anti-vaccine advocates and other controversial stances. In 2021, Florida saw record-breaking surges in Covid infections, which DeSantis dismissed as \u8220\'20\'1Cseasonal\u8221\'20\'1D. It was his aggressive defiance of pandemic policies that helped him rise to national prominence, as he capitalized on anti-mask and anti-vaccine fervor rising across the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a new Twitter Spaces stream, this one with notably fewer listeners, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has finally begun to speak, reading off prepared remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am running for president of the United States to lead our great American comeback,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, reiterating lines from his announcement video. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no substitute for victory \u8230\'20\'26 we must look forward, not backwards,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  laid off scores of employees who kept the social media platform running, glitches and errors have become somewhat commonplace on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has yet to say a word, but amid all the feedback, Musk said, with more than 400,000 listeners on the stream: \u8220\'20\'1CThe servers are straining somewhat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s social media team seems to be having a bit of fun with it all:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis link works: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9PzIJkseYI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9PzIJkseYI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1661496322980028423?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The event is off to a glitchy start \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The audio line has bad feedback. \u8220\'20\'1CWe got so many people here that we are kind of melting the servers, which is a good sign,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Sacks, the Republican donor and friend of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  who is moderating the audio event.\par \par \uc2 Some have reported that their \uc2 Twitter\uc2  apps are crashing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is about to make his presidential announcement on \uc2 Twitter\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor is about to join \uc2 Twitter\uc2  owner \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in a live audio event on the site, to officially announce his bid for president.\par \par \uc2 The conversation will be streamed on Twitter Spaces, a dedicated audio streaming feature on the social media platform. Ahead of the event, DeSantis is teasing a new slogan on his campaign website: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve only just begun to fight for our Great American Comeback.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m running for president to lead our Great American Comeback. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YmkWkLaVDg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YmkWkLaVDg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (@RonDeSantis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonDeSantis/status/1661491799393964034?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, at Capitol Hill, GOP House leader Steve Scalise told lawmakers they could go home for Memorial Day weekend, with no deal on increasing the debt limit yet.\par \par \uc2 Scalise said members should be ready to come back with 24hrs notice if a deal is reached. Kevin McCarthy, meanwhile, said that a compromise had yet to be reached.\par \par \uc2 If and when there is a debt-limit deal, members will get 72 hours to review legislative text before they have to vote on it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Sierra Club Florida has joined in condemning \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , saying that he has \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinuously failed Florida\u8217\'20\'19s environment, residents, economy, and democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSierra Club Florida has consistently graded Governor DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 environmental record with \u8220\'20\'1CF\u8217\'20\'19s\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 for good reason. Rather than prioritizing the wellbeing of our people and environment, the governor and his administration have focused on culture war signaling and spending taxpayer dollars on political stunts that harm real people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Gorman, the Sierra Club Florida director. \u8220\'20\'1CDeSantis\u8217\'20\'19 constant mismanagement and lack of leadership have had a devastating impact on our state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, DeSantis signed a bill barring officials from investing public money to promote environmental, social and governance (ESG) goals. It was one of the farthest-reaching efforts by a Republican lawmaker to stop sustainable investing efforts.\par \par \uc2 Despite initially signaling a pragmatic approach toward environmental protections when he took office, the Florida governor has also signed bills that blocked coral reef protections in Key West, prevented local electrification initiatives and defined natural gas as \u8220\'20\'1Crenewable\u8221\'20\'1D energy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis changes law to ease White House run\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has just taken a small but significant step to smooth his run at the White House: he\u8217\'20\'19s signed a bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.votepinellas.gov/Candidates-Committees/Candidates/-Resign-to-Run#:~:text=The%20%E2%80%9Cresign%2Dto%2Drun%20law%E2%80%9D%20essentially%20prohibits%20an,office%20the%20person%20presently%20holds."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repealing an element of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cresign to run\u8221\'20\'1D law}}}\uc2  that would have prevented him continuing to serve as governor while campaigning for higher office.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2023/05/24/desantis-president-resign-to-run-florida-governor/?trk_msg=J01CLJOKHQB4J7MT50R34Q37KO&trk_contact=0T55GG7QPQFBVSNQ684F1F4IKC&trk_sid=VU7Q01IEOFA6MG1GCASNN5O92S&trk_link=KLLH09DO9GB4325V8RG69ISTS8&utm_email=d34169d191d0178e24f2f8ec80b8d799e8f89ec943f653069d4e1e402fad79bb&utm_source=Breaking+News&utm_medium=MG2_Newsletter&utm_term=Read+the+full+report&utm_campaign=times-breaking-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Tampa Bay Times}}}\uc2 , DeSantis put his signature on the bill just hours after filing the official paperwork earlier Wednesday formalizing his campaign for the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Last month, compliant Republicans in the state legislature passed a measure that said the resign to run restriction would no longer apply to those running for president or vice-president.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who was reelected Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor in November, would otherwise have had to resign from that office because his term would have overlapped the start of the next presidential period beginning in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovRonDeSantis?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GovRonDeSantis}}}\uc2  signs change to resign-to-run law the same day he launches presidential bid\par \par \uc2 Reporting by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jacobogles?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JacobOgles}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uzMvmPVvJi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uzMvmPVvJi}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FlaPol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FlaPol}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Florida Politics (@Fla_Pol) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Fla_Pol/status/1661478460680708097?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the second bill this month DeSantis has signed to ease himself into the campaign. On 11 May he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/05/11/politics/ron-desantis-state-travel-records-covid-mandate/index.html#:~:text=Under%20the%20new%20law%2C%20law,are%20requested%20by%20the%20governor.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a measure reducing transparency over political spending and his travel arrangements}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers and DeSantis cited security concerns to justify the law. But Democrats and transparency advocates said it was a brazen effort to keep DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s travel secret.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere a governor goes, who travels with the governor, who the governor meets with is all information of critical importance to the public. Who is influencing the governor? We need to know that,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Barbara Petersen\uc2 , executive director of the Florida center for government accountability, said at the time.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/ron-desantis-florida-laws-presidential-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Impossible to hold him accountable\u8217\'20\'19: DeSantis signs laws to ease 2024 run}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of background on DeSantis, from my colleague Maya Yang:\par \par \uc2 DeSantis became a national figure when he aggressively opposed Covid measures\par \par \uc2 Throughout the pandemic, DeSantis remained staunchly opposed to Covid-19 precautionary measures including lockdowns and mask mandates. He has also widely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/25/florida-governor-ron-desantis-vaccine-mandates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spread}}}\uc2  Covid-19 vaccine denialism. In 2021, as Florida experienced record-breaking surges in Covid-19 cases, DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/05/ron-desantis-florida-governor-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed}}}\uc2  the spikes as \u8220\'20\'1Cseasonal\u8221\'20\'1D and called the growing struggle faced by state hospitals \u8220\'20\'1Cmedia hysteria\u8221\'20\'1D. Earlier this year, DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/21/ron-desantis-covid-mandates-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a proposal to permanently ban Covid-19 mandates in the state. The governor\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive stance has since earned him a variety of nicknames online including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/05/ron-desantis-florida-governor-covid-coronavirus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPied Piper\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/politico-nightly/2021/03/18/how-ron-desantis-won-the-pandemic-492163"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeathsantis\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CDeSatan\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is waging a war against \u8216\'20\'18woke\u8217\'20\'19 culture, attacking minority groups in his state\par \par \uc2 Since becoming governor, DeSantis has launched a war against \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D culture in Florida and signed into law a slew of bills that civil rights organizations have widely condemned as violations of individual freedoms. In 2022, DeSantis approved the so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/florida-education-board-approves-expansion-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D ban which prohibits discussions of sexual orientation and gender identity in schools across all grade levels. In January, DeSantis banned African American studies from the state\u8217\'20\'19s high schools, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/19/ron-desantis-bans-african-american-studies-florida-schools#:~:text=Ron%20DeSantis%20bans%20African%20American%20studies%20class%20from%20Florida%20high%20schools,-This%20article%20is&text=Ron%20DeSantis%2C%20Florida's%20Republican%20governor,and%20%E2%80%9Clacks%20educational%20value%E2%80%9D."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  that the course \u8220\'20\'1Clacks educational value\u8221\'20\'1D. He also signed a bill approving a six-week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban in the state and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/02/ron-desantis-block-dei-program-state-colleges-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  plans to block state colleges from having programs on diversity, equity and inclusion, and critical race theory.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, who got married at Disney World, is engaged in a legal feud with \uc2 Disney\par \par \uc2 Following DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/09/disney-v-desantis-florida-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight}}}\uc2  against LGBTQ+ rights in Florida and pressure from its own employees, \uc2 Disney\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s biggest employers \u8211\'20\'13 publicly opposed the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D ban last year. DeSantis retaliated by seizing control of \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s self-governing special district near Orlando and assumed new powers which allow him to appoint members of the development board that supervises the theme park. DeSantis has proposed building low-income housing on land next to the theme parks and also touted building a state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/ron-desantis-prison-near-disney-theme-park"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prison}}}\uc2  in the area.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s police program is luring officers with violent records\par \par \uc2 As an incentive to attract police officers from other states who are frustrated by Covid-19 vaccination requirements, DeSantis launched a new law enforcement relocation program on which he has spent $13.5m to date. The program offers a one-time $5,000 bonus for new recruits. However, a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/22/ron-desantis-police-relocation-violent-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  of state documents found that among the nearly 600 officers who relocated to Florida, a \u8220\'20\'1Csizable number\u8221\'20\'1D have a slew of complaints against them or have since had criminal charges filed against them. Those charges include murder, as well as domestic battery and kidnapping.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-republican-president-candidate-facts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis: 10 things to know about the Republican White House hopeful}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the National \uc2 Association for the Advancement of Colored People\uc2  civil rights organization issued a travel advisory over \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies in Florida, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports, it\u8217\'20\'19s not stopping there:\par \par \uc2 Leaders of the National \uc2 Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP) \uc2 say its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/22/naacp-florida-travel-warning-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel advisory highlighting Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cactive hostility\u8221\'20\'1D to minorities}}}\uc2  is only the beginning of a campaign to engage voters in the state and nationally, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , prepares to launch his presidential run on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Leon Russell, chair of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , also told the Guardian that the group rejected calling for an economic boycott of the state similar to one that ended with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/storyline/confederate-flag-furor/naacp-votes-end-south-carolina-boycott-after-confederate-flag-comes-n390616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina lowering the confederate flag}}}\uc2  in 2015.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVery simply put, we questioned the effectiveness of a boycott,\u8221\'20\'1D Russell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2 , this is about the politics of the situation and so people need to buckle in and organize, and get themselves arranged to deal with elections and the consequences of the elections.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/florida-travel-warning-naacp-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NAACP says Florida travel warning is just the start of organizing effort}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 For four lonely years, \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2  was the sole Democrat elected to a statewide position in Florida as its agricultural commissioner.\par \par \uc2 That gave Fried, now the state Democratic party chair, a unique view into DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s governorship, and she apparently did not think much of what she saw.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she said after news broke of his presidential run:\par \par \uc2 enltrCountdown until Ron bows out is on.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2  (@NikkiFried) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikkiFried/status/1661448784964997125?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 24, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 But just who is \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ? Many Americans will be asking themselves that question in the months to come, as the Florida governor embarks on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-646e0c028f087efbd541dbb9#block-646e0c028f087efbd541dbb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what\u8217\'20\'19s reported to be}}}\uc2  an aggressive campaign of outreach to voters, particularly in the states that vote first in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nominating process. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  with a look at what we know about DeSantis, and what he might do as president of the United States:\par \par \uc2 The official Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s website invites visitors to \u8220\'20\'1CMeet Governor DeSantis\u8221\'20\'1D. But anyone who clicks on that option is greeted with the message \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Biography \u8211\'20\'13 coming soon\u8221\'20\'1D, along with his photo and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flgov.com/meet-governor-desantis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a big white space}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s admirers project on to that blank page the ideal of a strong chief executive, \u8220\'20\'1Canti-woke\u8221\'20\'1D warrior and consistent election winner. His detractors fill the vacuum with warnings that the Florida governor represents \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/27/opinion/desantis-trump-republican-party.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump 2.0}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump with a brain\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CTrump without the circus\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Six months ago DeSantis was being hailed as the future of a Republican party grown tired of former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s losing streak. He had offered blueprints for beating Democrats in elections and for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/ron-desantis-florida-blueprint-usa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exporting a rightwing agenda nationwide}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But after filing papers with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  on Wednesday to seek the 2024 Republican presidential nomination, DeSantis still has everything to prove about his readiness for the ultimate stage.\par \par \uc2 Florida political insiders suggest that he is undercooked and will fail the \u8220\'20\'1Clikability test\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which candidate would you rather {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/right-turn/wp/2015/04/15/who-flunks-and-who-passes-the-beer-test/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have a beer with}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have been saying DeSantis was an overpriced political stock for a year and a half,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/27/rick-wilson-lincoln-project-dismiss-trump-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rick Wilson}}}\uc2 , a Republican strategist who has been involved in more than 30 political campaigns in the state. \u8220\'20\'1CThis guy is all hat and no cattle. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have that natural verbal and political grace that you need to pull off a win against Trump, who is a powerful performer on stage.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/florida-governor-ron-desantis-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18All hat, no cattle\u8217\'20\'19: Ron DeSantis, the \u8216\'20\'18anti-woke\u8217\'20\'19 Florida governor running for president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  about the rollout of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, and what we can expect in the days to come:\par \par \uc2 The governor of Florida, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , has officially declared his candidacy for the Republican nomination for president.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docquery.fec.gov/cgi-bin/forms/C00841130/1705819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  paperwork on Wednesday with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 , ahead of a planned \uc2 Twitter\uc2  event with the owner of the social media site, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , and an interview with Fox News.\par \par \uc2 The announcement was long {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/ron-desantis-2024-presidential-campaign-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected}}}\uc2 . DeSantis won re-election in a landslide last November, published a campaign-oriented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/26/the-courage-to-be-free-review-ron-desantis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memoir}}}\uc2  in February and was widely reported to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/ron-desantis-2024-presidential-campaign-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staffing}}}\uc2  up while visiting states that will vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/13/desantis-secures-endorsements-on-visit-to-iowa-in-preparation-for-likely-2024-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early}}}\uc2  in the primary next year.\par \par \uc2 He retains support from powerful donors, has amassed significant campaign funds and is consistently a clear second to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in polling of the Republican field.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-announces-2024-presidential-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida governor Ron DeSantis announces 2024 presidential bid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has for months been hurling insults, accusations and invective at \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and today is no different.\par \par \uc2 Much of the vitriol can be found on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth social account}}}\uc2 , where over the past hour he\u8217\'20\'19s been sharing polls showing him beating DeSantis in support.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a typical Trump attack on DeSantis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110423420684156481"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from earlier today}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSanctus can\u8217\'20\'19t win the General Election (or get the Nomination) because he VOTED TO OBLITERATE SOCIAL SECURITY, EVEN WANTING TO RAISE THE MINIMUM AGE TO 70 (or more!), VOTED TO BADLY WOUND MEDICARE, AND FOUGHT HARD AND VOTED FOR A 23% \u8220\'20\'1CTAX ON EVERYTHING\u8221\'20\'1D SALES TAX. He was, and is, a disciple of horrible RINO \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 , and others too many to mention. Also, he desperately needs a personality transplant and, to the best of my knowledge, they are not medically available yet. A disloyal person!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear more from \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  later today when he officially announces his campaign on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  alongside \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats, meanwhile, are reacting with dismay to DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s entrance into the race, though it\u8217\'20\'19s far from a surprise. In a statement, \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  said the governor \u8220\'20\'1Chas pushed an extreme Maga agenda focused on ripping Floridians\u8217\'20\'19 freedoms away and now he wants to take that agenda nationwide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Harrison:\par \par \uc2 DeSantis got his start as a co-founder of the ultra-right wing House Freedom Caucus where he supported \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to end Medicare and Social Security as we know it, voted for national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, worked to repeal the Affordable Care Act, and supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax giveaways to the biggest corporations. Now, as Floridians suffer under some of the highest housing and health care costs in the nation, DeSantis has tripled down on a MAGA agenda \u8211\'20\'13 including banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making it easier for criminals to carry guns, signing laws that allowed book bans, parroting Putin\u8217\'20\'19s talking points, and bailing out huge corporations while Florida families foot the bill.\par \par \uc2 If there was any doubt \u8211\'20\'13 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s announcement turns up the volume on an already messy Republican primary. One thing is guaranteed \u8211\'20\'13 whoever makes it out will only have done so by catering to the most MAGA, right-wing Republicans in the primary.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis officially begins presidential campaign, election filing shows\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has formally filed paperwork to start his presidential campaign, the Associated Press reports, pitting him against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a host of other Republicans in the competition for the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Polls indicate DeSantis is in second place among Republican voters, but with a wide gulf between him and the former president. DeSantis is expected to publicly launch the campaign in an appearance later today on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with its billionaire owner \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley will soon get a big opportunity to promote her candidacy to Republican voters and the American public at large: a CNN town hall.\par \par \uc2 The network announced today that it will hold an event with Haley, a former South Carolina governor and ambassador to the United Nations under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on 4 June in Iowa.\par \par \uc2 The big question here is whether the town hall will go any better than the event CNN hosted earlier this month with Trump, which ended with the network criticized even by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/18/cnn-trump-town-hall-christiane-amanpour-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its own employees}}}\uc2  for allowing the former president to make personal attacks and repeat a variety of debunked lies and accusations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 While DeSantis is still gearing up to announce his candidacy later today, his rival Nikki Haley is out and about in Manchester, New Hampshire, talking about her plans for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The Republican pledged to sign a federal ban but suggested passing one would be highly unlikely without significantly more Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 The former US ambassador to the United Nations said \u8220\'20\'1Cno one has been honest\u8221\'20\'1D about how difficult a ban could be to achieve, according to AP.\par \par \uc2 The comments come amid a continuing debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  among Republicans seeking their party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 As South Carolina governor, Haley signed a ban on abortions after about 20 weeks. On Tuesday, South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Senate passed a ban on the procedure after about six weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Joan E Greve has the latest on the debt ceiling talks \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s not looking like an agreement is imminent.\par \par \uc2 She writes:\par \par \uc2 Debt ceiling talks between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and the House speaker, Kevin McCarthy, dragged on Wednesday, as negotiators met again to hash out the details of a potential deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a number of places that we\u8217\'20\'19re still far apart,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told reporters on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we can make progress today. I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping that we can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/mccarthy-biden-debt-ceiling-nearing-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McCarthy and Biden \u8216\'20\'18still far apart\u8217\'20\'19 in debt ceiling talks despite nearing deadline}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 The pressure group Accountability.US is out with a stinging statement directed at \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , over the chief justice\u8217\'20\'19s contention in remarks in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/24/supreme-court-john-roberts-highest-standards-conduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last night}}}\uc2  that the supreme court is capable of regulating its own behaviour, even after a torrent of reports about \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and his friendship with, and acceptance of gifts from, the rightwing megadonor Harlan Crow.\par \par \uc2 Kyle Herrig, president of Accountable.US, says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChief Justice Roberts sat back and watched while the supreme court corruption crisis reached a fever pitch, causing public trust in his court to plummet. Now, he\u8217\'20\'19s admitting more can be done \u8211\'20\'13 but keeps pretending he isn\u8217\'20\'19t responsible for cleaning up his own court. Americans deserve more than a few noncommittal comments behind closed doors.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Roberts himself has the power to change the ethics standards of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, but so far, he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t shown the courage. Instead of preaching to a private crowd, he should take action.\par \par \uc2 The full story is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/24/supreme-court-john-roberts-highest-standards-conduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here, meanwhile, is what the Rhode Island Democratic senator Sheldon Whitehouse had to say about the argument that Congress cannot investigate the supreme court, as Senate judiciary Democrats would like to do in the case of Thomas, because of the separation of powers in the US constitution \u8211\'20\'13 a concept cited both by Roberts and lawyers for Crow:\par \par \uc2 In a series of tweets, Whitehouse, a champion of the fight against dark money in politics, linked to Crow\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers\u8217\'20\'19 letter to Dick Durbin, the Senate judiciary chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWhitehouse/status/1661373373463535617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a ritualistic quality to these \u8216\'20\'18separation of powers\u8217\'20\'19 claims that are being made to protect Justice Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s ethics reporting problem from scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor instance, the reporting violations at issue violate a reporting statute passed by Congress, which the court has obeyed without complaint until now (see 2011 Thomas review by Judicial Conference to enforce that statute).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore: review by the Judicial Conference is by a body created by statute by Congress. The notion that Congress has no business in the Thomas/billionaire reporting mischief is belied both by the law in question and the body in question.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn all these pages of legal verbiage, the lawyers manage never to note either fact. Seriously?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 An \u8220\'20\'1Canti-fascist\u8221\'20\'1D group in Miami has been looking into the woman reportedly behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/amanda-gorman-poem-ban-florida-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning of Amanda Gorman\u8217\'20\'19s presidential inauguration poem}}}\uc2  from a Florida elementary school, and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like what it found.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://amp.miamiherald.com/news/local/education/article275671496.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami Herald identified the woman}}}\uc2  who complained about The Hill We Climb as Daily Salinas, the parent of two students at the Bob Graham education center Miami Lakes, and, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MIAagainstFash/status/1661078713411223563?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter thread}}}\uc2  posted by a group calling itself Miami Against Fascism, a supporter of white supremacist and far-right groups including the Proud Boys.\par \par \uc2 It posted screenshots allegedly of social media posts made by Salinas promoting antisemitism, a photograph of her at a Proud Boys rally in Miami last year, and video of her with members of the extremist Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MIAagainstFash/status/1550291433336217600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disrupting a meeting of the Miami-Dade school board}}}\uc2  last summer.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Phil Sears/AP\par \par \uc2 Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  has been aggressively campaigning in several Florida school districts for certain books and materials it considers inappropriate for children to be censored, emboldened by Republican governor and upcoming presidential hopeful \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/09/ron-desantis-florida-education-censorship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to reshape education}}}\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Salinas, it said, has also shared QAnon propaganda on her own \uc2 Twitter\uc2  page.\par \par \uc2 Gorman, who delivered a much-applauded recital of The Hill We Climb at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s January 2021 inauguration, has also condemned the banning of her book of the same name containing the poem on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 So they ban my book from young readers, confuse me with @oprah [Winfrey], fail to specify what parts of my poetry they object to, refuse to read any reviews, and offer no alternatives,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unnecessary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/bookbans?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #bookbans}}}\uc2  like these are on the rise, and we must fight back.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/amanda-gorman-poem-ban-florida-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Gorman \u8216\'20\'18gutted\u8217\'20\'19 after Florida school bans Biden inauguration poem}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e27bd8f087efbd541dcf2#block-646e27bd8f087efbd541dcf2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on Congress}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and specifically Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 to tighten firearm access one year after a gunman killed 19 students and two teachers at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e36c88f088e0216a846ed#block-646e36c88f088e0216a846ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak}}}\uc2  about the tragedy at 3.30pm this afternoon and also call on the GOP to support stricter gun regulations. Meanwhile, in the Capitol, negotiations continue over raising the debt ceiling, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e33ac8f088e0216a846b7#block-646e33ac8f088e0216a846b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no breakthrough yet apparent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e1ad48f087efbd541dc69#block-646e1ad48f087efbd541dc69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested a meeting}}}\uc2  with attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and aired a litany of grievances about special counsel Jack Smith and other prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  will later today announce the start of his presidential campaign, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e0c028f087efbd541dbb9#block-646e0c028f087efbd541dbb9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spend big}}}\uc2  on door-knocking in early voting states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated legislature{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-2024-musk-twitter-debt-ceiling-deadline-live-updates?page=with:block-646e206d8f087efbd541dca9#block-646e206d8f087efbd541dca9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be moving}}}\uc2  to curb political power in its most-populous county, which is run by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Uvalde, Texas is today peppered with memorials as the town marks the one-year anniversary of the elementary school shooting that killed 21 people:\par \par \uc2 A memorial to the Uvalde school shooting, pictured today. Photograph: Brandon Bell/Getty Images A memorial outside the school where the shooting happened. Photograph: Brandon Bell/Getty Images Veronica Mata visits a mural honoring her daughter, Tess, in Uvalde on 3 May. Photograph: Eric Gay/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to call on GOP to 'help stop the epidemic of gun violence'\par \par \uc2 In his speech this afternoon marking one year since a gunman killed 19 students and two teachers at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will call on Republicans to support measures to address gun violence, a White House official said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president will remember those lost in Uvalde and reiterate his call for Republicans in Congress to act and help stop the epidemic of gun violence that has become the number one killer of kids in America,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s address, which is scheduled for 3.30pm today.\par \par \uc2 The official noted that since the shooting in Uvalde and another shortly before it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/16/buffalo-shooting-gunman-details-plan-before-rampage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Buffalo, New York}}}\uc2 , the president has signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/bipartisan-gun-control-law-house-vote-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a modest gun control measure}}}\uc2  passed by Congress, and \u8220\'20\'1Ccontinued to implement two dozen executive actions to help reduce gun violence and keep weapons of war out of dangerous hands \u8211\'20\'13 and he has consistently called on Republicans in Congress to take action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom universal background checks, to requiring safe storage of guns, to ending immunity from liability for gun manufacturers, to banning assault weapons and high-capacity magazines, the President has called for Congress to enact commonsense policies that Americans support,\u8221\'20\'1D the official continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy is speaking to reporters at the Capitol about the ongoing debt ceiling negotiations, but the gist remains basically the same as it has for the past few days: no deal has been reached between the two sides.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we can make progress today,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican House speaker said, noting that talks were continuing. The deadline to reach a deal or face a potential US debt default remains 1 June.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 With the executive and legislative branches locked in a standoff over raising the debt ceiling, let\u8217\'20\'19s check on the third branch of government: the judiciary. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  gave a speech in which he vowed that the court would maintain the highest ethical standards, despite allegations of improper ties between some justices and parties with interests in their cases:\par \par \uc2 The chief justice of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2 , \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , said he and the other justices were working to hold themselves to the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest standards\u8221\'20\'1D of ethical conduct.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to assure people that I am committed to making certain that we as a court adhere to the highest standards of conduct,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts told an awards dinner in Washington on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He was speaking the same day lawyers for Harlan Crow said the Republican mega-donor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/clarence-thomas-gifts-harlan-crow-senate-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not cooperate}}}\uc2  with the Senate judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 The panel asked for list of gifts Crow has given to the conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and which Thomas mostly did not declare: the source of scandal and calls for Thomas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/09/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-resignation-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to resign or be removed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/may/24/supreme-court-john-roberts-highest-standards-conduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chief justice says US supreme court keeps \u8216\'20\'18highest standards\u8217\'20\'19 of conduct}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress, however, is preoccupied with the standoff over increasing the debt ceiling ahead of the 1 June deadline after which the \uc2 US government\uc2  could default for the first time in history.\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy is leading the Republicans in negotiations with the Biden administration over raising the limit, and his office just announced he will speak with reporters at 11.45am. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see what he has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris, Jeffries call for gun control on anniversary of Uvalde shooting\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats including vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  have called for stricter laws to address gun violence on the one-year anniversary of the killings of 21 students and teachers at an elementary school in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNevaeh. Jacklyn. Makenna. Jose. Eliahna. Uziyah. Amerie Jo. Xavier. Jayce. Tess. Maranda. Alithia. Annabell. Maite. Alexandria. Layla. Jailah. Eliahna. Rojelio. And their teachers, Irma Garcia and Eva Mireles. Nineteen children and two educators who should be here with us today. They should still have birthdays to celebrate, graduations to plan, careers and lives to look forward to. Instead, one year ago today, they were killed in their elementary school in Uvalde, Texas, in a mass shooting carried out with a weapon of war,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the past year, so many Uvalde families have channeled their anguish into advocacy,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CTogether, they demand that we act to save lives. With their help, President Biden signed the most significant gun safety legislation in 30 years and implemented important executive actions in the months since. But more must be done. Today, Doug and I pray for the people of Uvalde. And we urge leaders in Congress and in state legislatures to meet this heartbreaking moment not just with words, but with action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jeffries was more forceful, accusing Republicans in a statement of blocking meaningful action to stop mass shootings and gun violence at large.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Democrats will continue to fight for commonsense gun safety legislation, like universal criminal background checks and an assault weapons ban. Extreme MAGA Republicans have shown that they are willing to flood our communities with weapons of war that have been consistently used to shred innocent children, including in Nashville, Tennessee earlier this year. The gun violence epidemic is unacceptable, unconscionable and un-American,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today is the first anniversary of the school shooting in Uvalde, Texas, in which a gunman killed 19 students and two teachers. For the Guardian, Charlie Scudder reports that gun control advocates in the firearm-friendly state seemed to have score a rare victory a few weeks ago, only for it to suddenly fall apart:\par \par \uc2 Days after a deadly mass shooting in a Dallas suburb, families of another horrific killing gathered in the Texas capitol, demanding a change to the state\u8217\'20\'19s famously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/08/allen-texas-mall-shooting-gun-culture"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lax gun laws}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It had been nearly a year since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/17/uvalde-shooting-report-caretakers-officials-missed-red-flags"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a gunman}}}\uc2  shot 19 students and two teachers at an elementary school in Uvalde, with police waiting more than an hour to confront and kill him. Those children\u8217\'20\'19s parents and relatives hadn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped lobbying Texas lawmakers for stricter gun control.\par \par \uc2 And after eight others were killed at an Allen shopping mall on 7 May, the Uvalde families quickly descended to tell lawmakers to pass their number one priority: to raise the minimum age for Texans to purchase semi-automatic firearms from 18 to 21.\par \par \uc2 They lined the hallways as lawmakers walked through to the House chamber, holding signs and loudly chanting \u8220\'20\'1Craise the age\u8221\'20\'1D, which in part is an allusion to the 18-year-old Uvalde shooter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHad this bill been the law in the state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  one year ago, the gunman would not have been able to [buy] the semi-automatic weapon he used to murder our daughter,\u8221\'20\'1D Kimberly Mata-Rubio, whose daughter Lexi died at the Uvalde school, testified in a Texas house committee hearing. \u8220\'20\'1COur hearts may be broken but our resolve has never been stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/uvalde-school-shooting-texas-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People were stunned\u8217\'20\'19: Uvalde families\u8217\'20\'19 Texas gun safety win lasts just 24 hours}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s shift the focus for a minute away from Washington DC and to Texas, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/kira-lerner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kira Lerner}}}\uc2  reports the GOP is moving to strip political power away from Democratic authorities in Houston, the state\u8217\'20\'19s most-populous city:\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  are targeting Houston, the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city and Democratic stronghold, with a series of bills that would limit local authority to administer elections and give that power to the state.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans on Tuesday gave final approval to two bills, both already passed by the senate in April, that would impact elections in Harris county, the third most populous county in the country. One bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/bill/SB1750/2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 1750}}}\uc2 , would get rid of the election administrator position in the county, eliminating a nonpartisan role, and give their authority to the county clerk and tax assessor-collector. Another, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legiscan.com/TX/bill/SB1933/2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 1933}}}\uc2 , could give the Texas secretary of state, currently a Republican appointed by Greg Abbott, the governor, administrative oversight of a county office administering elections.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/texas-republicans-houston-local-election-authority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Republicans target state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city with voting restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers request meeting with attorney general Garland over special counsel\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have asked attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  for a meeting, saying the former president is being \u8220\'20\'1Ctreated unfairly\u8221\'20\'1D and accusing special counsel Jack Smith and other prosecutors of perpetrating \u8220\'20\'1Congoing injustice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Garland last year appointed Smith to investigate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the January 6 insurrection, the efforts to overturn the 2020 election result and the classified documents found at Mar-a-Lago. The Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/special-counsel-is-wrapping-up-trump-mar-a-lago-probe-99cd2517"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported yesterday}}}\uc2  that Smith is finishing up his investigation into the government materials federal agents retrieved from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s south Florida resort last August, and will recommend to Garland whether charges are warranted.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110420928827917285"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter to the attorney general}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys John P Rowley and James M Trusty take the tone of grievance and persecution familiar to anyone who has read the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s missives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo President of the United States has ever, in the history of our country, been baselessly investigated in such an outrageous and unlawful fashion,\u8221\'20\'1D it reads.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Part of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pitch to Republican voters centers on being more electable than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who, despite his popularity, is in the center of a swirl of legal entanglements. One of those is the indictment filed by the Manhattan district attorney alleging Trump falsified business records, which the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly }}}\uc2  reports now has a trial date with potential significance to the presidential campaign:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial in New York on criminal charges over hush money payments to the porn star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2  will begin on 25 March 2024, amid the Republican presidential primary and less than than eight months before the general election the former president hopes to contest.\par \par \uc2 The trial date was announced in a hearing in a Manhattan courtroom on Tuesday, Trump attending by video link from his Florida home.\par \par \uc2 The judge, Juan Merchan, advised the former president to cancel all other obligations for the duration of the trial, which could last for several weeks.\par \par \uc2 Trump was muted for most of the hearing, which lasted around 15 minutes. The video feed showed the former president sitting and conferring with his lawyer, Todd Blanche, in front of a backdrop of American flags.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/trump-court-appearance-video-hush-money-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump hush money trial set for March 2024 during Republican primaries}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential run is no surprise, but his decision to kick the campaign off with a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  event certainly is. Politicians announcing a bid for office typically do so with speeches surrounded by allies, family and wellwishers. The Florida governor will instead hang out with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and whoever else tunes in to the live Twitter Spaces event. So what\u8217\'20\'19s in it for Musk, the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  owner and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO whose star has lately been on the rise in conservative circles? Let the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/kari-paul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Paul}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/johana-bhuiyan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Johana Bhuiyan}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  tell you:\par \par \uc2 The news that \uc2 Ron DeSantis{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/ron-desantis-2024-republican-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will launch his presidential campaign}}}\uc2  during a live \uc2 Twitter\uc2  appearance with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  marks the tech billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s latest attempts to shore up engagement with the social network at a moment of crisis for the company.\par \par \uc2 The event \u8211\'20\'13 which will take place Wednesday on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2  Spaces, a live stream feature that is often broadcasted at the top of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s feed \u8211\'20\'13 was confirmed by Musk on Tuesday afternoon. Speaking at the Wall Street Journal CEO Summit, Musk called the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s decision \u8220\'20\'1Cground breaking\u8221\'20\'1D and said it won\u8217\'20\'19t be the last political event that \uc2 Twitter\uc2  will host.\par \par \uc2 When asked if Musk plans to interview other candidates, particularly Democrats, he said \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/may/23/with-desantis-campaign-event-musk-seeks-to-shore-up-a-sinking-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 With DeSantis campaign event, Musk seeks to shore up a sinking Twitter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis plans door-knocking surge in early primary states \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Backed by a Super Pac and its $200m budget, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/24/us/politics/ron-desantis-2024-super-pac.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported today}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign will deploy thousands of workers to knock on doors in early Republican primary voting states \u8211\'20\'13 repeatedly.\par \par \uc2 The plan is for these workers to visit the doors of every potential DeSantis voter in South Carolina, Nevada and New Hampshire at least four times, and five times in Iowa, whose caucuses typically kick off the Republican nomination process. The campaign is going as far as to set up a boot camp on the outskirts of Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Des Moines, to train volunteers, as Ted Cruz did when he defeated Trump in the 2016 Republican contest in the state.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 Top officials with the pro-DeSantis group, a super PAC called Never Back Down, provided their most detailed account yet of their battle plan to aid Mr. DeSantis, whom they believe they can sell as the only candidate to take on \u8211\'20\'13 and win \u8211\'20\'13 the cultural fights that are definitional for the Republican Party in 2024.\par \par \uc2 The group said it expected to have an overall budget of at least $200 million, including more than $80 million to be transferred from an old DeSantis state political account, for the daunting task of vaulting the Florida governor past former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 , who has established himself as the dominant early front-runner.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis is set to enter the presidential race on Wednesday in a live audio conversation on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , and the super PAC\u8217\'20\'19s enormous cash reserves are expected to be among the few advantages that Mr. DeSantis has in the race.\par \par \uc2 The group is already taking on many tasks often reserved for the campaign itself: securing endorsements in early primary states, sending mailers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/19/desantis-super-pac-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing on campuses}}}\uc2 , running television ads, raising small donations for the campaign in an escrow account and working behind the scenes to build crowds for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s events. Hiring is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/desantis-trump-iowa-2024-president-3c653361802f34c95607e3d18d77450b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 underway in 18 states}}}\uc2  and officials said plans were in the works to assemble various pro-DeSantis coalitions, such as for voters who are veterans or those focused on issues like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , guns or agriculture.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one has ever contemplated the scale of this organization or operation, let alone done it,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Chris Jankowski\uc2 , the group\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive. \u8220\'20\'1CThis has just never even been dreamed up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Iowa, the group has opened a boot camp on the outskirts of Des Moines, giving the facility the code name \u8220\'20\'1CFort Benning,\u8221\'20\'1D after the old Army training outpost, with 189 graduates of an eight-day training program the first wave of an organizing army to follow. Door knocking begins on Wednesday in New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 The endeavor echoes the \u8220\'20\'1CCamp Cruz\u8221\'20\'1D that Senator Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 presidential campaign set up near Des Moines.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis's well-funded, coordinated presidential campaign to get underway\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The biggest presidential campaign announcement since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s entry to the race will happen this evening, when Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  officially throws his hat into the ring for the Republican nomination. He\u8217\'20\'19s chosen an unusual venue to make the bid official: \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , where he will appear at 6pm Eastern Time in a live event alongside the social media network\u8217\'20\'19s owner and budding conservative maven \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19ll do an interview with Fox News after that.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has been building up to this moment for months by raising funds \u8211\'20\'13 a super Pac supporting his campaign plans to work with a $200m budget, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/24/us/politics/ron-desantis-2024-super-pac.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported}}}\uc2  today \u8211\'20\'13 egging on GOP lawmakers in Florida to pass laws that he\u8217\'20\'19s sure to campaign on and insinuating that he\u8217\'20\'19s a better bet to beat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  than Trump. If polls are to be believed, voters do not believe him. The former president is far and away the leader in most surveys, with DeSantis a distant second. He still has time to turn it around, and you can bet that will be his first priority after today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Debt ceiling negotiations between Biden and Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy are continuing. The situation remains broadly the same as yesterday: the two sides have yet to come to a deal, and the \uc2 US government\uc2  could default on its debt by as soon as 1 June.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will at 3.30pm deliver a speech marking the one-year anniversary of the school shooting in Uvalde, Texas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  briefs reporters at 2.15pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230524ej5o001s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
