\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Chevron\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s carbon offsets are \u8216\'20\'18mostly junk and some may harm\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Tim Walker \par \uc2 1,577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2023\par 10:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Investigation finds 93% of fossil fuel company\u8217\'20\'19s climate pledge offsets are worthless. Plus, the truth about booze: how alcohol really affects your body\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A new investigation into \uc2 Chevron\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s climate pledge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/may/24/chevron-carbon-offset-climate-crisis#:~:text=A%20new%20investigation%20into%20Chevron's,actually%20be%20causing%20communities%20harm."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found the fossil fuel company relies on \u8220\'20\'1Cjunk\u8221\'20\'1D carbon offsets and \u8220\'20\'1Cunviable\u8221\'20\'1D technologies}}}\uc2 , which do little to offset its vast greenhouse gas emissions and in some cases may actually be causing communities harm.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , which reported $35.5bn in profits last year, is the US\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest fossil fuel company with operations stretching from Canada and Brazil to the UK, Nigeria and Australia.\par \par \uc2 Despite major expansions in five continents, \uc2 Chevron\uc2  has said that it \u8220\'20\'1Caspires\u8221\'20\'1D to achieve net zero upstream emissions by 2050. To do this, it is mostly relying on carbon offset schemes \u8211\'20\'13 environmental projects meant to cancel out its greenhouse gas emissions \u8211\'20\'13 and carbon capture and storage (CCS) technologies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://corporateaccountability.org/ChevronsJunkAgenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Research by Corporate Accountability}}}\uc2 , a nonprofit, transnational corporate watchdog, found that 93% of the offsets \uc2 Chevron\uc2  bought and counted towards its climate targets from voluntary carbon markets between 2020 and 2022 were too environmentally problematic to be classified as anything other than worthless or junk.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is a carbon offset? A carbon offset is characterized as having low environmental integrity, or being worthless, if it is linked to a forest or plantation or green energy project, including those involving hydroelectric dams, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t lead to additional greenhouse gas reductions, exaggerates benefits or risks emitting emissions, among other measures.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  to launch presidential campaign on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with \uc2 Elon Musk\par \par \uc2 The rightwing governor of Florida, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , will launch his campaign for the Republican presidential nomination this evening in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/ron-desantis-2024-republican-president-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live appearance with Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the billionaire owner of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NBC News first reported the plan, saying the Twitter Spaces talk at 6pm ET would be moderated by David Sacks, a tech entrepreneur, Musk confidant and DeSantis supporter. Multiple outlets later confirmed the scheme and Musk himself retweeted one report.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire also trailed the interview in remarks to a conference hosted by the Wall Street Journal, adding that though he would \u8220\'20\'1Cnot at this time \u8230\'20\'26 endorse any particular candidate\u8221\'20\'1D he was \u8220\'20\'1Cinterested in \uc2 Twitter\uc2  being somewhat of a public town square where more and more organizations \u8230\'20\'26 make announcements\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Having convened a widely reported gathering of donors in Miami, DeSantis was also expected to release an announcement video on Wednesday. Fox News said the governor would be interviewed by its host \uc2 Trey Gowdy\uc2 , a former Republican congressman, at 8pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s his plan after launching his campaign? Plans for a kick-off rally in DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s home town, Dunedin, have been reported. NBC said the governor would visit early voting states next week, after the Memorial Day holiday. DeSantis has repeatedly visited such states already, in an extended run-up to his formal campaign launch including the release of a campaign-oriented book.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina passes six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after heated debate\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s state senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/south-carolina-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved an anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bill}}}\uc2  yesterday that would ban most abortions at about six weeks, a period when most people are unaware they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 During a special session to decide whether the bill advances to the governor, who has promised to sign it, the Republican-controlled senate launched into a heated debate over the ban.\par \par \uc2 The Fetal Heartbeat and Protection From \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act would ban abortions at the earliest detection of cardiac activity, and, if signed into law, would set up a judicial battle over whether the bill is constitutional. The bill already passed the state house legislature with overwhelming support, and is part of a wave of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation passed or proposed throughout the country since the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/24/1102305878/supreme-court-abortion-roe-v-wade-decision-overturn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  last year and eliminated the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south \u8211\'20\'13 which already has some of the most restrictive laws in the country \u8211\'20\'13 has been dramatically curtailed with new legislation in North Carolina and Florida. A series of Texas laws prohibit abortions after six weeks and make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-abortion-law-lawsuit-6346a3b98dd3ece069177f88172ce7b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performing abortions a felony}}}\uc2  punishable up to life in prison.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who was opposed? A group of female lawmakers, known as the \u8220\'20\'1Csister senators\u8221\'20\'1D, opposed the bill during the special session. The five senators, who are the only female lawmakers out of the 46-seat senate, previously blocked a bill in April that would have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at conception. On Tuesday, one member of the group offered an amended version of the House bill that would instead restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 12 weeks and allow up to 20 weeks for cases of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The leaders of the ChatGPT developer \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  have called for the regulation of \u8220\'20\'1Csuperintelligent\u8221\'20\'1D AIs, arguing that an equivalent to the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/may/24/openai-leaders-call-regulation-prevent-ai-destroying-humanity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 needed to protect humanity}}}\uc2  from the risk of accidentally creating something with the power to destroy it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2  claimed that the government of the US Virgin Islands is \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplicit in the crimes of \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/23/jeffrey-epstein-crimes-jp-morgan-virgin-islands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a legal filing yesterday}}}\uc2 , saying the convicted sex trafficker maintained a \u8220\'20\'1Cquid pro quo relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with some of the territory\u8217\'20\'19s highest officials over two decades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Canadian police say they have solved one of the highest-profile cold cases in Quebec history, linking the 1975 rape and murder of a 16-year-old girl to a West Virginia man who died more than 40 years ago. Police in Longueuil, Quebec, said that DNA evidence allows them to be 100% certain that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/23/canadian-police-solve-48-year-old-murder-sharron-prior"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Franklin Maywood Romine murdered teenager Sharron Prior}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s last known survivor of Japan\u8217\'20\'19s wartime sexual slavery has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/24/taiwans-last-known-comfort-woman-dies-aged-92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died at the age of 92}}}\uc2 , according to the island\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry, which called the issue a \u8220\'20\'1Cwound in human history\u8221\'20\'1D. Referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Ccomfort women\u8221\'20\'1D, more than 200,000 women were sexually enslaved by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s military during the second world war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A man who moved to the US from Mali and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/23/north-carolina-lottery-winner-mali-dance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won a six-figure lottery prize}}}\uc2  plans to invest in supporting schoolchildren in his war-torn home country. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was my dream,\u8221\'20\'1D Souleymane Sana said of being in a position to help schoolchildren in Mali, according to lottery administrators.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The truth about booze: how alcohol really affects your body, from first flush of happiness to hangover hell\par \par \uc2 Birds do it, when they eat berries that have fermented in the first frost. Bees do it, when they suck on tree sap, writes Joel Snape. Educated fleas don\u8217\'20\'19t do it, obviously \u8211\'20\'13 but \u8220\'20\'1Cmany kinds of monkeys\u8221\'20\'1D, noted Charles Darwin in The Descent of Man, \u8220\'20\'1Chave a strong taste for \u8230\'20\'26 spirituous liquors\u8221\'20\'1D. There is evidence that humans were brewing their own booze even before the wheel caught on, but how much do we know about how it works on our brains and bodies? Well, quite a bit. Recent decades have seen dozens of studies validate some old sayings, debunk others, and give the medical establishment a much clearer understanding of how alcohol affects us and how much it is really OK to drink. Is red wine good for you? Is it healthier to drink a little than not at all? Is there such a thing as hangxiety? It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2023/may/24/the-truth-about-booze-how-alcohol-really-affects-your-body-from-first-flush-of-happiness-to-hangover-hell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 time to sort fact from fiction}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: CEO of biggest carbon credit certifier to resign after claims offsets worthless\par \par \uc2 The head of the world\u8217\'20\'19s leading carbon credit certifier has announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/may/23/ceo-of-worlds-biggest-carbon-credit-provider-says-he-is-resigning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will step down as CEO next month}}}\uc2 . It comes amid concerns that Verra, a Washington-based nonprofit, approved tens of millions of worthless offsets that are used by major companies for climate and biodiversity commitments, according to a joint Guardian investigation earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  on Monday, Verra\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, David Antonioli, said he would leave his role after 15 years leading the organisation that dominates the $2bn voluntary carbon market, which has certified more than 1bn credits through its verified carbon standard (VCS). Antonioli thanked current and former staff, and said he was immensely proud of what Verra had accomplished through the environmental standards it operates. He did not give a reason for his departure and said he would be taking a break once he left the role.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Bears, burlesque and Phil Collins: the \uc2 Disney\uc2  songs that ruled our youths\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook \u8211\'20\'13 for \u8211\'20\'13 the\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and then the pub-piano thump of that first chord triggers a singalong reflex I\u8217\'20\'19ve been unable to suppress these 50 years \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cbare necessities, the simple bare necessities / Forget about your worries and your strife!\u8221\'20\'1D The Dixieland parp of brass and jangle of banjo strings, with Phil Harris\u8217\'20\'19s easygoing delivery, lasered into my seven-year-old mind. Baloo\u8217\'20\'19s classic song to Mowgli from the 1967 classic The Jungle Book advocates the good life, the easy life, a radical Zen refusal of possessions: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you find out you can live without it and go along without thinkin\u8217\'20\'19 about it!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Disney\uc2  celebrates its centenary \u8211\'20\'13 and a decade of Frozen shows no sign of dimming Let It Go\u8217\'20\'19s hold on tots \u8211\'20\'13 we remember the cursed cats, R&B hounds and self-actualisation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/24/bears-burlesque-and-phil-collins-the-disney-songs-that-ruled-our-youths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anthems that defined our childhoods}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230524ej5o001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
