\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Fresh US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans show Republicans trying to soften message\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 875 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2023\par 17:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in Nebraska and North Carolina shift to \u8216\'20\'18common sense\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that are more restrictive than they seem\par \par \uc2 After repeated failed attempts to pass stricter bans, Republicans in some US states are changing their messaging, touting \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws presented as more lenient than outright bans, but that are more restrictive than they seem when looked at in detail.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s state legislature passed a 12-week ban on Friday, days after another 12-week ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/north-carolina-abortion-ban-veto-override"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared}}}\uc2  its final hurdle in North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s senate will again weigh a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that the legislature has repeatedly tried and failed to pass in previous weeks.\par \par \uc2 In Nebraska, Republican lawmakers praised the ban as a compromise, but their Democratic colleagues did not see it that way. \u8220\'20\'1CThis place is morally bankrupt,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Omaha state senator Machaela Cavanaugh. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to 2025 when I no longer have to serve with many of you.\u8221\'20\'1D Cavanaugh {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/06/nebraska-senator-filibuster-trans-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filibustered for hundreds of hours}}}\uc2  in recent months in an attempt to stop the bill passed on Friday, an anti-trans measure to which the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was attached.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago, a six-week ban was tanked in Nebraska, partly by one of its original co-sponsors \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican state senator Merve Riepe \u8211\'20\'13 who had come to think of it as too extreme, as many women do not yet realize they are pregnant at six weeks. Ahead of the earlier vote, which Riepe abstained from, he passed around a news article warning that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hurting the Republican party, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/05/07/abortion-ban-nebraska/?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . Polling has consistently found that strong majorities of Americans oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The Nebraska ban includes no exceptions for fetal anomalies or pregnancies incompatible with life and threatens doctors with jail time.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s technically non-partisan legislature (where each lawmaker nonetheless identifies either as Republican or Democrat) have painted the bill as a huge step down from the six-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Nebraskans crowded the statehouse as the bill progressed on Wednesday, drowning out the lively debate on the house floor with angry chants and foot stomping. By the end of the night, lawmakers were forced to seek refuge, fleeing the capitol rotunda through a back tunnel flanked by police escorts in a bid to avoid angry protesters.\par \par \uc2 With the legislative session about to end, lawmakers craftily advanced the ban by attaching it to a measure limiting gender-affirming care to transgender people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are willing to drive this state into the ground. You look ridiculous,\u8221\'20\'1D Cavanaugh, said on Wednesday, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWomen will die, children are dying, and you are responsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, the 12-week ban was passed on Wednesday, when Republican politicians overrode the Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto. The fresh ban brings the current limit down from 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republicans described the bill as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life plan, not an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D, as they passed it amid protestors chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cshame\u8221\'20\'1D from inside the state legislature. But the bill will make it incredibly difficult to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in North Carolina, a state that has become somewhat of a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the increasingly restrictive Bible belt.\par \par \uc2 Most notably, the bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acluofnorthcarolina.org/en/sb20-key-facts?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limits the use of medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the most common US method of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to 10 weeks of pregnancy, and requires three in-person visits to get pills or any other form of the procedure. Those restrictions will make it harder to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for those with uncompromising work schedules, those who can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to pay for childcare and those traveling from out of state.\par \par \uc2 Further worsening the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on low-income people and women of color, it will also make people seeking abortions wait 72 hours between visits. It will require women to watch ultrasounds before they have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and to be warned about unfounded medical side-effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before having one.\par \par \uc2 Strict licensing requirements written into the bill could also shutter a number of the state\u8217\'20\'19s remaining 14 clinics, and oblige \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to report details on people who have sought an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the state department of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 And in South Carolina on Wednesday, a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban finally progressed to the senate, after weeks of Republicans repeatedly trying and failing to move it forward. But even if it passes, it must be upheld by the state supreme court, which blocked a similar six-week ban earlier this year. (The composition of that supreme court has since changed \u8211\'20\'13 the judge who wrote the decision striking down the ban has been replaced by judge who GOP lawmakers hope will overturn it.) Meanwhile, Republican and Democratic women have repeatedly united in a filibuster to stop the bill from passing. They have said they plan to do so again.\par \par \uc2 Some 900 amendments were affixed to the legislation \u8211\'20\'13 many by Democrats hoping to delay the passage of the bill. Some of those amendments included making the state liable for funeral costs of people who die after being denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and making men liable for child support and the costs of half of all pregnancy expenses, starting from fertilization.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230521ej5l000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
