\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The exact opposite of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19: Republican senator Tim Scott\u8217\'20\'19s vision for America\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Manchester, New Hampshire \par \uc2 2,108 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2023\par 16:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Can the politician\u8217\'20\'19s Reaganesque optimism and rightwing principles convince the GOP to pick its first Black presidential candidate?\par \par \uc2 About 45 minutes into his New Hampshire town hall, Tim Scott said he needed to reveal a secret to the Republican voters who had gathered to hear from the presidential hopeful.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CListen, this might surprise some of y\u8217\'20\'19all,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott told attendees with subtle laughter in his voice. He paused briefly: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m Black.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The line was met with loud laughter from the mostly white crowd, and it underscored the unique role that Scott faces in the Republican presidential primary ahead of the 2024 election. The 57-year-old senator of South Carolina and erstwhile \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally, who filed paperwork on Friday to declare his presidential candidacy ahead of a formal launch event on Monday, hopes to become the first Black politician to win his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination and go on to defeat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the general election next November.\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s chances of success appear slim, as Trump continues to dominate in national polls thanks to the enduring loyalty of many Republican primary voters. But Scott believes his sunny vision for America\u8217\'20\'19s future can sway a significant number of Republicans who are ready for \u8220\'20\'1Cnew leadership\u8221\'20\'1D in the party.\par \par \uc2 To do that, Scott will need to take on Trump and convince fellow Republicans to abandon the vengeful worldview embraced by the former president in favor of a more positive message about the direction of the country. Relying on Reaganesque optimism about the brighter days ahead, Scott has called for a new era of American policy based on \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D, deeply rooted in rightwing principles like restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and rigorously enforcing border security.\par \par \uc2 But it remains unclear whether enough Republicans are interested in dumping Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot lean into \u8216\'20\'18the best days ahead of you\u8217\'20\'19 until you deal with the cancer inside of you at the moment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Steele, a former chair of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  and a vocal Trump critic. \u8220\'20\'1CThe way you do that is to take down the guy who\u8217\'20\'19s perpetuating that narrative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18From cotton to Congress\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 As he spoke to the voters at Saint Anselm College in New Hampshire earlier this month, Scott pointed to his own family history as an example of America\u8217\'20\'19s promise. He was raised by a single, working mother, and his grandfather dropped out of school in the third grade to pick cotton on a South Carolina farm.\par \par \uc2 That grandfather lived long enough to see his grandson win a seat in the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 , where Scott served one term before being appointed to the Senate in 2013. Scott is currently the only Black Republican serving in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the reasons why we say in my family \u8216\'20\'18from cotton to Congress in one lifetime\u8217\'20\'19 is because my grandfather had a stubborn faith,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott told the New Hampshire voters. \u8220\'20\'1CHe had faith in God. He had faith in the American people, but he also had faith in the future of this great nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Echoing his message from 2021, when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/28/tim-scott-joe-biden-congressional-address-rebuttal-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered}}}\uc2  the Republican response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first presidential speech to a joint session of Congress, Scott accused Democrats of turning Americans against each other by bringing attention to systemic oppression.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I talk to my friends on the other side of the aisle, particularly the ones who disagree with me vehemently, the one thing I can tell them is that the proof of my life disproves your lies,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said at the town hall. \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is a beautiful country. We are the land of opportunity and not the land of oppression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott went on to list the benefits of his \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity zones\u8221\'20\'1D policy, an initiative aimed at directing private investment into America\u8217\'20\'19s economically disadvantaged communities. He encouraged Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake responsibility for yourself\u8221\'20\'1D and reject \u8220\'20\'1Ctoday\u8217\'20\'19s cultural victimhood\u8221\'20\'1D, alluding to the \u8220\'20\'1Cpull yourself up by your bootstraps\u8221\'20\'1D narrative that has been criticized on the left as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/02/19/opinion/economic-mobility.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unrealistic}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/21/herschel-walker-tim-scott-black-republican-bootstraps-racist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy mentor literally taught me that if you take responsibility for yourself, that in that mirror, you see the problem. But in the same mirror, you find the promise,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said at the town hall.\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s upbeat tone cast quite a contrast from Trump, whose presidential campaign thus far has focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/05/i-am-your-retribution-trump-rules-supreme-at-cpac-as-he-relaunches-bid-for-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cretribution\u8221\'20\'1D to his political enemies if he wins the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything about Tim Scott is out of the ordinary. He is the exact opposite of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and that\u8217\'20\'19s why he is so intriguing,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Republican pollster Frank Luntz. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is as nice and kind-hearted as Trump is tough and critical.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s message was greeted like a breath of fresh air from attendees of his town hall, some of whom said they are looking for the Republican party to break free from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s influence and move in a new direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI really liked the guy. I thought he was very good and forthcoming, and he\u8217\'20\'19s got a great message,\u8221\'20\'1D Bruce Nest, a 70-year-old anti-Trump voter from Nashua, said after Scott\u8217\'20\'19s town hall.\par \par \uc2 Though Scott\u8217\'20\'19s tone is markedly different from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s, the two politicians\u8217\'20\'19 platforms have far more in common. Like Trump, Scott has called for a tougher stance against China and emphasized the importance of preventing migrants from entering the US. On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which will take center stage in the 2024 election because of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision last year to overturn Roe v Wade, Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/sen-tim-scott-says-back-conservative-life-legislation-congress-sends-rcna79321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has vowed}}}\uc2  to sign \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most conservative, pro-life legislation\u8221\'20\'1D that could pass Congress. But Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/sen-tim-scott-says-back-conservative-life-legislation-congress-sends-rcna79321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has refused}}}\uc2  to specify his preferred timeframe for a potential federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In the Republican primary, the senator\u8217\'20\'19s tone and temperament alone may be enough to sway some voters.\par \par \uc2 Nest\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Debra, 70, argued it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime to give someone else a chance\u8221\'20\'1D to lead the Republican party. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to pass the baton,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking for someone to pass the baton to.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s enduring popularity left some town hall attendees skeptical.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he has a really good backstory, and I think he will connect to a lot of different ethnicities and different cultures of America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Robert Plourde, a 59-year-old voter from Loudon. \u8220\'20\'1CIt remains to be seen whether he has enough traction with the Republican party that really doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know him, I think, nationally right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stuck at 1%\par \par \uc2 When Scott formally launches his campaign on Monday, he will join a growing Republican primary field where candidates not named Trump have struggled to break through. The most recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2024-gop-primary-election-tracker/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Morning Consult poll}}}\uc2  showed Scott has drawn the support of just 1% of Republican primary voters across the country.\par \par \uc2 There is some evidence to suggest that a crucial share of Republican voters are looking to move on from Trump. One {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/trumps-legal-issues-have-little-impact-on-his-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP/NORC poll}}}\uc2  taken last month found that nearly half of Republicans do not want Trump to seek re-election, but the same survey showed Trump still enjoys a favorability rating of 68% among Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Even in Scott\u8217\'20\'19s home state of South Carolina, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.winthrop.edu/winthroppoll/2023-april-winthroppoll-results.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Winthrop University survey}}}\uc2  taken last month found that 7% of Republicans supported the senator, putting him in fourth place. The former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador Nikki Haley, who served as South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s governor and appointed Scott to the Senate, outpaced him by 11 points while Trump and Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  led in the poll.\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s advisers point out that the Iowa caucuses are still nine months away. Speaking to reporters on Wednesday, senior campaign officials noted Scott\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/members-of-congress/tim-scott/summary?cid=N00031782"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign committee}}}\uc2  has nearly $22m in cash on hand. Scott has also received hefty financial support from some Republican megadonors; last year, the tech billionaire and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/08/09/tim-scott-mega-millions-fundraising-502764"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fellow school choice proponent}}}\uc2  Larry Ellison {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/02/19/larry-ellison-pumps-15m-into-super-pac-aligned-with-tim-scott-00010377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poured}}}\uc2  $15m into a Super Pac aligned with the senator.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Scott\u8217\'20\'19s greatest challenge at this early stage will be distinguishing himself from the other Republican presidential candidates. Scott has not made much of an effort thus far to distance himself from Trump on matters of policy, even as he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tim-scott-wont-say-whether-hed-back-trump-if-hes-republican-nominee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to commit}}}\uc2  to supporting the former president in the election if he wins the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Appearing on the Fox News host \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s show in February, Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/campaigns/tim-scott-downplays-differences-trump-amid-2024-buzz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was asked}}}\uc2  what differences there were between his campaign platform and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProbably not very many at all,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott replied. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m so thankful that we had President Trump in office. Frankly, the policies that we were able to pass from 2017 to 2020 were monumental.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s embrace of his opponent\u8217\'20\'19s record has intensified speculation that this White House bid is simply a ploy to bolster his chances of becoming Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, although the senator has dismissed those suggestions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re going to go for it, go for it all,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/15/us/politics/tim-scott-president-2024.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters}}}\uc2  last month. \u8220\'20\'1CPeriod.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Trump maintaining his massive lead in national polls, Steele is skeptical that Scott or any other Republican candidate can seriously fight for the nomination without directly confronting the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnless your name is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you\u8217\'20\'19re running for vice-president,\u8221\'20\'1D Steele said. \u8220\'20\'1CUntil shown otherwise, that they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to take this man down and willing to really press the point that he is wholly incompetent and too politically damaged to be the nominee of the party again, everybody\u8217\'20\'19s running for something other than the current presidential race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I know it because I\u8217\'20\'19ve lived it\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 As Scott continues to insist that he is truly running to win the Republican nomination, his team has pointed to two factors that could help him: his personal story and his evangelical faith. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pqu52y1B6qc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video}}}\uc2  released last month, Scott emphasized those points.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was raised by a single mother in poverty. The spoons in our apartment were plastic, not silver,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said in the video. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we had faith. We put in the work and we had an unwavering belief that we too could live the American dream. I know America is the land of opportunity, not a land of oppression. I know it because I\u8217\'20\'19ve lived it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s video was filmed at Fort Sumter, the South Carolina military site where the civil war began in 1861, which Scott said represented America\u8217\'20\'19s strength and resilience. That message of unity may not resonate with all Republican primary voters; after all, when a group of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters stormed the Capitol on 6 January 2021, some of them entered the building {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/09/jan-6-attack-confederate-flag-prison-kevin-seefried"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 waving Confederate flags}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat storyline doesn\u8217\'20\'19t land the same way it used to because a lot of the folks that you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be talking to don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily look at that as a positive,\u8221\'20\'1D Steele said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey see that as part of the problem, which is why white nationalism has reared its ugly head the way it has.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to connect with white evangelical voters, who make up a substantial portion of the Republican primary electorate, will also likely encounter roadblocks. Evangelical voters represent a core piece of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s base, and they have shown hesitation in abandoning the former president. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/spotlight/prior-to-trumps-indictment-key-republican-constituencies-gave-him-favorable-ratings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data compiled}}}\uc2  by the nonpartisan Public Religion Research Institute (PRRI) in March, 62% of white evangelicals held favorable views of Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be pretty heavy lifting for Senator Tim Scott, or really any other candidate aside from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to gain a lot of loyalty from white evangelical voters,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melissa Deckman, the chief executive of PRRI.\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s fumbled answers on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy could add to his troubles with that cohort. He remains staunchly anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he has bristled when reporters try to nail down his specific views on enacting a nationwide ban. When asked about his preferred cut-off point for banning the procedure, Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/sen-tim-scott-says-back-conservative-life-legislation-congress-sends-rcna79321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  last month: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to talk about six or five or seven or 10 [weeks].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the [Republican] base, the positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  really matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Deckman said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when you have someone like Tim Scott or Nikki Haley sort of waffling on that issue, not trying to pin down the specifics of where they stand, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be harder for them to pull people away from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the primary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That task is already proving difficult for Scott. On Monday, he will start finding out if it is, in fact, impossible.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230521ej5l000mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
