\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democratic senators urge Biden to invoke 14th amendment to prevent debt default \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,623 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 20:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senators want to use amendment that says validity of US debt cannot be questioned, arguing Republicans not acting in good faith\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Negotiators representing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464ef958f08293047a55dc5#block-6464ef958f08293047a55dc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finally getting to work}}}\uc2  on finding an agreement to raise the debt ceiling before America potentially defaults on 1 June. The speaker of the house says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464fc668f08053fbe093465#block-6464fc668f08053fbe093465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans want}}}\uc2  tighter requirements on government aid recipients in any deal and no tax hikes, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-646501488f08053fbe0934a8#block-646501488f08053fbe0934a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president said}}}\uc2  he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interested in further restricting access to anti-poverty programs, underscoring an issue that could prove a wedge before the two sides. The president then left town for Japan on a truncated trip to Asia, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with leaders from the \uc2 G7\uc2  as well as countries in the Quad, a bloc intended to counter China\u8217\'20\'19s influence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464f39e8f08053fbe0933e7#block-6464f39e8f08053fbe0933e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deflected criticism}}}\uc2  that by skipping planned visits to Australia and Papua New Guinea, he\u8217\'20\'19s undercutting his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to build alliances against Beijing in the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-646528118f088021e118a398#block-646528118f088021e118a398"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 want Biden to consider}}}\uc2  invoking the constitution\u8217\'20\'19s 14th amendment, which they say would guarantee the \uc2 US government\uc2  could keep paying its bills even if the debt ceiling is not raised.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464edde8f08293047a55da3#block-6464edde8f08293047a55da3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to block}}}\uc2  Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s ban on military-style weapons from taking effect while legal challenges make their way through the courts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House GOP{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464eaa28f088021e118a080#block-6464eaa28f088021e118a080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears ready}}}\uc2  to block a Democratic resolution that would expel indicted fabulist George Santos from the chamber. They would instead refer the resolution to the ethics committee, which is investigating him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Are Democrats regaining strength in Florida? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-646522e28f08053fbe09362b#block-646522e28f08053fbe09362b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The triumph}}}\uc2  of a mayoral candidate in Jacksonville could be a positive sign for the party, which has appeared weak in recent state elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even as Republican-led states push ahead with restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has stayed vague about the degree to which he would support cutting off access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s provided \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  an opening. In a tweet, he dissected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110384051064378318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a cryptic Truth social post}}}\uc2  Trump made today to argue the former president favors national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions:\par \par \uc2 enltrThat\u8217\'20\'19s about as clear as it gets. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and MAGA Republicans are responsible for killing Roe v. Wade. And if you vote for them, they\u8217\'20\'19ll go even further. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IsPEy8pm7M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IsPEy8pm7M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1658921350390530048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The battle over access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone is continuing today, as an appeals panel with a history of hostility to reproductive rights hears arguments in the case, which narrowly escaped being taken out of pharmacies last month. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  has the latest on the ongoing hearing:\par \par \uc2 Three US appeals court judges who have previously favored \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions prepared to hear oral arguments on Wednesday on the future of the major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-supreme-court-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case \u8211\'20\'13 which has landed before judges Jennifer Walker Elrod, James Ho and Cory Wilson \u8211\'20\'13 essentially calls on them to rule on whether the federal government should suspend or scale back the \uc2 federal Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approval of mifepristone in 2000, along with later actions that made the pill more widely accessible.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone has consistently been found to be safe and effective, and advocates argue that it is safer than the erectile dysfunction medication Viagra and low-level pain reliever Tylenol.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/17/abortion-pill-lawsuit-conservative-judges-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative judges hear challenge to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill access in controversial lawsuit }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators call on Biden to invoke 14th amendment to prevent default\par \par \uc2 Arguing that Republicans are not negotiating \u8220\'20\'1Cin good faith\u8221\'20\'1D, a group of Democratic senators is planning to send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a letter requesting he use his authority under the 14th amendment of the constitution to continue paying the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bills, even if the debt ceiling is not raised.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unfortunate that Republicans in the House of Representatives and Senate are not acting in good faith. Instead, Republicans have made it clear that they are prepared to hold our entire economy hostage unless you accede to their demands to reduce the deficit on the backs of working families. That is simply unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the letter obtained by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe write to urgently request that you prepare to exercise your authority under the 14th Amendment of the Constitution, which clearly states: \u8216\'20\'18the validity of the public debt of the United States... shall not be questioned.\u8217\'20\'19 Using this authority would allow the United States to continue to pay its bills on-time, without delay, preventing a global economic catastrophe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letter is being circulated among lawmakers, and current signatories include Democratic senators \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2 , Elizabeth Warren, \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2 , \uc2 Jeff Merkley\uc2  and \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , an independent who caucuses with the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a story to watch. Last night, Jacksonville, Florida, elected a Democratic mayor, turning away a Republican candidate backed by governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Florida is often considered a swing state, but has turned rightward in recent elections and saw Democratic candidates perform especially poorly in the last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. Could the outcome of the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race in Jacksonville be a positive sign for the party statewide? The Associated Press has the latest on the election:\par \par \uc2 In a major electoral upset on Tuesday, voters in Jacksonville elected their first female mayor, defeating a Republican backed by business leaders and endorsed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , the state governor and prospective presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Jacksonville is the most populous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  city, with about 950,000 residents. \uc2 Donna Deegan\uc2 , a Democrat, earned 52% of the vote, beating \uc2 Daniel Davis\uc2 . About 217,000 people voted, a turnout of 33%.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s hard-right agenda has often made national headlines.\par \par \uc2 But in Jacksonville, Deegan said: \u8220\'20\'1CLove won tonight, and we made history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a new day in Jacksonville because people chose unity over division \u8211\'20\'13 creating a broad coalition of people across the political spectrum that want a unified city.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/florida-jacksonville-mayor-donna-deegan-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida: blow to DeSantis as Democrat wins Jacksonville mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kaitlan Collins has been given a primetime slot on CNN \u8211\'20\'13 a week after struggling to hold the hospital pass that was trying to manage \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a New Hampshire town hall which landed the network in hot water.\par \par \uc2 Kaitlan Collins. Photograph: Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Luis Maga\u241\'00\'F1a/AP\par \par \uc2 In a memo to staff today, reported by the Associated Press, Chris Licht, the CNN chairman who has come under fire for hosting Trump, called Collins \u8220\'20\'1Ca smart and gifted journalist who we\u8217\'20\'19ve all seen hold lawmakers and newsmakers accountable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe pushes politicians off their talking points, gets real answers \u8211\'20\'13 and as everyone who\u8217\'20\'19s worked with her knows \u8211\'20\'13 breaks a lot of news.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, defending the decision to host Trump, Licht {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/11/cnn-chris-licht-trump-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that CNN had covered the news as well as making it.\par \par \uc2 Collins\u8217\'20\'19s performance at St Anselm\u8217\'20\'19s College in Manchester was generally well reviewed, for the way she attempted to call out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies about the Capitol attack, election subversion and other subjects.\par \par \uc2 But fact checks she inevitably missed (on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for example), coupled with displays of audience merriment \u8211\'20\'13 such as when Trump attacked E Jean Carroll, the writer he was found liable for sexually assaulting and defaming \u8211\'20\'13 ensured a bumpy ride.\par \par \uc2 Collins will take over an evening slot formerly filled by Chris Cuomo, who left CNN amid controversy over his coverage of and advice to his brother, the now disgraced former New York governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the Associated Press reports, CNN \u8220\'20\'1Chas struggled to gain traction without Cuomo. On Monday, for example, CNN averaged 454,000 viewers in the time slot, compared to Rachel Maddow\u8217\'20\'19s 2.41 million viewers on MSNBC and \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 1.97 million on Fox, the Nielsen company said\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Collins\u8217\'20\'19s move takes her away from CNN\u8217\'20\'19s revamped but troubled morning show, from which her co-anchor Don Lemon was fired last month. Poppy Harlow will continue on that show with guest hosts, Licht said today.\par \par \uc2 Licht also said CNN \u8220\'20\'1Cprioritize[s] reporting over punditry and separate the news from the noise\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Victoria Bekiempis is quick with the news, out of New York City, that the former mayor and prominent Trump ally \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has a new legal problem today \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 A heckler who was charged with assaulting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani}}}\uc2  at a Staten Island grocery store last year has filed suit against the former New York mayor and prominent Trump ally, alleging he levied an empty accusation.\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit filed by Daniel Gill in Manhattan federal court also names as defendants the city and several police officers.\par \par \uc2 It says they \u8220\'20\'1Cparticipated in an unlawful conspiracy \u8230\'20\'26 to deprive [Gill] of his right to liberty, to his right to speak freely without retribution, and to be free from unreasonable seizures, in violation of his rights under the first, fourth and 14th amendments to the constitution of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Filed by the prominent civil rights attorney Ron Kuby, the civil action seeks monetary damages \u8220\'20\'1Cfor false arrest, civil rights conspiracy resulting in false arrest and false imprisonment, defamation, intentional infliction of emotional distress, and negligent infliction of emotional distress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  contacted a Giuliani attorney for comment.\par \par \uc2 On 26 June 2022, Giuliani was campaigning with his son, \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2 , a candidate for governor of New York \u8211\'20\'13 in what the new suit calls a \u8220\'20\'1Cvanity run\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 when Gill, a grocery store employee, walked past and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/eric-adams-rudy-giuliani-falsely-reported-claim-assault-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clapped the former mayor on the back}}}\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s up, scumbag?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, then 78, accused Gill of hitting him on the back \u8211\'20\'13 and said the feeling was like being shot or struck with a boulder.\par \par \uc2 In the words of Gill\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, \u8220\'20\'1Cvideo footage captured the entire encounter. One person called 911 and [officers] arrived on the scene, followed by other \uc2 NYPD\uc2  officers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gill was arrested and spent more than 24 hours in jail before being arraigned on misdemeanor charges including third-degree assault.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/rudy-giuliani-lawsuit-daniel-gill-staten-island-store"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Man sues Giuliani over false arrest after \u8216\'20\'18pat\u8217\'20\'19 on back led to assault charge}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stepping way from Washington and the debt ceiling fight for a moment, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a slate of anti-LGBTQ+ bills earlier, using a Christian school in Tampa as a stage for his latest culture-war-fueled move towards declaring a run for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Octavio Jones/Reuters\par \par \uc2 In front of a cheering crowd, the governor signed bills banning gender-affirming care for minors, restricting pronoun use in public schools and forcing people to use bathrooms corresponding to their sex in some situations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s kind of sad that we even have some of these discussions,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said, speaking from a lectern carrying the slogan: Let Kids Be Kids.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe never did this through all of human history until like, what, two weeks ago? Now this is something? They\u8217\'20\'19re having third-graders declare pronouns? We\u8217\'20\'19re not doing the pronoun Olympics in Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/ron-desantis-florida-laws-presidential-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announce his run for the presidency}}}\uc2  soon. He places a clear second in Republican polling \u8211\'20\'13 if a long way behind the former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Observers \u8211\'20\'13 and donors \u8211\'20\'13 have questioned whether his hard-right record in Florida, enabled by Republican supermajorities in the state legislature, will place him too far from the mainstream to win a general election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , should he secure the GOP nomination.\par \par \uc2 A six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/may/09/disney-v-desantis-florida-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a legal fight with Disney}}}\uc2 , over its opposition to some of his anti-LGBTQ+ legislation, have also been raised as possible obstacles to success for DeSantis on the national stage.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, on another aspect of Florida politics rather less thrilling for DeSantis:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/florida-jacksonville-mayor-donna-deegan-ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida: blow to DeSantis as Democrat wins Jacksonville mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive House Democrats are signaling their opposition to Republican attempts to tighten access to federal anti-poverty programs.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  of Massachusetts:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe should NOT be cutting access to critical safety net programs, ever.\par \par \uc2 Full stop.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congresswoman \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  (@RepPressley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepPressley/status/1658833021309526024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrKevin McCarthy is extorting the President of the United States and the entire world economy to take away healthcare and food assistance from working people.\par \par \uc2 Stop pretending it\u8217\'20\'19s anything else. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IbhmcbEOuG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/IbhmcbEOuG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  (@IlhanMN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IlhanMN/status/1658590760722219010?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Democratic senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  said he may not vote for a measure to raise the debt ceiling that cuts support for the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP), often called food stamps. Here\u8217\'20\'19s his statement:\par \par \uc2 No one I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever met wants to stay on SNAP for life. They need it to make ends meet. I sure didn\u8217\'20\'19t come to Washington to take vital assistance away from working people at the same time big bank CEOs nearly crash the economy and get to jet off to Hawaii scot-free. I cannot in good conscience support a debt ceiling proposal that pushes people into poverty.\par \par \uc2 He raised the issue again in a Tuesday hearing with former executives from the failed Signature and Silicon Valley banks:\par \par \uc2 enltr'Shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t you have a working requirement after [the U.S. bails out] your bank?'\par \par \uc2 In a hearing with execs of failed SVB & Signature Bank, Sen. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  questioned why the GOP is 'more preoccupied' with work requirements for SNAP recipients than keeping banks accountable. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x9Ebmw2gJP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/x9Ebmw2gJP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1658559678945677322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The flare up in the debt ceiling standoff has provided \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a perhaps welcome break from the public spotlight, as he deals with a swirl of scandals, investigations and prosecutions. But the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone}}}\uc2  reports that Trump hasn\u8217\'20\'19t relented in his zeal to attack his foes, raising concerns among some legal observers:\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles mount at the federal, state and local levels, the ex-president and his lawyers are banking on their political allies in the Republican party to make attacks on a New York prosecutor who has charged Trump with criminal offenses, and to also get them to help derail investigations that endanger his 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 Former prosecutors and members of both parties have voiced strong criticism about the drives by Trump, his lawyers and Republican House allies to attack prosecutors who have filed charges against Trump or are investigating him, calling such moves antithetical to democratic principles and the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 Such criticism has not deterred Trump, his lawyers or pliable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  from trying to discredit prosecutors with political attacks that in part reflect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lack of success in convincing courts to curb prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 In April, the House judiciary committee chairman, Jim Jordan, a key Trump ally, publicly launched an inquiry into the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , soon after he filed a 34-count indictment of Trump for falsifying business records tied to alleged hush money payments that Trump made in 2016 to Stormy Daniels, the porn star who claimed Trump had an affair with her.\par \par \uc2 In a Fox News interview last month, Jordan echoed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Bragg for \u8220\'20\'1Cinterfering\u8221\'20\'1D in the coming election charging that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  used federal tax dollars to go after a former president, to indict a former president for no crime, [which] interferes with the federal election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/donald-trump-republican-allies-prosecutors-investigations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies attempt to undermine prosecutors endangering his 2024 bid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Negotiators representing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464ef958f08293047a55dc5#block-6464ef958f08293047a55dc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finally getting to work}}}\uc2  on finding an agreement to raise the debt ceiling before America potentially defaults on 1 June. McCarthy says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464fc668f08053fbe093465#block-6464fc668f08053fbe093465"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans want}}}\uc2  tighter requirements on government aid recipients in any deal and no tax hikes, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-646501488f08053fbe0934a8#block-646501488f08053fbe0934a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden said}}}\uc2  he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interested in further restricting access to anti-poverty programs, underscoring an issue that could prove a wedge before the two sides. The president then left town for Japan on a truncated trip to Asia, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with leaders from the \uc2 G7\uc2  as well as countries in the Quad, an alliance intended to counter China\u8217\'20\'19s influence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s news so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464f39e8f08053fbe0933e7#block-6464f39e8f08053fbe0933e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deflected criticism}}}\uc2  that by skipping planned visits to Australia and Papua New Guinea, he\u8217\'20\'19s undercutting his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to build alliances against Beijing in the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464edde8f08293047a55da3#block-6464edde8f08293047a55da3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to block}}}\uc2  Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s ban on military-style weapons from taking effect while legal challenges make their way through the courts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House GOP{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/17/debt-ceiling-deadline-biden-mccarthy-abortion-pill-ruling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6464eaa28f088021e118a080#block-6464eaa28f088021e118a080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears ready}}}\uc2  to block a Democratic resolution that would expel indicted fabulist George Santos from the chamber. They would instead refer the resolution to the ethics committee, which is investigating him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , meanwhile, said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interested in imposing work requirements \u8220\'20\'1Cof any consequences\u8221\'20\'1D on federal anti-poverty programs.\par \par \uc2 His comments, at the tail end of his speech about an hour ago, indicate that the new requirements proposed by Republicans could be a sticking point in the negotiations with Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of the president\u8217\'20\'19s comments:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden says he will support only limited safety net work requirements, which he has previously given conflicting answers on and which have emerged as a top GOP priority:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to accept any work requirements that go much beyond what is already [there].\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xJ9Z9krMLj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xJ9Z9krMLj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658858098474221569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCarthy says no to tax hikes, yes to work requirements for aid in debt limit deal\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy just concluded a press conference alongside Republican lawmakers from the House and Senate, where he ruled out increasing taxes in a debt ceiling deal and signaled he would push for stricter work requirements for recipients of federal government aid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo!\u8221\'20\'1D he replied when asked if he would consider higher taxes on wealthy Americans as part of a debt limit compromise.\par \par \uc2 He also justified the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s push to insist people in programs like Temporary Assistance for Needy Families and Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program work in order to receive the benefits. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t he want to help people get out of poverty?\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy asked, tying stricter work requirements to the programs\u8217\'20\'19 effectiveness \u8211\'20\'13 a link studies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/58199"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have found is uneven}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also said he would stick to a promise made during his contentious election as speaker of the House to give lawmakers 72 hours to review any legislation before it is voted on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes so many days to get through the Senate, so many days through the House. We have a 72 hour rule, which I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to break. I think the American public and all the members should have 72 hours to read what we end up with, if we\u8217\'20\'19re able to end up with it,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he departed the White House\u8217\'20\'19s Roosevelt Room after speaking to reporters, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked if he had given China a win by cancelling his visits to Australia and Papua New Guinea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re still formidable allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And while it was difficult to hear exactly what he said, the president signaled he intended to speak or meet in the future with the Chinese president, \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 In order to return to Washington DC on Sunday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  canceled visits to Australia and Papua New Guinea intended to shore up America\u8217\'20\'19s alliances against China.\par \par \uc2 In his speech at the White House, Biden signaled he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/may/17/cancelled-quad-summit-meeting-china-us-pacific-standing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aware of the criticism}}}\uc2  that his administration isn\u8217\'20\'19t taking efforts to counter China\u8217\'20\'19s influence seriously.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the meantime, I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken to the Australian leader [Anthony] Albanese \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be seeing him at the \uc2 G7\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding he would also see the Indian prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , and the Japanese prime minister, \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 , at the meeting. Biden was to meet with the leaders at a meeting of the Quad regional group in Australia, which has now been canceled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Quad members will be there, will get a chance to talk separately at the meeting, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be going on to Australia,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he would remain in touch with his negotiators along with Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy during his trip to meet \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders in Japan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll be in constant contact with my team while I\u8217\'20\'19m at the \uc2 G7\uc2  and be in close touch with Speaker McCarthy and other leaders as well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I have done in anticipation that we won\u8217\'20\'19t get it all done till I get back is, I\u8217\'20\'19ve cut my trip short in order to be [here] for the final negotiations and sign the deal with the majority leader.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said he expected to return to Washington DC on Sunday and hold a press conference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'confident' US will avoid default\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says he is \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D that a deal will be reached to increase the debt ceiling and avoid a \uc2 US government\uc2  default.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident that we\u8217\'20\'19ll get the agreement on the budget, that America will not default,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said in a speech at the White House following his meeting yesterday afternoon with the Republican House speaker, Kevin McCarthy, and other leaders of Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to come together because there\u8217\'20\'19s no alternative way to do the right thing for the country. We have to move on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court leaves Illinois assault weapons ban in effect\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has declined to block {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/11/supreme-court-new-york-gun-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a ban on military-style weapons }}}\uc2  approved by Illinois\u8217\'20\'19s legislature from taking effect, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING; Supreme Court leaves in place Illinois restrictions on military-style weapons while legal battles continue. No noted dissents\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Barnes (@scotusreporter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scotusreporter/status/1658850808778174465?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in the midwestern state had passed the measure about six months after seven people were killed and more than 30 injured in a mass shooting in the Chicago suburb of Highland Park.\par \par \uc2 While the supreme court did not stop the law from taking effect, it allowed legal challenges filed against it to proceed in state and federal courts.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech on the debt limit, CNN reports that House Republicans believe they have the votes to refer the resolution expelling George Santos to the ethics committee \u8211\'20\'13 thus keeping him in the chamber for a while longer:\par \par \uc2 enltrA sign McCarthy will have the votes to refer Santos expulsion resolution to House Ethics. Freshman GOP Rep. Mike Lawler says he will vote to refer to committee. Dems, including Jeffries, are expected to oppose referral to ethics to try to force expulsion vote now\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1658837753285468169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLawler to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kristin__wilson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kristin__wilson}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe committee will move very expeditiously. He won\u8217\'20\'19t be here for long. Whether he cuts a deal and resigns, or the committee makes a recommendation to expel him. What the Democrats are doing is bullshit. It\u8217\'20\'19s just politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1658837958705795077?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we await the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks on the debt ceiling, let\u8217\'20\'19s check in on the saga of George Santos, the Republican House representative who admitted to lying prolifically and is now the subject of a federal indictment.\par \par \uc2 House Democrat Robert Garcia yesterday introduced a resolution to expel him from the chamber, but it needs the support of two-thirds of lawmakers to pass and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if Republicans, who control the House by a small majority, will support it.\par \par \uc2 According to the Democratic House whip, Katherine Clark, it\u8217\'20\'19s possible the resolution\u8217\'20\'19s fate will become known today, when it could come up for consideration. Republicans may vote to send the resolution to the House ethics committee, which is investigating Santos.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to speak on efforts to prevent \uc2 US government\uc2  default\par \par \uc2 The White House has just announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak at 10.45am ET \u8220\'20\'1Con preventing a first-ever government default\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The speech was not previously scheduled. The president still plans to later this morning begin his journey to Japan as part of a trip that was cut short so he could return to Washington to deal with the debt limit standoff.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll cover the speech on this blog as it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 If high-stakes negotiations and last-minute deals over raising the debt ceiling all sound familiar, that\u8217\'20\'19s because they are.\par \par \uc2 This has happened repeatedly in Washington over the last decade or so, as Punchbowl News points out. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a list of all the increases agreed to, and how they were agreed to, since 1993:\par \par \uc2 enltrI am a nerd, so here are all (i think!) the debt-limit increases since 1993\par \par \uc2 April 1993 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 August 1993 \u8212\'20\'14 part of an omnibus spending bill\par \par \uc2 Feb 1996 \u8212\'20\'14 declaration congress would raise DL before march 1996. And ensured social security would be paid.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658828513560915975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMarch 1996 \u8212\'20\'14 DL with strings (prioritizing)\par \par \uc2 March 1996 \u8212\'20\'14 DL within \u8220\'20\'1Ccontract with America advancement act\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 host of Republican priorities.\par \par \uc2 August 1997 \u8212\'20\'14 DL in the \u8220\'20\'1Cbalanced budget act of 1997\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 June 2002 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 May 2003 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 Nov 2004 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 March 2006 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658828515402186753?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSept 2007 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 july 2008 \u8212\'20\'14 Housing and Economic Recovery Act of 2008\par \par \uc2 oct 2008 \u8212\'20\'14 TARP\par \par \uc2 feb 2009 \u8212\'20\'14 American Recovery and Reinvestment Act\par \par \uc2 dec 2009 \u8212\'20\'14 clean\par \par \uc2 feb 2010 \u8212\'20\'14 statutory pay go, Elimination of Duplicative and Wasteful Spending,\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658828516572504064?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltraug 2011 \u8212\'20\'14 Budget Control Act\par \par \uc2 Feb 2013 \u8212\'20\'14 No Budget, No Pay\par \par \uc2 Oct 2013 \u8212\'20\'14 spending bill\par \par \uc2 Feb 2014 \u8212\'20\'14 Clean (mostly)\par \par \uc2 Nov 2015 \u8212\'20\'14 Bipartisan Budget Act\par \par \uc2 Sept. 2017 -\u8212\'20\'14 Spending bill, disaster relief\par \par \uc2 Feb 2018 \u8212\'20\'14 Bipartisan budget act (spending bill, etc)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658828517872680961?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAug 2019 \u8212\'20\'14 Bipartisan Budget Act (increases discretionary spending limits, suspends the debt limit, and modifies budget enforcement procedures.)\par \par \uc2 Dec. 2021 -- clean\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658828519462383616?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 This morning, Kevin McCarthy went on CNBC to take a mini victory lap after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  agreed to talks over raising the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 But the Republican House speaker warned that the two sides don\u8217\'20\'19t have much time left to reach an agreement. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltr"The President should appoint either himself or people from his administration to negotiate directly with myself. The challenge here is the President waited 104 days until he came to this conclusion," says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SpeakerMcCarthy}}}\uc2  on the debt ceiling. "The timeline is very short." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5iXeKFvz0I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5iXeKFvz0I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Squawk Box (@SquawkCNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SquawkCNBC/status/1658807980454821894?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats ready plan B in case debt limit negotiations fail\par \par \uc2 The top Democrat in the House of Representatives said the party is moving ahead with a parliamentary tactic that could force a vote on raising the debt ceiling in case negotiations between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Speaker Kevin McCarthy fail.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Democrats, the House minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , encouraged his lawmakers to support a discharge petition filed by \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2 , the ranking member of the budget committee. The unusual maneuver circumvents that usual committee process bills must undergo by bringing legislation directly to the floor, but is time consuming and faces uncertain prospects of success.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the next few weeks, at the reckless urging of former President Trump, we confront the possibility that right-wing extremists will intentionally plunge our country into a default crisis. Emerging from the White House meeting, I am hopeful that a real pathway exists to find an acceptable, bipartisan resolution that prevents a default,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Jeffries, who attended the meeting yesterday where Biden and McCarthy agreed to appoint deputies to negotiate over an agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, given the impending June 1 deadline and urgency of the moment, it is important that all legislative options be pursued in the event that no agreement is reached. Accordingly, later on this morning, Budget Committee Ranking Member \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2  will file a discharge petition to provide a vehicle that may be necessary to protect the full faith and credit of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, asking every Democrat to sign the petition today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden scores own goal on Asian diplomacy with cancelled trip\par \par \uc2 A hint of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s newfound seriousness over the debt limit negotiations emerged yesterday, shortly before his meeting with Republican Kevin McCarthy and other congressional leaders. The giveaway was an unnamed administration official telling reporters that Biden would cut short his trip to Asia and return to Washington work on a deal \u8211\'20\'13 which the White House later confirmed would indeed happen, shortly after the president reversed his policy of not negotiating over the debt ceiling and appointed deputies to sit down with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 While Biden will still travel to Japan to meet with \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders and the country\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, he\u8217\'20\'19s cut out visits to two other countries that were intended to shore up the influence of Washington and its allies against China. Biden will no longer visit Australia and attend a meeting of nations in the Quad, a group formed to stand against Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s influence. Nor will he make the first ever visit by an American president to Papua New Guinea, a stop seen as intended to bring the country under the US\u8217\'20\'19s wing.\par \par \uc2 From Australia, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/daniel-hurst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daniel Hurst}}}\uc2  reports that by cancelling his visits to the two countries, Biden has dealt a blow to US diplomacy in Asia:\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government is probably the biggest winner from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to pull out of his trip to Australia and Papua New Guinea, forcing the cancellation of the Quad summit in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 Chinese state media outlets won\u8217\'20\'19t need to muster much creative energy to weave together some of Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s preferred narratives: that the US is racked by increasingly severe domestic upheaval and is an unreliable partner, quick to leave allies high and dry.\par \par \uc2 To make matters worse for the US\u8217\'20\'19s standing in the region, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s planned visit to PNG on Monday had been trumpeted as a clear statement of intent about his commitment to the Pacific amid growing competition for influence with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read the rest of his story below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/may/17/cancelled-quad-summit-meeting-china-us-pacific-standing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The cancelled Quad summit is a win for China and a self-inflicted blow to the US\u8217\'20\'19s Pacific standing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Finally, Biden and McCarthy agree to negotiate over debt ceiling\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spent weeks refusing to negotiate with Republicans over raising the debt ceiling, even as the party gave no ground on the issue and the 1 June deadline for a potential \uc2 US government\uc2  default grew nearer.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the president met with the speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, and the two men agreed to appoint deputies to hash out a bipartisan measure that will probably include some policy concessions demanded of Democrats by conservatives and also raise the limit.\par \par \uc2 In a sign of how seriously he is taking the deadline, Biden cut short the trip to Asia he will begin today, scrapping a stop in Australia and the first visit to Papua New Guinea by a US president. And while the government estimates it will need an increase approved by the start of June to avoid missing bond and salary payments for the first time in history, lawmakers are under an even tighter deadline.\par \par \uc2 Congress only works certain days, and McCarthy has estimated a framework must be agreed to by the end of this week in order for legislation to be approved by both the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what we expect to happen today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is departing Washington DC for Japan, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with prime minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  and attend a summit of \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 McCarthy and top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  will brief reporters in the Capitol at 11:15am ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will take questions from reporters as Air Force One heads to Japan. She\u8217\'20\'19ll be joined by national security adviser Jake Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230517ej5h00164\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
