\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 North Carolina bans  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  at 12 weeks, overriding Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto\b0\par\par\uc2 Makaelah Walters in Durham \par \uc2 788 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 16:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 18\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Move expected to deal fresh blow to one of last bastions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has passed legislation banning most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy after the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled general assembly successfully overrode the Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto on Tuesday evening.\par \par \uc2 Both the state senate and house voted along party lines, with the senate voting 30-20. The house completed the second and final part of the override with a vote of 72-48. The bill will repeal the current law, which bans abortions after 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The move is expected to deal a fresh blow to one of the last bastions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south, which has been significantly curtailed after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year. And it is part of a growing push across the US to further cripple \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections \u8211\'20\'13 Tuesday also saw Republicans pushing for stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in South Carolina and Nebraska. Both debates are still ongoing, despite the party\u8217\'20\'19s recent losses in states where they are focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , a Democrat, had honored a vow he made to his state to protect reproductive rights by vetoing SB 20 during a public rally in Raleigh which was attended by thousands.\par \par \uc2 Cooper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NC_Governor/status/1658634585847087104/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  the decision to override his veto and move forward with the ban, and said he would do \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything I can to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in North Carolina, because women\u8217\'20\'19s lives depend on it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gov. Cooper Statement on Republican vote to override SB20 veto: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Kh06weg4zQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Kh06weg4zQ}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  (@NC_Governor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NC_Governor/status/1658634585847087104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 17, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, Republicans had rushed the bill through the house, drawing criticism from other legislators and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates. The 46-page bill, in addition to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks, extends the waiting period for people seeking abortions to 72 hours, requires providers to send sensitive information to the state department of health and human services, and requires clinics to obtain special licensing that would result in clinic closures throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 The new restrictions pose grave concerns for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, who have already witnessed a sharp uptick in patients traveling to North Carolina for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care after Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 During Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s debate, state Democrats spoke out against the new restrictions. Diamond Staton-Williams, the house representative for Cabarrus county, even shared her own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  story and how it helped her family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was not an easy decision, at all, it was not made lightly or frivolously,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on the house floor. \u8220\'20\'1CI knew that in order for my family to prosper and to continue with the opportunities in front of us, this was the best decision for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House also issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/05/16/statement-from-white-house-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre-on-north-carolinas-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  condemning the decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, Republican state legislators in North Carolina overturned Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s veto of a dangerous bill that is out of touch with the majority of North Carolinians and will make it even more difficult for women to get the reproductive healthcare they need,\u8221\'20\'1D said the press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has a unique position as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in the south, especially after the overturn of Roe v Wade. A third of North Carolina patients seeking abortions since the supreme court decision come from outside the state, Planned Parenthood estimates. One report shows the number of people traveling to North Carolina for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care rose by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/SFPWeCountReport_AprtoAug2022_ReleaseOct2022-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 37%}}}\uc2  as restrictions tightened in neighboring southern states since last summer. Others show an average increase of 788 patients monthly after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, advocates who foresaw the overturning of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto of SB 20 had sprung into action hoping to sway lawmakers who showed support for reproductive rights in the past, such as Tricia Cotham, a representative who handed house Republicans a supermajority after switching parties last month.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Votes! South Atlantic launched a television ad campaign reminding viewers of Republican state representative Ted Davis\u8217\'20\'19s promise to uphold North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s 20-week ban.\par \par \uc2 The group also supported Governor Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to reach constituents and providers in Mecklenburg, Guilford and New Hanover counties last week during a series of round tables. At each talk, the governor informed constituents about the contents of the bill. Cooper also called out Republican lawmakers in the state who had previously said they would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 But their efforts were quashed on Tuesday when the lawmakers remained aligned with the rest of their party.\par \par \uc2 Agencies contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230516ej5g0028o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
