\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 How mifepristone became a target of the US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,138 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 15:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, first invented in 1980 in France, was slow to be accepted in the US. Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s at the center of a major court fight\par \par \uc2 The future of mifepristone, a crucial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug, is currently in question as US courts consider a challenge brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups. Considering medication is the most common US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  method, it is the most significant reproductive rights case to make its way through the courts since Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The groups suing the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  over its approval of the drug claim that the drug poses a threat to women and girls \u8211\'20\'13 contrary to scientific consensus \u8211\'20\'13 and should never have been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than two decades ago. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  vehemently stands by its approval of the pill, with the Biden administration emphasizing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s rigorous safety reviews of the drug.\par \par \uc2 So what\u8217\'20\'19s the story of the drug, and how did we get here?\par \par \uc2 The history of mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a global perspective\par \par \uc2 In 1980, mifepristone was invented by French drug company \uc2 Roussel Uclaf\uc2  and was approved for market use in France in 1988. After its approval, following threats of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metacrs1360/m1/1/high_res_d/RL30866_2001Feb23.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 boycotts and violence}}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9146386/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  groups}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Roussel Uclaf\uc2  decided to suspend distribution of mifepristone for two days before the French government stepped in, ordering the drug back on the market.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the moment governmental approval for the drug was granted, RU-486 became the moral property of women,\u8221\'20\'1D said France\u8217\'20\'19s then health minister Claude Evin in reference to mifepristone, shutting down anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups\u8217\'20\'19 protest.\par \par \uc2 The UK and China followed France in approving mifepristone in 1991 and Sweden\u8217\'20\'19s 1992 approval came quickly after.\par \par \uc2 But while the Clinton administration had high hopes of also quickly approving mifepristone, the same pattern did not emerge in the US.\par \par \uc2 In 1993, on the 20th anniversary of Roe v Wade, \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  signed a host of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-signing-memorandums-medical-research-and-reproductive-health-and-exchange-with"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive orders}}}\uc2  in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, in one of his first acts as president. One of those orders directed the health secretary to review an import ban that had been imposed on the drug, to determine whether it had any basis. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time to learn the truth about what the health and safety risks of the drug really are,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said.\par \par \uc2 On that day, he was met by about 75,000 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters, angered by the change of direction after years of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies during the Reagan years. It was a harbinger of times to come: a fraught, seven-year battle for approval, putting the US behind many of its European counterparts in the approval of a potentially life-saving drug.\par \par \uc2 In 1996, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  met for the first time to consider the drug\u8217\'20\'19s approval. Concerned about the potential for violence, officials held the meeting under strict security requirements, using metal detectors and a rigid travel itinerary to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/1996/07/19/us/abortion-pill-reaches-new-us-juncture.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep violence at bay}}}\uc2 . Those attending the meeting were to be bussed in from a nearby hotel, and only camera crews were allowed to wait outside the meeting in the parking lot.\par \par \uc2 Fierce anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  backlash continued, and the \uc2 FDA\uc2  continued to review evidence on the drug\u8217\'20\'19s safety, while the rest of the world continued to move ahead in approving it. By 1999, Austria, Belgium, Denmark, Finland, Georgia, Germany, Greece, Israel, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Norway, Russia, Spain, Switzerland, Taiwan, Tunisia and Ukraine had all approved mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 In 2000, mifepristone was finally approved in the US, for terminations through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2016/020687s020lbl.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven weeks}}}\uc2  of pregnancy. That time period was later extended, to 10 weeks of pregnancy in 2016. Until 2021, mifepristone could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/media/164648/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only be dispensed}}}\uc2  in clinics, medical offices and hospitals \u8211\'20\'13 even though countries such as Canada and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26096369/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia}}}\uc2  had begun lifting those kinds of restrictions years prior.\par \par \uc2 With lockdowns in place across the world, the US finally began reconsidering its dispensing restrictions in 2020 during the Covid pandemic. By April 2021, in response to mounting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smfm.org/mife#:~:text=April%2020%2C%202020%3A%20SMFM%20and,%2Dperson%20dispensation%2C%20especially%20mifepristone."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressure}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 FDA\uc2  temporarily lifted its restrictions on mifepristone, allowing it to be sent in the mail. Those changes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/questions-and-answers-mifepristone-medical-termination-pregnancy-through-ten-weeks-gestation#:~:text=On%20December%2016%2C%202021%2C%20the,in%2Dperson%20dispensing%20requirement%E2%80%9D)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became permanent}}}\uc2  in December 2021. In 2023, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  announced that pharmacies could become certified to dispense mifepristone, lifting the strict requirements on who can dispense it.\par \par \uc2 The fifth circuit court of appeals, which is currently considering the future of mifepristone in the US, in April invalidated all of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s post-2016 actions to loosen restrictions on the drug. The supreme court temporarily blocked that decision, and mifepristone currently remains available in pharmacies and through the mail as the case proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Are \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs safe?\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs challenging the approval of mifepristone have claimed the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of mifepristone has put the safety of women and girls at risk.\par \par \uc2 In reality, years of research on tens of thousands of women has shown it to be safe and effective. Many point out that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ansirh.org/sites/default/files/publications/files/mifepristone_safety_4-23-2019.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mifepristone is safer}}}\uc2  than Tylenol and Viagra, and have lambasted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.acog.org/news/news-articles/2022/03/understanding-the-practical-implications-of-the-fdas-december-2021-mifepristone-rems-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remaining restrictions}}}\uc2  on the drug in the US, even at a time when it is listed as an essential medicine by the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/clinical-update/english/recommendations-for-abortion-before-13-weeks-gestation/medical-abortion/safety-and-effectiveness/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meta-analyses}}}\uc2  within the last decade, on almost 270,000 people using the drug through nine weeks of pregnancy, have consistently shown a less than 1% rate of serious complications associated with use of the drug (such as an infection, or need for a blood transfusion). Only two deaths have been reported in that subsample \u8211\'20\'13 one caused by pneumonia, and one from an ectopic pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 both of which are listed as likely not the result of taking medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 The rise in use\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  only recently became the most common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  method in the US. The most recent comprehensive data, from 2020, suggests that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 53%}}}\uc2  of US abortions could be attributed to medication (both misoprostol and mifepristone used together). But that number does not account for any likely increase in usage after the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2021 decision to expand access to the pill by mail, nor from the likely increase in pills being acquired from the internet \u8211\'20\'13 including from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/20/abortion-pills-us-ruling-rebecca-gomperts-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overseas}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 since Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par \uc2 Prior to 2017, the incidence of medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was far lower: around 39% of all US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/sites/default/files/report_pdf/abortion-incidence-service-availability-us-2017.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abortions in 2017}}}\uc2 , according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/journals/psrh/2017/01/abortion-incidence-and-service-availability-united-states-2014"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 31% in 2014}}}\uc2  ; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/sites/default/files/pdfs/pubs/journals/psrh.46e0414.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23% in 2011}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/sites/default/files/pdfs/pubs/journals/4304111.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17% in 2008}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/journals/psrh/2008/abortion-united-states-incidence-and-access-services-2005"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6% in 2005}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1931-2393.2003.tb00079.x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6% in 2001}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  banned in more than a dozen states since Roe v Wade fell, the number of legal abortions in the US has been reported to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/WeCountReport_April2023Release.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fallen by 6%}}}\uc2 . However, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2023/04/13/us/abortion-pill-order-online-mifepristone.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase}}}\uc2  in people ordering pills online may be significantly mitigating that drop.\par \par \uc2 It may be this impact, in offsetting the effect of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, that is fueling the rightwing push against the pills.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230517ej5h000h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
