\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  pill case: where does the lawsuit against the pill currently stand?\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,122 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 13:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The fifth circuit court of appeals is considering the future of mifepristone after the supreme court blocked new restrictions\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the fifth circuit court of appeals will consider the future of mifepristone, a crucial drug used in over half of US abortions, after a district court judge ruled the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) was wrong to approve it more than two decades ago. Access to the drug remains unchanged in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal while the case proceeds.\par \par \uc2 The hearings follow a lengthy succession of court judgments. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-latest-news-supreme-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 late April}}}\uc2 , the supreme court blocked court-ordered restrictions on mifepristone while a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups targeting the pill continues.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is the most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case to make its way through the courts since Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022. Fourteen states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last 11 months, but new restrictions on the pill would apply even in states where the procedure is still allowed.\par \par \uc2 What happened?\par \par \uc2 In November a lawsuit was filed by the Christian legal group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/Alliance-for-Hippocratic-Medicine-v-FDA-2022-11-18-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing that}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2  exceeded its regulatory authority and ignored safety concerns when it approved mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a drug that blocks progesterone, a hormone needed for a pregnancy to develop \u8211\'20\'13 more than two decades ago. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  vigorously rejected those arguments, pointing to repeated and rigorous reviews of the highly regulated drug.\par \par \uc2 A Trump-appointed federal judge in Texas, Matthew Kacsmaryk, sided with the plaintiffs, issuing a preliminary injunction on 7 April suspending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 23-year-old approval of mifepristone. He also endorsed the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 views that a previously dormant, 150-year-old anti-vice law called the Comstock Act \u8220\'20\'1Cplainly forecloses mail-order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ADF\uc2  is thought to have chosen to file the lawsuit in Amarillo, Texas, specifically so it would appear before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kacsmaryk}}}\uc2 , who is known for his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views, and employed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/08/texas-judge-kacsmaryk-abortion-pills-ruling-anti-abortion-rhetoric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rhetoric}}}\uc2  throughout his decision, referring to mifepristone as a drug used to \u8220\'20\'1Ckill the unborn human\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration took the decision to the fifth circuit court of appeals, where two judges \u8211\'20\'13 also appointed by Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 blocked the part of the ruling overturning the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s initial 2000 approval of mifepristone, but reimposed restrictions on the drug previously lifted by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . They include limiting mifepristone use after seven weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 it is currently approved through 10 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and banning delivery by mail. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  had decided in 2021 to remove the drug\u8217\'20\'19s in-person dispensing requirement during the pandemic, which broadened access by allowing the drug to be prescribed via telehealth and sent in the mail.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration appealed the ruling to the supreme court, which temporarily blocked the lower courts\u8217\'20\'19 decisions, returning the case to the fifth circuit. The high court also ruled that access to the pill will remain unchanged for the duration of the suit, which will very likely make its way back to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 What is the status of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill?\par \par \uc2 For the moment, mifepristone has not been banned and access remains unaffected as the case proceeds. Misoprostol, the second drug commonly administered alongside mifepristone to induce a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is not at issue in this lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Even a supreme court ruling should have little impact in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already banned: neither misoprostol nor mifepristone has been legally available for abortions in these states since bans came into place after the fall of Roe.\par \par \uc2 While misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 which helps to empty the uterus by causing the cervix to soften and dilate, and the uterus to contract \u8211\'20\'13 can be used safely on its own, it is less effective. Misoprostol-only abortions result in successful termination 88% of the time, and with more complicated side-effects and more need for follow-up care, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1363/psrh.12219"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent research has shown}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some of the main \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers \u8211\'20\'13 including Planned Parenthood, Carafem and \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Delivered \u8211\'20\'13 have confirmed that they are prepared to prescribe a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/mifepristone-ban-misoprostol-only-abortions-in-the-us-1850083070"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misoprostol-only regimen for abortions}}}\uc2  in the event of mifepristone being pulled off the market. Aid Access, the international group that ships \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to the US, trialled misoprostol-only regimens for abortions during the pandemic, with success.\par \par \uc2 What does the Comstock Act have to do with it?\par \par \uc2 Court watchers are looking out for what the judges will say, if anything, about the Comstock Act \u8211\'20\'13 an 1873 anti-vice law banning certain products such as contraceptives, pornography and abortifacients from being sent through the mail. That law has effectively long been dead in the water, but the plaintiffs have tried to revive it, suggesting that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  ran afoul of the Comstock Act when it made pills obtainable by mail in 2021. Other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have made similar efforts to bring back the law, viewing it as a possible avenue for banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice issued an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/olc/opinion/file/1560596/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion}}}\uc2  on Comstock in December 2022, clarifying its own opinion that the law does not apply when the sender of pills intends for them to be used lawfully. When the appeals court first considered the mifepristone case in April, the panel of judges seemed to favor the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19 arguments on Comstock, writing that the \u8220\'20\'1Cplain text\u8221\'20\'1D of of the law prohibits the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs, regardless of whether they are intended for abortions.\par \par \uc2 If Comstock is ultimately affirmed as good law, it would have sweeping impacts on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, as it could also be read to ban the mailing of any instrument used to perform abortions.\par \par \uc2 What could this case mean for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access?\par \par \uc2 If mifepristone becomes less available, and since medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts for more than half of US abortions, providers fear a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2023/02/10-us-states-would-be-hit-especially-hard-nationwide-ban-medication-abortion-using"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surge of demand}}}\uc2  on clinics providing surgical procedures. Many are already under strain from an increase in patients traveling from states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned or heavily restricted.\par \par \uc2 Online pharmacies and other telehealth providers have proliferated since Roe v Wade was overturned, enabled by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2021 decision to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent in the mail}}}\uc2 . If the courts ultimately rule that mifepristone cannot be mailed, this could shutter those businesses.\par \par \uc2 Do the implications of the case go beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration, along with a coalition of pharmaceutical companies, warned of ensuing regulatory chaos around drug approvals should the judiciary be permitted to order regulations on mifepristone opposed by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf this ruling were to stand, then there will be virtually no prescription, approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , that would be safe from these kinds of political, ideological attacks,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/04/07/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-decision-in-alliance-for-hippocratic-medicine-v-fda/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written statement}}}\uc2  after Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision in early April.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230517ej5h00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
