\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Quad summit cancelled after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calls off trip to Australia\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,740 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2023\par 10:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leaders will instead meet on sidelines of \uc2 G7\uc2  in Hiroshima this weekend. Plus, how mifepristone became a target of the US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movementDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Anthony Albanese has confirmed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/17/quad-summit-meeting-cancelled-joe-biden-calls-off-australia-trip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Sydney Quad meeting will not go ahead}}}\uc2 , after the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , pulled out of his Australian visit to deal with domestic issues.\par \par \uc2 Early this morning Albanese was still hopeful the meeting with the leaders of India and Japan could proceed with a senior representative from the US, but hours later he confirmed the event was off. Instead, the Quad nations are expected to have a sideline meeting at the \uc2 G7\uc2  summit in Hiroshima this weekend, with all four leaders still attending.\par \par \uc2 Biden has cancelled a planned visit to Australia and Papua New Guinea to focus on debt limit talks as Washington stares into the abyss of a potentially catastrophic default.\par \par \uc2 The move came as the president hosted a fresh round of talks with congressional leaders at the White House in an effort to break the deadlock \u8211\'20\'13 and faced criticism from his left flank over rumored concessions to Republicans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 When will the trip be rescheduled for? It is not known when Biden will be able to reschedule his Australia trip. The postponement, due to hostile negotiations with the Republican-heavy \uc2 US Congress\uc2  over the government\u8217\'20\'19s debt ceiling, comes at a delicate time in the US\u8217\'20\'19s engagement with the Pacific region. The visit was supposed to help cement the US\u8217\'20\'19s renewed interest in the Indo-Pacific and help quell regional concerns over the Aukus agreement.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 12 weeks, overriding Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto\par \par \uc2 North Carolina has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/north-carolina-abortion-ban-veto-override"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed legislation banning most abortions after 12 weeks}}}\uc2  of pregnancy after the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-controlled general assembly successfully overrode the Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto yesterday evening.\par \par \uc2 The house completed the second and final part of the override with a vote of 72-48. The move is expected to deal a fresh blow to one of the last bastions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the south, which has been significantly curtailed after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , a Democrat, had honored a vow he made to North Carolinians to protect reproductive rights by vetoing SB 20 during a public rally in Raleigh on Saturday, which was attended by thousands. But in separate votes yesterday, the state senate and house cleared the path to put new restrictions into place.\par \par \uc2 Cooper condemned the decision to override his veto and move forward with the ban, and said he would do \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything I can to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in North Carolina because women\u8217\'20\'19s lives depend on it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What does the legislation say? Last week, Republicans had rushed the bill through the house, drawing criticism from other legislators and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates. The 46-page bill, in addition to banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks, extends the waiting period for people seeking abortions to 72 hours, requires providers to send sensitive information to the state department of health and human services, and requires clinics to obtain special licensing that would result in clinic closures throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 Court rules \uc2 Theranos\uc2  founder \uc2 Elizabeth Holmes\uc2  must go to prison while she appeals against sentence\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Theranos\uc2  founder \uc2 Elizabeth Holmes\uc2  must begin serving her prison sentence while she appeals against her conviction on charges of defrauding investors in her failed blood-testing startup and must jointly pay $452m in restitution to the victims of her crimes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/may/17/court-rules-theranos-founder-elizabeth-holmes-must-go-to-prison-while-she-appeals-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a court in San Francisco has ruled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Holmes, who rose to fame after claiming \uc2 Theranos\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s small machines could run an array of diagnostic tests with just a few drops of blood, was convicted at a trial in San Jose, California, in 2022 and sentenced to 11 years and three months in prison.\par \par \uc2 She had asked the ninth US circuit court of appeals to pause her sentence on 25 April, two days before she was to report to prison. The court denied her bail application yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The judge will set a new date for Holmes, 39, to leave her home in the San Diego area and report to prison. In a separate ruling, Judge \uc2 Edward Davila\uc2  held Holmes jointly liable for the restitution payments and ordered her to pay the $452m with her former lover and top \uc2 Theranos\uc2  lieutenant, Ramesh \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Sunny\u8221\'20\'1D Balwani\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is Balwani in prison? Yes, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/dec/07/former-theranos-exec-sunny-balwani-prison-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began a nearly 13-year prison sentence in April}}}\uc2  after being convicted on 12 counts of fraud and conspiracy last July. He was put in a southern California prison last month after losing a similar effort to remain free on bail while appealing against his conviction.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s state assembly is to consider legislation to stop registered charities\par \par \uc2 sending tens of millions of dollars a year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/new-york-law-aims-stop-funding-israeli-settlements-west-bank"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to fund illegal Israeli settlements}}}\uc2 . The state assembly member Zohran Mamdani has introduced the \u8220\'20\'1CNot on Our Dime!: Ending New York Funding of Israeli Settler Violence\u8221\'20\'1D Act to prohibit tax-deductible donations from being used to expel Palestinians from their land.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kim Jong-un\par \par \uc2 has inspected North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s first military spy satellite and given the go-ahead for its \u8220\'20\'1Cfuture action plan\u8221\'20\'1D, according to state media. Kim met the \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-permanent satellite launch preparatory committee\u8221\'20\'1D yesterday before viewing the satellite, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/17/glimpse-of-north-korean-spy-satellite-in-kim-jong-un-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California police are seeking the assailant who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/california-attack-homeless-man-severed-hand-sword"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severed a homeless man\u8217\'20\'19s hand}}}\uc2  with a sword. Investigators with the police department\u8217\'20\'19s robbery-homicide unit have yet to arrest anyone over the incident in Riverside, a city about 50 miles south-east of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A bizarre exchange with reporters has raised new questions about the return of\par \par \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\par \par \uc2 , California\u8217\'20\'19s senior senator who has been absent from Washington for months due to shingles. The 89-year-old legislator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/dianne-feinstein-says-hasnt-been-gone-from-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insisted she had been working}}}\uc2  when questioned by reporters yesterday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats have moved to expel George Santos from Congress. The New York Republican won election in November last year but his r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9 has been shown to be largely made up and his campaign finances and past behaviour, some allegedly criminal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/17/george-santos-democrats-expel-indicted-republican-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been scrutinised in tremendous detail}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Plastic pollution could be slashed by 80% by 2040, \uc2 UN\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 Global {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/may/16/plastic-pollution-could-be-slashed-by-80-by-2040-un-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plastic pollution could be slashed by 80% by 2040}}}\uc2 , according to a report from the \uc2 UN Environment Programme\uc2  (Unep). The changes needed were major, but were also practical and affordable, the agency said. The first step was to eliminate unnecessary plastics, such as excessive packaging, the report said. Then next steps were to increase the reuse of plastics, such as refillable bottles, boost recycling and replace plastics with greener alternatives. Such a shift, driven by government policies and changes in the plastic industry, would mean plastic pollution would drop to about 40m tons in 2040, rather than 227m tons if no action were taken. The changes would bring benefits worth trillions of dollars between now and 2040, the report said, by reducing the damage caused by plastics to health, the climate and the environment.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: How mifepristone became a target of the US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\par \par \uc2 The future of mifepristone, a crucial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug, is currently under question as US courts consider a challenge brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups. Considering medication is the most common US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  method, it is the most significant reproductive rights case to make its way through the courts since Roe v Wade was overturned in 2022. The groups suing the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  over its approval of the drug claim that the drug poses a threat to women and girls \u8211\'20\'13 contrary to scientific consensus \u8211\'20\'13 and should never have been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than two decades ago. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  vehemently stands by its approval of the pill, with the Biden administration emphasizing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s rigorous safety reviews of the drug. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/16/how-mifepristone-became-a-target-of-the-us-anti-abortion-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 So what\u8217\'20\'19s the story of the drug, and how did we get here?}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: The women wearing \u8216\'20\'18subway T-shirts\u8217\'20\'19 over outfits to avoid creepy stares\par \par \uc2 New Yorkers love to shed their winter layers as soon as the first signs of spring hit the city. But for women who take advantage of sundress season, the much-anticipated warm weather can also bring unwanted attention. Not that it should. There is little evidence that harassment or assault is motivated by what a victim wears, and clothing is never a justification for cat-calling. Still, anyone who does not want to risk it may use the subway shirt, which is also known colloquially as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2023/may/16/subway-t-shirt-new-york-women-tiktok"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an \u8220\'20\'1Coutfit dampener\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Everyone has a subway shirt in their closet: a baggy, shapeless cover-up meant to divert eyeballs away from the body. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an oversized shirt we wear over cute outfits so strange men don\u8217\'20\'19t bother you on the train,\u8221\'20\'1D one creator wrote on TikTok. \u8220\'20\'1CJust know if you see me in a white button down, the real fit is underneath,\u8221\'20\'1D another woman commented.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Cop28 host UAE\u8217\'20\'19s approach is \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19, says \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s\par \par \uc2 former climate chief\par \par \uc2 The United Arab Emirates\u8217\'20\'19 approach to the Cop28 climate summit it will preside over in November is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect threat to the survival of vulnerable nations\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/may/16/cop28-host-uae-climate-united-arab-emirates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the UN\u8217\'20\'19s former climate chief}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Christiana Figueres\uc2 , who was pivotal to the delivery of the landmark Paris climate agreement in 2015, also said the country holding the presidency of the \uc2 UN\uc2  summit could not put forward its own position and had to be neutral. The UAE is a big oil and gas producer, and the designated president of the Cop28 summit is Sultan \uc2 Al Jaber\uc2 , who is also the head of the UAE\u8217\'20\'19s national oil and gas company, Adnoc. Figueres was responding to a speech by \uc2 Al Jaber\uc2  in which he said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must be laser focused on phasing out fossil fuel emissions, while phasing up viable, affordable zero-carbon alternatives.\u8221\'20\'1D That was widely interpreted to mean using carbon capture and storage technology to capture CO 2 emissions, and not completely phasing out fossil fuels themselves.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230517ej5h000uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
