\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden reportedly cuts Asia trip short as debt ceiling talks enter crunch time \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Chris Stein and Fran Lawther (earlier) \par \uc2 5,068 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2023\par 21:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President will return to the US on Sunday immediately following G7 to ensure Congress takes action to avoid 1 June default\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re only 16 days away from 1 June, when the \uc2 US government\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 having hit the legal limit on how much money it can borrow months ago \u8211\'20\'13 is expected to exhaust its cash on hand and could default on its debt obligations, potentially causing a financial calamity.\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with top Republican and Democratic lawmakers in congress to negotiate a deal to raise the debt ceiling. Biden will be cutting his trip to Asia short, so he can continue negotiations. House Speaker Kevin McCarthy signaled that the talk was promising, even though Republicans and Democrats remain \u8220\'20\'1Cfar apart\u8221\'20\'1D on issues.\par \par \uc2 Republicans want to cut federal spending before agreeing to lift the debt ceiling \u8211\'20\'13 scaling safety net back programs for poor Americans and seniors. They want to impose work requirements for recipients of public assistance, which could be a non-starter for many Democrats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A number of elections are happening today. Kentucky Republicans will vote on a challenger to take on the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , and special elections in Pennsylvania could determine which party control\u8217\'20\'19s the state\u8217\'20\'19s house of representatives.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the Senate banking committee, Democratic and Republican lawmakers were skeptical of explanations from former \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  CEO \uc2 Gregory W Becker\uc2  for why the institution went under.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the White House said the meeting today was \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive and direct \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president directed staff to continue to meet daily on outstanding issues. He said that he would like to check in with leaders later this week by phone, and meet with them upon his return from overseas,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The US could default on its debts by 1 June if negotiations do not conclude, and the debt ceiling is not raised, by then.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s explainer on the debt ceiling, and the significance of these talks:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/may/16/what-is-debt-ceiling-limit-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is the US debt ceiling and what will happen if it is not raised?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a positive meeting,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , the House minority leader. \u8220\'20\'1CWe all agreed that default was not an option.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said that he and Jeffries were \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted\u8221\'20\'1D to getting a bipartisan bill done. \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is that we all came to agreement that we were going to continue discussions in the way that I believe Speaker McCarthy described, which was agreed to by all of us in the room together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers speak to press after debt limit meeting\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy, the Republican House speaker, said the two sides are still \u8220\'20\'1Cfar apart\u8221\'20\'1D on a debt limit deal. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is possible to get a deal by the end of the week,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, and noted that the \u8220\'20\'1Cstructure of the talks\u8221\'20\'1D has improved.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy said they\u8217\'20\'19ve agreed to have Biden appoint someone to negotiate with Republican leaders.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back in Congress, CBS News tracked down George Santos to ask him what he thinks about the push by Democrats to expel him.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he has to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrONLY ON {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSantosNY03?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepSantosNY03}}}\uc2  tells me what he thinks of a resolution introduced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRobertGarcia?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepRobertGarcia}}}\uc2  to expel him from Congress. ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/v7bUIQKDJY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/v7bUIQKDJY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nikole Killion (@NikolenDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikolenDC/status/1658551867180306434?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  is taking the blog over to keep you updated on the rest of the news for today, including the outcome of the ongoing debt ceiling talks at the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden cuts Asia trip short to address debt limit \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has cut short his trip to Asia and will return on Sunday from visiting Japan to work on reaching a deal over the debt ceiling, NBC News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING BIDEN TRIP CHANGE According to a source familiar with the president's trip planning\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden has decided to return to the United States on Sunday, immediately following the completion of the G7, to ensure Congress takes action by the deadline to avert default.\u8220\'20\'1C\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kelly O'Donnell (@KellyO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellyO/status/1658558357593116680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The president had been set to stop in Australia, and pay the first visit by an American president to Papua New Guinea. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/05/16/biden-trip-japan-australia-china/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , the three-country trip was meant to solidify allied efforts to counter China, as well as rally support for Ukraine and for fighting the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Biden is still expected to meet with leaders from the G7 group of the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest countries while in Hiroshima, Japan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 A quick vibe check from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the start of the meeting with Republican and Democratic congressional leaders in the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHello folks. Get a good picture of all of us. We\u8217\'20\'19re having a wonderful time. Everything\u8217\'20\'19s going well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said to reporters, with a laugh that seemed to indicate everything is, perhaps, not going well.\par \par \uc2 See the moment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?528128-1/president-biden-meeting-congressional-leaders-debt-limit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, McCarthy convene at White House for debt ceiling talks\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Kevin McCarthy are now in the Oval Office for their latest attempt to find an agreement on raising the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit ahead of the estimated 1 June deadline for default.\par \par \uc2 Joining them is vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and the Democratic House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 . The group said little to reporters who were allowed in briefly as the meeting began, but the lawmakers are expected to address the media at the White House once the gathering wraps up.\par \par \uc2 The question now is whether they\u8217\'20\'19ll have anything substantive to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2 , a former secretary of labor professor of public policy at the \uc2 University of California, Berkeley\uc2 , and Guardian US columnist, has also weighed in on the standoff over raising the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 He does not have much time for Republicans saying raising the debt ceiling would lead to higher spending and bigger federal debts.\par \par \uc2 Writing on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , he said:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m sick and tired of hearing this lie peddled by the GOP and corporate media. Raising the debt ceiling does not increase spending or the federal debt. It simply allows the government to pay bills it has already taken on\u8212\'20\'14 and defaulting on the debt would be catastrophic.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2  (@RBReich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RBReich/status/1658499178878623744?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And spelling out what he thinks a GOP plan would mean, he wrote on Monday:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe GOP\u8217\'20\'19s debt ceiling plan would mean:\par \par \uc2 -A reduction of up to 108K teachers and aides\par \par \uc2 -200K children kicked off Head Start\par \par \uc2 -Meals on Wheels taken away from 1 million seniors\par \par \uc2 -7K fewer rail safety inspection days next year alone\par \par \uc2 It's just ruthless \u8212\'20\'14 plain and simple.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert Reich\uc2  (@RBReich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RBReich/status/1658233295908347907?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy is heading to the White House now to discuss the debt limit standoff with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , alongside top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  and the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such talks have in the past not yielded a breakthrough, but there are signs that both parties are looking for a deal. Case in point: at the just-concluded White House press briefing, a reporter asked National Security Council spokesman John Kirby if Biden would continue with a trip to Asia scheduled to start on Wednesday, given the ongoing debt ceiling negotiations. Kirby indicated the president might cut his trip short:\par \par \uc2 enltrAP\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZekeJMiller?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ZekeJMiller}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CRest of [Biden's] trip is now up in the air because of debt limit negotiations?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 National Security Council\u8217\'20\'19s John Kirby: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I can speak to is G7 and going to Hiroshima. The president\u8217\'20\'19s looking forward to that. We\u8217\'20\'19re taking a look at the rest of the trip.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oOtIyRlZtI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oOtIyRlZtI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658541621044994077?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden is scheduled to attend a meeting of G7 leaders in Japan, before visiting Australia and Papua New Guinea.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Democrat introduces resolution to expel George Santos\par \par \uc2 House Democrat Robert Garcia has introduced a resolution to expel indicted fabulist George Santos from the chamber. Santos was elected as a Republican to represent the New York City suburbs last year, after which reports emerged that he lied about large parts of his resume. Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/10/george-santos-court-federal-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was indicted}}}\uc2  on federal charges of fraud and money laundering, among other allegations.\par \par \uc2 Garcia\u8217\'20\'19s resolution requires a two-thirds majority vote to pass, which is a steep hill to climb, considering Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy has said he would call for Santos to resign only if the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s ethics committee recommends it. The GOP has a slim majority in the House, and Santos supported McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s election as speaker, as well as many of his legislative priorities.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the moment Garcia introduced the resolution on the House floor:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Robert Garcia (D-CA) introduces a resolution to order \u8220\'20\'1CRep. George Santos be, and hereby is, expelled from the House of Representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/y5lwAihdtt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/y5lwAihdtt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658543043291537448?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Phillips, the founder of Democracy in Color, has written for the Guardian about what he calls the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s timidity when it comes to the debt ceiling fight with Republicans.\par \par \uc2 He writes:\par \par \uc2 One wonders what the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  is afraid of when it comes to calling the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19s bluff on raising the federal debt ceiling. While White House officials no doubt have genuine legal and policy concerns about their ability to act unilaterally to defuse the crisis, the overriding reason is probably fear of the political consequences, and on that front they are both misreading the moment and misunderstanding the composition of the country\u8217\'20\'19s electorate.\par \par \uc2 Read his full opinion piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/may/15/republicans-democrats-biden-us-debt-ceiling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House timidity on the debt ceiling is infuriating. What is it afraid of? | Stephen Phillips}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Away from US national politics, the state department has condemned the arrest of a former US consulate employee in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Robert Shonov was detained in the Russian city of Vladivostok on suspicion of \u8220\'20\'1Ccooperation on a confidential basis with a foreign state, international or foreign organization\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to AP, the state department says Shonov is a Russian national who worked at the now-closed US consulate in Vladivostok for more than 25 years. He then worked at a company the US contracted with to support its embassy in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 State department spokesman Matthew Miller told AP: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Shonov\u8217\'20\'19s only role at the time of his arrest was to compile media summaries of press items from publicly available Russian media sources.His being targeted under the \u8216\'20\'18confidential cooperation\u8217\'20\'19 statute highlights the Russian Federation\u8217\'20\'19s blatant use of increasingly repressive laws against its own citizens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 A man who allegedly attacked two congressional workers with a metal baseball bat had a history of mental illness and had assaulted someone else earlier in the day, authorities said.\par \par \uc2 The man, identified as Xuan-Kha Tran Pham, 49, of Fairfax, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , attacked the Democratic congressman \uc2 Gerry Connolly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office on Monday, shattering windows and striking two women, including an intern on her first day on the job, authorities said.\par \par \uc2 AP reports:\par \par \uc2 Staffers then managed to shelter in an inner office until officers arrived, within five minutes. Connolly said they used a stun gun to subdue Pham.\par \par \uc2 Pham, 49, has been violent before, attacking police officers last year. His father, Hy Pham, told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  his son was schizophrenic and had dealt with mental illness since his late teens. He said he had been trying, without success, to arrange mental health care for his son.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/virginia-baseball-bat-attacker-congress-mental-illness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alleged attacker of congressman\u8217\'20\'19s staff had history of mental illness, police say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the debt ceiling hangs over Washington and the US economy as a whole, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  has the answers to all your question about the high-stakes policy logjam:\par \par \uc2 The US faces an \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented economic and financial storm\u8221\'20\'1D, the treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , warned on Tuesday as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with his Republican counterparts for the latest in a series of tense talks over the US debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Time is quickly running out to find a solution, said Yellen. Without raising the debt limit, the \uc2 US government\uc2  will default on its bills, a historic first, with likely catastrophic consequences. Federal workers would be furloughed, global stock markets would crash and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  would probably drop into a recession.\par \par \uc2 Here is more on the debt ceiling and what it means for the \uc2 US government\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/may/16/what-is-debt-ceiling-limit-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What is the US debt ceiling and what will happen if it is not raised?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 In questioning before the Senate banking committee, former \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  CEO \uc2 Greg Becker\uc2  took responsibility for its collapse, but would not say if he would give back his bonus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was the CEO of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 . I take responsibility for what ultimately happened,\u8221\'20\'1D Becker said in response to questions from Republican senator Katie Britt, who asked what he would have done differently.\par \par \uc2 Britt asked him if he would return a $1.5m bonus he received before the institution went under, but Becker was vague. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m committed to cooperate with the process, with the regulators and other agencies that I know are going to be looking into that specific question,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 Greg Becker\uc2 , former CEO of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 , arrives to testify on Capitol Hill on 16 May. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COK, well, I hope even if, for whatever reason, they say you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to, I hope that you dig deep and you decide that that needs to be somewhere besides in your pocket,\u8221\'20\'1D Britt replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy says he intends to push for more work requirements on public programs\par \par \uc2 Ahead of his meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  later today, Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy has made clear that he intends to push for more work requirements on public assistance programs:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker Kevin McCarthy calls for work requirements for \u8220\'20\'1Call the programs\u8221\'20\'1D as part of debt limit negotiations:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat work requirements actually do: help people get a job \u8230\'20\'26 The public wants it, both parties want it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lyUHBDu0si"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lyUHBDu0si}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658482087329136640?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Major anti-poverty programs the federal government runs include Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP), also known as food stamps, and Temporary Assistance for Needy Families, which states can use to offer cash and services to the poor. Republicans have long called for more requirements to ensure people receiving such aid are made to work or be looking for a job, but supporters of the programs say that would harm their effectiveness.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the Senate, the top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  made clear that he\u8217\'20\'19s letting McCarthy take the lead in negotiating with the White House:\par \par \uc2 enltrAhead of the second debt ceiling meeting, Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  signals he\u8217\'20\'19s still backing the House GOP:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, for the second time, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be glad to sit in at the White House to support Speaker McCarthy and to urge President Biden to start operating in reality.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a72rmq3kXD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a72rmq3kXD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658483491221417984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 While Republicans in statehouses under their control are moving to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, the party\u8217\'20\'19s current presidential frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has remained mum about how far he would go in curbing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 He was asked repeatedly last week at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/10/trump-voters-republican-new-hampshire-cnn-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 town hall hosted by CNN}}}\uc2  if he would sign a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, but refused to answer. He was similarly unclear in an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://themessenger.com/news/exclusive-trump-interview-with-the-messenger-hits-desantis-abortion-new-media-blitz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published yesterday by the Messenger}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That vagueness has provided an opening for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who is expected to run for the Republican nomination while trying to close what polls indicate is a wide deficit in support between him and Trump. The former president has attacked DeSantis with a variety of colorful nicknames, and while the Florida governor has refrained from firing back to the same degree, he did criticize Trump over the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue in a press conference today:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) criticizes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for refusing to commit to a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban during his CNN town hall:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe didn\u8217\'20\'19t give an answer about, \u8216\'20\'18Would you have signed the heartbeat bill?\u8217\'20\'19 \u8230\'20\'26 I was proud to do it. He won\u8217\'20\'19t answer whether he would sign it or not.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JPueGjEp8B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JPueGjEp8B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658473442981859328?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, Republicans are today set to use their recently achieved supermajority in the state legislature to override the Democratic governor\u8217\'20\'19s veto of a bill banning most abortions after 12 weeks of pregnancy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-veto-override-north-carolina-4282913637b499490494dd3e3cce3478"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democratic governor Roy Cooper vetoed the ban this weekend, which allows abortions at up to 24 weeks of pregnancy for \u8220\'20\'1Clife threatening\u8221\'20\'1D anomalies and 20 weeks for cases of rape and incest, according to the AP. The GOP has a veto-proof majority in the Senate, and attained the same in the House after a Democrat who said she supported protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access switched parties.\par \par \uc2 Republican leaders in both chambers believe they have the votes lined up to override Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s veto, while the AP says the governor has singled out four Republican lawmakers who he said campaigned on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in an effort to get them to oppose the bill.\par \par \uc2 Cooper discussed the ban in an interview with MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. Roy Cooper (D-NC), ahead of GOP-controlled state legislature potentially overturning his veto of a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight-wing politicians should not be in the exam room with women and their doctors... We need to leave the medicine to doctors and decisions to women.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/C4FTDyUfp7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/C4FTDyUfp7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1658482371992354819?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-\uc2 SVB\uc2  chief criticised for not having a chief risk officer before collapse\par \par \uc2 Back to the Senate banking committee, Democratic and Republican lawmakers were skeptical of explanations from former \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  CEO \uc2 Gregory W Becker\uc2  for why the institution went under.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat sounds a lot like the dog ate my homework,\u8221\'20\'1D remarked the committee\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic chair \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , after Becker in his opening statement blamed the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest rate hikes as well as what he called a social media-fueled bank run for the collapse.\par \par \uc2 Brown asked Becker to explain why \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/mar/17/why-silicon-valley-bank-collapsed-svb-fail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not have a chief risk officer on its staff}}}\uc2  for some of last year. That\u8217\'20\'19s a position typically tasked with guarding against the type of insolvency that the bank eventually fell into. \u8220\'20\'1CWe took risk management seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D Becker responded, and blamed the gap on the time it took to find a suitable candidate.\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican Tim Scott indicated he found Becker\u8217\'20\'19s explanation wanting. \u8220\'20\'1CYou said you took risk management seriously. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to believe that comment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, pointing out that at the time of its collapse, 90% of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deposits were uninsured by the federal government.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are a few of the other elections happening across the United States today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kentucky Republicans will vote on a challenger to take on the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , who is standing for a second term in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Control of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives \u8211\'20\'13 and the fate of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access referendum the GOP may put before voters \u8211\'20\'13 is at stake in two special elections that will determine which party controls the chamber, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pennsylvania-election-legislature-politics-campaign-fe4d515358ba45a9f83283afac3c8fe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 . Democrats need to win just one of these to cement their majority, and thwart Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 efforts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Pennsylvania, today is the day of the city\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary for mayor \u8211\'20\'13 the victor of which is likely to win the general election in the solidly blue city. As with the Chicago mayor\u8217\'20\'19s race earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/14/us/politics/philadelphia-mayor-democratic-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2  that the contest will serve as a bellwether of voters\u8217\'20\'19 appetites for progressive leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jacksonville, Florida is one of the few major cities in the United States with a Republican mayor, \uc2 Lenny Curry\uc2 . Term limits prevent him from running for another term, and polls are open in a runoff election today where voters will decide whether to replace him with another Republican, or hand the reins of the city to the Democratic candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are a number of elections happening across the country today, including in Kentucky, where a Republican secretary of state who has taken pride in expanding voter turnout is facing a challenge from within his party, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/kira-lerner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kira Lerner}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s Republican secretary of state has earned widespread praise for increasing his state\u8217\'20\'19s voter turnout during the coronavirus pandemic and for expanding opportunities to vote. He has also shot down conspiracy theories about the 2020 election and defended his state\u8217\'20\'19s election system from claims of fraud, a stance that could cost him his job.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Michael Adams is facing a primary challenge from two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  who align themselves with the growing faction within the GOP who believe elections are frequently rigged and stolen. The winner will face Buddy Wheatley, a Democrat and former state representative, in November.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Adams said it would \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D be worth it if he loses the race to have defended and expanded Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s elections, but he was hopeful that Kentucky Republicans understood the ways his reforms had benefited them.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/16/kentucky-republican-secretary-of-state-primary-michael-adams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky Republican who expanded voting faces primary threat from right}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Failed Silicon Valley, Signature bank executives face Senate grilling\par \par \uc2 The former leaders of collapsed financial institutions \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  and \uc2 Signature Bank\uc2  are set to testify before the Senate banking committee in a hearing starting now.\par \par \uc2 The witnesses include the former \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Gregory W Becker\uc2 , Scott A Shay, former chairman and co-founder of \uc2 Signature Bank\uc2 , and its former president, \uc2 Eric R Howell\uc2 . The two banks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/mar/12/silicon-valley-bank-collapse-no-bailout-janet-yellen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were shut down by federal authorities}}}\uc2  in the course of a weekend in March after suddenly becoming insolvent, raising fears of a crisis that could spread across the financial system. Another major regional bank, First Republic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/may/01/us-banking-titan-jp-morgan-to-snap-up-most-of-first-republic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed the following month}}}\uc2 , and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear the extent of the risk posed to other financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 Senators will probably ask about that at the hearing, which you can follow at the live stream embedded at the top of the page.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Congress gurus at Punchbowl News have a rundown of all the reasons to be worried about lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to actually pass a debt limit compromise ahead of the 1 June deadline.\par \par \uc2 Their concerns focus on the logistics of both reaching a compromise and getting a bill approved by Congress. Despite all the meetings, including the one scheduled for this afternoon between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Kevin McCarthy and other congressional leaders, the sides still appear to be far apart.\par \par \uc2 Here, according to Punchbowl, are a few of the things that could still go wrong:\par \par \uc2 enltrTiming. House Republican leadership estimates congress needs 10 days to move this deal if and when it comes together. There are 10 weekdays until June 1 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B89V6Nad6k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B89V6Nad6k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658456474526392320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrUnlike other negotiations, this thing is real big. And there is no driving principal. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HaMl1p8iCZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HaMl1p8iCZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658456506965061635?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden leaves for Japan *tomorrow* for an eight-day trip. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/isQuW9YWxu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/isQuW9YWxu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1658456522626588675?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 16, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  says failing to raise debt ceiling would spark new financial crisis\par \par \uc2 In a speech this morning to a group of community bankers, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  outlined the consequences of failing to raise the debt ceiling, saying the economy\u8217\'20\'19s recovery from the Covid-19 pandemic would be undone and a new financial crisis would be triggered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my assessment \u8211\'20\'13 and that of economists across the board \u8211\'20\'13 a US default would generate an economic and financial catastrophe. Over the past few years, American families and businesses \u8211\'20\'13 including many of yours \u8211\'20\'13 have worked hard to mount a historic economic recovery. A default would reverse all of the hard-earned progress that we\u8217\'20\'19ve made. And it would set us back even further,\u8221\'20\'1D she told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1484"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a meeting}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 Independent Community Bankers of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 . Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 She described a scenario where the government would be unable to pay its bills, disrupting government services such as air traffic control and law enforcement as well as payments to military veterans and social security recipients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd of course, the financial crisis that accompanies a default on our debt could multiply the severity of the downturn,\u8221\'20\'1D Yellen continued. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  market serves as the very bedrock of the global financial system. There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason for that: the world has never doubted that America will pay the principal and interest on its bonds \u8211\'20\'13 in full and on time. That\u8217\'20\'19s a fundamental principle of modern finance. A default would crack open the foundations upon which our financial system is built. It is very conceivable that we\u8217\'20\'19d see a number of financial markets break \u8211\'20\'13 with worldwide panic triggering margin calls, runs and fire sales.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yellen confirms 1 June deadline for debt limit standoff\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1483"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  to the Republican speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, released yesterday, the treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , confirmed the first day of June remains the estimated date when the \uc2 US government\uc2  could default if the debt limit is not raised, dashing hopes that incoming tax revenue or other measures could push the deadline back further.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith additional information now available, I am writing to note that we still estimate that Treasury will likely no longer be able to satisfy all of the government\u8217\'20\'19s obligations if Congress has not acted to raise or suspend the debt limit by early June, and potentially as early as June 1,\u8221\'20\'1D Yellen wrote, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe actual date Treasury exhausts extraordinary measures could be a number of days or weeks later than these estimates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then warned McCarthy that even if a default is avoided at the last minute, the protracted uncertainty has already caused problems for the US economy:\par \par \uc2 We have learned from past debt limit impasses that waiting until the last minute to suspend or increase the debt limit can cause serious harm to business and consumer confidence, raise short-term borrowing costs for taxpayers, and negatively impact the credit rating of the United States. In fact, we have already seen Treasury\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing costs increase substantially for securities maturing in early June. If Congress fails to increase the debt limit, it would cause severe hardship to American families, harm our global leadership position, and raise questions about our ability to defend our national security interests.\par \par \uc2 I continue to urge Congress to protect the full faith and credit of the United States by acting as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and McCarthy to meet as debt ceiling talks enter crunch time\par \par \uc2 Good mornings, US politics blog readers. Talks between Democrats and Republicans over raising the debt limit have gone the direction the pessimists told us they would. We\u8217\'20\'19re only 16 days away from 1 June, when the \uc2 US government\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 having hit the legal limit on how much money it can borrow months ago \u8211\'20\'13 is expected to exhaust its cash on hand and could default on its debt obligations, potentially causing a financial calamity.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and top lawmakers in Congress have seen this day coming for months, and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been negotiating for weeks, but there\u8217\'20\'19s still no deal to raise the borrowing limit even though both parties say a default must be avoided.\par \par \uc2 The good news here is that Biden, Kevin McCarthy and congressional leaders are meeting at 3pm ET, so perhaps a breakthrough is in the offing.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The treasury secretary, \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , is speaking this morning to a conference of the \uc2 Independent Community Bankers of America\uc2  in Washington DC, where she may elaborate on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s view of the debt ceiling standoff.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 You may hear more about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/fbi-durham-report-trump-russia-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the report}}}\uc2  special counsel John Durham released on Monday examining the origins of the 2016 investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ties to Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michael McCaul, the Republican chair of the House foreign affairs committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/blinken-mccaul-afghanistan-withdrawal-kabul-e5710fb04c170739b3de1bec02d15daa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may hold}}}\uc2  the secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , in contempt over his refusal to turn over a 2021 dissent cable written by embassy staff in Kabul, Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230516ej5g001jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
