\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley downplays federal  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 785 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2023\par 13:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The former South Carolina governor \u8211\'20\'13 far behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the polls \u8211\'20\'13 says nationwide ban is currently unviable\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nikki-haley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nikki Haley}}}\uc2 , the former governor of South Carolina who is vying for the 2024 Republican presidential nomination, has distanced herself from calls for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, saying that to promise such a universal barrier to terminations would be to lie to the American people.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with CBS News\u8217\'20\'19s Face the Nation on Sunday, Haley declined to follow some of her other potential Republican rivals for the presidency by backing a nationwide ban through congressional legislation. Instead, she said it was up to each state to set its own limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some states that have been pro-life \u8211\'20\'13 I welcome that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some states that have erred on the side of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 I wish that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the case. We need to make sure that people\u8217\'20\'19s voices are heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley, 51, is firmly in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  wing of the Republican party and has the track record to prove it. As South Carolina governor, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2016/05/25/politics/sc-abortion-bill/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law}}}\uc2  a provision that bans abortions after 20 weeks, with no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 That law went into effect after the decision by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  last June to overturn the nationwide right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite her hardline position, the Republican presidential candidate is now attempting to soften that image by detaching herself from talk of a federal ban. The disappointing result of the party in last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections was widely attributed to Republican messaging on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which stands starkly out of line with the broad pro-choice sentiments of American public opinion.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Haley, who was ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, pointed to the filibuster in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  as the reason for her hesitation on a federal ban. Under its terms, such a prohibition could only be secured with 60 votes in favour.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are in the minority in the 100-member Senate by two seats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to tell the American people the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to do a national standard, you\u8217\'20\'19d have to have a majority of the House, 60 Senate votes and a president. We haven\u8217\'20\'19t had 60 pro-life senators in 100 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CSo the idea that a Republican president could ban all abortions is not being honest with the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley\u8217\'20\'19s double-edged posture \u8211\'20\'13 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at state level, ambivalent at national level \u8211\'20\'13 will partly define the terms of her engagement with Republican competitors. She is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/03/08/1160113954/2024-republican-presidential-candidates-who-is-running-tracker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four Republican candidates}}}\uc2  who have formally declared their candidacies for the presidency, with several others waiting in the wings.\par \par \uc2 Haley launched her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/15/nikki-haley-launches-2024-presidential-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in February}}}\uc2 , presenting herself as a president for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation\u8221\'20\'1D. But she has so far struggled to find her footing, laboring from low public name recognition and only 4.2% in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2024/president/us/2024_republican_presidential_nomination-7548.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Real Clear Politics}}}\uc2  rolling average of the polls.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican hopefuls are also wrestling with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. In his fractious CNN town hall this week, Trump repeatedly declined to answer whether he would support a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, offering only such bland statements as: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is going to make a determination what he thinks is great for the country and what\u8217\'20\'19s fair for the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haley continues to tread with extreme caution around Trump, who remains the clear Republican frontrunner. Asked by Face the Nation to comment on the fact that Trump was last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/09/e-jean-carroll-wins-trump-trial-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found liable}}}\uc2  for sexually abusing E Jean Carroll, she prevaricated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a verdict and I think there\u8217\'20\'19s been an appeal, and I think the American people need to make their decision based on that,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the Republican senator from South Carolina who is exploring the possibility of a presidential run, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tim-scott-republican-president-new-hampshire-abortion-fe4edf79d4a1aa0dc77b8625e8e14135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has backed}}}\uc2  a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at 20 weeks. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican governor of Florida who spent the weekend in the critical early-voting state of Iowa in preparation for a potential presidential bid, has also aligned himself with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  hardliners.\par \par \uc2 In April he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/florida-abortion-ban-approved-c9c53311a0b2426adc4b8d0b463edad1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into Florida law}}}\uc2  an extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that comes into effect at six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Haley and DeSantis have been going at each other with increasing intensity in recent weeks, as both languish some distance behind Trump in the polls. Haley has trolled the Florida governor over his feud with \uc2 Disney\uc2 , calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cthin-skinned\u8221\'20\'1D and inviting the entertainment giant to move Disney World to South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230514ej5e001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
