\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump town hall live: ex-president repeats election lies and denies sexual abuse verdict to mostly Republican crowd \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 3,005 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 May 2023\par 02:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican voter event in New Hampshire comes after Trump is told to pay $5m in damages to E Jean Carroll\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Well, that happened.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of about an hour, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  dodged questions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c41ca8f08c38c9839a869#block-645c41ca8f08c38c9839a869"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c378f8f08247b22aa6885#block-645c378f8f08247b22aa6885"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsehoods}}}\uc2  and lobbed insults at his enemies, all before a frequently clapping and cheering crowd of New Hampshire Republicans. CNN host Kaitlan Collins tried to get the former president to answer the questions she and audience members put to him, and what he did and did not say was indeed telling.\par \par \uc2 Here are the highlights, if you can call them that:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-645c33658f08e5a61abaf5a9#block-645c33658f08e5a61abaf5a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would pardon}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmany\u8221\'20\'1D of those convicted for crimes related to the January 6 insurrection \u8211\'20\'13 a brutal attack which he repeatedly downplayed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite a jury\u8217\'20\'19s finding yesterday that Trump was civilly liable for sexual abuse and defamation, the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c362f8f08247b22aa687e#block-645c362f8f08247b22aa687e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied knowing}}}\uc2  advice columnist E Jean Carroll, whose lawsuit led to the judgment.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrat \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  said CNN hosting the town hall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c3b158f08e5a61abaf5d4#block-645c3b158f08e5a61abaf5d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a mistake}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Collins pressed Trump on whether or not he would sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c39a28f08247b22aa688b#block-645c39a28f08247b22aa688b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would not say}}}\uc2  either way.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former president{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c3d1d8f08247b22aa689c#block-645c3d1d8f08247b22aa689c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remained cagey}}}\uc2  about supporting Ukraine against Russia, instead insisting he could stop their war in \u8220\'20\'1C24 hours\u8221\'20\'1D. A former ally said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/10/trump-town-hall-cnn-republicans-live-updates?page=with:block-645c454f8f08c38c9839a870#block-645c454f8f08c38c9839a870"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what Trump really means}}}\uc2  is that he would let Moscow win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am BST\par \par \uc2 You can expect to hear about this town hall for days.\par \par \uc2 Critics will seize on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s statements, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s decision to hold the event and host Kaitlan Collins \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to nail down the former president\u8217\'20\'19s positions on various issues.\par \par \uc2 Already, Politico reports that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s advisers see his appearance as a success:\par \par \uc2 enltrA Trump adviser called tonight's CNN town hall a "home run" and "presidential." The printout of tweets about Jan. 6 was Trump's idea.\par \par \uc2 Another said it was "fantastic" and an opportunity for CNN viewers to hear him talk about policy. They are happy with Trump's performance.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Meridith McGraw (@meridithmcgraw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/meridithmcgraw/status/1656470771558916096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC) \uc2 says the town hall served as a reminder of what kind of politician Trump is.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people were just reintroduced, in primetime, to a dangerous, extreme candidate who seeks to undermine democracy and is the frontrunner for the nomination of a party that is increasingly beholden to its most right-wing fringes,\u8221\'20\'1D the DNC said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , the former Republican governor of New Jersey who is today among the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s foes, said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wavering on whether he would support Ukraine was telling:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump says he would end the war in Ukraine in 24 hours tonight on CNN. Despite how ridiculous that is to say, I suspect he would try to do it by turning Ukraine over to Putin and Russia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Putin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Putin}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19sPuppet\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  (@GovChristie) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovChristie/status/1656467572383010817?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump asked Georgia election officials to "find" more votes\par \par \uc2 Questioned about the ongoing criminal investigation into election interference in Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  misrepresented a phone call with the state\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, falsely claiming, \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask him to find anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A recording of the phone call to Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , revealed that Trump had said, \u8220\'20\'1CI just want to find 11,780 votes.\u8221\'20\'1D The former president said in the town hall that he called to \u8220\'20\'1Cquestion\u8221\'20\'1D the election. But the recording suggested that he clearly pressured the official to overturn the election results in his favor.\par \par \uc2 enltrCOLLINS: You asked him to find you votes\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : I didn't ask him to find anything\par \par \uc2 COLLINS: We've heard the audio {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KvKQxMUBYb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KvKQxMUBYb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1656466685061132288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 'Do you want four more years of that?' asks Biden\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wasted no time in responding to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s statements at the just-concluded CNN town hall:\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s simple, folks.\par \par \uc2 Do you want four more years of that?\par \par \uc2 If you don\u8217\'20\'19t, pitch in to our campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EwCflbYn22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/EwCflbYn22}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1656467466145415171?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am BST\par \par \uc2 After an hour and change, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s town hall with CNN has wrapped up.\par \par \uc2 The former president was slippery as always, often refusing to outline his positions in response to questions put to him by host Kaitlan Collins. She closed by asking him if he would commit to accepting the results of the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, if I think it\u8217\'20\'19s an honest election, absolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D he said \u8211\'20\'13 a statement that left plenty of room for him to not accept the result.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: do family separations deter migrants?\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who as president faced widespread outrage for separating families at the US southern border, defended the policy, saying it has a deterrent effect: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople don\u8217\'20\'19t come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is not clear evidence suggesting that harsh policies such as family separation deter asylum seekers from coming to the US. A 2017 pilot program of family separation was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/monkey-cage/wp/2018/05/31/does-separating-families-at-the-border-discourage-immigration-heres-what-the-research-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed by an increase}}}\uc2  of families entering the US at the border. A 2018 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/family-separation-detention-deter-immigration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis found}}}\uc2  that the policy was not having the intended effect.\par \par \uc2 Immigrant rights groups note that policies like detaining children or separating them from their families do not discourage people from coming and can instead lead to more dangerous journeys.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump demurs on supporting Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Host Kaitlan Collins repeatedly asked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to clarify his position on supporting Ukraine against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion, but the former president instead danced around the questions and refused to condemn Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think in terms of winning and losing, I think in terms of getting it settled so we stop killing all these people,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he wants Russia or Ukraine to win, Trump replied, \u8220\'20\'1CI want everybody to stop dying,\u8221\'20\'1D before implying he could end the war as soon as he returned to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwenty-four hours, I\u8217\'20\'19ll have it done,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: no, it is not legal to kill babies after they are born\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  falsely claimed that pro-choice Democrats want to \u8220\'20\'1Ckill the baby\u8221\'20\'1D after they are born, an assertion that went unchecked in the CNN town hall.\par \par \uc2 The former president also suggested \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups want doctors to be able to \u8220\'20\'1Cexecute\u8221\'20\'1D babies. This false and inflammatory claim was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/04/28/us/politics/trump-abortion-fact-check.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 common refrain}}}\uc2  of the former president during the last election and has no basis in fact.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent much of the town hall so far repeating false claims about the 2020 election and further attacking E Jean Carroll, who a jury determined yesterday he is liable for sexually abusing.\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , an influential progressive Democrat in the House of Representatives, says CNN should never allowed the event to happen:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN should be ashamed of themselves.\par \par \uc2 They have lost total control of this \u8220\'20\'1Ctown hall\u8221\'20\'1D to again be manipulated into platforming election disinformation, defenses of Jan 6th, and a public attack on a sexual abuse victim.\par \par \uc2 The audience is cheering him on and laughing at the host.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1656454979790487553?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve just hit the first commercial break of this two-hour long town hall, but before that, host Kaitlan Collins tried repeatedly to get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to say whether he would sign a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The former president danced around the question again and again, saying only that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery complex issue\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was \u8220\'20\'1Clooking at a solution\u8221\'20\'1D for it. He also brought up various other accomplishments of his administration, such as the three conservative supreme court justices he appointed.\par \par \uc2 All three signed on to last June\u8217\'20\'19s opinion overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: Trump did have chance to testify in Carroll case\par \par \uc2 Trump misleadingly suggested that the judge in the sexual abuse and defamation trial brought by writer E Jean Carroll had prevented him from producing evidence, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHe allowed us to put nothing in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly made false claims that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot allowed to speak or defend\u8221\'20\'1D himself. But Trump did not call any witnesses, nor did he make an appearance during the two week-trial, except when excerpts of a video deposition from last year were played in the courtroom.\par \par \uc2 The judge, Lewis A Kaplan, whom the former president has repeatedly attacked, told Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team that he could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-lawsuit-e-jean-carroll-trump-will-not-testify-rape-defemation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file a request to testify}}}\uc2 , but he chose not to. The jury found that the former president sexually abused Carroll, meaning subjecting her to sexual contact with the use of force and without her consent, and ordered him to pay $5m in damages.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump denies sexual abuse finding\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just addressed yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s verdict in advice columnist E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s civil lawsuit against him, in which a federal jury found him liable for sexual abuse and defamation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis woman, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know her. I never met her. I have no idea who she is,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Carroll, saying he had a picture taken with Carroll and her husband \u8220\'20\'1Cyears ago\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: no evidence countries sending migrants to US from 'mental institutions'\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed without evidence that other countries are sending migrants from \u8220\'20\'1Cmental institutions\u8221\'20\'1D into the US.\par \par \uc2 The former president has repeatedly made this claim, but there is no evidence to support it. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has been unable to produce evidence of this, CNN recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/29/politics/fact-check-trump-mental-institutions-migrants-doctor/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . Anti-immigration groups have also said they are unaware of what Trump may be referencing with these remarks. CNN did a \u8220\'20\'1Cbroad search\u8221\'20\'1D for any evidence of this story and came up empty.\par \par \uc2 Trump also said the US was suffering from \u8220\'20\'1Copen borders\u8221\'20\'1D in his initial remarks on immigration. On the contrary, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/08/us/politics/biden-trump-immigration-title-42.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maintained many of the policies of the Trump administration}}}\uc2 , angering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/2023/feb/23/joe-biden-immigration-policy-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigrant rights\u8217\'20\'19 groups}}}\uc2 . The Biden administration also recently announced it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/biden-sends-troops-to-mexico-border-title-42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending}}}\uc2  1,500 active-duty troops to the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump would pardon 'many' January 6 rioters\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he would pardon \u8220\'20\'1Cmany\u8221\'20\'1D of those convicted for crimes related to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am inclined to pardon many of them. I can\u8217\'20\'19t say for every single one because a couple of them, probably, they got out of control,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said in response to question from a Republican voter in the audience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have two standards of justice of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued. \u8220\'20\'1CMy answer is I am most likely, if I get in, I will, most likely. I would say it will be a large portion of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Fact check: 2020 election fraud claims remain baseless\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no evidence of widespread fraud, and election officials across the US, including Republican leaders, have repeatedly reaffirmed this over the last two years.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s own efforts to show that thousands of ballots cast under the names of deceased people in Georgia came up empty, with findings that contradicted the former president\u8217\'20\'19s claims, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/17/trump-research-voter-fraud-claims-debunked"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent report revealed}}}\uc2 . There is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/11/10/us/politics/voting-fraud.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no evidence}}}\uc2  in any state of fraud or irregularities that affected any election outcomes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wasted no time in repeating his debunked claims that the 2020 election was stolen from him.\par \par \uc2 In response to a question from host Kaitlan Collins about why he should be returned to the White House considering the January 6 insurrection and his refusal to acknowledge his defeat three years ago, Trump quickly veered into his oft-repeated conspiracy theories about his loss to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that when you look at that result, and when you look at what happened during that election, unless you\u8217\'20\'19re a very stupid person, you see what happens a lot of people in this audience and maybe a couple of people understand what happened was a rigged election,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said.\par \par \uc2 Collins pressed him to acknowledge his 2020 election loss. Trump demurred, instead shifting to complaining about border security.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just walked onstage in New Hampshire, where he was greeted with applause and cheers from the crowd, some of whom stood up to clap.\par \par \uc2 All of which makes sense: Trump remains popular among the GOP, and many in the audience are supporters of the party.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN town hall with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  begins\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s town hall with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has kicked off in New Hampshire, with the former president and current frontrunner for the Republican nomination facing questions from GOP and undeclared voters over the next two hours. Expect them to ask about everything from his stances on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and US assistance to Ukraine to his myriad legal troubles \u8211\'20\'13 particularly the sexual abuse verdict that came yesterday.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be covering the town hall as it happens on this blog, and be joined by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levin}}}\uc2  in Los Angeles, who will be focused on fact-checking Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 In a post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110345987304603640"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his Truth }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/110345987304603640"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Social network}}}\uc2  a few hours ago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , sounding very much like his usual self, had this to say about the CNN town hall:\par \par \uc2 Heading to the Great State of New Hampshire. CNN LIVE, Tonight, 8:00 P.M. Is CNN making a comeback, or is it just a charade? They must treat MAGA, the greatest political movement in our Country\u8217\'20\'19s history, with respect. I think they will, but we will soon find out? Big long term opportunity for CNN!!!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN town hall first chance for Trump to address sexual abuse finding\par \par \uc2 The CNN town hall will be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first television appearance since being found liable for sexual abuse and defamation by a federal jury in New York City on Tuesday. Don\u8217\'20\'19t expect contrition; among other things, the former president called the verdicts a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgrace\u8221\'20\'1D minutes after they were handed down. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports, the curious among the audience of Republican and undeclared voters may still decide to ask him about it:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could face questions about being found to have sexually abused E Jean Carroll when he participates in a CNN town hall on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 The town hall comes just one day after a jury found him liable for sexual abuse and defamation, underscoring the former president\u8217\'20\'19s mounting legal threats amid his effort to recapture the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 The CNN anchor Kaitlan Collins will moderate the town hall at 8pm ET at St Anselm College in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2 , where Trump will take questions from Republican and undeclared voters in the early voting state.\par \par \uc2 Town hall attendees will probably press Trump on how he intends to run for president as he faces legal threats in multiple states. On Tuesday, a New York jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/09/e-jean-carroll-wins-trump-trial-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concluded}}}\uc2  that Trump had sexually abused the advice columnist E Jean Carroll 27 years earlier, ordering the former president to pay her $5m in damages for her battery and defamation claims.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/10/cnn-trump-town-hall-rape-trial-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump could face questions on sexual abuse verdict in CNN town hall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to face CNN town hall after sexual abuse verdict\par \par \uc2 Good evening, US politics blog readers, and thanks for joining us as we cover CNN\u8217\'20\'19s town hall with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the former president who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls indicate}}}\uc2  is the frontrunner for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024. Moderated by host Kaitlan Collins, the event starts at 8pm ET in New Hampshire and will see Trump take questions from an audience of Republican and undeclared voters.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few ideas of what they might ask:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s his reaction to the finding by a federal jury on Tuesday that he was civilly liable for sexually abusing and defaming advice columnist E Jean Carroll ? The verdict in the lawsuit was one of the biggest legal losses Trump has suffered recently, and in that regard, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be out of the woods yet \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will happen if he\u8217\'20\'19s indicted by a grand jury for tampering with the 2020 election, hiding classified documents or instigating the January 6 insurrection? Justice department-appointed special counsel Jack Smith is looking into all of the above, while Atlanta-area district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  is investigating his attempts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s win in Georgia three years ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Would he back a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are a major voting bloc for Republicans, but Trump has demurred as to whether he would support banning the practice nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Follow along here for coverage of the town hall as it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230510ej5a002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
