\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 These  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinics no longer provide abortions \u8211\'20\'13 but are still hanging on\b0\par\par\uc2 Rebecca Grant \par \uc2 1,633 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2023\par 22:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Even in states with bans, a handful of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics are still open, providing \u8216\'20\'18aftercare\u8217\'20\'19 for patients who travel out of state or manage their own abortions\par \par \uc2 The patient on 9 March was a tricky case.\par \par \uc2 She was pregnant and seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but had previously had a cesarean section, which could create complications if the placenta embedded in her surgical scar. Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services couldn\u8217\'20\'19t perform the procedure because Texas had banned abortions, but the clinic could do an ultrasound and communicate with the provider in New Mexico, where the patient was heading for her appointment. Then, once the patient was back in Texas, the Houston clinic would provide any follow-up care and support she needed.\par \par \uc2 Before the supreme court ruled in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services (HWRS) provided medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to about 50 patients a day. When it became clear that the overturning of Roe v Wade was imminent, the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s administrator, Kathy Kleinfeld, had a choice to make \u8211\'20\'13 shut down, relocate or stay open and serve patients on either side of their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She decided to stay open as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic that no longer provides abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really important to us to continue to help in whatever way we can legally do so,\u8221\'20\'1D Kleinfeld said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2022/10/100-days-post-roe-least-66-clinics-across-15-us-states-have-stopped-offering-abortion-care#:~:text=New%20Guttmacher%20research%20found%20that,clinics%20that%20provided%20abortion%20care."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sixty-six clinics across 15 states}}}\uc2  have closed in the wake of the Dobbs decision. Others have moved, or are planning to move, to states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ineedana.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 INeedAnA}}}\uc2 , an online resource for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  seekers, 32 former \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://still-open-clinics.webflow.io/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  clinics have remained open in states with bans}}}\uc2  to provide other services, such as birth control prescriptions, STI testing and gender-affirming care. Of those 32, just four, like Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services, are providing pre-and-post \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, primarily for patients who travel out-of-state or who self-manage their abortions.\par \par \uc2 The services they offer include medical support, such as pregnancy tests and ultrasounds, and informational support, such as advice on how much bleeding is too much and how medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  works.\par \par \uc2 They also provide emotional support, \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom the moment of the phone call where there\u8217\'20\'19s sheer panic, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t know what to do\u8221\'20\'1D, Kleinfeld said, \u8220\'20\'1Cto the point where they come in and we watch their stress level just, step-by-step, get reduced\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kleinfeld, who has spent over two decades working for clinics in Texas, opened Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services in 2019. In 2020, Covid broke out, and the Texas governor shut down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics for a month because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t consider it \u8220\'20\'1Cessential healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D. In 2021, another hit came when the state passed SB8, a law that in effect banned abortions at or around six weeks. And then came the Dobbs decision in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fully banned in Texas, Kleinfeld found it painful to walk down the hall past the dark and empty rooms. She used to turn all the lights on, just to make it less depressing. It was expensive to pay for space they didn\u8217\'20\'19t need, so the clinic sold most of its equipment and moved into a smaller facility in October.\par \par \uc2 Now, Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services sees 170 patients a month. Half of them are seeking \u8220\'20\'1Caftercare\u8221\'20\'1D following out-of-state procedures or self-managed abortions with pills sourced online or through community networks. HWRS fields questions about symptoms like bleeding or nausea, confirms the pregnancy has ended with a follow-up ultrasound and provides referrals if necessary.\par \par \uc2 This comes with some risk, as Texas officials, in particular the state attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , have threatened to target people who help others access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The state\u8217\'20\'19s 2021 law SB8 criminalized the \u8220\'20\'1Caiding and abetting\u8221\'20\'1D of illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and after the Dobbs decision, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/texas-abortion-funds-resume-service-legal-reprieve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted operations}}}\uc2  until they were sure that helping people access legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of state did not violate any laws. One man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/11/texas-women-sued-wrongful-death-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has sued}}}\uc2  his ex-wife\u8217\'20\'19s friends for $1m each for allegedly supporting her efforts to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kleinfeld said she was not concerned about prosecution because her clinic provides straightforward evaluation, counseling and referrals for legal options \u8211\'20\'13 and because they don\u8217\'20\'19t ask too many questions.\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t ask where or how they got their medications, we only ask when they took the pills. The rest does not matter\par \par \uc2 Kathy Kleinfeld, clinic administrator\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome patients may choose self-managed care,\u8221\'20\'1D Kleinfeld said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t ask where or how they got their medications, we only ask when they took the pills. The rest does not matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Patients are also vulnerable to legal risk. From a medical perspective, induced abortions are essentially the same as a spontaneous miscarriage, which means anyone experiencing pregnancy loss \u8211\'20\'13 regardless of the circumstances \u8211\'20\'13 can find themselves under suspicion.\par \par \uc2 The website of West Alabama Women\u8217\'20\'19s Center (WAWC) \u8211\'20\'13 which provided abortions in Tuscaloosa before the Dobbs decision and now provides aftercare, among other services \u8211\'20\'13 explicitly states: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will NOT ask questions to see if you may have instigated or attempted to initiate this miscarriage\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe will also NOT do anything that would begin a potential investigation into your \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robin Marty, WAWC\u8217\'20\'19s administrator, said the clinic had to be strategic about how to continue supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients while also complying with the state\u8217\'20\'19s legal restrictions. Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general has threatened to treat the act of helping someone get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alreporter.com/2022/09/15/alabama-ag-state-may-prosecute-those-who-assist-in-out-of-state-abortions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a criminal conspiracy}}}\uc2 , so when patients ask where they can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the clinic directs them to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alabortionclinic.com/what-you-need-to-know-about-being-pregnant-in-alabama/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 document on its website}}}\uc2  that lists its services and outlines patients\u8217\'20\'19 options, alongside other resources, like adoption services and a Medicaid application.\par \par \uc2 Marty described a patient who had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  out-of-state, returned to Alabama and ran a fever. When she went to the hospital and said she had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Marty recounted, the staff would not see her. She found her way to West Alabama Women\u8217\'20\'19s Center, which prescribed her antibiotics to prevent sepsis.\par \par \uc2 In another case, an Alabama woman named Alison, who asked to go only by her first name, was six weeks pregnant when she started to bleed. Her OB/GYN found a blighted ovum, in which the gestational sac and placenta had formed, but there was no fetus. Standard treatments would have included a prescription for misoprostol, one of the two drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or a dilation and curettage, which is a method of surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But when Alison and her wife asked about next steps, the doctor apologized and said she couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything. They had to wait to see if the miscarriage would pass on its own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was pissed,\u8221\'20\'1D Alison said. \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to keep going back and keep going back and [be] told there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing we can do, yet \u8211\'20\'13 that we need to wait until your health is in serious danger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The next week, Alison made the two-hour drive to West Alabama Women\u8217\'20\'19s Center to get an ultrasound to confirm the miscarriage was complete.\par \par \uc2 A growing desert for maternity care\par \par \uc2 But the mass closure of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in red states means that dedicated aftercare providers are few and far between. There are 600 miles between Houston Women\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Services and West Alabama Women\u8217\'20\'19s Center, with no clinics left in Louisiana or Mississippi. What do exist in those gaps are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/15/us-anti-abortion-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  centers}}}\uc2 , often called crisis pregnancy centers, which provide free pregnancy tests and ultrasounds and profess to counsel people on their options, but are primarily dedicated to steering them away from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s very likely a patient would end up in a place that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t provide the healthcare they need, but also face stigma and shame for their decision\par \par \uc2 Dr Bhavik Kumar\par \par \uc2 Compounding the situation, rural areas are facing mass hospital closures and about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marchofdimes.org/maternity-care-deserts-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7 million women live in maternity care deserts}}}\uc2 , with low or no access to obstetric care. As a result, people seeking aftercare may end up in the emergency room because they\u8217\'20\'19re not sure where else to go. According to Dr Bhavik Kumar, a family medicine physician and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with Planned Parenthood, that is far from ideal. Aside from long wait times and the risk of legal jeopardy, the rates of serious complications from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are vanishingly low, and going into an ER may subject a patient to treatments or interventions that aren\u8217\'20\'19t appropriate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very likely a patient would end up in a place that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t provide the healthcare they need, but also face stigma and shame for their decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Kumar said.\par \par \uc2 Other groups are trying to bridge the gaps. There are \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doulas, websites like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plancpills.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plan C}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://womenhelp.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women Help Women}}}\uc2  that connect people with information and resources, and underground community networks that support people throughout the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  process.\par \par \uc2 The Miscarriage + \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Hotline receives 50 to 70 calls a day from people who are anxious they might need aftercare. \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of the time,\u8221\'20\'1D said its medical director, April Lockley, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe hotline provides reassurance to people that they don\u8217\'20\'19t need to go for in-person care, but people deserve that if that\u8217\'20\'19s their preference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While much of the energy on saving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US is focused on blue states, Marty wants people to recognize the need for the services that remain in states with bans. \u8220\'20\'1CCouldn\u8217\'20\'19t we invest in the red state clinics that could try to stay open locally for people who did leave and came back, or who managed their own care, so we could keep people out of hospitals and out of jail?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230505ej55001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
