\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  scandal deepens with report of rightwing activist\u8217\'20\'19s secret payments to wife \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 3,996 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2023\par 20:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  arranged for Virginia \u8216\'20\'18Ginni\u8217\'20\'19 Thomas to be paid $25,000 and emphasized \u8216\'20\'18no mention of Ginni\u8217\'20\'19 on the paymentsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s slightly past 4pm in Washington DC. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rightwing judicial activist \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  made secret payments to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife, Virginia \u8220\'20\'1CGinni\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas, ten years ago and emphasized \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni\u8221\'20\'1D on the documents, according to a new \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/05/04/leonard-leo-clarence-ginni-thomas-conway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation.}}}\uc2  The investigation comes amid a handful of reports in recent weeks surrounding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas,}}}\uc2  who received luxury gifts, travel and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/clarence-thomas-mega-donor-great-nephew-private-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tuition payments }}}\uc2  from the GOP billionaire donor Harlan Crow without publicly disclosing them. He has since faced a slew of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment calls.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne Conway has pushed back against the recent \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  investigation into Ginni Thomas, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThese people will stop at nothing,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the slew of ethics advocates, protestors and Democratic lawmakers who have called for investigations into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2  and his impeachment. \u8220\'20\'1CThey want \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign. So \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , of all people, can replace him with one of his own,\u8221\'20\'1D Conway said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in North Carolina have passed a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a change from the current 20-week ban in response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe v Wade last year. The vote, which came on Thursday as a 29-20 party-line vote, was met with opposition from about 100 observers who watched the debate in the state senate, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-abortion-restrictions-legislature-fc7f84c6b4e4398da1b7ab920150fa27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 . The Democratic governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  has vowed to veto the bill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator and member of the senate judiciary committee Peter Welch has condemned the secret payments made to Ginni Thomas, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoverup\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cevasion\u8221\'20\'1D. Speaking to MSNBC on Friday, Welch said: \u8220\'20\'1CI use the word \u8216\'20\'18deceit\u8217\'20\'19. I used the word \u8216\'20\'18coverup\u8217\'20\'19. I\u8217\'20\'19d use the word \u8216\'20\'18evasion\u8217\'20\'19 \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  knew that if this saw the light of day, it would cause controversy. And the bottom line here is that the court is getting itself in this amount of trouble and that\u8217\'20\'19s bad for our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on Friday, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accused Maga {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  of trying to hold the debt \u8220\'20\'1Chostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhether you pay the debt or not doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a damn thing to do with what your budget is \u8230\'20\'26 let\u8217\'20\'19s get it straight. They\u8217\'20\'19re trying to hold the debt hostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts, magnificently difficult, damaging cuts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , head of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , says she is resigning effective 30 June. Walensky\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes as the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/05/covid-19-no-longer-global-health-emergency-world-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  that the Covid-19 virus is no longer a global health emergency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The court in New York has released some material from defendant \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pre-trial deposition \u8211\'20\'13 the session in which he mistook plaintiff Carroll for his second wife, Marla Marples, despite saying the writer was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot his type\u8221\'20\'1D. And he says the picture was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery blurry\u8221\'20\'1D. It clearly shows Carroll. Trump is depicted next to his first wife, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/ivana-trump-dies-donald-trump-first-wife"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivana Trump}}}\uc2 . Trump points to a photograph he\u8217\'20\'19s been shown and says: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s Marla, yeah, that\u8217\'20\'19s my wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has chosen \uc2 Neera Tanden\uc2 , the current White House staff secretary and senior adviser, to be his new domestic policy adviser, the Associated Press reports. Tanden, who has 25 years of experience of public policy, will be the first Asian American to lead any of the three major White House policy operations, he said. She will succeed Susan Rice who was previously a foreign policy expert.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An investigation by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  has found that South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Democrat representative James Clyburn sought GOP assistance in protecting his district at a cost to Black Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CFacing the possibility of an unsafe district, South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful Democrat sent his aide to consult with the GOP on a redistricting plan that diluted Black voting strength and harmed his party\u8217\'20\'19s chances of gaining seats in Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the outlet reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former North Carolina representative \uc2 Madison Cawthorn\uc2  has been fined $250 after pleading guilty to a misdemeanor following the discovery of a loaded gun in his carry-on luggage at Charlotte airport last year. According to the Associated Press, a judge in Mecklenburg county court where the hearing took place allowed Cawthorn to keep the 9mm gun, which \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  seized last year.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former North Carolina representative \uc2 Madison Cawthorn\uc2  has been fined $250 after pleading guilty to a misdemeanor following the discovery of a loaded gun in his carry-on luggage at Charlotte airport last year.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, a judge in Mecklenburg county court where the hearing took place allowed Cawthorn to keep the 9mm gun, which \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  seized last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very happy and thankful that the judge gave a really clear ruling that sides with the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Cawthorn told reporters after the hearing, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, Cawthorn was found with an unloaded gun while trying to board a plane at Asheville Regional Airport. Cawthorn was eventually allowed to board but had his gun confiscated.\par \par \uc2 Cawthorn served one term in Congress after winning the election at age 25, which made him one of the youngest members in Congress at the time. Cawthorn, a Trump supporter, lost the 2022 GOP primary to Chuck Edwards.\par \par \uc2 Madison Cawthorn\uc2 . Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C How Rep. James Clyburn Protected His District at a Cost to Black Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D is the alarming \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/how-rep-james-clyburn-protected-his-district-at-a-cost-to-black-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the investigative website\u8217\'20\'19s standfirst to go with their scoop: \u8220\'20\'1CFacing the possibility of an unsafe district, South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful Democrat sent his aide to consult with the GOP on a redistricting plan that diluted Black voting strength and harmed his party\u8217\'20\'19s chances of gaining seats in Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 , a Clyburn spokesperson acknowledged that the office \u8220\'20\'1Cengaged in discussions regarding the boundaries of the 6th Congressional District by responding to inquiries\u8221\'20\'1D but did not reveal the extent of Clyburn\u8217\'20\'19s role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny accusation that Congressman Clyburn in any way enabled or facilitated Republican gerrymandering that wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have otherwise occurred is fanciful,\u8221\'20\'1D Clyburn\u8217\'20\'19s office said in a statement to the outlet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has chosen \uc2 Neera Tanden\uc2 , the current White House staff secretary and senior adviser, to be his new domestic policy adviser, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Tanden, who has 25 years of experience of public policy, will be the first Asian American to lead any of the three major White House policy operations, he said. She will succeed Susan Rice who was previously a foreign policy expert.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Senior Advisor and Staff Secretary, Neera oversaw decision-making processes across my domestic, economic and national security teams. She has 25 years of experience in public policy, has served three Presidents, and led one of the largest think tanks in the country for nearly a decade,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/05/05/president-biden-announces-key-white-house-personnel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was a key architect of the Affordable Care Act and helped drive key domestic policies that became part of my agenda, including clean energy subsidies and sensible gun reform. While growing up, Neera relied on some of the critical programs that she will oversee as Domestic Policy Advisor, and I know those insights will serve my Administration and the American people well,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Neera Tanden\uc2  testifies during a \uc2 Senate Committee on the Budget\uc2  hearing on Capitol Hill in Washington, Feb. 10, 2021. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced Friday, May 5, 2023, that he has chosen \uc2 Neera Tanden\uc2 , currently the White House staff secretary and a senior adviser to the president, to be his new domestic policy adviser. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Video clips of Trump testimony in E Jean Carroll case released\par \par \uc2 The jury in the civil trial, where writer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/trump-civil-rape-trial-last-witness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 E Jean Carroll accuses Donald Trump}}}\uc2  of raping her and then defaming her by calling her a liar, is not sitting today, but there is still some news.\par \par \uc2 The court in New York has released some material from defendant Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pre-trial deposition \u8211\'20\'13 the session in which he mistook plaintiff Carroll for his second wife, Marla Marples, despite saying the writer was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot his type".\par \par \uc2 And he says the picture was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery blurry\u8221\'20\'1D. It clearly shows Carroll. Trump is depicted next to his first wife, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/ivana-trump-dies-donald-trump-first-wife"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivana Trump}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Trump points to a photograph he\u8217\'20\'19s been shown and says: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s Marla, yeah, that\u8217\'20\'19s my wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrA rush of E. Jean Carroll v. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  exhibits have been released \u8212\'20\'14 including the former president's video deposition.\par \par \uc2 Here's an excerpt where Trump mistakes Carroll with his ex-wife Marla Maples.\par \par \uc2 Background, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawcrimenews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LawCrimeNews}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SqzCH2RjpY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SqzCH2RjpY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IIkbCBGCNL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IIkbCBGCNL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1654544896802406402?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s then told it\u8217\'20\'19s actually Carroll. He responds, apparently nonchalantly: \u8220\'20\'1CI assume that\u8217\'20\'19s Carroll, because it\u8217\'20\'19s very blurry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carroll, second from left, laughing, does not appear blurry in this image.\par \par \uc2 enltrRecall: Trump claimed Carroll was not his "type."\par \par \uc2 After corrected on the gaffe, Trump said the photo was "blurry." For reference, this is the photograph.\par \par \uc2 (L-R: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , E. Jean Carroll, John Johnson and \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2 ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/w2ZifMY829"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/w2ZifMY829}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Klasfeld (@KlasfeldReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KlasfeldReports/status/1654545769813221380?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello again, US politics live blog readers, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have gone for tacos (truly) and the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s right wing is once again in trouble. It\u8217\'20\'19s a lively Friday, so stay with us.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , head of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC), says she is resigning effective 30 June.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accused Maga Republicans of trying to hold the debt ceiling negotiations \u8220\'20\'1Chostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in North Carolina passed a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a change from the current 20-week ban in response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rightwing judicial activist \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  made secret payments to \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife, Virginia \u8220\'20\'1CGinni\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas, 10 years ago and emphasized \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni\u8221\'20\'1D on the documents, according to a new \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/05/04/leonard-leo-clarence-ginni-thomas-conway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There was some confusion late morning, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , during his remarks about jobs figures and the economy, said he\u8217\'20\'19d be holding an important press conference this afternoon (that reporters did not know about.). Turns out that\u8217\'20\'19s not the case, the White House soon clarified. Meanwhile, Potus and Veep ( \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  ), unannounced, went out in town for some 5 May tacos together.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappy Cinco de Mayo. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  with a rare joint OTR stop at Taqueria Habanero in NE DC\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Memoli (@mikememoli) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli/status/1654529966145404944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Head of \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  to step down\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , head of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , says she is resigning effective 30 June.\par \par \uc2 Walensky\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes as the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/05/covid-19-no-longer-global-health-emergency-world-health-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  that the Covid-19 virus is no longer a global health emergency.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised Walensky\u8217\'20\'19s leadership at the CDC, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDr. Walensky has saved lives with her steadfast and unwavering focus on the health of every American. As Director of the CDC, she led a complex organization on the frontlines of a once-in-a-generation pandemic with honesty and integrity. She marshalled our finest scientists and public health experts to turn the tide on the urgent crises we\u8217\'20\'19ve faced.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Walensky leaves CDC a stronger institution, better positioned to confront health threats and protect Americans. We have all benefited from her service and dedication to public health, and I wish her the best in her next chapter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  speaks during a Senate committee hearing on preparing for the next public health emergency and reauthorizing the Pandemic and All-Hazards Preparedness Act on 4 May 2023. Photograph: Bonnie Cash/UPI/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accuses Maga Republicans of holding debt 'hostage'\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on Friday, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accused M aga Republicans of trying to hold the debt \u8220\'20\'1Chostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether you pay the debt or not doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have a damn thing to do with what your budget is \u8230\'20\'26 let\u8217\'20\'19s get it straight. They\u8217\'20\'19re trying to hold the debt hostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts, magnificently difficult, damaging cuts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy predecessor, in the four years he was president, increased that total debt by 40%,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, this is no small part about paying our bills that we\u8217\'20\'19ve accumulated, not by me, not by my administration, but by former presidents and previous Congresses \u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re not a deadbeat nation. We pay our bills.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: "Whether you pay the debt or not doesn't have a damn thing to do with what your budget is... let's get it straight. They're trying to hold the debt hostage to get us to agree to some draconian cuts." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZX2pugDl8i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZX2pugDl8i}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1654522499336478720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic senator and member of the senate judiciary committee Peter Welch has condemned the secret payments made to Ginni Thomas, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoverup\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cevasion \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to MSNBC on Friday, Welch said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI use the word \u8216\'20\'18deceit\u8217\'20\'19. I used the word \u8216\'20\'18coverup\u8217\'20\'19. I\u8217\'20\'19d use the word \u8216\'20\'18evasion\u8217\'20\'19 \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  knew that if this saw the light of day, it would cause controversy. And the bottom line here is that the court is getting itself in this amount of trouble and that\u8217\'20\'19s bad for our democracy \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Whatever the relationship is with Thomas and his benefactor, it\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty shocking thing to be getting vacations on yachts in Greece, in New Zealand, to be flying on private chats and have that not be known. And obviously the whole \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  relationship is something that\u8217\'20\'19s extraordinarily important. It\u8217\'20\'19s been very discouraging.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to explain the extent that the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  has over the nomination process of supreme court justices, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen these nominees are put forward, the judiciary committee is an afterthought. \uc2 The Federalist Society\uc2  is the interview that really matters for those folks to get the \u8230\'20\'26 approval on the Republican side. And that has been a long term concerted, unfortunately, effective effort by \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We have to have a supreme court in this country that people respect \u8230\'20\'26 Anything that any one of those justices does that erodes the confidence that our people are all entitled to \u8230\'20\'26is wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports that \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  directed $25k to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife, but emphasized the paperwork should have \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni, of course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 "I\u8217\'20\'19d use the word deceit. I\u8217\'20\'19d use the word coverup. I\u8217\'20\'19d use the word evasion,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeterWelch?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PeterWelch}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chrislhayes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @chrislhayes}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/phERVuRJmP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/phERVuRJmP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 All In with Chris Hayes (@allinwithchris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/allinwithchris/status/1654286441839579137?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina lawmakers pass 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in North Carolina have passed a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a change from the current 20-week ban in response to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturn of Roe v Wade last year.\par \par \uc2 The vote, which came on Thursday as a 29-20 party-line vote, was met with opposition from about 100 observers who watched the debate in the state senate, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-abortion-restrictions-legislature-fc7f84c6b4e4398da1b7ab920150fa27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights now!\u8221\'20\'1D some observers shouted while others yelled: \u8220\'20\'1CShame!\u8221\'20\'1D The state House passed the bill on Wednesday evening on a similar party-line vote.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Republican state senator Joyce Krawiec hailed the bill on Thursday, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CMany of us who have worked for decades to save unborn babies for the sanctity of human life, we saw it as an opportunity to put forth a very pro-life, pro-woman legislation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a pro-life plan, not an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic state senator Sydney Batch pushed back against the bill, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill is an extreme and oppressive step backwards for our society and one that will deny women the right to make decisions about their own health care and future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  has vowed to veto the bill, saying it is an \u8220\'20\'1Cegregious, unacceptable attack on the women of our state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bill also includes additional medical and paperwork requirements for patients and physicians, as well as increased licensing requirements for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics that would make the procedure more difficult to attain.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, across the state are growing fears as Mark Robinson, an extreme Republican who once labeled the transgender movement \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonic\u8221\'20\'1D and called Muslims \u8220\'20\'1Cinvaders\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/05/mark-robinson-republican-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 runs}}}\uc2  for the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have bills right now going through our general assembly to ban gender-affirming care for trans youth. We have a ban against trans athletes or young people competing in sports right now. We have a lot of discriminatory, just persecuting our own citizens-type of legislation happening in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Anderson Clayton, chair of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/05/mark-robinson-republican-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told}}}\uc2  the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd Mark Robinson is only going to be the person who\u8217\'20\'19s going to make that worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kellyanne Conway has pushed back against the recent \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  investigation into Ginni Thomas, saying : \u8220\'20\'1CThese people will stop at nothing,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the slew of ethics advocates, protestors and Democratic lawmakers who have called for investigations into \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and his impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Fox News on Friday, Conway said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese people will stop at nothing. They want \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign. So \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , of all people, can replace him with one of his own \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas was one of my contractors and she had worked with \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , she \u8230\'20\'26 is part of the grassroots. She had worked in the Reagan administration. This is a serious person who for years had worked in public policy At the Polling Company, we did public opinion research and data analytics. We had no business before the court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrKellyanne Conway on Fox News downplays her role in funneling payments to Ginni Thomas, and also portrays the Thomas as victims {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1N9vksBkb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1N9vksBkb6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1654483559070023689?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 'No mention of Ginni': conservative legal activist directed money to wife of justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Rightwing judicial activist \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  made secret payments to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife, Virginia \u8220\'20\'1CGinni\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas, ten years ago and emphasized \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni\u8221\'20\'1D on the documents, according to a new \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/05/04/leonard-leo-clarence-ginni-thomas-conway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation.}}}\par \par \uc2 In January 2012, Leo directed GOP pollster Kellyanne Conway to bill the Judicial Education Project, a non-profit group he advises. He then ordered that money be used to pay Ginni Thomas, telling Conway that he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cgive\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas \u8220\'20\'1Canother 25k\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni, of course,\u8221\'20\'1D Leo told Conway, who later became a senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Post reports. The subsequent bill sent to the JEP by Conway\u8217\'20\'19s firm, the Polling Company, titled the purpose as \u8220\'20\'1CSupplement for Constitution Polling and Opinion Consulting\u8221\'20\'1D, according to documents reviewed by the Post.\par \par \uc2 Later that year, the JEP filed an amicus brief in a case that challenged a civil rights law that sought to protect minority voters. In a 5-to-4 majority which \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  was part of, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-court-voting-idUSBRE95O0TU20130626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped away}}}\uc2  a formula in the Voting Rights Act that determined which states had to get federal permission before altering their voting rules and procedures.\par \par \uc2 Following the Post\u8217\'20\'19s revelations about the secret payments, Leo defended himself, telling the outlet:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is no secret that Ginni Thomas has a long history of working on issues within the conservative movement, and part of that work has involved gauging public attitudes and sentiment. The work she did here did not involve anything connected with either the Court\u8217\'20\'19s business or with other legal issues\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As an advisor to JEP I have long been supportive of its opinion research relating to limited government, and The Polling Company, along with Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s help, has been an invaluable resource for gauging public attitudes\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Knowing how disrespectful, malicious and gossipy people can be, I have always tried to protect the privacy of Justice Thomas and Ginni.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investigation comes amid a handful of reports in recent weeks surrounding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas,}}}\uc2  who received luxury gifts, travel and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/clarence-thomas-mega-donor-great-nephew-private-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tuition payments }}}\uc2  from the GOP billionaire donor Harlan Crow without publicly disclosing them. He has since faced a slew of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/clarence-thomas-supreme-courts-gifts-republican-megadonor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment calls.}}}\par \par \uc2 In response to the reports, Democrats have been calling for investigations into \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and for tighter ethics standards for the supreme court justices, which Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  condemned }}}\uc2  as an \u8220\'20\'1Cassault \u8230\'20\'26 well beyond ethics \u8230\'20\'26 [and] about trying to delegitimize a conservative court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Leo himself has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/leonard-leo-watchdog-complaint-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  of illegally misusing $73m from non-profit groups and diverting money to his businesses, according to a complaint from the non-profit watchdog organization, Campaign for Accountability.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservative activist reportedly organized secret payments to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 's wife\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. A prominent conservative judicial activist arranged for Virginia \u8220\'20\'1CGinni\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas, wife of the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , to be paid tens of thousands of dollars for consulting work over ten years ago and emphasized \u8220\'20\'1Cno mention of Ginni\u8221\'20\'1D on the payments, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2023/05/04/leonard-leo-clarence-ginni-thomas-conway/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  revealed that \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , a leader of the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  who led campaigns to support the nominations of a handful of conservative supreme court justices, directed GOP pollster Kellyanne Conway in 2012 to bill the Judicial Education Project, a non-profit Leo advises.\par \par \uc2 Leo then told Conway, a former advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , that he wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cgive\u8221\'20\'1D Ginni Thomas \u8220\'20\'1Canother $25k\u8221\'20\'1D, according to documents reviewed by the Post. \u8220\'20\'1CNo mention of Ginni, of course,\u8221\'20\'1D Leo emphasized.\par \par \uc2 The $25,000 bill Conway sent to the Judicial Education Project listed the purpose as \u8220\'20\'1CSupplement for Constitution Polling and Opinion Consulting\u8221\'20\'1D the Post reports.\par \par \uc2 The investigation comes amid a handful of reports in recent weeks surrounding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas,}}}\uc2  who received luxury gifts, travel and tuition payments from the GOP billionaire donor Harlan Crow without publicly disclosing them.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Carolina lawmakers have{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/north-carolina-abortion-restrictions-legislature-fc7f84c6b4e4398da1b7ab920150fa27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which Democratic governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2  promised to veto.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York mayor Eric Adams and police are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/jordan-neely-eric-adams-nypd-subway-killing-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing}}}\uc2  increasing criticism from protestors for a lack of action over 30-year-old Jordan Neely\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/debt-ceiling-senate-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticizing }}}\uc2  House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 proposal to raise the government\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit in exchange for spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230505ej55001xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
