\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Proud Boys leader and three others convicted of seditious conspiracy for January 6 attack \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 4,031 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2023\par 20:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conviction follows seven-day jury deliberationSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 4pm in Washington DC today. Here is a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A grandnephew of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , whom the supreme court justice described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cson\u8221\'20\'1D, had his private school tuition paid for by billionaire GOP donor Harlan Crow, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-private-school-tuition-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . Financial documents reviewed by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  showed that in July 2009, a payment was made by \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s company to Hidden Lake Academy, a private boarding school in northern Georgia where tuition ran over $6,00 monthly.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Proud Boys extremist group leader \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  has been convicted of seditious conspiracy. The conviction follows a seven-day jury deliberation on five members of the far-right neo-fascist organizations who have been accused of conspiring against the peaceful power transition between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seeking to move his his criminal case by Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney to federal court, his lawyers said on Thursday. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Todd Blanche, said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense team is planning to file a motion on Thursday that will transfer the case involving hush-money payments from state court to federal court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor Eric Adams has criticized representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  over her remarks that condemned the death of a homeless subway rider. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s very responsible at the time where we are still investigating the situation,\u8221\'20\'1D Adams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/05/04/mayor-adams-rips-aoc-for-saying-jordan-neely-was-murdered/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on CNN on Wednesday night after Ocasio-Cortez called the death of Jordan Neely a \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the latest behind-the-scenes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/foxleaks-tucker-carlson-asks-makeup-artist-if-pillow-fights-ever-break-out-womens-bathroom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Tucker Carlson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/foxleaks-tucker-carlson-asks-makeup-artist-if-pillow-fights-ever-break-out-womens-bathroom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  by the progressive watchdog \uc2 Media Matters for America\uc2 , the now fired Fox News host asks a makeup artist about what women do in the bathroom and if they ever have pillow fights. The footage of the insinuating comments follows the leak of video of Carlson making coarse remarks about a woman and Fox News viewers in general.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Following vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting today with CEOs of tech companies including \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2 , Harris said the private sector has a \u8220\'20\'1Clegal responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure the safety of AI products. \u8220\'20\'1CAs I shared today with CEOs of companies at the forefront of American AI innovation, the private sector has an ethical, moral, and legal responsibility to ensure the safety and security of their products. And every company must comply with existing laws to protect the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/may/04/[object%20Attr]"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has declined to comment on the recent reports surrounding supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of undisclosed luxury gifts. Jean-Pierre told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CRight now\u8230\'20\'26as it relates to the ethics, as it relates to that process, the senate is clearly moving forward with their own senate procedural process. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to leave it there for now,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Following the verdict delivered earlier today that found three members and the leader of the neo-fascist group Proud Boys guilty of seditious conspiracy, the White House declined to comment on the case,\u8221\'20\'1D saying that it does not want to \u8220\'20\'1Cinterfere.\u8221\'20\'1D Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen the verdict but while the verdict has been reached in this case, we are also mindful that there are other similar cases pending and so we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to interfere with those.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , chairman of the senate finance committee, has announced that he is urging Harlan Crow \u8220\'20\'1Cfor answers\u8221\'20\'1D on his luxury gifts to supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pushing Harlan Crow for answers on his lavish gifts to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . If he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t comply by May 8, I will absolutely explore other tools at the Finance Committee\u8217\'20\'19s disposal to shed more light on what appears to be blatant corruption,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, Maya Yang, as we wrap up the blog for today. Thank you for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2 , chairman of the senate finance committee, has announced that he is urging Harlan Crow \u8220\'20\'1Cfor answers\u8221\'20\'1D on his luxury gifts to supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, following reports that Thomas accepted private school tuition payments made to his grandnephew by the GOP billionaire donor, Wyden tweeted:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pushing Harlan Crow for answers on his lavish gifts to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . If he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t comply by May 8, I will absolutely explore other tools at the Finance Committee\u8217\'20\'19s disposal to shed more light on what appears to be blatant corruption.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrFor everyone asking: I'm pushing Harlan Crow for answers on his lavish gifts to \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . If he doesn't comply by May 8, I will absolutely explore other tools at the Finance Committee's disposal to shed more light on what appears to be blatant corruption.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  (@RonWyden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RonWyden/status/1654166633269587968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following the verdict delivered earlier today that found three members and the leader of the neo-fascist group Proud Boys guilty of seditious conspiracy, the White House declined to comment on the case,\u8221\'20\'1D saying that it does not want to \u8220\'20\'1Cinterfere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen the verdict but while the verdict has been reached in this case, we are also mindful that there are other similar cases pending and so we don\u8217\'20\'19t want to interfere with those.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would refer you to the department of justice for comment on this case\u8230\'20\'26.but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be mindful as we know there are other pending issues here,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has declined to comment on the recent reports surrounding supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of undisclosed luxury gifts.\par \par \uc2 When asked by a reporter during Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing on why she has not commented on any stories related to Thomas and his code of conduct, Jean-Pierre replied:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now\u8230\'20\'26as it relates to the ethics, as it relates to that process, the senate is clearly moving forward with their own senate procedural process. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to leave it there for now,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, following reports of Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s acceptance of undisclosed luxury gifts including travel and private school tuition from GOP billionaire donor Harlan Crow, senate Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/10/senate-democrats-supreme-court-investigation-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to investigate the undisclosed luxury trips.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, senate Democrats called for tighter rules on the supreme court justices surrounding ethics standards but met resistance from Republicans who condemned Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts as an \u8220\'20\'1Cassault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  Democrats, labeling their efforts as an attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Cdelegitimize a conservative court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says tech companies have "legal responsibility" over AI safety\par \par \uc2 Following vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting today with CEOs of tech companies including \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2 , Harris said the private sector has a \u8220\'20\'1Clegal responsibility\u8221\'20\'1D to ensure the safety of AI products.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I shared today with CEOs of companies at the forefront of American AI innovation, the private sector has an ethical, moral, and legal responsibility to ensure the safety and security of their products. And every company must comply with existing laws to protect the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/05/04/statement-from-vice-president-harris-after-meeting-with-ceos-on-advancing-responsible-artificial-intelligence-innovation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement.}}}\par \par \uc2 She added that she is working alongside president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  are working on advancing potential new regulations and supporting new legislation \u8220\'20\'1Cso that everyone can safety benefit from technological innovations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 More lunchtime reading, this time from Poppy Noor, who considers the considerable political challenges facing Republicans over strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans passed after the downfall of Roe v Wade \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In one state, Republican women filibustered to block a near total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban introduced by their own party.\par \par \uc2 In another, the Republican co-sponsor of a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban tanked his own bill. On the federal level , a Republican congresswoman warns that the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance could meaning \u8220\'20\'1Closing huge\u8221\'20\'1D in 2024.\par \par \uc2 As states continue to bring in tighter restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the fall of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , internal divisions within the Republican party on the issue are starting to show.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/04/republican-lawmakers-reject-abortion-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Republicans reject \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans as \u8216\'20\'18campaign-enders\u8217\'20\'19 in warning to party}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our regular guest columnist, the Vermont senator and former presidential hopeful Bernie Sanders, would like a word about American workplace culture and particularly the toll of so spending so many hours in the office, factory, shop or other place of gainful employ \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In 1938, as a result of a massive grassroots effort by the trade union movement, the Fair Labor Standards Act was enacted by Congress to reduce the work week to 40 hours. Back then, the American people were sick and tired of working 80, 90, 100 hours a week with very little time for rest, relaxation or quality time with their families. They demanded change and they won a huge victory. That\u8217\'20\'19s the good news.\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders. Photograph: Will Oliver/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 The bad news is that despite an explosion in technology, major increases in worker productivity, and transformational changes in the workplace and American society, the Fair Labor Standards Act has not been reformed in 80 years. The result: millions of Americans are working longer hours for lower wages, with the average worker making nearly $50 a week less than he or she did 50 years ago, after adjusting for inflation. Further, family life is suffering, as parents don\u8217\'20\'19t have adequate time for their kids, life expectancy for working people is in decline, and increased stress is a major factor in the mental health crisis we are now experiencing.\par \par \uc2 Compared with other countries, our workplace record is not good. In 2021, American employees {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stats.oecd.org/viewhtml.aspx?datasetcode=ANHRS&lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worked}}}\uc2  184 more hours than Japanese workers, 294 more hours than British workers, and 442 more hours than German workers. Unbelievably, in 2023 there are millions of Americans who work at jobs with no vacation time.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s time to reduce the work week to 32 hours with no loss in pay. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to reduce the stress level in our country and allow Americans to enjoy a better quality of life. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to make sure that working people benefit from rapidly increasing technology, not just large corporations that are already doing phenomenally well.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/may/04/us-workers-bernie-sanders-32-hours-working-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US workers deserve a break. It\u8217\'20\'19s time for a 32-hour working week | Bernie Sanders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the latest behind-the-scenes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/foxleaks-tucker-carlson-asks-makeup-artist-if-pillow-fights-ever-break-out-womens-bathroom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Tucker Carlson{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/foxleaks-tucker-carlson-asks-makeup-artist-if-pillow-fights-ever-break-out-womens-bathroom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  by the progressive watchdog \uc2 Media Matters for America\uc2 , the now fired Fox News host asks a makeup artist about what women do in the bathroom and if they ever have pillow fights.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . Photograph: \uc2 Twitter\uc2  | @TuckerCarlson\par \par \uc2 The footage of the insinuating comments follows the leak of video of Carlson making coarse remarks about a woman and Fox News viewers in general; a discussion of sexual technique with Piers Morgan ; disparaging remarks about the Fox Nation streaming service; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/03/tucker-carlson-video-fox-news-dominion-lawyer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments}}}\uc2  about a lawyer who deposed Carlson in the \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  defamation suit, who the host called a \u8220\'20\'1Cslimy little motherfucker\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That suit, over Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 broadcast of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lies about the 2020 US election, was settled last month for $787.5m. Shortly after that, Carlson was surprisingly fired.\par \par \uc2 Speculation and reporting about why Carlson was fired continues.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/03/tucker-carlson-text-message-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a racially inflammatory text message}}}\uc2  Carlson sent after the Capitol attack. That message was redacted in Dominion filings but other message, including abusive comments, were released. Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Fox News executives were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/28/why-tucker-carlson-fired-fox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  linked to his firing, including one in which he is reported to have called a female executive a \u8220\'20\'1Ccunt\u8221\'20\'1D. A former booker on his show also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/26/tucker-carlson-abby-grossberg-fox-news-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed suit}}}\uc2 , alleging a misogynistic working atmosphere.\par \par \uc2 Fox News has not commented on why Carlson was fired. It has called the suit from the former booker, Abby Grossberg, \u8220\'20\'1Cunmeritorious\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Criddled with false allegations against the network and our employees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a person close to Carlson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/28/why-tucker-carlson-fired-fox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  the firing was not over abusive messages or crude comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn elderly Australian man\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Fox News owner, \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 , 92 \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cfired his top anchor with no warning because he was so offended by a dirty word? Stupidest explanation ever. Please. A big decision requires a powerful motive. Naughty words in text messages don\u8217\'20\'19t qualify.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the footage released on Thursday, Carlson is seen on-set, having makeup applied by an unidentified woman.\par \par \uc2 He says: \u8220\'20\'1CCan I ask you a question? You don\u8217\'20\'19t have to answer, it\u8217\'20\'19s personal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The woman indicates assent.\par \par \uc2 Carlson says: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not speaking of you, but more in general with ladies, when they go to the ladies room and \u8216\'20\'18powder their noses\u8217\'20\'19, is there actually nose-powdering going on?\par \par \uc2 The woman says: \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson says: \u8220\'20\'1COooh. I like the sound of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The woman says: \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the time, it\u8217\'20\'19s lipstick.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson says: \u8220\'20\'1CDo pillow fights ever break out? You don\u8217\'20\'19t have to, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to \u8211\'20\'13\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The woman says: \u8220\'20\'1CNot in the bathroom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Carlson says: \u8220\'20\'1COK. Not in the bathroom. That\u8217\'20\'19d be more a dorm activity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After an unintelligible remark off camera, Carlson apologises.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CYou are such a good sport. Such a good person. Thank you. I know you do, but you do not deserve that. And I mean it with great affection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/may/03/tucker-carlson-video-fox-news-dominion-lawyer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New video reveals Tucker Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s coarse remark about Dominion lawyer}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor Eric Adams has criticized representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  over her remarks that condemned the death of a homeless subway rider.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s very responsible at the time where we are still investigating the situation,\u8221\'20\'1D Adams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/05/04/mayor-adams-rips-aoc-for-saying-jordan-neely-was-murdered/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on CNN on Wednesday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s the DA conduct his investigation with the law enforcement officials. To really interfere with that is not the right thing to do,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 Adams\u8217\'20\'19 remarks comes after Ocasio-Cortez condemned the death of Jordan Neely, a 30-year old Black homeless person who died after a 24-year-old former marine placed him in a chokehold on the subway.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJordan Neely was murdered. But bc Jordan was houseless and crying for food in a time when the city is raising rents and stripping services to militarize itself while many in power demonize the poor, the murderer gets protected w/ passive headlines + no charges. It\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1653880169516466178?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  tweeted.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is appalling how so many take advantage of headlines re: crime for an obsolete \u8216\'20\'18tough on crime\u8217\'20\'19 political, media, & budgetary gain, but when a public murder happens that reinforces existing power structures, those same forces rush to exonerate & look the other way. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  seeks to move Manhattan criminal case to federal court\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seeking to move his his criminal case by Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney to federal court, his lawyers said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Todd Blanche, said that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense team is planning to file a motion on Thursday that will transfer the case involving hush-money payments from state court to federal court.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes a month after Trump appeared at a Manhattan courtroom for his arraignment as prosecutors accused him of committing 34 felony counts involving an alleged cover up of an extramarital sex scandal involving adult star Stormy Daniels.\par \par \uc2 Trump has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to transfer the case to federal court will likely be a \u8220\'20\'1Clong shot,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/04/nyregion/trump-bragg-trial-date.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports,}}}\uc2  and will not have any immediate impact on the current state case.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge will decide whether to approve the request or not.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Proud Boys leader and other members convicted of seditious conspiracy\par \par \uc2 Former Proud Boys extremist group leader \uc2 Enrique Tarrio\uc2  has been convicted of seditious conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 The conviction follows a seven-day jury deliberation on five members of the far-right neo-fascist organizations who have been accused of conspiring against the peaceful power transition between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Three other members of the Proud Boys \u8211\'20\'13 Ethan Nordean, Joseph Biggs and Zachary Rehl \u8211\'20\'13 have also been convicted after facing a slew of charges including conspiracy charges, evidence tampering and obstruction of the Electoral College vote.\par \par \uc2 Member Domic Pezzola was also charged but the jury was unable to reach a verdict on his seditious conspiracy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/04/proud-boys-convicted-seditious-conspiracy-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  charge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrTarrio, Biggs, Rehl, Nordean, Pezzola found guilty of\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 obstructing an official proceeding\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 conspiracy to prevent officer from discharging duties\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 obstruction of law enforcement during civil\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 destruction of govt property and aiding and abetting\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1654142981404872705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Tarrio was not in Washington on January 6, 2021 during the deadly Capitol riots but prosecutors said he organized and directed the attack by Proud Boys who stormed the Capitol where 5 people died.\par \par \uc2 Since the riots, Tarrio became a top target of the largest investigation by the justice department in American history.\par \par \uc2 Defense lawyers argued that there was no plan to attack the Capitol or stop Congress\u8217\'20\'19 certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win. One of Tarrio\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer tried to divert the blame on Trump, saying that the former president incited the attack after he told the mob to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell,\u8221\'20\'1D the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The seditious conspiracy charge carries a prison sentence of up to 20 years.\par \par \uc2 FILE - Proud Boys leader Henry \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Enrique\u8221\'20\'1D Tarrio\uc2  wears a hat that says The War Boys during a rally in Portland, Ore., Sept. 26, 2020. Photograph: Allison Dinner/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several political advocacy organizations have issued statements condemning \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  in light of recent reports surrounding his failure to disclose luxury gifts.\par \par \uc2 Stand Up America, a nonprofit grassroots organization focusing combatting corruption and voter suppression, has called for a \u8220\'20\'1Cthorough investigation\u8221\'20\'1D into Thomas.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the Guardian, Brett Edkins, managing director of policy and political affairs, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ethical crisis at the Supreme Court just keeps getting worse\u8230\'20\'26 We don\u8217\'20\'19t yet know the full extent of Justice Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 ethical violations, but the existing evidence of a corrupt relationship is overwhelming and should alarm every American.\par \par \uc2 Congress must hold this Court in check and restore public trust in our justice system by conducting a thorough investigation into Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 financial dealings with Crow and finally passing a code of ethics for the Supreme Court. The American people should have confidence that their highest court is free from corruption.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Similarly, Acccountable.US, a nonpartisan watchdog organization that sheds light on special interests and unchecked power, has called for \u8220\'20\'1Curgent reform\u8221\'20\'1D in the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the Guardian, Accountable.US president Kyle Herrig said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaire benefactor Harlan Crow didn\u8217\'20\'19t just bankroll Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s luxury travel, his mother\u8217\'20\'19s house, and his wife\u8217\'20\'19s job \u8212\'20\'14 he also covered his kid\u8217\'20\'19s private school tuition, which he conveniently didn\u8217\'20\'19t disclose.\par \par \uc2 Over decades, these two have maintained a highly problematic financial relationship that has facilitated what looks like corruption at the highest levels. Meanwhile, Chief Justice Roberts has completely dodged responsibility by refusing to take action while the Court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy crisis grows. We need urgent reform to restore public trust in our Court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Private school tuition for \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 's grandnephew paid for by billionaire GOP donor: report\par \par \uc2 A new investigation by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  revealed that billionaire GOP donor Harlan Crow paid the tuition of Mark Martin, a grandnephew of supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 , Mark Martin, whom Thomas obtained legal custody over when Martin was 6-years old, attended a private boarding school in northern Georgia called Hidden Lakes Academy for about a year.\par \par \uc2 During his time at the school, his tuition was paid for by Crow, former school administrator Christopher Grimwood told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . A bank document reviewed by the investigative outlet from 2009 showed a wire transfer of $6,200 to the school from Crow\u8217\'20\'19s company. The transfer was labeled with \u8220\'20\'1CMark Martin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investigation also found that before and after Martin\u8217\'20\'19s time at Hidden Lake Academy, he attended Randolph-Macon Academy in Virginia, another boarding school. \u8220\'20\'1CHarlan said he was paying for the tuition at Randolph-Macon Academy as well,\u8221\'20\'1D Grimwood recalled Crow telling him during a visit to the real estate magnate\u8217\'20\'19s estate in the Adirondacks.\par \par \uc2 Despite disclosing a gift of $5,000 for Martin\u8217\'20\'19s education from another friend several years earlier, Thomas did not disclose \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tuition payments, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s spokespersons have defended Crow\u8217\'20\'19s payments, telling \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  in a statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarlan Crow has long been passionate about the importance of quality education and giving back to those less fortunate, especially at-risk youth\u8230\'20\'26 he and his wife have supported many young Americans through scholarship and other programs at a variety of schools\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Harlan and Kathy have particularly focused on students who are at risk of falling behind or missing out on opportunities to better themselves\u8230\'20\'26 Tuition and other financial assistance is given directly to academic institutions, not to students or to their families. These scholarships and other contributions have always been paid solely from personal funds, sometimes held at and paid through the family business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report follows last month\u8217\'20\'19s bombshell report by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that revealed Thomas had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  luxury travel from Crow annually for decades without publicly disclosing them.\par \par \uc2 The revelations have caught the ire of many lawmakers and ethics experts.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Democrats called for tighter rules and ethics standards for the supreme court justices, which Republicans pushed back against, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/02/republicans-democrats-supreme-court-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling }}}\uc2  Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts an \u8220\'20\'1Cassault\u8230\'20\'26[and] about trying to delegitimize a conservative court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Private school tuition for \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 's great-nephew paid for by billionaire GOP donor: report\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. A great- nephew of \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , whom the supreme court justice described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cson \u8221\'20\'1D, had his private school tuition paid for by billionaire GOP donor Harlan Crow, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-private-school-tuition-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Financial documents reviewed by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  showed that in July 2009, a payment was made by \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s company to Hidden Lake Academy, a private boarding school in northern Georgia where tuition ran over $6,00 monthly. The payment of $6,200 was labeled with the name of Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s great-nephew, Mark Martin.\par \par \uc2 Martin, who was taken into legal custody by Thomas when he was six years old, had his tuition paid for entirely by Crow during his time at Hidden Lake Academy, which was about a year, according to a former school administrator Christopher Grimwood.\par \par \uc2 Thomas did not report \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tuition payments on his annual financial disclosures, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  revealed in its investigation. This investigation follows another \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report last month which revealed that Thomas accepted luxury travel from Crow for decades without disclosing them on his financial reports.\par \par \uc2 Here are other developments in US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A New York judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/03/donald-trump-lawsuit-new-york-times-mary-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thrown out}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2021 lawsuit that accused the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  of an \u8220\'20\'1Cinsidious plot\u8221\'20\'1D to obtain his tax records.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will meet with \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  CEOs today to discuss AI risks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iowa lawmakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/05/03/politics/iowa-child-labor-bill-passes/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  a Republican-led bill that allows teenagers to work longer hours and take previously banned jobs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230504ej54001mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
