\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republicans reject  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans as \u8216\'20\'18campaign-enders\u8217\'20\'19 in warning to party\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,232 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2023\par 17:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As states continue to bring in tighter restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , internal divisions within the GOP are starting to show\par \par \uc2 In one state, Republican women filibustered to block a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban introduced by their own party. In another, the Republican co-sponsor of a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban subsequently tanked his own bill. On the federal level , a Republican congresswoman warns that the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance could mean \u8220\'20\'1Closing huge\u8221\'20\'1D in 2024.\par \par \uc2 As states continue to bring in tighter restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the fall of Roe v Wade, internal divisions within the Republican party on the issue are starting to show.\par \par \uc2 Divisions became most apparent last week in the deep red states of South Carolina and Nebraska, where Republicans roundly rejected further attempts to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights last week.\par \par \uc2 In South Carolina on Thursday, all five female senators \u8211\'20\'13 three of them Republican \u8211\'20\'13 led a filibuster that ultimately blocked a bill which would have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from conception with very few exceptions.\par \par \uc2 That was the third time a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed in the Republican-dominated senate in South Carolina since Roe was overturned last summer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe told them, \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t take us down this path again for the third time in six months \u8211\'20\'13 you will regret it.\u8217\'20\'19 And so we made them regret it,\u8221\'20\'1D said state senator Sandy Senn, who spoke at length on the senate floor on Thursday, of the male Republican senators continually pushing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in her state \u8211\'20\'13 including in an earlier attempt this year to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess125_2023-2024/bills/3549.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a crime punishable by the death penalty}}}\uc2 . Abortions remain legal until 22 weeks in the state, which has become a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a region with increasingly limited options.\par \par \uc2 With nothing having changed since the last two times the senators brought the bill, Senn said her Republican counterparts knew another \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban had no hopes of passing. But with an election looming in 2024, she believes they are keen to flaunt their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was just trying to flex his Republican credentials,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of Shane Massey, the senate leader, who voted in favor of the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants people to know, \u8216\'20\'18I want a strict ban, I want no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19m going to try it for the third time and lose, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not my fault that we lost \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s these Republicans who voted against me.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Nebraska, an attempt to bring a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban failed by a single vote in the majority Republican chamber. Merv Riepe, a Republican senator who had initially co-sponsored the bill chose to withhold his vote on Thursday, becoming an unlikely player in the bill\u8217\'20\'19s demise, having voted in its favor as recently as two weeks prior.\par \par \uc2 But Riepe had raised hesitations about the bill back in March, telling local press that six weeks might not be enough time for a person to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.klkntv.com/report-cosponsor-of-nebraskas-6-week-abortion-ban-now-says-its-too-extreme/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 realize they are pregnant and get an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He did propose an amendment to the bill on Thursday, proposing a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 12 weeks, but other Republican legislators rejected it, saying they had already compromised enough.\par \par \uc2 Barrett Marson, a GOP strategist based in Arizona, said that these increasingly visible tensions may speak to a difficulty that Republicans are having trying to balancing different wings of the party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a tension between the base of the Republican party and moderate Republicans. The hardcore base wants outright bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the broader electorate, and certainly a substantial amount of right-leaning independents and moderate Republicans, want to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal but rare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marson.\par \par \uc2 Those tensions are certainly becoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/30/republicans-divided-abortion-democrats-united-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clear on the national stage}}}\uc2 , with growing numbers of Republicans sounding the alarm that the party should not lean too far right on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially since last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms showed a string of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/11/abortion-midterm-elections-republicans-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victories for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  that seem to suggest the party\u8217\'20\'19s stance on the issue is out of sync with the general public.\par \par \uc2 Recent weeks have also seen a number of Republican presidential hopefuls trying to walk back the party\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Last week, the former South Carolina governor Nikki Haley asked the party for a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/30/republicans-divided-abortion-democrats-united-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 humanizing, not demonizing}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D conversation on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Donald Trump has indicated he thinks a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 touted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senator Lindsey Graham}}}\uc2  last year \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a losing proposal for 2024}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following a supreme court decision to keep access to a crucial drug in medication abortions widely available for the time being, the Republican congresswoman Nancy Mace said told ABC she agreed with the ruling.\par \par \uc2 As Republicans, we need to read the room on this issue, because the vast majority of folks are not in the extremes\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Nancy Mace\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want us to find some middle ground,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said. \u8220\'20\'1CI represent a very purple district \u8230\'20\'26 As Republicans, we need to read the room on this issue, because the vast majority of folks are not in the extremes,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Mace criticized a recent decision by the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , to sign a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in his own state \u8211\'20\'13 a bill she said he \u8220\'20\'1Csigned in the dead of the night\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to lose huge if we continue down this path of extremities \u8230\'20\'26 [People] want exceptions for rape and incest, they want women to have access to birth control. These are very commonsense positions that we can take and still be pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace said.\par \par \uc2 Senn\u8217\'20\'19s own decision to join the filibuster in South Carolina, she said, was about principle \u8211\'20\'13 but she added that the politics are also compelling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs far as in my state, 53% of the Republican voters agree with me. And in my district, 70% agree with me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want any woman to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I hope she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to, but I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to judge her. And she has to have a meaningful opportunity to make her decision,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Senn supports a ban after 12 weeks, with exceptions for people who have been raped, victims of incest, or whose life is threatened by a pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 and said she continues to be shocked by fellow Republican who disagree with that stance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe baby is not even a baby at that point. In my state, 19 lawmakers in our house of representatives signed on to a bill that would make a woman guilty of murder if she had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any stage,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to a recent bill. \u8220\'20\'1CI just wish we had more people in the middle, with common sense on all issues. And on this issue, why not have some mercy?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks.\par \par \uc2 Marson, the strategist, believes the mixed messaging from the party could end in catastrophe for Republicans in 2024 if they don\u8217\'20\'19t heed those calls.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have to guess what will happen. Just a little over six months ago, we saw what the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  does to the electorate \u8211\'20\'13 it pushes them to Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen states like Kansas, one of the more conservative states in the country, reject \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. A six-week ban that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t allow for exception of rape and incest and life of the mother \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s a campaign-ender for a Republican,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230504ej54000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
