\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We need to read the room\u8217\'20\'19: GOP divided on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  as Democrats unite for 2024\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington DC \par \uc2 1,817 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2023\par 07:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats center \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in early stages of presidential campaign while Republicans waver over unpopular position\par \par \uc2 Hours after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his re-election campaign on Tuesday, his vice-president and 2024 running mate, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , delivered a fiery call to action for voters alarmed by the loss of constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a moment for us to stand and fight,\u8221\'20\'1D she said to a packed auditorium at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , a historically Black college in Washington and her alma mater. To the \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist so-called leaders\u8221\'20\'1D rolling back access to reproductive rights, Harris warned: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t get in our way because if you do, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to stand up, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to organize and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to speak up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Across the Potomac, Republican presidential candidate Nikki Haley appealed for a \u8220\'20\'1Cnational consensus\u8221\'20\'1D on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a carefully worded speech delivered earlier that day from the Arlington headquarters of a leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group. Sidestepping the thorny policy debates already animating the Republican primary contest, she said her focus was on \u8220\'20\'1Chumanizing, not demonizing\u8221\'20\'1D the conversation around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in compassion, not anger,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t judge someone who is pro-choice any more than I want them to judge me for being pro-life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nearly a year after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade, the battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is shaping the opening stages of the 2024 presidential contest.\par \par \uc2 In dueling speeches this week, Harris and Haley previewed sharply contrasting approaches to an issue that is energizing Democrats and dividing Republicans. It\u8217\'20\'19s a sign of just how dramatically \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics have shifted in the post-Roe era.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, who for decades championed the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda of the religious right, are now wavering on their positions, no longer sure of how to navigate an abiding principle of American conservatism in their quest to win control of the White House and Congress.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democrats running for office at every level of government \u8211\'20\'13 from the presidential ticket on down \u8211\'20\'13 are placing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the heart of their campaigns, presenting themselves as bulwarks against Republican extremism on the issue. It was a strategy the party used to surprising success in the 2022 midterm elections last year, when voters in red states, blue states and swing states resisted attempts to advance \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 And it worked again earlier this month, when a liberal judge won a pivotal Wisconsin supreme court race after clearly telegraphing her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Her victory likely guarantees the court\u8217\'20\'19s new liberal majority will strike down the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a defining issue for millions and millions of Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cecile Richards, a former CEO of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  who is now a co-chair of Democratic Super Pac American Bridge 21st Century. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, she predicted, would be \u8220\'20\'1Ceven more important\u8221\'20\'1D in 2024 than they were last year, as Americans grapple with the consequences of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and restricted access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the harm to American people, to women, to families is going to continue to be on display and that you can lay directly at the feet of the Republican party,\u8221\'20\'1D Richards said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are almost universally aligned in their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and largely unified in their messaging: Republicans, they warn, will not stop until \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is outlawed in all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir ultimate goal is clear: a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic senator ?Dick Durbin? of Illinois? said this week, in remarks opening a committee hearing titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Assault on Reproductive Rights in a Post-Dobbs America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The high court\u8217\'20\'19s June decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cpaved the way for activist judges and Republican lawmakers to try to impose their anti-choice agenda on everyone else, even in states that have protected the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During the session, Democratic senators assailed a ruling earlier this month by a conservative judge in Texas to suspend the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. Republicans, meanwhile, were largely muted in their response to the decision.\par \par \uc2 If allowed to stand, the Texas order would have far-reaching implications for access to one of the most common methods of terminating a pregnancy in the US, including in places where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal. For now, the supreme court ordered the pill to remain widely available while the appeals process plays out.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are divided over how to counter the attacks. Some Republicans have argued that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a matter best left to the states, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 position recently endorsed}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America (SBA), one of the most powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbaprolife.org/newsroom/press-releases/sba-donald-trumps-states-only-position-unacceptable-pro-life-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired back }}}\uc2  with a warning to the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 hopefuls: any candidate who does not endorse a national ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy will not receive their support.\par \par \uc2 The rift between Trump and the movement leaders who once anointed him the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D president in history for his role delivering the conservative supreme court majority that struck down Roe underscores the challenge for Republican candidates as they seek to appeal to their party\u8217\'20\'19s socially conservative base in the primary without alienating independents and swing voters in a general election.\par \par \uc2 Haley sought to strike that balance In her speech from SBA\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters this week. Emphasizing her \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D record both as the governor of South Carolina and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , she said there was a role for the federal government to play in regulating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but largely avoided specific policy prescriptions.\par \par \uc2 In a statement after the speech, SBA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sbaprolife/status/1650903014708854787"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Haley had made \u8220\'20\'1Cclear\u8221\'20\'1D to the group that she was committed to \u8220\'20\'1Cacting on the American consensus against late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by protecting unborn children by at least 15 weeks\u8221\'20\'1D. (A spokesman for the Haley campaign said she wanted to build \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus to ban late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D but did not say whether she supported such a proposal. SBA did not respond to an email seeking clarity.)\par \par \uc2 Senator Tim Scott of South Carolina waffled on his position in the days after launching a presidential exploratory committee, declining to say if he would support a national 15-week ban. He later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/tim-scott-republican-president-new-hampshire-abortion-fe4edf79d4a1aa0dc77b8625e8e14135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed a 20-week ban}}}\uc2  before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DNCWarRoom/status/1650541901911666690?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying in an interview}}}\uc2  that he would sign \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most conservative pro-life legislation you could bring to my desk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates applauded Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida, seen as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most formidable challenger for the nomination, after he signed into law legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans#:~:text=Ron%20DeSantis%20signs%20bill%20approving%20six%2Dweek%20abortion%20ban%20in%20Florida,-Bill%20gives%20governor&text=The%20Republican%2Ddominated%20Florida%20legislature,for%20an%20expected%20presidential%20run."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions after six weeks}}}\uc2 , before many women realize they are pregnant. But the decision to do so has alarmed some Republicans, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/ron-desantis-republican-donor-thomas-peterffy-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a top party donor}}}\uc2  who cited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of the reason he was pausing plans to fund DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s yet-to-be announced presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose huge if we continue down this path of extremities\par \par \uc2 Republican congresswoman Nancy Mace\par \par \uc2 Perhaps no potential Republican contender has taken a harder line on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , a staunch social conservative. He has embraced a national ban and recently welcomed the Texas decision on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Disagreement among the party\u8217\'20\'19s notional field of Republican presidential contenders all but guarantees a robust policy debate on the issue, forcing them to articulate a federal plan that details how early in a pregnancy to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and when to allow exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Americans almost universally agree that women should be able to terminate their pregnancy in cases of rape, incest or to save the life of the mother, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23786178-nbc-april-2023-poll?responsive=1&title=1&utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC poll}}}\uc2 . And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/04/11/by-more-than-two-to-one-americans-say-medication-abortion-should-be-legal-in-their-state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a survey by the Pew Research Center}}}\uc2  recently found that Americans, by a margin of two to one, believe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Republicans, we need to read the room on this issue because the vast majority of folks are not in the extremes,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican congresswoman Nancy Mace of South Carolina said in an appearance on ABC News\u8217\'20\'19s This Week. Mace, who like most of her party describes herself as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, is part of an increasingly vocal group of Republicans urging her party to avoid politically perilous positions that risk alienating the broader American public that supports legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose huge if we continue down this path of extremities,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Leaders of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement say Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 silence on the issue, not their policy positions, is to blame for the string of recent electoral setbacks. They point to DeSantis, Georgia Governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  and Ohio Governor \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2  as examples of Republicans who sailed to re-election last year, after signing into law new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . All are from right-leaning but still-contested states.\par \par \uc2 Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategists are advising Republican candidates to talk as little as possible about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Meanwhile, Biden plastered \b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  all over his new campaign video,\u8221\'20\'1D Kristan Hawkins, the president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life of America, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KristanHawkins/status/1650954256147443732"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey are talking about it, so we 100% should be too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking recently at the Reagan Library, \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  , the chair of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , urged the party faithful not to impose \u8220\'20\'1Crigid, ideological purity tests\u8221\'20\'1D while pushing her candidates to lean into the debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can win on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that means putting Democrats on the defense and forcing them to own their own extreme positions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, citing polling that showed support for a 15-week federal ban.\par \par \uc2 But corralling her party behind a unified policy is no easy task. After a half-century of pushing to eliminate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, conservatives feel emboldened to push ever more restrictive laws in places where they hold power.\par \par \uc2 This week, North Dakota became the latest state to dramatically limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , banning the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy, with no exceptions for rape or incest. And a new law in Idaho would criminalize those who help a minor obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in another state without a parent\u8217\'20\'19s permission.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in South Carolina and Nebraska, the state\u8217\'20\'19s conservative-majority legislatures failed to pass new bills banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , another sign of just how complicated the issue has become for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Molly Murphy, a Democratic pollster who has studied public attitudes on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said voters are highly attuned to the fast-changing legal and political landscape. And repeatedly since Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, she noted, they have made clear their opposition to further restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat voters want is for Republican politicians to stay out of their personal lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy said. Until then, she said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would continue to be a powerful motivator for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe energy has not waned,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230430ej4u000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
