\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  says leaked  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  draft made conservative justices \u8216\'20\'18targets of assassination\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,068 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2023\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade last yearSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644beeaf8f08e1eb821c8931#block-644beeaf8f08e1eb821c8931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handed down a ruling}}}\uc2  that paves the way for partisan gerrymandering in the state, which its GOP-controlled legislature is expected to use to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bf1c58f08a11e50b4b5d1#block-644bf1c58f08a11e50b4b5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oust four Democratic House lawmakers}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues, with former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bc06e8f08ac41bd013b1d#block-644bc06e8f08ac41bd013b1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearing before}}}\uc2  his grand jury yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , author of the supreme court opinion overturning Roe v Wade, said a leak of the decision\u8217\'20\'19s draft {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644c12b98f08e1eb821c8b18#block-644c12b98f08e1eb821c8b18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put conservative justices in danger}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644be5c38f08e1eb821c88a0#block-644be5c38f08e1eb821c88a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing a reckoning}}}\uc2  over his actions while deployed at the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo prison camp, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644be8d88f0856aad1f25a61#block-644be8d88f0856aad1f25a61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not like}}}\uc2  being asked about it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An investigation into allegations of misconduct by \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  prior to his supreme court confirmation contained omissions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bc82e8f089fb8070f7b72#block-644bc82e8f089fb8070f7b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Guardian investigation}}}\uc2  has found.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers nationwide are accusing their opponents of inciting \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrections\u8221\'20\'1D, even when their actions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bcf848f08ac41bd013c07#block-644bcf848f08ac41bd013c07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t fit}}}\uc2  the definition of the word.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644c04598f0856aad1f25c0b#block-644c04598f0856aad1f25c0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was not pleased}}}\uc2  with Axios, after a report from the outlet detailing concerns about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/28/this-was-unexpected-abortion-bans-blocked-in-nebraska-and-south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was defeated}}}\uc2  in part due to a revolt by female Republican senators, who joined with Democrats to vote down the proposal.\par \par \uc2 One of those lawmakers, Sandy Senn, spoke to MSNBC about what motivated her stand:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I'm not going to vote in a way that's going to oppress women simply because the party might want me to pander to them."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 South Carolina State Rep. Sandy Senn (R) defends joining Democrats to vote down a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban Thursday in the legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5igAVMyrCz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5igAVMyrCz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1652038382199906313?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats have a tough order next year. They will need to defend their control of the White House and majority in the Senate, and try to retake the House. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  has more details on how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to deploy vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to to win a second term:\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  seeks to conquer public concern he is too old to run for and complete a second term in office, the White House is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/biden-looks-elevate-harris-work-core-re-election-bid-rcna80996"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  planning to boost support for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , in the face of increasing Republican attacks.\par \par \uc2 An unnamed source \u8220\'20\'1Cfamiliar with conversations inside the White House\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/biden-looks-elevate-harris-work-core-re-election-bid-rcna80996"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThey need her to be strong. They know she is a target, and the attacks have always been intense, and the ante is going to be upped. So they want to make sure she is on the best possible footing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An unnamed Democratic strategist, meanwhile, pointed to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s eight years as vice-president to Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/kamala-harris-biden-age-2024-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House boosts Kamala Harris as Biden faces age-related attacks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  and Babydog yesterday, when he announced his campaign for \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . Photograph: Chris Jackson/AP\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade was overturned after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed three conservative justices to the supreme court, which he was able to do because Republicans controlled the Senate. And Republicans gained control of the Senate by spending the 2010s ousting Democrats from their seats, as states once friendly to the party turned against them.\par \par \uc2 One of the last Democratic senators hanging on in a red state is West Virgnia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 . He is up for re-election next year in a contest that could decide Senate control, and while he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said if he will seek a third full term, he gained a new challenger this week.\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  announced his candidacy alongside his pet, Babydog. The English Bulldog was right next to him in a public event to kick off his campaign, and in a Fox News interview:\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  (R-WV), with Babydog seated next to him, reacts to Sen. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  (D-WV) saying \u8220\'20\'1CI will win any race I enter\u8221\'20\'1D after Justice announced a run for his seat:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI welcome \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  to come into the race \u8230\'20\'26 But, at the end of the day, I think we\u8217\'20\'19ll be OK.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/00htCIAp0h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/00htCIAp0h}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1651963388300279810?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 By overturning Roe v Wade, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and other conservative supreme court justices allowed states to ban the procedure, and some Republican-led governments already have. But the Associated Press reports that such efforts have faced surprising headwinds in some Republican jurisdictions:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights campaigners won notable victories in Nebraska and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  on Thursday, blocking a six-week ban in the first state and a near-total ban in the second.\par \par \uc2 In Lincoln, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nebraska"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska}}}\uc2 , a vote to end debate so the bill could advance failed by one vote. Cheers erupted as opponents of the bill waved signs and chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CWhose house? Our house!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jo Giles, executive director of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Fund of Omaha, was brought to tears.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWow!\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was unexpected, but we\u8217\'20\'19re so glad to have this win. We have fought so hard. This bill is not what the majority of women in this state wanted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/28/this-was-unexpected-abortion-bans-blocked-in-nebraska-and-south-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This was unexpected\u8217\'20\'19: \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans blocked in Nebraska and South Carolina }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opinion leak made conservative justices 'targets of assassination': Alito\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the author of last year\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade and allowing states to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/supreme-court-abortion-law-leak-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the leak of a draft ruling}}}\uc2  put conservative justices in peril.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose of us who were thought to be in the majority, thought to have approved my draft opinion, were really targets of assassination,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito said in an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-samuel-alito-this-made-us-targets-of-assassination-dobbs-leak-abortion-court-74624ef9?st=coy6yyy6bi923ji"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt was rational for people to believe that they might be able to stop the decision in Dobbs by killing one of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The leak of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization marked a rare moment in which the public learned of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision before its official announcement. Supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  ordered an investigation into the leak, and this past January, the court\u8217\'20\'19s marshal said she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/jan/19/us-supreme-court-leaked-dobbs-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 couldn\u8217\'20\'19t say who was the culprit}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI personally have a pretty good idea who is responsible, but that\u8217\'20\'19s different from the level of proof that is needed to name somebody,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a part of an effort to prevent the Dobbs draft... from becoming the decision of the court. And that\u8217\'20\'19s how it was used for those six weeks by people on the outside\u8212\'20\'14as part of the campaign to try to intimidate the court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justices rarely grant interviews, but Alito, who was appointed by Republican \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , spoke to an an editor on the Journal\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board, which is reliably conservative. The other interviewer was David B Rivkin Jr, a former attorney in the administrations of \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 A woman who was jailed for her participation in the Jan. 6 insurrection embraced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a campaign event and called for the execution of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At a Thursday campaign event in New Hampshire, QAnon supporter Micki Larson-Olson was pointed out to Trump as someone who participated in Jan 6. Trump then found Larson-Olsen, gave her a hug, and called her \u8220\'20\'1Cterrific\u8221\'20\'1D, reported the Hill. Trump also told Larson-Olsen to \u8220\'20\'1Chang in there\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During an NBC interview the following day, the woman called Trump the \u8220\'20\'1Creal president\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that she \u8220\'20\'1Cwould like a front seat of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  being executed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Larson-Olsen was previously sentenced to six months in prison for her participation in Jan. 6 riots.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House hits back over Biden 'age' article\par \par \uc2 The White House has responded to claims made by the political website Axios that White House staffers face challenges with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because of his age.\par \par \uc2 In an article published Friday, Axios said voters were concerned about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age amid recent announcements that he plans to run for a second term.\par \par \uc2 The article also White House officials were \u8220\'20\'1Camazed at Biden\u8217\'20\'19s stamina \u8211\'20\'13 often adding the caveat \u8216\'20\'18for his age\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D and had difficulty scheduling meetings with Biden outside of 10am to 4pm on weekdays.\par \par \uc2 In response to the article, White House deputy press secretary Andrew Bates criticized the outlet on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , writing that Axios previously claimed White House advisers as sources on a story claiming Biden would not announce a reelection campaign. He posted:\par \par \uc2 enltrFunnily, half our on record response was omitted. For transparency: \u8220\'20\'1CAre these the same \u8216\'20\'18advisers and close allies\u8217\'20\'19 who you wrote on April 3 \u8216\'20\'18don't expect him to announce a run for re-election any time soon?\u8217\'20\'19"\par \par \uc2 Age well, kids: "Biden holds back '24 launch" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PuGtQKzfk1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PuGtQKzfk1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yfBCDTSp9M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yfBCDTSp9M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Bates (@AndrewJBates46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewJBates46/status/1651903914780884992?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our columnist Moira Donegan considers the current impasse between the Democratic-controlled Senate judiciary committee and the conservative \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , over ethics rules and the justices, in light of reporting about \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 It was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1650993343608782848/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short letter}}}\uc2 . \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , chief justice of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , was brief in his missive to Democratic senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , who chairs the Senate judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 Citing \u8220\'20\'1Cseparation of powers concerns and the importance of preserving judicial independence\u8221\'20\'1D, Roberts declined to appear before the committee to discuss disturbing recent revelations of ethics violations at the court.\par \par \uc2 Congress is meant to exert checks on judicial power \u8211\'20\'13 to investigate or even impeach judges who abuse their office or interpret the law in ways that violate its spirit, and to affirm that the elected branches will hold more sway over policy than the appointed one. But the chief justice\u8217\'20\'19s show of indifference to congressional oversight authority reflects a new reality: that there are now effectively no checks on the power of the court \u8211\'20\'13 at least none that Democrats have the political will to use \u8211\'20\'13 and that the justices can be assured that they will face no repercussions even if they act in flagrant violation of ethical standards. It seems that they intend to.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/28/supreme-court-ethics-issues-worse-than-you-realize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s alleged ethics issues are worse than you probably realize | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some lunchtime reading from Jason Stanley, Jacob Urowsky professor of philosophy at \uc2 Yale University\uc2 , and the author of How Fascism Works\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Fox News has finally broken ties with its most popular star, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . His ousting has been bemoaned by some commentators, who have taken Carlson to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://prospect.org/politics/2023-04-25-tucker-carlson-smuggest-man-on-air/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebellious anti-war populist}}}\uc2 , evading easy political characterization. But is it really so complicated to classify Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s political ideology?\par \par \uc2 In late February 2022, Carlson, in the face of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, began a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1496290844797992960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1496290844797992960%7Ctwgr%5E5d2be7eb0cd217bb85030710de9922aedf43af79%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fmedia%2F2022%2F02%2F23%2Ftucker-carlson-putin-russia-ukraine%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-Russia monologue}}}\uc2  urging his audience to ask themselves the question: \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do I hate Putin so much?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The gist of Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s leader is that Putin should not be regarded as an enemy. Instead, the real enemies of America are those who call white Americans racist, those who teach so-called critical race theory in schools, business elites who ship jobs abroad, and those who imposed Covid lockdowns on the United States.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/28/tucker-carlson-politics-fascism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tucker Carlson is not an antiwar populist rebel. He is a fascist | Jason Stanley}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 More shots have been fired in the brewing Republican brouhaha over \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fight with \uc2 Disney\uc2 , if from an unexpected artillery piece: that fielded by Kevin McCarthy, the speaker of the US House.\par \par \uc2 Kevin McCarthy. Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d give him the same advice I gave President Biden,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy told CNBC, while basking in having managed to pass a budget proposal amid a standoff with the White House over the increasingly pressing need to raise the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t you sit down and negotiate and talk? If there\u8217\'20\'19s differences, you can always find ways that you can solve this problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis and \uc2 Disney\uc2  are at odds over the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law about teaching gender and LGBTQ+ issues in schools, and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s power grab at self-governing powers long enjoyed by the entertainment giant around its \uc2 Disney\uc2  World theme park near Orlando.\par \par \uc2 This week, \uc2 Disney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/26/disney-sues-governor-ron-desantis-florida-resort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued the governor}}}\uc2  and the governor, while on an international tour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/disney-lawsuit-desantis-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 snapped back}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a big employer inside Florida. I think the governor should sit down with them. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the idea of building a prison next to a place that you bring your family\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a threat made by DeSantis, possibly in jest \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cis the best idea. I think it\u8217\'20\'19d be much better if you sat down and solved the problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s standing in the Republican presidential primary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/22/desantis-2024-polls-florida-disney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has slipped}}}\uc2 , as concerns about issues including his attempt to bend \uc2 Disney\uc2  to his will are expressed within the party.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re going to be a large employer inside this state, you should also abide by the rules and run your business and don\u8217\'20\'19t think you should get into politics. You can take whatever position you want, but remember, if you\u8217\'20\'19re elected to run a business, that\u8217\'20\'19s what your shareholders want you to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here, as previously trailed today, is some further reading about DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s military service:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/ron-desantis-guantanamo-bay-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo: how questions about his past haunt the Florida governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644beeaf8f08e1eb821c8931#block-644beeaf8f08e1eb821c8931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has handed down a ruling}}}\uc2  that paves the way for partisan gerrymandering in the state, which its GOP-controlled legislature is expected to use to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bf1c58f08a11e50b4b5d1#block-644bf1c58f08a11e50b4b5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oust four Democratic House lawmakers}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continues, with former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bc06e8f08ac41bd013b1d#block-644bc06e8f08ac41bd013b1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearing before}}}\uc2  his grand jury yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644be5c38f08e1eb821c88a0#block-644be5c38f08e1eb821c88a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing a reckoning}}}\uc2  over his actions while deployed at the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo prison camp, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644be8d88f0856aad1f25a61#block-644be8d88f0856aad1f25a61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does not like}}}\uc2  being asked about it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An investigation into allegations of misconduct by \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  prior to his supreme court confirmation contained omissions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bc82e8f089fb8070f7b72#block-644bc82e8f089fb8070f7b72"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Guardian investigation}}}\uc2  has found.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers nationwide are accusing their opponents of inciting \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrections\u8221\'20\'1D, even when their actions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/28/jan-6-trump-pence-biden-debt-ceiling-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644bcf848f08ac41bd013c07#block-644bcf848f08ac41bd013c07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t fit}}}\uc2  the definition of the word.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The verdict on the North Carolina supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision from elections doyen Dave Wasserman is that Democrats are poised to lose four seats in the state:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: as expected, new GOP majority on NC Supreme Court reverses previous court's ruling that partisan gerrymandering is illegal. This could wipe out four Dem seats, nearly doubling the GOP's cushion in the House. Full backstory at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CookPolitical?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CookPolitical}}}\uc2  : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HkgUv9uCuJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HkgUv9uCuJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1651983903958224896?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The big winner here could be House speaker Kevin McCarthy, who\u8217\'20\'19s had a tough time running the chamber with the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s mere four-vote majority. Another four Republican seats would certainly make his job easier.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina supreme court OKs partisan gerrymandering\par \par \uc2 The newly Republican-dominated North Carolina supreme court has handed down a decision that reverses a previous ruling declaring partisan gerrymandering illegal, setting the stage for the GOP to redraw the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map to their favor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/28/north-carolina-supreme-court-clears-way-for-partisan-gerrymandering-00094433"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision was not unexpected, and sets the stage for Democrats to lose House seats representing the states. Here\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of the case from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  last month, after oral arguments:\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina supreme court heard oral arguments on Tuesday in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/north-carolina-voting-rights-cases-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major gerrymandering case}}}\uc2  that could have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/06/supreme-court-voting-rights-moore-v-harper-gerrymander-voter-id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant implications}}}\uc2  for US voting rights.\par \par \uc2 In a highly unusual move, the North Carolina court appears poised to overrule itself and get rid of congressional and state legislative districts it approved last year. The GOP-drawn map that was struck down could have produced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/02/04/north-carolina-congressional-map-struck-down-00005974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11-3 advantage}}}\uc2  for Republicans in the congressional delegation. The one that replaced it was far less advantageous to the GOP and wound up producing a 7-7 split in the 2022 midterm elections. The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision would probably allow Republicans to get a more advantageous map back in place.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/14/north-carolina-court-gerrymandering-case-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina court appears poised to overrule itself in gerrymandering case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has obtained new images taken of Barack Obama and his top officials on the day in 2011 that US forces killed \uc2 Osama bin Laden\uc2  in Pakistan.\par \par \uc2 The images, which are interesting and coupled with a retelling of how the raid went down from the White House\u8217\'20\'19s perspective, also feature people still active in Washington politics today, most notably \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Have a look {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  grew angry on Thursday when asked by a reporter in Israel about his time at Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s BS\u8221\'20\'1D: \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  demolishes legacy media for using Guantanamo Bay TERRORISTS as sources to fit their "pre-ordained narrative" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uuZkH2TU57"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uuZkH2TU57}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DeSantis War Room ?? (@DeSantisWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DeSantisWarRoom/status/1651607965378441218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 27, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 One interesting thing about this clip is that it\u8217\'20\'19s been shared on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  both by DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s own media operation (which is posted above) and by Democrats looking to attack the presumptive candidate for the GOP presidential nomination. Make of that what you will.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is expected to announce a campaign for the Republican presidential nomination any day now. He\u8217\'20\'19ll do that amid a swirl of questions about his actions while working at the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo prison camp, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/laughland-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Laughland}}}\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 In the middle of a June night 17 years ago in the Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo prison camp, guards and medical orderlies were urgently summoned to one of the inmate clinics, where an emergency was unfolding.\par \par \uc2 Two inmates, Ali Abdullah Ahmed and Mani Shaman al-Utaybi, had been brought in dead. A third, Yasser Talal al-Zahrani, had been rushed to the hospital on the US naval base but was declared dead there soon afterwards. The three men were found hanging from their necks, with their hands and feet bound and rags in their throats.\par \par \uc2 It was the worst loss of life in the prison camp\u8217\'20\'19s history \u8211\'20\'13 in the midst of a turbulent year in which there were hunger strikes and riots as well as the three deaths \u8211\'20\'13 and officers around the base were roused from their sleep and rushed to Camp Delta, the main internment centre.\par \par \uc2 Rear Admiral Harry Harris arrived, the base commander who would go on to command the Pacific fleet, accompanied by Col Michael Bumgarner, the head of the overall prison complex. At some point, witnesses say, a more junior officer turned up, a 27-year-old navy lawyer, or judge advocate general (JAG), Lt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/ron-desantis-guantanamo-bay-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis in Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo: how questions about his past haunt the Florida governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration announced on Thursday a set of new initiatives to discourage immigrants from illegally crossing into the US via the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 The measures include harsher crackdowns on those who do come and new pathways that offer an alternative to the dangerous journey, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Such alternatives include setting up migration centers in other countries, increasing the amount of immigrants allowed in, and faster processing of migrants seeking asylum. Those not eligible for asylum who cross over will be penalized, AP further reports.\par \par \uc2 The policies come as May 11 approaches, which will end the public health rule instituted amid the Covid-19 pandemic that allowed for many migrants to be quickly expelled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Montana governor was lobbied by his non-binary child to reject several bills that would harm transgender people in the state, according to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The son of the Republican governor of Montana, \uc2 Greg Gianforte\uc2 , met their father in his office to lobby him to reject several bills that would harm transgender people in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://montanafreepress.org/2023/04/26/montana-governor-gianforte-lobbied-by-son-to-veto-trans-bills/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Montana Free Press reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 David Gianforte told the paper they identify as non-binary and use he/they pronouns \u8211\'20\'13 the first time they disclosed their gender identity publicly. They told the outlet they felt an obligation to use their relationship with their father to stand up for LGBTQ+ people in the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of important issues passing through the legislature right now,\u8221\'20\'1D they said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CFor my own sake I\u8217\'20\'19ve chosen to focus primarily on transgender rights, as that would significantly directly affect a number of my friends \u8230\'20\'26 I would like to make the argument that these bills are immoral, unjust, and frankly a violation of human rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/montana-governor-greg-gianforte-anti-trans-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/montana-governor-greg-gianforte-anti-trans-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana governor lobbied by non-binary son to reject anti-trans bills}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Tennesee lawmaker who was previously outsted for calling for gun control after a Nashville mass shooting has spoken about Zephyr being silenced.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Democracy Now, Tennessee representative Justin Jones spoke with Zephyr about the need for continued solidarity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn attack on one of us is an attack on all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zephyr, after Jones said that several communities stood with Zephyr amid attempts to silence her.\par \par \uc2 enltr"An attack on one of us is an attack on all of us."\par \par \uc2 Rep. Justin Jones of Tennessee and Rep. Zooey Zephyr of Montana share why they continue to act and advocate for their communities, in solidarity across the country. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0MzVAG6dxs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/0MzVAG6dxs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Democracy Now! (@democracynow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/democracynow/status/1651941195252224004?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 28, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Republicans in Montana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/26/zooey-zephyr-banned-montana-house-transgender-care"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barred the state\u8217\'20\'19s sole transgender lawmaker}}}\uc2 , Democrat Zooey Zephyr, from the floor of the state House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Their justification? That Zephyr\u8217\'20\'19s interaction with protesters who were demonstrating against her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/24/montana-republicans-silence-transgender-lawmaker"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier silencing}}}\uc2  by the House\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraging an insurrection.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/zooey-zephyr-montana-transgender-insurrection-trump-tennessee-9eadf09c9670659bee4ec759a4393c9d?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that such claims have become increasingly common in recent months in state legislatures where Republicans rule. Case in point, the rhetoric used by GOP lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/justin-pearson-tennessee-reinstated-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to briefly expel}}}\uc2  two Democrats from the Tennessee state House of Representatives earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Silenced by her Republican colleagues, Montana state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/zooey-zephyr-transgender-montana-house-updates-3054b6bed9ac04920249e6302821e130?utm_source=apnews&utm_medium=relatedcontentmodule"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rep. Zooey Zephyr}}}\uc2  looked up from the House floor to supporters in the gallery shouting \u8220\'20\'1CLet her speak!\u8221\'20\'1D and thrust her microphone into the air \u8212\'20\'14 amplifying the sentiment the Democratic transgender lawmaker was forbidden from expressing.\par \par \uc2 While seven people were arrested for trespassing, the boisterous demonstration was free of violence or damage. Yet later that day, a group of Republican lawmakers described it in darker tones, saying Zephyr\u8217\'20\'19s actions were responsible for \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraging an insurrection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the third time in the last five weeks \u8212\'20\'14 and one of at least four times this year \u8212\'20\'14 that Republicans have attempted to compare disruptive but nonviolent protests at state capitols to insurrections.\par \par \uc2 The tactic follows a pattern set over the past two years when the term has been misused to describe public demonstrations and even the 2020 election that put Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the White House. It\u8217\'20\'19s a move experts say dismisses legitimate speech and downplays the deadly Jan. 6, 2021, assault on the U.S. Capitol by supporters of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Shortly after, the U.S. House voted to impeach him for \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement of insurrection.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ever since, many Republicans have attempted to turn the phrase on Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to ring alarm bells and they want to compare this to Jan. 6,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andy Nelson, the Democratic Party chair in Missoula County, which includes Zephyr\u8217\'20\'19s district. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely no way you can compare what happened on Monday with the Jan. 6 insurrection. Violence occurred that day. No violence occurred in the gallery of the Montana House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s events in the Montana Legislature drew comparisons to a similar demonstration in Tennessee. Republican legislative leaders there used \u8220\'20\'1Cinsurrection\u8221\'20\'1D to describe a protest on the House floor by three Democratic lawmakers who were calling for gun control legislation in the aftermath of a Nashville school shooting that killed three students and three staff. Two of them chanted \u8220\'20\'1CPower to the people\u8221\'20\'1D through a megaphone and were expelled before local commissions reinstated them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports on the latest steps in Florida authorities\u8217\'20\'19 march to tighten down on voting access, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  edges closer to announcing a presidential campaign:\par \par \uc2 Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  are on the verge of passing new restrictions on groups that register voters, a move voting rights groups and experts say will make it harder for non-white Floridians to get on the rolls.\par \par \uc2 The restrictions are part of a sweeping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/7050/BillText/e1/PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 96-page election bill}}}\uc2  the legislature is likely to send to Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s desk soon. The measure increases fines for third-party voter registration groups. It also shortens the amount of time the groups have to turn in any voter registration applications they collect from 14 days to 10. The bill makes it illegal for non-citizens and people convicted of certain felonies to \u8220\'20\'1Ccollect or handle\u8221\'20\'1D voter registration applications on behalf of third-party groups. Groups would also have to give each voter they register a receipt and be required to register themselves with the state ahead of each general election cycle. Under current law, they only have to register once and their registration remains effective indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/florida-republicans-new-voter-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A dangerous trend\u8217\'20\'19: Florida Republicans poised to pass more voter restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  reports that a 2018 investigation that played a role in \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s confirmation to the supreme court was less thorough than it appeared. If you read one Guardian story today, make it this one:\par \par \uc2 A 2018 Senate investigation that found there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno evidence\u8221\'20\'1D to substantiate any of the claims of sexual assault against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  contained serious omissions, according to new information obtained by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 The 28-page report was released by the Republican senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , the then chairman of the Senate judiciary committee. It prominently included an unfounded and unverified claim that one of Kavanaugh\u8217\'20\'19s accusers \u8211\'20\'13 a fellow Yale graduate named Deborah Ramirez \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D mistaken when she alleged that Kavanaugh exposed himself to her at a dormitory party because another Yale student was allegedly known for such acts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/28/brett-kavanaugh-investigation-omissions-senate-sexual-assault-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: Senate investigation into Brett Kavanaugh assault claims contained serious omissions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence at center of Trump's attempt to keep Biden from White House\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  about \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s interview with federal investigators, and why his testimony may be so important to any case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  testified before a federal grand jury on Thursday in Washington about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election results, according to a source familiar with the matter, a day after an appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/26/trump-appeal-pence-testimony-january-6-attack-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a last-ditch motion}}}\uc2  to block his appearance.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s testimony lasted for around seven hours and took place behind closed doors, meaning the details of what he told the prosecutors hearing evidence in the case remains uncertain.\par \par \uc2 His appearance is a moment of constitutional consequence and potential legal peril for the former president. Pence is considered a major witness in the criminal investigation led by special counsel Jack Smith, since Trump pressured him to unlawfully reject electoral college votes for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the joint session of Congress, and was at the White House meeting with Republican lawmakers who discussed objections to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/mike-pence-testifies-donald-trump-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence testifies to grand jury about Donald Trump and January 6}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence interviewed by grand jury investigating January 6 insurrection\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. On Thursday, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/27/mike-pence-testifies-donald-trump-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared before the grand jury}}}\uc2  empaneled by special counsel Jack Smith to consider charges against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the January 6 insurrection. The possibility that Trump could face a federal indictment over the attack, as well as his involvement in plots to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office and the classified materials found at Mar-a-Lago, is a major unknown in the presidential race, particularly since polls show Trump as the most popular Republican candidate. There\u8217\'20\'19s no saying when Smith could make his charging recommendation, but Pence\u8217\'20\'19s testimony is a reminder that the investigation remains a real threat to the former president.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leadership will hold their weekly press conference at 10.30am eastern time. Expect plenty of railing against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/26/us-house-debt-ceiling-bill-passed-kevin-mccarthy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the debt limit proposal}}}\uc2  Republicans passed earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is keeping it low key, presenting the Commander-in-Chief\u8217\'20\'19s trophy to the Air Force Falcons, champions of last year\u8217\'20\'19s Armed Forces Bowl, at 2.30pm, then heading to a Democratic fundraiser in the evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the conservative Democrat representing deep-red West Virginia, yesterday afternoon again called on Biden to negotiate with Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy on an agreement to raise the debt limit. The president has thus far refused to do so.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230428ej4s001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
