\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden foregrounds  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  as he announces bid for second term as US president \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,900 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2023\par 20:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic president, 80, confirms intention to run in 2024Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Washington digested \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he is running for a second term, with Democrats sounding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447decb8f08e51b9c9fff3b#block-6447decb8f08e51b9c9fff3b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very much ready}}}\uc2  for him to remain in office for another four years, and Republicans giving Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447c9118f084a2f5d00ff47#block-6447c9118f084a2f5d00ff47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447ce098f08e51b9c9ffe81#block-6447ce098f08e51b9c9ffe81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sorts}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f0e18f0802b5b51ddebe#block-6447f0e18f0802b5b51ddebe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447ff658f08e51b9ca00183#block-6447ff658f08e51b9ca00183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reasons}}}\uc2  not to vote for him. We\u8217\'20\'19re 560 days away from the 2024 election; prepare for lots more of this.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden said he would veto the Republican debt ceiling bill if it ever gets to his desk, which it probably won\u8217\'20\'19t, at least not in its current form.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Ed Markey{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f9598f084a2f5d0101d3#block-6447f9598f084a2f5d0101d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has called on}}}\uc2  supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign over his recently revealed links to a Republican megadonor. The Democrat is the first senator to make such a demand.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , a conservative supreme court justice, sold a property to the head of a law firm who argues cases before the tribunal shortly after his confirmation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f4148f0802b5b51ddee5#block-6447f4148f0802b5b51ddee5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil trial over a rape allegation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447e80a8f084a2f5d0100ae#block-6447e80a8f084a2f5d0100ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is under way}}}\uc2  in New York City.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Please don\u8217\'20\'19t talk about Biden or Trump\u8217\'20\'19s age, a UK-based charity that focuses on ageing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-64482ace8f08e51b9ca00324#block-64482ace8f08e51b9ca00324"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House congratulated Washington state for enacting tighter restrictions on guns today, including a ban on the sale of certain assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, \uc2 Washington State\uc2  has become the tenth state in the nation alongside Washington DC to ban assault weapons and get weapons of war off America\u8217\'20\'19s streets. President Biden commends the leadership of Washington Governor \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2 , and legislative leaders, as well as the advocates, survivors and elected officials who fought for years to make today a reality. In so doing, they have made every community in the state \u8211\'20\'13 from Seattle to Spokane and everywhere in between \u8211\'20\'13 safer and more secure,\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/semiautomatic-rifle-ban-washington-adbbc5bc0d3b92da0122a91d42bcd4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , Democratic governor \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2  signed three bills today that impose a 10-day waiting period on gun purchases, bans dozens of semi-automatic firearms and allow family members of people who die from gun violence to sue a seller or manufacturer if it \u8220\'20\'1Cis irresponsible in how they handle, store or sell those weapons\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the oldest president ever elected when he won in 2020, and the 80-year-old will continue that record-breaking streak if he wins a second term.\par \par \uc2 Many of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s potential GOP candidates are in their 40s or 50s, but the current frontrunner \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is 76. Age seems certain to be one of the considerations voters will weigh, should the 2024 election come down to the two men. But the UK-based Centre for Ageing Better has a message for Trump, Biden and the 2024 primary field as a whole: leave age out of it.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what their chief executive Carole Easton had to say:\par \par \uc2 Whatever happens over the next 18 months in the US Presidential elections, at the Centre for Ageing Better we have one simple request. No one mentions the age of any of the candidates.\par \par \uc2 The date of birth of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or any other candidate is a completely irrelevant factor in the race. Their competency, their policies, their personal integrity, even their personal finances and health, are all relevant factors in deciding who should be the next occupant of the White House. Their age is not. Whatever the strengths or weaknesses of the candidates, that is a matter of their individual character, not their age.\par \par \uc2 Ageism is so prevalent within society, we are still only now getting to grips with its impact and its seriousness. Ageism assumes that all experiences of getting older are homogenous when we know that is not the case. We must end the continual use of harmful stereotypes about ageing and older age and avoid fuelling intergenerational conflict.\par \par \uc2 The race to become the next US President should be about the competency of individuals. Our concern at Ageing Better is that the campaign provides the background for an outpouring of outdated and offensive stereotypes which will only serve to demonstrate how far we still need to travel to eradicate the scourge of ageism from society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden threatens to veto GOP debt limit bill\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will veto {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/23/us-debt-ceiling-analysis-congress-squabble-default"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Republican proposal}}}\uc2  to raise the debt ceiling while slashing spending and implementing a number of conservative policies, the White House announced today.\par \par \uc2 GOP leaders in the House of Representatives are expected to this week call a vote on the Limit, Save, Grow Act of 2023. Biden has refused to negotiate with Republicans over the debt limit, saying it should be increased without conditions ahead of an estimated June deadline where the \uc2 US government\uc2  will run out of money and potentially default on its obligations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Congress has a solemn obligation to prevent default and ensure that the United States meets its obligations. The Administration strongly opposes the Limit, Save, Grow Act of 2023, which is a reckless attempt to extract extreme concessions as a condition for the United States simply paying the bills it has already incurred,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House office of management and budget (OMB) said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The office takes specific issue with the bill\u8217\'20\'19s mandatory spending reductions, which would \u8220\'20\'1Cforce severe cuts to education (including for students with disabilities), food safety inspections, rail safety, healthy meals for seniors, research on cancer and other diseases, border security, public safety and veterans\u8217\'20\'19 medical care\u8221\'20\'1D. The OMB also objected to the bill\u8217\'20\'19s provisions blocking Biden from relieving some student loan debt, and repealing tax credits included the Inflation Reduction Act, among other issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bill stands in stark contrast to the President\u8217\'20\'19s vision for the economy. The President\u8217\'20\'19s budget invests in America, lowers costs for families, grows the economy, and reduces the deficit by nearly $3tn by asking the wealthy and large corporations to pay their fair share. Therefore, if the president were presented with the Limit, Save, Grow Act of 2023, he would veto it,\u8221\'20\'1D the OMB said.\par \par \uc2 Republicans hold a slim majority in the House, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if they have the votes yet to pass the bill, since some rightwing lawmakers have refused to increase the debt ceiling for any reason. It\u8217\'20\'19s also unlike the measure would attract enough Democratic support to pass the Senate, which they control.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nate Silver is reportedly being forced out of his data-driven political journalism outlet FiveThirtyEight amid the latest round of job cuts at ABC News\u8217\'20\'19s corporate owner, \uc2 Disney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Silver sent an internal message to employees at FiveThirtyEight \u8211\'20\'13 which is hosted by ABC News \u8211\'20\'13 that he expects to leave \uc2 Disney\uc2  when his contract expires \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D, according to an article published by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/digital/nate-silver-leaves-538-abc-news-disney-layoffs-1235401689/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hollywood Reporter}}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Nate Silver. Photograph: Graeme Robertson/The Guardian\par \par \uc2 The Hollywood Reporter said ABC News plans to retain the FiveThirtyEight brand but aims to generally streamline the site ahead of the 2024 presidential election. A statement that ABC issued to the Hollywood Reporter added: \u8220\'20\'1C?We are grateful for the invaluable contributions of the team members who will be departing the organization and know they will continue to make an important impact on the future of journalism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Silver founded FiveThirtyEight in 2008 before taking it with him to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and selling it to the \uc2 Disney\uc2 -owned sports network \uc2 ESPN\uc2 . \uc2 Disney\uc2  later moved FiveThirtyEight to ABC News.\par \par \uc2 According to the internal message from Silver, whose expected departure would mark the first time he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been involved with the site he started, FiveThirtyEight\u8217\'20\'19s staff was in for \u8220\'20\'1Ca hard day\u8221\'20\'1D sooner rather than later because of upcoming layoffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately the day we\u8217\'20\'19ve been worried about has arrived,\u8221\'20\'1D Silver\u8217\'20\'19s message read, according to the Hollywood Reporter. Suggested he was among those who would be leaving the site soon, Silver\u8217\'20\'19s missive added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t yet know the scope of these layoffs, exactly who is [affected], or the terms under which they are departing, but it is going to be a hard day for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Silver later went {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NateSilver538/status/1650899581108994056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Twitter}}}\uc2  and said he \u8220\'20\'1Chad been worried about an outcome like this\u8221\'20\'1D and had already been engaging in conversations about \u8220\'20\'1Copportunities elsewhere\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so proud of the work of FiveThirtyEight staff,\u8221\'20\'1D Silver said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt has never been easy. I\u8217\'20\'19m sorry to the people [affected] by this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The cuts which have ensnared Silver are part of a larger cost-reduction campaign at \uc2 Disney\uc2 , which seeks to eliminate 7,000 jobs to save $5.5bn in expenses, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/apr/24/disney-latest-job-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters}}}\uc2 . It is the second wave of layoffs associated with the cost-cutting plan, Reuters added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Washington is digesting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he\u8217\'20\'19s running for a second term, with Democrats sounding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447decb8f08e51b9c9fff3b#block-6447decb8f08e51b9c9fff3b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very much ready}}}\uc2  for him to stay in office for another four years, and Republicans giving Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447c9118f084a2f5d00ff47#block-6447c9118f084a2f5d00ff47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447ce098f08e51b9c9ffe81#block-6447ce098f08e51b9c9ffe81"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sorts}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f0e18f0802b5b51ddebe#block-6447f0e18f0802b5b51ddebe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447ff658f08e51b9ca00183#block-6447ff658f08e51b9ca00183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reasons}}}\uc2  not to vote for him. We\u8217\'20\'19re 560 days away from the 2024 election; prepare for lots more of this.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Ed Markey{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f9598f084a2f5d0101d3#block-6447f9598f084a2f5d0101d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has called on}}}\uc2  supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign over his recently revealed links to a Republican megadonor. The Democrat is the first senator to make such a demand.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , a conservative supreme court justice, sold a property to the head of a law firm who argues cases before the tribunal shortly after his confirmation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447f4148f0802b5b51ddee5#block-6447f4148f0802b5b51ddee5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil trial over a rape allegation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-trump-us-politics-live?page=with:block-6447e80a8f084a2f5d0100ae#block-6447e80a8f084a2f5d0100ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is under way}}}\uc2  in New York City.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wrapped up his speech, with an exhortation that he\u8217\'20\'19s been using for months: \u8220\'20\'1CFinish the job!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CManufacturing has come alive again. People can afford decent healthcare. Towns that have been forgotten and left behind for dead are coming alive again because of you all and what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing now. Now we\u8217\'20\'19ve just got to keep going. Finish the job!\u8221\'20\'1D the president said as he concluded his remarks.\par \par \uc2 He used the same line in his re-election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1650801827728986112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement today}}}\uc2 , but the speech otherwise avoided mentioning the campaign. That may be because of rules governing the separation between his activities as president \u8211\'20\'13 such as today\u8217\'20\'19s speech \u8211\'20\'13 and as a candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during his speech to the North America's Building Trades Unions legislative conference in Washington DC. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Thus far, this address has proven to be a standard \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stump speech, with no mention of his campaign for re-election.\par \par \uc2 The president is talking about infrastructure, the importance of unions and his promotion of policies that encourage more consumption of American-produced goods. Biden has left the big news of the day \u8211\'20\'13 that he\u8217\'20\'19s running for a second term \u8211\'20\'13 unmentioned, at least so far.\par \par \uc2 The crowd, however, has clearly heard the news. \u8220\'20\'1CFour more years! Four more years!\u8221\'20\'1D they began chanting a few minutes ago. Biden, taking a breather in speech, hung his head and smiled.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has kicked off his speech focusing on manufacturing and his legislative accomplishments.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s before a friendly crowd of union workers, many of whom chanted \u8220\'20\'1CJoe, Joe\u8221\'20\'1D as he walked onstage. Watch it as it happens at the live stream embedded at the top of the page.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden set for first speech since re-election announcement\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will in a few minutes make his first public appearance since announcing his re-election campaign, with an address to a North America\u8217\'20\'19s Building Trades Unions conference in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 According to excerpts released by the White House, the president will cover familiar ground, such as the 2021 infrastructure measure he succeeded in getting Congress to enact. \u8220\'20\'1CUnder my predecessor, Infrastructure Week was a punchline. On my watch, we\u8217\'20\'19re making Infrastructure Decade a headline,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden will say.\par \par \uc2 This blog will be keeping an eye out for any comments the president makes about his campaign for a second term.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Fox News, Republican congressman John James sought to place blame on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for not getting Americans out of harm\u8217\'20\'19s way in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/25/airstrikes-threaten-three-day-truce-in-sudan-khartoum-laboratory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conflict-torn Sudan}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CJoe Biden doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about Black lives until election years, and it's never been more clear than today, with 14,000 Sudanese Americans and our allies being left behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. John James (R-MI) calls out Biden for announcing his re-election today amid the conflict in Sudan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/m5JTmOkziG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/m5JTmOkziG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1650898582373900289?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Democratic candidates have counted on Black voters for decades, and Biden is no exception. Their support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/05/black-voters-wisconsin-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was viewed as key}}}\uc2  to turning around his flagging presidential campaign in 2020, and to his defeat of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  later that year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  has called on supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Senator \uc2 Ed Markey\uc2  calls on \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to resign.\par \par \uc2 Markey\u8217\'20\'19s the first Senator to do so.\par \par \uc2 Thomas \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot judge right from wrong, so why should he be judging the countries most important cases on the highest court.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1f5thMgIDi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1f5thMgIDi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Dworkin (@funder) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/funder/status/1650879732408352770?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Thomas has faced mounting questions over his ethics after investigative news outlet \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/24/harlan-crow-clarence-thomas-ron-wyden-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed his ties}}}\uc2  to a Republican megadonor.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Senate judiciary committee, led by its Democratic chair \uc2 Richard Durbin\uc2 , asked supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to testify about the court\u8217\'20\'19s ethics code.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report reveals link between conservative Justice Gorsuch and law firm\par \par \uc2 Days after he was confirmed to the supreme court, \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  sold a property he co-owned to the head of a law firm that has argued cases before the justices, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/25/neil-gorsuch-colorado-property-sale-00093579"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The story reveals another entanglement between the high court and parties outside it, after \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-harlan-crow-luxury-gifts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ties between}}}\uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , one of the court\u8217\'20\'19s best-known conservative jurors, and a Republican mega-donor. Gorsuch, a conservative, was appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the court in 2017, filling a vacancy created by the death of fellow conservative \uc2 Antonin Scalia\uc2  the year before \u8211\'20\'13 which \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , then the Republican Senate majority leader, prevented Barack Obama from filling.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Politico\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 For nearly two years beginning in 2015, Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  sought a buyer for a 40-acre tract of property he co-owned in rural Granby, Colorado.\par \par \uc2 Nine days after he was confirmed by the Senate for a lifetime appointment on the Supreme Court, the then-circuit court judge got one: The chief executive of \uc2 Greenberg Traurig\uc2 , one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s biggest law firms with a robust practice before the high court. Gorsuch owned the property with two other individuals.\par \par \uc2 On April 16 of 2017, Greenberg\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Brian Duffy\uc2  put under contract the 3,000-square foot log home on the Colorado River and nestled in the mountains northwest of Denver, according to real estate records.\par \par \uc2 He and his wife closed on the house a month later, paying $1.825 million, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://politico.com/f/?id=00000187-b4de-dbff-a3df-bedee6670000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a deed in the county\u8217\'20\'19s record system}}}\uc2 . Gorsuch, who held a 20 percent stake, reported making between $250,001 and $500,000 from the sale on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fixthecourt.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/Gorsuch-NM-J3.-SUP_R_17.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal disclosure forms}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gorsuch did not disclose the identity of the purchaser. That box was left blank.\par \par \uc2 Since then, \uc2 Greenberg Traurig\uc2  has been involved in at least 22 cases before or presented to the court, according to a POLITICO review of the court\u8217\'20\'19s docket.\par \par \uc2 They include cases in which Greenberg either filed amicus briefs or represented parties. In the 12 cases where Gorsuch\u8217\'20\'19s opinion is recorded, he sided with \uc2 Greenberg Traurig\uc2  clients eight times and against them four times.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Capitol Hill, Republican speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy continues to push \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to negotiate with him over raising the debt ceiling:\par \par \uc2 enltrI know President Biden might be focused on his own political future today, but he should be focused on the future of America.\par \par \uc2 Biden should have announced he will finally come to the table and negotiate a responsible debt limit increase to avoid the first default in our history.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1650829698094465024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden has refused to consider anything but a simple increase to America\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit, but McCarthy wants the White House and Democrats to agree to big spending cuts and other conservative priorities, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/23/us-debt-ceiling-analysis-congress-squabble-default"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has proposed legislation}}}\uc2  to implement those. The \uc2 US government\uc2  has already reached the limit on how much it can borrow, and could default on its debt around early June if it isn\u8217\'20\'19t able to borrow more cash.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, Republican lawmaker Tom Cotton, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/11/06/tom-cotton-passes-on-2024-presidential-run-00065334"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ruled out}}}\uc2  a presidential run next year, also hit Biden for not negotiating with McCarthy:\par \par \uc2 enltrFinish the job?\par \par \uc2 Based on Biden's record, this sounds like a threat. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0BYgghDxye"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0BYgghDxye}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Cotton (@TomCottonAR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TomCottonAR/status/1650848273731670017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf Biden can't handle a meeting with Speaker McCarthy, then he's far too old to be president.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Cotton (@TomCottonAR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TomCottonAR/status/1650863482164871174?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal entanglements are many, but polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/nbc-news-poll-nearly-70-gop-voters-stand-trump-indictment-investigatio-rcna80917"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have repeatedly shown}}}\uc2  he remains the most popular candidates among Republicans.\par \par \uc2 A rematch of the 2020 election, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ousted Trump from the White House appears possible, but \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2 , a Democratic congressman and co-chair of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, downplayed the two men\u8217\'20\'19s rivalry in an interview with MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe this is about stopping Trump. This is about continuing our pursuit of a more perfect union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  (D-SC), a co-chair of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, after his endorsement in 2020 was seen as key to Biden's comeback in the primary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/g1DJt1eMDb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/g1DJt1eMDb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1650877432398749696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 While Washington digests the official start of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is probably keeping an eye on a New York courthouse, where a civil case alleging he committed rape is going to trial today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A federal court in New York will begin selecting a jury on Tuesday to hear evidence that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  raped the famed advice columnist E Jean Carroll nearly three decades ago.\par \par \uc2 Carroll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/23/donald-trump-e-jean-carroll-trial-rape"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleges }}}\uc2  that Trump pinned her against the wall of a New York department store and sexually assaulted her in late 1995 or early the following year as they shopped together. She brought the case last year under a New York state law opening a one-year window for adult victims of sexual assault to file civil cases after the statute of limitations has expired.\par \par \uc2 The case is, at least so far, the only one to come to court among more than a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2016/10/13/497799354/a-list-of-donald-trumps-accusers-of-inappropriate-sexual-conduct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dozen allegations}}}\uc2  of rape, groping and other sexual assaults against the former president as well as accusations that he walked unannounced into women\u8217\'20\'19s dressing rooms at beauty pageants.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/donald-trump-rape-trial-jury-selection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jury selection to begin in Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s civil rape trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is running for president in part to protect reproductive rights, another Republican-led state moved yesterday to almost entirely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s exactly the sort of split-screen the Biden campaign is hoping Americans pay attention to. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 North Dakota on Monday adopted one of the strictest anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the US as the Republican governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  signed legislation banning the procedure throughout pregnancy, with slim exceptions up to six weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation.\par \par \uc2 In those early weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be allowed only in cases of rape, incest or medical emergency, such as ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill clarifies and refines existing state law \u8230\'20\'26 and reaffirms North Dakota as a pro-life state,\u8221\'20\'1D Burgum said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Last year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  ruling overturning the 1973 Roe v Wade decision that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide has triggered multiple state laws banning or restricting the procedure. Many were met with legal challenges. Currently, bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all stages of pregnancy are in place in at least 13 states and on hold in others because of court injunctions. On the other side, Democratic governors in at least 20 states this year launched a network intended to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the wake of the supreme court decision that eliminated women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to end a pregnancy and shifted regulatory powers over the procedure to state governments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/24/north-dakota-passes-strictest-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Dakota governor signs law banning nearly all abortions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  re-election train: Barack Obama.\par \par \uc2 Here he is with a show of support for his former deputy:\par \par \uc2 enltrProud of all that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JoeBiden}}}\uc2  and his administration have accomplished these last few years. He\u8217\'20\'19s delivered for the American people \u8212\'20\'14 and he\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to do so once he\u8217\'20\'19s re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s get to work! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eEt7bAueIT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eEt7bAueIT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uBMyS1QQ0V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uBMyS1QQ0V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1650862300289720326?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Also congratulating Biden is California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , who was considered a potential replacement for Biden if the president decided not to run again:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur democracy is under attack. Our freedom is being stripped away.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s time to step up\u8212\'20\'14and there\u8217\'20\'19s no one better to lead that fight than President Biden.\par \par \uc2 Looking forward to another 4 years of his leadership.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s show up big today. Every dollar counts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xNHCc1gaGm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xNHCc1gaGm}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QcVNUwpHc6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QcVNUwpHc6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1650862280098328584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a big day for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but there are plenty of obstacles standing between him and another four years in the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  with a look at some of them:\par \par \uc2 Legend has it that when the artist Benjamin West told King George III that George Washington, the first US president, had decided to resign, the king {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blogs.loc.gov/manuscripts/2022/12/george-washington-the-greatest-man-in-the-world/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replied}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf he does that, he will be the greatest man in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/06/opinion/biden-shouldnt-run-2024.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , the 46th president, to follow suit and, at the age of 80, hand power to a new generation. Who were they kidding? The worst-kept secret in Washington is out: Biden is running for re-election next year.\par \par \uc2 There was an air of inevitability around the announcement. Biden coveted the job for decades, mounting failed campaigns in 1988 and 2008 then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/07/joe-biden-victory-speech-donald-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 succeeding in 2020}}}\uc2 , motivated by a need to rescue \u8220\'20\'1Cthe soul of America\u8221\'20\'1D from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He relishes the most powerful office in the world. He is having too much fun.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/joe-biden-2024-reelection-white-house-democrats-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden gears up for Trump rematch with age and approval front and center}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to making his campaign official, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced key members of its staff.\par \par \uc2 As co-chairs, he named Democratic house representatives \uc2 Lisa Blunt-Rochester\uc2 , \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2 , \uc2 Veronica Escobar\uc2  and Jeffrey Katzenberg, senators Chris Coons and Tammy Duckworth as well as \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s up-and-coming governor.\par \par \uc2 His campaign manager is Julie Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, currently one of his senior advisors and the director of intergovernmental affairs at the White House. She was previously deputy manager of his 2020 campaign, and worked on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ll notice \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign announcement video almost immediately draws viewers\u8217\'20\'19 attention to the topic of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/15/abortion-republicans-election-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a streak of wins at the ballot box}}}\uc2  ever since the conservative-dominated supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last year and allowed states to ban it entirely. Biden clearly hopes that enthusiasm continues when they go to the polls in 2024.\par \par \uc2 To press the message home, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will this evening speak at Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s Howard University during \u8220\'20\'1Ca political event with reproductive rights organizations and advocates\u8221\'20\'1D, according to her office. Expect to hear plenty about how a second term in the White House would allow Biden to continue protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access where he can \u8211\'20\'13 and how a GOP president would do the opposite.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chris Coons, the Democratic senator from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s home state of Delaware, went on CNN this morning to talk up the president\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments, now that he\u8217\'20\'19s made his campaign for a second term official:\par \par \uc2 enltr???? from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisCoons?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ChrisCoons}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump talked about infrastructure. President Biden got it done.\par \par \uc2 Trump talked about cutting drug prices. President Biden got it done.\par \par \uc2 President Biden, working across the aisle, delivering where Trump failed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/T74hmw16YP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/T74hmw16YP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ammar Moussa (@ammarmufasa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ammarmufasa/status/1650842531553320962?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The Republicans are meanwhile rolling out videos attacking Biden for various statements he\u8217\'20\'19s made in the past. Here\u8217\'20\'19s one about his stance on fossil fuels:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden promised to destroy American energy independence. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/e1usgfbVEU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/e1usgfbVEU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 RNC Research (@RNCResearch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RNCResearch/status/1650844244897087489?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 With Biden running again, Republicans ask 'what if?'\par \par \uc2 Here it is, folks, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s official word that he wants a second term in the White House:\par \par \uc2 enltrEvery generation has a moment where they have had to stand up for democracy. To stand up for their fundamental freedoms. I believe this is ours.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m running for reelection as President of the United States. Join us. Let\u8217\'20\'19s finish the job. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V9Mzpw8Sqy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/V9Mzpw8Sqy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y4NXR6B8ly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Y4NXR6B8ly}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1650801827728986112?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot in there, including the January 6 insurrection and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which come first in the video and give a sense of which issues he thinks Americans care most about, as well as \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , the supreme court justice he appointed who is also the first Black woman on the court, and even his old boss Barack Obama, who you can glimpse for a split second.\par \par \uc2 In response, the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  has prepared a post-apocalyptic-style video that Axios reports is AI generated. It asks viewers to ponder \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat if\u8221\'20\'1D Biden remains president while various crises break out:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/axios?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Axios}}}\uc2  w/ a first look at \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s video response to Biden\par \par \uc2 It is also the committee\u8217\'20\'19s first video that is 100% generated by AI software meant to create images that look and feel real (in this case an imagined dystopia look at the future of Biden wins)\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S9qH0MXINc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S9qH0MXINc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Thompson (@AlexThomp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexThomp/status/1650817703584645122?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 25, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a lengthy statement in response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s renewed candidacy, which starts with these lines: \u8220\'20\'1CYou could take the five worst presidents in American history, and put them together, and they would not have done the damage \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done to our Nation in just a few short years. Not even close.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the rest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://djt.nucleusemail.com/amplify/v/aSjYdKj3gN?hids=63BUw4b&utm_medium=email&utm_source=ncl_amplify&utm_campaign=230424-statement_from_president_donald_j_trump_on_joe_bidens_announcement&utm_content=ncl-nY5jWsBbpH&_nlid=nY5jWsBbpH&_nhids=63BUw4b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden formally announces run for second term\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced his campaign for a second term as president with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1650801827728986112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video address released this morning}}}\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s a big decision by the 80-year-old, who has been dogged by low approval ratings throughout most of his term thus far, but managed to get several major pieces of legislation passed by Congress and help Democrats defend a surprising number of seats in last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 There will be lots to say about this announcement, which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/24/first-lady-signals-joe-biden-president-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not at all a surprise}}}\uc2 , but here\u8217\'20\'19s one takeaway: with Biden facing no serious primary contenders and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back on the campaign trail and well ahead in the polls among Republicans, presidential ballots in 2024 could look a lot like they did in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we expect to happen today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8217\'20\'19s first speech since announcing his bid for a second term is at 12.30pm ET in Washington, where he\u8217\'20\'19s set to talk about manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  briefs reporters at 2pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The trial of author E Jean Carroll \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/who-is-e-jean-carroll-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defamation suit against }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/25/who-is-e-jean-carroll-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  begins in New York at 9.30am.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230425ej4p001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
