\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republican Graham loses cool over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after supreme court pill ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 932 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2023\par 10:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senator deflects questions with false claim Democrats want a \u8216\'20\'18barbaric\u8217\'20\'19 law allowing abortions on demand until birth\par \par \uc2 Republican frustration with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-latest-news-supreme-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court decision}}}\uc2  which on Friday blocked restrictions on a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill spilled into public on Sunday, as the South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  lost his cool in a television interview when challenged on his flip-flopping position.\par \par \uc2 Graham, who last September {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed a national 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  only a month after insisting it was an issue for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/remember-when-lindsey-graham-said-abortion-should-be-left-to-the-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states to decide}}}\uc2 , became angry on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, deflecting questions with false claims Democrats wanted a law allowing abortions until birth on demand.\par \par \uc2 The flustered senator accused his interviewer, Dana Bash, of covering for opponents he said wanted to see \u8220\'20\'1Cbarbaric\u8221\'20\'1D late-term abortions \u8220\'20\'1Cout of line with the rest of the civilised world\u8221\'20\'1D and commonplace, he said, only in China and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo, no, no, you [in the] media keep covering for these guys,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham shouted. \u8220\'20\'1CThey introduced legislation that allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand with taxpayer funds to the moment of birth, that\u8217\'20\'19s the law they want to pass and nobody in your business will talk about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bash replied she was covering for nobody and had frequently challenged Democrats on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  blows up when CNN's Dana Bash checks his false on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and says, "Just for the record, Roe went up to viability." Graham responded by yelling about the media covering for the Democrats' position, which isn't the Democratic position. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EX9FxapmEh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EX9FxapmEh}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Reese Jones (@PoliticusSarah) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PoliticusSarah/status/1650132290847088640?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 23, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The official position of the Democratic party is to codify federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , guaranteed by the Roe v Wade decision of 1973 until {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned by the supreme court last year}}}\uc2 , that permitted the procedure until \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal viability\u8221\'20\'1D, generally accepted to be at about 24 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation.\par \par \uc2 The spectacle of Graham\u8217\'20\'19s anger underscored how Republicans are struggling to find a cohesive response to Friday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-supreme-court-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill mifepristone}}}\uc2  and on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts and party members believe the issue cost votes in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, following the supreme court Dobbs v Jackson ruling that overturned Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Moves by several Republican-led states to tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, including the signing by the Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nation\u8217\'20\'19s most extreme ban}}}\uc2 , at six weeks, have prompted voter backlash. Polling shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/01/22/1150628013/roe-v-wade-50-years-dobbs-ipsos-poll-abortion-legal-public-opinion-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three in five Americans approve of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  access in most or all cases.\par \par \uc2 On ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week, the South Carolina Republican congresswoman Nancy Mace said the court was right to block restrictions last month placed on mifepristone by a Texas judge appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a hand-picked case with a hand-picked judge to get this outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when you look at the ruling in Texas, in part at least, it used a law that the supreme court in 1983 said was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the basis for his ruling, I argue, was debunked and it should not have been.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mace, who has spoken of being raped as a teenager, said the approach of her party to the wider issue was too rigid, and colleagues needed to show more sympathy and compassion for victims of rape who found it difficult or impossible to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want us to find some middle ground,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a Republican and conservative, a constitutional conservative who\u8217\'20\'19s pro-life, I saw what happened after Roe v Wade [fell] \u8230\'20\'26 I saw the sentiment change dramatically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Republicans, we need to read the room because the vast majority of folks are not in the extremes. We just saw a fetal heartbeat bill signed in the dead of night in Florida. In my home state a very small group of state legislators filed a bill that would execute women who have abortions and gave more rights to rapists than women who have been raped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is the wrong message heading into 2024. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to lose huge if we continue down this path of extremities. It hurt us in the midterms. We actually lost seats. We\u8217\'20\'19ve buried our heads in the sand. We want to go to the extreme corners of this issue, but that\u8217\'20\'19s not where the vast majority of Americans are right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amy Klobuchar, a Democratic senator for Minnesota and a leading voice for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, also hailed the mifepristone decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Graham knows where the American people are on this,\u8221\'20\'1D she told CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are with Democratic leaders, and the people of this country believe that the women of this country should be able to make their own decisions about their healthcare and not politicians.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar also attacked the legal arguments advanced by those seeking to ban mifepristone, which in part relied on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/what-does-comstock-act-a-law-from-the-1870s-have-to-do-with-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 150-year-old Comstock Act}}}\uc2  prohibiting the mailing of contraceptives, \u8220\'20\'1Clewd\u8221\'20\'1D writings and any \u8220\'20\'1Cinstrument, substance, drug, medicine, or thing\u8221\'20\'1D that could be used in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The law has not been enforced since the 1930s, according to NPR.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was literally passed in 1873,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is 10 years before the Yellowstone prequel, at a time when we were treated for pneumonia through bloodletting, back in the age of the Pony Express.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people do not want to go backwards. And what I heard today is that Republican leaders in Washington aren\u8217\'20\'19t backing down on their opposition to reproductive freedom. They are doubling down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230423ej4n001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
