\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  will enter presidential race \u8216\'20\'18well before late June\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 if he does at all\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 829 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2023\par 21:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former vice-president, adrift of Trump and DeSantis in polls, makes less-than-bold presidential prediction to \uc2 CBS\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has not decided whether to enter the Republican presidential primary but if he does he will enter \u8220\'20\'1Cwell before late June\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former congressman, Indiana governor and vice-president to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been moving towards a run for months, releasing a memoir, visiting early voting states and establishing a political staff.\par \par \uc2 He made his less-than-bold prediction in an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FaceTheNation/status/1649881713596612609"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with CBS Face the Nation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think if we have an announcement to make, it\u8217\'20\'19ll be well before late June,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CAnyone that would be serious about seeking the Republican nomination would need to be in this contest by June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we have an announcement to make it will be well before then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence must perform a balancing act, distancing himself from Trump, the rival candidate whose supporters chanted for Pence to be hanged when they attacked the US Capitol, while trumpeting their achievements together in office.\par \par \uc2 It seems a doomed effort in a party and primary dominated by Trump, particularly as Pence recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/mike-pence-testify-justice-department-grand-jury"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped}}}\uc2  attempts to avoid testifying in the justice department investigation of the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 In March, in perhaps his boldest break from Trump, Pence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/12/mike-pence-donald-trump-was-wrong-history-will-hold-him-accountable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told a Washington dinner}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump was wrong. I had no right to overturn the election, and his reckless words endangered my family and everyone at the Capitol that day, and I know that history will hold \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  accountable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 CBS\uc2 , asked if he was \u8220\'20\'1Cleaning in or leaning away\u8221\'20\'1D, Pence said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I\u8217\'20\'19m here in Iowa.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His interviewer, Robert Costa, said: \u8220\'20\'1CSounds like you\u8217\'20\'19re leaning in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence said: \u8220\'20\'1CI would tell you that I\u8217\'20\'19m very humbled by the encouragement that we\u8217\'20\'19re receiving. And I promise when we have something to announce, you\u8217\'20\'19ll be among the first to know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence spoke on Saturday at an event in Clive, Iowa, staged by the Faith & Freedom Coalition, a rightwing nonprofit.\par \par \uc2 Trump also addressed the event. Responding to a recent rebuke from a leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-abortion-2024-president-81373a7c8523db24f928d713ff90aa31"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  his opposition to a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally indefensible\u8221\'20\'1D, the former president highlighted the decision by which a supreme court including three justices he named removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose justices delivered a landmark victory for protecting innocent life,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, in a speech delivered by video. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody thought it was going to happen. They thought it would be another 50 years. Because Republicans had been trying to do it for exactly that period of time, 50 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Roe v Wade decision which protected the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in 1973 \u8211\'20\'13 49 years before it was overturned by Dobbs v Jackson.\par \par \uc2 The Iowa caucuses will kick off the Republican primary in February. Ten months out, Trump enjoys clear leads in polling.\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has maintained a hold on second place without declaring a run.\par \par \uc2 But DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s numbers are tanking. The governor faces his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2023/apr/23/disney-v-desantis-diversity-lgbtq-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 difficulties at state level}}}\uc2  while Trump surfs a wave of support generated by his criminal indictment in New York, over a hush money payment to an adult film star, and other forms of legal jeopardy including a civil rape trial due to open next week.\par \par \uc2 Trump denies wrongdoing and claims to be the victim of Democratic witch-hunts: a potent combination for attracting donations and support. On Sunday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/nbc-news-poll-nearly-70-gop-voters-stand-trump-indictment-investigatio-rcna80917"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an NBC poll}}}\uc2  said 68% of Republican voters thought Trump was the victim of politically motivated attacks and it was important to support him.\par \par \uc2 Pence is contesting third place with Nikki Haley, the former South Carolina governor who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/09/nikki-haley-presidential-run-ron-desantis-donald-trump-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  her run in February. Both are at around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2024/president/us/2024_republican_presidential_nomination-7548.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 4% support}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The other mainstream Republican to have declared, former Arkansas governor \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , struggles to break 1%. The South Carolina senator Tim Scott has all but declared a run but remains all but invisible in polling.\par \par \uc2 Polls do not provide uniformly good news for Trump. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/trumps-legal-issues-have-little-impact-on-his-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll this week}}}\uc2  from the Associated Press and the \uc2 University of Chicago\uc2  said 44% of Republicans (and 70% of Americans) do not want him to be the nominee.\par \par \uc2 The Dispatch, a conservative anti-Trump site, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thedispatch.com/article/mike-pence-plots-his-presidential-bid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Pence was planning a launch in Indiana, followed by another trip to Iowa.\par \par \uc2 Pence, the site said, \u8220\'20\'1Cplans to campaign as the traditional conservative he is, eschewing momentary cultural flashpoints that inflame passions and attract eyeballs \u8230\'20\'26 [to] instead focus on wonky topics fraught with political peril, like how to address the ballooning federal debt and reforming popular programs like Social Security and Medicare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Pence is eager to highlight his opposition \u8211\'20\'13 and his commitment to signing federal legislation limiting the procedure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such positions have proved unpopular with general election voters. The Dispatch also said Pence planned to \u8220\'20\'1Caim fire directly at\u8221\'20\'1D Trump.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230423ej4n00130\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
