\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Democratic states stockpile  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pills as legal fight for access looms\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 908 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 April 2023\par 16:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has preserved access to mifepristone for now, but blue states announce plans to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Despite a reprieve by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , a growing number of Democratic states are stockpiling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills as the legal fight for access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone is set to continue.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the supreme court decided to temporarily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-latest-news-supreme-court-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 block}}}\uc2  a lower court ruling that would have significantly restricted the availability of mifepristone, an \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, as the case continues to wind through America\u8217\'20\'19s court system and remains challenged by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, more Democratic states are now stockpiling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills amid an unpredictable legal battle.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Matthew Kacsmaryk, a Trump-appointed federal judge in Texas issued a preliminary injunction that suspended the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-supreme-court-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  it a drug that is used to \u8220\'20\'1Ckill the unborn human\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Swiftly after Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, Democratic states have been stockpiling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills including mifepristone as well as misoprostol, the second drug in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen which can also be used on its own, although less effectively.\par \par \uc2 At the Massachusetts governor \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request, the \uc2 University of Massachusetts Amherst\uc2  has purchased approximately 15,000 doses of mifepristone. The stockpile is expected to offer \u8220\'20\'1Csufficient coverage\u8221\'20\'1D in the state for over a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMifepristone has been used safely for more than 20 years and is the gold standard. Here in Massachusetts, we are not going to let one extremist judge in Texas turn back the clock on this proven medication and restrict access to care in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Healey {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mass.gov/news/governor-healey-announces-immediate-action-to-protect-access-to-medication-abortion-in-massachusetts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Democratic governors of New York and California both announced plans to stockpile misoprostol in attempts to safeguard their states\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  announced last week that New York will be purchasing misoprostol in order to stockpile 150,000 doses, a five-year supply.\par \par \uc2 Hochul also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.ny.gov/news/governor-hochul-announces-actions-protect-access-medication-abortion-new-york-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledged}}}\uc2  that if mifepristone is removed from the market, New York will commit up to an additional $20m to providers to support other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  methods.\par \par \uc2 In a similar move, governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California announced last week that the state has secured an emergency stockpile of up to 2m misoprostol pills\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not cave to extremists who are trying to outlaw these critical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal in California,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2023/04/10/california-announces-emergency-stockpile-of-abortion-medication-defending-against-extreme-texas-court-ruling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , adding that California has shared the negotiated terms of its misoprostol purchase agreement to assist other states in securing the pill at low cost.\par \par \uc2 Since then, additional Democratic states have followed suit.\par \par \uc2 The governor of Maryland, Wes Moore, recently announced a partnership with the University of Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s medical system to purchase a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial amount of mifepristone\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis purchase is another example of our administration\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to ensure Maryland remains a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and quality reproductive health care,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.maryland.gov/press/pages/ICYMI-Governor-Moore-Announced-Plan-in-Partnership-with-UMMS-to-Ensure-Access-to-Mifepristone-in-Maryland.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Moore, who also released $3.5m in previously withheld funding for the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care clinical training program.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Oregon made a similar announcement, with its governor \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  revealing the state has secured a three-year supply of mifepristone, regardless of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling on the pill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere in Oregon, I will make sure that patients are able to access the medication they need and providers are able to provide that medication without unnecessary, politically motivated interference and intimidation,\u8221\'20\'1D Kotek {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oregon.gov/newsroom/pages/NewsDetail.aspx?newsid=87939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With Democratic states rushing to stock up on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, the tumultuous legal fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is far from over. In the last nine months, 13 states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-supreme-court-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups fighting for increased pill restrictions nationwide, even states that have legalized the procedure may become affected.\par \par \uc2 Following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to temporarily block mifepristone restrictions, the next stage of the litigious battle over the drug will take place in the fifth circuit, with oral arguments scheduled for 17 May. The case will then likely return back to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , Erik Baptist, a senior counsel for the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a conservative legal organization representing a coalition of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and doctors, pledged to continue fighting against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FDA\uc2  must answer for the damage it has caused to the health of countless women and girls and the rule of law by failing to study how dangerous the chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug regimen is and unlawfully removing every meaningful safeguard, even allowing for mail-order abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/21/us/politics/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  about the 23-year-old \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drug.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Joe Biden administration and civil rights organizations promised to continue fighting for reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to fight attacks on women\u8217\'20\'19s health. The American people must also continue to use their vote as their voice and elect a Congress that will restore the protections of Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1649557289672617984?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  shortly after the supreme court issued its decision.\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  echoed similar sentiments, with Jennifer Dalven, \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Freedom Project director {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/press-releases/aclu-comment-on-stay-issued-by-supreme-court-in-medication-abortion-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake, we aren\u8217\'20\'19t out of the woods by any means \u8230\'20\'26 And as this baseless lawsuit shows, extremists will use every trick in the book to try to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dalven added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut if our opponents think we will allow them to continue to pursue their extreme goals without fierce backlash, they are sorely mistaken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230422ej4m001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
