\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  expected to rule on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access lawsuit \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,232 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justices consider appeal by White House following lower court order reimposing restrictions on drug mifepristoneSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We continue to await {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-64428c1f8f086890899d72ab#block-64428c1f8f086890899d72ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potential supreme court action}}}\uc2  on a petition from the justice department challenging a federal appeals panel\u8217\'20\'19s reimposition of restrictions on mifepristone, a drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A stay of the appeals court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling expires today at midnight, and it\u8217\'20\'19s possible the justices will before then announce an action that restricts access to the drug, or keeps it as is. The decision could arrive at any time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442d2cb8f08155e59b76476#block-6442d2cb8f08155e59b76476"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as soon as next Tuesday}}}\uc2  officially announce plans to run for a second term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442ab1b8f08155e59b76213#block-6442ab1b8f08155e59b76213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sitting for an interview}}}\uc2  with special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors for the second day in a row.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be charged}}}\uc2  with four federal crimes, some of which are felonies, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans love Trump and Democrats are willing to put up with Biden: Those are the conclusions from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442b24b8f08155e59b76277#block-6442b24b8f08155e59b76277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a pair}}}\uc2  of new public opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who had the worst week in Washington? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442dea28f087731d3ccb47a#block-6442dea28f087731d3ccb47a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It might be}}}\uc2  Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 At today\u8217\'20\'19s White House press briefing, reporters tried their best to get the president\u8217\'20\'19s spokeswoman \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  to confirm that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would run for a second term.\par \par \uc2 They did not succeed, but ABC News made a particularly clever attempt that\u8217\'20\'19s worth watching:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marykbruce?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @marykbruce}}}\uc2  : "Does the President have any plans to mark the fourth anniversary of his announcement of his 2020 campaign?" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  : "That's very good...I don't have anything else beyond the week ahead that I just laid out, but I really appreciate the effort. That was very good" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wkvp2iVIlR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wkvp2iVIlR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Molly Nagle (@MollyNagle3) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MollyNagle3/status/1649495986639720479?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another showdown between Democratic and Republican state lawmakers is brewing in Montana, where the GOP leader of the house of representative is refusing to allow a transgender lawmaker to speak on the floor.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/transgender-lawmaker-silenced-montana-censure-ee3e30ee6a1cd7c0faa8fd072d580a94?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_04"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press has}}}\uc2  the latest on that:\par \par \uc2 Montana\u8217\'20\'19s house speaker on Thursday refused to allow a transgender lawmaker to speak about bills on the House floor until she apologizes for saying lawmakers would have \u8220\'20\'1Cblood on their hands\u8221\'20\'1D if they supported a bill to ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/science-health-mental-ce8f5a9ee53768af03c3c65d5331045b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender-affirming medical care}}}\uc2  for transgender youth, the lawmaker said.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Zooey Zephyr, who was deliberately referred to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/transgender-minor-health-montana-misgender-censure-e3b82e5fa4b21aba0611200ab5efd4a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 using male pronouns}}}\uc2  by some conservative lawmakers demanding her censure, said she will not apologize, creating a standoff between the first-term state lawmaker and Republican legislative leaders.\par \par \uc2 Speaker Matt Regier refused to acknowledge Zephyr on Thursday when she wanted to comment on a bill seeking to put a binary definition of male and female into state code.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is up to me to maintain decorum here on the House floor, to protect the dignity and integrity,\u8221\'20\'1D Regier said Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd any representative that I don\u8217\'20\'19t feel can do that will not be recognized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Regier said the decision came after \u8220\'20\'1Cmultiple discussions\u8221\'20\'1D with other lawmakers and that previously there have been similar problems.\par \par \uc2 Democrats objected to Regier\u8217\'20\'19s decision, but the House Rules committee and the House upheld his decision on party-line votes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHate-filled testimony has no place on the House floor,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican Rep. Caleb Hinkle, a member of the Montana Freedom Caucus that demanded the censure, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Zephyr said she stands by what she said about the consequences of banning essential medical care for transgender youth.\par \par \uc2 The bill would ban transgender minors in Montana from receiving puberty blockers, cross-sex hormones or surgical procedures. Those are treatments for gender dysphoria, the clinically significant distress caused by feeling that one\u8217\'20\'19s gender identity does not match one\u8217\'20\'19s biological sex. Medical professionals who provided such care would lose their medical licenses for at least a year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 If it seems like it\u8217\'20\'19s been a rough few days for \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s because it has.\par \par \uc2 The Florida governor keeps getting outmaneuvered by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has managed to keep up a steady flow of Republican endorsements for his presidential campaign \u8211\'20\'13 including from one lawmaker who did so {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/ron-desantis-ally-backs-trump-latest-florida-defection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right after a meeting with DeSantis}}}\uc2 . The governor has reportedly gone as far as to ask his state\u8217\'20\'19s congressmen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/desantis-florida-stop-endorsing-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to cut it out}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It got even worse for DeSantis this morning, when Politico published its daily Playbook, one of the most-read newsletters in Washington. In today\u8217\'20\'19s edition, they report that a former Republican lawmaker who served on the House foreign affairs committee with DeSantis during his time as a congressman called them up to offer his thoughts about the now-governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s an asshole,\u8221\'20\'1D David Trott said.\par \par \uc2 There you have it. You can read the rest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/04/21/how-to-lose-friends-and-alienate-people-by-ron-desantis-00093235?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 When he\u8217\'20\'19s not railing against the media, Democrats or other perceived enemies, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has recently channelled a lot of his vitriol towards Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is expected to soon announce a campaign for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 But now, a Trump-aligned Republican House representative from the state has joined in on the criticism. Citing an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/20/florida-republicans-desantis-campaign-00092994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 article from Politico}}}\uc2  that says Florida\u8217\'20\'19s state lawmakers have grown tired of passing legislation they view as little more than props for DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign, \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2  called on them to stand up to the governor. Here are the tweets:\par \par \uc2 enltrSad to see the Florida House and Senate, two bodies I had the honor to serve in, carrying the water for an unannounced presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2  (@gregsteube) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gregsteube/status/1649478744816361480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTo my fellow elected officials serving in Tallahassee, your constituents voted you into those positions to represent them, not to kowtow to the presidential ambitions of a Governor! Be strong and courageous, the people of Florida will thank you. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WP7kcjHCbO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WP7kcjHCbO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2  (@gregsteube) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gregsteube/status/1649478746758324244?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden may announce re-election campaign next week: report\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to run for a second term as president has been the worst-kept secret in Washington for months, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports, Biden is reportedly planning to soon put an end to the speculation with a formal announcement:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is preparing to announce his bid for re-election as soon as Tuesday, the anniversary of the launch of the 2020 campaign that put him in the White House, multiple news outlets reported.\par \par \uc2 The president has long and clearly signalled that he intends to seek re-election. Last week, he said he would launch his campaign \u8220\'20\'1Crelatively soon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But as he is the oldest president ever inaugurated, and will be 82 on inauguration day in 2025 and 86 by the end of a second term, questions have persisted about his hunger and fitness to run.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have sought to make an issue of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age, despite the clear leader in the GOP presidential primary, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , being only four years younger.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/biden-may-announce-2024-presidential-run-next-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden reportedly preparing to announce 2024 re-election bid on Tuesday}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 More details are emerging about the motivations of the gunman in a mass shooting that took place in Louisville earlier this month, one of a wave of killings across the United States that have underscored the severity of the country\u8217\'20\'19s gun violence problem:\par \par \uc2 The family of a man who killed five people at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisville}}}\uc2  bank this month is working to destroy the AR-15 rifle he used, despite a Kentucky state law that sends firearms confiscated by law enforcement to auction and uses the proceeds to buy law enforcement equipment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Sturgeon family was aghast to learn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kentucky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky}}}\uc2  law mandated the assault rifle used in the horrific event last week be sold to the highest bidder at public auction,\u8221\'20\'1D a family statement said.\par \par \uc2 It was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/04/20/us/louisville-kentucky-bank-mass-shooting-shooter-writings/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 , meanwhile, that the gunman, 25-year-old Connor Sturgeon, left two notes before he went to the \uc2 Old National Bank\uc2  and opened fire.\par \par \uc2 According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2023/04/20/us/louisville-kentucky-bank-mass-shooting-shooter-writings/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to CNN}}}\uc2 , citing two law enforcement sources, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe notes reveal that part of the shooter\u8217\'20\'19s goal was to show how easy it was in America for someone dealing with a serious mental illness to buy an assault-style weapon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/louisville-bank-shooting-gun-auction-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Family of Louisville gunman fights law that would see weapon auctioned}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re awaiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-64428c1f8f086890899d72ab#block-64428c1f8f086890899d72ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potential supreme court action}}}\uc2  on a petition from the justice department challenging a federal appeals panel\u8217\'20\'19s reimposition of restrictions on mifepristone, a drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A stay of the appeals court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling expires today at midnight, and it\u8217\'20\'19s possible the justices will before then announce an action that restricts access to the drug, or keeps it as is. The decision could come at any time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442ab1b8f08155e59b76213#block-6442ab1b8f08155e59b76213"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sitting for an interview}}}\uc2  with special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s prosecutors for a second day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hunter Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be charged}}}\uc2  with four federal crimes, some of which are felonies, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans love Trump and Democrats are willing to put up with Biden: Those are the conclusions from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/21/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-latest-joe-biden-environment?page=with:block-6442b24b8f08155e59b76277#block-6442b24b8f08155e59b76277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a pair}}}\uc2  of new public opinion polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 A worrying, not to say roundly depressing report from the Associated Press, over what the database of mass killings it maintains with USA Today in partnership with \uc2 Northeastern University\uc2  says about the year so far\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The US is setting a record yearly pace for mass killings, with around one each week. According to a database tracking such events, the death toll from 17 mass killings in 111 days is 88. All were shot. Only 2009 saw as many such killings in the same period.\par \par \uc2 At {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Nashville elementary school}}}\uc2 , three children and three adults were killed. In northern California, farm workers died {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/24/california-shooting-half-moon-bay-suspect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over a workplace grudge}}}\uc2 . At a ballroom outside Los Angeles, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/23/monterey-park-california-shooting-victims-motive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dancers were massacred}}}\uc2  as they celebrated the Lunar New Year.\par \par \uc2 In the last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/alabama-shooting-two-arrested-dadeville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four partygoers were killed}}}\uc2  and 32 injured at a Sweet 16 party in Dadeville, Alabama. In Bowdoin, Maine, a man just released from prison {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/maine-shootings-bowdoin-highway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fatally shot four people}}}\uc2  including his parents before firing on motorists on an interstate highway.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody should be shocked,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fred Guttenberg, whose 14-year-old daughter Jaime was one of 17 people killed at a high school in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Parkland, Florida}}}\uc2 , in 2018. \u8220\'20\'1CI visit my daughter in a cemetery. Outrage doesn\u8217\'20\'19t begin to describe how I feel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read on:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/us-mass-shooting-2023-alabama-tennessee-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One mass killing every 6.53 days: US shootings are on a record pace }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would subpoena \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2 , for testimony over corruption allegations against \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , the Senate judiciary committee chair made clear his frustration with a continued absence from the panel that has left Democrats unable to make such a move.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes a majority,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  of Illinois said yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats do not have a majority because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/us-house-democrats-dianne-feinstein-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dianne Feinstein}}}\uc2  , the 89-year-old California senator, has been hospitalised with shingles. Some Democrats have called for Feinstein to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/sen-dianne-feinstein-faces-first-call-resign-member-congress-rcna79445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resign}}}\uc2 . Others have labelled such calls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/15/clinging-to-power-does-not-make-dianne-feinstein-a-feminist-hero"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexist}}}\uc2 . Feinstein has said she hopes to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/us-house-democrats-dianne-feinstein-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return}}}\uc2 . Republicans blocked a move for a temporary committee replacement.\par \par \uc2 Thomas is the senior conservative on a court tilted 6-3 to the right. This month, he has been the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/clarence-thomas-investigation-fox-news-juan-williams"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subject}}}\uc2  of bombshell reporting from \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 , about his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long relationship}}}\uc2  with and acceptance of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-real-estate-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gifts}}}\uc2  from Harlan Crow, a rightwing megadonor and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/08/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-harlan-crow-hitler-memorabilia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collector of Hitler memorabilia}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Crow\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s links to Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s wife, the rightwing activist Ginni Thomas, have also come under the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 Thomas and Crow deny wrongdoing, the justice saying he was advised he did not have to declare gifts, the donor saying he and Thomas did not discuss politics or business before the court. Observers counter that Thomas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2023/04/clarence-thomas-broke-the-law-harlan-crow.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke the law}}}\uc2 . But though supreme court justices are subject to federal ethics rules, they essentially govern themselves.\par \par \uc2 Durbin invited Roberts to testify on 2 May. He also said Roberts could send another justice in his place, pointing to testimony by \uc2 Antonin Scalia\uc2  and \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Durbin said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been no discussion of subpoenas for anyone at this point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans opposed the request. But there is pressure on Democrats to act over what \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  of Maryland has called the \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D way in which \u8220\'20\'1Cthe supreme court has exempted itself from the accountability that applies to all other members of our federal courts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Richard Blumenthal of Connecticut has suggested Thomas and Crow should be the ones receiving subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/dianne-feinstein-supreme-court-clarence-thomas-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Feinstein absence blocks push for supreme court chief Thomas testimony}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 More on Matthew Kacsmaryk, the judge whose mifepristone ruling set us barreling down the track to today\u8217\'20\'19s expected supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lucaskuncemo/status/1649075829932949505?s=46&t=-Kf0FhfLJs6Ix5i_RLjQAQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted}}}\uc2  by Lucas Kunce, a Democratic US Senate hopeful in Missouri, in 2018 Kacsmaryk made his first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/individual-contributions/?contributor_name=Kacsmaryk%2C+Matthew&max_date=12%2F31%2F2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political donation}}}\uc2  in three years: $500 to the Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , after Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to a federal judgeship in Texas by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but before his confirmation by the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing wrong with that, as Carl Tobias, a law professor at the \uc2 University of Richmond\uc2  in Virginia, explains: \u8220\'20\'1CA federal judge can\u8217\'20\'19t [make donations] under \uc2 Canon\uc2  5 of the Code of Conduct for Federal Judges, but a federal judicial nominee can contribute as nominees have a first-amendment right to support a political candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is arcane, but makes sense, as federal judges must at least appear to be impartial, because we trust them to be fair in dispensing justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the donation \u8211\'20\'13 which appears in \uc2 Federal Election Commission{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/individual-contributions/?contributor_name=Kacsmaryk%2C+Matthew&max_date=12%2F31%2F2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 records}}}\uc2 , alongside previous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/individual-contributions/?contributor_name=Kacsmaryk%2C+Matthew&max_date=12%2F31%2F2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donations}}}\uc2  to other Republicans including Ted Cruz and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , the last before the Hawley donation coming in 2015 \u8211\'20\'13 does point to Hawley\u8217\'20\'19s close connection to the mifepristone case.\par \par \uc2 The senator\u8217\'20\'19s wife, \uc2 Erin Morrow Hawley\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/03/erin-josh-hawley-abortion-medication-texas-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a lead lawyer presenting arguments}}}\uc2  for the banning of mifepristone before Kacsmaryk in Texas.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/03/erin-josh-hawley-abortion-medication-texas-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  by Vanity Fair: \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that the wife of a senator is involved in a high-profile lawsuit is not necessarily noteworthy on its face.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Kunce charges: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what corruption looks like \u8230\'20\'26 senators shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be in the business of using their position to benefit their family\u8217\'20\'19s legal careers and activism, especially if there is financial incentive to do so. And there shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even be a hint of campaign donations impacting who, when, and how a judge gets on a court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our columnist Lloyd Green considers the current plight of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican Florida governor with big plans for a presidential run but who has seen his poll numbers plunge in the face of an onslaught from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The DeSantis boomlet is done. He consistently trails Trump by double-digits. A Wall Street Journal poll out Friday pegs Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor in severe retrograde, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-tops-ron-desantis-in-test-of-gop-presidential-field-wsj-poll-finds-88c84663?st=gzhpc1oa9hfmqkc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slipping 27 points since December}}}\uc2 . DeSantis mistakenly conflates his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s bulging war chest with adulation. Wrong!\par \par \uc2 He forgot that working-class Americans dominate the Republican party and that mien matters. Voting to gut social security comes with fatal backlash, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/03/ron-desantis-chocolate-pudding-denial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eating pudding with your fingers}}}\uc2  is gross. Said differently, largesse from the party\u8217\'20\'19s donor base coupled with little else is a losing recipe.\par \par \uc2 Charles Koch\uc2  has but a single vote and \uc2 David Koch\uc2  is gone. Before he goes any further, DeSantis needs to be reminded of past campaign flame-outs \u8211\'20\'13 Jeb Bush, John Connally and \uc2 Mike Bloomberg\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 if he is to avoid their inglorious endings.\par \par \uc2 Read on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/21/ron-desantis-donald-trump-republican-nomination-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis is flaming out \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump is on course for a Republican coronation | Lloyd Green}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , two polls were released today concerning the men that tell us \u8230\'20\'26 not much new.\par \par \uc2 The first, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-tops-ron-desantis-in-test-of-gop-presidential-field-wsj-poll-finds-88c84663?st=gzhpc1oa9hfmqkc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 , confirms that Trump remains the most popular figure among contenders for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination in 2024. The WSJ was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the few surveys}}}\uc2  that found Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who has not entered the race yet but is widely expected to, with an edge over Trump in a survey released last December. That trend has now reversed: in a hypothetical head-to-head matchup, Trump gets 51% support, and DeSantis 38%. The former president also beats DeSantis even in a poll that includes other potential Republican candidates \u8211\'20\'13 none of whom crack double-digit support.\par \par \uc2 As for Biden, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-poll-2024-white-house-economy-873663f6e3cbca8f2dae2f018c8be9d3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research survey}}}\uc2  released today finds the president is not particularly popular among Democrats, but they will support him anyway. It\u8217\'20\'19s probably a wise choice for voters if they want to keep the White House in Democratic hands, considering Biden has no serious primary challengers.\par \par \uc2 The poll finds 26% of Americans and 47% of Democrats want to see Biden stand for a second term. Those aren\u8217\'20\'19t great numbers, but at least the president has the support of his party \u8211\'20\'13 81% of Democrats would probably or definitely support Biden if he is the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/09/trump-indictment-women-stormy-daniels-karen-mcdougal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plenty of legal peril}}}\uc2 , but his Republican defenders may soon receive more ammunition for their counterattack against his rival \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 : criminal charges against his son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GOP lawmakers have for years alleged \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is involved in criminal activity, but a federal investigation into his business conduct has yet to produce charges. That could change, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/federal-prosecutors-hunter-biden-taxes-gun-charge-rcna80692"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 . Prosecutors in Delaware are eyeing four criminal charges against him related to lying on a gun purchase background check and tax evasion. They also report \u8220\'20\'1Cgrowing frustration\u8221\'20\'1D that charges have not been brought yet.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that from NBC:\par \par \uc2 The possible charges are two misdemeanor counts for failure to file taxes, a single felony count of tax evasion related to a business expense for one year of taxes, and the gun charge, also a potential felony.\par \par \uc2 Two senior law enforcement sources told NBC News about \u8220\'20\'1Cgrowing frustration\u8221\'20\'1D inside the \uc2 FBI\uc2  because investigators finished the bulk of their work on the case about a year ago. A senior law enforcement source said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/irs-agent-wants-whistleblower-protections-discuss-hunter-biden-probe-rcna80564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the IRS}}}\uc2  finished its investigation more than a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/10/06/hunter-biden-tax-gun-charges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2  that federal investigators believed they had gathered enough evidence to charge \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  with tax crimes and a false statement related to a gun purchase.\par \par \uc2 The decision on which charges to file, if any, will be made by U.S. Attorney David Weiss, who was appointed by President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and retained by the Biden administration to continue the Hunter Biden investigation. There are no indications a final decision has been made, said the two sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump adviser faces second day of questioning by special counsel: report\par \par \uc2 Boris Epshteyn, a top adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is being questioned for a second day by special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/top-trump-adviser-boris-epshteyn-questioned-2nd-day/story?id=98751205"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors for Smith, who has been tasked with investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to overturn the 2020 election, involvement in the January 6 insurrection and possession of classified documents, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/trump-adviser-boris-epshteyn-interview-special-counsel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to Epshteyn yesterday}}}\uc2 , and ABC says today\u8217\'20\'19s questioning was pre-arranged. Smith reportedly sat in for yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s interview, but did not ask any questions.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from ABC about what prosecutors are hoping to learn:\par \par \uc2 The interview was largely focused on the efforts by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election loss. The second day of questioning was planned in advance, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 Epshteyn did not immediately respond to a request for comment from ABC News.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 questions focused around Epshteyn\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with former Trump attorneys \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , Kenneth Chesebro and John Eastman, in addition to Trump himself, according to sources.\par \par \uc2 Smith was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/attorney-general-names-special-counsel-oversee-dojs-mar/story?id=93568451"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed in November}}}\uc2  by Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to investigate efforts to overturn the 2020 election, as well as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified information after leaving the White House.\par \par \uc2 Epshteyn was not questioned in the probe into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of classified documents, sources said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voters elsewhere have been rejecting rightwing candidates, particularly for a slew of school board seats that were voted on in April. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/adam-gabbatt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adam Gabbatt}}}\uc2  with a look at the results of the influential local elections:\par \par \uc2 Scores of rightwing US extremists were defeated in school-board elections in April, in a victory for the left and what Democrats hope could be effective for running against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in the year ahead.\par \par \uc2 In Illinois, Democrats said more than 70% of school-board candidates it had endorsed won their races, often defeating the kinds of anti-LGBTQ+ culture-warrior candidates who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/21/books-bans-gag-orders-suppress-discussion-racism-lgbtq-us-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taken control of school boards across the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican-backed candidates in Wisconsin also fared poorly. Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2 , a rightwing group linked to wealthy Republican donors which has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/24/us-conservatives-campaign-books-ban-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 behind book-banning campaigns}}}\uc2  in the US, said only eight of its endorsed candidates won election to school boards, and other conservative groups also reported disappointing performances.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/2023/apr/21/school-board-elections-illinois-wisconsin-republicans-lose"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rightwing extremists defeated by Democrats in US school board elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk sits in Texas, a state where the legislature took steps yesterday to make time for prayer in public schools, and force them to display the Ten Commandments.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2023/04/20/texas-senate-passes-ten-commandments-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 , the lawmaker behind the Ten Commandments push in the state cited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/27/supreme-court-coach-prayers-joseph-kennedy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a supreme court decision last year}}}\uc2  in which its conservative majority determined a public high school football coach should not have been removed from his job for leading prayers with players. The coach was represented by \uc2 First Liberty Institute\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where Kacsmaryk worked before becoming a federal judge.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Texas Tribune on the campaign to bring religion into the state\u8217\'20\'19s public schools:\par \par \uc2 Public schools in Texas would have to prominently display the Ten Commandments in every classroom starting next school year under a bill the Texas Senate approved Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Senate Bill 1515 by Sen. Phil King, R-Weatherford, now heads to the House for consideration.\par \par \uc2 This is the latest attempt from Texas Republicans to inject religion into public schools. In 2021, state Sen. \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2 , a Mineola Republican, authored a bill that became law requiring schools to display donated \u8220\'20\'1CIn God We Trust\u8221\'20\'1D signs.\par \par \uc2 King said during a committee hearing earlier this month that the Ten Commandments are part of American heritage and it\u8217\'20\'19s time to bring them back into the classroom. He said the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  cleared the way for his bill after it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/06/27/supreme-court-school-prayer-texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sided}}}\uc2  with \uc2 Joe Kennedy\uc2 , a high school football coach in Washington state who was fired for praying at football games. The court ruled that was praying as a private citizen, not as an employee of the district.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The bill] will remind students all across Texas of the importance of the fundamental foundation of America,\u8221\'20\'1D King said during that hearing.\par \par \uc2 The Senate also gave final passage to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=88R&Bill=SB1396"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Bill 1396}}}\uc2 , authored by Sen. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/directory/mayes-middleton/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mayes Middleton}}}\uc2 , R-Galveston, which would allow public and charter schools to adopt a policy requiring every campus to set aside a time for students and employees to read the Bible or other religious texts and to pray.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk, the Texas federal judge who earlier this month revoked the government\u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone after a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, holds some unusual views on gay rights, divorce and contraception that he did not share with the Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/20/politics/kfile-judge-kacsmaryk-disclose-interviews-nomination/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported yesterday}}}\uc2  on radio interviews in which Kacsmaryk called being gay a \u8220\'20\'1Clifestyle\u8221\'20\'1D and made comments critical of \u8220\'20\'1Cno-fault divorce\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpermissive contraception policies\u8221\'20\'1D. The interview was not included in the materials Kacsmaryk sent to the Senate judiciary committee as it considered his appointment in 2017, even though nominees typically submit exhaustive lists of public statements to lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s views, from CNN:\par \par \uc2 enltrMatthew Kacsmaryk, the judge who issued the ban on mifepristone, failed to disclose two 2014 interviews on Christian talk radio during his confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 In the interviews, he blames "no-fault divorce" and \u8220\'20\'1Cpermissive contraception policies\u8221\'20\'1D for the "sexual revolution." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/shxbi8D3rj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/shxbi8D3rj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1649175195603857410?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is facing mounting scrutiny over its approach to ethics after revelations emerged of unreported ties between conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and a Republican megadonor. The Senate judiciary chair wants chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to make a rare appearance before his committee, but as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports, the absence of a key Democratic senator could complicate that:\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would subpoena the chief justice of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  for testimony over corruption allegations against the conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , the chair of the Senate judiciary committee made clear his frustration with a continued absence from the panel that has left Democrats unable to make such a move.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes a majority,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  of Illinois said on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have a majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats do not have a committee majority because of the absence of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/us-house-democrats-dianne-feinstein-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dianne Feinstein}}}\uc2 , the 89-year-old California senator who has been hospitalised with shingles.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/21/dianne-feinstein-supreme-court-clarence-thomas-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Feinstein absence blocks push for supreme court chief Thomas testimony}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  with more on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case the supreme court is considering today:\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to rule on Friday on whether to allow restrictions on mifepristone to go into effect while a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups targeting the pill proceeds.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  extended an administrative stay on a lower court ruling that reimposes pre-2016 restrictions on the drug. Access to the drug remains unchanged while the supreme court deliberates.\par \par \uc2 An order upholding lower court rulings in favor of limiting the drug would drastically curtail access to the most common method of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, with consequences for miscarriage care, as well.\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court allows the lower court rulings to stand, this will have huge implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and miscarriage care nationally, even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal. Considering more than half of abortions in the US are completed using pills, it could mean the biggest blow to reproductive rights since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was overturned.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-texas-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill ruling: will the US supreme court hear another \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Four directions the supreme court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill case could take\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s possible that today ends with a supreme court decision allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone to stay available at pharmacies nationwide. Or, the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority could again display its willingness to throttle reproductive care access and allow an appeals court decision reimposing restrictions on the drug to go into effect.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at four ways the ruling on the mifepristone case could go, from Steve Vladeck of the University of Texas School of Law:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere we go again:\par \par \uc2 Four possible {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/mifepristone?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #mifepristone}}}\uc2  rulings from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  today:\par \par \uc2 1) Grant stay pending appeal;\par \par \uc2 2) Deny stay pending appeal;\par \par \uc2 3) Weird mixed ruling; or\par \par \uc2 4) No ruling.\par \par \uc2 (1) means no change to mifepristone access anytime soon; (2)-(4) mean big changes starting Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1649386448619970560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s also *possible* that Justice Alito extends the administrative stay *again* (what happened on Wednesday), but that seems exceedingly unlikely.\par \par \uc2 One way or the other, I expect that we get something from the full Court today\u8212\'20\'14although *when* and *what* is anyone\u8217\'20\'19s guess.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1649386956252663809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 And a reminder of how this complex case reached this point, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge in Texas, declared that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  improperly approved the drug in 2000, in effect saying it should be pulled from the market even where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration appealed to a federal court, where a divided three-judge panel said mifepristone could remain available but imposed several barriers to how the drug is accessed and administered.\par \par \uc2 Following the appellate ruling, the justice department sought emergency relief from the supreme court, asking the justices to block a lower court ruling that would have sharply curtailed access to the pill by reversing a series of regulatory actions on mifepristone that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  loosened, beginning in 2016.\par \par \uc2 The pause gives the justices additional time to study arguments and consider the restrictions ordered by the lower court, which include limiting mifepristone use after seven weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 it is currently approved through 10 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and banning delivery by mail.\par \par \uc2 If the justices allow the appeals court ruling to stand, the Biden administration has argued, it would dramatically limit the accessibility of mifepristone for both women seeking it and providers dispensing it, causing chaos.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/19/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court delays decision on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill restrictions until Friday}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court expected to act today on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill lawsuit\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The supreme court could again wade into the debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access today, as it considers an appeal by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/19/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent court order}}}\uc2  reimposing restrictions on the drug mifepristone. The case stems from a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups seeking to revoke the government\u8217\'20\'19s approval of the drug, which is used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The high court remains dominated by conservatives who less than a year ago overturned Roe v Wade and ended nationwide access to the procedure. A stay on the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling expires at midnight today, and the justices are expected to announce which way they will rule in this case sometime before then.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will announce new actions to advance environmental justice in a speech at 2.15pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is heading to Florida, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll give a televised interview to Telemundo and speak about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to help communities survive extreme weather.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters at 1pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230421ej4l0020m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
