\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to decide on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access after extending deadline\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 791 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2023\par 16:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Legal challenge to \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone could have implications for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health across the country\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is poised to decide whether to preserve access to a widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication, after extending its deadline to act until at least Friday.\par \par \uc2 Less than a year after the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority overturned Roe v Wade and eliminated a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the justices are now reviewing new legal questions raised by an escalating case in Texas with potentially sweeping implications for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health and the federal drug approval process.\par \par \uc2 For now, the court is not weighing the merits of a legal challenge brought by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents seeking to suspend the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 23-year-old approval of mifepristone. At issue before the court is whether to allow restrictions on the drug imposed by a lower court that would sharply limit access to the drug, including in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 The court had initially set a deadline of 11.59pm on Wednesday, but that afternoon, Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issued a brief order extending its stay by up to 48 hours. The one-sentence order provided no explanation for the delay but indicated the court expects to act before midnight on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The legal controversy erupted in Texas, where US district judge Matthew Kacsmaryk issued a ruling earlier this month that would revoke the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, a drug first approved more than two decades ago and used by more than 5 million women \u8211\'20\'13 in combination with a second pill, misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 to terminate their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration immediately appealed the order, which it assailed as an unprecedented attack on the the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision-making. The US court of appeals for the fifth circuit then temporarily blocked the Texas decision, declining to suspend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone while the legal case plays out. But, in a partial victory for the challengers, it reinstated regulatory barriers taken by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  since 2016 that loosened restrictions on the pill.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court has scheduled oral arguments in the case on 17 May.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration and drugmakers next asked the supreme court to pause the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, arguing that reimposing the barriers would create chaos in the marketplace and cause confusion for providers and patients.\par \par \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , a coalition of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors and organizations, has argued that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  failed to follow proper protocols and adequately assess safety concerns when it approved mifepristone for use in 2000 and in the regulatory actions it has taken since. Medical experts have said the claims are dubious and ignore decades of research and data from hundreds of medical studies showing mifepristone is both a safe and an effective way to end a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The challengers filed their lawsuit in Amarillo, where Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former attorney at Christian law group}}}\uc2  with long-held conservative views on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gender and reproductive rights}}}\uc2 , is the only sitting judge.\par \par \uc2 Complicating the legal landscape, on the same day that Kacsmaryk ruled, a federal judge in Washington state, Thomas Rice, issued a contradictory order in a separate lawsuit brought by Democratic attorneys general in 17 states and the District of Columbia. The decision, which Rice reaffirmed after the appeals ruling in the Texas case, blocked the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from limiting the availability of mifepristone in those states.\par \par \uc2 Since the fall of Roe, more than a dozen US states have banned or severely restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But many other states have moved in the opposite direction, passing legislation and approving ballot initiatives that protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Amid the patchwork legal landscape, attention has turned to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which can be obtained by mail and administered at home.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is the first pill in a two-drug regimen that is the most common method of ending a pregnancy, accounting for more than half of all abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 The drug first won \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval in 2000, and over the years the agency has loosened restrictions on its use. Those changes include allowing the drug\u8217\'20\'19s use from seven to 10 weeks of pregnancy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/mar/30/fda-approves-new-abortion-drug-labeling-reproductive-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowering the dosage}}}\uc2  of mifepristone needed to safely end a pregnancy, allowing the pills to be delivered by mail, eliminating the in-person doctors visit requirement and approving a generic version.\par \par \uc2 Depending on how the justices rule, those changes could be reversed, at least while the case proceeds through the courts. On Wednesday, GenBioPro, the manufacturer of the generic form of mifepristone, sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to keep the drug on the market, setting up a new front in the legal battle over access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230421ej4l0018n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
