\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Senate asks supreme court chief justice to testify on ethics amid \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  revelations \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,272 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par 20:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thomas under scrutiny after accepting luxury giftsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Democratic chair of the Senate judiciary committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644161918f0880cc85b2f480#block-644161918f0880cc85b2f480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has asked}}}\uc2  supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to testify early next month about the panel\u8217\'20\'19s approach to ethics. The request comes after a series of articles published by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  raised questions about conservative justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6#block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6#block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ties}}}\uc2  to Republican megadonor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 . Roberts has not responded yet, and the judiciary chair \uc2 Richard Durbin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644166638f08643c39fd68eb#block-644166638f08643c39fd68eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  he\u8217\'20\'19s not looking to compel his testimony with a subpoena.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The debt limitbattle has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64413a0e8f08c57ca81ba77b#block-64413a0e8f08c57ca81ba77b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially started}}}\uc2 . Latest development: one Democratic senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6441502e8f0880cc85b2f372#block-6441502e8f0880cc85b2f372"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thinks}}}\uc2 Joe Biden should negotiate with House speaker Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644154788f08d162e69d1075#block-644154788f08d162e69d1075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed through}}}\uc2  a measure to ban transgender athletes from women\u8217\'20\'19s sports at schools and universities, a bill that will meet its doom in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644147358f08643c39fd6721#block-644147358f08643c39fd6721"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was scheduled to be interviewed}}}\uc2  by the special counsel investigating the former president\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the January 6 insurrection and possession of classified documents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64418a5c8f0880cc85b2f65d#block-64418a5c8f0880cc85b2f65d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being left to the states displeased an influential group opposed to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Lindell, a noted conspiracy theorist and pillow magnate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644185b58f08d162e69d1327#block-644185b58f08d162e69d1327"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be}}}\uc2  on the hook for $5mn to a software expert who took him up on his challenge to debunk data Lindell claimed proved fraud in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  official alleges an investigation into the president\u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  has been mishandled, and is seeking whistleblower protection to inform Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/hunter-biden-irs-whistleblower-joe-biden-investigation-ce0c0769e61e7b5886af37a0cfa7cc32?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The GOP has for months been trying to use the younger Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legal trouble to tar the president. The US attorney in Delaware, who was appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and whom \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s White House kept in his post after taking office, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/07/hunter-biden-reports-say-fbi-has-enough-evidence-for-prosecution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  considering charges against \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  related to lying on a gun purchase background check form and failing to report some business activities to the tax authorities.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP, the unnamed \uc2 IRS\uc2  employee contacted through their attorney the leaders of several congressional committees after sharing their information within the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , and with the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s watchdog. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their report:\par \par \uc2 Mark Lytle, the attorney for the \uc2 IRS\uc2  whistleblower, wrote to lawmakers Wednesday that his client has information about a \u8220\'20\'1Cfailure to mitigate clear conflicts of interest in the ultimate disposition\u8221\'20\'1D of a criminal investigation related to the younger Biden\u8217\'20\'19s taxes and whether he made a false statement in connection with a gun purchase.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite serious risks of retaliation, my client is offering to provide you with information necessary to exercise your constitutional oversight function and wishes to make the disclosures in a nonpartisan manner to the leadership of the relevant committees on both sides of the political aisle,\u8221\'20\'1D Lytle said in a letter, obtained by \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2 , that was sent to the chairmen and ranking members of several House and Senate committees.\par \par \uc2 The letter states that the supervisory special agent previously disclosed the information they are seeking to share with Congress internally with the \uc2 IRS\uc2  and a watchdog for the Justice Department. Lytle added that his client is able to contradict sworn testimony to lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Cby a senior political appointee.\u8221\'20\'1D That appointee is not named.\par \par \uc2 The special agent also wants to disclose \u8220\'20\'1Cexamples of preferential treatment and politics improperly infecting decisions and protocols that would normally be followed by career law enforcement professionals in similar circumstances if the subject were not politically connected,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawyer added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles are continuing, with a civil case over an alleged rape heading to trial in New York City. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports on a clash between the judge in the case and a lawyer for the former president:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Thursday was rebuked by the judge in his looming civil rape trial over a request for jurors to be told that if the former president did not testify, it would be out of concern that his presence would adversely affect New York City.\par \par \uc2 This week, a lawyer for Trump, Joe Tacopina, first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/judge-denies-trumps-bid-delay-civil-rape-trial-rcna80014"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to delay}}}\uc2  the trial then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-testify-person-e-jean-carroll-civil-rape-trial-rcna80533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested}}}\uc2  the jury instruction.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Kaplan on Wednesday, Tacopina said jurors should be told: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile no litigant is required to appear at a civil trial, the absence of the defendant in this matter, by design, avoids the logistical burdens that his presence, as the former president, would cause the courthouse and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  City.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/trump-new-york-civil-rape-trial-jurors-request"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rebuked by judge over jury request in New York civil rape trial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America has taken issue with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stance that he regards \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue to be decided by the states.\par \par \uc2 Citing a statement the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/20/republicans-abortion-dobbs-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the Washington Post}}}\uc2 , the group\u8217\'20\'19s president Marjorie Dannenfelser hit out at Trump, who played an instrumental role in the overturning of Roe v Wade by appointing three conservative justices to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that the Supreme Court returned the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  solely to the states is a completely inaccurate reading of the Dobbs decision and is a morally indefensible position for a self-proclaimed pro-life presidential candidate to hold,\u8221\'20\'1D Dannenfelser said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will oppose any presidential candidate who refuses to embrace at a minimum a 15-week national standard to stop painful late-term abortions while allowing states to enact further protections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the rest of the statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbaprolife.org/newsroom/press-releases/sba-donald-trumps-states-only-position-unacceptable-pro-life-movement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Lindell, who is best known outside the world of pillow enthusiasts for spreading baseless tales about the 2020 election, may now have to pay up big time after challenging a software expert to debunk data supposedly proving fraud was behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election loss. It\u8217\'20\'19s an unusual story, and the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  tells it well:\par \par \uc2 Mike Lindell must make good on a promise and pay $5m to a software expert who debunked data the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/25/mike-lindell-mypillow-trump-big-lie-midterms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspiracy theorist}}}\uc2  touted in advancing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lie that his 2020 presidential election defeat was the result of voting fraud, an arbitration panel decided.\par \par \uc2 In its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/documents/a68b42f4-d5dc-4ff9-b34e-84d52fa3fc32.pdf?itid=lk_inline_manual_11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2 , the panel said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe data Lindell LLC provided, and represented reflected information from the November 2020 election, unequivocally did not reflect November 2020 election data.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump in 2020 was conclusive: by more than 7m votes and a clear margin in the electoral college.\par \par \uc2 But Lindell, who is recovering from substance use disorder and is chief executive of MyPillow, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/mypillow-mike-lindell-trump-big-lie-election-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent millions}}}\uc2  in support of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/mike-lindell-mypillow-trump-2020-election-lie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Lindell ordered to pay $5m to man who debunked data used to push big lie}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Florida, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s feud with \uc2 Disney\uc2  is escalating, all while the governor appears to be moving towards announcing a run for the Republican presidential nomination next year. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  has the latest from Miami:\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated legislature in Florida has moved quickly to amplify Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/ron-desantis-prison-near-disney-theme-park"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feud with Disney over LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2 , advancing a proposal to overcome the company\u8217\'20\'19s thwarting of his earlier plan to seize control of the theme park giant.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, a likely candidate for the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 2024 presidential nomination, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/chris-christie-ron-desantis-disney-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outfoxed by Disney}}}\uc2  after installing a hand-picked board of directors with oversight of the state\u8217\'20\'19s biggest private employer. At its first meeting, the board discovered a last-minute deal between \uc2 Disney\uc2  and outgoing directors had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/disney-ron-desantis-florida-dont-say-gay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rendered it in effect impotent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, in a move Democrats say is unconstitutional, lawmakers on Wednesday introduced a measure handing the DeSantis loyalists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article274492771.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retroactive power to nullify the agreement}}}\uc2  by amending a land use law relating to special taxing districts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/disney-world-desantis-lgbtq-housing-taxes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis v Disney feud escalates as Republicans advance takeover plan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Oklahoma, the fallout continues from revelations that local officials fantasized about killing Black people and news reporters. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 A county commissioner in far south-east Oklahoma who was identified by a local newspaper as one of several officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/oklahoma-mccurtain-county-sheriff-officials-recording-racist-threatening-remarks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 caught on tape}}}\uc2  discussing killing reporters and lynching Black people has resigned from office, the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor confirmed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Governor \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 , Carly Atchison, said their office received a handwritten resignation letter from the McCurtain county commissioner Mark Jennings. In it, Jennings says he is resigning immediately and that he plans to release a formal statement \u8220\'20\'1Cin the near future regarding the recent events in our county\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The threatening comments by Jennings and officials with the McCurtain county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office were obtained after a 6 March meeting and reported by the McCurtain Gazette-News earlier this week in its weekend edition. They have sparked outrage and protests in the city of Idabel, the county seat.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/oklahoma-county-official-resigns-mark-jennings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma county official resigns after threatening remarks caught on tape}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Democratic chair of the Senate judiciary committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644161918f0880cc85b2f480#block-644161918f0880cc85b2f480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has asked}}}\uc2  supreme court chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to testify early next month about the panel\u8217\'20\'19s approach to ethics. The request comes after a series of articles published by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  raised questions about conservative justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6#block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6#block-644169948f0880cc85b2f4f6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ties}}}\uc2  to Republican megadonor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 . The judiciary chair \uc2 Richard Durbin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644166638f08643c39fd68eb#block-644166638f08643c39fd68eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  he has no intention of compelling Roberts\u8217\'20\'19s testimony with a subpoena \u8211\'20\'13 thus, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an eye out to see if the chief justice responds.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The debt limitbattle has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-64413a0e8f08c57ca81ba77b#block-64413a0e8f08c57ca81ba77b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially started}}}\uc2 . Latest development: one Democratic senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6441502e8f0880cc85b2f372#block-6441502e8f0880cc85b2f372"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thinks}}}\uc2 Joe Biden should negotiate with House speaker Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644154788f08d162e69d1075#block-644154788f08d162e69d1075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed through}}}\uc2  a measure to ban transgender athletes from women\u8217\'20\'19s sports at schools and universities, a bill that will meet its doom in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/20/debt-ceiling-biden-trump-classified-documents-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-644147358f08643c39fd6721#block-644147358f08643c39fd6721"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is scheduled to be interviewed}}}\uc2  by the special counsel investigating the former president\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the January 6 insurrection and possession of classified documents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Once they\u8217\'20\'19re confirmed, supreme court justices don\u8217\'20\'19t appear before Congress often. How did we get to the point where a top Democrat wants the court\u8217\'20\'19s chief justice to appear before his committee? This piece from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edpilkington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2  answers that question:\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  put out a statement in which he addressed the storm of criticism that has engulfed him following the blockbuster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica report}}}\uc2  that revealed his failure to disclose lavish gifts of luxury vacations and private-jet travel from a Texan real estate magnate.\par \par \uc2 Thomas confirmed that the Dallas billionaire and Republican mega-donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2  and his wife Kathy were \u8220\'20\'1Camong our dearest friends\u8221\'20\'1D. Thomas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23745868-clarence-thomas-statement-4-7-23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 admitted, too}}}\uc2 , that he and his wife Ginni had \u8220\'20\'1Cjoined them on a number of family trips during the more-than-a-quarter-century we have known them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The justice, who is the longest-serving member of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court and arguably its most staunch conservative, insisted he had taken advice that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis sort of personal hospitality from close personal friends\u8221\'20\'1D did not have to be reported under federal ethics laws. He emphasized that the friend in question \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not have business before the court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-harlan-crow-luxury-gifts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judicial record undermines Clarence Thomas defence in luxury gifts scandal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 CBS News reports that Senate judiciary chair \uc2 Richard Durbin\uc2  hopes \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  will honor his invitation to testify before his committee, and isn\u8217\'20\'19t considering sending the chief justice a subpoena:\par \par \uc2 enltrDurbin told reporters, "There's been no discussion of subpoenas for anyone at this point."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jack Turman III (@jackturmanIII) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jackturmanIII/status/1649083544717647872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate invites supreme court chief justice to testify on ethics\par \par \uc2 The Democratic chair of the Senate judiciary committee has asked chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to testify on 2 May about the court\u8217\'20\'19s ethics, following revelations of undisclosed links between a Republican megadonor and conservative justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judiciary.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/chair_durbin_invitation_to_chief_justice_roberts_to_testify_before_sjc.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter to Roberts}}}\uc2 , judiciary committee chair \uc2 Richard Durbin\uc2  did not mention those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/20/clarence-thomas-supreme-court-harlan-crow-luxury-gifts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports about Thomas }}}\uc2  specifically, but noted that since he last addressed the court\u8217\'20\'19s ethics in 2011 \u8220\'20\'1Cthere has been a steady stream of revelations regarding Justices falling short of the ethical standards expected of other federal judges and, indeed, of public servants generally. These problems were already apparent back in 2011, and the Court\u8217\'20\'19s decade-long failure to address them has contributed to a crisis of public confidence. The status quo is no longer tenable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Durbin said the hearing would focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ethical rules that govern the Justices of the Supreme Court and potential reforms to those rules,\u8221\'20\'1D while noting that the \u8220\'20\'1Cscope of your testimony can be limited to these subjects, and that you would not be expected to answer questions from Senators regarding any other matters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 At a press conference following the House\u8217\'20\'19s passage of a measure to keep transgender athletes out of women\u8217\'20\'19s sports, CNN reports speaker Kevin McCarthy made it clear he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t interested in discussing conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s links to a major GOP donor:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CNo, not all,\u8221\'20\'1D Speaker McCarthy said when I asked if he had any concerns that \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  received gifts from a GOP megadonor and didn\u8217\'20\'19t disclose them. He then moved onto the next question and didn\u8217\'20\'19t entertain a follow\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1649078475209289728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The GOP\u8217\'20\'19s offensive into so-called culture war issues \u8211\'20\'13 like the transgender sports ban \u8211\'20\'13 apparently has limits. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  report, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is unconvinced that a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is a good idea for the party to pursue:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  considers a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban a losing proposal for Republicans as the party prepares to enter the first presidential election since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 and is unlikely to support such a policy, according to people close to him.\par \par \uc2 The former president has told allies in recent days that his gut feeling remains leaving the matter of reproductive rights to the states \u8211\'20\'13 following the court\u8217\'20\'19s reasoning in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization that ended 50 years of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 But Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crystallizing stance appears to be, in essence, a recognition that a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could cost him in the 2024 election should he become the Republican nominee, mainly because a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority of Americans}}}\uc2  simply do not support making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly or entirely illegal.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/donald-trump-federal-abortion-ban-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump considers federal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban a vote-loser and is unlikely to support one}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 House passes ban on transgender athletes in women's sports\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have succeeded in passing the Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act, a ban on transgender athletes playing in women\u8217\'20\'19s sports at schools and colleges that receive federal funding.\par \par \uc2 The bill, which attracted no Democratic support, will not make it through the Senate, but was cast by the GOP as a necessary measure to ensure fairness in sports. \u8220\'20\'1COur daughters should not be forced to compete against biological men in competitive sports, which is why House Republicans took a stand for fairness and to protect the future of women\u8217\'20\'19s sports from being diminished by the radical gender fluidity agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , the third-ranking House Republican, said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats like House minority leader \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  have condemned the bill as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbullying\u8221\'20\'1D measure targeted at the transgender community:\par \par \uc2 enltrTransgender children simply want to live, make friends and belong.\par \par \uc2 Instead they face bullying by Extreme MAGA Republicans in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Voted NO on the cruel right-wing effort to ban kids from sports.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  (@RepJeffries) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJeffries/status/1649065249700732928?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Similar legislation has been passed by 21 Republican-controlled states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lgbtmap.org/equality-maps/youth/sports_participation_bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Movement Advancement Project}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin, the White House\u8217\'20\'19s best frenemy. Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 At some point, the Senate will have to consider legislation to raise the debt ceiling, and while Democrats may control that chamber, getting all their lawmakers on board with whatever deal is agreed to is no sure thing.\par \par \uc2 A new reminder of that dynamic just arrived this morning in the form of a statement from Joe Manchin. He represents deep-red West Virginia and, should he choose to run, faces a tough re-election battle next year. He also has proven to be a thorn in the side of the Biden administration and its priorities over the past two years.\par \par \uc2 Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s statement was far from an endorsement of McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s plan, but also called on Biden to negotiate with the House speaker \u8211\'20\'13 something the president has refused to do, saying the debt ceiling should be increased, and fiscal reforms should be discussed separately.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Manchin said:\par \par \uc2 America is facing a historic economic crisis brought on by an abject failure to address our exploding national debt, chronic inflation, a looming recession, and the more immediate need to raise the debt ceiling. Our elected leaders must stop with the political games, work together and negotiate a compromise. Instead, it has been more than 78 days since President Biden last met with Speaker McCarthy. This signals a deficiency of leadership, and it must change. The fact is we are long past time for our elected leaders to sit down and discuss how to solve this impending debt ceiling crisis.\par \par \uc2 While it is reasonable to sincerely disagree with any specific debt ceiling approach, we will achieve a historic default, and the economic whirlwind which follows, if President Biden continues to refuse to even negotiate a reasonable and commonsense compromise. To that end, I applaud Speaker McCarthy for putting forward a proposal that would prevent default and rein in federal spending. While I do not agree with everything proposed, the fact of the matter is that it is the only bill actually moving through Congress that would prevent default. For the sake of the country, I urge President Biden to come to the table, propose a plan for real and substantive spending cuts and deficit reduction, and negotiate now. Failing to do so may score political points with the extremes of the Democratic Party, but make no mistake, it will be the American people \u8211\'20\'13 and our nation \u8211\'20\'13 who will pay the ultimate price if partisan politics continues to define our politics and policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shifting back to the debt ceiling debate, one of the biggest problems Republicans face is getting all their lawmakers to back House leadership\u8217\'20\'19s proposal to raise the limit while cutting government spending.\par \par \uc2 The GOP controls the House but only by a narrow margin, and some of its most conservative lawmakers say they won\u8217\'20\'19t vote to raise the debt ceiling at all. George Santos, the Republican congressman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/02/house-ethics-committee-george-santos-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prolific liar}}}\uc2 , is among that group, Punchbowl News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrSANTOS says he\u8217\'20\'19s a hard no \u8212\'20\'14 but he wants to talk to McCarthy and he\u8217\'20\'19s opening to coming around.\par \par \uc2 So not much of a hard no.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1649055833291108353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not all the news there is about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  today. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that a top adviser to the former president is being interviewed by the special counsel tasked with getting to the bottom of his attempts to overturn the 2020 election and his possession of classified documents:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s senior adviser and legal counsel Boris Epshteyn is scheduled to be interviewed on Thursday by special counsel prosecutors investigating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  retention of classified-marked documents at his Mar-a-Lago resort and his role in the January 6 Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 The investigation Epshteyn is being asked to talk about \u8211\'20\'13 potentially both \u8211\'20\'13 remains unclear, according to a person familiar with the matter who confirmed the meeting on the condition of anonymity. His lawyer could not immediately be reached for comment.\par \par \uc2 But the interview, which was requested by special counsel prosecutors, marks a moment of potential peril for Trump given Epshteyn has been one of his closest advisers in recent years, with more knowledge about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal entanglements than perhaps anyone else.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/trump-adviser-boris-epshteyn-interview-special-counsel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Trump adviser to be interviewed by special counsel prosecutors}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Appeals court blocks GOP subpoena to former Trump prosecutor\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court has temporarily stayed a subpoena from the Republican-led House judiciary committee that would have compelled the deposition of Mark Pomerantz, a former prosecutor for Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  who was looking into alleged misconduct by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pomerantz left Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s office in 2022, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/03/donald-trump-mob-boss-john-gotti-insane-mark-pomerantz-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a book}}}\uc2  this year outlining why he believes there\u8217\'20\'19s a criminal case against the former president. The House GOP subpoenaed Pomerantz following Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s indictment of Trump last month on charges of allegedly falsifying business records. The prosecutor then sued the committee and its chair Jim Jordan to block the subpoena, a petition that was initially turned down by a judge before being upheld by a federal appeals court today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/20/appeals-court-house-gop-subpoena-trump-pomerantz-00093020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 With Republican proposal, debt limit battle begins\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been brewing for months, but with the release of the House Republican proposal to raise the debt ceiling yesterday, it\u8217\'20\'19s safe to say that the latest skirmish in the perennial Washington standoff has officially kicked off.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot to say about the debt ceiling, but here\u8217\'20\'19s the gist: the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/articles/2013/10/11/why-do-only-us-and-denmark-have-a-debt-ceiling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 somewhat uniquely}}}\uc2 , places a legal limit on how much debt the government can take on. The US borrows continuously and that limit was reached in January, meaning everything the government does \u8211\'20\'13 from social security payments to the salaries of government workers \u8211\'20\'13 is being paid for by the cash the government has on hand. As soon as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bipartisanpolicy.org/debt-limit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early June}}}\uc2 , by some estimates, those funds will be exhausted, meaning the US won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to pay its bills. Of chief concern are the payments it must make on its outstanding debt \u8211\'20\'13 if American defaults on one of those, it could have major consequences for the economy.\par \par \uc2 Led by House speaker Kevin McCarthy, the Republicans yesterday unveiled the Limit, Save, Grow Act of 2023, which would raise the limit through March of next year, while targeting several of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s priorities. The bill would block his plan to cancel some federal student loans, rescind $80bn in new funding for the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2 , which was meant in part to crack down on tax cheats, and make across-the-board spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people expect and deserve serious, sensible action to address our soaring national debt,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy and other House Republican leaders said in a statement announcing the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, President Biden has avoided taking any action, even though he added $6 trillion to our nation\u8217\'20\'19s debt burden in two years and caused historic inflation that continues to hurt families and small businesses. The President seems to have no interest in negotiating a responsible debt limit increase. What President Biden is demanding is irresponsible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden immediately criticized the idea, and his press secretary\u8217\'20\'19s statement this morning makes clear the White House is not happy with the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s starting position in what will likely be weeks of negotiating. But with the fate of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy in the balance, negotiating is all the two sides can do.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House excoriates Republican debt limit proposal\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The White House apparently spent the evening at the whetstone, sharpening their rhetorical knives for use against the proposal released by the House Republicans to increase the debt ceiling while also cutting spending to a variety of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s priorities. Press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is out with a statement first thing this morning that says: \u8220\'20\'1CMaga House Republicans are holding the American economy hostage in order to take a hatchet to programs Americans rely on every day to make ends meet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the \uc2 US government\uc2  expected to exhaust its cash on hand sometime in early June (a date that could change), we are surely going to be hearing a lot about this battle in the weeks to come.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not all that\u8217\'20\'19s happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House will vote on GOP legislation to ban transgender athletes from women\u8217\'20\'19s athletics at schools and colleges, with speaker Kevin McCarthy holding a press conference about the bill around 11.15am eastern time, after its expected passage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican senator{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1649029716332912641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has introduced}}}\uc2  a motion of no confidence in homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, a frequent target of Republican ire over migrant arrivals at the southern border.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser Boris Epshteyn{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/19/us/politics/boris-epshteyn-special-counsel.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is scheduled to be interviewed today}}}\uc2  by Jack Smith, the special prosecutor looking into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s possession of classified documents and involvement in trying to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230420ej4k001e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
