\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court delays decision on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill restrictions until Friday \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,350 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2023\par 15:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Justices will decide by end of week on whether to allow ruling reversing drug\u8217\'20\'19s authorization from taking effectSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 In a surprise move, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-644040c58f0861d5fd875db9#block-644040c58f0861d5fd875db9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court extended its review}}}\uc2  of an appeals court ruling reimposing restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone until Friday, meaning there would be no changes to the drug\u8217\'20\'19s availability until then, if at all. The body is dominated by conservative jurors who just last year overturned Roe v Wade, but it\u8217\'20\'19s too soon to tell if they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to crack down on a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates have been hoping would allow people nationwide to continue accessing the procedure. Meanwhile in the Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-6440346b8f0861d5fd875d3a#block-6440346b8f0861d5fd875d3a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Republicans unveiled}}}\uc2  a proposal to increase the debt ceiling that would also cut spending and stop the White House\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to relieve some student loans debt. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-6440385c8f0861d5fd875d5b#block-6440385c8f0861d5fd875d5b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not sound open}}}\uc2  to the plan.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top House Republican said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-64400d5a8f081795c4358b19#block-64400d5a8f081795c4358b19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the party plans}}}\uc2  to impeach homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A mother and son{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-644011d08f081795c4358b5d#block-644011d08f081795c4358b5d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were convicted}}}\uc2  for storming the Capitol on January 6, with zip-ties in hand.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  went to Washington yesterday, hoping to drum up support for his much-anticipated presidential bid. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-643ff36c8f08018c1abae5ad#block-643ff36c8f08018c1abae5ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It did not go well}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-644019848f0861d5fd875bfa#block-644019848f0861d5fd875bfa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Monday welcome}}}\uc2  to the White House the \u8220\'20\'1CTennessee Three\u8221\'20\'1D, as the Democratic lawmakers who protested on the floor of the state House of Representatives in favor of gun control are known.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s indictment is not exactly changing a lot of minds, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-6440256e8f081795c4358c70#block-6440256e8f081795c4358c70"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new poll found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Before the supreme court decided to extend its decision until Friday, a ruling in the mifepristone case had been expected today, since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s stay on the appeals court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was to expire at midnight. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a story by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  on the twists and turns in this complex case:\par \par \uc2 The future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was once again before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  on Wednesday, as the justices weighed whether to sharply restrict access to the most common method of ending pregnancies while a lawsuit over the drug proceeds.\par \par \uc2 An order was expected less than a year after the supreme court overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , returning the matter the states. It was the latest development in a legal battle initiated by campaigners seeking to revoke a 23-year-old Food and Drug Administration approval of the pill, mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge in Texas, declared the \uc2 FDA\uc2  improperly approved the drug in 2000, effectively saying it should be pulled from the market even where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/19/us-supreme-court-abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court poised to rule on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 The decision to keep mifepristone available until midnight on Friday while the supreme court weighs its fate was made by conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-mifepristone-abortion-drug-8457b38f7a4799778e894da1858c8aa2?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_03"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the author of the decision last June overturning Roe v Wade and ending nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Earlier this month, Matthew Kacsmaryk, a federal judge in Texas, revoked the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of the medication in response to a lawsuit brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration appealed that decision, and a three-judge panel partially reversed Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision, allowing the drug to continue to be prescribed but reimposing restrictions that had been repealed in recent years.\par \par \uc2 That prompted the White House to appeal again to the conservative-dominated supreme court, where the matter awaits a ruling.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to specify that the supreme court is considering the appeals court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, not Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court extends \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication review till Friday\par \par \uc2 The supreme court will preserve existing levels of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone until Friday, while it considers whether to allow restrictions on the drug that were removed in 2016 to be reimposed, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Follow this blog for more on this developing story.\par \par \uc2 This post has been updated to clarify the content of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s order.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Firing salvos in the ongoing debt ceiling standoff is not all the Republican-controlled House is up to today.\par \par \uc2 The chamber {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1648735049909403655"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has started debate}}}\uc2  on the Protection of Women and Girls in Sports Act of 2023, which would ban transgender athletes from women\u8217\'20\'19s athletics at schools and universities that receive federal funding. Twenty-one GOP-led states have already passed such measures, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lgbtmap.org/equality-maps/youth/sports_participation_bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the}}}\uc2  Movement Advancement Project, a pro-LGBTQ+ rights think tank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe policies of the woke, progressive Left have invaded schools and campuses across America. Allowing biological males on women\u8217\'20\'19s sports teams and in their locker rooms creates an unfair competitive environment for female athletes,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Greg Steube\uc2 , the Florida Republican who sponsored the bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://steube.house.gov/media/press-releases/steube-legislation-to-save-women-s-sports-advances-out-of-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said following its passage}}}\uc2  out of the House education committee.\par \par \uc2 Progressive House Democrat Maxwell Frost had some particularly pointed remarks about the proposal in a speech on the House floor:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThese are the priorities of the Republican majority, not addressing gun violence, rising rent, or medical bills \u8230\'20\'26 They want the government to be in children\u8217\'20\'19s pants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Maxwell Frost (D-FL) slams House GOP bill that would ban transgender athletes from girls\u8217\'20\'19 school sports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Huyjhgwi1u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Huyjhgwi1u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648757747322699776?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This post was amended on 20 April 2023 to correct the number of states that have already passed bans on transgender athletes in women\u8217\'20\'19s athletics.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking at a union training facility in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s Maryland suburbs, and he\u8217\'20\'19s not holding back in condemning the Republican proposal to address the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the president\u8217\'20\'19s response, as reported by USA Today:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I was telling you it's going to happen," Biden says, minutes after McCarthy unveiled $4.5 trillion in proposed cuts. "Massive cuts to programs you count on," Biden says. "It would destroy this economy. And who do you think it will hurt the most? You. Hard-working people."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joey Garrison (@joeygarrison) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joeygarrison/status/1648759504916344832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The comment does not bode well for the president\u8217\'20\'19s negotiations with House speaker Kevin McCarthy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 As expected, the Republican bill to increase the debt ceiling also includes a laundry list of conservative wishes.\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy just unveiled the proposal, which would undo the funding increase the Internal Revenues Service won last year to go after tax cheats and improve its operations, prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from canceling some federal student loans and cut into government spending, among other provisions.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from States Newsroom:\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy says that within divided government, "the House, the Senate and the White House should be negotiating a responsible debt limit increase right now."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Shutt (@JenniferShutt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferShutt/status/1648754939718430721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy says House Rs bill will raise the debt limit into next year and "provide more than $4.5 trillion in savings to the American taxpayer."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Shutt (@JenniferShutt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferShutt/status/1648755539877191696?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy says House Rs debt limit bill would\par \par \uc2 - set FY24 spending at last year's levels\par \par \uc2 - limit spending increases to 1% per year\par \par \uc2 - "claw back billions of dollars of unspent COVID money"\par \par \uc2 - eliminate \uc2 IRS\uc2  funding boost from IRA\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Shutt (@JenniferShutt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferShutt/status/1648756148181295104?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMcCarthy says the bill would bar the Biden administration from implementing its student loan forgiveness plan.\par \par \uc2 It would also require "adults without dependents, earn a paycheck, and learn new skills" in order to get federal aid.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Shutt (@JenniferShutt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferShutt/status/1648756718321426436?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Kennedy III\uc2  insisted today he will be sticking to the job given to him by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in December \u8211\'20\'13 US economic envoy to Northern Ireland \u8211\'20\'13 even though his uncle, \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , today formally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/robert-kennedy-jr-announces-run-for-president-anti-vaccine-activist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared he will stand}}}\uc2 , in all likelihood against Biden, for the Democratic presidential nomination next year.\par \par \uc2 Joe Kennedy III\uc2 . Photograph: Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, scion of the famous political dynasty and a former US congressman from Massachusetts, was asked about his uncle\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Belfast today, while on his first trip as the US envoy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love my uncle, and nothing\u8217\'20\'19s ever going to come between that,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am honoured that the president selected me for this position. I support the president and look forward to supporting him in the next few years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Further reading:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/robert-kennedy-jr-announces-run-for-president-anti-vaccine-activist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anti-vaccine activist Robert Kennedy Jr announces run for president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 As yet today has brought no new congressional endorsements of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , but there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/ron-desantis-ally-backs-trump-latest-florida-defection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plenty of drama yesterday}}}\uc2  as two Florida Republicans, one formerly a close ally of the governor, threw their support behind Trump, the clear early leader in the race for the Republican presidential nomination.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 Amid reports that DeSantis allies have been calling Florida Republicans to ask them not to abandon the governor, Politico reported that Trump aides also placed calls before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  defections.\par \par \uc2 One unnamed source said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe amazing part of it is how easy it was.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s more on that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/ron-desantis-ally-backs-trump-latest-florida-defection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  (and below). But perhaps the most dramatic move came from a Republican from Texas, Lance Gooden.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis was in Washington to meet members of Congress. At least one attendee was evidently not sold on the deal. Emerging from what he called \u8220\'20\'1Ca positive meeting\u8221\'20\'1D with the governor, Gooden swiftly \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Lancegooden/status/1648448172845568002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released his endorsement}}}\uc2  of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/ron-desantis-ally-backs-trump-latest-florida-defection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis ally backs Trump for president in latest Florida defection}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 New polling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/04/18/majority-of-americans-say-trumps-indictment-wont-affect-their-vote-cnbc-survey-finds.html?__source=iosappshare%7Ccom.apple.UIKit.activity.PostToTwitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from CNBC}}}\uc2  tells us 58% of Americans say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criminal indictment in New York will not effect how they vote.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Ron Johnson/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor independents, it does lean them a little bit negative, but not overwhelmingly so,\u8221\'20\'1D Jay Campbell of Hart Research, the Democratic pollster for the survey, told CNBC.\par \par \uc2 Around 25% of respondents said the 34 counts of falsification of business records, relating to a hush money payment to the porn star Stormy Daniels, would make them less likely to vote for Trump, who is leading the race for the Republican nomination for president next year.\par \par \uc2 Asked if they agreed that the Trump indictment \u8220\'20\'1Cis a good thing for the country, because it shows that no one is above the law, not even the former president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D, 53% of respondents said they did.\par \par \uc2 Polling regarding the Republican primary has shown little but good news for Trump since his indictment and arraignment, which happened earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who has not formally declared a run but is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s closest challenger, has concurrently suffered \u8211\'20\'13 also while registering plenty of missteps of his own.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/chris-christie-ron-desantis-disney-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris Christie derides Ron DeSantis for being outfoxed by Disney}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida has expanded its ban on classroom lessons about sexual orientation and gender identity to all grades at the request of governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Decried by critics as the \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law, Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/dont-say-gay-bill-florida-senate-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last year passed the ban}}}\uc2  on such lessons in kindergarten through third grade. Similar legislation has spread to other conservative-led states, while in Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/20/republicans-national-dont-say-gaw-law-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans have proposed}}}\uc2  a nationwide ban on the instruction.\par \par \uc2 This year, DeSantis asked the state\u8217\'20\'19s board of education to expand the ban up to the 12th grade, which it did today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the move, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/desantis-florida-dont-say-gay-ban-684ed25a303f83208a89c556543183cb?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the AP}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The proposal will take effect after a procedural notice period that lasts about a month, according to an education department spokesman.\par \par \uc2 The rule change would ban lessons on sexual orientation and gender identity from grades 4-12, unless required by existing state standards or as part of reproductive health instruction that students can choose not to take. Florida currently bans such lessons in kindergarten through third grade.\par \par \uc2 The DeSantis administration put forward the proposal last month as part of the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive conservative agenda, with the governor leaning heavily into cultural divides ahead of his looming White House candidacy.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has not commented on the proposal. He previously directed questions to Education Commissioner Manny Diaz Jr., who said it was meant to clarify confusion around the existing law and reinforce that teachers should not deviate from existing curriculums.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not removing anything here,\u8221\'20\'1D Diaz Jr. said on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CAll we are doing is we are setting the expectations so our teachers are clear: that they are to teach to the standards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prohibition, which began last year with the law banning sexual orientation and gender identity lessons in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-lifestyle-education-florida-ron-desantis-322e0a40da909f48954b8b1bd9190750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kindergarten through third grade}}}\uc2 , has drawn intense {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-education-ron-desantis-gender-identity-49dfb9a4f63b2497846df8e96fd652cc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash}}}\uc2  from critics who argue it marginalizes LGBTQ+ people and has vague terms that result in self-censorship from teachers. Democratic President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called it \u8220\'20\'1Chateful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The current law is also the root of an ongoing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/disney-desantis-dont-say-gay-orlando-florida-f963348d31f4746a06957264faf7e2b2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feud with Disney}}}\uc2 , one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest employers and political donors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s put it plainly: This is part of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s assault on freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Joe Saunders\uc2 , senior political director of the LGBTQ advocacy group Equality Florida, said in a statement, adding the policy will \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther stigmatize and isolate a population of young people who need our support now more than ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2  may have avoided a potentially embarrassing trial by agreeing to pay \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  $787.5m to settle its defamation lawsuit, but the reckoning for its airing of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election conspiracy theories is far from over. Election equipment firm \uc2 Smartmatic{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-6440005f8f0861d5fd875a74#block-6440005f8f0861d5fd875a74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has vowed}}}\uc2  to press ahead with its lawsuit, while \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shareholders are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-643fe9ea8f08018c1abae527#block-643fe9ea8f08018c1abae527"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly angry}}}\uc2  about the payout. Meanwhile in Washington, the long-running debt ceiling battle is heating up, with the House GOP set to unveil their proposal to up the borrowing limit \u8211\'20\'13 but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-644016b08f08018c1abae7d1#block-644016b08f08018c1abae7d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only through next March}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A top House Republican said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-64400d5a8f081795c4358b19#block-64400d5a8f081795c4358b19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the party plans}}}\uc2  to impeach homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A mother and son were convicted for storming the Capitol on January 6, with zip-ties in hand.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  went to Washington yesterday, hoping to drum up support for his much-anticipated presidential bid. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/19/fox-news-dominion-settlement-biden-debt-trump-live-updates?page=with:block-643ff36c8f08018c1abae5ad#block-643ff36c8f08018c1abae5ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It did not go well}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to meet 'Tennessee Three' on Monday\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet on Monday with the three Democratic lawmakers who faced expulsion votes in the Tennessee House of Representatives after they protested in favor of gun control, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am pleased to share that the president looks forward to welcoming Tennessee state representative Justin Jones, Justin Pearson and Gloria Johnson to the White House this coming Monday,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said at her daily briefing, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6wXjNZueBVE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which is ongoing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated chamber expelled Jones and Pearson, both of whom are Black, after they participated in a protest on the House chamber floor calling for tighter gun laws following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/02/nashville-school-shooting-teacher-cindy-peak-funeral"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Nashville mass shooting}}}\uc2 . Johnson, who also participated and is white, narrowly survived her expulsion vote. Within days, authorities in their districts reappointed Jones and Pearson back to their seats, though they will have to win upcoming special elections to keep them.\par \par \uc2 The saga won the trio of lawmakers a new moniker: the \u8220\'20\'1CTennessee Three\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republicans want debt limit fight during 2024 election\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that Republicans in the House of Representatives are proposing legislation that would put the \uc2 US government\uc2  in a position to again hit its debt limit at the end of March 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 right as the presidential election is heating up:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Republicans are planning to raise the debt ceiling by $1.5 trillion or until March 31 of next year, whichever comes first, the sources said\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1648718809564426240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The news comes as House Republicans are reported to today release the text of their proposal to increase the borrowing limit, which is expected to include spending cuts and other concessions from Democrats. The \uc2 US government\uc2  could default by about June if the limit is not raised.\par \par \uc2 As CNN report, the increase would not last long, and lawmakers would again have to reach a deal to raise it months before voters head to the polls in the 2024 presidential election, which very likely could see a rematch between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Zip-tie wielding mother, son convicted over January 6 insurrection\par \par \uc2 A mother and son who brought zip ties with them when they stormed the Senate gallery during the January 6 insurrection have been found guilty by a federal judge, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/capitol-riot-zip-ties-munchel-eisenhart-c25ea7fe087495994d6e22d97116efe6?utm_source=ForYou&utm_medium=HomePage&utm_id=Taboola"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lisa Eisenhart and her son Eric Munchel face an 8 September sentencing after their conviction on 10 counts related to the attack, one of which was obstructing Congress. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on their case, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 Lamberth decided the case without a jury after a \u8220\'20\'1Cstipulated bench trial,\u8221\'20\'1D an unusual legal proceeding in which defendants do not admit guilt to charges but agree with prosecutors that certain facts are true. At least three dozen Capitol riot defendants have resolved their cases that way \u8212\'20\'14 which allows defendants to preserve their right to an appeal \u8212\'20\'14 rather than opting for a traditional trial or pleading guilty.\par \par \uc2 A jury trial for the pair had been scheduled to start last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur goal at the end of the day was to show the court that (Munchel) is accepting responsibility for what occurred on Jan. 6,\u8221\'20\'1D his attorney, Joe Allen, said after the proceedings ended.\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for Eisenhart didn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately respond on Tuesday to an email seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 Munchel, 32, of Nashville, Tennessee, worked at a restaurant. Eisenhart, 59, of Woodstock, Georgia, has worked as a traveling nurse.\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 6, they attended then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D rally before joining the crowd that marched to the Capitol. Both of them were wearing tactical vests. Munchel had a stun gun holstered to his right hip.\par \par \uc2 After grabbing plastic handcuffs that they found inside the Capitol, Munchel and Eisenhart entered the gallery above the Senate chamber and stepped over a railing that separated portions of the gallery. Eisenhart chanted, \u8220\'20\'1CTreason! Treason!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Munchel \u8220\'20\'1Cgleefully\u8221\'20\'1D entered the Capitol during a riot while carrying a dangerous weapon, the stun gun, the judge said in a February 2021 ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy word and deed, Munchel has supported the violent overthrow of the \uc2 United States government\uc2 . He poses a clear danger to our republic,\u8221\'20\'1D Lamberth wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 A top House Republican has signaled that the party will indeed try to impeach homeland security secretary Alejandro Mayorkas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/18/us/politics/republicans-mark-green-mayorkas-impeachment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mark Green, the chair of the House homeland security committee, told donors this weekend that the effort would kick off this week when the secretary testifies before his committee, which happened Tuesday. The Times, citing a recording of a House Freedom Caucus fundraiser it obtained, said the case would focus on Mayorkas\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdereliction of duty and his intentional destruction of our country through the open southern border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Green said his committee would \u8220\'20\'1Cput together a packet, and we will hand it to Jim Jordan and let Jim do what Jim does best.\u8221\'20\'1D Jim Jordan is the chair of the House judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have used a sharp uptick in migrant arrivals at the US southern border to criticize \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration, and Mayorkas in particular. The most conservative corners of the party have said they want to impeach the homeland security chief, which is an exceedingly rare step to take against a cabinet secretary. On Tuesday, Republicans grilled Mayorkas during his appearance before the homeland security committee, but have yet to make the impeachment push formal.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 As bad as \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s day in Washington was yesterday, he does have some supporters in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s conservative Texas representative Chip Roy \u8217\'20\'19s view. He has endorsed DeSantis over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , arguing in a Fox News interview that the Republican party needs new blood:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to have someone who\u8217\'20\'19s not a baby boomer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Chip Roy (R-TX) explains his decision to endorse Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  (R-FL) as the 2024 Republican presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/otoG0Bx5Cz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/otoG0Bx5Cz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648698965708140548?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 It wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a day in Washington without some news about the debt ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Jack Lew, who was Treasury secretary under Barack Obama in 2011 when the nation came so close to defaulting that one of the major ratings agencies downgraded the United States\u8217\'20\'19s debt for the first time ever, spoke to House Democrats today about the ongoing standoff with Republicans, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrJack Lew, who ran Obama's OMB during '11 debt standoff, tells House Dems in whips this am:\par \par \uc2 Lew: "This topic is a combination of Groundhog Day and PTSD for me. But it\u8217\'20\'19s more dangerous than in the past because of the political environment," per person attending\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Ferris (@sarahnferris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarahnferris/status/1648683023397732352?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrLew, a former Treasury sec, also said he worries about "accidental" default on debt, with Biden and McCarthy in standoff\par \par \uc2 He called it "just as dangerous", per person attending\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Ferris (@sarahnferris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarahnferris/status/1648686491420196867?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy is looking to make the most of the impasse between the two parties ahead of a projected early June deadline for Congress to raise the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s borrowing limit or face a default. The GOP is demanding spending cuts and the enactment of some of its legislative priorities in exchange for its votes to raise the limit, while Democrats want an increase without preconditions.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what McCarthy had to say today:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor 77 days, President Biden has ignored the impending debt ceiling crisis.\par \par \uc2 Instead of leaving town today to give a speech, Biden should sit down with me, find agreement, and avoid the prospect of his administration bumbling into the first default in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@SpeakerMcCarthy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerMcCarthy/status/1648694973615726592?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Following Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s settlement with \uc2 Fox\uc2  yesterday, voting systems firm \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  vowed to push on with its own defamation lawsuit, Semafor reported:\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement from \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  lawyer Erik Connolly: \u8220\'20\'1CDominion\u8217\'20\'19s litigation exposed some of the misconduct and damage caused by \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s disinformation campaign. \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  will expose the rest. 1/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Smith (@semaforben) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/semaforben/status/1648419670565990400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSmartmatic remains committed to clearing its name, recouping the significant damage done to the company, and holding \uc2 Fox\uc2  accountable for undermining democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D 2/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Smith (@semaforben) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/semaforben/status/1648419712009900032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Fox\uc2  responded defiantly, saying they were ready to fight \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim:\par \par \uc2 enltr1/2 Remarkable statement from Fox to me just now in response to \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers saying they are ready to pick up where Dominion left off.\par \par \uc2 "There is nothing more newsworthy than covering the president of the United States and his lawyers making allegations of voter fraud.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0j7tDdsATb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0j7tDdsATb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sara Fischer (@sarafischer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarafischer/status/1648680384165724161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr2/2\par \par \uc2 (cont) \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom of the press is foundational to our democracy and must be protected, in addition to the damages claims being outrageous, unsupported, and not rooted in sound financial analysis."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sara Fischer (@sarafischer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarafischer/status/1648680509743022083?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t alone in facing legal consequences for its embrace of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election lies.\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  also filed a lawsuit against the conservative \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  network, which gave wide coverage to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy theories after the presidential vote. Following \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s settlement yesterday, CNN reports \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  released a statement in which it attempts to draw a line between its coverage and Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s:\par \par \uc2 enltrNewsmax, which also faces a major lawsuit from Dominion, issues statement saying it "stands by its coverage and analysis of the 2020 election" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KvPJP1ik4E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KvPJP1ik4E}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oliver Darcy (@oliverdarcy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverdarcy/status/1648695269842722818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 19, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has, of course, already announced his bid for the White House, but is doing so among a swirl of legal troubles. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports on a new and curious development in the complex investigation of his and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to overturn the 2020 election result in Georgia:\par \par \uc2 A new legal filing has exposed a potentially major fracture among a group of so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D in Georgia, who sought to aid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in overturning the 2020 election results in a scheme now under criminal investigation.\par \par \uc2 According to a court document filed on Tuesday, a group of people involved in the scheme recently told state prosecutors that another one of the fake electors committed crimes that they were not involved in.\par \par \uc2 The finger pointing, included in a document submitted by Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , exposes a rift within the group as prosecutors near the end of the investigation and consider bringing charges against the former president and dozens of allies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/georgia-fake-electors-crimes-trump-rift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Claims of crime expose rift in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s pro-Trump fake elector group}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  popped by Washington DC yesterday to meet with Republican congressmen\u8230\'20\'26 who turned around and endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Not a good sign for the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s potential bid for president. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  has more:\par \par \uc2 In a blow to \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a prominent ally of the rightwing governor was on Tuesday one of two Florida Republicans in Congress to back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for president, the latest in a string of defections.\par \par \uc2 The news came amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/ron-desantis-team-tries-stop-florida-gop-endorsing-trump-rcna79379"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s team has pressured US representatives from his state not to endorse Trump.\par \par \uc2 Brian Mast\uc2  told CNN he planned to endorse the former president and would chair a veterans committee in support of his re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 Peter Schorsch, publisher of FloridaPolitics.com, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeterSchorschFL/status/1648420391692668929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Brian Mast\uc2  has been DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s ally on environment and water issues in South Florida. Mast is at DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s hip during press conferences. They\u8217\'20\'19re both veterans, too. Wow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/19/ron-desantis-ally-backs-trump-latest-florida-defection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis ally backs Trump for president in latest Florida defection}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2  may have to pay up big time to settle Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, but it won\u8217\'20\'19t have to publicly apologize or otherwise own up to its long record of falsehoods. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  took a closer look at the settlement\u8217\'20\'19s finer points, from Wilmington, Delaware \u8211\'20\'13 the city where the case almost went to trial:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/fox-dominion-settle-us-defamation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staggering $787.5m}}}\uc2  settlement between \uc2 Fox\uc2  and the voting equipment company Dominion marked the end of one of the most aggressive efforts to hold someone accountable for spreading misinformation after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Dominion sued \uc2 Fox\uc2  for $1.6bn in damages for knowingly broadcasting false information about the company after the election. The money from the settlement, one of the largest libel payouts in media history, was just the icing on a cake Dominion had, in many ways, already won.\par \par \uc2 And yet, while Fox doled out an unprecedented sum, they were able to avoid something priceless: the public humiliation of a trial and an apology.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/dominion-wins-but-the-public-loses-fox-settlement-avoids-paying-the-highest-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Dominion wins but the public loses\u8217\'20\'19: Fox settlement avoids paying the highest price}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 From \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  to Crikey, here's a rundown of \uc2 Fox\uc2 's legal troubles\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s one takeaway from the US$787.5m settlement \uc2 Fox\uc2  agreed to cough up in exchange for \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 dropping its defamation lawsuit, it\u8217\'20\'19s this: it pays to be a lawyer in \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s employ. It also pays to be a lawyer suing Fox.\par \par \uc2 And there are plenty of both groups, since the media empire and in particular its conservative Fox News network remain in deep legal hot water for their enthusiastic promotion of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election conspiracy theories. Below is a rundown of the outstanding cases that could wrack up the legal fees and potentially imperil outlet\u8217\'20\'19s finances:\par \par \uc2 In a last-minute settlement on Tuesday, \uc2 Fox\uc2  agreed to pay voting equipment company Dominion US$787.5m, ending a dispute over whether the network and its parent company knowingly broadcast false and outlandish allegations that Dominion was involved in a plot to steal the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 According to analysts, while the settlement amount is incredibly costly, \uc2 Fox\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/18/dominion-wins-but-the-public-loses-fox-settlement-avoids-paying-the-highest-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoided the more damaging spectacle}}}\uc2  of a trial and a public apology.\par \par \uc2 But it still faces a number of legal challenges over the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Smartmatic\par \par \uc2 A global election technology company headquartered in London, \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 , lodged a defamation suit against Fox in February 2021. The complaint\u8217\'20\'19s striking opening sentence read: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Earth is round. Two plus two equals four. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  won the 2020 election \u8230\'20\'26 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like Dominion, \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  is suing \uc2 Fox\uc2  for defamation related to its coverage of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stolen-election lie, but the company\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit has so far attracted only a fraction of the attention.\par \par \uc2 On paper, \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s suit could be the more dangerous: it is demanding damages of $2.7bn compared with Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s claim for $1.6bn.\par \par \uc2 In March, the New York state supreme court in Manhattan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/13/smartmatic-defamation-lawsuit-against-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave the green light for the case to proceed against Fox News}}}\uc2 , the Fox Business host \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2 , the former business anchor Lou Dobbs and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company argues that that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  broadcast a series of blatant lies in support of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stolen election conspiracy theory and that hosts and guests broadcast 100 false statements: among them, that \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  was involved in 2020 election counts in six battleground states when in fact it was present only at the count in Los Angeles county.\par \par \uc2 Claims broadcast on Fox described \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  as having been founded in Venezuela at the behest of corrupt dictators. In fact, it was founded by \uc2 Antonio Mugica\uc2  and \uc2 Roger Pi\u241\'00\'F1ate\uc2  in 2000 in Boca Raton, Florida, in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2000/nov/22/uselections2000.usa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Changing chad\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  fiasco, with the aim of using technology to restore people\u8217\'20\'19s faith in election results.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/19/the-legal-problems-still-overshadowing-fox-news-after-its-dominion-settlement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The legal problems still overshadowing Fox News after its Dominion settlement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2 's legal troubles are far from over\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics readers. \uc2 Fox\uc2  may have yesterday forestalled a lengthy trial by agreeing to pay \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  $787.5m to settle its defamation lawsuit, but its lawyers will remain plenty busy for the time being. The media empire remains in legal peril over Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/09/fox-news-dominion-voter-systems-zero-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enthusiastic promotion}}}\uc2  of various lies regarding the 2020 election, with another defamation lawsuit from global election firm \uc2 Smartmatic\uc2  still pending and even the company\u8217\'20\'19s shareholders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/fox-investors-seek-records-possible-step-toward-suing-directors-2023-04-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly pondering}}}\uc2  a trip to the courts. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping an eye out for any developments in these cases today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what to expect:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading to a union training facility in Maryland where he\u8217\'20\'19ll contrast \u8220\'20\'1Chis vision for the economy with Maga House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 vision\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the White House. This comes as negotiations over raising the US debt limit heat up.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Republicans are going after Washington DC again, this time with a disapproval resolution targeting a police reform bill the city recently enacted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who sure seems like he wants to run for president, is expected to again criticize (obliquely) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a speech today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2023/04/19/how-trump-ambushed-desantis-in-d-c-00092761?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230419ej4j001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
