\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge who denied girl  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  over grades shortlisted for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s top court\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2023\par 15:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jared Smith, who was ousted for decision, will be interviewed before \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  picks new supreme court member\par \par \uc2 A Florida judge rejected by voters after denying a teenage girl an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  citing her poor school grades is in line for a seat on the state supreme court as the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , continues to turn the bench to the right.\par \par \uc2 Jared Smith will be interviewed alongside 14 others next month by a nominating commission that will make recommendations to DeSantis, who last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban into law.\par \par \uc2 The governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/22/ron-desantis-appoints-judge-abortion-girl-school-grades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed Smith}}}\uc2  to the newly established sixth district court of appeal in December, four months after voters in Hillsborough county ousted him from the circuit court following his controversial ruling.\par \par \uc2 Smith said the 17-year-old was unfit to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as he questioned her \u8220\'20\'1Coverall intelligence, emotional development and stability\u8221\'20\'1D. The decision was overturned by a three-member appeals court that said Smith abused his judicial discretion.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s decision to disregard that rebuke was the second time he had looked favorably on Smith, having first appointed him to the circuit court in 2019.\par \par \uc2 The Florida supreme court seat opened up last month when the long-serving justice Ricky Polston {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2023/03/20/ricky-polston-resigning-florida-supreme-court-giving-desantis-another-appointment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced he was standing down}}}\uc2 . Filling the vacancy will mean DeSantis will have picked five of the court\u8217\'20\'19s seven members, a potentially crucial factor for the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the state.\par \par \uc2 The panel is expected to hear arguments later this year in a lawsuit challenging the validity of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s existing 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit. A ruling to endorse it would open the way for the more extreme six-week ban to take effect.\par \par \uc2 The Tampa Bay Times on Wednesday named other candidates vying for the seat, including Meredith Sasso, chief judge of the sixth district court of appeal, of which Smith is a member; and another appellate court judge, John Stargel, a Republican state representative.\par \par \uc2 Significantly, Stargel was the only dissenting vote in the 2-1 decision that overturned Smith\u8217\'20\'19s ruling blocking the teenager\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeSantis began his transformation of the Florida supreme court immediately after taking office in 2019, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jacksonville.com/story/news/courts/2019/01/22/desantis-appoints-third-supreme-court-justice/6231398007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointing three justices in his first month}}}\uc2 . John Stemberger, president of the Florida family policy council, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flfamily.org/resources/blog/florida-conservative-judicial-philosophy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said at the time}}}\uc2  the court had \u8220\'20\'1Cthe potential to have the most reliably consistent and conservative judicial philosophy in the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s fourth pick, in August last year, was Renatha Francis, a Jamaica-born immigrant whose first judicial appointment was under DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor, \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , now a Republican US senator.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis tried and failed to elevate her to the supreme court two years earlier, with justices ruling he exceeded his authority by naming a judge lacking the 10 years\u8217\'20\'19 membership of the Florida Bar required by the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 According to the Times, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2023/04/03/3-apply-florida-supreme-court-seat-including-hillsborough-judge-tampa-attorney/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only three candidates applied}}}\uc2  after Polston, who the newspaper described as \u8220\'20\'1Creliably conservative\u8221\'20\'1D, announced his resignation in March.\par \par \uc2 A slew of other judges and experienced prosecutors put their names forward on 4 April, when the nominating commission decided to extend the deadline.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230419ej4j001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
