\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Dominion lawyer says \u8216\'20\'18lies have consequences\u8217\'20\'19 as Fox settles defamation suit for $787.5m \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now), Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 5,330 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2023\par 22:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Settlement comes just as opening statements were to begin in trialExplainer: what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake in the $1.6bn defamation lawsuitSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Recap\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  reached a settlement in its $1.6bn defamation lawsuit against Fox. \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth matters. Lies have consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dominion lawyer Justin Nelson, noting that the $787.5m settlement with \uc2 Fox\uc2  represents accountability. However, Fox News hosts are not expected to retract or acknowledge the falsehoods they spread about Dominion on air.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643eaf3c8f08610f35db714c#block-643eaf3c8f08610f35db714c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown no inclination}}}\uc2  in helping Democrats replace the ailing senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  on the judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643ea12e8f08f991ea540878#block-643ea12e8f08f991ea540878"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke last night with}}}\uc2 Ralph Yarl, the Black teenager shot after ringing the doorbell at the wrong house in Kansas City, Missouri. Meanwhile, police arrested the alleged shooter after protests over the attack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643ec1ad8f08610f35db725d#block-643ec1ad8f08610f35db725d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have filed}}}\uc2  their response before the supreme court, which is considering whether to uphold a Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone off shelves nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Representative Cori Bush has joined in calls for for supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  to be impeached, following reports that the he did not disclose his financial dealings with Republican donor and real estate developer \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bush said:\par \par \uc2 It is clear that Justice Thomas holds a complete disregard for law and ethics that is incompatible with the trust and confidence placed in federal judges. For these reasons, and because the federal judiciary has failed to hold Justice Thomas accountable, I am calling for impeachment proceedings to begin regarding Justice Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s apparent violations of federal law.\par \par \uc2 Holding judges accountable for their behavior is a matter of life-or-death for our communities. They wield enormous power, and the current hands-off approach to the judiciary has only emboldened lawless, corrupt, far-right judges to strip away our rights and make our lives worse off.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t have to acknowledge that it lied about Dominion on air, according to CNN media reporter Oliver Darcy.\par \par \uc2 Although Fox acknowledged, in a circuitous statement, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Court\u8217\'20\'19s rulings finding certain claims about Dominion to be false\u8221\'20\'1D, Fox News hosts won\u8217\'20\'19t have to admit to lying to its viewers, or directly take accountability for spreading false information.\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: I'm told that, as part of the terms of its settlement, Fox News will *not* have to acknowledge ON AIR that it told lies about Dominion in the wake of the 2020 election. \uc2 Fox\uc2  did acknowledge falsehoods in its statement. But don't expect hosts to have to read statements.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oliver Darcy (@oliverdarcy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oliverdarcy/status/1648432832266801158?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that \uc2 Fox\uc2  shareholders are seeking records to review executives\u8217\'20\'19 oversight of Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 coverage of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election claims.\par \par \uc2 From Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Fox Corp\uc2  shareholders are demanding company records that may show whether directors and executives properly oversaw Fox News\u8217\'20\'19 coverage of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election-rigging claims, sources told Reuters, in what could be a prelude to lawsuits seeking to make directors liable for costs.\par \par \uc2 Investors are using provisions in Delaware corporate law to demand internal Fox records to investigate how \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leaders acted as its Fox News network aired segments on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims that he lost the 2020 presidential election due to voter fraud, two sources confirmed.\par \par \uc2 In moves not previously reported, shareholders are looking for records such as board minutes, emails and texts that may contain evidence that \uc2 Fox\uc2  directors and executives were derelict by allowing the network to air the false claims.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s a longer statement from John Poulos, Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s CEO:\par \par \uc2 Fox\uc2  has admitted to telling lies about Dominion that caused enormous damage to my company, our employees, and our customers.\par \par \uc2 Nothing can ever make up for that.\par \par \uc2 Throughout this process, we have sought accountability, and believe the evidence brought to light through this case underscores the consequences of spreading and endorsing lies.\par \par \uc2 Truthful reporting in the media is essential to our democracy. Dominion, our employees and our partners are grateful to the court for allowing the process for the truth to come out.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement addressing the settlement, Fox News acknowledged the falsehoods aired on the network, without going much further to take accountability.\par \par \uc2 The statement reads:\par \par \uc2 We are pleased to have reached a settlement of our dispute with \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 . We acknowledge the Court\u8217\'20\'19s rulings finding certain claims about Dominion to be false. This settlement reflects \uc2 FOX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s continued commitment to the highest journalistic standards. We are hopeful that our decision to resolve this dispute with Dominion amicably, instead of the acrimony of a divisive trial, allows the country to move forward from these issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth matters. Lies have consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dominion lawyer Justin Nelson, noting that the $787.5m settlement with Fox News represents accountability.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  speak at a news conference outside the New Castle county courthouse in Wilmington, Delaware. Photograph: Matt Rourke/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFox has admitted to telling lies about Dominion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dominion CEO John Poulos.\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a press conference outside the court, Dominion attorney says \u8220\'20\'1CTruth matters. Lies have consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Settlement is $787 million {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/myKyZwQXIl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/myKyZwQXIl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kira Lerner (@kira_lerner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kira_lerner/status/1648420971618119681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Even though \uc2 Fox\uc2  ultimately settled its $1.6bn defamation lawsuit against Dominion, \u8220\'20\'1CThe stain this leaves on Fox can\u8217\'20\'19t be wiped out with money,\u8221\'20\'1D Angelo Carusone, the president of \uc2 Media Matters for America\uc2 , a media watchdog group, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFox News lied about the 2020 election; they all knew it was a lie, right up to the Murdochs themselves. What the Dominion trial offered was a keyhole view into the day-to-day industrial-scale deceit that takes place at \uc2 Fox\uc2 . It helped illustrate why the company is such a uniquely destructive force.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The settlement in \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit against Fox News came just as opening arguments were to begin in the trial, which was being held in Wilmington, Delaware.\par \par \uc2 A jury had been seated earlier today, and opening arguments were expected this afternoon, before being delayed without explanation \u8211\'20\'13 until now.\par \par \uc2 Dominion was seeking $1.6bn in compensation from Fox, alleging the broadcaster knowingly defamed it with reports that baselessly claimed the elections firm rigged the 2020 election against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  settles defamation case against Fox News\par \par \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  has reached a settlement in its $1.6bn defamation lawsuit against Fox News, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 We will post more details as they come in.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns McCarthy's debt ceiling strategy\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House earlier today, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cast Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy \u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on the debt ceiling as irresponsible. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip of his comments:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden calls out Speaker Kevin McCarthy over the debt ceiling:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe proposed huge cuts to important programs that millions of Americans count on \u8230\'20\'26 He threatened to become the first Speaker to default on our national debt \u8230\'20\'26 What are MAGA Republicans in Congress doing?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yzIyqf5BsR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yzIyqf5BsR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648403224276389888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The two men are at loggerheads over the issue, which could pose a grievous threat to the health of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy. Biden wants to increase the borrowing limit without preconditions, while McCarthy wants the president and his Democratic allies to agree to spending cuts, arguing that the country\u8217\'20\'19s budget deficit is out of control.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, White House deputy press secretary Andrew Bates condemned rightwing House Republicans who want to see the Inflation Reduction Act dismantled. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a statement he shared with the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 By targeting the Inflation Reduction Act, Scott Perry and Chip Roy just showed the real agenda of the ultra MAGA hardliners who increasingly dominate the House Republican Conference. Not only are House Republicans threatening to hold Americans\u8217\'20\'19 jobs and retirement savings hostage by engaging in the dangerous brinkmanship that Presidents Reagan and Trump warned against. Now, the increasingly empowered extreme MAGA Republicans want their ransom to be killing tens of thousands of manufacturing jobs in a windfall for China, raising prescription drug and energy costs for middle class families, and sending the deficit skyward \u8211\'20\'13 all in the name of sweetheart deals for rich special interests. That\u8217\'20\'19s on top of a multitude of other tax handouts they\u8217\'20\'19re seeking for big corporations and the wealthy. Like even \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said in 2019, avoiding a catastrophic and unprecedented default is non-negotiable. And threatening default to sell working people out to Big Pharma and billionaires is incredibly revealing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge orders special master to investigate alleged \uc2 Fox\uc2  withholding of evidence\par \par \uc2 The judge in \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against Fox News has appointed a special master to ensure Fox News turned over all evidence in the case, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNews: The judge has formally tasked the special master in the Fox/Dominion case with launching an investigation that "should include a determination whether Fox News Network... complied with their discovery allegations"\par \par \uc2 A report is due to the judge by May 15\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Barr (@jeremymbarr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremymbarr/status/1648395345171447809?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHere is the back-story: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XO2GeF3HZp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XO2GeF3HZp}}}\par \par \uc2 It's worth noting that the judge has said he is satisfied with the issue regarding \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 's title, though Dominion has claimed that \uc2 Fox\uc2  did not properly turn over materials including secret recordings of \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Barr (@jeremymbarr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremymbarr/status/1648399781440684032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Jury selection in the case concluded earlier today, and opening arguments were expected to begin afterward, but have been delayed without explanation.\par \par \uc2 Dominion is seeking $1.6bn in compensation from \uc2 Fox\uc2 , arguing the conservative network harmed its business by falsely told its viewers the company was involved in rigging the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 It seems unlikely we\u8217\'20\'19ll hear full opening arguments this afternoon, if we hear anything at all.\par \par \uc2 There has been an unexplained delay since lunch. Both sides earlier told Judge Eric Davis they had planned more than an hour opening arguments and court is scheduled to end today at 4.30pm. The trial had already been pushed back a day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The outlines of what rightwing House Republicans want in exchange for increasing the debt ceiling are becoming clear.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that Scott Perry, leader of the Freedom Caucus that includes some of the House\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative lawmakers, wants to repeal the Inflation Reduction Act \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s signature legislative achievement that also includes the strongest measures Congress has ever enacted against climate change:\par \par \uc2 enltrLeaving a meeting in Speaker McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s office, Freedom Caucus Chairman Scott Perry warned that the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s debt ceiling plan, \u8220\'20\'1Cif it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna pass, it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna have to\u8221\'20\'1D include a repeal of the Inflation Reduction Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Melanie Zanona (@MZanona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MZanona/status/1648394430506844161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox-Dominion trial opening statements delayed\par \par \uc2 Confusion is rampant in the packed courtroom, as opening statements were scheduled to start at 1.30pm after a lunch break, but still have not kicked off as of 2.40pm.\par \par \uc2 Court staff said they could not explain the delay. Attorneys for Fox and Dominion appeared to huddle with each other at least once, and the judge and jurors have not been seated.\par \par \uc2 Each party\u8217\'20\'19s opening statement is supposed to last around 90 minutes. With a 4.30pm recess today, there is no longer time for both parties to preview their evidence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs an update, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have an update,\u8221\'20\'1D a court staffer said to the overflow room of journalists, resulting in many laughs.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , one of the best known progressive Democrats in the House, has again condemned supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  for his ties to a Republican mega donor.\par \par \uc2 Thomas is a conservative stalwart on the court, but in recent days \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  revealed he had accepted luxury trips as well as a real estate deal from \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 , a deep-pocketed GOP supporter.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Ocasio-Cortez had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AOC}}}\uc2  (D-NY) hits \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  for not disclosing gifts and luxury trips from GOP donor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 "The justice is required by law to disclose something like that... If they want to live that kind of lifestyle, then they can resign from the court \u8212\'20\'14 they can retire." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SpdP1oVy2p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SpdP1oVy2p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648375250068049921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/10/senate-democrats-supreme-court-investigation-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have also demanded}}}\uc2  the supreme court investigate Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s ties.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for the opening arguments in the trial of \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defamation suit against Fox News, which is expected to start later this afternoon in Wilmington, Delaware, after the jury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643eaf638f08f991ea540946#block-643eaf638f08f991ea540946"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was seated}}}\uc2  this morning. Back in Washington, House Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-643ebae68f08610f35db71fd#block-643ebae68f08610f35db71fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are said to be}}}\uc2  nearing a vote on their proposal for raising the debt ceiling, but its chances of passage are uncertain.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643eaf3c8f08610f35db714c#block-643eaf3c8f08610f35db714c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown no inclination}}}\uc2  in helping Democrats replace ailing senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  on the judiciary committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643ea12e8f08f991ea540878#block-643ea12e8f08f991ea540878"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke last night with}}}\uc2 Ralph Yarl, the Black teenager shot after ringing the doorbell at the wrong house in Kansas City. Meanwhile, police arrested the alleged shooter following protests over the attack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/18/fox-news-dominion-defamation-trial-live-updates-us-politics?page=with:block-643ec1ad8f08610f35db725d#block-643ec1ad8f08610f35db725d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have filed}}}\uc2  their response before the supreme court, which is considering whether to uphold a Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone off shelves nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s finances could take another hit as the author E Jean Carroll\u8217\'20\'19s civil suit alleging defamation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/17/republicans-new-york-kevin-mccarthy-us-politics-live?page=with:block-643d77ed8f0846cd323c86c6#block-643d77ed8f0846cd323c86c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heads to trial}}}\uc2  later this month.\par \par \uc2 But the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t appear on the witness stand when the proceedings begin:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is currently not expected to take the stand at E Jean Caroll defamation and battery trial scheduled to start April 25, per person familiar\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1648366879793201162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes try to get drugs used in the procedure off the shelves, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  spoke to a New York doctor about a technique that could be used to expand reproductive care access:\par \par \uc2 Joan Fleischman has always had people flying in from across the world to her private \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  practice in Manhattan. In the two decades her clinic has been open, she has seen clients from places such as Ireland, the Bahamas and Mexico, who couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get abortions in their home countries. In the past year, that has changed. Since the US federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overturned in June last year, she is now more likely to see patients flying in from her own country.\par \par \uc2 Often they are from Texas, sometimes Ohio, or Florida. Some with links to the city, others with none.\par \par \uc2 After years of providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, Fleischman, 60, still finds these trips shocking. \u8220\'20\'1CUsually, if somebody needs unusual medical care, they are willing to fly around the world for it \u8211\'20\'13 like for advanced neurosurgery or something. It\u8217\'20\'19s always struck me as incredible that people are flying to me for the most simple procedure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason people fly to see Fleischman. She provides abortions through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://myanetwork.org/about-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 manual uterine aspiration}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 using a small, hand-held device to remove pregnancy tissue. The device is gentle enough that the tissue often comes out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2022/oct/18/pregnancy-weeks-abortion-tissue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  almost completely intact}}}\uc2 . It is a quick and discreet procedure where a patient might be in and out of the door in less than an hour.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/18/abortion-reproductive-rights-manual-uterine-aspiration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A gamechanger\u8217\'20\'19: this simple device could help fight the war on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups who convinced a federal judge to order mifepristone off the shelves have asked the supreme court to uphold the rulings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/anti-abortion-coalition-asks-supreme-court-restrict-mifepristone-rcna80090"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ruling earlier this month by conservative federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk has been stayed temporarily by the supreme court while it reviews petitions from the Biden administration and a manufacturer of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication to allow its continued access.\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports that the groups that originally brought a suit trying to revoke the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authorization of the pill have formally filed before the supreme court:\par \par \uc2 The groups, led by the Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine, said in a filing that the court should leave in place a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/appeals-court-partially-blocks-ruling-imperils-access-key-abortion-pil-rcna79144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling last week}}}\uc2  by the 5th US Circuit Court of Appeals that would suspend several regulatory decisions by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  since 2016 that made it easier to obtain the drug.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the groups wrote that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  over decades has \u8220\'20\'1Cstripped away every meaningful and necessary safeguard on chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , demonstrating callous disregard for women\u8217\'20\'19s well-being, unborn life, and statutory limits\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They dismissed the government\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csky-is-falling argument\u8221\'20\'1D about the implications of allowing the lower court ruling to go into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lower courts\u8217\'20\'19 meticulous decisions do not second-guess the agency\u8217\'20\'19s scientific determinations; they merely re- quire the agency to follow the law,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawyers wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 House GOP debt limit vote could come next week: report\par \par \uc2 House Republicans could as soon as next week vote on their proposal to raise the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s debt limit, while also cutting spending to a variety of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s priorities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/41823-punchbowl-news-am/?utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=4/18/23%20%20Punchbowl%20News%20AM&utm_term=Punchbowl%20AM%20and%20Active%20Subscribers%20from%20Memberful%20Combined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Punchbowl News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  has hit the legal limit on how much debt it can take on, and is expected to run out of money sometime in early June, which could cause it to default on its debt for the first time in history. That would have major negative ramifications for the economy, but the GOP lawmakers say they won\u8217\'20\'19t support increasing the debt ceiling without concessions from Democrats, such as spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 But House speaker Kevin McCarthy and his allies only control the chamber by a slim margin, and in a sign of how fraught the debt ceiling has become among Republicans, CNN reports at least one lawmaker won\u8217\'20\'19t vote to increase the debt limit at all:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Burchett, a Tennessee Republican, says he\u8217\'20\'19s still opposed to raising the debt limit, a sign of the challenges ahead for McCarthy to limit defections ahead of a possible vote next week. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m open to it but I\u8217\'20\'19m still a no vote.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4iGu9ZADul"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4iGu9ZADul}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1648350758784360453?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats in the White House and Senate, meanwhile, say they will only support a \u8220\'20\'1Cclean\u8221\'20\'1D debt ceiling increase that raises the limits without changes to spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was a brief hiccup in jury selection Tuesday morning in the closely watched Dominion v Fox defamation trial.\par \par \uc2 After the twelve jurors were sworn in, one of the jurors stood up and said he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do it. The judge and lawyers from both sides spoke with him out of court and he was dismissed. Another juror was quickly sworn in.\par \par \uc2 There were a few moments of levity in the packed Delaware courtroom.\par \par \uc2 At one point, judge Eric Davis told jurors that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t mind if they brought water or drinks in the court, as long as they had a lid. He quickly added \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-alcoholic\u8221\'20\'1D, prompting laughter.\par \par \uc2 There was also some laughing as jurors had to slide past one another as they were called into the jury box then excused. Some jurors arrived, had to shimmy down a row past all the other jurors, only to shimmy out moments later when they were excused.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s shift to Washington politics for a minute to examine the bind Senate Democrats are in. They may control the chamber, but they\u8217\'20\'19re having trouble confirming federal judges because of the absence of California senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 89-year-old is a member of the judiciary committee, but has been out of Washington to receive treatment for shingles, delaying crucial votes to move nominees through committees.\par \par \uc2 Last week, she asked to be temporarily replaced on the committee, but that would require the cooperation of at least some Republicans. In the clearest sign yet that the GOP won\u8217\'20\'19t go along, their leader in the Senate \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  today said he would oppose replacing her:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  argues against replacing Sen. \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  (D-CA) on Judiciary Committee, despite Feinstein requesting the removal herself:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe far left wants the full Senate to move a senator off a committee so they can ram through... their nominees.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZGwjvKevYj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZGwjvKevYj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1648338733480181768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Fox-Dominion defamation trial officially kicked off at 9 am in Delaware superior court and the 12 jurors who will determine whether Fox News acted with actual malice were seated roughly 90 minutes later.\par \par \uc2 The jury appears to be comprised of seven Black and five white or non-Black people. A set of 12 alternates were also seated for what\u8217\'20\'19s expected to be a six-week trial.\par \par \uc2 The jury selection comes after Judge Eric Davis delayed the start of the trial by one day. Either the two sides could not reach an agreement on Monday, or speculation that settlement talks were underway was untrue.\par \par \uc2 Opening arguments are set to begin after a short break. The judge and an attorney for Fox have already indicated that \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  has numerous objections to \uc2 Fox\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opening slides.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Fox-Dominion trial is now under way in Delaware, where CNBC reports the first witness will testify to his efforts to convince \uc2 Fox\uc2  that what they were broadcasting about the 2020 election was false:\par \par \uc2 enltrOne of the first witnesses we could see on the Dominion side of the \uc2 FOX\uc2  defamation case as soon as today is Tony Fratto - now head of communications for \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  who was an outside crisis communications consultant for Dominion in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eamon Javers (@EamonJavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EamonJavers/status/1648334571933499392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHe will testify about his real-time efforts in 2020 to convince Fox anchors and producers that the claims they were airing about Dominion were not true. That effort, clearly, was unsuccessful and led ultimately to the trial today.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eamon Javers (@EamonJavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EamonJavers/status/1648334575007854594?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 18, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is in Washington DC today, where he\u8217\'20\'19s expected to meet with Republican members of Congress as he nears a potential run for president. That would escalate his clash with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who remains the strongest challenger for the presidency in the Republican party. Before he departed for the capital, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports the governor made a new threat of retaliation against \uc2 Disney\uc2  for its criticism of his conservative policies:\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has unveiled the latest act of retaliation against \uc2 Disney\uc2  for speaking out against his \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law: he\u8217\'20\'19s threatening to build a new state prison next to the company\u8217\'20\'19s central Florida theme parks.\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor dropped the suggestion at a hastily convened Monday lunchtime press conference, at which he laid out steps the state legislature would take to try to regain control over Florida\u8217\'20\'19s largest private employer.\par \par \uc2 The move is the latest in an ongoing feud that began in March 2022 when \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s then chief executive \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2  spoke out against a bill limiting discussion of sexuality and gender identity in Florida elementary school classrooms, dubbed the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/02/dont-say-gay-florida-week-in-patriarchy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D law.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/ron-desantis-prison-near-disney-theme-park"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis threatens prison near Disney theme park in latest retaliation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday evening, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called Ralph Yarl, the Black teen shot in Kansas City after ringing the doorbell at the wrong address, and \u8220\'20\'1Cshared his hope for a swift recovery\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the incident and the shooter\u8217\'20\'19s arrest, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levin}}}\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 A white homeowner in Kansas City, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2 , has been charged with armed assault after he shot a Black teenager who rang his doorbell by mistake, authorities announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Lester, 85, is also facing a charge of armed criminal action after shooting Ralph Yarl, 16, twice on Thursday. The teenager, a high school junior, was going to pick up his younger twin brothers from a play date when he went to the wrong address. Zachary Thompson, the prosecuting attorney, announced the charges late on Monday after intense local protests and widespread outrage over the police\u8217\'20\'19s decision to briefly detain Lester before releasing him without charges.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/black-kansas-city-teen-shot-wrong-address"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Police charge white man for shooting Black teen boy who had wrong address}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Fox-Dominion trial was supposed to start on Monday, but was unexpectedly delayed \u8211\'20\'13 fueling speculation that the two sides were nearing a settlement that would forgo a trial. That apparently didn\u8217\'20\'19t pan out, but \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/marksweney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Sweney}}}\uc2  took a look at why settling might be in the conservative network\u8217\'20\'19s interest:\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/judge-delays-dominion-and-fox-news-trial-until-tuesday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push to try to bury a landmark defamation case against Fox News}}}\uc2  aims to avoid further damage to his media empire\u8217\'20\'19s reputation \u8211\'20\'13 and protect the 92-year-old from a gruelling court appearance as he formulates succession plans.\par \par \uc2 Judge Eric M Davis moved on Sunday to delay the start of the $1.6bn (\u163\'00\'A31.3bn) defamation trial between \uc2 Fox Corporation\uc2  and Dominion, which has alleged Fox News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/16/fox-news-lawsuit-dominion-trial-rupert-murdoch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly broadcast false claims that its voting machines were rigged}}}\uc2 , amid reports of a settlement.\par \par \uc2 However, the following day Davis confirmed the six-week trial would begin a day later than planned, with jury selection starting on Tuesday, after talks between the parties failed \u8211\'20\'13 for now at least.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/17/murdoch-settle-dominions-fox-news-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It avoids a public grilling\u8217\'20\'19: why Murdoch could settle Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s Fox News lawsuit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The two most important words in the Fox-Dominion trial: 'actual malice'\par \par \uc2 The defamation lawsuit filed by \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  against Fox News has already led to embarrassing revelations from inside the conservative network\u8217\'20\'19s newsroom, including that some of its top stars {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/08/tucker-carlson-hates-trump-capitol-footage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Chate\u8221\'20\'1D }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/08/tucker-carlson-hates-trump-capitol-footage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and did not believe his claims {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/mar/08/fox-news-dominion-lawsuit-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that the 2020 election was stolen}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But to get $1.6bn \u8211\'20\'13 or any sum \u8211\'20\'13 out of Fox for the harm it allegedly caused to its business, Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers will have to prove the network acted with \u8220\'20\'1Cactual malice\u8221\'20\'1D when it aired those falsehoods in the tense weeks following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  is in Wilmington, Delaware, where the trial is opening today, and breaks it all down here. Have a read:\par \par \uc2 The blockbuster $1.6bn defamation suit between \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  and \uc2 Fox\uc2  is set to begin on Tuesday in a courtroom in Wilmington, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delaware}}}\uc2 , opening a six-week tribunal that represents one of the most muscular efforts to hold the powerful news network accountable for its role in spreading lies about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Dominion is suing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  and its parent company \uc2 Fox Corporation\uc2  for knowingly spreading false claims about its equipment after the 2020 election. \uc2 Fox\uc2  repeatedly broadcast outlandishly false allegations that the company had paid government bribes, switched votes and was founded in Venezuela to rig elections for \uc2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The trial was scheduled to begin on Monday, but Eric Davis, the Delaware superior court judge overseeing the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/17/judge-delays-dominion-and-fox-news-trial-until-tuesday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed it back}}}\uc2  by a day without giving a reason. It was reported that both sides were engaged in negotiations over a settlement to avoid a trial.\par \par \uc2 Jury selection will be completed on Tuesday, followed by opening arguments.\par \par \uc2 The trial is likely to be a media frenzy. Rupert and \uc2 Lachlan Murdoch\uc2 , the top \uc2 Fox\uc2  executives, are expected to be called as witnesses. Fox News anchors \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/sean-hannity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean Hannity}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2  and Jeanine Pirro are expected to testify at the trial.\par \par \uc2 At the heart of Dominion\u8217\'20\'19s case is a trove of internal messages from \uc2 Fox\uc2  hosts and executives in which they openly say they knew the outlandish claims about Dominion were false. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  is lying, by the way. I caught her. It\u8217\'20\'19s insane,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson wrote in one such message, even as \uc2 Fox\uc2  continued to air Powell\u8217\'20\'19s claims about Dominion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the coming weeks, we will prove Fox spread lies causing enormous damage to Dominion. We look forward to trial,\u8221\'20\'1D a Dominion spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Defamation cases rarely go to trial because there is such a high bar a plaintiff has to clear to win. But experts observing the lawsuit say Dominion has put together an unusually strong case. The company may have strong enough evidence to show that \uc2 Fox\uc2  acted with \u8220\'20\'1Cactual malice\u8221\'20\'1D, that Fox knew the claims were false, or that \uc2 Fox\uc2  acted with reckless disregard for the truth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a rarity that we\u8217\'20\'19ll see something of this caliber play out in front of a jury,\u8221\'20\'1D said RonNell Andersen Jones, a first amendment scholar at \uc2 the University of Utah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News faces major test as Dominion defamation case goes to trial\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The biggest news this morning is happening in Wilmington, Delaware, where the defamation lawsuit filed by \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2  against Fox News is going to trial. Dominion, which makes hardware and software used in elections, is suing the conservative news outlet on claims it knowingly defamed its business in the aftermath of the 2020 election, when \uc2 Fox\uc2  was a leading conduit for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s unfounded conspiracy theories of vote rigging. Dominion wants the huge sum of $1.6bn for the damage caused, and the trial could see top \uc2 Fox\uc2  executives such as owner its \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  appear on the witness stand. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see what emerges from the courtroom today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is heading to Washington DC to meet with Republicans in Congress as he continues his slow, sure progress towards announcing a run for president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will deliver remarks on his efforts to lower childcare costs at 2pm ET. White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters at 2.45 pm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican-led House committee on the Covid-19 pandemic holds a hearing at 9.30am examining the origins of the virus and China\u8217\'20\'19s involvement.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230418ej4i0018q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
