\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Democratic senators condemn federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling to block  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drug\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 757 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2023\par 12:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmakers from New York, Minnesota and Wisconsin decry the ruling, now on hold by supreme court until at least 19 April\par \par \uc2 Top Democratic senators across the US are pushing back after a federal judge in Texas decided to block the \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, the New York senator Kirsten Gillibrand criticized as an \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage\u8221\'20\'1D Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which is currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/14/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-temporary-block"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted}}}\uc2  until at least Wednesday 19 April by the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/audio/podcasts/state-of-the-union-with-jake-tapper/episodes/5d0f2ec4-d122-49d7-9fb1-afe600f49c5e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 , Gillibrand said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo take away the right to have medicine is an extension of taking away this right to privacy, to say we can\u8217\'20\'19t have medicine sent by doctors by mail to people across the country is further invading into this right to privacy, where the court and government has a right to what\u8217\'20\'19s in your mail, and who you\u8217\'20\'19re talking to and what communications you\u8217\'20\'19re having. It\u8217\'20\'19s an outrage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She went on to condemn the supreme court, which in June 2022 decided to overturn Roe v Wade, a ruling that declared the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly half a century.\par \par \uc2 Gillibrand said the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision was an \u8220\'20\'1Call-out assault on women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we are seeing in these Republican legislatures as well as these very conservative courts is a continuation of that assault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the Minnesota senator Amy Klobuchar called Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision \u8220\'20\'1Cunbelievable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is going to be next? Is that judge going to not like birth control pills? Are we going to have a judge that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like [cholesterol medication] Lipitor? There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason that Congress gave the \uc2 FDA\uc2  the power to make these decisions about safety,\u8221\'20\'1D Klobuchar told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/ThisWeek/video/texas-abortion-pill-ruling-unbelievable-amy-klobuchar-98616121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can tell you who is harmed by this. It\u8217\'20\'19s women that are going to have to take a bus across the country from Texas to Minnesota or to Illinois. That\u8217\'20\'19s the problem right now,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, pledging to \u8220\'20\'1Caggressively litigate\u8221\'20\'1D the ruling if the supreme court decides to uphold it.\par \par \uc2 The Wisconsin senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , meanwhile, said that Kacsmaryk \u8220\'20\'1Cis not guided by science\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we have in Texas is a judge who is not guided by science, but is part of an extreme Republican concerted effort to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/texas-judge-part-gops-effort-ban-abortion-sen-baldwin-rcna79891"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  NBC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not need judges, politicians or government telling women about what sort of healthcare they can have. It is an issue that is not only playing out in the court in Texas, but in the state of Florida, with the governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signing}}}\uc2  a near six-week ban, Idaho forbidding travel out of state for minors, Wisconsin where we\u8217\'20\'19ve gone back to literally 1849. That is the date our criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was passed and that\u8217\'20\'19s 174 years ago,\u8221\'20\'1D Baldwin said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Baldwin and the Connecticut senator Richard Blumenthal, a Democrat, led the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.baldwin.senate.gov/news/press-releases/baldwin-blumenthal-lead-47-members-in-introducing-legislation-to-restore-and-protect-americans-right-to-an-abortion-nationwide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduction}}}\uc2  of the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act of 2023, which would safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide and \u8220\'20\'1Crestore the right to comprehensive reproductive healthcare for millions of Americans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Following Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, the justice department and the drug\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturer, Danco Laboratories, asked the supreme court to intervene in an attempt to halt the restrictions, which would have limited mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s use after seven weeks of pregnancy as well as ban mail delivery of the drug. Mifepristone is currently approved until 10 weeks.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  temporarily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/14/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-temporary-block"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  the Texas lower court ruling and instead imposed on to it a five-day stay, allowing the justices more time to decide on their next steps.\par \par \uc2 Alito\u8217\'20\'19s move allows for the country\u8217\'20\'19s most common method of pregnancy termination to remain unchanged until at least the end of Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Despite nationwide outrage from progressive lawmakers and reproductive rights activists, conservative lawmakers have defended the growing wave of various \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/concerns-texas-ruling-upending-fda-authority-are-alarmist-cassidy-rcna79922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  on Sunday with NBC, the Republican senator \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  of Louisiana said reactions to the Texas ruling were \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally alarmist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s totally alarmist. And by the way, when did the \uc2 FDA\uc2  think they could go above the law?\u8221\'20\'1D Cassidy said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CDobbs, I think, was the correct decision,\u8221\'20\'1D in reference to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights last year.\par \par \uc2 Cassidy\u8217\'20\'19s comments come two days after Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/florida-six-week-abortion-ban-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  into law a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban across the state, which previously had a 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230416ej4g001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
