\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They created this\u8217\'20\'19: are Republicans willing to lose elections to retain their  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  stance?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 1,620 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par 19:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The right has, for decades, relied on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rally their conservative base, but now their unified policy is flagging\par \par \uc2 Democrats have taken multiple actions in response to what they say is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/08/abortion-pill-mifepristone-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdraconian\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  decision by a federal judge in Texas threatening access to the most commonly used method of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic governors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/11/democratic-governors-stockpile-abortion-drugs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begun to stockpile}}}\uc2  doses of the drugs used in medication abortions. Nearly every Democrat in Congress signed onto an amicus brief urging an appeals court to stay the decision, while some called on the Biden administration to simply \u8220\'20\'1Cignore\u8221\'20\'1D the ruling, should it be allowed to stand. A group of House Democrats introduced a bill that would give the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) final approval over drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Their fury over the ruling has been met with relative silence from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Only a handful of congressional Republicans offered immediate comment on judge Matthew Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision last week to revoke the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 23-year-old approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone. Just a fraction of Republicans on Capitol Hill signed an amicus brief urging an appeals court to uphold the ruling. And among the party\u8217\'20\'19s national field of Republican presidential nominees, just one \u8211\'20\'13 the former vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 unabashedly praised the decision.\par \par \uc2 The starkly different reactions underscores just how dramatically the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have shifted since last June, when conservatives achieved their once-unimaginable goal of overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Republicans relied on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rally their conservative base, calling for the reversal of Roe v Wade and vowing to outlaw the procedure if given the chance. But since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has emerged as a potent issue for Democrats, galvanizing voters furious over the thicket of state bans and restrictions ushered in by the decision.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have struggled to respond, lacking a unified policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the nearly 10 months since the landmark decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDobbs really did get Republicans, especially elected Republicans, running scared,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jon Schweppe, policy director at the conservative American Principles Project.\par \par \uc2 Polling has consistently found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/abortion-attitudes-in-a-post-roe-world-findings-from-the-50-state-2022-american-values-atlas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a clear majority}}}\uc2  of Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain legal in all or most cases, though partisan divisions have deepened over the years. A new survey released by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2023/04/11/by-more-than-two-to-one-americans-say-medication-abortion-should-be-legal-in-their-state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2  this week showed that by a margin of more than 2 to 1, Americans believe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is at the center of the current legal battle, should be legal in their state.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Let the states work this out\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A post-Dobbs backlash fueled a string of victories for abortions rights, including in more conservative states, and powered Democratic victories in last year\u8217\'20\'19s November midterm elections. And this month, just days before the Texas ruling on mifepristone, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were a dominant force in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results-janet-protasiewicz-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liberal judge\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  landslide victory in a key race for a Wisconsin supreme court seat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that GOP candidates are scared to tie themselves to a decision that is wildly out of step with what voters want,\u8221\'20\'1D Mini Timmaraju, the president of Naral Pro-Choice American told reporters this week. \u8220\'20\'1CThey can\u8217\'20\'19t be eager to repeat last week\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Daniel_Kelly_(Wisconsin)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 double-digit}}}\uc2  walloping of extremist judicial candidate, Dan Kelly, in Wisconsin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In that race, Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s opponent, judge Janet Protasiewicz, had effectively promised voters that if she won, flipping the ideological balance of the court from conservative to liberal, the new majority would overturn Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s 1849 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople understood the stakes and they were ready to vote for Judge Protasiewicz,\u8221\'20\'1D said Timmaraju, whose group was active in the contest.\par \par \uc2 Now, with the 2024 presidential election looming, an increasingly vocal group of Republicans are urging moderation on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warning that the uncompromising positions of their party\u8217\'20\'19s culturally conservative base risk alienating crucial swing voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an issue that Republicans have been largely on the wrong side of,\u8221\'20\'1D congresswoman Nancy Mace, a Republican from South Carolina, said in a recent appearance on CNN.\par \par \uc2 Mace, who considers herself \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, said her party had \u8220\'20\'1Cnot shown compassion towards women\u8221\'20\'1D since the fall of Roe. She has urged flexibility, pushing Republicans to expand access to contraception and include exceptions for abortions in cases of rape, incest or when the life of the mother is at risk or the fetus is no longer viable.\par \par \uc2 Since June, Republican-led legislatures have charged ahead with new restrictions. More than a dozen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/state-policy/explore/state-policies-later-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/dec/13/abortion-restrictions-us-state-legislatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with several other}}}\uc2  Republican-led state legislatures considering new restrictions this session.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Florida legislature voted to prohibit abortions after six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before many women realize they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 delivering a major policy victory for the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Hours later, DeSantis, who is widely expected to run for president in 2024, quietly signed the ban into law with little fanfare, underscoring just how complicated the issue has become for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 In Nebraska, the state legislature is in the process of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-nebraska-4b23b7c3531b12f303cc0e175239accd#:~:text=(AP)%20%E2%80%94%20Nebraska%20lawmakers%20advanced,even%20know%20they%20are%20pregnant."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debating a six-week ban}}}\uc2 . But even in the reliably conservative state, some Republican lawmakers are floating an alternative that would expand the window to 12 weeks, a sign that a ban any earlier in pregnancy could stoke public outcry.\par \par \uc2 One option floated as a politically palatable \u8220\'20\'1Ccompromise\u8221\'20\'1D is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/4840/cosponsors?s=7&r=4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal}}}\uc2  by South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  that would implement a federal ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 But the legislation divided Republicans and ultimately only attracted a handful of co-sponsors when he introduced it last year ahead of the midterms. Several Republicans, including the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , argued that limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be set by the states.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he supported Graham\u8217\'20\'19s proposal, Senator Tim Scott, a Republican from South Carolina who this week formed an exploratory committee for a 2024 presidential run, said was \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1646261339361361921?cxt=HHwWgoC-wej92NgtAAAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined}}}\uc2  to answer the question directly. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/politicongress/status/1646534465055780864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarified}}}\uc2  later that he would back a federal ban at 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador who is running for the nomination, urged Republicans to seek consensus on the issue, asserting that she was \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D but did not \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge anyone who is pro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s let the states work this out,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/elections/presidential/caucus/2023/04/12/nikki-haley-courts-women-voters-talks-abortion-in-iowa-campaign-stop/70089341007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Des Moines Register}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIf Congress decides to do it \u8211\'20\'13 but don\u8217\'20\'19t get in that game of them saying \u8216\'20\'18how many weeks, how many\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 no. Let\u8217\'20\'19s first figure out what we agree on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has sought to position himself as a reliable ally of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, hoping his support of a six-week ban will appeal to social conservatives searching for an alternative to Trump in the early-voting states Iowa and South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Trump, whose conservative supreme court appointees enabled Roe to be struck down, angered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents when he warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a political liability for Republicans and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/3796452-anti-abortion-group-fires-back-after-trump-comments-about-the-midterms/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed}}}\uc2  extremism on the issue for their lackluster performance in the 2022 midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Ostrich strategy\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In the escalating legal battle over access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  on Friday temporarily halted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/mifepristone-abortion-pill-to-remain-available-in-us-with-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal appeals court ruling}}}\uc2  that would have reimposed restrictions on mifepristone. The stay will expire on Wednesday while the court deliberate next steps.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates say the ongoing threat to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide makes clear that Republicans never actually believed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an issue best handled by the states, as Alito wrote in his 2022 decision overturning the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are seeking a nationwide ban \u8211\'20\'13 but they are not going to stop there,\u8221\'20\'1D Jennifer Dalven, director of the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  Reproductive Freedom Project, told reporters this week. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are already seeing attacks on birth control.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a starting point, Schweppe believes social conservatives must be willing to compromise on a federal ban, possibly accepting legislation that falls well short of their long-held goal to end all abortions. He urged Republicans to adopt positions that are broadly popular with wide swaths of voters, including allowances for pregnancies that result from rape or incest, or when the health or life of the mother is at risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be honest about where the fault lines lie,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CExceptions are what drives voter sentiment. That\u8217\'20\'19s what Democrats are attacking us on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many leading \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents blame recent losses on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 embrace of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/20/republicans-abortion-march-for-life-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so-called \u8220\'20\'1Costrich strategy\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 avoiding the topic or trying to change the subject \u8211\'20\'13 not their opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans have cowered in fear as the consultants and campaign advisors tell them not to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Penny Young Nance, the chief executive and president of evangelical Christian group, Concerned Women for America. In the Wisconsin supreme court race, she said the conservative\u8217\'20\'19s defeat was an example of what happens when Republicans are badly outspent and fail to \u8220\'20\'1Cboldly\u8221\'20\'1D defend their position on an issue that has been a defining policy of American conservatism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe winning strategy is to tell the truth about the left\u8217\'20\'19s extremist position on the issue that is out of [sync] with the views of the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Nance said in an email.\par \par \uc2 As Republicans search for a path forward, Democrats, confident public opinion is on their side, are already preparing to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central theme of the coming election cycles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven though some in the GOP are trying to stay quiet about the Texas ruling, back home they\u8217\'20\'19re still passing and signing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D Timmaraju said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey created this reality,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CThey cannot run away from it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230415ej4f000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
