\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Popularity is optional as Republicans find ways to impose minority rule\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,609 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par 08:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s party\u8217\'20\'19s signature policies enjoy only meagre public support but rightwing judges and state legislators are proving adept at finding workarounds\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe called for you all to ban assault weapons, and you respond with an assault on democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D These were the words of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1644055892822827010?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Jones}}}\uc2 , a Black Democrat, to Tennessee Republicans after he and a colleague, Justin Pearson, were expelled for leading a gun protest on the state house of representatives floor.\par \par \uc2 A week later, Jones and Pearson were reinstated amid applause, whoops and cheers at the state capitol in Nashville. But few believe that the assault on democracy is at an end. What happened in Tennessee is seen as indicative of a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -led Republican party ready to push its extremist agenda by any means necessary.\par \par \uc2 Opinion poll after opinion poll shows that Republicans are increasingly out of touch with mainstream sentiment on hot button issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and gun safety. Accordingly, the party has suffered disappointment in elections in 2018, 2020 and 2022. Yet instead of rethinking its positions, critics say, it is turning to rightwing judges and state legislators to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/05/american-democracy-threat-republicans-donald-trump-voter-suppression"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enforce minority rule}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhh.umn.edu/directory/larry-jacobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Jacobs}}}\uc2 , director of the Center for the Study of Politics and Governance at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe ballot box didn\u8217\'20\'19t work \u8211\'20\'13 the voice of the people said, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to tolerate these kind of threats by Republicans. But Republicans are using other tools and shredding the fabric of American democracy . It\u8217\'20\'19s a kind of minority authoritarianism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite extraordinary pressures, democracy has proved resilient in recent years. It survived an insurrection at the US Capitol on 6 January 2021. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was sworn in as the duly elected president and declared in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2021/01/20/inaugural-address-by-president-joseph-r-biden-jr/#:~:text=The%20will%20of%20the%20people,my%20friends%2C%20democracy%20has%20prevailed."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his inaugural address}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy has prevailed.\u8221\'20\'1D And election deniers were routed in last year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 But while Democrats control the White House and Senate, Republicans have proved expert at finding workarounds, using cogs in the machine that have typically received less attention from activists, journalists and voters. One of them is the judiciary.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court, which includes three justices appointed during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s single term, last year overturned the Roe v Wade ruling that had enshrined the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly half a century, despite opinion polls showing a majority wanted to protect it.\par \par \uc2 Lower courts have also flexed their muscles. Matthew Kacsmaryk, a judge nominated by Trump in Amarillo, Texas, has ruled against the \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administration on issues including immigration and LGBTQ+ protections. Earlier this month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/08/texas-judge-kacsmaryk-abortion-pills-ruling-anti-abortion-rhetoric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he blocked}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone, the most common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  method in America.\par \par \uc2 A legal battle ensued with the justice department pledging to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/mifepristone-abortion-pill-to-remain-available-in-us-with-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take its appeal}}}\uc2  all the way to the supreme court. The political backlash was also swift.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/person/mini-timmaraju/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mini Timmaraju}}}\uc2 , the president of Naral Pro-Choice America, said: \u8220\'20\'1COne extremist judge appointed by a twice impeached, now-indicted former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was attempting to effectively ban medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. The decision is a prime example of minority rule at its worst. These extremists will not stop until they control our reproductive health decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling by \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  shows that two-thirds of Americans believe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should remain legal, including 84% of Democrats, 67% of independents and 49% of Republicans. Timmaraju added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s obvious that anti-choice extremists and lawmakers are out of step with Americans. It\u8217\'20\'19s really worth remembering how far out of step they are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If judges fall short of the Republican wishlist, state governors have shown willingness to intervene. In Texas, Greg Abbott has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/texas-governor-seeks-pardon-man-convicted-murder-black-lives-matter-shooting-2023-04-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will pardon}}}\uc2  an \uc2 Uber\uc2  driver convicted of murder in the July 2020 shooting of a man at a Black Lives Matter protest in downtown Austin, the state capital.\par \par \uc2 The case hinged on whether the shooting was in self-defence. A jury found that Perry, who is white, shot and killed Garrett Foster, a 28-year-old white man, who was carrying an AK-47, according to the Austin American-Statesman newspaper. Abbott tweeted that he will pardon Daniel Perry, 37, an army sergeant, as soon as a request from the parole board \u8220\'20\'1Chits my desk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year Abbott also led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.click2houston.com/news/local/2023/03/15/tea-to-take-over-houston-isd-after-weeks-of-speculation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a state takeover of Houston\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  public school district, the eighth biggest in the country with nearly 200,000 students, infuriating Democrats who condemned the move as politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 In Florida another Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/florida-man"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has centralised power}}}\uc2  as he assails gun safety and voting rights, the teaching of gender and race in schools and major corporations such as \uc2 Disney\uc2 . On Thursday he signed a bill to ban most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In this he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/18/ron-desantis-florida-republican-supermajority-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed by a supermajority}}}\uc2  in the Florida state legislature. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/30/republicans-radical-extreme-state-parties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State governments}}}\uc2 , which receive less and less scrutiny as local newspapers go extinct, are another key weapon in the Republican arsenal. In deep red states they have imposed near or total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , loosened gun restrictions, curbed LGBTQ+ and voting rights and endorsed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Race\par \par \uc2 Minority rule is, more than anything, about race. Whereas white Christians made up 54% of the population when Barack Obama was first running for president in 2008, they now make up only 44%.\par \par \uc2 Activists point to Republican-dominated state governments pushing legislation that would allow them to control Black-led cities and push hardline policies on crime. Examples include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=dOOQzUBvOXAxCaULtariHaVaygIaCeF80y-2BrpEanftdJLXcFpuPimohRnGN9fnVQI7qcyVHspj0jMO5PkHN7bT1atNtgOs-2FVsM-2FzauxH7U14HKvA2vMxGWXtIaAqDCulZPMPHvGpC3Y2d01-2B342FuxdPbFQzaMuzbqjULZawuVg-3Do6g0_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23dztoAT9Kx65j-2FLzJh3gs46qWBHX491YTlrqXDe8-2FdwfcL8I-2B-2FlH-2FZsb0BgxxkRBvbdyaOk4aAcyagoefx3IRngzfWn39knd6MjjAAe9wfyZvJcTm6wAzIu9QZ4LGr-2BJX6W2ojMGFri9r8VCQwPIKN1vJvmkxL2g9qsPROFRs4-2FvPiqRdTxFXPV7l8RBKSSGsatgp5e-2Fw1x-2FCVyG3sxoJykTe07RHlaeHCQ-2BzglFRVsLs-2FNJ4x0DWL3JY9sR-2BcctiuRqmEGtjQR06OA6m-2FITwHG3CuL4wn-2FYYsLxhVaMQ-2Ff80WCS4bOKQlxrjB3JLTkeBPsP31Oqi3755G-2FH6jCLjYUpPHeI0Kd35-2F2TWnwuC-2FD8d-2B4XXHjc-2Fa4JtyB56IVCR0g-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding the jurisdiction}}}\uc2  of state police in Jackson, Mississippi, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=dOOQzUBvOXAxCaULtariHckvixptOKz5UZ4zOC8nCOOIe2wyBy8F8HWnE1rzDra8IyR4JGM2N0Qzd4-2FgDHIbYsTGBsI72xKmHMHxSj4qoB0ivgtISIoD6RC1iTV-2FbSIdaltH6-2Bm9KOhpVKo0LiQv-2Fg-3D-3DZZxx_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23dztoAT9Kx65j-2FLzJh3gs46qWBHX491YTlrqXDe8-2FdwfcL8I-2B-2FlH-2FZsb0BgxxkRBvbdyaOk4aAcyagoefx3IRngzfWn39knd6MjjAAe9wfyZvJcTm6wAzIu9QZ4LGr-2BJX6W2ojMGFri9r8VCQwPIKN1vJvmkxL2g9qsPROFRs4-2FvPiqRdTxFXPV7l8RBKSSGsatgp5e-2Fw1x-2FCVyG3sxoJykRtcaY99N91c78jOM3jvRUqZg57zYU5k4KNdthEaFbBHLpWi38tLlKeFz-2FgKXFPwLmaLjYn1Yp-2Fv5vrPB-2BzT-2BRtiGNUbNiAdpYaQPw-2BPOFHUwE-2FmAtOgt3dZhqBTZANQ2a9h4jlcn9WSHEyNR6L9T-2FN96aiL35Kxtysibch4YZ40Q-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removing local control}}}\uc2  of the St Louis police department in Missouri. Republicans in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  itself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=dOOQzUBvOXAxCaULtariHZ2CPPOpJgCCTV-2FaylZBDxPUr3xjmpnSH7l6fT1nLPTWbLRPec63G76ToSUfmd1iWJft90KZ-2Bmiz9XKoHUdH7kVqzAMTIDy-2FedR12qYlkergqFyK_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23dztoAT9Kx65j-2FLzJh3gs46qWBHX491YTlrqXDe8-2FdwfcL8I-2B-2FlH-2FZsb0BgxxkRBvbdyaOk4aAcyagoefx3IRngzfWn39knd6MjjAAe9wfyZvJcTm6wAzIu9QZ4LGr-2BJX6W2ojMGFri9r8VCQwPIKN1vJvmkxL2g9qsPROFRs4-2FvPiqRdTxFXPV7l8RBKSSGsatgp5e-2Fw1x-2FCVyG3sxoJykSGCF-2Fo3igC1AmzfF98QHrDtZs5XoP8gFT9arr7cD17UjWx-2F0auy0lb8kYpEaKuYi8Sj7C73wTVFqINGP4DGpiqy4vD9f0Ba-2FuKqGCczM0EbfNTw6U7giYnJxV6jndGAwXtzImiqFLFbTPmY01uy6AFNI0Iqwdv3JukjZSNwrbLvA-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned police reform}}}\uc2  in Washington DC.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.mediaoutreach.meltwater.com/ls/click?upn=dOOQzUBvOXAxCaULtariHcchHUd-2Bi9FMKcXz13gNDQfzPI9qoaf8apRE5feYdynOPchcVdmeIhk0b-2FXfHIBxGw-3D-3Dwr-c_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23dztoAT9Kx65j-2FLzJh3gs46qWBHX491YTlrqXDe8-2FdwfcL8I-2B-2FlH-2FZsb0BgxxkRBvbdyaOk4aAcyagoefx3IRngzfWn39knd6MjjAAe9wfyZvJcTm6wAzIu9QZ4LGr-2BJX6W2ojMGFri9r8VCQwPIKN1vJvmkxL2g9qsPROFRs4-2FvPiqRdTxFXPV7l8RBKSSGsatgp5e-2Fw1x-2FCVyG3sxoJykSsGr9SzSKs5yUIV-2Fq3vwVBugG1ndn3GpuEa3FrXBz41PxD2guqqpkxtXgOeKm9plaUZ-2FDabVsiHPAe5zzJZ1mZz5DYxmBX90iCXYT0yv8BWJFLb9WfU-2Ffe6zwbaV8kCPYVhExz-2BwDJWLNAzAkvZF-2F9J06iSM3-2BPA0kPiv9OUXiXg-3D-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Makia Green}}}\uc2 , a lead strategist for the Movement for Black Lives, said: \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of it is not only taking away the people we sent to speak for us \u8211\'20\'13 to make sure that our voices are heard and that we are part of the process \u8211\'20\'13 but also to overwhelm Black voters, to instil apathy in Black voters so that it feels like, \u8216\'20\'18I went out, I voted, I did what I had to do, and they took the power away from me, so why should I show up next year?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Green, co-founder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harrietsdreams.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harriet\u8217\'20\'19s Wildest Dreams}}}\uc2 , a Black community organisation in the Washington area, added: \u8220\'20\'1COur democracy has holes in it, especially with the record number of attacks on voting rights and civic education. Republican and rightwing extremists have been making it harder and harder for our people to vote and so people are questioning, do I still live in a democracy?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then there was Tennessee where, on 6 April, Republicans sparked national outrage by kicking out Jones and Pearson, two young Black Democrats, as punishment for breaking rules of decorum a week earlier by leading a protest inside the house chamber. The demonstration was prompted by a March school shooting in Nashville in which three children, three adults and the attacker were killed.\par \par \uc2 Just as on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Republicans are demonstrably at odds with public opinion on gun safety. A poll last year by the University of Chicago Harris School of Public Policy and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research}}}\uc2  shows 71% of Americans say gun laws should be stricter, including about half of Republicans, the vast majority of Democrats and a majority of those in gun-owning households.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/importantmeagan?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Meagan Hatcher-Mays}}}\uc2 , director of democracy policy at the progressive movement Indivisible, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s never the situation that the GOP moderates their position on something. It\u8217\'20\'19s always a reflexive pivot to attacking and undermining democracy and that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what they did in this situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Hatcher-Mays added: \u8220\'20\'1C If there\u8217\'20\'19s any silver lining to the way that the GOP behaves it\u8217\'20\'19s that they can\u8217\'20\'19t hide forever from the bad and unpopular things that they do. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long been struggling against demographic headwinds and political trends. They have lost the national popular vote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/democrats-popular-vote-win-d6331f7e8b51d52582bb2d60e2a007ec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven of the last eight}}}\uc2  presidential elections. They suffered another reminder of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s potency when a Democratic-backed Milwaukee judge won a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-abortion-trump-81e311c9d0416d4a04489ad7a38c134d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin supreme court race}}}\uc2  with the fate of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the line.\par \par \uc2 Republicans remain competitive in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the body that approves nominated judges \u8211\'20\'13 because small, predominantly white states get two seats each, carrying as much weight as vast, racially diverse ones. In 2018 David Leonhardt of the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/10/14/opinion/dc-puerto-rico-statehood-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calculated that the Senate}}}\uc2  gives the average Black American only 75% as much representation as the average white American, and the average Hispanic American only 55% as much.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kurtbardella"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kurt Bardella}}}\uc2 , a Democratic strategist, noted that the government was founded with checks and balances to ensure that minority viewpoints could be heard. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it was not the intent of the framers and founders to have those minority views imposed on the majority and certainly not to have those in the minority attack the rule of law to try to unravel majority rule, which is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening right now. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get more anti-democratic than expelling members from a legislative body for expressing themselves in a constitutionally protected way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are inflicting injury and harm on democracy. It\u8217\'20\'19s a continuation of what they started to do with the big lie [that the 2020 election was stolen] \u8230\'20\'26 which paved the way for an insurrectionist attempt. We\u8217\'20\'19re seeing other extreme iterations of that play out in individual states. When you have a minority of people exercising power over the majority, that\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarianism .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Additional reporting by Lauren Gambino\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230415ej4f000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
