\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice blocks ruling that limits  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 3,169 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par 21:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Temporary pause on lower court rulings gives court additional time to consider a longer staySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, New Jersey Congressman Josh Gottheimer introduced new legislation: the freedom to decide act, a bill that, if passed, would protect prescriptions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills issued across state lines.\par \par \uc2 Endorsed by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , Naral Pro-Choice America, the \uc2 National Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center\uc2  (NWLC), and the Center for Reproductive Rights, the bill is intended to codify access across the country, and ensure that states like California can continue to act as so-called \u8220\'20\'1Csafe havens\u8221\'20\'1D that issue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care from afar. The state recently secured a stockpile of 2m \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in response to the ruling to block mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, I'm leading and introducing the Freedom to Decide Act w/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJasmine?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepJasmine}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAngieCraig?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepAngieCraig}}}\uc2  to protect doctor-prescribed access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone & to support telemedicine across state lines.\par \par \uc2 Endorsed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPact?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PPact}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NARAL?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NARAL}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nwlc?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NWLC}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReproRights?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ReproRights}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 read our bill here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tKWicRGrqE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tKWicRGrqE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep Josh Gottheimer (@RepJoshG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJoshG/status/1646963883544834048?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe freedom to decide act affirms what we all know,\u8221\'20\'1D Gottheimer wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  announcing the bill. \u8220\'20\'1CAccess to mifepristone does not violate federal law and it is essential to protecting the fundamental right for all women to make personal, private health care decisions about their own bodies, lives, and futures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Highlighting that the pill has been available for more than 2 decades and circulates in roughly 80 countries, the legislators behind the bill emphasized its safety record even when prescribed via telemedicine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ruling from Alito, a conservative justice, has ensured access to the drug will continue \u8211\'20\'13 for now. Set to be pulled from the shelves at midnight tonight, the drug will continue to be available until another order from the supreme court comes through.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll this essentially stops the clock this weekend,\u8221\'20\'1D Chuck Todd of Meet the Press said, explaining that it will essentially shut down both the stay and the original Texas ruling for the time being. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it still could go into effect at a later point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alito also wrote last year\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access up to individual states, eliminating rights established by the Roe v Wade decision. Since then, 12 US states have banned abortions while several others added new limits.\par \par \uc2 You can read more about the ruling here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/14/abortion-pill-ruling-supreme-court-temporary-block"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court temporarily blocks ruling limiting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 We are wrapping up this evening but as always you can find the latest news and analysis on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For now, here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of what we covered today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has temporarily blocked lower court rulings that limit access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, giving the court 5 days to consider emergency requests from the Biden administration, department of justice, and pill manufacturer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rep. Josh Gottheimer introduced new legislation that would codify access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill when prescribed, even via telehealth appointments. If passed, the bill would help ensure safe-haven states could administer care across state lines.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harrismentioned the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida while speaking at the National Action Network annual conference in New York today. While delivering her keynote address, the vice president noted that several civil rights are \u8220\'20\'1Cunder attack\u8221\'20\'1D, listing out Florida\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban as an example.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration and department of justice asked the supreme court to stop limits from lower courts on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill as the government seeks to defend the drug against attacks from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and Republican legislators.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill manufacturer Danco Laboratories asked the supreme court to intervene in attempts to restrict the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed off on a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida. Florida\u8217\'20\'19s most recent ban will only take effect if the state\u8217\'20\'19s current 15-week ban is upheld before its supreme court, which has a conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for reading our live blog. Have a good night!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court temporarily blocks lower court ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has temporarily blocked lower court rulings that limit access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Alito implemented a five-day hold on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that came after a ruling by a federal judge in Texas.\par \par \uc2 The temporary pause on lower court rulings give the court additional time to consider the fate of the drug amid arguments from the Biden administration and drug manufacturer.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Alito puts five-day hold on new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill restrictions. Administrative stay gives \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  more time to consider longer delay. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6h84eLAvXu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6h84eLAvXu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Stohr (@GregStohr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GregStohr/status/1646963369327448077?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor is scheduled to sign a number of bills on Friday that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the healthcare access for transgender people.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2  will sign several laws that enshrine access to abortions, gender-affirming care, and other rights that are under attack by conservative legislators nationwide, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-transgender-colorado-law-0ac4525f076692b479c9c16f3a1f72b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The passage of these bills in Colorado would also help those traveling from more restrictive states, including Oklahoma, Utah, and Wyoming, which are border Colorado.\par \par \uc2 Wyoming and Oklahoma have passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans; Utah has banned gender-affirming care for minors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Scott\u8217\'20\'19s comments from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Joan Greve.\par \par \uc2 Scott, who is wrapping up a swing through early voting states, would not specify his preferred time frame for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to talk about six or five or seven or ten [weeks],\u8221\'20\'1D Scott said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just saying that whatever the most conservative legislation is that can come through Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Scott\u8217\'20\'19s comments come just after Republican Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is expected to soon announce his own presidential bid, approved a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Pressed by Vitali on whether a six-week ban is the appropriate policy, Scott replied, \u8220\'20\'1CThe people have decided that their elected leaders have the opportunity to do so. So I say absolutely. As the culture of life is being protected, we should celebrate that. States will have different varying views on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 After launching an exploratory committee for a 2024 presidential run, South Carolina senator Tim Scott has vowed to pass restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits if elected president.\par \par \uc2 When asked about his view on federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections on Friday, Scott replied: \u8220\'20\'1CIf I were president of the United States, I would literally sign the most conservative, pro-life legislation that they can get through Congress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From Semafor reporter Shelby Talcott:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIf I were president of the United States, I would literally sign the most conservative, pro-life legislation that they can get through Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D Sen. Tim Scott said in S.C. today:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DYPN1Z4Vxi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DYPN1Z4Vxi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shelby Talcott (@ShelbyTalcott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShelbyTalcott/status/1646942400181424128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 US vice president slams latest attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  mentioned the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida while speaking at the National Action Network annual conference in New York today.\par \par \uc2 While delivering her keynote address, the vice president noted that several civil rights are \u8220\'20\'1Cunder attack\u8221\'20\'1D, listing out Florida\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban as an example.\par \par \uc2 From Bloomberg correspondent Akayla Gardner:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2 , speaking at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NationalAction?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NationalAction}}}\uc2 , says the country is in \u8220\'20\'1Ca moment in which our hard-won freedoms are under attack,\u8221\'20\'1D listing Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restriction, voting rights, books bans and LGBTQ rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Akayla Gardner (@gardnerakayla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gardnerakayla/status/1646920124710936620?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris has spoken out strongly on the latest wave of attacks on reproductive rights underway from right-wing America, especially since the conservative-dominated supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last June in the Dobbs case out of Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala D. Harris\uc2  speaks at the National Action Network (NAN) conference at the Sheraton Hotel 2023 National Action Network (NAN) Convention, Day 3, New York. Photograph: Erik Pendzich/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 A day after signing the six-week ban on abortions, DeSantis spoke at \uc2 Liberty University\uc2 , a Christian college.\par \par \uc2 But the Florida governor did not mention the legislation in his speech.\par \par \uc2 From \uc2 CBS\uc2  political reporter Aaron Navarro:\par \par \uc2 enltrAt \uc2 Liberty University\uc2 , a notable evangelical institution in Virginia, Florida Gov. DeSantis did not bring up the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban he signed late last night.\par \par \uc2 Campus pastor Johnathan Falwell brought it up in his intro, to applause. But nothing from DeSantis himself (cont.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 aaron navarro (@aaronlarnavarro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aaronlarnavarro/status/1646919390749683713?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"Last night, after the legislature there in Florida passed the bill, he signed the Heartbeat Protection act. And as he signed that into the law in the state of Florida, it will protect all unborn babies because he recognizes and knows that life is a gift from god," Falwell said.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 aaron navarro (@aaronlarnavarro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aaronlarnavarro/status/1646919392150650880?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s request to the supreme court to block lower court limitations on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill from Mary Tuma for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration appealed to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  on Friday asking it to halt an appellate ruling that adds onerous restrictions to a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug. The restrictions were slated to go into effect at 12.01am on Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 The ruling at the center of the emergency application to the high court was issued on Wednesday night by the fifth circuit court of appeals. The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  had asked the appeals court to block a lower court order revoking the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approval of mifepristone in 2000.\par \par \uc2 The Louisiana-based appellate court \u8211\'20\'13 considered one of the most conservative in the US \u8211\'20\'13 blocked part of that order, but allowed other parts to stand, and temporarily reimposed restrictions on the drug that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  had lifted starting in 2016.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf allowed to take effect, the lower courts\u8217\'20\'19 orders would thwart \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s scientific judgment and undermine widespread reliance in a healthcare system that assumes the availability of mifepristone as an alternative to more burdensome and invasive surgical abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote the solicitor general, \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , in the filing.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/14/abortion-pill-supreme-court-biden-administration-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration asks US supreme court to halt \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Danco Laboratories has said that they will continue to distribute the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, according to an email from the company.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported that the company emailed a statement confirming that they will still continue to dispense Mifeprex to its customers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The majority of Americans do not support restrictive bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 72% of Americans oppose \u8220\'20\'1Claws that make it illegal to use or receive through the mail \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drugs for a medical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a survey by the nonpartisan Public religion research institute.\par \par \uc2 62% are against six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or bans around when a fetus\u8217\'20\'19 heartbeat is detected.\par \par \uc2 52% of Americans are opposed to restrictions on abortions after 15-weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signing a six-week ban on abortions may have political consequences ahead of his rumored presidential run, reports Politico.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis backing the near-total ban could rally some Republican voters, especially in what is expected to be a packed 2024 presidential candidate race.\par \par \uc2 But enacting a total ban could bring political trouble and weaken support for DeSantis amid any voters who see such harsh abortions restrictions as too far.\par \par \uc2 From Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Sally Goldenberg and Alice Miranda Ollstein:\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is banking on support in the primary from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters, particularly those angry at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8230\'20\'26 But a six-week ban pushes the outer boundary of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights proposals. And it could spell trouble for DeSantis among independents and suburban voters in a general election, if he makes it that far.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Danco Laboratories, US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill manufacturer, has said that it may have to stop producing the medication if the supreme court cannot intervene on lower court limitations, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 New court-imposed restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone could cut off access to the drug entirely for months, the Biden administration and the drug\u8217\'20\'19s distributor, Danco Laboratories, said in petitions asking the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  to lift the curbs.\par \par \uc2 Marketing the drugs under the conditions imposed by the 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals on Wednesday will require a new approval process and new labeling, they said.\par \par \uc2 Danco, whose sole product is the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, said that if the Supreme Court does not act, it may have to halt its operations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights groups have denounced the six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban signed into law by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , warning that the policy would carry disastrous consequences for the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s constituents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese policy decisions disproportionately hurt Black and Latino people, LGBTQ+ people, and people with low incomes due to systemic racism and discrimination,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 , said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will keep fighting back in the days, months, and years to come until all Floridians can get the care they deserve without barriers or delay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Noting that a majority of Floridians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/religious-landscape-study/state/florida/views-about-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do not support}}}\uc2  such restrictions, reproductive rights leaders predicted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans would spell electoral disaster for Republicans next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Republicans are learning in every single election since Dobbs, it is not a path to victory,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mini Timmaraju, president of Naral. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more harm DeSantis and extremists are willing to inflict on their constituents in their quest for power, the worse Election Night will be for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 As apart of its appeal to the supreme court, the Biden administration argued that limits on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill from lower courts would require the relabeling of the drug, a process that could take months and deny people access to the medication, reported Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The administration noted that the lower court orders would have \u8220\'20\'1Csweeping consequences\u8221\'20\'1D for those who require access to mifepristone, one of two common medications used in abortions.\par \par \uc2 The administration added that the ruling could impact the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s scientific judgment authority over drug safety.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden admin asks supreme court to block \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill limits\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has asked the supreme court to stop limits from lower courts on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill as the government seeks to defend the drug against attacks from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists and Republican legislators, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the justice department has filed an emergency request for supreme court justices to put on hold a ruling by a federal Texas judge that would significantly restrict the distribution of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, Reuters further reported.\par \par \uc2 The latest developments come as litigation by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups is underway, challenging mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s regulatory approval.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  quietly signed off on a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban late last night, after the majority-GOP legislature approved of the bill.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban is not in effect yet, as the state\u8217\'20\'19s original 15-week ban faces a legal challenge in its supreme court, which is mostly conservative.\par \par \uc2 Up until Thursday, Florida was one of few southern states that had not enacted a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban--serving as a resource for southern people who could not access the procedure in their own state, reported Axios.\par \par \uc2 Since the overturning of Roe v wade, Florida has seen one of the largest increases in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand. Clinicians provided 7,190 more abortions in the six months following the Dobbs decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/WeCountReport_April2023Release.pdf?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to data from the Society of family planning}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last six months since Dobbs, the number of out-of-state patients coming to [us] for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care has quadrupled,\u8221\'20\'1D said Damien Filer, a representative of Planned Parenthood of South, East, and North Florida (PPSEN), to the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/27/florida-abortion-refuge-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview last month}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, and other nearby states have either completely banned or severely restricted the procedure--with many clinics closing completely.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/27/florida-abortion-refuge-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida, \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  refuge in US south, poised to pass six-week ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill maker calls for supreme court to intervene\par \par \uc2 US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill manufacturer Danco Laboratories has asked the supreme court to intervene in attempts to restrict the medication, ahead of a possible appeal file from the Department of Justice today, reported Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The pill maker put out a statement yesterday in response to a federal judge in Texas suspending US approval of mifepristone, one of two medications commonly used in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a dark day for public health, especially for reproductive rights and the reliance on science and medical expertise to guide decisions about what drugs are safe and effective and should be available to patients,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/this-week-in-health-news-13-stories-you-need-to-see-301797255.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  Abby Long, Danco\u8217\'20\'19s Director of Public Affairs in a statement.\par \par \uc2 A separate ruling from a Washington judge followed shortly, ordering the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) to avoid taking any action that could impact the availability of the medication.\par \par \uc2 The two conflicting rulings have set off a complicated legal battle, which could put the pill\u8217\'20\'19s future availability in jeopardy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-mifepristone-trump-judge-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill access in doubt after Texas judge suspends approval}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida enacts six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Republican-controlled states are facing additional coordinated attacks, with Florida and Texas serving as major political battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday after the bill was approved by the GOP-majority legislature.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s most recent ban will only take effect if the state\u8217\'20\'19s current 15-week ban is upheld before its supreme court, which has a conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 The ban could give DeSantis, who is expected to run for president in 2024, a key victory with Republican primary voters.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Department of Justice may file an appeal with the supreme court today, attempting to stop the restriction of mifepristone, the at-home \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Follow this blog for more updates on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics news.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230414ej4e001s8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
