\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  temporarily blocks ruling limiting  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 622 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par 21:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  imposes five-day stay after ruling by Texas federal judge that would have imposed restrictions on mifepristone\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has temporarily blocked lower court rulings which would have imposed temporary restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone that were set to go into effect this weekend.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/nov/19/rights-group-calls-for-samuel-alito-to-be-investigated-after-claims-of-leaked-2014-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alito}}}\uc2  imposed a five-day stay after a ruling by a conservative federal judge in Texas, parts of which were then upheld by a conservative appellate court based in New Orleans. For now, access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the most common method of pregnancy termination in the US \u8211\'20\'13 is unchanged until at least Wednesday 19 April.\par \par \uc2 The pause gives the high court more time to deliberate the restrictions imposed by the lower court. The Department of Justice and the drug\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturer, Danco, had asked the supreme court to intervene to stop those restrictions earlier on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approved mifepristone in 2000. The US fifth circuit court of appeal decision, upholding parts of the ruling by federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk of Texas, had rolled back action taken by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  after 2016 to expand access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 The restrictions that were set to take effect this weekend include limiting mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s use after seven weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 it is currently approved until 10 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and banning the delivery of the drug by mail.\par \par \uc2 The stay is not considered necessarily indicative of how the court, which is dominated by a conservative supermajority, may ultimately rule on the overall merits of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug case. Alito wrote the landmark \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling last year that eliminated the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been established with the Roe v Wade decision in 1973. Last year\u8217\'20\'19s ruling left it up to individual states to decide the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within their boundaries.\par \par \uc2 The justice department wrote in its appeal to the high court on Friday that the restrictions would create \u8220\'20\'1Cprofound disruption and grave harm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf allowed to take effect, the lower courts\u8217\'20\'19 orders would upend the regulatory regime for mifepristone, with sweeping consequences for the pharmaceutical industry, women who need access to the drug, and \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to implement its statutory authority,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 , the US solicitor general.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court was widely expected to take up the case, in part because of a ruling from a Washington state district court that conflicts with the decisions out of Texas and Louisiana. The Washington ruling orders the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to maintain the status quo for the drug in 17 states and the District of Columbia. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  faces an \u8220\'20\'1Cobvious threat of irreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D from conflicting court orders, the justice department writes.\par \par \uc2 Danco, the mifepristone drug manufacturer, also appealed to the supreme court for intervention on Friday, pointing to the \u8220\'20\'1Cregulatory chaos\u8221\'20\'1D that would be unleashed if limitations on the drug went into effect. The result of dueling federal court orders creates an \u8220\'20\'1Cuntenable limbo, for Danco, for providers, for women and for healthcare systems all trying to navigate these uncharted waters\u8221\'20\'1D, the drug company wrote, arguing that casting doubt on the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approvals process would create a dangerous precedent for the drug market broadly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a dark day for public health, especially for reproductive rights and the reliance on science and medical expertise to guide decisions about what drugs are safe and effective and should be available to patients,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/this-week-in-health-news-13-stories-you-need-to-see-301797255.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Abby Long, Danco\u8217\'20\'19s director of public affairs, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court does not act, wrote justice department lawyers, the \u8220\'20\'1Cresulting disruption would deny women lawful access to a drug \uc2 FDA\uc2  deemed a safe and effective alternative to invasive surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230414ej4e002jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
