\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DoJ \u8216\'20\'18strongly disagrees\u8217\'20\'19 with  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill ruling and will appeal to supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Attorney general says DoJ will ask supreme court to review appeals court decision that preserved drug access but with limitsFBI arrests suspect behind Pentagon leak \u8211\'20\'13 follow liveSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will fight to preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, with attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64382c438f08791e579d449f#block-64382c438f08791e579d449f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  the justice department would appeal to the supreme court to ensure its availability and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64382c438f08791e579d449f#block-64382c438f08791e579d449f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling the effort}}}\uc2  to get it off shelves \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next step to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D Meanwhile, in Tennessee, ousted Democratic lawmaker Justin Pearson was sworn back in to the state House of Representatives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-643827df8f08791e579d446c#block-643827df8f08791e579d446c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where he vowed}}}\uc2  to protect the rights of minorities.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the Republican senator who seems close to announcing a presidential run, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643816f88f0885230b2da23f#block-643816f88f0885230b2da23f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would support a federal ban on abortions after 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Clarence Thomas{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643853518f08791e579d4632#block-643853518f08791e579d4632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to sell}}}\uc2  three properties to Republican megadonor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 , but did not report the sale on disclosure forms he is required to file, according to a new \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  story.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64380d4a8f0885230b2da18e#block-64380d4a8f0885230b2da18e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went back}}}\uc2  to New York City to appear for a deposition as part of state attorney general Letitia James \u8217\'20\'19s fraud lawsuit against him and his children.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US investigators{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643858128f08791e579d4658#block-643858128f08791e579d4658"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  a 21-year-old air national guardsman suspected of leaking secret Pentagon documents on social media.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6438502a8f0885230b2da53f#block-6438502a8f0885230b2da53f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will be back}}}\uc2  in the Capitol next week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Republican lawmaker Andy Biggs. Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Rightwing House Republican Andy Biggs has introduced two pieces of legislation intended to frustrate Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-arraignment-court-hush-money-politics-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prosecution of Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first, called the Accountability for Lawless Violence In Our Neighborhoods (ALVIN) Act, \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibits federal funds from being awarded to the Manhattan District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office and requires the Office to repay federal funds granted after January 1, 2022,\u8221\'20\'1D according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://biggs.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-biggs-introduces-new-legislation-defund-weaponized-and-lawless"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a press release}}}\uc2  from the Arizona lawmaker\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 The second stops state and local law enforcement from using money obtained through asset forfeitures for criminals prosecutions of presidents, vice-presidents and presidential candidates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis weaponized prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s office has spent thousands of federal taxpayer dollars to subsidize this political indictment and is demanding millions more in federal grants,\u8221\'20\'1D Biggs said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s disturbing to see District Attorney Bragg waste federal resources for political purposes rather than addressing the serious crime in his city. As a member of the House Judiciary and Oversight & Accountability Committees, and with an almost insurmountable national debt that exceeds $31 trillion, the nation simply cannot afford to support Mr. Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s politicization of the criminal justice system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have rushed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defense since his indictment late last month, demanding documents and testimony from Bragg and sending a subpoena demanding testimony from Mark Pomerantz, a former prosecutor in Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s office who wrote a book detailing why believes there\u8217\'20\'19s a criminal case against Trump. Earlier this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/11/alvin-bragg-sues-republican-jim-jordan-trump-case-interference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bragg sued}}}\uc2  the chair of the House judiciary committee Jim Jordan to quash the subpoena against Pomerantz.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 US authorities this afternoon arrested a young airman on suspicion of leaking the secret Pentagon materials that have spread on social media over the past days. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest:\par \par \uc2 A 21-year-old US air national guardsman suspected of leaking highly classified Pentagon files has been arrested in Massachusetts, the US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  confirmed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Jack Teixeira is believed to have led Thug Shaker Central, an online group where about 20 to 30 people shared their love of guns, racist memes and video games, the New York reported, citing interviews and documents it reviewed.\par \par \uc2 Garland told reporters that Texeira was arrested \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout incident\u8221\'20\'1D and would be arraigned later on Thursday in a Massachusetts federal court.\par \par \uc2 The leaked documents, which were disseminated widely online, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/12/leaked-us-intelligence-document-claims-serbia-agreed-to-arm-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have laid bare secrets}}}\uc2  about Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s preparations for a spring counteroffensive, US spying on allies, such as South Korea and Israel, and the tensions between Washington and allied capitals over arming Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/pentagon-leaked-documents-suspect-arrested"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US arrests suspect behind leak of Pentagon documents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  failed to disclose property sale to Republican megadonor: report\par \par \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  sold three real estate properties to Republican megadonor \uc2 Harlan Crow\uc2 , but didn\u8217\'20\'19t report the deal on a disclosure form in a potential breach of federal law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-harlan-crow-real-estate-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The revelation comes from the second article the investigative news site has published on the links between Crow and Thomas, one of the most ardent rightwing justices on the supreme court. Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/clarence-thomas-scotus-undisclosed-luxury-travel-gifts-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica reported}}}\uc2  that Thomas had accepted luxury trips from Crow for years, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t include the travel on his disclosure forms.\par \par \uc2 Thomas has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/07/clarence-thomas-statement-undisclosed-gifts-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended his involvement}}}\uc2  with Crow, but Senate Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2023/apr/10/senate-democrats-supreme-court-investigation-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have urged}}}\uc2  chief justice of the supreme court \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  to investigate Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the megadonor, while vowing to hold a hearing into the matter.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest story:\par \par \uc2 The transaction marks the first known instance of money flowing from the Republican megadonor to the Supreme Court justice. The Crow company bought the properties for $133,363 from three co-owners \u8212\'20\'14 Thomas, his mother and the family of Thomas\u8217\'20\'19 late brother, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23774051-sales-document-pt61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state tax document}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23774272-warranty-deed-thomas-and-crow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deed}}}\uc2  dated Oct. 15, 2014, filed at the Chatham County courthouse.\par \par \uc2 The purchase put Crow in an unusual position: He now owned the house where the justice\u8217\'20\'19s elderly mother was living. Soon after the sale was completed, contractors began work on tens of thousands of dollars of improvements on the two-bedroom, one-bathroom home, which looks out onto a patch of orange trees. The renovations included a carport, a repaired roof and a new fence and gates, according to city permit records and blueprints.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/5/13104"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal disclosure law}}}\uc2  passed after Watergate requires justices and other officials to disclose the details of most real estate sales over $1,000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/23774093-2014-clarence-thomas-disclosure#document/p5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thomas never disclosed}}}\uc2  his sale of the Savannah properties. That appears to be a violation of the law, four ethics law experts told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The disclosure form Thomas filed for that year also had a space to report the identity of the buyer in any private transaction, such as a real estate deal. That space is blank.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe needed to report his interest in the sale,\u8221\'20\'1D said Virginia Canter, a former government ethics lawyer now at the watchdog group CREW. \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the role Crow has played in subsidizing the lifestyle of Thomas and his wife, you have to wonder if this was an effort to put cash in their pockets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thomas did not respond to detailed questions for this story.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The top Senate Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said he would return to work next week, more than a month after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/09/mitch-mcconnell-in-hospital-after-fall-in-washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was hospitalized}}}\uc2  following a fall:\par \par \uc2 enltrI am looking forward to returning to the Senate on Monday. We've got important business to tackle and big fights to win for Kentuckians and the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Leader McConnell (@LeaderMcConnell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell/status/1646581751924269056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 As a number of prominent Republicans prepare to gather at the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual meeting this weekend, Democratic leaders warned that the GOP will suffer electoral consequences for their refusal to back gun safety laws.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , a Democrat of Connecticut, noted that congressional Republicans helped pass the Bipartisan Safer Communities Act last year, marking the first time in nearly 30 years that the US enacted a major gun safety bill at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters today on a press call organized by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , Murphy lamented that Republicans who support gun safety are \u8220\'20\'1Cthe exception, not the rule\u8221\'20\'1D in their party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want Republicans to join with the rest of us and work to build a bipartisan majority behind common sense gun laws, but it appears that they\u8217\'20\'19re not ready for that,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Republican Party continues to give the middle finger to kids and kids\u8217\'20\'19 fears for their safety, they are just asking for an electoral tidal wave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders denounced Republican inaction on gun safety ahead of the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual meeting, which kicks off tomorrow in Indianapolis, Indiana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Republican that\u8217\'20\'19s thrown their hat in the ring to run for president is showing up this weekend to pledge their undying loyalty to the \uc2 NRA\uc2  and the gun lobby,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2 , a Democrat of Connecticut, said today on a press call organized by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to speak at the \uc2 NRA\uc2  conference, and Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is expected to launch his own presidential bid in the coming weeks, will appear at the event via video.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NRA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting comes just weeks after a shooter attacked Covenant School in Nashville, Tennessee, killing three children and three adults.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur kids are being hunted,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the \uc2 NRA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business model is to give aid to the hunters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19ve been wondering what \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is up to today, the answer is addressing a joint session of the \uc2 Irish parliament\uc2 , where he\u8217\'20\'19s calling for a permanent end to political violence.\par \par \uc2 We have a live blog following the president\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Ireland as it happens, which you can read here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2023/apr/13/rishi-sunak-keir-starmer-labour-attack-ad-angela-rayner-politics-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden says political violence \u8216\'20\'18must never be allowed to take hold again\u8217\'20\'19 in address to Irish parliament \u8211\'20\'13 politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s state senators relocated to a secure, remote facility after a \u8220\'20\'1Ccredible threat\u8221\'20\'1D forced the Assembly to abandon its Thursday session.\par \par \uc2 An email from senate secretary Erika Contreras told lawmakers: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 California Highway Patrol\uc2  (\uc2 CHP\uc2 ) has notified the senate of a threat they consider to be credible involving the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 CHP\uc2  and security partners are present in higher numbers in the Capitol area, and are alert of the situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Contreras said the session was moved to another state building nearby. Staff were told to stay home or remain in their offices.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is playing catch-up with the flooding emergency in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Broward county, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/fort-lauderdale-flooding-rain-storms-weather-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cone in a thousand\u8221\'20\'1D weather event}}}\uc2  that left large areas under water following an overnight deluge.\par \par \uc2 The Republican governor spent the morning in Ohio on his nationwide book tour. At a lunchtime press conference/update, the mayor of Fort Lauderdale, \uc2 Dean Trantalis\uc2 , said he had spoken with the White House but not the governor.\par \par \uc2 enltrJesus. Fort Lauderdale, Florida is underwater right now and the mayor just said \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chas not yet called. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what\u8217\'20\'19s going on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is in Ohio on a book tour. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Q6HuxEyhsx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Q6HuxEyhsx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 No Lie with Brian Tyler Cohen (@NoLieWithBTC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NoLieWithBTC/status/1646559787377623042?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor DeSantis has not yet called. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what\u8217\'20\'19s going on, but I\u8217\'20\'19m sure he\u8217\'20\'19s very interested in what\u8217\'20\'19s going on here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Bryan Griffin, DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BryanDGriffin/status/1646544803562135552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broke cover on Twitter}}}\uc2  shortly after midday Thursday, linking to a Florida department of emergency management {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.floridadisaster.org/news-media/news/20230413-governor-ron-desantis-issues-updates-on-southeast-florida-flooding/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bulletin}}}\uc2  on the flooding.\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s schedule for the day was sent out at 1.22pm, showing afternoon calls were set with state emergency management director Kevin Guthrie and Broward county commissioner Michael Udine.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/fort-lauderdale-flooding-rain-storms-weather-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Foot of rain causes severe flooding in South Florida in \u8216\'20\'181-in-1,000 year event\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 A supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who joined the invasion of US Capitol on January 6 2021, and expressed admiration for Adolf Hitler, was sentenced Thursday to three years in prison on firearms charges.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reported that the sentence Alexandria district court judge Michael Nachmanoff imposed on former navy reservist Hatchet Speed was five months less than the term sought by federal prosecutors, and much longer than the one-year term sought by Speed\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers.\par \par \uc2 Hatchet Speed. Photograph: AP\par \par \uc2 Speed, 41, of McLean, is a military veteran who held top-secret clearances while working for a defense contractor.\par \par \uc2 The gun charges against him in Virginia are separate from charges brought in Washington DC for obstructing an official proceeding, namely the January 6 joint session of Congress to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defeat of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Speed will be sentenced on those charges next month and could receive up to six additional years in prison.\par \par \uc2 In conversations with an \uc2 FBI\uc2  undercover agent last year, Speed expressed admiration for Hitler and domestic terrorists in the US. He also made antisemitic comments, proposed targeting Jewish people with acts of violence, and collected neo-Nazi memorabilia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will fight to preserve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, with attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64382c438f08791e579d449f#block-64382c438f08791e579d449f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  the justice department would appeal to the supreme court to ensure its availability and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64382c438f08791e579d449f#block-64382c438f08791e579d449f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling the effort}}}\uc2  to get it off shelves \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next step to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D Meanwhile, in Tennessee, ousted Democratic lawmaker Justin Pearson was sworn back in to the state House of Representatives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-643827df8f08791e579d446c#block-643827df8f08791e579d446c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where he vowed}}}\uc2  to protect the rights of minorities.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott, the Republican senator who seems close to announcing a presidential run, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643816f88f0885230b2da23f#block-643816f88f0885230b2da23f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would support a federal ban on abortions after 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64380d4a8f0885230b2da18e#block-64380d4a8f0885230b2da18e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is back}}}\uc2  in New York City to appear for a deposition as part of state attorney general Letitia James \u8217\'20\'19s fraud lawsuit against him and his children.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US investigators{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/13/abortion-pill-ruling-florida-ban-trump-deposition-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643809148f08791e579d4294#block-643809148f08791e579d4294"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are closing in}}}\uc2  on the leaker of Pentagon documents that reveal Washington\u8217\'20\'19s secret assessments of the war in Ukraine, among other secrets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls mifepristone lawsuit 'next step to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue fighting\u8221\'20\'1D to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while calling the lawsuit that seeks to ban mifepristone \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next step to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement, she the vice-president also warned that if allowed to proceed, the decision could jeopardize access to medication intended to treat a variety of ailments.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full text of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s statement:\par \par \uc2 Last night, the Fifth Circuit issued a decision which invalidates the scientific, independent judgment of the \uc2 FDA\uc2  about when and how a medicine is available to Americans. The Justice Department has already announced that they are seeking emergency relief from the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 More than 20 years ago, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as safe and effective for the American people. Last week, a Texas district court ruled to block access to this medication in every state in the country.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth Circuit\u8217\'20\'19s decision\u8212\'20\'14just like the district court\u8217\'20\'19s\u8212\'20\'14second-guesses the agency\u8217\'20\'19s medical experts. If this decision stands, no medication\u8212\'20\'14from chemotherapy drugs, to asthma medicine, to blood pressure pills, to insulin\u8212\'20\'14would be safe from attacks. This decision threatens the rights of Americans across the country, who can look in their medicine cabinets and find medication prescribed by a doctor because the \uc2 FDA\uc2  engaged in a process to determine the efficacy and safety of that medication.\par \par \uc2 This lawsuit is the next step to a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The decision severely limits access to mifepristone, standing between doctors and their patients. President Biden and our Administration remain firmly committed to protecting access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the President and I have made clear since the day of the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs.\par \par \uc2 There is a reproductive health care crisis in America. Our Administration will continue fighting to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s health and the right to make decisions about one\u8217\'20\'19s own body.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ousted Democrat Pearson returns to Tennessee statehouse\par \par \uc2 Justin Pearson, a Black Democratic lawmaker who was expelled from the Tennessee House of Representatives by its Republican majority last week, was sworn back into office today.\par \par \uc2 Pearson was removed from his seat representing Memphis after he joined in a protest on the House floor calling for tighter gun control with Justin Jones, who represents Nashville. Local authorities in that city voted reappointed Jones back into his seat earlier this week, while the Shelby County Commissioners did the same for Pearson yesterday.\par \par \uc2 In a speech after his swearing in, Pearson vowed \u8220\'20\'1CWe will never quit\u8221\'20\'1D in fighting to protect rights. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what he said:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 DOJ 'strongly disagrees' with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling, will appeal to supreme court\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said the justice department will ask the supreme court to review an appeals court decision that preserved access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone but placed new restrictions on its use and distribution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Justice Department strongly disagrees with the Fifth Circuit\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine v. \uc2 FDA\uc2  to deny in part our request for a stay pending appeal,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will be seeking emergency relief from the Supreme Court to defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s scientific judgment and protect Americans\u8217\'20\'19 access to safe and effective reproductive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, conservative federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk had sided with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes and revoked the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of the drug, in a ruling that was to take effect this Friday. The justice department appealed, and late yesterday the fifth circuit court of appeals in New Orleans blocked the deauthorization. However, the judges allowed to go into effect portions of Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that required mifepristone be prescribed during in-person doctor\u8217\'20\'19s appointments and limiting its use to the first seven weeks of pregnancy from its current 10 weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Senate Democrats, they\u8217\'20\'19re in a bit of a quandary over the situation of California senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , who has been away from the Capitol for weeks to receive medical treatment. That\u8217\'20\'19s held up confirmation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s picks for the federal judiciary, and yesterday, a fellow California Democrat called on her to resign. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , the Democratic senator who is the oldest member of the upper chamber of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , said she plans on serving out her term despite growing calls for her to resign.\par \par \uc2 Feinstein, 89, has not voted in Congress since February, and has been away from Capitol Hill after being hospitalized for shingles treatment in March. \u8220\'20\'1CI intend to return as soon as possible once my medical team advises that it\u8217\'20\'19s safe for me to travel. In the meantime, I remain committed to the job and will continue to work from home in San Francisco,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The statement comes after the Democratic representative \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2  tweeted on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for @SenFeinstein to resign. We need to put the country ahead of personal loyalty.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/us-house-democrats-dianne-feinstein-resignation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dianne Feinstein vows to return to her post as Democrats call for her to resign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has condemned the federal appeals court that blocked a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling deauthorizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, but placing new restrictions on its distribution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority Maga panel of judges on the fifth circuit appellate court continue to undermine the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawful expansion of access to safe medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on dubious legal grounds and baseless pseudo-science,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese extremist judges are putting their own anti-choice opinions before the medical expertise of providers and the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and the interests of patients. Senate Democrats will continue to fight back against this right-wing campaign against women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 If elected president, Republican senator Tim Scott said he would support a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s his interview with WMUR in New Hampshire \u8211\'20\'13 one of the early states in the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s nomination process:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn a 1-on-1 interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WMUR9?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WMUR9}}}\uc2 , Sen. Tim Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/votetimscott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @votetimscott}}}\uc2  says the Dobbs decision left \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to the states, but if he's President he says he would sign a 20-week federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FITN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FITN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NHPolitics?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NHPolitics}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WMUR?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WMUR}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fHPGZ4gr5z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fHPGZ4gr5z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Sexton (@AdamSextonWMUR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamSextonWMUR/status/1646517385049026560?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Scott hasn\u8217\'20\'19t officially declared his candidacy, but yesterday announced the formation of an exploratory committee, a key step in running for the White House. The senator represents South Carolina, and his fellow Republican senator from the state \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  last year proposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a federal ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Most Americans, including just over half of Republicans, believe a federal judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision last week that would have taken \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone off the shelves was motivated by politics, according to a new poll.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/half-republicans-say-politics-drove-us-abortion-pill-court-ruling-reutersipsos-2023-04-13/#:~:text=Fifty%2Done%20percent%20of%20Republicans,supports%20limiting%20access%20to%20abortion."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters/Ipsos survey}}}\uc2  completed yesterday found 56% of overall respondents believed the decision by conservative judge Matthew Kacsmaryk was politically motivated. The view was shared by 67% of Democrats and 51% of Republicans, according to the data.\par \par \uc2 The poll also found support for medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across party lines. Restrictions on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills as the state level were opposed by 51% of Republicans and 73% of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you are wondering where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is today, the answer is back in New York City, site of last week\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/video/2023/apr/05/its-a-circus-outside-trumps-surreal-day-in-court-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 circus-like}}}\uc2  arraignment on felony charges of falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 This time, he\u8217\'20\'19s sitting for a deposition before New York attorney general Letitia James as part of her case alleging massive fraud by the former president and some of his children. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the scene as his motorcade arrived in Manhattan, from the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump motorcade arriving at AG\u8217\'20\'19s office to chants of \u8220\'20\'1CNew York hates you.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CjKtJZlrY0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CjKtJZlrY0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shayna Jacobs (@shaynajacobs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shaynajacobs/status/1646510618583924737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump had previously been deposed by James last August, where he invoked his fifth amendment right not to testify hundreds of times.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 US 'close' to learning identity of Pentagon leaker\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told reporters today that investigators are \u8220\'20\'1Cgetting close\u8221\'20\'1D to identifying the person behind the leak of military documents that have revealed Washington\u8217\'20\'19s views of the war in Ukraine and other matters, CNN reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a full blown investigation going on as you know," Pres Biden said when asked for comment about the leaked classified docs. "The intelligence community and the Justice Department. And they\u8217\'20\'19re getting close. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have an answer for you."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kylie Atwood (@kylieatwood) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylieatwood/status/1646491653870329856?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 13, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  yesterday interviewed a teenage associate of the leaker, who painted a disturbing picture of his motivations. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The man responsible for the leak of hundreds of classified Pentagon documents is reported to be a young, racist gun enthusiast who worked on a military base, and who was seeking to impress two dozen fellow members of an internet chat group.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2023/04/12/discord-leaked-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  interviewed a teenage member of the group, who described the man, referred to by the initials \u8220\'20\'1COG\u8221\'20\'1D, from their online correspondence, and shared photographs and videos. The Post also viewed a video of a man identified as OG at a shooting range with a large rifle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe yells a series of racial and antisemitic slurs into the camera, then fires several rounds at a target,\u8221\'20\'1D the report said. OG told fellow members of the same internet group that he worked on a military base, which was not named in the report, where his job involved viewing large amounts of classified information.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/pentagon-leaks-og-source-military-base-discord-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pentagon leaks linked to young gun enthusiast who worked at military base \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic lawmakers are doing all they can to stop a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from becoming law. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  with a look at the quixotic effort by the top Democrat in the state Senate to halt its passage there:\par \par \uc2 Last week, Lauren Book, the top Democrat in the Florida senate \u8211\'20\'13 was placed in handcuffs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.talgov.com/Main/News/5432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/florida-democrats-arrested-abortion-ban-capitol-trespassing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with trespassing}}}\uc2 , after refusing to leave an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstration near the state capitol building in Tallahassee.\par \par \uc2 Hours before, Republican lawmakers in the state senate advanced the legislation, which would dramatically restrict the state\u8217\'20\'19s current ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 15 weeks of pregnancy to six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even realize they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. Critics say the narrow window would amount to a \u8220\'20\'1Cnear-total\u8221\'20\'1D ban on abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 The bill would have far-reaching implications across the south. After the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to eliminate a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/27/florida-abortion-refuge-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  became a haven}}}\uc2  for women seeking reproductive care from states where access was prohibited or severely restricted, including Louisiana and Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/florida-democrat-lauren-book-fight-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a scary time\u8217\'20\'19: Florida Democrat vows to keep fighting six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will further cut off access in south\par \par \uc2 The southern United States is the country\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/policies/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 least friendly region}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and access will soon grow even tighter as Florida moves to pass a ban on the procedure after six weeks. The GOP-controlled state House of Representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.baynews9.com/fl/tampa/news/2023/04/13/florida-house-prepares-to-vote-on-6-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is voting on}}}\uc2  the measure today, which contains exceptions for the life of the mother, and governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has said he\u8217\'20\'19ll sign it. While it\u8217\'20\'19s not the outright ban imposed by some of the state\u8217\'20\'19s neighbors, it\u8217\'20\'19ll reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  availability to a time period when most women aren\u8217\'20\'19t yet aware they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The greater battle in reproductive rights appears to be over mifepristone, which is used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the subject of an ongoing federal court battle. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/mifepristone-abortion-pill-to-remain-available-in-us-with-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more from Reuters}}}\uc2  on the late Wednesday ruling from an appeals court that preserved its availability, but imposed restrictions it that made it more difficult to access:\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone will remain available in the US for now but with significant restrictions, including a requirement for in-person doctor visits to obtain the drug, a federal appeals court ruled late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The New Orleans-based fifth circuit court of appeals put on hold part of last Friday\u8217\'20\'19s order by the US district judge Matthew Kacsmaryk in Amarillo, Texas, which suspended the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) approval for the drug while he heard a lawsuit by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups seeking to ban it.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration and the maker of the mifepristone brand, Danco Laboratories, had quickly asked for an emergency stay of that order.\par \par \uc2 However, the appeals court declined to block portions of Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s order that in effect reinstate restrictions on the pill\u8217\'20\'19s distribution, which had been lifted since 2016. In addition to a requirement of in-person doctor visits to prescribe and dispense the drug, those restrictions include limiting its use to the first seven weeks of pregnancy, down from 10 weeks. Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s order will take effect on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida to tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, medication survives court challenge\par \par \uc2 Good mornings, US politics blog readers. Americans will be able to continue accessing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/07/abortion-pill-ruling-explainer-mifepristone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medication \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  after a federal appeals court early this morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/mifepristone-abortion-pill-to-remain-available-in-us-with-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2  a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that would have revoked its authorization \u8211\'20\'13 but did impose new limits on the medication. The conservative assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains in full swing, with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/florida-democrat-lauren-book-fight-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to vote}}}\uc2  today on a bill that would ban the procedure after six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 a point at which most women are not yet aware they are pregnant. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/03/florida-six-week-abortion-bill-state-legislature-ron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill is expected to pass}}}\uc2  and be signed into law by Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who is thought to soon announce a presidential campaign that will center on bringing the policies he pioneered in Florida to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  continues his travels in Ireland, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/13/white-house-corrects-black-and-tans-to-all-blacks-after-biden-gaffe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he made headlines}}}\uc2  with a gaffe involving a rugby team and a military force. He was in Belfast yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/apr/12/joe-biden-us-investment-northern-ireland-power-sharing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to coax}}}\uc2  a power-sharing agreement out of Northern Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Justin Pearson, the second of two ousted Black Democratic lawmakers who were reappointed to their seats in the Tennessee House of Representatives by local authorities, will be sworn in today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in New York today, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll sit for a deposition in attorney general Letitia James $250mn lawsuit alleging fraud in his company.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230413ej4d001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
