\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill providers see surge in interest after judge targets mifepristone\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 876 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par 20:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 People are seeking the advance provision of medication before Friday\u8217\'20\'19s deadline, when the drug may become unavailable\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill websites and providers are seeing a surge of interest following a series of court decisions that threaten to block access to one of the major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs, mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 Carafem, a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider with a wide range of telehealth services, said it had seen a 38% increase in people booking virtual appointments since the first ruling on Friday upending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of mifepristone. Many customers have been asking whether they can order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication before becoming pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 what is known as \u8220\'20\'1Cadvance provision\u8221\'20\'1D, a number of providers said.\par \par \uc2 The online provider Hey Jane says it has seen a 30% increase in patients in the last week and a 58% increase in traffic to its website, while the website Plan C has seen an almost twofold increase in traffic to its website since the decision. More than half of the visitors to Plan C viewed the organization\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plancpills.org/guide-how-to-get-abortion-pills#faq-overview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guide on how to order \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills online}}}\uc2 . And the online \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  telehealth provider Choix says it had seen as many patients asking about the advance provision of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills since Friday as it usually sees in a month.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the fifth circuit court of appeals ruled to impose restrictions on mifepristone that include lowering the use of the drug to seven weeks of pregnancy instead of the current 10-week limit, and requiring in-person doctor visits for those looking to obtain the drug. The Biden administration subsequently expressed its intention to immediately appeal that decision before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The providers told the Guardian they were studying the implications of the appellate court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, while news of whether the case will be heard in the supreme court is pending. A number of them use telehealth to see patients and the mail to ship the pills.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk ruled in favor of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups challenging the Food and Drug Administration\u8217\'20\'19s 23-year-old approval of mifepristone \u8211\'20\'13 a drug commonly prescribed alongside misoprostol to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Biden administration appealed the decision, and an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/13/mifepristone-abortion-pill-to-remain-available-in-us-with-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeals court ruled late on Wednesday}}}\uc2  that the drug can remain available, but with significant restrictions.\par \par \uc2 On the same day as Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision, a federal judge in Washington state issued a conflicting ruling, stating that the \uc2 FDA\uc2  is not to take any action that would affect the availability of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The dueling decisions increase the likelihood that the issue of mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorization will ultimately be decided by the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAdvance provision helps to alleviate the stress and barriers that comes with accessing a highly stigmatized and politicized form of care \u8211\'20\'13 even in states where it remains legal,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cindy Adam, CEO of Choix, which has been at the forefront of advocating for advanced provision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that recent uptake in utilization correlates with the mifepristone case, and, in general, we see spikes in interest when there is more information shared about attacks on reproductive rights in the press and social media,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Research {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/WeCountReport_April2023Release.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by WeCount}}}\uc2  on Tuesday showed that the number of legal abortions performed in the US dropped by 6% since Roe v Wade was overturned in June 2022. That data does not account for people accessing pills outside the healthcare system, or through advance provision, which probably offsets the drop to some extent.\par \par \uc2 There has been a longstanding debate about the safety of doctors prescribing medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in advance of pregnancy. Many drugs are prescribed in advance \u8211\'20\'13 for example, antibiotics can be prescribed in advance in cases where a patient repeatedly gets the same infection, or ahead of travel. Many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers argue that US restrictions on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are overly burdensome and not in keeping with the rest of the world. But the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has argued against advance provision of mifepristone in the US.\par \par \uc2 Generally, two drugs are used in combination to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : mifepristone and misoprostol. Misoprostol can be prescribed on its own to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it is thought to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/feb/20/abortion-pills-us-ruling-rebecca-gomperts-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slightly less effective and more painful}}}\uc2 , and it is more likely to require follow-up care than when it is used in combination with mifepristone. Some providers have said they will continue prescribing misoprostol should Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling impair access to mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 But other providers have vowed to continue to prescribe mifepristone as long as they can, and a number of Democratic states have begun stockpiling the pill in response to Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want patients to know that in the meantime, Carafem is still providing mifepristone and misoprostol to our clients that want to have medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We did so last week, we\u8217\'20\'19re doing so this week and we look to continue to do that until we get a message from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  that we\u8217\'20\'19re unable to offer that medication any more,\u8221\'20\'1D stated Carafem\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, Melissa Grant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we get a message to stop, we are able to pivot to offering misoprostol alone, and if necessary, we will flex to be able to accommodate more people in person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230413ej4d000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
