\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a scary time\u8217\'20\'19: Florida Democrat vows to keep fighting six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,469 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par 13:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lauren Book has led the fight against the \u8216\'20\'18near-total\u8217\'20\'19 ban and the \u8216\'20\'18dangerous consequences\u8217\'20\'19 of bill that is expected to pass the state house and to be signed by Governor DeSantis\par \par \uc2 Last week, Lauren Book, the top Democrat in the Florida senate \u8211\'20\'13 was placed in handcuffs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.talgov.com/Main/News/5432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/florida-democrats-arrested-abortion-ban-capitol-trespassing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with trespassing}}}\uc2 , after refusing to leave an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstration near the state capitol building in Tallahassee.\par \par \uc2 Hours before, Republican lawmakers in the state senate advanced the legislation, which would dramatically restrict the state\u8217\'20\'19s current ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 15 weeks of pregnancy to six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even realize they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant. Critics say the narrow window would amount to a \u8220\'20\'1Cnear-total\u8221\'20\'1D ban on abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 The bill would have far-reaching implications across the south. After the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to eliminate a woman\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/mar/27/florida-abortion-refuge-six-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  became a haven}}}\uc2  for women seeking reproductive care from states where access was prohibited or severely restricted, including Louisiana and Alabama.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a scary time,\u8221\'20\'1D Book told the Guardian ahead of the vote. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are being put in very, very dangerous situations to get the healthcare they need and deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican dominance in the state legislature means the bill\u8217\'20\'19s fate is \u8220\'20\'1Call but sealed\u8221\'20\'1D, she acknowledged. The Republican-controlled house is expected to give the bill final approval as soon as this week. It will then be sent to Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a Republican who is widely expected to run for president and who has signaled his support.\par \par \uc2 But Book, who has led the opposition to this bill in the state senate, vowed to keep fighting \u8211\'20\'13 as a political leader and, she said, as a mother furious that her twins \u8211\'20\'13 a boy and a girl \u8211\'20\'13 no longer have the same rights to bodily autonomy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the course of just two generations, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen our rights won and lost,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a floor speech last week. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is up to us to get them back. No one is going to save us but ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 Book became senate minority leader in 2021, having served in the chamber since 2017. The following year, DeSantis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-supreme-court-health-ron-desantis-florida-lifestyle-8e8fb722fcb84ae86fd6be17f48503a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed into law}}}\uc2  a ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, without exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 A sharp backlash to last summer\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade fueled a string of ballot-box successes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and powered Democrats to victory in states across the country in the 2022 midterm elections. But not in Florida.\par \par \uc2 In November, DeSantis won re-election by nearly 20 points in a state that was once a presidential battleground, while Republicans claimed a supermajority in both chambers of the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 Emboldened, Republican lawmakers have advanced a dizzying array of legislative proposals that have thrilled conservatives, alarmed liberals and offered a policy platform from which the governor could launch a presidential bid.\par \par \uc2 As minority leader, Book believes it is her role to rally the opposition \u8211\'20\'13 and help Democrats claw back power in 2024. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to do the work to get the numbers out in \u8217\'20\'1924,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause the alternative is not acceptable. It\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous and it is killing women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican lawmakers are pressing forward with legislation that would impose {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/04/04/florida-senate-ban-transgender-treatments-kids-00090481"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  new controls}}}\uc2  on trans youth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sun-sentinel.com/news/politics/fl-ne-drag-permits-florida-legislature-parades-20230405-fok5u457qbbmbgi3yk5naz2jkq-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  limit drag performances}}}\uc2 , ease media defamation suits, expand the state\u8217\'20\'19s controversial \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/florida-hb-999-diversity-equity-inclusion-college-campus-bill-advances/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ban diversity and equity programs}}}\uc2  at public universities and colleges, place {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/politics/2023/03/16/florida-education-association-service-employees-inernational-union-payback-desantis-republicans/70016057007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  new restrictions}}}\uc2  on public-sector unions, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/miami/news/death-penalty-revamp-headed-to-full-florida-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  allow a divided jury}}}\uc2  to impose a death sentence. Already this session, DeSantis signed a law expanding Florida\u8217\'20\'19s school voucher system, and another allowing Floridians to carry a concealed weapon without a permit.\par \par \uc2 But while DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s conservative crusade may excite his base, Book said she expects it will backfire on him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not doing the things that matter to Floridians. We\u8217\'20\'19re not doing the things that make life here better,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, arguing that the legislature should be focused on tackling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.firstcoastnews.com/article/news/local/florida-homeowners-insurance-rates-new-defamation-law/77-4433b3a5-777a-4799-9045-ba14b23001c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising cost}}}\uc2  of property insurance. \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, we\u8217\'20\'19re attacking small groups of people, we\u8217\'20\'19re taking away women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, all under the banner of freedom and allowing this guy to run for president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s office did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 With the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill barrelling toward the governor\u8217\'20\'19s desk, Book said she and her Democratic colleagues are using every legislative tool at their disposal to draw attention to the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous consequences\u8221\'20\'1D of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 They offered numerous amendments, including one that would allow women seeking abortions to cite religious exemption. Another put forward by Book would have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlannaVagianos/status/1641166265015316481/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  renamed}}}\uc2  the so-called \u8220\'20\'1CHeartbeat Protection Act\u8221\'20\'1D to the \u8220\'20\'1CElectrical activity that can be manipulated to sound like a heartbeat through ultrasound protection at the expense of pregnant people\u8217\'20\'19s health and well being act.\u8221\'20\'1D All were rejected.\par \par \uc2 When the bill came before the senate health policy committee for debate, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderBookFL/status/1637957090781155328?cxt=HHwWgMC-lffSmLstAAAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended the session}}}\uc2  so medical providers and opponents would have more than the allotted \u8220\'20\'1C30 seconds\u8221\'20\'1D to testify, Book said. In speeches, she shared the stories of women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/10/pprom-florida-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including a constituent}}}\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/11/16/health/abortion-texas-sepsis/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced life-threatening complications }}}\uc2  after the loss of desired pregnancies because their states new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions prevented doctors from administering miscarriage care.\par \par \uc2 And last week, senate Democrats engaged in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderBookFL/status/1641539463489933312?cxt=HHwWgMDS4bvc9cctAAAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emotional floor debate}}}\uc2  ahead of the senate vote on the six-week ban. From the public gallery overlooking the chamber, protesters repeatedly disrupted the proceedings, shouting down lawmakers who spoke supportively of the legislation. Several were removed before the senate president ordered the gallery cleared.\par \par \uc2 The displays of opposition have had little effect.\par \par \uc2 State senator Erin Grall, a Republican sponsor of the bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/media/VideoPlayer?EventID=1_nty0d3lq-202304031000&Redirect=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  during the debate that \u8220\'20\'1Cbodily autonomy should not give a person the permission to kill an innocent human being\u8221\'20\'1D. Republicans have sought to emphasize that the measure allows for exceptions in cases of rape, incest or human trafficking until 15 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 additions DeSantis has called \u8220\'20\'1Csensible\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Critics counter that the exceptions are narrow, noting that the proposal will require victims to \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide a copy of a restraining order, police report, medical record, or other court order\u8221\'20\'1D before they can receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Book, a sexual assault survivor, says the paperwork requirement will keep women from seeking care. \u8220\'20\'1CShow your documents to prove that you were raped?\u8221\'20\'1D Book said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t even need to do that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/11/ron-desantis-florida-gun-control-permitless-carry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  now to carry a gun}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill\u8217\'20\'19s proponents also tout provisions that would expand funding for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pregnancy centers and provide families car seats, cribs and diapers. Book called the initiatives \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re going to give them car seats or a crib? What about healthcare? What about child care? Those are things that people need,\u8221\'20\'1D Book said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not pro life. They\u8217\'20\'19re pro-birth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Book sees a backlash brewing in Florida, though it won\u8217\'20\'19t come in time to stop Republicans from passing the ban.\par \par \uc2 According to a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/abortion-attitudes-in-a-post-roe-world-findings-from-the-50-state-2022-american-values-atlas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey by the Public Religion Research Institute}}}\uc2 , nearly two-thirds of Floridians believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most or all cases. Another poll published last month found that roughly three in four Florida voters, including 61% of Republican respondents, say they oppose a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with no exceptions for rape or incest. (Notably, the measure that passed the Florida senate does allow for exceptions, which was not asked as part of the polling question.)\par \par \uc2 Activists on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate are, meanwhile, waiting on a decision by the Florida supreme court, which is weighing a challenge to the state\u8217\'20\'19s current 15-week ban. The six-week proposal would only go into effect if the 15-week ban is upheld.\par \par \uc2 Book said she would like to see the matter settled by Florida voters in the form of a ballot initiative, like it was in Michigan and other states. In the meantime, she is urging women in Florida and around the country \u8220\'20\'1Cnot to take matters into your own hands\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Protesters have once again gathered in Tallahassee, as the Republican-controlled house charges ahead with a debate on the measure scheduled for Thursday. Among them will be \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , chair of the Florida Democratic party, who was arrested alongside Book last week. For Book, the women\u8217\'20\'19s resistance is proof that however bleak it may appear now, the fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Florida is only just beginning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C? I\u8217\'20\'19m heartened by the women who are now occupying Tallahassee and not going quietly into the night,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that is emblematic that this is not over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230413ej4d00131\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
