\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  reportedly sues former lawyer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  for $500m \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,922 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2023\par 20:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit claims former fixer breached attorney-client privilege and unjustly enriched himself, among other allegationsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Less than a week after Republicans booted them from the Tennessee state house of representatives, Black Democratic lawmakers Justin Jones and Justin Pearson have been reappointed back to their old seats, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436fe0e8f0891526bb4132b#block-6436fe0e8f0891526bb4132b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latter\u8217\'20\'19s return confirmed}}}\uc2  this afternoon by local authorities in Memphis. The episode, which began when the duo joined with a white colleague (who was not expelled) to demonstrate for stricter gun control on the House floor, appears far from over. In Washington, two Democratic senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436cd0b8f0885230b2d968f#block-6436cd0b8f0885230b2d968f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have called for}}}\uc2  attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to investigate their expulsion, arguing it appears to have violated free speech and anti-discrimination laws. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436d1d48f0891526bb41146#block-6436d1d48f0891526bb41146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if the statements}}}\uc2  of two Kentucky lawmakers following Monday\u8217\'20\'19s mass shooting in Louisville are any indication, the partisan divide over gun rights remains as wide as ever.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436b50d8f0885230b2d9525#block-6436b50d8f0885230b2d9525"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he\u8217\'20\'19ll \u8220\'20\'1Cnever drop out\u8221\'20\'1D of the 2024 presidential race, even if convicted of a crime.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rupert Murdoch{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643703bb8f0885230b2d9919#block-643703bb8f0885230b2d9919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be on the witness stand}}}\uc2  as soon as Monday, as Dominion Voting System\u8217\'20\'19s defamation complaint against Fox News heads to trial.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Tim Scott inched closer to an all-out presidential run {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436be508f08791e579d3785#block-6436be508f08791e579d3785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by announcing}}}\uc2  an exploratory committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The new Secret Service director downplayed concerns about politicization of the agency raised by the January 6 investigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436c88f8f08791e579d37df#block-6436c88f8f08791e579d37df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a rare interview}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436f63c8f08791e579d39fd#block-6436f63c8f08791e579d39fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suing}}}\uc2  his former lawyer and fixer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  for $500mn, alleging he unjustly enriched himself and breached attorney-client privilege. You may remember Cohen as being the vehicle for the former president\u8217\'20\'19s hush money payment to adult film actor Stormy Daniels, which is at the center of the indictment filed by Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  against him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s news of a link-up between a certain likely candidate for the Republican presidential nomination, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and Hungarian strongman \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/flora-garamvolgyi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Flora Garamvolgyi}}}\uc2 writes for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s far-right prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/viktor-orban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n}}}\uc2 , one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s biggest international supporters, has made overtures in recent weeks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2  and one of the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s key billionaire backers.\par \par \uc2 Orb\u225\'00\'E1n has repeatedly voiced strong support for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies and political style, even long after he left the White House. But meetings between a key Orb\u225\'00\'E1n ally and the DeSantis camp suggest the Hungarian leader is hedging his bets amid uncertainty over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s electoral prospects.\par \par \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 . Photograph: Denes Erdos/AP\par \par \uc2 Katalin Nov\u225\'00\'E1k, the Hungarian president, met DeSantis last month. She also met DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Casey, and Republican mega-donor Thomas P\u233\'00\'E9terffy, who has announced he would not be backing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential candidacy. The Hungarian-born billionaire has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/13/magazine/ron-desantis.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  called}}}\uc2  DeSantis his \u8220\'20\'1Cfavorite man\u8221\'20\'1D and donated $570,000 to his campaign in 2022, according to the campaign finance watchdog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.followthemoney.org/entity-details?eid=17657831&default=candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OpenSecrets}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/10/orban-loyalist-katalin-novak-elected-hungary-first-female-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  first female president}}}\uc2  of Hungary and a close ally of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/30/alarm-grows-as-orban-prepares-to-take-pure-nazi-rhetoric-to-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Orb\u225\'00\'E1n}}}\uc2 , Novak previously served as minister for family affairs. Like DeSantis, she has ultra-conservative views regarding family policies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KatalinNovakMP/status/1330099356259782656?lang%3Dhu&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1680500011875421&usg=AOvVaw3y40JsXcCUAJPIl7s2gVZg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/26/the-network-of-organisations-seeking-to-influence-abortion-policy-across-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . She has been a key part of Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to make Budapest a hub for discussions between rightwing and far-right forces from around the world, including the US right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the Orb\u225\'00\'E1n government, bilateral relations have a strong party-politics angle. They have been contemplating whether it was worth putting all their cards on Trump. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-pdf-full-text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indictment against the former president}}}\uc2  only confirmed that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daniel Hegedus, a Central Europe fellow at the German Marshall Fund.\par \par \uc2 Separately to the DeSantis meetings, Hungarian government officials have started to contact other Republican figures, according to a former Hungarian diplomat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese outreaches have increased for the past nine months, and more government officials have visited the US than before,\u8221\'20\'1D said the diplomat.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/12/viktor-orban-ron-desantis-trump-hungary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\u8217\'20\'19s support for Trump seems to wane as ally meets with DeSantis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Murdoch could testify in Fox-Dominion trial as soon as Monday: report\par \par \uc2 Fox News chairman \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  could as soon as Monday appear on the witness stand when the trial of \uc2 Dominion Voting Systems\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defamation case against the conservative media network begins, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-04-12/murdoch-to-take-stand-in-fox-dominion-trial-as-early-as-monday?utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&utm_content=politics&leadSource=uverify+wall&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The trial, in which the election systems company is asking for $1.6bn in compensation from Fox for allegedly harming its reputation in the aftermath of the 2020 election, begins in Delaware on Thursday. Opening arguments are set to start on Monday, and \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 , citing people familiar with the matter, say Murdoch could appear on that day or Tuesday as the second witness called.\par \par \uc2 Following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s loss in the 2020 election, his supporters accused Dominion of rigging the vote in favor of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  though its voting equipment, which is used by municipalities nationwide. Dominion says \uc2 Fox\uc2  amplified these claims repeatedly, even though they knew the network\u8217\'20\'19s employees knew were false. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the case:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/apr/11/fox-news-rupert-murdoch-title-dominion-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News under fire for \u8216\'20\'18credibility problem\u8217\'20\'19 over late disclosure of Murdoch role}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pumping his fist in the air with a vow of \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s get back to work\u8221\'20\'1D, Justin Pearson and his supporters were jubilant after local authorities in Memphis reappointed him to his seat in the statehouse.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s clip of his remarks following the Shelby county commission vote, which was unanimous:\par \par \uc2 enltrShelby County Commission sends Justin Pearson back to Nashville.\par \par \uc2 "You can't expel our voice, and you sure can't expel our fight. We look forward to continuing to fight, continuing to advocate, until justice rolls down like water and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tLXHJkKDIl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tLXHJkKDIl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alejandro Alvarez (@aletweetsnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aletweetsnews/status/1646227121906253861?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justin Pearson reinstated to Tennessee statehouse Justin Pearson and his supporters march to the Shelby County Board of Commissioners meeting in Memphis today. Photograph: Chris Day/AP\par \par \uc2 Justin Pearson, who was one of two Black Democratic lawmakers ejected from the Tennessee house of representatives by its Republican supermajority last week, has been reappointed to his position, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The Shelby county board of commissioners voted to send Pearson back to his seat representing Memphis. On Monday, the Nashville metropolitan council had done the same for Justin Jones, the other Democrat expelled after staging a noisy protest on the House floor in favor of stricter gun laws following a mass shooting in Nashville. Both men will need to win a forthcoming special election to remain in their seats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Memphis, protesters have gathered while the Shelby county commission reviews the reappointment of Democratic representative Justin Pearson.\par \par \uc2 He was one of two young Black Democrats removed from the Tennessee house of representatives along with Justin Jones, who was reappointed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting a decision from Memphis shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump sues former attorney Cohen for $500m: report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  slapped his former lawyer \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2  with a $500m lawsuit on Wednesday, according to Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Cohen is, of course, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s one-time fixer, notorious for making the $130,000 pay-off to adult movie star Stormy Daniels that led to the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in a Manhattan courtroom on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/04/trump-indictment-pdf-full-text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 felony counts of falsifying business records}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trump-sues-michael-cohen-for-500-million"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Fox}}}\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team filed a 30-page federal lawsuit in the US southern district court in Florida earlier today, claiming that Cohen breached of his attorney-client relationship and unjustly enriched himself, among other allegations.\par \par \uc2 Michael Cohen\uc2 . Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an action arising from [Cohen\u8217\'20\'19s] multiple breaches of fiduciary duty, unjust enrichment, conversion and breaches of contract by virtue of [Cohen\u8217\'20\'19s] past service as [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s] employee and attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit states, per the Fox report.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, the network said, details Cohen\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmyriad of public statements, including the publication of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/michael-cohen-writing-tell-all-book-on-trump-to-be-released-before-election-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two books}}}\uc2 , a podcast series, and innumerable mainstream media appearances,\u8221\'20\'1D while ignoring \u8220\'20\'1Ccease and desist\u8221\'20\'1D orders.\par \par \uc2 It claims Cohen has, in recent months, \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased the frequency and hostility of the illicit acts\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cappears to have become emboldened and repeatedly continues to make wrongful and false statements\u8221\'20\'1D about Trump through various platforms.\par \par \uc2 Cohen has become one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sharpest critics since being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jul/24/michael-cohen-prison-release-trump-book-aclu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released from a prison term in 2020}}}\uc2  for crimes including tax evasion, lying to Congress and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/26/the-fixers-review-donald-trump-michael-cohen-porn-star-stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facilitating illegal payments to silence}}}\uc2  both Daniels and Karen McDougal, a former Playboy model.\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2020/sep/27/disloyal-a-memoir-by-michael-cohen-review-disgraced-trump-lawyers-kiss-and-tell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote a memoir}}}\uc2 , entitled Disloyal, later that year chronicling his time as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s henchman, and has become a regular analyst on cable TV channels on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal perils.\par \par \uc2 Trump has always denied the affairs, or making payments to the women.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Wisconsin senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  says she\u8217\'20\'19s running for a third term, news greeted enthusiastically by the chair of the state party.\par \par \uc2 Ben Wikler says Republicans are \u8220\'20\'1Chiding under a rug\u8221\'20\'1D because none so far have announced they are challenging for Baldwin\u8217\'20\'19s seat in the key swing state, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s official: I\u8217\'20\'19m running for reelection!\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s working families deserve a Senator who\u8217\'20\'19s going to fight for them\u8212\'20\'14not shady special interests or big corporations. We\u8217\'20\'19ve made a lot of progress, but the stakes have never been higher and our work isn\u8217\'20\'19t over yet.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  (@tammybaldwin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tammybaldwin/status/1646119750081077249?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Baldwin, in a statement, said she intends to continue fighting for the working class and families struggling with inflation, as well as opposing Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s ban on elective abortions.\par \par \uc2 She became the state\u8217\'20\'19s first female member of congress in 1998, and was elected to the Senate in 2012, handing Republican former governor \uc2 Tommy Thompson\uc2  his first defeat in a statewide race.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warnock.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Warnock-Letter-to-DOJ-on-Tennessee-Representatives-Expulsions-FINAL1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the letter}}}\uc2  we told you about earlier from \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and other senior Democrats calling for the justice department to investigate the expulsion by Republicans in Tennessee of two young Black state representatives for taking part in a gun reform protest.\par \par \uc2 In it, Schumer, the Senate majority leader, and Warnock, of Georgia, join fellow Democrats \uc2 Chris Murphy\uc2  (Connecticut), Alejandro Padilla (California) and \uc2 Brian Schatz\uc2  (Hawaii), in asking attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to look into whether citizens\u8217\'20\'19 rights of representation were breached when the lawmakers were removed.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 A press release from Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s office announcing the letter reads in part:\par \par \uc2 On March 30, three Tennessee lawmakers peacefully protested in the well of the state\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives following the state legislature\u8217\'20\'19s inaction on gun violence prevention after the slaughter of three nine-year-olds and three adults at Covenant School in Nashville, Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 The next week, two of the three lawmakers, representatives Justin Pearson and Justin Jones, were expelled, while their colleague, representative Gloria Johnson, was spared by one vote.\par \par \uc2 The senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warnock.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/Warnock-Letter-to-DOJ-on-Tennessee-Representatives-Expulsions-FINAL1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  the DOJ to investigate whether actions by the Tennessee state legislature violated any constitutional rights of Tennessee citizens to be represented by the legislators of their choice, or violated any of representatives Jones\u8217\'20\'19 and Pearson\u8217\'20\'19s 14th amendment or first amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 We cannot allow states to cite minor procedural violations as pretextual excuses to remove democratically-elected representatives, especially when these expulsions may have been at least partially on the basis of race. Allowing such behavior sets a dangerous, and undemocratic, precedent.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll find out this afternoon if commissioners in Memphis have voted to restore Pearson to his seat. Nashville city leaders voted unanimously on Monday to send Jones back to the state house until a special election can be held.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/tennessee-justin-pearson-vote-reinstate-memphis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee council to vote on return of second Democrat to legislature}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Investigators asking whether Trump reviewed classified material: report\par \par \uc2 Special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s investigators are trying to determine whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  personally reviewed classified materials in his possession after the government asked last year that it be returned, and are asking witnesses whether he showed off a map containing sensitive information, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/12/us/politics/trump-map-classified-documents-justice-department.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Smith has been tasked by attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to investigate the classified materials the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort last August, as well as his involvement in the January 6 insurrection and efforts to overturn the 2020 election. According to the Times, who cited four people with knowledge of the matter, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s investigators have asked witnesses whether he displayed a map after leaving office. The details of the map are unknown, but it is said to contain secret information.\par \par \uc2 They have also asked whether Trump requested to personally review boxes of sensitive material at his Mar-a-Lago resort after receiving a subpoena last May to hand over all classified documents in his possession. A lawyer for the former president later signed a document asserting Trump had handed over all the material in his possession, which turned out not to be true.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 The question of whether Mr. Trump was displaying sensitive material in his possession after he lost the presidency and left office is crucial as investigators try to reconstruct what Mr. Trump was doing with boxes of documents that went with him to his Florida residence and private club, Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Among the topics investigators have been focused on is precisely when Mr. Trump was at the club last year. In particular, they were interested in whether he remained at Mar-a-Lago to look at boxes of material that were still stored there before Justice Department counterintelligence officials seeking their return came to visit in early June, according to two people familiar with the questions.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump typically leaves Florida for his club in Bedminster, N.J., earlier than he did last year, when he was still at Mar-a-Lago for the visit from the Justice Department officials, on June 3. Investigators have been gathering evidence about whether Mr. Trump had aides bring him boxes to sift through after a grand jury subpoena was issued in May for any government documents Mr. Trump still had in his possession, the people said.\par \par \uc2 After the June 3 visit, when Justice Department officials were handed a batch of documents with classified markings that had been found at Mar-a-Lago, a lawyer for Mr. Trump signed a certification saying a \u8220\'20\'1Cdiligent search\u8221\'20\'1D had been conducted and all government material had been returned. That statement proved untrue two months later when the F.B.I. found hundreds of pages of additional classified documents during a court-authorized search.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The second of two Democratic lawmakers expelled last week from Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s house of representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436aa448f0891526bb40f51#block-6436aa448f0891526bb40f51"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may get his seat back today}}}\uc2 , after a meeting of local commissioners in Memphis. In Washington, two Democratic senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436cd0b8f0885230b2d968f#block-6436cd0b8f0885230b2d968f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have called for}}}\uc2  attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to investigate the episode, arguing the Black lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 banishment appears to have violated free speech and anti-discrimination rights. The whole affair started with a protest in favor of stricter gun control \u8211\'20\'13 an issue over which partisan divisions are as wide as ever, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436d1d48f0891526bb41146#block-6436d1d48f0891526bb41146"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if the statements}}}\uc2  of two Kentucky lawmakers are any indication.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436b50d8f0885230b2d9525#block-6436b50d8f0885230b2d9525"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  he\u8217\'20\'19ll \u8220\'20\'1Cnever drop out\u8221\'20\'1D of the 2024 presidential race, even if convicted of a crime.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Tim Scott inched closer to an all-out presidential run {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436be508f08791e579d3785#block-6436be508f08791e579d3785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by announcing}}}\uc2  an exploratory committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The new Secret Service director downplayed concerns about politicization of the agency raised by the January 6 investigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/12/tennessee-democrats-biden-ireland-abortion-republicans-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6436c88f8f08791e579d37df#block-6436c88f8f08791e579d37df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a rare interview}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 A group of pharmaceutical firms and executives have filed a brief encouraging a federal appeals court to half a judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that last week decertified mifepristone, one of the drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe district court\u8217\'20\'19s approach would have ripple effects across \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s programs for drugs intended to treat serious and life-threatening diseases and conditions \u8212\'20\'14programs that are essential to facilitating and expediting the development and review of critical medicines,\u8221\'20\'1D the group of dozens of organizations and individuals writes in their amicus brief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would narrow eligibility for these programs, delay patient access to life-saving medications, and discourage development in the first instance. Without sufficient flexibility, sponsors would lose considerable efficiency in bringing new drugs to market \u8212\'20\'14 and in updating and innovating on existing approved applications. And patients would lose access to potentially lifesaving and life-improving treatments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The justice department is asking for a stay on the ruling from the fifth circuit court of appeals \u8211\'20\'13 which is considered the most conservative federal appellate body in the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates are scrambling ahead of a Friday deadline after which a drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be deauthorized, thanks to a conservative federal court judge. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/mary-tuma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mary Tuma}}}\uc2  with a look at the effort to get a higher court to intervene:\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  authorization for a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug could be nullified after Friday, unless an appeals court acts on a Biden administration request to block last week\u8217\'20\'19s ruling suspending approval of the drug.\par \par \uc2 The drug, mifepristone, is used in more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half of all the abortions}}}\uc2  in the US. The ruling, issued by a federal judge in Texas, applies across the country.\par \par \uc2 Writing that the ruling would \u8220\'20\'1Cinflict grave harm on women, the medical system, and the public\u8221\'20\'1D if it went into effect, the Department of Justice on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/10/us-appeals-texas-judge-abortion-pill-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requested the fifth US circuit court of appeals}}}\uc2  temporarily block Judge Matthew Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s ruling while the appeals process plays out.\par \par \uc2 The issue may ultimately fall into the hands of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  and its conservative supermajority, which eradicated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights last year by overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/12/mifepristone-abortion-drug-hangs-in-balance-friday-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fate of US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drug hangs in balance ahead of Friday deadline}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 A coalition of media organizations has filed a lawsuit asking for the release of surveillance footage from the January 6 insurrection that House speaker Kevin McCarthy provided to Fox News but no other outlet, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/12/politics/media-organizations-sue-surveillance-tapes/index.html?utm_content=2023-04-12T14%3A58%3A05&utm_medium=social&utm_term=link&utm_source=twCNNp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The suit filed against the justice department under its public records law argues that because the Republican speaker provided the footage to Fox, it should be made available to the public at large.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat denial of access is a stark change of pace for these Plaintiffs, as over the past two years they have diligently, cooperatively, and successfully pursued and obtained access to thousands of videos of the Capitol riot that have been used as evidence or otherwise become judicial records in more than a hundred cases in this District against those charged with organizing or participating in the riot,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the suit, which was filed by CNN, \uc2 Advance Publications\uc2 , the Associated Press, CBS News, \uc2 EW Scripps\uc2 , Gannett, Politico, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  and the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 McCarthy in February handed the footage to conservative Fox commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/12/kevin-mccarthy-jan-6-footage-tucker-carlson-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cslowly roll out\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  footage to other outlets \u8211\'20\'13 which he has not done. Carlson used the footage in segments that attempted to downplay the severity of attack on lawmakers as they were certifying the results of the 2020 election. The release also sparked concerns that it could compromise security arrangements in the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s neighbor Kentucky is having its own reckoning with gun violence after a mass shooting in Louisville on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/louisville-active-shooting-attack-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left five people dead}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/12/gun-divide-stark-relief/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 , the partisan divide over what to do about these repeated acts of violence is as wide as ever in the solidly Republican state. The Post tuned into public events held by two freshman House representatives from the state, one the sole Democrat in its delegation, the other a Republican.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe left and this White House is using the victims of this tragedy \u8211\'20\'13 three children and three adults \u8211\'20\'13 to pursue their agenda, which is to take your constitutional rights,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican Andrew Ogles said in a telephone town hall that the Post described as \u8220\'20\'1Ctightly controlled\u8221\'20\'1D. He went on to blame \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople with mental illness\u8221\'20\'1D for the violence, though ruled out new funding to address the problem, instead saying the education department should redirect money allocated to promote \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical race theory\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which is something the Post notes it is not involved in.\par \par \uc2 At a Louisville news conference, Democratic representative Morgan McGarvey embraced the party\u8217\'20\'19s preferred solutions to America\u8217\'20\'19s gun violence epidemic, including \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking weapons of war off our streets\u8221\'20\'1D, more funding for mental health programs and universal background checks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlease if you are a person of faith and you want to give us your thoughts and your prayers, we want them, and we need them. But we need policies in place that will keep this from happening again so thoughts and prayers do not need to be offered to after another community [is] ripped apart from the savage violence coming from guns,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senators reportedly call for investigation of Tennessee Democrats' ousting\par \par \uc2 Two Democratic senators want the justice department to investigate last week\u8217\'20\'19s expulsion of two Democratic lawmakers from the Tennessee House of Representatives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/04/12/tennessee-expulsions-prompt-senate-democrats-call-doj-inquiry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The letter from \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader representing New York, and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  of Georgia asks attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake all steps necessary to uphold the democratic integrity of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s legislative bodies\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cuse all available legal authorities\u8221\'20\'1D to determine if the expulsion votes against Justin Jones and Justin Pearson broke federal law.\par \par \uc2 The pair of Black lawmakers were removed from the chamber by its Republican supermajority after participating in a protest calling for stricter gun control on the House floor, after six people died in a mass shooting at a Nashville school. A white Democratic colleague who participated in the protest was not expelled, which some Tennessee lawmakers have said was because she did not participate in the disruption to the extent the others did.\par \par \uc2 Jones has already been reinstated to his seat by local authorities in Nashville, while commissioners in Memphis are expected to do the same for Pearson today. In their letter, Warnock and Schumer argue their banishment may have violated the rights of their district\u8217\'20\'19s citizens to be represented, the lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 first amendment rights to free assembly and speech, and federal laws banning racial discrimination.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  Director Kimberly Cheatle. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Even though its agents literally stand next to the president, the Secret Service takes pains to stay out of the political fray, but couldn\u8217\'20\'19t escape questions over how its agents reacted to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 These concerns centered on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/28/secret-service-cellphones-agents-january-6-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the deletion of phone data}}}\uc2  from around the time of the insurrection, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/30/secret-service-tony-ornato-january-6-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unusual decision}}}\uc2  for top agent Tony Ornato to take a political job in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s White House and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/mike-pence-capitol-attack-secret-service-donald-trump-security-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the actions}}}\uc2  of its agents protecting Vice-President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  on the day the Capitol was breached.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2023/04/12/secret-service-trump-indictment-2024-election/11528488002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with USA Today}}}\uc2 , the agency\u8217\'20\'19s recently arrived director Kimberly Cheatle addresses some of these questions. \u8220\'20\'1CI think, unfortunately, the Secret Service has been painted, at times inaccurately, as being a political organization and we\u8217\'20\'19re not,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t talk politics here. We are an agency that truly does take pride in our apolitical mission.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Regarding Ornato taking a job in the White House, Cheatle said in the interview that she did not \u8220\'20\'1Cfault\u8221\'20\'1D the agency\u8217\'20\'19s previous leadership, but \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that I would necessarily make the same decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also addressed concerns that the Secret Service had plans to remove Pence from the Capitol during the insurrection, which could have prevented him from certifying the results of the 2020 election and potentially upending the transition from Trump to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was the assistant director of Protective Operations at the time, and I know the planning that went on for both the rally site \u8230\'20\'26 on the [White House] Ellipse that day and for the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the Capitol. There was no nefarious intent to have anything stopped that day. Our folks, again, did their job \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D she said in the interview.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another Republican thought to be inching their way towards announcing a presidential run is \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor who has transformed the state\u8217\'20\'19s politics since taking office in 2019. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports on how his aggressive use of gerrymandering and attacks on voting rights have undermined Black political power in the Sunshine state:\par \par \uc2 Al Lawson felt the weight of his victory the night he was elected to Congress in 2016.\par \par \uc2 He was born in Midway, a small town that\u8217\'20\'19s part of a stretch of land in northern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  dotted with tobacco fields once home to plantations. A former basketball star, he was once reprimanded for drinking out of a whites-only water fountain. In some of his early campaigns for the state legislature, he ran into the \uc2 Ku Klux Klan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There was jubilation when he was elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverywhere I would go, it was like a celebration,\u8221\'20\'1D Lawson said one morning last month in his office in downtown Tallahassee. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople saying: \u8216\'20\'18Boy, I wish my daddy, my granddaddy \u8211\'20\'13 I really wish they could see this.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Congress, Lawson was a low-key member known for delivering federal money for things like new storm shelters to help his northern Florida communities. He was easily re-elected to the House in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/election-results/2018/florida/#FL-05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2018}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2020/results/state/florida/house/district-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020}}}\uc2 . But when he ran for re-election in 2022, he lost to a white Republican by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/2022-election/results/florida/house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 20 points}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawson\u8217\'20\'19s loss was nearly entirely attributable to Governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 . The governor went out of his way to redraw the boundaries of Lawson\u8217\'20\'19s district to ensure that a Republican could win it. It was a brazen scheme to weaken the political power of Black voters and a striking example of how DeSantis has waged one of the most aggressive \u8211\'20\'13 and successful \u8211\'20\'13 efforts to curtail voting rights in Florida.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/12/ron-desantis-voting-rights-black-voters-florida-gerrymander"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Ron DeSantis waged a targeted assault on Black voters: \u8216\'20\'18I fear for what\u8217\'20\'19s to come\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Election day 2024 is a long way off, and should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s candidacy somehow be felled before then, another Republican appears ready to step in: Tim Scott.\par \par \uc2 The South Carolina lawmaker is the only Black senator in the GOP. Today, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://votetimscott.com/tim-scott-launches-exploratory-committee-for-president-of-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  the formation of an exploratory committee for a presidential run, a key step before launching a campaign outright. Adopting the slogan \u8220\'20\'1CFaith in America\u8221\'20\'1D, he released a video that checks all the boxes for Republican candidates who aren\u8217\'20\'19t Trump: harken back to trying moments in America\u8217\'20\'19s history, attack \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and drop GOP buzz phrases like \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSee, I was raised by a single mother in poverty. The spoons in our apartment were plastic, not silver. But we had faith. We put in the work and we had an unwavering belief that we too could live the American dream. I know America is the land of opportunity, not a land of oppression. I know it because I\u8217\'20\'19ve lived it. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it pains my soul to see the Biden liberals attacking every rung of the ladder that helped me climb,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott says.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full video:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s questions to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about being convicted of a crime weren\u8217\'20\'19t theoretical: the former president has been indicted in Manhattan for allegedly falsifying business records.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have rushed to his defense since the charges were filed late last month, and on Monday, the GOP-controlled House judiciary committee will hold a hearing in New York City on crime, as part of their counterattack to Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 . Democrats have in the past shunned such hearings, but will reportedly show up to this one to defend prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority this morning announced the witnesses who would appear at the hearing. From their press release:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jose Alba, former Manhattan bodega clerk\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Madeline Brame, chairwoman of the Victims Rights Reform Council and mother of a homicide victim\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Harrison, founder of Victims Rights NY\par \par \uc2 They may also announce more witnesses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump: 'I'd never drop out'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gave a lengthy interview to conservative Fox News commentator \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  last night in which he made his usual bombastic claims, as well as a bit of news.\par \par \uc2 Carlson asked the former president, who is vying to return to the White House in next year\u8217\'20\'19s election, whether he would consider dropping out of the presidential race if he was convicted of a crime. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d never drop out. It\u8217\'20\'19s not my thing, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can see the moment where he says that in the clip below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is set to take a major step towards weaning the American car industry off fossil fuels with new regulations announced today. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dani-anguiano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dani Anguiano}}}\uc2  to tell you what they are:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  on Wednesday proposed strict new automobile pollution limits that would require that all-electric vehicles account for as many as two of every three new vehicles sold in the US by 2032 in a plan that would transform the US auto industry.\par \par \uc2 Under the proposed regulation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epa.gov/newsreleases/biden-harris-administration-proposes-strongest-ever-pollution-standards-cars-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ), greenhouse gas emissions for the 2027 through 2032 model years for passenger vehicles would be limited to even stricter levels than the auto industry agreed to in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EPA\uc2  administrator, \uc2 Michael Regan\uc2 , insisted the targets were \u8220\'20\'1Creadily achievable\u8221\'20\'1D, with EV sales tripling since Biden came to office, and despite the skepticism of some automakers about the pace of the transition needed for the plans.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/apr/12/biden-electric-vehicles-pollution-auto-industry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden team proposes strict vehicle pollution limits to boost EV sales}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Those who seek to silence us will not have the final say' declares ousted TN Democrat\par \par \uc2 Justin Pearson and Justin Jones were both Black Democratic lawmakers in the Tennessee House, until the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Republican supermajority last Thursday voted to remove them.\par \par \uc2 The stated reason was that they took part in a demonstration held on the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s floor in which they used bullhorns to join protesters calling for more gun protection following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/27/tennessee-nashville-school-shooting-covenant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mass shooting at a Nashville school}}}\uc2  that killed six people late last month. A white Democratic lawmaker who joined in was not expelled.\par \par \uc2 But Pearson and Jones are both set to boomerang right back to their seats. Jones was reappointed by the Nashville metropolitan council on Monday, while Pearson\u8217\'20\'19s appointment will be up for consideration by the Shelby county board of commissioners in Memphis today. However, both lawmakers will need to win forthcoming special elections to keep their seats for good.\par \par \uc2 In his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/12/opinion/justin-pearson-tennessee.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times essay}}}\uc2 , Pearson outlined the reasons why he wants his seat back, and why he fought so vigorously for gun control. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he has to say:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just our individual voices that were sanctioned and silenced last Thursday. It was the voices of the nearly 135,000 Tennesseans we represented \u8212\'20\'14 many who are desperate for protection from the absence of many common-sense gun safety laws in our state. Since the Covenant School shooting, the Republican supermajority in the State House has done little but advance a bill that would allow teachers to carry guns in school and propose a $140 million budget increase to pay for the presence of armed guards in public schools, further militarizing them without adequate evidence that this makes schools safer.\par \par \uc2 Besides expanding already expansive gun rights, Republican-led statehouses across the country are proposing and passing staggering numbers of bills that serve a fringe, white evangelical agenda that abrogates the rights and freedoms of the rest of us. They\u8217\'20\'19re passing legislation to control the intellectual freedom of writers and educators, proposing laws that would restrict the bodily autonomy of transgender children and people who can become pregnant, and curtailing even our right to vote. Combined with a shrinking social safety net as people lose access to resources to meet basic health, housing and food needs, we have a nation in pain and peril.\par \par \uc2 In a small victory for our people clamoring for change, Gov. \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2  announced Tuesday that he would sign an executive order strengthening background checks for buying firearms and called for Republican lawmakers to support a red flag law.\par \par \uc2 I was elected early this year by the people of Memphis and Millington to stand up for all of us against encroachments on our freedoms.\par \par \uc2 I will continue to fight with and for our people, whether in or out of office. We and the young protesters are the future of a new Tennessee. Those who seek to silence us will not have the final say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Second ousted Tennessee Democrat could be returned to statehouse today\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Justin Pearson was one of two Democratic lawmakers the Tennessee house of representatives expelled last week for holding a noisy protest in favor of gun control, but his exile could end today. Local commissioners in his district will vote on whether to reappoint him to his seat, which is what happened on Monday to Justin Jones, the other legislator booted by the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s GOP majority. \u8220\'20\'1CI wasn\u8217\'20\'19t elected to be pushed to the back of the room and silenced,\u8221\'20\'1D Pearson declared in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/12/opinion/justin-pearson-tennessee.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York Times op-ed}}}\uc2  published this morning. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see if his local counterparts agree.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Northern Ireland, where has met with British prime minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , and will head to Dublin later today. Follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2023/apr/12/joe-biden-us-president-northern-ireland-dup-ireland-rishi-sunak-uk-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our live blog}}}\uc2  for the latest on the president\u8217\'20\'19s travels to the land of his ancestors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will convene the White House\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health care taskforce at 2.45pm as access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/12/mifepristone-abortion-drug-hangs-in-balance-friday-deadline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears imperiled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Scott has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://votetimscott.com/tim-scott-launches-exploratory-committee-for-president-of-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formed an exploratory committee}}}\uc2  to run for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination next year. To succeed, he\u8217\'20\'19ll have to beat the 800-pound Republican gorilla: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230412ej4c001pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
