\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrives in Belfast for Good Friday agreement anniversary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 4,495 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par 21:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US president says he wants to safeguard agreement, signed 25 years ago this week, and support Sunak\u8217\'20\'19s post-Brexit dealSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet with Northern Ireland political party leaders tomorrow, but is not expected to hold a news conference in Ireland.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of today\u8217\'20\'19s news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38#block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 New York Stock Exchange\uc2  next week regarding the debt ceiling. He will probably reiterate the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s demand that the Biden administration accept spending cuts in exchange for their votes to raise it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643562698f08791e579d2b43#block-643562698f08791e579d2b43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will next week}}}\uc2  introduce a resolution to condemn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calls to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and justice department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7#block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning their counterattack}}}\uc2  to House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans next week to hold a hearing on crime in New York City \u8211\'20\'13 where Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  recently filed criminal charges against Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Bragg, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6435aa5f8f08791e579d2ea1#block-6435aa5f8f08791e579d2ea1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  against House judiciary committee chair Jim Jordan to get him to stop messing with his prosecution of the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Montana\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6435a58e8f0891526bb40773#block-6435a58e8f0891526bb40773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might be about}}}\uc2  to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the second trimester of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden arrives in Belfast\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was accompanied by his sister Valerie Biden Owen, his son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , and recently appointed economic envoy to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/northernireland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Northern Ireland}}}\uc2 , Joseph Kennedy II. The president was greeted by Rishi Sunak.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden greeted on windy, chilly Belfast night by UK\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RishiSunak?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RishiSunak}}}\uc2 , UK\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KarenPierceUK?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KarenPierceUK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USAmbUK?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USAmbUK}}}\uc2 Jane Hartley\uc2 , Northern Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chhcalling?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @chhcalling}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 POTUS\u8217\'20\'19s sister Valerie and son Hunter joined the tarmac receiving line. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eUvaoiyTUD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eUvaoiyTUD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Jacobs (@JenniferJJacobs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferJJacobs/status/1645891002631340032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Some background, from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rorycarroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rory Carroll}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lisaocarroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lisa O\u8217\'20\'19Carroll}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The US president was due to be met at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/belfast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Belfast}}}\uc2  international airport by Rishi Sunak on Tuesday night for the start of a visit expected to mix delicate political choreography with economic announcements and events linked to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Irish and Catholic heritage.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters before taking off in Air Force One, Biden said he wanted to safeguard the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/good-friday-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Good Friday agreement}}}\uc2 , which was signed 25 years ago this week, and support Sunak\u8217\'20\'19s post-Brexit deal for the region. Asked what his priorities for the trip were, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CMake sure the Irish accords and Windsor agreements stay in place. Keep the peace and that\u8217\'20\'19s the main thing. It looks like we\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep our fingers crossed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Heavy security on both sides of the border preceded the US entourage, which will include the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , and a recently appointed economic envoy to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/northernireland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Northern Ireland}}}\uc2 , Joseph Kennedy III.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of police and US secret service vehicles sealed off rain-drenched streets around central Belfast on Tuesday. Manhole covers were lifted and checked and sniffer dogs inspected hotel rooms as part of a \u163\'00\'A37m security operation \u8211\'20\'13 bolstered by 300 extra police from the British mainland.\par \par \uc2 In Derry, police recovered four suspected pipe bombs from a cemetery where republicans had staged an Easter Monday commemoration that led to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2023/apr/10/derry-security-operation-under-way-before-dissident-republican-parade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  petrol bomb attacks}}}\uc2  on police. The discovery was a \u8220\'20\'1Csinister and worrying development\u8221\'20\'1D, said the Police Service of Northern Ireland assistant chief constable, Bobby Singleton, with the Police Federation for Northern Ireland saying it was a clear statement of intent to cause harm to police officers.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/11/joe-biden-to-meet-british-pm-and-taoiseach-on-island-of-ireland-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden lands in Belfast ahead of four-day visit to island of Ireland}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden expected to land in Belfast as Ireland trip begins\par \par \uc2 In about 20 minutes, Air Force One is expected to touch down in Belfast, Northern Ireland where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will begin his five-day trip to the island. While he has no public events scheduled this evening, tomorrow he will meet with UK prime minister Rishi Sunak and deliver a speech at \uc2 Ulster University\uc2 , before departing for Dublin.\par \par \uc2 Keep it turned to this blog, where the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  will be covering Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Belfast arrival as it happens. Until then, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what\u8217\'20\'19s happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38#block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 New York Stock Exchange\uc2  next week regarding the debt ceiling. He will probably reiterate the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s demand that the Biden administration accept spending cuts in exchange for their votes to raise it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643562698f08791e579d2b43#block-643562698f08791e579d2b43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will next week}}}\uc2  introduce a resolution to condemn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calls to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and justice department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7#block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning their counterattack}}}\uc2  to House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans next week to hold a hearing on crime in New York City \u8211\'20\'13 where Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  recently filed criminal charges against Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Bragg, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6435aa5f8f08791e579d2ea1#block-6435aa5f8f08791e579d2ea1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  against House judiciary committee chair Jim Jordan to get him to stop messing with his prosecution of the former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Montana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-6435a58e8f0891526bb40773#block-6435a58e8f0891526bb40773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might be about}}}\uc2  to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the second trimester of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate leader demands briefing on leaked Pentagon documents\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  has asked that the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers be briefed on the leaked Pentagon documents concerning US assessments of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMajority Leader Schumer has requested a classified briefing for all senators on the leaked classified US documents on the war in Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson for the senator told the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics live blog.\par \par \uc2 Among the revelations from the documents is that Washington is concerned about Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s military strength ahead of a counteroffensive against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s forces, which expected to start soon. Read more about that below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/11/us-ukraine-counter-offensive-pentagon-leaks-reveal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US feared Ukraine could fall \u8216\'20\'18well short\u8217\'20\'19 in spring counter-offensive, leaks reveal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Republican House judiciary committee chair Jim Jordan has to say about the lawsuit the Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  filed against him:\par \par \uc2 enltrFirst, they indict a president for no crime.\par \par \uc2 Then, they sue to block congressional oversight when we ask questions about the federal funds they say they used to do it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Jim Jordan (@Jim_Jordan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jim_Jordan/status/1645868074644406272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The president he\u8217\'20\'19s referring to here is, of course, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The family of \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , the American Wall Street Journal reporter detained in Russia on espionage charges, has released a statement after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called them today.\par \par \uc2 Read it here:\par \par \uc2 enltrEvan Gershkovich's family released the following statement after their call with President Biden on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5yrL0Z6vab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/5yrL0Z6vab}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UQc3VvYBCL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UQc3VvYBCL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Restuccia (@AndrewRestuccia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewRestuccia/status/1645853470249951234?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manhattan DA sues top Republican to halt meddling with Trump case\par \par \uc2 Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  has filed a lawsuit against Jim Jordan, the Republican chair of the House judiciary committee, to stop his efforts aimed at publicizing details of his office\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/11/nyregion/bragg-lawsuit-jim-jordan-trump-indictment.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jordan is one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s top allies in Congress, and together with other Republicans has demanded documents and testimony from Bragg, who late last month indicted the former president on charges of falsifying business records. Last week, Jordan subpoenaed Mark Pomerantz, a former prosecutor in Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/feb/11/people-vs-donald-trump-review-mark-pomerantz-manhattan-da-alvin-bragg-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who wrote a book}}}\uc2  about why he thinks Trump should face charges. The subpoena requires Pomerantz sit for a deposition before the judiciary committee, which has played a major role in the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s campaign of investigations against the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 Accusing Jordan of a \u8220\'20\'1Cbrazen and unconstitutional attack\u8221\'20\'1D on Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution, and a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransparent campaign to intimidate and attack\u8221\'20\'1D the Manhattan prosecutor, the lawsuit filed in federal court asks a judge to halt the subpoena to Pomerantz, and any future summons.\par \par \uc2 The Times reports that Pomerantz \u8220\'20\'1Chas shown no indication that he is willing to testify voluntarily\u8221\'20\'1D, but declined to comment on Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 A bill to restrict abortions in Montana will become law \u8211\'20\'13 at least temporarily \u8211\'20\'13 if the governor signs it, a judge has ruled, and the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The latest ruling denies a request by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates to preemptively block legislation that would ban the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  method most commonly used in the second trimester.\par \par \uc2 District court judge Kathy Seeley said the request by Planned Parenthood of Montana was made before the bill became law, so there is nothing to block.\par \par \uc2 Montana\u8217\'20\'19s legislature approved the bill on Friday. It would ban dilation and evacuation abortions, which are typically used later than 15 weeks into a pregnancy. The ban will take effect immediately if Republican governor \uc2 Greg Gianforte\uc2  signs it.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood argued the law is unconstitutional based on a 1999 Montana supreme court ruling that found that the state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s right to privacy includes the right to have a pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a provider of the patient\u8217\'20\'19s choice.\par \par \uc2 The organization asked the court to freeze the law preemptively to make sure patients wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be prevented from getting care while the court considered the case.\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1C90 years of service\u8221\'20\'1D poster hangs on the side of a Planned Parenthood office, this one in Missouri, not Montana. Photograph: Lawrence Bryant/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rightwinger \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , a senior aide in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s White House, was spotted this morning in Washington DC, \u8220\'20\'1Centering the area where the grand jury tied to special counsel Jack Smith \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6}}}\uc2  investigation meets,\u8221\'20\'1D NBC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/former-trump-adviser-stephen-miller-appears-dc-federal-court-jan-6-gra-rcna79143?cid=sm_npd_nn_tw_ma&taid=64359921eea76d00011ef574&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Miller and his attorney reportedly would not tell reporters why they were there.\par \par \uc2 The US court of appeals for the DC circuit last week denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s emergency motion to block several senior aides being called to testify, including Miller, former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and former deputy White House chief of staff Dan Scavino, NBC adds.\par \par \uc2 A year ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/15/stephen-miller-january-6-deposition-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miller testified}}}\uc2  to the House of Representatives select committee investigating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the insurrection}}}\uc2  on 6 January 2021, by extremist supporters of Trump who were seeking to keep the then president in office by preventing the official certification by Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 Sources told the Guardian at the time that Miller was testifying about the extent to which Trump encouraged his supporters to march on the US Capitol, inciting an insurrection (for which he was later impeached in an unprecedented move by the House to impeach a US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-impeachment-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for a second time}}}\uc2 , although, once again he was later acquitted by the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Miller was a senior adviser to the-then president Trump and director of speechwriting, known for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/24/stephen-miller-white-nationalist-trump-immigration-guru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hard-right anti-immigration}}}\uc2  beliefs.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  speaking at the Conservative Political Action Conference (CPAC) gathering in March 2023. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic House representative \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2  has announced she has been diagnosed with Parkinson\u8217\'20\'19s disease:\par \par \uc2 enltrOn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WorldParkinsonsDay?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WorldParkinsonsDay}}}\uc2 , I'm here to share that I've been diagnosed with Parkinson's Disease.\par \par \uc2 I'm doing well, and I want to bring about as much good from this diagnosis as I can\u8212\'20\'14including here in Congress. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bvEwzZQbqp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/bvEwzZQbqp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2  (@RepWexton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepWexton/status/1645766336386039812?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Wexton, who represents Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s suburbs near Washington DC, was among the Democrats considered vulnerable in last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election, though she ended up being re-elected with more than 53% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64354f918f0891526bb402fa#block-64354f918f0891526bb402fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is finally getting the access}}}\uc2  it has demanded to the classified documents taken from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , though the materials will only be viewed in secret and by the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top leaders. Meanwhile, Democrats have made an important decision: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64356fe98f0891526bb40490#block-64356fe98f0891526bb40490"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago will be the host city}}}\uc2  for their convention next year. Still no definitive word from Biden on his re-election plans, though yesterday he made it plain as can be by saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI plan on running.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House speaker Kevin McCarthy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38#block-64357f608f0885230b2d8b38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 New York Stock Exchange\uc2  next week regarding the debt ceiling, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll likely demand the Biden administration accept spending cuts in exchange for the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s support in raising it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643562698f08791e579d2b43#block-643562698f08791e579d2b43"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will next week}}}\uc2  introduce a resolution to condemn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s calls to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and justice department.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2023/apr/11/lassified-documents-trump-biden-pentagon-leak-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7#block-643589fa8f0885230b2d8bb7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are planning their counterattack}}}\uc2  to House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans next week to hold a hearing on crime in New York City \u8211\'20\'13 where Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  recently filed criminal charges against Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shifting to the realm of less public Republican activities, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone}}}\uc2  reports on an intensifying conservative effort to undermine voter rolls nationwide:\par \par \uc2 An influential conservative group that has filed numerous lawsuits to force states to clean up their voter rolls, has joined \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other election denial groups in attacking the most robust tool that accurately improves those voter rolls.\par \par \uc2 Judicial Watch\uc2 , whose leader \uc2 Tom Fitton\uc2  urged Trump in 2020 to claim victory before all the votes were tallied, released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judicialwatch.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/ERIC-White-Paper-final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flawed report}}}\uc2  alleging potential violations of federal law by the Electronic Registration Information Center (Eric), a bipartisan consortium of over two dozen states that exchange voter registration data to ensure election security.\par \par \uc2 Fitton\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Eric is part of a growing campaign by Trump-allied election denialist groups and Trump to urge member states to leave the consortium, prompting scathing criticism from voting rights advocates and election experts including some GOP officials.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/11/judicial-watch-electronic-registration-information-center-eric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Key conservative group joins attacks on partnership that improves voter rolls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2  (center) is a Democratic congressman and avowed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  foe. Photograph: Lev Radin/Pacific Press/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Punchbowl News reports today that a group of Democrats will take part in the House judiciary committee hearing in New York City, reversing their non-participation in some of the field visits organized recently by the committee\u8217\'20\'19s GOP chair Jim Jordan.\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s ranking member, New York representative \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , and other Democrats are expected to hold a press conference with city officials around the time of the hearing, Punchbowl reports. The event will be part of their counter-attack to the argument Jordan and other Republicans are expected to make, which is that Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  is focused less on fighting crime, and more on prosecuting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Also journeying to New York City next week is the House judiciary committee, which plans to hold a hearing on crime.\par \par \uc2 The inquiry is part of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to discredit Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , who days ago indicted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for allegedly falsifying business records related to hush money payments made ahead of the 2016 presidential election. Ahead of the hearing, the committee\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account has taken to highlighting violent crimes committed on New York\u8217\'20\'19s streets:\par \par \uc2 enltrMAN SHOT IN THE HEAD IN EAST HARLEM {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vcbOGKsUjl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vcbOGKsUjl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Judiciary GOP (@JudiciaryGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1645808532850360326?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSUSPECT SOUGHT AFTER 17-YEAR-OLD SHOT AND INJURED IN MANHATTAN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nJwkfjsvsU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/nJwkfjsvsU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Judiciary GOP (@JudiciaryGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JudiciaryGOP/status/1645795537252397065?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 New York is considered one of the safest large cities in America, though like many municipalities, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/05/nyregion/new-york-crime-stats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced a recent uptick in crime}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Kevin McCarthy will next week deliver a speech at the New York Stock Exchange, Punchbowl News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the same day ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jim_Jordan?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Jim_Jordan}}}\uc2  ? is holding a hearing on crime in New York, McCarthy is giving a speech at the stock exchange. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NXSrPvwi6I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NXSrPvwi6I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1645807730035400711?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis speech will be debt limit related. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XmzK8T1cwT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XmzK8T1cwT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1645809376660447235?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Congress and the White House need to agree on a way to increase the government\u8217\'20\'19s legal borrowing limit sometime within the next few months, otherwise the United States could default on its debt for the first time in history. That could have catastrophic consequences for the stock market, among other things.\par \par \uc2 Republicans want the Biden administration and his Democratic allies to agree to cut spending in exchange for increasing the debt ceiling, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has refused to negotiate over the issue, saying the limit should be raised without preconditions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democratic-run states are stockpiling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication following a conservative Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that revoked authorization for one of the drugs used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic governors have moved swiftly to protect access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their states after a ruling by a Texas judge late last week threatened access to the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 In an announcement on Monday, Governor \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/massachusetts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massachusetts}}}\uc2  said her state had ordered about 15,000 doses of mifepristone, the first of two drugs in a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen that has been approved for use up to the 10th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Healey also issued an executive order that she said would help protect access to medication abortions and shield providers who perform them.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 , Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , also a Democrat, said his state had secured an emergency stockpile of up to 2m pills of misoprostol, the second drug in the regimen that can be used safely on its own, though is slightly less effective as a single medication. That drug, which is used to treat other medical conditions, is also being targeted by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups seeking to remove it from the market.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/11/democratic-governors-stockpile-abortion-drugs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not cave\u8217\'20\'19: governors stockpile \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drugs as access is threatened}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Tennessee last week ousted two Democratic lawmakers who had staged a noisy protest in favor of gun control on the floor of the house of representatives, but it was a pyrrhic victory. One of the lawmakers was reinstated to the legislature yesterday, and the second may be voted back in tomorrow. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on this ongoing saga:\par \par \uc2 The city of Nashville\u8217\'20\'19s governing council on Monday afternoon voted unanimously to return the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/06/tennessee-gun-control-protest-house-expel-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expelled Black lawmaker}}}\uc2  Justin Jones to the Tennessee state legislature.\par \par \uc2 The body\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority state lawmakers had expelled Jones and fellow house member Justin Pearson late last week because they led protests in the chamber demanding gun control after yet another mass shooting in an American school, this one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at an elementary school}}}\uc2  in the city days before.\par \par \uc2 Moments later, Jones marched to the capitol several blocks away. He took the oath of office on the steps and entered the building while supporters sang This Little Light of Mine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/nashville-council-votes-reinstate-expelled-democrat-justin-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville council votes to reinstate expelled Democrat Justin Jones}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chicago to host 2024 Democratic national convention\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC) \uc2 today selected Chicago as the host city for its convention next year, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will likely again receive the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination to contest the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats will gather to showcase our historic progress including building an economy from the middle out and bottom up, not from the top down,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement announcing the decision.\par \par \uc2 DNC chair \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe midwest reflects America and will give Democrats an opportunity to showcase some of President Biden and Vice-President Harris\u8217\'20\'19s most significant accomplishments for American families. I\u8217\'20\'19m grateful to the leadership of Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s bid for being great partners, as well as to the other cities for putting forward such strong bids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chicago beat out Atlanta, Houston and New York in the race for the convention\u8217\'20\'19s host city.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has boarded Air Force One for a flight to Belfast, Northern Ireland, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll meet with British prime minister Rishi Sunak before traveling to the Republican of Ireland.\par \par \uc2 Just before the flight, the president spoke to reporters are his ongoing efforts to free \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2 , an American reporter for the Wall Street Journal detained in Russia. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video:\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the Biden administration officially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/journalist-evan-gershkovich-wrongfully-detained-russia-wall-street-journal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared Gershkovich}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongfully detained\u8221\'20\'1D, indicating they give no credence to Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s espionage allegations against him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The bigger classified documents scandal gripping Washington today involves batches of leaked materials from the Pentagon that have revealed a number of secrets embarrassing to the United States. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/justinmccurry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin McCurry}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ben-doherty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ben Doherty}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The US is attempting to mend fences with key allies after leaked Pentagon documents claimed Washington had been spying on friendly countries including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/south-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Korea}}}\uc2  and Israel.\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of defence, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , spoke to his South Korean counterpart on Tuesday as officials in Seoul denied the possibility that the president\u8217\'20\'19s office could have been the source of leaks over South Korean arms sales to the US.\par \par \uc2 The disclosure of the highly classified material represents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/10/us-defense-documents-leak-analysts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington\u8217\'20\'19s worst national security breach in many years}}}\uc2  and included details about Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s lack of ammunition and US intelligence collection methods used against Russia.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/11/pentagon-leaks-us-seeks-to-mend-ties-after-claims-washington-spied-on-key-allies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pentagon leaks: US seeks to mend ties after claims Washington spied on key allies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has for months appeared apoplectic about the investigation into his possession of classified documents, among other matters. That anger has lately resolved itself into a call, taken up by his supporters, to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and justice department.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an uncomfortable message for his fellow Republicans, who like to tell Americans that they\u8217\'20\'19re the real tough-on-crime party. The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  intends to take full advantage of that dynamic with a resolution he plans to introduce next week repudiating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s call to defund federal law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he wrote in a letter to senators:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s call for defunding federal law enforcement agencies is a baseless, self-serving broadside against the men and women who keep our nation safe. The good work of the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  and the Department of Justice sends criminals to prison for bank robbery, sex trafficking, child pornography, hate crimes, terrorism, fraud and so much more. The former president and his allies in Congress must not subjugate justice and public safety because of their own personal grievances.\par \par \uc2 Senators from across the political spectrum and of both political parties should denounce such attempts by the former president and his allies to degrade public trust in our federal law enforcement agencies. The Senate must recommit that the United States is a nation of laws. As free people, we rely on the necessary and professional work of our federal law enforcement agencies to promote the safety and general welfare of our country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three powerful men in trouble: the classified documents scandal, explained\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s one lesson to be drawn from the classified documents scandal that\u8217\'20\'19s gripped Washington since last August, it\u8217\'20\'19s this: people who work at the White House apparently like to hang on to government secrets.\par \par \uc2 Now, the three powerful men implicated here are in varying degrees of trouble, though with none of their cases resolved, we don\u8217\'20\'19t know yet how severe the consequences could be.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appears to be in the greatest peril. He\u8217\'20\'19s being investigated by special counsel Jack Smith over the secret materials the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found when they searched Mar-a-Lago last August \u8211\'20\'13 which only happened after the former president refused months of entreaties to hand over all the materials that he had. Smith is also looking into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the January 6 insurrection and the broader effort to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 But it turns out \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had his own stash of classified documents. Unlike Trump, the president reportedly started handing them over to government secret keepers as soon as he became aware he had the materials \u8211\'20\'13 which date back to his time as a senator and vice-president \u8211\'20\'13 at his former office and residence, though the White House did keep quiet for months about the discoveries after they were first made around the time of last November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election. Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has appointed another special prosecutor, Robert Hur, to look into whether Biden broke the law here.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  also kept classified documents at his home in Indiana, and has since turned them over to the powers that be. Garland has not appointed a special prosecutor to look into this.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders get to see Trump, Biden, Pence classified documents\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. We\u8217\'20\'19ve known for months that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  were holding on to classified documents they apparently should not have possessed \u8211\'20\'13 but what, exactly, did they have? The leaders of Congress are finding out, after the Democratic and Republican leaders in each chamber as well as the top lawmakers on the intelligence committees were given access to the material taken from three men, Punchbowl News reports. It remains to be seen if the lawmakers will keep quiet about what they saw, or air their views about the issue, which presents varying degrees of legal peril for the three men.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Washington continues to reel from a major leak of US intelligence materials, and national security officials say they don\u8217\'20\'19t know yet if the apparently purloined documents have been contained.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is heading to Northern Ireland where he will, among other things, celebrate the 25th anniversary of the Good Friday peace agreement that mostly quelled decades of violence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief reporters during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flight to Belfast.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230411ej4b001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
