\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  pill access in doubt after Texas judge suspends approval\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor and agencies \par \uc2 1,067 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par 11:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling on mifepristone, widely used for medical abortions, sets up legal showdown as Washington state issues conflicting order\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Texas on Friday suspended US approval of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication mifepristone, one of the two drugs commonly used for medication abortions, in a closely watched case brought by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 But shortly after, a conflicting ruling came out of another federal court in Washington state, ordering the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  to refrain from taking any action that would affect the pill\u8217\'20\'19s availability. The two rulings throw the future of the drug into question, increasing the chances that the supreme court will ultimately decide its fate.\par \par \uc2 The Texas decision, a preliminary injunction issued by US district judge Matthew Kacsmaryk, orders the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to pause mifepristone\u8217\'20\'19s approval while a lawsuit challenging the safety and approval of the drug proceeds.\par \par \uc2 His ruling, however, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately go into effect, as he gives the federal government seven days to appeal, which federal lawyers representing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  are expected to do so swiftly.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said his administration would fight the Texas decision. \u8220\'20\'1CIf this ruling were to stand, then there will be virtually no prescription, approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , that would be safe from these kinds of political, ideological attacks,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said the ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cthreatens the rights of women nationwide to make decisions about their healthcare and the ability to access medication prescribed to them by their doctors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CThe justice department strongly disagrees with the decision of the district court for the northern district of Texas in Alliance for Hippocratic Medicine v FDA and will be appealing the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision and seeking a stay pending appeal. Today\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturns the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s expert judgment, rendered over two decades ago, that mifepristone is safe and effective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conflicting Washington decision came in a lawsuit brought by Democratic state attorneys general seeking to remove federal restrictions on how the pill can be distributed .\par \par \uc2 The Texas case against the \uc2 FDA\uc2  was brought by \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (\uc2 ADF\uc2 ), a Christian conservative legal advocacy group, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/sites/default/files/2022-11/Alliance-for-Hippocratic-Medicine-v-FDA-2022-11-18-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arguing that}}}\uc2  the \uc2 FDA\uc2  exceeded its regulatory authority when it approved mifepristone more than two decades ago, in 2000.\par \par \uc2 The Trump-appointed judge didn\u8217\'20\'19t go as far as the plaintiffs wanted by withdrawing the approvals of chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs and removing them from the list of approved drugs. But he put a \u8220\'20\'1Cstay\u8221\'20\'1D or hold on approval of the drug.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs included widely disputed claims in their case, arguing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to extend the gestational age up to which mifepristone could be prescribed put pregnant women and girls at risk; and that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2021 decision to remove the in-person dispensing requirement over mifepristone during the pandemic put pregnant people at risk. They also claimed the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfailed to acknowledge and address the federal laws that prohibit the distribution of chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs by postal mail\u8221\'20\'1D, invoking a 19th-century law which made it illegal to send \u8220\'20\'1Cobscene, lewd or lascivicious\u8221\'20\'1D items through the mail, including pornography and abortifacients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSimply put, \uc2 FDA\uc2  stonewalled judicial review \u8211\'20\'13 until now,\u8221\'20\'1D Kacsmaryk wrote in his 67-page ruling.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone has been repeatedly found to be safe and effective and is used across the world. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration, responding to the lawsuit, has said the drug\u8217\'20\'19s approval was well supported by science and that the challenge to the \uc2 FDA\uc2  comes much too late.\par \par \uc2 The US justice department has also argued that a ruling in favor of the plaintiffs would undercut trust in the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , the agency that signs off on the safety of food products and drugs in the US and would increase the burden on surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics already overcrowded with women coming from states that now ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  warned in legal arguments in January that a decision in favor of the \uc2 ADF\uc2  would do \u8220\'20\'1Clongstanding scientific determination based on speculative allegations of harm\u8221\'20\'1D, and would \u8220\'20\'1Cupend the status quo and the reliance interests of patients and doctors who depend on mifepristone, as well as businesses involved with mifepristone distribution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jenny Ma, senior counsel to the Center for Reproductive Rights, warned that \u8220\'20\'1Cif plaintiffs can just bring lawsuits like this, based on junk science, the impact goes far beyond medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It really seeks to undermine the entirety of \uc2 FDA\uc2  authority over drug approval.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kacsmaryk, a Trump-appointed judge, is thought to have been targeted by the \uc2 ADF\uc2  in a process known as \u8220\'20\'1Cjudge shopping\u8221\'20\'1D because of his work with far-right organizations. He previously worked for the \uc2 First Liberty Institute\uc2 , a conservative Christian organization that focuses on litigation against LGBTQ+ and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Clinics and doctors that prescribe the two-drug combination have said that if mifepristone were pulled from the market, they would switch to using only the second drug, misoprostol. That single-drug approach has a slightly lower rate of effectiveness in ending pregnancies, but it is widely used in countries where mifepristone is illegal or unavailable.\par \par \uc2 The decision represents major victory for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement less than a year after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, which guaranteed a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and led to full \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in 13 states, while 16 states have laws specifically targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications.\par \par \uc2 Advocates and progressive states have been bracing for the national reverberations of Kacsmaryk\u8217\'20\'19s decision. This week the governor of Washington state said it had purchased a three-year supply of the leading \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication in anticipation.\par \par \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2 , a Democratic lawmaker, said he ordered the department of corrections, which has a pharmacy license, to buy 30,000 doses of the generic version of mifepristone at a cost of about $1.28m, or $42.50 each pill. The shipment arrived in late March.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Texas lawsuit is a clear and present danger to patients and providers all across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Inslee said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWashington will not sit by idly and risk the devastating consequences of inaction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is also the subject of lawsuits in West Virginia and North Carolina seeking to expand access to the drug by arguing that state restrictions conflict with federal law.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press and Reuters contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230411ej4b0020o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
