\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will not cave\u8217\'20\'19: governors stockpile  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  drugs as access is threatened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,125 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par 12:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Massachusetts, California and Washington pledge to provide medication after a federal judge invalidated 23-year \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic governors have moved swiftly to protect access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their states after a ruling by a Texas judge late last week threatened access to the widely used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 In an announcement on Monday, Governor \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  of Massachusetts said her state had ordered about 15,000 doses of mifepristone, the first of two drugs in a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen that has been approved for use up to the 10th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Healey also issued an executive order that she said would help protect access to medication abortions and shield providers who perform them.\par \par \uc2 In California, Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , also a Democrat, said his state had secured an emergency stockpile of up to 2m pills of misoprostol, the second drug in the regimen that can be used safely on its own, though is slightly less effective as a single medication. That drug, which is used to treat other medical conditions, is also being targeted by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups seeking to remove it from the market.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn response to this extremist ban on a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug, our state has secured a stockpile of an alternative medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug to ensure that Californians continue to have access to safe reproductive health treatments,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not cave to extremists who are trying to outlaw these critical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal in California.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Their actions come after US district judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/10/judge-abortion-pill-ruling-trump-appointed-matthew-kacsmaryk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matthew Kacsmaryk}}}\uc2 , an appointee of Donald Trump known for his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views, issued a ruling late on Friday that invalidated the 23-year-old approval of mifepristone by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ). On the same night, a federal judge in Washington state issued a contradictory ruling that ordered the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to maintain the drug\u8217\'20\'19s approval in at least 17 states where Democrats had sued.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/10/us-appeals-texas-judge-abortion-pill-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justice department appealed}}}\uc2  the Texas ruling, asking a federal appeals court to place a hold on the \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary and unprecedented order\u8221\'20\'1D. Underscoring the legal uncertainty surrounding the dueling orders, the administration separately asked the federal court in Washington state for clarity.\par \par \uc2 With access to the drug imperiled, and Democrats stymied in Washington by the Republican majority in the House of Representatives, a handful of liberal state governors said they were taking matters into their own hands.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA judge has made a politically motivated decision to override doctors, patients and medical experts and block access to critical medications,\u8221\'20\'1D Healey said on Monday, unveiling the plan at a press conference outside the Massachusetts statehouse in Boston. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we collectively are saying loud and clear: not on our watch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of the Texas ruling, the Democratic governor of Washington, \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2 , announced last week that his state would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/04/04/1167867948/washington-state-stockpiles-thousands-of-abortion-pills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stockpile}}}\uc2  a three-year supply of mifepristone in the event the drug became more difficult to access. Days later, Kacsmaryk issued his ruling.\par \par \uc2 Several other Democratic governors and state attorneys general have condemned the ruling while seeking to make clear that, at least for now, the drug remains available. Some went further, promising to keep medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal and accessible in their states, although without providing further details.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/02/medication-abortion-now-accounts-more-half-all-us-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than half}}}\uc2  of abortions in the US rely on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and most of those involve the two-drug protocol. If the appeals court doesn\u8217\'20\'19t intervene, the Texas ruling would take effect on Friday with far-reaching implications for access.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone to terminate pregnancy in 2000, when used with misoprostol. Despite claims made in the Texas lawsuit, there is decades\u8217\'20\'19 worth of scientific research concluding that mifepristone is safe.\par \par \uc2 States have become the epicenter of the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark decision}}}\uc2  last June to overturn Roe v Wade. Since then, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2023/01/six-months-post-roe-24-us-states-have-banned-abortion-or-are-likely-do-so-roundup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen Republican-led states}}}\uc2  have enacted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or severely restricted access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 ?Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have long targeted medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the most common method for terminating a pregnancy in the US. But it became the focus of efforts after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark decision}}}\uc2  last June to overturn Roe v Wade, allowing states to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2023/01/six-months-post-roe-24-us-states-have-banned-abortion-or-are-likely-do-so-roundup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen Republican-led states}}}\uc2  moved quickly to ban or severely restrict abortions?, with scores of new limits pending before state legislatures this session, Democratic-led states have pushed in the opposite direction. Yet if the Texas ruling stands, experts say it would upend access nationwide, limiting the drug even in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents in blue states denounced the efforts by Democratic governors to preserve access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is appalling that \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  is so obsessed with ending the lives of children in the womb that he is attempting to stockpile dangerous and potentially illegal drugs,\u8221\'20\'1D the California Family Council president, Jonathan Keller, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonathanKeller/status/1645505807470194689?cxt=HHwWgsDToYm0gdYtAAAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia again proves the only \u8216\'20\'18choice\u8217\'20\'19 they care about is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Newsom said the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1Cignores facts, science and the law\u8221\'20\'1D in a way that puts \u8220\'20\'1Cthe health of millions of women and girls at risk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal and accessible here in California and we won\u8217\'20\'19t stand by as fundamental freedoms are stripped away,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Other supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights similarly denounced the conservative judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cunprincipled\u8221\'20\'1D and out of step with the American public. In states where the issue has been put on the ballot, from right-leaning Kansas to battleground Michigan and liberal Vermont, voters have opted to preserve or expand access.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve fought like hell to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and I\u8217\'20\'19m not backing down,\u8221\'20\'1D Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , said on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CI will keep taking steps to expand access to reproductive healthcare and fight against anyone threatening our rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitmer recently signed legislation repealing the state\u8217\'20\'19s nearly century-old \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, after Michigan voters overwhelmingly approved a ballot initiative in November to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections into the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and reproductive rights advocates believe the issue will continue to motivate voters in the coming election cycles after lifting them to victories across the country in the 2022 midterms. Last week\u8217\'20\'19s election of a liberal judge to serve on the Wisconsin supreme court brought fresh evidence of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/apr/05/wisconsin-supreme-court-election-results-janet-protasiewicz-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enduring potency of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  politics}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision will only enrage Americans further and move them to more action,\u8221\'20\'1D Mini Timmaraju, president of the Naral Pro-Choice America advocacy group, said on a call with reporters on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1COur eyes are on 2023 and 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 2022 was just the beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020230411ej4b000rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
